{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition","id":462775,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Werewolf 2e Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T16:22:33-07:00","id":462775,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Werewolf 2e Edition","content":"I know -I- could use a thread like this while I'm digesting the new core, so I figured it would be helpful for multiple people.<br /> <br /> First question: if I combine Gaze of the Moon from Gift of Dominance with Gaze of the Moon from Gift of Change, how long would the resulting Awestruck condition last? Since it only inflicts Lunancy for a moment and Awestruck lasts until the being stops inflicting Lunacy, RAW says it'd last for only a moment before resetting...but that seems a little iffy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T16:32:57-07:00","id":462797,"title":"","content":"With Gaze of the Moon, the werewolf's eyes only change for a moment, the Lunacy lasts. With Glorious Lunacy, depending on how strict you are to the words, it might not be compatible with Gaze of the Moon, as it activates, 'When entering a form that inflicts Lunacy.' But if you did want to allow it to work with Gaze of the Moon you would just let it last like all the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:10:16-07:00","id":462844,"title":"","content":"Does a &quot;major template&quot; Wolf-Blood retain its ability to use rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:17:51-07:00","id":462873,"title":"","content":"I'd say the rules say no. At that point you aren't a Wolf-Blooded, you're a Thing with a Tell. But it really seems like the kind of thing you might allow anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T20:53:25-07:00","id":463062,"title":"","content":"There's nothing about Pack Rites that require you to be Wolf-Blooded, as far as I can tell. Plain humans can do them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:09:36-07:00","id":463073,"title":"","content":"You need the appropriate Tells to lead them, Errol. Horse, Spirit Double and Waystone are sufficient. It's in the sidebar Other Ritemasters on pg. 143.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:33:24-07:00","id":464187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=463073#post463073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need the appropriate Tells to lead them, Errol. Horse, Spirit Double and Waystone are sufficient. It's in the sidebar Other Ritemasters on pg. 143.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go down two paragraphs, it's explicitly noted that (in &quot;very rare occasions&quot;), there are &quot;humans who are performing Pack Rites by themselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> Being Wolf-Blooded with a particular Tell is required only if you want to pretend to be a werewolf ritemaster, not a ritemaster at all.<br /> <br /> So, as examples, Banish and Hunting Ground would fail if it was just a group of humans, because they rely on Shadow laws invoking a connection to Father Wolf, but Harness the Cycle and Moon's Mad Love have the standard chance to succeed, because they require no such connection.<br /> <br /> There's a further bit about Claimed acting as ritemasters, but the note about how the rites are &quot;completely unknown to the People&quot; suggest that they're rites invoking laws unavailable to humans but available to other spirits, which is not at all a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:31:21-07:00","id":466446,"title":"","content":"I have a question that hopefully has a simple answer... If an Uratha encounters one of their active Kuruth Triggers, do they immediately go into Wasu-im or do they get a resistance roll (Resolve + Composure) first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5361-nicebrian","name":"NiceBrian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5361_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:33:22-07:00","id":466449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NiceBrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=466446#post466446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question that hopefully has a simple answer... If an Uratha encounters one of their active Kuruth Triggers, do they immediately go into Wasu-im or do they get a resistance roll (Resolve + Composure) first?</div> </div> </div> </div>No roll, straight to Wasu-Im.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T01:37:00-07:00","id":467131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=466449#post466449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No roll, straight to Wasu-Im.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I had a feeling that was the case but wasn't sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5361-nicebrian","name":"NiceBrian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5361_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T03:34:32-07:00","id":469275,"title":"","content":"For those kuruth triggers: do they reset after the death rage wears off? It's the new moon and my irraka sees it in the sky, however, her packmates are prepared and manage to contian her without too much damage being done (and let's just pretend none of them fall to kuruth too). When she comes to and sees the new moon, does the cycle start again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:37:00-07:00","id":469857,"title":"","content":"If it's a common trigger then yes, the character would need to see/be aware of the trigger and then they would enter Wasu Im. Staying indoors and away from windows would be enough to avoid the trigger A passive trigger of your auspice moon means you may as well cage yourself for the evening and keep doing so until you get your Harmony back in balance. It doesn't matter if the character can see the moon or not, they don't have to be aware the moon is out before entering Wasu Im (being in a windowless basement room for example).<br /> <br /> This fits the &quot;uncontrollable rampaging monster under the moon&quot; part of the werewolf myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T03:04:40-07:00","id":469997,"title":"","content":"While I can understand the wolf-blooded of the pack getting aspirations (as they have actual traits), what exactly is the point of the humans in a pack getting them? Can you use their beats/xp to increase the rolls they can make?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T03:11:39-07:00","id":469999,"title":"","content":"It gives them a bit of characterisation the storyteller can use to flesh out their reactions and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T04:07:46-07:00","id":470049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=469857#post469857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a common trigger then yes, the character would need to see/be aware of the trigger and then they would enter Wasu Im. Staying indoors and away from windows would be enough to avoid the trigger A passive trigger of your auspice moon means you may as well cage yourself for the evening and keep doing so until you get your Harmony back in balance. It doesn't matter if the character can see the moon or not, they don't have to be aware the moon is out before entering Wasu Im (being in a windowless basement room for example).<br /> <br /> This fits the &quot;uncontrollable rampaging monster under the moon&quot; part of the werewolf myth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh no, I get that. What I meant was does the death rage basically last all night or will it end after however many minutes/hours your harmony states like a nomral kuruth? Basically, do you only have one nightly Death Rage or is your character staying in that cage all night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:46:40-07:00","id":470117,"title":"","content":"Since the Sacred Hunt doesn't require specifics, details, or even a name, could I specify a variable prey?<br /> <br /> Here's what I mean:<br /> <br /> <b>Ritemaster: </b>I declare &quot;The holder of the Thunderer's Hammer&quot; as prey.<br /> Result A: The current holder/keeper/whatever is designated as prey. If the hammer changes hands, the original target is still the prey for the effects of the Hunt.<br /> Result B: Whenever the hammer changes hands, the new keeper/holder/whatever becomes the prey, and effects targeting the prey will re-resolve.<br /> Result C: The Storyteller arches an eyebrow at the ritemaster and says, &quot;No.&quot; and then hurls him out of her house.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:19:11-07:00","id":470162,"title":"","content":"I think result B would be the one. But since the hunt doesn't seem to be about killing the target, if you just run into NPC-A and NPC-B, and NPC-A is the holder, perhaps your hunt would end before he tosses it to NPC-B, who decides to wail on you with it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could end up screwing yourself by putting the target of your hunt increasingly out of reach. What if someone just puts it in a box and has it sent to Timbuktu, who then drives west to the coast and tosses it in the ocean? No one's holding it and you're stuck in Siskur-Dah. I don't recall any specifics about this, but I think failing a hunt to that degree would be a depressing failure to beings that are part spirits of the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-06-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T09:20:43-07:00","id":470186,"title":"","content":"I think in that particular case you'd be better off naming the hammer itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:18:26-07:00","id":470233,"title":"","content":"I forget that you could theoretically name things or places in lieu of persons or organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:52:22-07:00","id":470250,"title":"","content":"You can call Siskur-Dah on anything. An infamous pack could call a sacred hunt on their bad reputation. A pack in California could call a sacred hunt on the drought. I recall one of the writers (I think it may have been Chris, but I'm not sure) during previews saying you could call a sacred hunt on Death if you wanted to, though you'd obviously have a hell of a time completing that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T18:32:21-07:00","id":471925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soonmot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=470049#post470049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh no, I get that. What I meant was does the death rage basically last all night or will it end after however many minutes/hours your harmony states like a nomral kuruth? Basically, do you only have one nightly Death Rage or is your character staying in that cage all night?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crap, sorry for overlooking this. It would last all night long if it was a passive trigger, as soon as one bout of Wasu Im ended the next would start because the moon was in the sky. Because it's passive the werewolf in question doesn't have to be aware of the trigger in order for it to affect him. Summertime might be a bit weird as the sun and moon are both visible simultaneously for some time at dusk and dawn. I might mess with my players using that (if/when I can get my friends to try something new.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:55:51-07:00","id":473804,"title":"","content":"Can you take both the Moon-oriented wolfblood merits and the Wolf-oriented wolfblood merits in 2e, or only one or the other? I know the fluff indicates wolfbloods either come from one side of the bloodline or the other, but wasn't there crossbreeding between bloodlines along the way, and not all wolfblood-wolfblood pairings produced full Uratha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T03:57:10-07:00","id":474051,"title":"","content":"My reading was that the two categories were fairly broad generalisations that don't exist in any metaphysical sense. It's just how uratha distinguish between wolfblooded with spirit powers and ones with more physical advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:36:51-07:00","id":474405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=473804#post473804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take both the Moon-oriented wolfblood merits and the Wolf-oriented wolfblood merits in 2e, or only one or the other? I know the fluff indicates wolfbloods either come from one side of the bloodline or the other, but wasn't there crossbreeding between bloodlines along the way, and not all wolfblood-wolfblood pairings produced full Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can take both, I believe. There aren't strictly two bloodlines of Wolf-Blooded, and Wolf-Blooded pairings often won't produce full Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:35:48-07:00","id":477076,"title":"","content":"Does violating a Tribal Vow count as a violation against the Oath of the Moon? I think it is, as the book states that those Vows are sworn upon the Oath, but I want to be sure, because that would help in the Conversion work I'm doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:13:47-07:00","id":477101,"title":"","content":"That's how I understand it, yes. Although personally, I would treat it more like violating a Totem's Ban.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T12:45:51-07:00","id":478237,"title":"","content":"In our group we did also treat it like Charlaquin said she would. The players even got some spritual vibe warning them to treat careful while doing things that could lead to a violation of the Tribal Vow &quot;ban&quot;. This made the player realize what was about to happen but if she had transgressed I would use the Ban condition to highten the relevance of the vow. <br /> <br /> Quick question about spirit negotiations:<br /> The Social Combat rules say, the number of Doors are based on Resolve and Composure - does that mean a spirit in Hisil always uses its Passive? We treated it like this for an rank 2 spirit with not that much Passive - but doesn't that lead to incredible long time spans only resolving this social combat considering that most spirits start with an impression level of hostile or neutral? Did we get something wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5433-zandruin","name":"Zandruin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:33:28-07:00","id":478308,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by passive. Since Spirits use the simplified traits, I would base their Doors on their Resistance. Probably the lower of Resistance or Rank. It does take a long time to maneuver anyone at a neutral impression (and it's impossible at hostile) unless you force doors. In my experience, most of the problems people have with the social maneuvering system is that they don't force doors nearly enough. I'm guessing that's because it's presented alongside hard leverage, so people assume forcing doors always means using coercion. But you actually don't need hard leverage to force doors (though it helps) and it doesn't need to involve threatening the mark. Forcing Doors is just your option for single-roll social actions. Also, telling a spirit &quot;do as I say or I'll call a <i>Siskur Dah</i> on you&quot; is a VERY Uratha thing to do, and I'd count that threat as pretty solid Hard Leverage, depending on the pack's strength relative to the spirit and their reputation among the local spirit courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T01:29:57-07:00","id":478873,"title":"","content":"Forcing doors could be done with the typical ice-king/queen treatment, or guilt-tripping, or say, withholding sex on your SO, to put things into perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T04:37:06-07:00","id":478946,"title":"","content":"So, I just noticed that I can't find any reference to werewolves always being able to shift back to human reflexively for free like they could in 1st edition. Is that not a thing any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T04:49:34-07:00","id":478952,"title":"","content":"At Harmony 4, 5 and 6 it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T04:56:35-07:00","id":478957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean aside from that. Before they could do that regardless of moon phase, so now I'm wondering if they can do it regardless of harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:05:01-07:00","id":478962,"title":"","content":"Nope. Shapeshifting is pretty easy providing you're not at the 9 or 10 Harmony. Human isn't your 'true' form anymore, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:06:37-07:00","id":478964,"title":"","content":"So getting stuck in wolf form is something that can actually happen now. Cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T16:47:45-07:00","id":481720,"title":"","content":"Is using a Numina a Reflexive Action or just an Action, or are they classified elsewhere?<br /> <br /> I do know Numina are rolled, Power + Finesse, and some are not rolled if specifically stated but I have yet to find an answer about what kind of action they are. Many seem to be powers you should spend a whole Action on, Telekinesis, Blast, etc. Others like Regenerate seem like they should be Reflexive but don't have an upper limit stated.<br /> <br /> I already posted about this, but I figure this is the better thread to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T04:56:19-07:00","id":482221,"title":"","content":"Regenerate seems to be a one-level-per-turn deal, which means the dread power version is a bit better and one more reason to be scared of idigam. <br /> <br /> Actually, while I'm here, how do the dread powers with dot ratings work? Does each dot take up a slot?<br /> <br /> And in the new version of the 2e book the Efficient Killer merit is noted to be a &quot;common kuruth trigger&quot;. By &quot;common&quot; do they mean as far as that harmony chart is concerned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:05:59-07:00","id":482343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=482221#post482221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regenerate seems to be a one-level-per-turn deal, which means the dread power version is a bit better and one more reason to be scared of idigam.<br /> <br /> Actually, while I'm here, how do the dread powers with dot ratings work? Does each dot take up a slot?<br /> <br /> And in the new version of the 2e book the Efficient Killer merit is noted to be a &quot;common kuruth trigger&quot;. By &quot;common&quot; do they mean as far as that harmony chart is concerned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dread Powers with dot ratings all take up one slot, they just have variable effects depending on the dots selected.<br /> <br /> I do indeed mean that Efficient Killer's trigger is common per the Harmony chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:10:56-07:00","id":482372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=481720#post481720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is using a Numina a Reflexive Action or just an Action, or are they classified elsewhere?<br /> <br /> I do know Numina are rolled, Power + Finesse, and some are not rolled if specifically stated but I have yet to find an answer about what kind of action they are. Many seem to be powers you should spend a whole Action on, Telekinesis, Blast, etc. Others like Regenerate seem like they should be Reflexive but don't have an upper limit stated.<br /> <br /> I already posted about this, but I figure this is the better thread to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame DaveB for the spirit rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As a rough guide, try the following.<br /> <br /> Innocuous and Stalwart are always on, other Numina can be used once per turn per the normal action rules.<br /> <br /> Ghost Eater, Mortal Mask, Regenerate, and Speed are reflexive actions, the others are instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:17:06-07:00","id":482375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=471925#post471925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crap, sorry for overlooking this. It would last all night long if it was a passive trigger, as soon as one bout of Wasu Im ended the next would start because the moon was in the sky. Because it's passive the werewolf in question doesn't have to be aware of the trigger in order for it to affect him. Summertime might be a bit weird as the sun and moon are both visible simultaneously for some time at dusk and dawn. I might mess with my players using that (if/when I can get my friends to try something new.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. You only hit passive/common/specific triggers once per night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:33:45-07:00","id":482406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=482343#post482343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do indeed mean that Efficient Killer's trigger is common per the Harmony chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a General or Personal Trigger? That is, if you are fighting a group of bad guys dedicated to using all-out attacks, could you efficiently kill them all and only hit the trigger once for the night, or does it fall under the &quot;no such limits&quot; category?<br /> <br /> Edit: looking a little closer at your more recent post, it seems you're saying passive/common/specific are never general. So... I guess this is answered already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:10:52-07:00","id":482446,"title":"","content":"The way it works if you hit it at all then the rest of the fight isn't going to be a problem, because you're going to be on a mindless rampage for the next ten minutes at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:19:49-07:00","id":482451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=482372#post482372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blame DaveB for the spirit rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As a rough guide, try the following.<br /> <br /> Innocuous and Stalwart are always on, other Numina can be used once per turn per the normal action rules.<br /> <br /> Ghost Eater, Mortal Mask, Regenerate, and Speed are reflexive actions, the others are instant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T11:32:07-07:00","id":482604,"title":"","content":"Question: Is carrying silver still a Harmony breaking point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:20:20-07:00","id":482622,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm aware, no. Just using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:02:00-07:00","id":482661,"title":"","content":"I might make it one at Harmony 3 and under, since it could be seen as violating the Oath of the Moon, which is a breaking point towards flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T13:52:24-07:00","id":483845,"title":"","content":"Can Uratha suffer the Madness Condition (pg. 309) even though they don't have an Integrity score?<br /> <br /> If so, is it just 10 - Resolve + Composure for the Madness penalty or how does one calculate or resolve this condition for Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T07:10:40-07:00","id":484521,"title":"","content":"How good are the sales from Werewolf 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5646-draven023","name":"Draven023","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T08:01:47-07:00","id":484567,"title":"","content":"They never show numbers for that sort of thing, but it's been in the top 'Hottest Titles' on DriveThruRPG since it came out,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:03:50-07:00","id":484627,"title":"","content":"Got platinum (whatever that means) already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T10:40:50-07:00","id":484736,"title":"","content":"Searching found me <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?669946-Puzzled-At-Drivethru-Economics&amp;p=16285014#post16285014\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a>, which may be out of date or just incorrect, and even if it's right doesn't exactly narrow it down. Essentially it says Platinum is over 1001 purchases.<br /> <br /> I expect we'll get a new round of purchases once the hardcover version is available, too, putting Werewolf 2e back in first for 'Hottest Titles.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T18:38:09-07:00","id":484989,"title":"","content":"A high Powerstat brings certain titles and advanced powers to supernatural beings. Powerful vampires are called Elders and powerful magi are Arch-magi. The former can use Elder Devotions and the latter can use Imperial Practices. But what is a werewolf with high Primal Urge called, and what are the possible names of his advanced powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T19:04:31-07:00","id":484998,"title":"","content":"Nothing at the moment. First Edition had 2 fully statted Elder Werewolves, and they could definitely fuck you and your whole pack. However, they didn't have any unique traits like the Elder Vampires get due to the blood mutating.<br /> <br /> First Edition also had Milestone Gifts...which would be somewhat weird at the moment due to the mechanics being different. My current idea is to work a system like Ciphers from Demon. Basically, if you buy all 5 Facets of a Gift you unlock the potential to learn the True Gift of Death/Dominance/Strength/Etc. Have to find a sufficiently powerful spirit and bargain for it. Probably a Rank 6 critter. Seeing how the Shadow Gifts all average out to 3 Dot powers I figure the True Gifts averaging out to 5 dot powers would fit the bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T19:41:46-07:00","id":485024,"title":"","content":"I guess some terms would be cool, though.<br /> <br /> I'm going to put my vote against Milestoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T22:35:06-07:00","id":485125,"title":"","content":"I thought a high PU werewolf was called a <i>Bodhisattva. </i>Currently, there are no Milestone Gifts or other <i>Bodhisattva</i>-only powers. Then again, there are no Elder Disciplines in 2e either, and while there are Devotions designed for Elders, they could technically be taken by any vampire with enough experience (though they'd be pretty hard for low-BP vampires to use). No word yet on Imperial Practices in Mage 2e as far as I'm aware, though I've not been following its development closely, so I may have missed them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T23:01:45-07:00","id":485143,"title":"","content":"I thought that was more of a term for what they're like. It's certainly unwieldy for a title, and might not be fitting for most regions of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Just for clarity's sake, I'd like to point out that an Archmage is not just a high Power Stat mage, but a sort of extra splat Mages can turn into. As rare as they are Power Stat 8, 9 or 10 mages aren't necessarily archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T00:37:51-07:00","id":485203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=483845#post483845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Uratha suffer the Madness Condition (pg. 309) even though they don't have an Integrity score?<br /> <br /> If so, is it just 10 - Resolve + Composure for the Madness penalty or how does one calculate or resolve this condition for Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> WWs are immune to the Madness condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T06:12:11-07:00","id":485377,"title":"","content":"Unless an idigam rips their soul out and sticks a new one in. That'll do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member