rsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=502128#post502128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much a contradiction as a simplification. Werewolves <i>do </i>come from wolfblooded. Mostly. And often those &quot;normal humans&quot; have a werewolf a couple of steps down the family tree somewhere. Most humans do if you go back far enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's a simple matter of <i>nuzusul</i> experiencing supernatural weirdness in the leadup to their Change, like, heightened spiritual activity around them, seeing things to do with the supernatural world, having weird fleeting transformations that make them doubt their own sanity\u2026<br /> <br /> Well goodness gracious, I just described a handful of Tells that might manifest on a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">~ * c o n s o l i d a t i o n * ~</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:53:46-07:00","id":502198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=502180#post502180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then there's a simple matter of <i>nuzusul</i> experiencing supernatural weirdness in the leadup to their Change, like, heightened spiritual activity around them, seeing things to do with the supernatural world, having weird fleeting transformations that make them doubt their own sanity\u2026<br /> <br /> Well goodness gracious, I just described a handful of Tells that might manifest on a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">~ * c o n s o l i d a t i o n * ~</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's kind of how I figured it usually went - even if a Werewolf wasn't Wolf-Blooded all their lives, they must have at least been for a breif period before their First Change. But evidently I was mistaken. That's cool, I'm glad I know now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:55:08-07:00","id":523208,"title":"","content":"The experience costs for Gifts are confusing to me.<br /> <br /> If I buy a dot of Renown then I get a free Gift facet? All facets of an affinity Gift cost 2xp except the first facet which costs 3xp but it's all moot if I gain them through Renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:59:52-07:00","id":523248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523208#post523208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The experience costs for Gifts are confusing to me.<br /> <br /> If I buy a dot of Renown then I get a free Gift facet? All facets of an affinity Gift cost 2xp except the first facet which costs 3xp but it's all moot if I gain them through Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>So:<br /> Buy a dot of Renown for 3 xp: Get a free Facet in any of your unlocked Gifts for that Renown. If you already have all your available Facets for that Renown, bank the free Facet until you unlock a new Gift.<br /> Unlock a new Gift for 3 xp (if favoured) or 5 xp (if otherwise): Get a free Facet in the newly unlocked Gift. Must have at leats one dot in the Renown of the Facet that you pick.<br /> Buy a Facet for 2xp: Gets a Facet of your choice in any of your unlocked Gifts, albeit you must have at least one dot in the Renown of the Facet you pick.<br /> <br /> Does that help?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:26:04-07:00","id":523268,"title":"","content":"If you want a facet form a gift you don't have any facets from, you need to unlock the gift by having it taught to you by a spirit which costs either 3 or 5 xp depending on whether it's affinity or not. Once that has been done you can buy the other four whenever you want for 2 xp each, provided you have at least one dot of renown in the corresponding category, <i>or</i> get one of them for free whenever you buy a dot of said renown. Wolf gifts are automatically open and facets can be bought for 1 xp whenever you like, or got for free with renown.<br /> <br /> You can't use your free facets on non-wolf gifts you haven't unlocked by buying the first facet at full price. And remember you need to do something fairly significant to justify getting more renown anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:30:26-07:00","id":523278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523248#post523248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So:<br /> Buy a dot of Renown for 3 xp: Get a free Facet in any of your unlocked Gifts for that Renown. If you already have all your available Facets for that Renown, bank the free Facet until you unlock a new Gift.<br /> Unlock a new Gift for 3 xp (if favoured) or 5 xp (if otherwise): Get a free Facet in the newly unlocked Gift. Must have at leats one dot in the Renown of the Facet that you pick.<br /> Buy a Facet for 2xp: Gets a Facet of your choice in any of your unlocked Gifts, albeit you must have at least one dot in the Renown of the Facet you pick.<br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also note that Wolf Gift Facets cost 1xp instead of 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:02:47-07:00","id":523434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523248#post523248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buy a Facet for 2xp: Gets a Facet of your choice in any of your unlocked Gifts, albeit you must have at least one dot in the Renown of the Facet you pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf Gifts are 1xp to unlock, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:04:47-07:00","id":523435,"title":"","content":"Wolf Facets are 1xp; all Wolf Gifts are automatically unlocked for werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:51:20-07:00","id":523481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523435#post523435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf Facets are 1xp; all Wolf Gifts are automatically unlocked for werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:05:28-07:00","id":523492,"title":"","content":"At some point I'm sure we'll get used to calling the individual powers facets and not gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:11:30-07:00","id":523497,"title":"","content":"While the cost of breaking open new gifts is killing me, I think it's a nice way to stall progression in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:15:14-07:00","id":523654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523497#post523497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the cost of breaking open new gifts is killing me, I think it's a nice way to stall progression in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you consider the cost of the &quot;free&quot; facet you get with a gift purchase, it's effectively only 3xp for the gift itself. 1 if it's Affinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:59:07-07:00","id":523694,"title":"","content":"Yeah but 5 Experience is 5-6 really good sessions. It's worth it, just takes a while to get there. Or alternatively you could get your Primal Urge up, which may be important in a more combat-heavy game unless you want to pop in and out of gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:46:04-07:00","id":523721,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's definitely a significant investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T17:45:48-07:00","id":523817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523248#post523248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So:<br /> Buy a dot of Renown for 3 xp: Get a free Facet in any of your unlocked Gifts for that Renown. If you already have all your available Facets for that Renown, bank the free Facet until you unlock a new Gift.<br /> Unlock a new Gift for 3 xp (if favoured) or 5 xp (if otherwise): Get a free Facet in the newly unlocked Gift. Must have at leats one dot in the Renown of the Facet that you pick.<br /> Buy a Facet for 2xp: Gets a Facet of your choice in any of your unlocked Gifts, albeit you must have at least one dot in the Renown of the Facet you pick.<br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you. I know I've asked this on a thread previously but now just to clarify, how many Gifts does a starting character begin with exactly? Three or four?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T19:46:23-07:00","id":523860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=523817#post523817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, thank you. I know I've asked this on a thread previously but now just to clarify, how many Gifts does a starting character begin with exactly? Three or four?</div> </div> </div> </div>Four Facets in total. The first dot of your Moon Gift, two Shadow Facets chosen from your affinity Gifts, and either the second dot of your Moon Gift, or a Wolf Facet, depending on if you start with one or two dots in your Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves only start with three Facets. The first dot of their Moon Gift, one Shadow Facet chosen from their Affinity gifts, and one Wolf Facet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:16:56-07:00","id":524167,"title":"","content":"Great, thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:58:11-07:00","id":526371,"title":"","content":"So some of the forms retain their Defense versus Firearms.<br /> <br /> Does this count against the Blast Numina?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing no, but since my character is currently being slaughtered I feel obliged to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T22:17:47-07:00","id":526394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=526371#post526371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So some of the forms retain their Defense versus Firearms.<br /> <br /> Does this count against the Blast Numina?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing no, but since my character is currently being slaughtered I feel obliged to ask.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you have to ask your ST about it. I personally would say &quot;sometimes&quot;. Honestly, most of the time I give people defence against Blast, because I want to show off what kind of cool blasts the odd creatures have, and if you can see it, you can defend against it. (If you are good.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T22:53:38-07:00","id":526417,"title":"","content":"I'd say no. Blast just states that if the activation roll is successful, it wounds as a +0 Firearm. It's not even an &quot;attack&quot; as defined by the combat rules, it just straight up causes damage. At least, that's my interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T22:56:18-07:00","id":526418,"title":"","content":"Yeah that seems right, Charlaquin, though I like Seidmadr's ideas for 'sometimes.' The Shadow's my favorite part of the setting in World of Darkness but I never get to run Werewolf so I don't usually bother with the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T05:00:05-07:00","id":526540,"title":"","content":"Wow, am I the only one who just immediately took it as read that defence against firearms <i>would </i>count? <br /> <br /> I mean, it's called <i>blast.</i> That to me suggests an ephemeral projectile of some sort. It might even take the appearance of an actual gun on some spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Joi