follow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I really like the Sagrim-Ur stories too, and Hikaon-Ur in general because I love the Hunters In Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two being mutually-respectful sibs has always been a refreshing thing for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T22:09:45-07:00","id":531735,"title":"","content":"Sangrim-Ur. I've always had a weakness for trickster types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T22:48:40-07:00","id":531745,"title":"","content":"Kamduis-Ur, with Sagrim a close second. What can I say? I like curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T01:47:23-07:00","id":531794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=531597#post531597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At what primal urge # does a werewolf stop aging? 7, 8, 9, 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is undefined at this time as to exactly how a werewolf's aging slows at higher Primal Urges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T01:54:32-07:00","id":531797,"title":"","content":"Are there any Lodges or bits of Forsaken lore tied to Egypt at all?<br /> <br /> I'm on an idiotic mission to make my obsession with Kemetic stuff blatant across every single nWoD line, but WtF is giving me trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T02:01:35-07:00","id":531798,"title":"","content":"If I had to pick, I would say it was the point where they become more spirit than man, ie the point where they can only subsist on essence. So 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T02:44:20-07:00","id":531815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=531797#post531797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any Lodges or bits of Forsaken lore tied to Egypt at all?<br /> <br /> I'm on an idiotic mission to make my obsession with Kemetic stuff blatant across every single nWoD line, but WtF is giving me trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a suspicion the answer to this is yes, but I can't remember the specific Lodge. I think it's tied into a linked history with the Ascending Ones and the Cult of the Phoenix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T05:26:06-07:00","id":531874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=531644#post531644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know who that is!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ninth Firstborn, theoretically. In the opening fiction of one of the books, it comes to help one of its tribe with a Harmony problem, then warns her that one of the enemies she thought she defeated, isn't defeated <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=531797#post531797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any Lodges or bits of Forsaken lore tied to Egypt at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of the Lost prepared for the battle with the Great Darkness, theorized to be Apep. And won. Also the Lodge of the Red Sands, which can be placed in any desert area, started in Egypt. Acrozatarim might be referring to the Lodge of Night, which has an origin in Thebes and follow Khonsu as their patron, and act as night hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:02:01-07:00","id":532645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=531794#post531794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it is undefined at this time as to exactly how a werewolf's aging slows at higher Primal Urges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just curious. Will there be a future supplement book focusing on high PU werewolves or any ideas for one? I'm planning on making a game of immortals. I'm waiting until Dark Ages comes out and make a chronicle using a distant past and modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:50:31-07:00","id":532693,"title":"","content":"I think everyone would like to see structure for 'high power' games. I'd certainly love to see some expansion on Werewolves above Primal Urge 5.<br /> <br /> So, you know, pretty please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-29-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:10:20-07:00","id":532708,"title":"","content":"There's a book about Elders in the work for Requiem 2e if I recall, so there is <i>some</i> precedence for that sort of thing. Though there are a lot of topics I'd rather see expanded first in new books for Forsaken 2e, like the Tribes (Forsaken, Pure, and the Bale Hounds) and the Prey, and I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who feels that way.<br /> <br /> It'd be cool, but yeah. Maybe there'll be some of that in The Pack. Maybe it'll be a mostly secondary section in another supplement. I don't see a full book being dedicated to it, or at least not a regular sized one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:11:57-07:00","id":532710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=532708#post532708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a book about Elders in the work for Requiem 2e if I recall</div> </div> </div> </div>A Thousand Years of Night. Great name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it'll be a mostly secondary section in another supplement. </div> </div> </div>But it seems like there would be a lot more than you'd fit into just a chapter. At that point, you truly have a wolf in sheep's clothing. The werewolf doesn't even eat real food. It eats essence. A maximum primal urge werewolf is a thing that can go into Kuruth for 12 hours, full healing every turn, gifts turning on automatically, dodging bullets and driving people mad as it seeks to do nothing more than destroy for half a day.<br /> <br /> You could have a chapter alone on the legends of the bodhisattva wolves, building up setting, before even getting into how different they'd be. Would they have humans and wolf-blooded in their packs, when they can't go without a sacred hunt for more than three days? What kind of things would a pack of high primal urge werewolves want to hunt? Because it would be something big.<br /> <br /> And that's just the Forsaken. What is a Primal Urge 10 Predator King or Fire-Touched like? A Bale Hound? A whole pack of them? Werewolf's had a lot of legends about big bad wolves and even a lot of hints about things that happen when you get 'up there' in power, but they've rarely been explored. When they do it shouldn't be just as just a chapter in another book. Stew and the others seem eager to give the setting the respect and treatment it deserves so I'm sure if it gets made it'll get made right.<br /> <br /> Certainly a smaller book could do it. I suppose it depends on the success of second edition.<br /> <br /> Also oh my god can someone fix the typo in the topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-30-2015, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:07:39-07:00","id":532733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=532708#post532708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a book about Elders in the work for Requiem 2e if I recall, so there is <i>some</i> precedence for that sort of thing. Though there are a lot of topics I'd rather see expanded first in new books for Forsaken 2e, like the Tribes (Forsaken, Pure, and the Bale Hounds) and the Prey, and I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who feels that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want a book that goes into more detail on the Pure. I want to see their unique Gifts updated to 2e, and I <i>really</i> want to see unique Siskur-Dah benefits for when the rite is performed by a ritemaster of each of the Pure Tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=532710#post532710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also oh my god can someone fix the typo in the topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... Didn't even notice that until you pointed it out. Fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:10:26-07:00","id":532735,"title":"","content":"A thousand thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:28:04-07:00","id":533168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=532710#post532710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it seems like there would be a lot more than you'd fit into just a chapter. At that point, you truly have a wolf in sheep's clothing. The werewolf doesn't even eat real food. It eats essence. A maximum primal urge werewolf is a thing that can go into Kuruth for 12 hours, full healing every turn, gifts turning on automatically, dodging bullets and driving people mad as it seeks to do nothing more than destroy for half a day.<br /> <br /> You could have a chapter alone on the legends of the bodhisattva wolves, building up setting, before even getting into how different they'd be. Would they have humans and wolf-blooded in their packs, when they can't go without a sacred hunt for more than three days? What kind of things would a pack of high primal urge werewolves want to hunt? Because it would be something big.<br /> <br /> And that's just the Forsaken. What is a Primal Urge 10 Predator King or Fire-Touched like? A Bale Hound? A whole pack of them? Werewolf's had a lot of legends about big bad wolves and even a lot of hints about things that happen when you get 'up there' in power, but they've rarely been explored. When they do it shouldn't be just as just a chapter in another book. Stew and the others seem eager to give the setting the respect and treatment it deserves so I'm sure if it gets made it'll get made right.<br /> <br /> Certainly a smaller book could do it. I suppose it depends on the success of second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it'd be pretty cool! I'd certainly welcome a chapter in some book entirely focusing on the topic, or a small book in the vein of Lore Of The Deceived.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Elders in Requiem are significantly more important to the setting as a whole than high-Primal Urge or ancient werewolves are in Forsaken. We've discussed the topic of those legendary predators in the forums before. A problem there is with them is that they're, by comparison, far more exceptional cases than Elders, who tend to be the movers and shakers of vampire politics and the driving force of their conflicts behind the masquerade. They're very integral pieces of Kindred society status quo on a widespread basis. Those mighty werewolves by contrast seem rarer, definitely less subtle in the impact of their presence, and probably matter less to the horror on a more personal scale and the misadventures of the 'average pack'.<br /> <br /> In my opinion anyways. Which is why I don't think we're very likely to see the writing for 2e explore them anytime soon, as much as I'd receive it with a grin otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-30-2015, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T02:34:05-07:00","id":534149,"title":"","content":"Question regarding Tracking, Perception, and two Facets.<br /> <br /> The two Facets are in the Gift of Hunting, Honed Senses (Cunning) and Impossible Spoor (Wisdom).<br /> <br /> Is Tracking (and its subsystem) a Perception roll? As in, do you get benefits for Perception on your Tracking rolls, like Honed Senses ( and the Trained Observer merit)?<br /> <br /> This would mean the Uratha in question (with both Facets)- who is Tracking Spoor- would only need a single success to get three successes, and qualify for an exceptional success; meaning he would get a Condition for the exceptional success, and a beat on top of that if he was on Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> This all feels right, but I wanted to see if I was missing something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2377-wyrm-sage","name":"Wyrm Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T03:29:57-07:00","id":534197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=533168#post533168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, Elders in Requiem are significantly more important to the setting as a whole than high-Primal Urge or ancient werewolves are in Forsaken. We've discussed the topic of those legendary predators in the forums before. A problem there is with them is that they're, by comparison, far more exceptional cases than Elders, who tend to be the movers and shakers of vampire politics and the driving force of their conflicts behind the masquerade. They're very integral pieces of Kindred society status quo on a widespread basis. Those mighty werewolves by contrast seem rarer, definitely less subtle in the impact of their presence, and probably matter less to the horror on a more personal scale and the misadventures of the 'average pack'.<br /> <br /> In my opinion anyways. Which is why I don't think we're very likely to see the writing for 2e explore them anytime soon, as much as I'd receive it with a grin otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a book on Archmasters, a book on how Changelings can become Gentry, and now a book on Elders. Why -wouldn't- this be coming out?<br /> <br /> Also, as has been noted, the tribes aren't just isolated to one geographic area. They're a worldwide organization. While it might be easy to say that Death Wolf or Red Wolf or whatever is pulling the strings, the Firstborn can't interact with the world. They need intermediaries too, and sometimes a Royal Avatar isn't a good fit for what they need. Someone has to pull the strings, lead by example, etc. The Firstborn can't do it all the time.<br /> <br /> So why -wouldn't- the high PU wolves be this person? They're old, they're powerful, and they probably got that way by being exemplars of heir practice. The fact that the same basic ideas found in Rwanda are found in Colorado is just another reason that these things have to be at least moderately overseen by a central authority. Look at the Catholic Church, for an example. Werewolves might not like to admit it, and might be focused on the Pack, but Tribes are important too. And those werewolves would be perfect to lead them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:04:24-07:00","id":534211,"title":"","content":"You should give a little more attention to the full context of my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=533168#post533168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I don't think we're very likely to see the writing for 2e explore them <b>anytime soon</b>, as much as I'd receive it with a grin otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is probably not going to happen soon&quot; is different from &quot;this will never happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> @Wyrm Sage: I believe Tracking does not count as a Perception roll for the purpose of the Honed Senses effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-31-2015, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T06:31:39-07:00","id":534273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyrm Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534149#post534149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding Tracking, Perception, and two Facets.<br /> <br /> The two Facets are in the Gift of Hunting, Honed Senses (Cunning) and Impossible Spoor (Wisdom).<br /> <br /> Is Tracking (and its subsystem) a Perception roll? As in, do you get benefits for Perception on your Tracking rolls, like Honed Senses ( and the Trained Observer merit)?<br /> <br /> This would mean the Uratha in question (with both Facets)- who is Tracking Spoor- would only need a single success to get three successes, and qualify for an exceptional success; meaning he would get a Condition for the exceptional success, and a beat on top of that if he was on Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> This all feels right, but I wanted to see if I was missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Tracking isn't Perception. (IMO) Perception (Wits + Composure) is noticing things without really thinking about it, taking in everything around you and seeing what stands out. Tracking (Wits + Skill) is deliberately searching for some spoor known to be related to the prey, then following that and finding the next spoor, and the next, etc.<br /> <br /> As designed, Honed Senses is the Facet for Perception, and Impossible Spoor is the Facet for Tracking.<br /> <br /> That said, werewolves are supposed to be utterly terrifying and implacable hunters, so if you want your Tracking/Perception focused characters to easily pursue quarry no matter how hard they hide, go ahead and do it.<br /> <br /> Just remember, your enemies can do the exact same thing back to you and everyone in your pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:20:57-07:00","id":534334,"title":"","content":"I was wondering, can a Glade be intentionally created through manipulation of the resonance of the Hisil? Perhaps through a powerful enough locus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:19:50-07:00","id":534476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534273#post534273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, Tracking isn't Perception. (IMO) Perception (Wits + Composure) is noticing things without really thinking about it, taking in everything around you and seeing what stands out. Tracking (Wits + Skill) is deliberately searching for some spoor known to be related to the prey, then following that and finding the next spoor, and the next, etc.<br /> <br /> As designed, Honed Senses is the Facet for Perception, and Impossible Spoor is the Facet for Tracking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Look at the wording of Trained Observer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character has spent years in the field, catch-<br /> ing tiny details and digging for secrets. She might not have a better chance of finding things, but she has a better chance of finding important things. Any time you make a Perception roll (<b>usually</b> Wits + Composure), you benefit from the 9-again quality. With the three-dot version, you get 8-again. </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Wits + Composure is a good go-to roll for perception-based actions, but as this wording clearly implies, it is not the only dice pool that can be used. Perception is not used like a keyword with a specific rules meaning, it's used like an English language word. Investigating a crime scene is Wits + Investigation, but still utilizes the character's powers of observation and in my opinion, Trained Observer should clearly apply. Likewise, tracking is very clearly perception-based, even though it doesn't use Wits + Composure as a dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:39:03-07:00","id":534495,"title":"","content":"Tracking is not a Perception roll. Honed Senses does not work on it. Impossible Spoor does.<br /> <br /> (Disclosure: I wrote Honed Senses; Bunyip wrote Impossible Spoor; if I remember correctly Bunyip also wrote the new tracking rules)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T10:35:37-07:00","id":534584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534476#post534476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine. Wits + Composure is a good go-to roll for perception-based actions, but as this wording clearly implies, it is not the only dice pool that can be used. Perception is not used like a keyword with a specific rules meaning, it's used like an English language word. Investigating a crime scene is Wits + Investigation, but still utilizes the character's powers of observation and in my opinion, Trained Observer should clearly apply. Likewise, tracking is very clearly perception-based, even though it doesn't use Wits + Composure as a dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Perception roll is a specific category of roll in the system, not any Wits + Trait roll that involves the use of the senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:22:38-07:00","id":534630,"title":"","content":"First edition said otherwise, for what is worth:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GillSans\">Skill-Based Perception<br /> During the course of play, you will be called upon frequently to roll dice to see if your character notices something in her vicinity, or that some detail is unusual. The Storyteller can always ask you to roll Wits + Composure to see if your character is aware of her surroundings, but there are other options. Perhaps more indicative of your character\u2019s life experience and training is combining Wits + a relevant Skill to determine if your character spots something amiss. It could be Wits + Survival to realize that a predatory animal lurks nearby in the woods. Or it might be Wits + Academics to notice that the books on a shelf aren\u2019t arranged alphabetically, but by date of publication. Sure, Wits + Composure might accomplish the same result, but if your character has some capability with a Skill that\u2019s more reliable than her Composure alone, the Storyteller might allow you to roll Wits plus that Skill, instead. As a general rule of thumb, the highest of Composure or the Skill is rolled along with Wits. While the stalked character in the example above might be a novice woodsman (Survival 1), he could still have decent Composure (say, 3). The latter of the two is rolled because the character\u2019s inherent senses and alertness compensate for his green status in the wilds. Bear in mind that dots in some Skills or under some circumstances simply don\u2019t matter, and Wits + Composure always applies. For example, if a gun lies in the corner of a room, having the Firearms Skill doesn\u2019t help spot it. Anyone who gets a successful Wits + Composure can see it. The Storyteller always has final say on whether a Skill can be combined with Wits to make a perception roll, or if Composure applies</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:37:11-07:00","id":534649,"title":"","content":"I have several questions.<br /> <br /> Does the bonus to &quot;perception-based rolls&quot; from Wolf Senses apply to tracking? Does it apply to rolls made to recognize other werewolves and wolf-blooded by scent? If a &quot;Perception Roll&quot; is a codified thing in the rules, why does it not appear in the common actions section? Why does Trained Observer say that &quot;Perception Rolls&quot; are <i>usually</i> Wits + Composure? <br /> <br /> I can understand that it was not the writer's intent for Honed Senses to work with Tracking rolls, but as far as I can tell, the Second Edition rules don't seem to include &quot;Perception Roll&quot; as a thing. The nearest I can find is the Attribute Tasks section, which says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some actions require no special expertise to perform. Mostly, these come in the form of Wits + Composure rolls to notice something that doesn\u2019t seem right, or using Strength + Stamina to lift something. In these rolls, you add two differ- ent Attributes together to make your dice pool. If an action doesn\u2019t seem to involve any particular Skill, it can be handled by an Attribute Task. </div> </div> </div>By my reading, a Wits + Composure roll would be an Attribute Task used to resolve an action that involved perception and did not require training in a particular Skill. If that's what Wolf Senses, Honed Senses, and Trained Observer are meant to apply to, it is not expressed very clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T12:17:05-07:00","id":534697,"title":"","content":"Wolf senses are mentioned to work in contested tracking. There's no mention of them working for <i>un</i>contested tracking but I'm just going to assume they do because otherwise that would be dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:38:26-07:00","id":534781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534495#post534495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tracking is not a Perception roll. Honed Senses does not work on it. Impossible Spoor does.<br /> <br /> (Disclosure: I wrote Honed Senses; Bunyip wrote Impossible Spoor; if I remember correctly Bunyip also wrote the new tracking rules)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Tracking and Imposible Spoor were designed to be separate from Perception rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:13:21-07:00","id":534803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534781#post534781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Tracking and Imposible Spoor were designed to be separate from Perception rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so I take it Tracking as a separate subsystem doesn't count as a Perception roll. Thank you for clarifying that. Do you know if using Wolf Senses to identify characters and to recognize werewolves and Wolf-Blooded as such by scent is meant to be considered Perception or not? Also, does the form-based dice bonus to Wolf Senses only apply to Perception rolls, or can it be added to Tracking rolls as well? It's written as &quot;perception-based rolls&quot; with a lower-case p, so I assume it can, but then the Contested Tracking rules specifically mention that you can add the bonus from your form, and the Resisted Tracking rolls don't, so I figured I should double-check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-31-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:31:04-07:00","id":538525,"title":"","content":"So, in the forms section, it mentions that in the wolf headed forms you can both damage and grapple with a bite. Does this mean you need to pick one when you make the move, or can you resolve it like a damaging attack and then go &quot;right, I'm grappling now&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:42:38-07:00","id":538535,"title":"","content":"With a Fetish activation role, can you make the role and if that fails, then spend a point of Essence to activate it anyway? I'm assuming no from the sentence, but a friend is planning to run a game of WtF2 and asked if I could double check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:19:55-07:00","id":538577,"title":"","content":"I'm presuming you mean without wasting an action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:29:08-07:00","id":538609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=538525#post538525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the forms section, it mentions that in the wolf headed forms you can both damage and grapple with a bite. Does this mean you need to pick one when you make the move, or can you resolve it like a damaging attack and then go &amp;quot;right, I'm grappling now&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It says they can establish a grapple in addition to causing damage. I assume that means if you hit with a bite attack in Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan (or with a claw attack in Gauru), you can establish a grapple and do damage with the same attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:32:54-07:00","id":538612,"title":"","content":"Yep, the potential St was wondering if you can do both in the same action, test and then spend. My gut says no, my reading says no, but hey, he's new <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:22:07-07:00","id":538708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=538609#post538609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says they can establish a grapple in addition to causing damage. I assume that means if you hit with a bite attack in Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan (or with a claw attack in Gauru), you can establish a grapple and do damage with the same attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's how it works in RL, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:27:42-07:00","id":538717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=538612#post538612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the potential St was wondering if you can do both in the same action, test and then spend. My gut says no, my reading says no, but hey, he's new <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is not spending Essence a Reflexive Action? If so, yes you can. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:54:06-07:00","id":538766,"title":"","content":"The section I'm querying is. &quot;Using a fetish normally requires the Uratha to succeed at a Resolve + Composure roll penalized by the fetish\u2019s dot rating. This attempt to will the bound spirit into action can be circumvented by spending a point of Essence instead.&quot; The way its worded sounds like a choice of making the roll or spending the Essence. However, I'm not certain, so I'll go with the wisdom of the forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:04:03-07:00","id":538774,"title":"","content":"Yes. You can roll to make it work, or spend an Essence to make it work. I'd allow you to spend an Essence if you failed to guarantee activation without having to wait for your next turn for it. I don't know if the rules clarify this, in which case it might just be up to the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:20:37-07:00","id":542485,"title":"","content":"Do PRIMARY Wolf-Blooded characters get 10 Merit-Points (as per Making a Monster), 7 (by virtue of being mortal WoD-Charakters) or 5 (like SECONDARY Wolf-Blooded characters)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6226-rulandor","name":"Rulandor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:55:28-07:00","id":542530,"title":"","content":"I'd say 10. It says to build them like you would a werewolf, with the exception of the noted alterations. Said alterations make no mention of merit dot number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:39:02-07:00","id":542609,"title":"","content":"I think mortal characters only got 5 merit points to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:45:36-07:00","id":542614,"title":"","content":"They're supposed to be able to keep up with werewolf characters though. It wouldn't be fair to deny them merit dots for no reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:05:20-07:00","id":542633,"title":"","content":"Ephsy, 5 merit dots is for the wolf-blooded in the pack creation rules where it uses a simpler version of character creation to make a weaker character. The 2e character creation rules don't reduce the merit dots you get, so it is still 7 merit dots for mortals and I think minor templates like ghouls, sleepwalkers and wolf-blooded. For a game where its a mix of full-template and 'minor' template characters (like vampires with ghouls, mages with sleepwalkers, uratha with wolf-blooded etc) I'd give all the PCs 10 merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5839-toganamede","name":"Toganamede","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:31:47-07:00","id":543376,"title":"","content":"Technically mortal-based PCs get 7 merit dots, but the devs have said they don't really see a problem with them getting 10 (I do 10 in my games; there's just so many merits anyway). The 5 is for minor NPC characters created as part of the back for background or troupe play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:51:05-07:00","id":554349,"title":"","content":"Wolf senses.<br /> <br /> You remove penalties for sensory deprivation such as blindness. However wolf sight only halves penalties from darkness. Why is it that you can perceive better while blind rather than while in dim lighting; or was this an issue already errata'd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6454-maxkojote","name":"MaxKojote","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:13:20-07:00","id":554391,"title":"","content":"It removes penalties for fighting someone because you can smell and hear them. It halves the penalties for <i>actually seeing stuff with your eyes.</i><br /> <br /> Say you were blinded, you could navigate around a room ok with your other senses, but if you needed to read a sign then you're shit out of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-14-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:39:56-07:00","id":555470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=534781#post534781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Tracking and Imposible Spoor were designed to be separate from Perception rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand that you are a writer, this is illogical. The process of tracking with the Survival skill (as opposed to say, Computers) is massively reliant upon the information gained from sensory perception. The only way this might not be the case is if each tracking roll required Wits + Composure to gain perception information prior to a Wits + Survival to make deductions based on that information.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:51:49-07:00","id":555472,"title":"","content":"Perception is different from perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:49:45-07:00","id":555855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=555472#post555472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perception is different from perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not according to the flavor text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:29:27-07:00","id":555911,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you have the official answer, straight from the person who wrote the rules for tracking. Tracking /= Perception. You don't have to agree with that answer, you don't have to run it that way in your games. But that's how the person who wrote it intended it to work, telling him it doesn't make sense or it doesn't agree with the flavor text (that he also presumably wrote) won't get you anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:49:48-07:00","id":555923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=555911#post555911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, you have the official answer, straight from the person who wrote the rules for tracking. Tracking /= Perception. You don't have to agree with that answer, you don't have to run it that way in your games. But that's how the person who wrote it intended it to work, telling him it doesn't make sense or it doesn't agree with the flavor text (that he also presumably wrote) won't get you anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does! If someone comes into the thread and sees several people supporting the idea, they might be more inclined to continue running it that way. Writers are human, and there is always room for improvement! It certainly makes for a more interesting setting (in my opinion) if Werewolves are exceptionally good at hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:06:35-07:00","id":556047,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are already exceptionally good at hunting. I've already said earlier in the thread that if you want the two systems to combine more than intended, you can choose to do that in your individual game, but it's not the rules as written, or intended. It's still fine to do as a house rule.<br /> <br /> You should also be aware that doing so makes everything you care about vulnerable to being found and destroyed. Nothing you do can protect them from the Predator Kings you've pissed off, or the Fire-Touched who want to kidnap all your wolf-blooded and maim every human you've ever talked to.<br /> <br /> The good news is that you'll know who ruined your life and pack, because you can track them in return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:50:17-07:00","id":556099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556047#post556047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are already exceptionally good at hunting. I've already said earlier in the thread that if you want the two systems to combine more than intended, you can choose to do that in your individual game, but it's not the rules as written, or intended. It's still fine to do as a house rule.<br /> <br /> You should also be aware that doing so makes everything you care about vulnerable to being found and destroyed. Nothing you do can protect them from the Predator Kings you've pissed off, or the Fire-Touched who want to kidnap all your wolf-blooded and maim every human you've ever talked to.<br /> <br /> The good news is that you'll know who ruined your life and pack, because you can track them in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only was I really surprised to discover that you did not intend for them to stack, but I checked with my players and the players of <i>four other different gaming groups</i> and every single one of them assumed they stacked.<br /> <br /> All of us have been operating under the assumption that it was a normal and important part of Werewolf society that everything they care about is vulnerable to being found and destroyed. Yes, the Predator Kings can eventually hunt and corner you if you push them too far, and the Fire-Touched can track down every single wolf-blooded and human that you've spoken to. That was one of the biggest driving reasons why political alliances are so incredibly important, why you need to set up ruses and clever tricks, and why you maintain a precarious balance of skirmishes and posturing with the Pure to prevent outright MAD on both sides.<br /> <br /> You can have many of those things without Werewolves being such exceptional trackers, but after considering it for a while?<br /> The setting is more interesting this way. The Wolf Must Hunt, and finding you is what Werewolves are absolutely the best at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 06-15-2015, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:53:54-07:00","id":556102,"title":"","content":"I don't think this got answered earlier, does the form-based perception bonus apply to resisted tracking? It doesn't say so, but it does apply to contested tracking so it seemed odd to me it would apply to one but not the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:07:27-07:00","id":556689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556102#post556102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this got answered earlier, does the form-based perception bonus apply to resisted tracking? It doesn't say so, but it does apply to contested tracking so it seemed odd to me it would apply to one but not the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean uncontested Tracking (rather than resisted)? I assume so.<br /> <br /> Form-based perception bonuses specifically *do not* apply to uncontested Tracking. This is because uncontested tracking is more abstract and assumes the Uratha switches forms as needed to blend in across however long it takes to track the prey. They add their Primal Urge bonus to this roll. <br /> <br /> Contested tracking more closely follows the Uratha's form changes - the werewolf might use Urhan in back alleys for one roll, but more prudently take Hishu for the next roll on a crowded street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:41:17-07:00","id":556711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556099#post556099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only was I really surprised to discover that you did not intend for them to stack, but I checked with my players and the players of <i>four other different gaming groups</i> and every single one of them assumed they stacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, they don't. Perception is a *Reflexive* Wits + Composure roll, Tracking is either an *Instant* Wits + Skill roll or *Extended/Contested* Wits + Skill roll. They're not the same, they have some overlapping modifiers, but their Gifts and Facets are separate. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are incredibly trackers, but they're not meant to be able to combine incompatible Facets to achieve Exceptional Success from rolling just one success on a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:12:29-07:00","id":556806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556711#post556711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, they don't. Perception is a *Reflexive* Wits + Composure roll, Tracking is either an *Instant* Wits + Skill roll or *Extended/Contested* Wits + Skill roll. They're not the same, they have some overlapping modifiers, but their Gifts and Facets are separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned before, tracking with Survival is massively reliant upon the information you gain from your senses. It simply makes no sense for your extraordinary capabilities of perception to fail the moment you attempt to track someone. This is not just limited to Honed Senses, but is inclusive of things like Trained Observer as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556711#post556711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are incredible trackers, but they're not meant to be able to combine incompatible Facets to achieve Exceptional Success from rolling just one success on a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works fine for everybody I know, so it is far from incompatible.<br /> It also informs the setting in really interesting ways, so I heartily recommend anyone to keep running it this way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:02:27-07:00","id":556956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=556689#post556689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean uncontested Tracking (rather than resisted)? I assume so.<br /> <br /> Form-based perception bonuses specifically *do not* apply to uncontested Tracking. This is because uncontested tracking is more abstract and assumes the Uratha switches forms as needed to blend in across however long it takes to track the prey. They add their Primal Urge bonus to this roll. <br /> <br /> Contested tracking more closely follows the Uratha's form changes - the werewolf might use Urhan in back alleys for one roll, but more prudently take Hishu for the next roll on a crowded street.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant uncontested. Thank you! Also not what I expected the answer to be, but I appreciate getting your input on the matter.<br /> <br /> How about rolls to identify characters and recognize werewolves and wolf-blooded by scent? I assumed since it's a roll that represents using your sense of smell with wolf senses, and the form bonuses apply to perception-based rolls made with your wolf senses that they would apply?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:48:51-07:00","id":560296,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this has been answered but is there any reason I couldn't use npc's like Pure and Hosts from the previous edition if I swapped out their gifts/numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6533-gingerkid88","name":"Gingerkid88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:45:40-07:00","id":560815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gingerkid88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=560296#post560296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this has been answered but is there any reason I couldn't use npc's like Pure and Hosts from the previous edition if I swapped out their gifts/numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they should be fine. It might be difficult with the Pure, since they had some unique Gifts that haven't been translated to 2e's new system for Gifts, but otherwise it should work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:13:23-07:00","id":561571,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this has been asked &amp; answered and I missed it, but...<br /> <br /> Have any supplements been confirmed as being developed yet for Second Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:03:45-07:00","id":561611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=561571#post561571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this has been asked &amp; answered and I missed it, but...<br /> <br /> Have any supplements been confirmed as being developed yet for Second Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Pack&quot; is currently on first drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:49:44-07:00","id":561850,"title":"","content":"How do 2e Uratha find Loci? And how do they recognise Resonance?<br /> <br /> Okay, that's two simple questions ...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6226-rulandor","name":"Rulandor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:55:34-07:00","id":561910,"title":"","content":"Presumably, Spirit Senses. They can just sort of... tell.<br /> <br /> Loci especially. They're characterized by very thin patches of gauntlet, and if a werewolf wants to know how thick the gauntlet is they can just try to peek through it and see how well they can see the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:12:31-07:00","id":561987,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Uratha just sense when they're inside the area of a Locus.<br /> <br /> Can't remember off-hand about Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:14:54-07:00","id":563238,"title":"","content":"So I'm pretty clear on how to make humans, other werewolves and spirits. I assume I can make a claimed by making a human/animal and a spirit and then mixing them with the claimed condition. How do I make a host? Is it the same as a claimed but taking Azlu/Beshilu powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6533-gingerkid88","name":"Gingerkid88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:45:24-07:00","id":563300,"title":"","content":"Pretty much just make a monster and tack on some dread powers. Sort of like Claimed, but without the spirit stuff. There's even some dread powers that are host only. Gauntlet Gnaw, Gauntlet Web, Discorporate, Warp Shard. You can find a lot more powers in the <i>Predators </i>book to turn into dread powers to round them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:33:16-07:00","id":568487,"title":"","content":"A couple quick questions about interacting with spirits.<br /> <br /> Can werewolves see spirits in Twilight? It says they can sense them, but that's not quite a clear description of how it works.<br /> <br /> How does one deal with a spirit in twilight if you can't interact with them? And why would a spirit ever materialize? Why do spirits even want to be in the Flesh anyway? What do they gain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:51:12-07:00","id":568501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=568487#post568487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can werewolves see spirits in Twilight? It says they can sense them, but that's not quite a clear description of how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take, 'Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested.' To mean that they can see them, smell them, hear them, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does one deal with a spirit in twilight if you can't interact with them? </div> </div> </div>Very carefully. Unless you have a bane, or the rite that kicks things out of Twilight. And a note to point out that werewolves count as banes to spirits more than two ranks below them. And a nice Death gift that lets you affect ghosts and death-oriented things in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And why would a spirit ever materialize? Why do spirits even want to be in the Flesh anyway? What do they gain? </div> </div> </div>Lack of competition. Bountiful essence. Are you a fire spirit? Just light a match. Set a car on fire. Drive it into a fireworks factory. It mostly revolves around essence and it being easier to get, which is their whole raison de vivre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:53:29-07:00","id":568504,"title":"","content":"Also, especially for weaker spirits it's much safer, having far fewer things that want to eat you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:22:33-07:00","id":568693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=568501#post568501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd take, 'Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested.' To mean that they can see them, smell them, hear them, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the rite Totemic Empowerment specifically states that 'The empowered pack member can see spirits in twilight clearly', which suggests that she couldn't before.<br /> <br /> Also, the Whisper Knife fetish says it 'allows an Uratha to strike entities in Twilight, but it does nothing to let the user see such beings' I'm paraphrasing for the sake of brevity, but these are both things that seem to contradict your conclusion. Errors, then you think? I'm guessing so but I just want a second opinion, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks (both of you) for your answers though. Especially about the spirit motives, that really makes a lot of sense. Last bit on that - Is there a benefit to materializing over just staying in twilight? Is it just the ability to affect things? Is there a change in how spirits interact with resonant essence in either form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:04:41-07:00","id":568736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=568693#post568693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the rite Totemic Empowerment specifically states that 'The empowered pack member can see spirits in twilight clearly', which suggests that she couldn't before.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you can use it on non-werewolves, such as wolf-blooded and humans and vampires and whoever else is in your pack that might not ordinarily be able to see spirits in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the Whisper Knife fetish says it 'allows an Uratha to strike entities in Twilight, but it does nothing to let the user see such beings' I'm paraphrasing for the sake of brevity, but these are both things that seem to contradict your conclusion. Errors, then you think? I'm guessing so but I just want a second opinion, I guess. </div> </div> </div>It's probably an artifact, yes, but spirits can also attempt to hide. 'Unless the spirit is intentionally trying to hide, Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks (both of you) for your answers though. Especially about the spirit motives, that really makes a lot of sense. Last bit on that - Is there a benefit to materializing over just staying in twilight? Is it just the ability to affect things? Is there a change in how spirits interact with resonant essence in either form? </div> </div> </div>Materializing allows you to confront mortals and actually do stuff. While in Twilight Form spirits are invisible to most and can't really come into contact with anything physical except their bane. So if you want to light that match and drive that car you'll need to materialize. Though there is a Telekinesis Numen, it's incapable of fine control. Aside from the invisibility and incorporeality, I <i>think </i>it's the same. So if a spirit seeks common essence, like of air or cars, they might be fine just hovering in Twilight form and harvesting it free of competition. But a spirit of something more specific might require a direct action to create to a surfeit of essence. Once in the material they start bleeding essence if they aren't in an area with an appropriate condition, so finding a steady source is a priority. And no problem for the answers, it seems like one of the few rules questions I've been able to somewhat handle here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:19:32-07:00","id":568747,"title":"","content":"Thanks. You are a national treasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T03:33:07-07:00","id":568967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=568693#post568693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the Whisper Knife fetish says it 'allows an Uratha to strike entities in Twilight, but it does nothing to let the user see such beings' I'm paraphrasing for the sake of brevity, but these are both things that seem to contradict your conclusion. Errors, then you think? I'm guessing so but I just want a second opinion, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can perceive Twilight spirits, and no, the Whisper Knife text is not an error. You'll note that it allows the Uratha to strike <i>any</i> entity in Twilight, not just spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:04:30-07:00","id":569042,"title":"","content":"Ohhh. Well there you go. That's a pretty nice fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T04:21:24-07:00","id":582143,"title":"","content":"What do you acually gain by outranking a spirit rankwise? this came up in our last session and we couldent find any information, thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6810-lurifix","name":"Lurifix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T04:29:00-07:00","id":582144,"title":"","content":"If you outrank a spirit by at least 2 ranks, your natural attacks count as its Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:29:24-07:00","id":586294,"title":"","content":"I'm working on some facets and I found myself at a bit of a loss. Some of the ways the renown mesh with the facets is obvious, notably with Cunning and Wisdom and Glory. But in what ways are the other renowns represented in the gift facets? A whole tally would be good.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:42:02-07:00","id":586299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=586294#post586294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on some facets and I found myself at a bit of a loss. Some of the ways the renown mesh with the facets is obvious, notably with Cunning and Wisdom and Glory. But in what ways are the other renowns represented in the gift facets? A whole tally would be good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you can be a bit more specific about what you're looking for, I may be able to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:19:46-07:00","id":586440,"title":"","content":"tl;dr 'Fluffwise,' what makes a facet a facet of a particular renown? Why is Memento Mori an Honor facet, while Bone Gnaw is a Purity one?<br /> <br /> The sections on renown are a little sparse in regards to the meaning of them. As I understand it, the spirit magic of gifts is not really a spirit thing. It is the magic of certain spirits as seen through the lens of the werewolf's soul, the soul of a hunter. So most facets are really built towards that and a few other things. And what you get is, with the spirit magic of a death spirit, refracted through the Cunning brands in the soul of a werewolf, an ability that allows you to use death in a cunning fashion. Wisdom gives you insight, awareness of certain things and knowledge. Glory tends to be overwhelming, big and grand or forceful. I'm not quite sure if those are right but that's how it seems just working off memory. Honor and Purity are a little more hazy for me. Is Honor more working 'within the confines' of the spirit magic? And Purity, maybe, more of the 'spirit side' of the gift?<br /> <br /> I was thinking about a second edition version of the Wound-born gift, for instance, and I figured a neat ability would be the ability to use a Wound as a locus for the purposes of Reaching, with a bonus to the dice pool based on the renown. But I couldn't figure if it would be Purity, symbolizing the Uratha's spirit side being attuned to the Wound, or Honor representing an 'agreement' with the Wound. Even Cunning seems like it could fit.<br /> <br /> I apologize if that's unclear, I know I can be that way at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:26:49-07:00","id":586846,"title":"","content":"All Gifts are intrinsic to the Uratha, so I disagree with them being spirit magic through an Uratha lens. That doesn't make the idea wrong or uninteresting though, and I think you ask a valid question. Some Gifts seem, at first glance, like they should be centered around two or three different renown instead of all five. Most are clearly correlated, some take a bit of thinking to see a correlation. Satchel raised a similar point in another conversation before the errata was finalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T01:19:12-07:00","id":586916,"title":"","content":"Yea. I was just remembering the first part of the gift section wrong. But the renown part was what I wanted to know about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:40:35-07:00","id":588044,"title":"","content":"How does one create a wolf-blooded character? Do you use the base Werewolf template like it says in the first section? In which case how do you know which features they DON'T get? Or do you add it to the Mortal template like the Appendix seems to insinuate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:49:16-07:00","id":588046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=586440#post586440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr 'Fluffwise,' what makes a facet a facet of a particular renown? Why is Memento Mori an Honor facet, while Bone Gnaw is a Purity one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and give a decent answer when I get home later today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T07:11:48-07:00","id":588106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=586440#post586440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr 'Fluffwise,' what makes a facet a facet of a particular renown? Why is Memento Mori an Honor facet, while Bone Gnaw is a Purity one?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm fairly sure it has to do with the Tribes. I haven't done an in depth analysis, but one thing that struck me, when I was reading through the Gift lists was how very much the different gifts seemed to lend to one Tribe or another. <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, Memento Mori is <i>such</i> a Storm Lord power! I can totally see Hunters in Darkness using Bone Gnaw to track down the Hosts.&quot; And so on. Auspice Gifts are based on Auspice Renown, Shadow Gifts reflect Tribe Renown. And Wolf Gifts are their own thing.<br /> <br /> Like I said, this isn't exactly something I looked into with any depth, but I absolutely got that impression while reading them over.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T07:41:21-07:00","id":588133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=588044#post588044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one create a wolf-blooded character? Do you use the base Werewolf template like it says in the first section? In which case how do you know which features they DON'T get? Or do you add it to the Mortal template like the Appendix seems to insinuate?</div> </div> </div> </div>You use the character creation rules that start at page 81, but skip step five (because they aren't Forsaken, so you shouldn't add the Forsaken template). Also, give them a Virtue and a Vice, Integrity instead of Harmony, and a Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:47:10-07:00","id":588170,"title":"","content":"Have I missed something, but it seems like fetish tats are no longer a thing? I'm getting the feeling that it has to be a solid, separate object. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:56:11-07:00","id":588347,"title":"","content":"They're not in the book so you haven't missed anything. They might be introduced in another book or gone for good. It's an easy thing to convert to second edition, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:07:33-07:00","id":590222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=586440#post586440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr 'Fluffwise,' what makes a facet a facet of a particular renown? Why is Memento Mori an Honor facet, while Bone Gnaw is a Purity one?<br /> <br /> The sections on renown are a little sparse in regards to the meaning of them. As I understand it, the spirit magic of gifts is not really a spirit thing. It is the magic of certain spirits as seen through the lens of the werewolf's soul, the soul of a hunter. So most facets are really built towards that and a few other things. And what you get is, with the spirit magic of a death spirit, refracted through the Cunning brands in the soul of a werewolf, an ability that allows you to use death in a cunning fashion. Wisdom gives you insight, awareness of certain things and knowledge. Glory tends to be overwhelming, big and grand or forceful. I'm not quite sure if those are right but that's how it seems just working off memory. Honor and Purity are a little more hazy for me. Is Honor more working 'within the confines' of the spirit magic? And Purity, maybe, more of the 'spirit side' of the gift?<br /> <br /> I was thinking about a second edition version of the Wound-born gift, for instance, and I figured a neat ability would be the ability to use a Wound as a locus for the purposes of Reaching, with a bonus to the dice pool based on the renown. But I couldn't figure if it would be Purity, symbolizing the Uratha's spirit side being attuned to the Wound, or Honor representing an 'agreement' with the Wound. Even Cunning seems like it could fit.<br /> <br /> I apologize if that's unclear, I know I can be that way at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'l try and cover all this in more depth in the eventual blog post on Gift design, but:<br /> <br /> There are various characteristics that get applied to categorising a Facet under a particular Renown, and they are not strict; context and feel are just as important.<br /> <br /> So for example, in mechanical terms, powers that enhance or augment other Uratha as well as the character tend to go under Honor, as do powers obviously relating to honor and discipline, and powers that protect and ward against outside influence. Purity tends towards either as pure and direct a reflection of the Gift's concept as possible, as pure a refinement of the hunter through that Gift's symbol, and of course direct concepts of purity and purification. Context and feel have a significant impact, in particular the nature of the Gift in question; Inspiration, for example, has lots of powers that enhance or augment other Uratha in the pack, and they can't all go under Honor.<br /> <br /> For the Wound Gift, for example, I'd look at what the general feel of the Gift you're going for is, that sort of thing. The Facet in question that you're considering is basically a transport power that's about giving you another option for nipping across the Gauntlet and generally cheating a bit on the usual metaphysics of how Wounds work, so likely to come under Cunning. I'd expect a Purity Facet to be something that is more inward-focused on the Uratha themselves; a transformation or warping power, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Above all, it takes several iterations to get a Gift and its Facets to shake out properly. You build, rebuild, chuck the crap ideas, refine, and so forth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T09:38:18-07:00","id":590267,"title":"","content":"Interesting, thank you very much. I'm looking forward to this blog post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:10:58-07:00","id":590440,"title":"","content":"Quick question about grappling. If I grapple someone, does the first contested grapple happen on their next turn or next round? The rules say each turn, I just don't know if that includes the current turn if the grappled target has yet to act.<br /> <br /> Secondly, since werewolves in wolf forms can apply a grapple after a bite attack, what overpower maneuvers can they do? Control Weapon seems unlikely, for example. Pretty much all of them seem unlikely except the Damage maneuver and perhaps the Hold maneuver.<br /> <br /> Next, the Damage maneuver indicates that it does bashing damage, but I can't see how that would be the case if you're being held by an Uratha in Urshul. Common sense would say it doesn't refer to those cases, but I want to ask anyway for support on that. It suggests that you can use a weapon bonus in the case of a controlled weapon, but doesn't specify that said damage would be lethal. Again, common sense, but still.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you establish a grapple, retain control of the grapple on the following turn, can you choose to (instead of applying an overpowering maneuver) drop the grapple and attack in some other way? And if so, does the opponent get to act again that turn? Alternatively, if I drop a grapple (via bite) to bite again (perhaps aiming at the leg or something) can I re-establish the grapple that same turn? Can I specify a target body part doing the Damage maneuver, or do I have to start over?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance. Sorry if that's all confusing, I'll try to edit for clarity when my brain isn't mush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:34:21-07:00","id":590452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590440#post590440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question about grappling. If I grapple someone, does the first contested grapple happen on their next turn or next round? The rules say each turn, I just don't know if that includes the current turn if the grappled target has yet to act.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be able to happen until the next round, since the contested roll happens on the higher of the two characters' Initiatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590440#post590440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, since werewolves in wolf forms can apply a grapple after a bite attack, what overpower maneuvers can they do? Control Weapon seems unlikely, for example. Pretty much all of them seem unlikely except the Damage maneuver and perhaps the Hold maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they remain in Urshul or Urhan during the grapple, I'd assume they could Break Free, Damage, Drop Prone, or Hold. But if they wanted to Control Weapon, Disarm, or Restrain, they'd have to shift to a form with opposable thumbs. I'm on the fence about Take Cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590440#post590440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, the Damage maneuver indicates that it does bashing damage, but I can't see how that would be the case if you're being held by an Uratha in Urshul. Common sense would say it doesn't refer to those cases, but I want to ask anyway for support on that. It suggests that you can use a weapon bonus in the case of a controlled weapon, but doesn't specify that said damage would be lethal. Again, common sense, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, werewolves do lethal damage with their Bite attack in all forms but Hishu, which is a specific use of the Damage maneuver. Although they don't <i>require</i> a Grapple to use it except in Hishu and Dalu, I'm sure they could still use it in a grapple normally. I'd assume they could also Damage with their claws, which are equal or worse in terms of damage in all forms anyway, unless the character has Living Weapon for a particular form's claws. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590440#post590440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, if you establish a grapple, retain control of the grapple on the following turn, can you choose to (instead of applying an overpowering maneuver) drop the grapple and attack in some other way? And if so, does the opponent get to act again that turn? Alternatively, if I drop a grapple (via bite) to bite again (perhaps aiming at the leg or something) can I re-establish the grapple that same turn? Can I specify a target body part doing the Damage maneuver, or do I have to start over?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have to use the Break Free maneuver to drop out of a Grapple, even if you're the one who initiated it. And since you can't take more than one action in a turn, neither combatant would be able to attack in the same turn, since they already both participated in a contested action.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:53:02-07:00","id":590462,"title":"","content":"That all makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> Though the Break Free maneuver says it's a reflexive action to succeed and you can take another action that turn, which is why I was wondering whether the other person gets their turn back, since they are no longer in a grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:20:14-07:00","id":590487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590462#post590462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> Though the Break Free maneuver says it's a reflexive action to succeed and you can take another action that turn, which is why I was wondering whether the other person gets their turn back, since they are no longer in a grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you're right, I'd forgotten that was a reflexive action. I guess then both combatants should be able to attack again that turn... Which definitely gives the character with the higher Initiative a huge advantage, especially if they can establish a grapple as part of an attack, since that would allow you to set up a sort of stun lock... Hadn't thought about that before, but holy crap!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:40:45-07:00","id":590501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=590452#post590452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, werewolves do lethal damage with their Bite attack in all forms but Hishu, which is a specific use of the Damage maneuver</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on 'The Predator's Jaws' sidebar, it looks like their Bite attack is lethal in all forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:49:10-07:00","id":591300,"title":"","content":"That's only to vampires (and possibly vampire-like things such as mummies). <br /> <br /> It's basically a metaphysical glitch. Teeth normally do bashing to vamps regardless of how pointy they are, but werewolves have magic sanctified killin' teeth, which bypass that protection and do lethal. Even if they wouldn't normally be doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:55:57-07:00","id":591306,"title":"","content":"Human teeth normally do bashing to everyone, they're considered a -1 damage unarmed attack. Bypassing the natural damage resistance of vampires is one thing, but they're either upgrading the damage for them or always do lethal.<br /> <br /> Offhand, I'd guess the writer thought, understandably, teeth did lethal damage across the board.<br /> <br /> Second edition could really stand to have an official errata or FAQ like <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Smoke</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-15-2015, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:10:30-07:00","id":591341,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's upgrading. <br /> <br /> It's sort of a really minor bane that nobody even notices because seriously why would a werewolf be biting vampires in hishu anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T16:29:12-07:00","id":602359,"title":"","content":"Quick question about how you guys read the Barghest facet.<br /> <br /> Duration: Permanent. <br /> <br /> The Uratha can perceive ghosts and other disembodied<br /> undead or death-infused beings in Twilight. While in Gauru,<br /> Urshul, and Urhan, she is able to attack such Twilight beings<br /> and damage them by spending 1 Essence per scene. <b>She adds<br /> her Glory Renown to Perception and Empathy dice pools<br /> against undead of any kind and,</b> if she damages a corporeal<br /> undead while in the above forms, she may reflexively spend<br /> 1 Essence to drain it of a single Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Is the section in bold part of the permanent effect? Or part of the first activated effect allowing you to attack ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T16:37:30-07:00","id":602362,"title":"","content":"I think its part of the permanent effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T16:47:24-07:00","id":602365,"title":"","content":"Yeah, everything else is clear on whether it costs anything, it seems that's permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:06:21-07:00","id":603264,"title":"","content":"When you use your Flaring Renown power with essence... lets say Cunning for the example: In the resolution section, it is written this: Once at least one individual has used the <br /> +2 bonus, you may choose to shed this Condition to add the character\u2019s Cunning Renown in automatic successes to any <br /> Larceny, Stealth, or Subterfuge action, even if she rolls no successes.<br /> <br /> 1- Question: Does that mean that you must have to win the roll vs that +2 penalty that someone will use on you ?<br /> <br /> 2- Question: When you add your cunning renown in automatic successes, to any Larceny, Stealth, or subterfuge action... you do that how many time ? One roll only, or is this have some durability ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:43:00-07:00","id":603283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=603264#post603264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you use your Flaring Renown power with essence... lets say Cunning for the example: In the resolution section, it is written this: Once at least one individual has used the <br /> +2 bonus, you may choose to shed this Condition to add the character\u2019s Cunning Renown in automatic successes to any <br /> Larceny, Stealth, or Subterfuge action, even if she rolls no successes.<br /> <br /> 1- Question: Does that mean that you must have to win the roll vs that +2 penalty that someone will use on you ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, they just have to use it. Doesn't matter the results of the roll, as long as they use that +2. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=603264#post603264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Question: When you add your cunning renown in automatic successes, to any Larceny, Stealth, or subterfuge action... you do that how many time ? One roll only, or is this have some durability ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:01:02-07:00","id":603336,"title":"","content":"The trick is having a packmate benefit from those +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:44:23-07:00","id":603355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=603336#post603336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trick is having a packmate benefit from those +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I imagine it might be common to develop little ritual &quot;plays&quot; based around fufulling the conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:28:14-07:00","id":604373,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the Maeljinn are basically very powerful demons that feed off vice yes? And their minions form a major antagonist faction for the Forsaken in the Bale Hounds. My question is, why were vice-demons chosen as a major antagonist for a werewolf game? Or even for a half-animist-spirit game? I'm not seeing a particular connection there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:34:28-07:00","id":604377,"title":"","content":"Everything has a spirit.<br /> <br /> Evil has a spirit as well. If your antagonists can be the spirit of a river, the personification of anger over a football game, and the essence of corruption in politics, why not a vice?<br /> <br /> It's unknown whether Maeljin are 'true' demons. Inferno says they are comparable to archdemons, but specifies it's only, 'for the purposes of this book,' while werewolf places them with spirits, more or less. All in all the books suggest they're a mix of both, like demon-corrupted spirits. Their interest is in the Hisil, expanding the Wounds within it until the entire Shadow is a bloody reflection of the world.<br /> <br /> It's also possible they have a Firstborn on their side.<br /> <br /> Due to their interests in the Hisil, it would make sense to reach out to Uratha to get things done, considering their abilities and renown. And in exchange, they offer rewards. Plus, considering the ease with which werewolves are tempted by vices, it's easy to fall into their service even if it's not your intention.<br /> <br /> There's not much information about them in second edition yet so a lot may have changed. They may be some vestiges of Pangea, the same way werewolves are. Except rather than being remnants of the pillar of predators, they're remnants of the pillars of evil.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the Maeljin aren't exactly antagonists except in games of large scope. It's more likely you would confront Bale Hounds and Pure, than Maeljin and Pure Firstborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-26-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:43:33-07:00","id":604382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=604373#post604373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the Maeljinn are basically very powerful demons that feed off vice yes? And their minions form a major antagonist faction for the Forsaken in the Bale Hounds. My question is, why were vice-demons chosen as a major antagonist for a werewolf game? Or even for a half-animist-spirit game? I'm not seeing a particular connection there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons (the vice-feeding kind from Inferno, not the fallen angels from Descent) are a particular kind of spirit. Forsaken is pretty big on spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T04:20:06-07:00","id":604587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=604373#post604373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the Maeljinn are basically very powerful demons that feed off vice yes? And their minions form a major antagonist faction for the Forsaken in the Bale Hounds. My question is, why were vice-demons chosen as a major antagonist for a werewolf game? Or even for a half-animist-spirit game? I'm not seeing a particular connection there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Forget the Maeljin themselves. They're basically rank 6+ entities, and beyond normal rules; you'll likely never run into one at all during a story. <br /> <br /> What is important? The Wounds themselves and the corrupt spirits inside. No one wants this kind of spirit inside their territory, or anywhere nearby. Its horrible, it makes everything pure shit on both sides of the Gauntlet. <br /> <br /> Everything in a werewolf game always comes down to roughly three things - pack, territory, and the hunt. Corrupt, evil spirits are nasty, and Wounds are a blight in the territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:29:04-07:00","id":612874,"title":"","content":"With the emphasis on lineage for some werewolves, most notably the Ivory Claws, do you think they count wolf-blooded created by their Lunacy who may turn into or eventually spawn werewolves?<br /> <br /> If so or not, do you think there would be a merit or rite or other ability to detect a connection like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:37:56-07:00","id":613112,"title":"","content":"I'd say no. Not least because of how it's effectively <i>Luna</i> that provides the wolfy side of these guys. Far from accepting them as their own, I think Ivory Claws may even deride them as freakish half-breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T04:10:35-07:00","id":613212,"title":"","content":"As Elfive said. Becoming Wolf-Blooded through Lunacy is an affliction of Luna, not of Father Wolf's purity. The Ivory Claws would most likely despise these moon-cursed, and the <i>Anshega</i> responsible for their creation would suffer loss of face for it. IMO, Ivory Claws would be the strongest adherents to 'The Herd Must Not Know', as there's always the chance of these Luna whelps springing up, which is a potent reminder that even the most ardent Pure can't escape the Bitch-Goddess entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T04:50:11-07:00","id":613223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=613212#post613212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Elfive said. Becoming Wolf-Blooded through Lunacy is an affliction of Luna, not of Father Wolf's purity. The Ivory Claws would most likely despise these moon-cursed, and the <i>Anshega</i> responsible for their creation would suffer loss of face for it. IMO, Ivory Claws would be the strongest adherents to 'The Herd Must Not Know', as there's always the chance of these Luna whelps springing up, which is a potent reminder that even the most ardent Pure can't escape the Bitch-Goddess entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was having a think on that when pondering a full updated-to-2e-Pure pitch. Let me know what you think of the following:<br /> <br /> Ignore that it's in the name for a moment, and just go with me - the Pure (or some Pure at least) refuse to believe Lunacy is anything to do with Luna.<br /> <br /> I mean, it can't be, right? Pure cause Lunacy and they've torn Luna's tumourous Auspice right out of themselves. What's left is <i>wolf</i>. Lunacy isn't about the moon - it's about human reaction to being faced with the most godawesome godawful terrifying predator they'll ever encounter, an inheritor of the Wolf itself. People aren't scared of the moon and it doesn't drive them into a desperate fight for survival - otherwise every time people looked at the sky it would be <i>bam</i>, there goes human civilisation. Put people in front of a wolf, though? Well they get fucking scared, or they get backed into a corner and fight cos there's nothing else to do, or they get crazy spiritual ideas about running with the wolves in their head after seeing the magnificence of the creatures. People going batshit crazy when seeing a werewolf, it's all just down to the predatory aura of <i>Urfarah</i> massively amplifying those basic responses.<br /> <br /> <i>Therefore</i> the Pure totally aren't hypocrites for making use of Lunacy. <i>Therefore</i> the Ivory Claws would totally be justified and in the right by using Lunacy exposure of selected herd of the 'right' bloodlines to try and force an early/spontaneous Change. Because it's all part of the Great Predator, see? The Warden Moon has nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> Given how Harmony has radically changed, the Pure need other, interesting new things to be hypocritical or disingenuous about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T04:59:56-07:00","id":613226,"title":"","content":"I could see some very passionate Ivory Claws lodges having very different views on the subject, and a willingness to take matters into their own hands to prove the supremacy of their belief...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:16:23-07:00","id":613318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=613223#post613223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Therefore</i> the Pure totally aren't hypocrites for making use of Lunacy. <i>Therefore</i> the Ivory Claws would totally be justified and in the right by using Lunacy exposure of selected herd of the 'right' bloodlines to try and force an early/spontaneous Change. Because it's all part of the Great Predator, see? The Warden Moon has nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> Given how Harmony has radically changed, the Pure need other, interesting new things to be hypocritical or disingenuous about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> In that case, I could see the Ivory Claws think of themselves as the &quot;parents&quot; of these new Wolf-Bloods. They were obviously spawned by the touch of an untainted werewolf, and thus clear of the Moon Bastard. Their lineage is therefore Pure and unsullied. Its like the equivalent of a commoner being raised to noble status.<br /> <br /> And the other two Pure tribes don't care about your origins, so long as you roughly follow their creeds. I imagine that the Pure have a baptism they put the wolf bloods through that strips Moon Birth Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T21:50:11-07:00","id":614562,"title":"","content":"I keep going back and forth on it myself. I was originally thinking the Ivory Claws'd have them in their 'families,' perhaps at a diminished stature until they proved themselves, so they could keep from sullying their name by bringing in a wildcard. But then Elfive and Bunyip reminded me about the origins of Lunacy. But then Acrozatarim reminded me how it works in the current edition, which is supposed to be a supernaturally-bolstered sort of primal fear of predators like Mother Wolf, and I think he had a solid argument for the Pure. That's not counting in other werewolves who might take in new members they caused to change or who have no werewolves in their own families to help them through things.<br /> <br /> Though Bunyip has a point, in werewolf and really the World of Darkness it feels 'right' when there's some groups with conflicting views. I originally asked because I could see wolves having a problem keeping their bloodlines alive solely through the old fashioned way, with all the wars popping up, but I do like how vampire has dynasties and in Masquerade there's pretty much a family tree connecting all the vampires. Which gets skewed if someone could just get 'chosen' and become one.<br /> <br /> Either way I like that they're a part of it, especially with the Ivory Claws. It's amusing to think of someone having such a horrible time with their first encounter with werewolves that they have a dramatic failure on their Lunacy check, later end up turning into a werewolf, then have a more horrible time as the Ivory Claws decide they're now part of the family. And they take family seriously.<br /> <br /> In the Autobiography of a Werewolf Hunter books, which I can't help but recommend, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">they have something like Vampire the Masquerade, with an ancient progenitor werewolf, the Beast, who created Princes beneath him by sharing parts of his soul to 'mark' them, and they in turn marked others, and they marked others, all the way down the line. The problem being that they have one shared soul, an evil and powerful thing, but sharing it too much can stretch that power too thin. Which calls for occasional cullings by the higher ups. They're sort of like the Hosts, too, I thought, with the shared soul angle.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyways, thanks for the input and ideas. I like that one, Acrozatarim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:48:30-07:00","id":615514,"title":"","content":"They would need to call it something else if they don't believe it comes from Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:58:21-07:00","id":615519,"title":"","content":"AROOOOnacy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:47:54-07:00","id":615605,"title":"","content":"I think Lunacy is more of a term for our benefit. Not entirely, but it doesn't seem like every werewolf is going to call the fear response Lunacy. Pure might just call it fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:52:50-07:00","id":615613,"title":"","content":"&quot;Knowing their place.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:59:20-07:00","id":615672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=615514#post615514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would need to call it something else if they don't believe it comes from Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word means madness. If the characters even refer to the atavistic, delusional, and receptive responses humans have to witnessing werewolves collectively as &quot;Lunacy&quot;, then they probably mean it by this definition, rather than specifically as a madness caused by Luna. In real life, plenty of folks aren't even aware that the root of the word has anything to do with the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:16:49-07:00","id":615691,"title":"","content":"Still, I can't see that &quot;plenty of folks&quot; including werewolves to any great extent. Not even the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:52:31-07:00","id":615731,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Middle English: from Old French </span></span><i>lunatique</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, from late Latin </span></span><i>lunaticus</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, from Latin </span></span><i>luna </i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2018moon\u2019 (from the belief that changes of the moon caused intermittent insanity).</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:04:10-07:00","id":616024,"title":"","content":"Couple quick questions. First two are just me looking for corroboration.<br /> <br /> 1. The Dice pool for the Hit &amp; Run facet is only referring to the stealth roll to hide, right? I'm assuming you don't roll for the interrupt action.<br /> <br /> 2. The Predator's Unmatched Pursuit facet has two different effects that you have to use essence for? First expenditure grants you a bonus to movement speed equal to your glory and a multiplier to jump rolls based on the same. Then you have to spend <i>another</i> essence to double your move speed? Can you activate the second effect without the first?<br /> <br /> 3. The Rahu Hunter's aspect inflicts the Swaggering condition, which states the target cannot prepare or alter their routine. What does this mean? Can an opponent hide or use stealth after being affected by this condition? Can he use cover? Can he call for bodyguards? Cam he run from battle? Fluffwise I read it as the character is compelled to face the rahu directly when challenged, but the description talks about preparation which, considering the aspect only lasts a scene, doesn't make sense to me. How does one &quot;prepare&quot; during an encounter that has basically already started?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your wisdom, guys. The last one especially is difficult for me to pin down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:29:38-07:00","id":616053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=615691#post615691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I can't see that &amp;quot;plenty of folks&amp;quot; including werewolves to any great extent. Not even the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Granted, but I was questioning wether Lunacy is even an in-character term, and if it is, wether it's used more because of its relationship with the moon, or more because of its apparently maddening effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T04:34:28-07:00","id":616286,"title":"","content":"Considering that a third of the Pure are religious extremists with a hate-on for anything Luna? I have to imagine that they'd be quick to vilify anything even remotely close to associating with the Moon. Its like the Church and demons - there's an obsession with detailing everything about it. <br /> <br /> Lunacy seems to be an in-character term, as far as I know. At least, as used by the Forsaken. Much like Death Rage still is an in character phrase, despite also having Kuruth, Wasu/Basu-Im. And, as an in character term, its probably one that the Fire Touched would jump on, even if its a stretch by some. My guess? The FT would use some First Tongue word for it exclusively. Or am I the only one who thinks it odd that Lunacy doesn't have a corresponding word for it, when virtually everything else does? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:16:40-07:00","id":616334,"title":"","content":"You could have the pure call it Delirium...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T08:40:07-07:00","id":616527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616286#post616286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that a third of the Pure are religious extremists with a hate-on for anything Luna? I have to imagine that they'd be quick to vilify anything even remotely close to associating with the Moon. Its like the Church and demons - there's an obsession with detailing everything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if a Fire-Touched walked into a gas station where they were selling moon pies, and hanging the flag of South Carolina and Buzz Aldrin was standing there, do you think they'd be triggered?<br /> <br /> What would the Pure think of the space program, specifically the moon landings? If the Uratha put it together that they are linked to the return of the idigam, the Pure might have more ammo in their arguments about Luna being evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:03:09-07:00","id":616675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616527#post616527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if a Fire-Touched walked into a gas station where they were selling moon pies, and hanging the flag of South Carolina and Buzz Aldrin was standing there, do you think they'd be triggered?</div> </div> </div> </div> Triggered? I'm not saying they'd fall into Kuruth here, just that they'd be annoyed by it. Its like a hard line Christian being flashed with what they think is Satanic signs all the time. Annoying, but they deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:08:21-07:00","id":616677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616024#post616024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Dice pool for the Hit &amp; Run facet is only referring to the stealth roll to hide, right? I'm assuming you don't roll for the interrupt action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this to be the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616024#post616024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The Predator's Unmatched Pursuit facet has two different effects that you have to use essence for? First expenditure grants you a bonus to movement speed equal to your glory and a multiplier to jump rolls based on the same. Then you have to spend <i>another</i> essence to double your move speed? Can you activate the second effect without the first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, 1 essence means multiply jump distance and +Glory to speed. Then you can spend say 3 essence to multiply their speed by 8 in a turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616024#post616024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Rahu Hunter's aspect inflicts the Swaggering condition, which states the target cannot prepare or alter their routine. What does this mean? Can an opponent hide or use stealth after being affected by this condition? Can he use cover? Can he call for bodyguards? Cam he run from battle? Fluffwise I read it as the character is compelled to face the rahu directly when challenged, but the description talks about preparation which, considering the aspect only lasts a scene, doesn't make sense to me. How does one &quot;prepare&quot; during an encounter that has basically already started?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cow the Prey Hunting Facet (Glory) makes the condition associated with it Persistent; without that? Scoring an exceptional success you apply it for a number of days equal to the inflicter's PU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:09:50-07:00","id":616681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616675#post616675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Triggered? I'm not saying they'd fall into Kuruth here, just that they'd be annoyed by it. Its like a hard line Christian being flashed with what they think is Satanic signs all the time. Annoying, but they deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think nofather may have meant &quot;triggered&quot; in Tumblr parlance, not Death Rage Triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:18:57-07:00","id":616688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616286#post616286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or am I the only one who thinks it odd that Lunacy doesn't have a corresponding word for it, when virtually everything else does?</div> </div> </div> </div>I put in a request for it in the First Tongue translation thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:19:25-07:00","id":616689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616681#post616681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think nofather may have meant &quot;triggered&quot; in Tumblr parlance, not Death Rage Triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant Death Rage, but I think it's sort of similar, most people just don't have an inner beast to fall back on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T13:40:48-07:00","id":616785,"title":"","content":"<i>The Rahu Hunter's aspect inflicts the Swaggering condition, which states the target cannot prepare or alter their routine. What does this mean? Can an opponent hide or use stealth after being affected by this condition? Can he use cover? Can he call for bodyguards? Cam he run from battle? Fluffwise I read it as the character is compelled to face the rahu directly when challenged, but the description talks about preparation which, considering the aspect only lasts a scene, doesn't make sense to me. How does one &quot;prepare&quot; during an encounter that has basically already started?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616677#post616677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cow the Prey Hunting Facet (Glory) makes the condition associated with it Persistent; without that? Scoring an exceptional success you apply it for a number of days equal to the inflicter's PU.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what does it mean during a single scene? Are you saying it doesn't really do anything without an exceptional success or Cow the Prey? And what does unable to prepare really mean? I'm just really having trouble getting a grip on what it means. Hence the questions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:04:27-07:00","id":616794,"title":"","content":"A scene doesn't really have to just encompass the fight. They don't prepare. No calling for help or getting new weapons, they probably wouldn't hide either, or they might only run after the Condition has been resolved by wounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:19:58-07:00","id":616800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616785#post616785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]The Rahu Hunter's aspect inflicts the Swaggering condition, which states the target cannot prepare or alter their routine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I'm lost here. What's the Swaggering Condition? My book says the Submissive condition for the Rahu Aspect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this mean? Can an opponent hide or use stealth after being affected by this condition? Can he use cover? Can he call for bodyguards? Cam he run from battle? </div> </div> </div> Conditions generally work by either giving dice penalties/bonuses for certain kinds of actions, or rewarding you with beats for certain actions, or both. You can always do something, but you won't get beats, and likely suffer some kind of penalty for doing it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:41:13-07:00","id":616805,"title":"","content":"The updated version of the book changed it from Submissive to Swaggering. If you go to DrivethruRpg the update is free if you bought the early access version (which I assume you did, since you have it). Though if my GM has trouble with it maybe I could just go back to that condition instead.<br /> <br /> And nofather, your comment on what constitutes a scene makes sense. I guess I just need to understand what fall under the scope of the condition though. I agree with everything you said, but it just feels uncertain how far it would extend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:45:59-07:00","id":616810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616800#post616800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, I'm lost here. What's the Swaggering Condition? My book says the Submissive condition for the Rahu Aspect.<br /> <br /> Conditions generally work by either giving dice penalties/bonuses for certain kinds of actions, or rewarding you with beats for certain actions, or both. You can always do something, but you won't get beats, and likely suffer some kind of penalty for doing it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably you have not downloaded the latest version of the pdf. If your printed book has a mistake like this I am not sure what you should do.<br /> The Submissive condition was swapped for Swaggering. Swaggering prevents the target from preparing in any way to fight the Rahu and his pack by making him feel too confident in his ability to take on the Werewolf(the target can break this by making resolve+composure rolls with a target equal to rahu's purity and a willpower).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T15:21:56-07:00","id":616845,"title":"","content":"How does bulletproof armor work with silver bullets?<br /> <br /> I.e. Fortified form grants 2/2 armor. Against normal bullets, that would remove two points of damage and then lower another two points of damage from lethal to bashing. What happens if those bullets are silver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T15:28:31-07:00","id":616850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616805#post616805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The updated version of the book changed it from Submissive to Swaggering. If you go to DrivethruRpg the update is free if you bought the early access version (which I assume you did, since you have it). Though if my GM has trouble with it maybe I could just go back to that condition instead.<br /> <br /> And nofather, your comment on what constitutes a scene makes sense. I guess I just need to understand what fall under the scope of the condition though. I agree with everything you said, but it just feels uncertain how far it would extend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems pretty clear to me. No going to get weapons, no calling for backup, no setting traps or preparing ambushes, no changing your normal routine. You just have to fight exactly as-is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T15:49:53-07:00","id":616864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616845#post616845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does bulletproof armor work with silver bullets?<br /> <br /> I.e. Fortified form grants 2/2 armor. Against normal bullets, that would remove two points of damage and then lower another two points of damage from lethal to bashing. What happens if those bullets are silver?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It works exactly the same with silver bullets would be my guess. Armor does not allow the bullets to actually wound you, the bashing you get is from blunt force. Any damage above the armor's rating would be aggravated as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T19:41:14-07:00","id":617053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616850#post616850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems pretty clear to me. No going to get weapons, no calling for backup, no setting traps or preparing ambushes, no changing your normal routine. You just have to fight exactly as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly\u200b. You can use it great effect if you catch an opponent unprepared, and it's also useful for keeping prey from running away when it would be in the prey's best interest to do so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:26:53-07:00","id":617152,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, Luna and Helios are the Rank 8 Spirits of the Moon and Sun, respectively. Uratha call them Lesser Celestines. Gaia is the Rank 9 Spirit of the entire Earth, if it exists. Gaia would be a Greater Celestine. But what about the rest of the Solar System? Do they have their own Rank 8 Spirits/Lesser Celestines? We admired, studied and worshiped the Sun, Moon and Stars for much longer than we knew there were other planets. That makes me think other Lesser Celestines would be weaker, capping at Rank 7. Then again, we have the Idigam now, who can summon spirits from the endless void, so maybe they could communicate with, control and reshape the more distant Lesser Celestines. But what about the Lesser Celestines of phenomena like super massive black holes, or ancient nebulae? Their near total, or straight up total lack of interaction with anything other than outer space spirits would make them exceptionally alien in appearance and personality, I bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:45:50-07:00","id":617163,"title":"","content":"Since they don't have humans or life they probably don't have as rich a spiritual ecosystem as Earth's Shadow, they might remain dormant most of the time. But if I recall correctly, Luna shields Earth from interference from other planets in the solar system. They probably don't want to have anything to do with Earth to begin with, though. Making the jump, if even possible, would put them in direct competition with a horde of greedy spirits. Smaller spirits of astronomical interest might seem alien, but there re bound to be some astronomers among werewolves who might be able to figure things out and planetariums and large-scale telescopes and labs in territories that might have smaller-scale versions of spirits of outer space phenomena.<br /> <br /> I believe there is a mage legacy that revolves around the spirits of other planets, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-06-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T23:08:13-07:00","id":617171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=617152#post617152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves, Luna and Helios are the Rank 8 Spirits of the Moon and Sun, respectively. Uratha call them Lesser Celestines. Gaia is the Rank 9 Spirit of the entire Earth, if it exists. Gaia would be a Greater Celestine. But what about the rest of the Solar System?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, I think, part of the reason 2e changed the Rank bands \u2014 the Firstborn are now lesser Celestines, there's no longer such a thing as a &quot;minor Incarna,&quot; and a named Rank is no longer dedicated solely to a wholly speculative class of entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, we have the Idigam now, who can summon spirits from the endless void, so maybe they could communicate with, control and reshape the more distant Lesser Celestines. </div> </div> </div>I think we'd have bigger things to worry about if there were in fact idigam above the Rank of Greater Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T02:46:06-07:00","id":617411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616864#post616864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It works exactly the same with silver bullets would be my guess. Armor does not allow the bullets to actually wound you, the bashing you get is from blunt force. Any damage above the armor's rating would be aggravated as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, with silver it's probably best to think of the damage as being lethal that then <i>upgrades</i> to aggravated once it's on the health track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:34:54-07:00","id":619344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=616850#post616850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems pretty clear to me. No going to get weapons, no calling for backup, no setting traps or preparing ambushes, no changing your normal routine. You just have to fight exactly as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask these questions primarily because it isn't clear to my group sometimes and this helps us determine which interpretation is in the minority. This time though nobody was certain how far it extended and I think we'll just have to play it by ear. Thanks for the help, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:20:34-07:00","id":619545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=617163#post617163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they don't have humans or life they probably don't have as rich a spiritual ecosystem as Earth's Shadow, they might remain dormant most of the time. But if I recall correctly, Luna shields Earth from interference from other planets in the solar system. They probably don't want to have anything to do with Earth to begin with, though. Making the jump, if even possible, would put them in direct competition with a horde of greedy spirits. Smaller spirits of astronomical interest might seem alien, but there re bound to be some astronomers among werewolves who might be able to figure things out and planetariums and large-scale telescopes and labs in territories that might have smaller-scale versions of spirits of outer space phenomena.<br /> <br /> I believe there is a mage legacy that revolves around the spirits of other planets, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes the Mage Legacy was the Thrice Great in Legacy the Ancients, and there is some description of the celestial courts. That could eventually be useful for Werewolf too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","user":"Arcanum Magicae","date":". 08-12-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","name":"Arcanum Magicae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T14:51:57-07:00","id":623669,"title":"","content":"I'm just curious. Are Unihar gone for good or are they still around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T15:03:10-07:00","id":623677,"title":"","content":"I believe they are gone for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T16:18:26-07:00","id":623740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=623669#post623669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just curious. Are Unihar gone for good or are they still around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Porting them over isn't difficult at all, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://for