nkedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:27:45-07:00","id":624275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=624257#post624257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have wolf blooded who's the child of two werewolves with the Spirit Double tell, only the double manifests as something that looks like a werewolf in gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the <i>unihar</i> and am glad for the removal of the Black Birth, but this is a cool idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T09:03:37-07:00","id":624421,"title":"","content":"Or maybe that just happens after said Wolfblood goes through their first change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T09:13:30-07:00","id":624429,"title":"","content":"Although I am glad Unihar were scrapped in this edition, I would not be opposed to them returning with completely new origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T09:51:55-07:00","id":624451,"title":"","content":"I could see it as a broader punishment. Spirits can't break their bans, but werewolves can. Second edition 'unihar' may be wolf-like Furies, spawned from the firstborn totems to harangue those who break their tribal oaths once too often. A fun part of that might be the varied kinds of unihar, representative of the different firstborn, and different methods with which they'd use to punish the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T14:37:57-07:00","id":624651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=624451#post624451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it as a broader punishment. Spirits can't break their bans, but werewolves can. Second edition 'unihar' may be wolf-like Furies, spawned from the firstborn totems to harangue those who break their tribal oaths once too often. A fun part of that might be the varied kinds of unihar, representative of the different firstborn, and different methods with which they'd use to punish the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Headcanon accepted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T04:41:55-07:00","id":625301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=624451#post624451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it as a broader punishment. Spirits can't break their bans, but werewolves can. Second edition 'unihar' may be wolf-like Furies, spawned from the firstborn totems to harangue those who break their tribal oaths once too often. A fun part of that might be the varied kinds of unihar, representative of the different firstborn, and different methods with which they'd use to punish the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is awesome. I don't really have anything to add, but I want you to know I think this is a cool thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T06:52:46-07:00","id":625407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=624451#post624451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it as a broader punishment. Spirits can't break their bans, but werewolves can. Second edition 'unihar' may be wolf-like Furies, spawned from the firstborn totems to harangue those who break their tribal oaths once too often. A fun part of that might be the varied kinds of unihar, representative of the different firstborn, and different methods with which they'd use to punish the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div> And then, of course, there's the nightmarish creatures that howl their hunting call when someone breaks the Oath of the Moon badly enough that <b><i>Luna</i></b> notices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:50:10-07:00","id":633131,"title":"","content":"Just two for now.<br /> <br /> 1. If a werewolf went through a labyrinth and got lost, would they be able to 'track' themselves and find their way back to their starting point? If so, would you suggest any special modifiers other than the ones offered by the book? This is providing it is not some sort of mystically created labyrinth that befuddles and confuses.<br /> <br /> 2. Would you allow Command Artifice to attempt to work on an Angel of the God Machine? What about an unfleshed Promethean, one that is essentially a robot?<br /> <br /> For clarification's sake, 'This Facet targets a single technological device that the Uratha can perceive.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-20-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:11:37-07:00","id":633170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=633131#post633131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Would you allow Command Artifice to attempt to work on an Angel of the God Machine? What about an unfleshed Promethean, one that is essentially a robot?<br /> <br /> For clarification's sake, 'This Facet targets a single technological device that the Uratha can perceive.'</div> </div> </div> </div>You're targeting something that either is <i>not</i> a device or is from certain perspectives an <i>instrument of God.</i><br /> <br /> The most permissive I'd get for that would be prompting a Clash of Wills against its Resolve/Resistance + Rank/Azoth + 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T13:44:08-07:00","id":638317,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this has been addressed or not. Started running WoD for the first time and had a conflict. Player wolves encountered a vampire with vanish from the minds eye. What facet or gift will trigger a clash of wills? Most of the sensing powers for the hunt involve smell and general location. Will I have to break out blind-fighting type rules or is there something I'm missing that might illuminate the vampire with this power to the wolves?<br /> <br /> As a player in another wolf game I'm also curious how anyone catches a vampire with celerity. If he has at least a small repository of blood and takes off, he's well out of reach by a few rounds...didn't see a gift that would allow a match for speed apart from urhan interrupt (But that's only if you're close)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T15:25:39-07:00","id":638407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tulpa Theory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=638317#post638317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this has been addressed or not. Started running WoD for the first time and had a conflict. Player wolves encountered a vampire with vanish from the minds eye. What facet or gift will trigger a clash of wills? Most of the sensing powers for the hunt involve smell and general location. Will I have to break out blind-fighting type rules or is there something I'm missing that might illuminate the vampire with this power to the wolves?<br /> <br /> As a player in another wolf game I'm also curious how anyone catches a vampire with celerity. If he has at least a small repository of blood and takes off, he's well out of reach by a few rounds...didn't see a gift that would allow a match for speed apart from urhan interrupt (But that's only if you're close)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Obfuscation discipline I'm guessing you're referring to Cloak of Night, where the text describes it like so, 'He doesn't just fade into the background, he vanishes entirely. He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.' From that I'd direct you to Impossible Spoor, where it says, 'The Uratha's senses are attuned to unusual or otherwise impossible traces. The lingering photons disturbed by the prey's shadow; the slowly settling ripple of air currents disturbed by the prey; the electromagnetic handshake of the prey's smartphone with a wireless hotspot - all leave a trail this werewolf can follow.' It seems this is a direct counter to the invisibility. Otherwise you may have to rely on other senses and blind-fighting, and gifts that might make the vampire reveal themselves, like those inflicting Shadow Paranoia, or something like Heaven's Unleashed or Cloak of Mist and Haze, which would leave abundant signs of someone passing through. There's also things like Lore of the Land to pinpoint everyone in your area and Scent the Unnatural, which could be used to scent out the <i>use </i>of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> For Celerity Predator's Unmatched Pursuit, Heaven's Unleashed, a few other gifts that allow for increasing the speed of Uratha or decreasing the speed of their prey, but the easiest would be running in urshul. Worse comes to worse, whip out a map and use One Step Ahead. The speed increase of Celerity is not really something you're going to be going long distances with without a large Vitae reservoir, one Vitae only activates it for one turn.<br /> <br /> Try and keep in mind with fetishes anything is possible, and you aren't limited to the book's gifts, let alone the book's fetishes. Also sometimes you'll just have to hoof it. Let the vampire get away, you can pick up the scent when the sun rises.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T06:12:36-07:00","id":639002,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;You can run but you can't hide&quot; is pretty much the werewolf motto now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T06:22:03-07:00","id":639009,"title":"","content":"Pretty much the Werewolf's motto in 1st Edition too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:25:25-07:00","id":640204,"title":"","content":"Another quick question.<br /> <br /> I saw somewhere on this board that werewolves have a certain resistance to mundane sources of damage. I couldn't find it in my 2.0 book. Does anyone know if wolves take damage like normal humans (albeit with increased regen) or do they downgrade lethal to bashing like vamps or aggro to lethal (except in the case of banes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:48:31-07:00","id":640255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tulpa Theory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=640204#post640204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another quick question.<br /> <br /> I saw somewhere on this board that werewolves have a certain resistance to mundane sources of damage. I couldn't find it in my 2.0 book. Does anyone know if wolves take damage like normal humans (albeit with increased regen) or do they downgrade lethal to bashing like vamps or aggro to lethal (except in the case of banes)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's ever been the case in general. You can get natural armor in some of your forms using Merits, but there aren't any Merits that I'm aware of that will give your character special damage resistances across all forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:49:54-07:00","id":640258,"title":"","content":"They take lethal and bashing normally, because unlike vamps they still have working organs. The difference is that in the case of extreme trauma (getting hit by a train or blown up or whatever) the storyteller can decide that a normal human will take aggravated damage straight up. With werewolves, they can't. Also I think they're immune to the fighting styles that can cause aggravated as well, because it's not supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:50:49-07:00","id":640262,"title":"","content":"I think werewolves dont take aggravated damage from mundane sources, and that might be what you are referring to. I could be wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:52:43-07:00","id":640264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tulpa Theory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=640204#post640204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw somewhere on this board that werewolves have a certain resistance to mundane sources of damage. I couldn't find it in my 2.0 book. Does anyone know if wolves take damage like normal humans (albeit with increased regen) or do they downgrade lethal to bashing like vamps or aggro to lethal (except in the case of banes)</div> </div> </div> </div>P94, 'Aggravated Damage: Aggravated damage regenerates much slower, closer to the speed of human wounds. Uratha heal one point of aggravated damage every four days. Only silver and supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly. Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha. As such, most unwitting attackers must do enough lethal damage to cause it to \u201croll over\u201d into aggravated damage before it poses a real problem for werewolves.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:00:46-07:00","id":640379,"title":"","content":"Splendid. Thanks so much for the help all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:07:52-07:00","id":656001,"title":"","content":"What kinds of magical effects should Unchained work against?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:37:32-07:00","id":656037,"title":"","content":"Based on the fluff I'd say it required a sort of component, like a chain wrapping around you, or magic wrapping around you, but based on this part, 'another supernatural power that would bind or hold her' I'd just use it against anything that inhibits their physical movement.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T05:09:02-07:00","id":657662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=656037#post656037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the fluff I'd say it required a sort of component, like a chain wrapping around you, or magic wrapping around you, but based on this part, 'another supernatural power that would bind or hold her' I'd just use it against anything that inhibits their physical movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, add a fetish into the mix and it could work even with mind altering powers. Something something Lordy Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T06:40:29-07:00","id":657800,"title":"","content":"What about a mystically enforced command to stay still? Does that count as a magical binding or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:07:02-07:00","id":657827,"title":"","content":"In that case your mind is acting as the binding agent. Sure, why not, but I could also see requiring Ephsy's proposed fetish alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:25:10-07:00","id":657855,"title":"","content":"I don't know how I'd feel about using Unchained against a mental effect, even with a Fetish altering the power. Mostly because mind altering explicitly cuts out agency. Like, if you're being mentally forced to behave a certain way, are you going to have the motivation to fight against the compulsion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:34:13-07:00","id":657859,"title":"","content":"It's a reflexive action that acts to offer a Clash of Wills chance when you normally wouldn't get one.<br /> <br /> 'The People are not domesticated dogs to be chained or leashed. Nothing can contain their rage and might.'<br /> <br /> It's sort of an amped up but focused version of the +2 to resist you can get for using Willpower defensively against mental manipulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:26:15-07:00","id":658081,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which tribes would consider each major template their problem? I figure Storm Lords have a good claim to Sin-Eaters, based on the 'opinions&quot; sidebar, but some of the others don't neccesarily make as much sense to me. Would a Beast be a Bone Shadow's problem due to fear spirits, or a Meninna or Storm Lord's due to the Devouring aspect? Or some other third thing</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4252-christhestalker","name":"ChrisTheStalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:32:31-07:00","id":658107,"title":"","content":"I think the Iron Masters claim most of the human-based splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:47:09-07:00","id":658117,"title":"","content":"There is a lot of overlap. At first glance it's easy, vampires and mages for Iron Masters, Prometheans and sin-eaters for Storm Lords, Demons for Bone Shadows, etc<br /> <br /> But it goes deeper than that and I'm pretty sure it's why they don't do anything like locking them down to one tribal sacred prey. Looking at a mage, you see a person doing magic, and it's easy to think they're just a human with some powers. But they also have this attunement with the Supernal that makes them obsess over mysteries, which might fit a distant sort of Claimed or Ridden. I think you could easily justify having a belief where mages are werewolves who've sacrificed their wolf-soul for power, giving you werewolf hunters.<br /> <br /> Vampires are human-seeming, of course, so there's the Iron Masters. But they could be controlled by the strix, they're certainly animated by a foreign power, suggesting claiming or the hosts, and thus Storm Lords of Hunters in Darkness. As pointed out by one of the writers there are some legends where vampires and werewolves are the same thing, so you have Blood Talons, and it wouldn't be too hard to see them as spirits manifest, perhaps they're the rogue human spirits, able to survive manifested due to feasting on the blood of humanity.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are humanoid, they're trying to be human, so Iron Masters. But they're also corpses or objects animated by a foreign spark, which can lend itself to Storm Lords or Hunters in Darkness. Maybe they're the Life Hosts. Maybe they aren't corpses claimed by spirits, but spirits manifesting alongside a corpse, trying to become real like the Scavenger Wolf from Skinchangers, a spirit being that, jealous of werewolves and their ability to straddle both worlds, they're forging a way through influencing demiurges and putting on corpses and mud until they 'fit in,' so Bone Shadows.<br /> <br /> The overlap is there on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:47:15-07:00","id":658118,"title":"","content":"We actually very deliberately didn't say, because it depends on the situation on the ground. <br /> <br /> Like, does a pack consider vampires to be post-living humans, a weird form of Claimed, related to ghosts, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:38:48-07:00","id":658344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChrisTheStalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=658081#post658081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which tribes would consider each major template their problem? I figure Storm Lords have a good claim to Sin-Eaters, based on the 'opinions&quot; sidebar, but some of the others don't neccesarily make as much sense to me. Would a Beast be a Bone Shadow's problem due to fear spirits, or a Meninna or Storm Lord's due to the Devouring aspect? Or some other third thing</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Masters. Everything that is remotely linked to humanity, including Vampires, Mages, etc, fall under their purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:51:57-07:00","id":658355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=658344#post658344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iron Masters. Everything that is remotely linked to humanity, including Vampires, Mages, etc, fall under their purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood Talons must be quite shocked at this turn of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T18:10:35-07:00","id":658701,"title":"","content":"To be fair? I'd make different lodges for other specialized prey, not usually limited to specific tribes, with their own versions of the Siskur Dah, and accompanying benefits.<br /> <br /> Lodge of the Willow Branch? Immune to Vinculum and whose blood is actually toxic to vampires? Check.<br /> <br /> But that's because I've been modeling them like mystery cults.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-09-2015, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:06:18-07:00","id":660768,"title":"","content":"What ways currently exist to spend permanent Willpower Dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:20:35-07:00","id":660785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=660768#post660768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ways currently exist to spend permanent Willpower Dots?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In werewolf? None.<br /> <br /> Idigam can alter your stats so you have less but that's not really spending them. A totem might be able to give you an Attribute change that gives you a point of Willpower, and offending it or losing the totem would lose the point but, again, it really wouldn't be 'spent.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:41:12-07:00","id":664476,"title":"","content":"Used to be that you could spend WIllpower Dot to regenerate lost limbs. Not in 2nd Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:43:41-07:00","id":664477,"title":"","content":"I think they've gone the other way. Now you don't <i>need</i> to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:44:40-07:00","id":664478,"title":"","content":"No, that just happens now through regeneration, I believe. No willpower necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:25:05-07:00","id":671665,"title":"","content":"I was running a goof-off game with a friend of mine to get used to a variety of WoD games and I ran into a bizarre situation. Once again, this was a one-on-one game where we were both more or less messing around, so he was using a god-like spirit to attack the material realm using a royal avatar and I quickly made a pack of werewolves to go fight it, and they managed to kill the royal avatar.<br /> <br /> But it made me wonder some things that I've not found a rule for in the various books I've collected. The question is regarding discorporated, but not destroyed spirits.<br /> <br /> When they reappear after &quot;gaining&quot; 1 essence for each healthbox, does a spirit have the same essence they had when they discorporated, like hibernation? If it has 3 essence left and 10 corpus, it takes 10 days to reform and has 3 essence when it reforms, making it vulnerable to destruction? Is that how it works?<br /> <br /> My second question is, when a spirit reforms after being discorporated from sheer trauma, does it reappear at full health or does it still have some degree of damage?<br /> <br /> Example, if I've got a Ensir rank 3 with 10 corpus and 20 essence, and it takes 10 aggravated from a bane, it will discorporate but not die and discorporate with 10 essence left... When it reappears at a resonant location, what's its health and essence like?<br /> <br /> My last question is how this also applies to a royal avatar. I think, I remember, that gods can't appear in the material world at all so they'd have to use a royal avatar (not that it WOULD go beserk or that its reasonable for an ST to expect werewolves to outright go to war with a god...) but, if you defeat the royal avatar, what then? How does a god make a new avatar, and how long does it take? Could it make one immediately, or does it only have the one avatar and has to wait for that one to re-corporate over time like any other spirit below rank 6? Is it difficult for a god to make a royal avatar if it is destroyed instead of merely discorporated?<br /> <br /> I don't remember seeing any rules on this sort of thing (and probably for a very good reason, this was a ridiculous scenario), but I am curious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T03:45:07-07:00","id":671772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=671665#post671665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they reappear after &quot;gaining&quot; 1 essence for each healthbox, does a spirit have the same essence they had when they discorporated, like hibernation? If it has 3 essence left and 10 corpus, it takes 10 days to reform and has 3 essence when it reforms, making it vulnerable to destruction? Is that how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the spirit is gaining essence normally, and needs to spend one to wake up. So it should have essence equal to corpus-1. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=671665#post671665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second question is, when a spirit reforms after being discorporated from sheer trauma, does it reappear at full health or does it still have some degree of damage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically rebuilt it's body from scratch, so I'd say full health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T01:40:00-07:00","id":672999,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, this has to happen around sources that give the spirit appropriate essence. If there aren't any source available, the spirit will stick to slumber indefinitely. Then there's the fact that other spirits of the same inclinations would already be on the hunt for such sources. Discorporation isn't a pleasant, or safe experience.<br /> <br /> @Royal Avatar: A spirit capable of creating a Royal Avatar of himself likely has the ability as a numina or manifestation. If it wants to make another, it uses it again. No, Royal Avatars wouldn't normally reform like normal spirits, unless the sponsor of it has some compulsion to invest more on it. And while the likes of spirits such as Firstborns have essence enough to make several avatars, I doubt it'd allow them to drive more than one at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-21-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:24:51-07:00","id":673370,"title":"","content":"Interesting answers. A discorporated spirit cannot be hunted though can it? If a spirit is discorporated it can't undergo further harm for the time being (although indefinite hibernation would probably be a sort of hell few spirits might want either.)) I was trying to figure out whether or not the discorporation manifestation was really good, really obnoxious, or really desperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:42:49-07:00","id":673381,"title":"","content":"Is a desperate move. Is basically going into who knows how long a coma on your terms instead of facing sure destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:57:25-07:00","id":673419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=673370#post673370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A discorporated spirit cannot be hunted though can it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Discorporation treats the spirit as if it had 'died' by losing all its Corpus to lethal injury. On page 186, it explains that spirits that lose all their Corpus like that return to a safe place and turns Dormant, which page 184 states puts them into a Twilight state of hibernation.<br /> <br /> Providing you can find where they've run off to and effect Twilight you should be able to destroy them. Other spirits of similar umia can awaken them or feast upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-21-2015, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:06:27-07:00","id":673456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=673419#post673419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Discorporation treats the spirit as if it had 'died' by losing all its Corpus to lethal injury. On page 186, it explains that spirits that lose all their Corpus like that return to a safe place and turns Dormant, which page 184 states puts them into a Twilight state of hibernation.<br /> <br /> Providing you can find where they've run off to and effect Twilight you should be able to destroy them. Other spirits of similar umia can awaken them or feast upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they can be found, it is not a <i><b>Safe Place</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:37:15-07:00","id":677594,"title":"","content":"What options do werewolves have for long range attacks, official or homebrewed? Besides Fetishes powered by a Spirit with the Blast Numen, how else do werewolves deal with, say, bird and airplane spirits, or the occasional vampire who is good with Protean? They seem very focused on melee combat, but that's a given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:44:55-07:00","id":677608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=677594#post677594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What options do werewolves have for long range attacks, official or homebrewed? Besides Fetishes powered by a Spirit with the Blast Numen, how else do werewolves deal with, say, bird and airplane spirits, or the occasional vampire who is good with Protean? They seem very focused on melee combat, but that's a given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gift of the Elements, Fetishes, and guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T08:47:38-07:00","id":677659,"title":"","content":"They can also throw stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:48:11-07:00","id":677786,"title":"","content":"You could jump, too. Strength + Athletics, each success gives you a foot of lift. Predator's Unmatched Glory multiplies the result by your Glory. The distance isn't going to be that great but it could be enough for low-flying things.<br /> <br /> I'd say Grasp of the Howling Winds would work on a lot of things, too, depending on how they fly. And of course a plane spirit would likely be anchored to a plane, which you can bring down safely or not using Gifts of Technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:19:10-07:00","id":684106,"title":"","content":"I have a bunch of questions after re-reading my 2nd ed copy:<br /> <br /> 1) As Lunacy only affect those with Integrity, does that mean animals are also inmune? Cannot I freak out a guard dog by inflicting the Delusion Condition?<br /> <br /> 2) Can I inflict other Lunacy Conditions besides the base three with Gaze of the Moon (Change-Glory) like Awestruck (Glorious Lunacy) or Berserker (Raging Lunacy) if I have the required Gift and can pay both activation costs?<br /> <br /> 3) Can animals get the Moon Tainted Condition from Maw of Madness (Pack-Purity)? The wording says any living being not an Uratha, but as it turns those afected into Dalu I was doubtuful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:33:13-07:00","id":684113,"title":"","content":"1) I think turning yourself into a wolf the size of a horse would freak out the guard dog sufficiently without any mystical intervention required. <br /> <br /> 2) Depends whether &quot;guy using gaze of the moon&quot; counts as a form or not. I'd say go for it. More fun that way. <br /> <br /> \u200b3) Just apply the dalu modifiers to whatever creature get bitten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T03:40:26-07:00","id":684196,"title":"","content":"Just got the book, and I'm wondering what ways Werewolves have of affecting beings in Twilight. So far I've got Banes (including the sufficiently-high-Spirit-Rank &quot;all my attacks are Banes&quot; thing), the Bone Shadow Sacred Hunt, and the Twilight Purge rite (to make them manifest), plus the Barghest facet of the Gift of Death for ghosts. Is that the lot? Can other powers be used on Twilight spirits, since all werewolves can sense them, or do you need to be in the same phase?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:07:04-07:00","id":684240,"title":"","content":"I think anything non-physical should work fine. They're still there, you just can't <i>touch</i> them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:24:22-07:00","id":684248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=684106#post684106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a bunch of questions after re-reading my 2nd ed copy:<br /> <br /> 1) As Lunacy only affect those with Integrity, does that mean animals are also inmune? Cannot I freak out a guard dog by inflicting the Delusion Condition?<br /> <br /> 2) Can I inflict other Lunacy Conditions besides the base three with Gaze of the Moon (Change-Glory) like Awestruck (Glorious Lunacy) or Berserker (Raging Lunacy) if I have the required Gift and can pay both activation costs?<br /> <br /> 3) Can animals get the Moon Tainted Condition from Maw of Madness (Pack-Purity)? The wording says any living being not an Uratha, but as it turns those afected into Dalu I was doubtuful.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u200b don't have my book to hand but:<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, animals are immune.<br /> <br /> 2) No.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes. Apply the Dalu stat mods to the creature when it changes. It will look monstrously primeval/feral/plain fucking weird when it changes depending on the creature in question.<br /> <br /> For some reason I now have Dalu jellyfish in my head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:26:00-07:00","id":684249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=684196#post684196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got the book, and I'm wondering what ways Werewolves have of affecting beings in Twilight. So far I've got Banes (including the sufficiently-high-Spirit-Rank &quot;all my attacks are Banes&quot; thing), the Bone Shadow Sacred Hunt, and the Twilight Purge rite (to make them manifest), plus the Barghest facet of the Gift of Death for ghosts. Is that the lot? Can other powers be used on Twilight spirits, since all werewolves can sense them, or do you need to be in the same phase?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also fetishes like the Whisper Knife.<br /> <br /> \u200bPowers can be used on spirits in Twilight that the werewolf can sense, yes, though obviously the effects may be limited depending on the nature of the power. You can catch a Twilight spirit in Knotted Paths but chucking fire at it with the Gift of the Elementals won't help unless its Bane is fire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:59:15-07:00","id":684283,"title":"","content":"Awww <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, then. At least I have an official answer now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T05:33:22-07:00","id":684298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=684196#post684196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got the book, and I'm wondering what ways Werewolves have of affecting beings in Twilight. So far I've got Banes (including the sufficiently-high-Spirit-Rank &quot;all my attacks are Banes&quot; thing), the Bone Shadow Sacred Hunt, and the Twilight Purge rite (to make them manifest), plus the Barghest facet of the Gift of Death for ghosts. Is that the lot? Can other powers be used on Twilight spirits, since all werewolves can sense them, or do you need to be in the same phase?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Uratha's rank is sufficiently high, they can smack spirits around in twilight just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:50:53-07:00","id":684432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=684298#post684298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Uratha's rank is sufficiently high, they can smack spirits around in twilight just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I meant by 'the sufficiently-high-Spirit-Rank &quot;all my attacks are Banes&quot; thing'. :-)<br /> <br /> Useful, but limited to the smaller end of Spirits, though that Gift that gives you +2 Rank in a defined area is pretty helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:33:26-07:00","id":685568,"title":"","content":"Not really. Get an Ithaeur with Symbolic Focus and Predator's Presence and you can fuck up quite a bit of spirits up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:51:17-07:00","id":685589,"title":"","content":"Not that trying to fight a rank 6 spirit is a particularly good idea, most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:15:40-07:00","id":685614,"title":"","content":"Predator's Claim says, 'This can allow the Uratha\u2019s Spirit Rank to temporarily rise over 5, though she still cannot physically challenge spirits of Rank 6 or more.' Suggesting that the aggravated damage from spirit rank never applies to rank 6 or higher spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:49:47-07:00","id":685660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=685614#post685614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator's Claim says, 'This can allow the Uratha\u2019s Spirit Rank to temporarily rise over 5, though she still cannot physically challenge spirits of Rank 6 or more.' Suggesting that the aggravated damage from spirit rank never applies to rank 6 or higher spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you managed to stack to Rank 8, you certainly can do Agg damage to Rank 6 spirits.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Rank 6 spirits are above the 'stat level' of the game so it's not likely to help you very much if you try to go in for a straight-up fight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:57:59-07:00","id":685678,"title":"","content":"Interesting, thank you for clearing that up. It looks like by the books 8 is the highest you can get, with the Predator's Claim facet giving 2 and the Symbolic Focus condition giving 1, and obviously 5 being the natural cap via renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T07:38:37-07:00","id":685750,"title":"","content":"Well, any higher and they'd outrank <i>Luna, </i>which is a somewhat theologically troublesome position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:32:21-07:00","id":685910,"title":"","content":"My turn.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Moon:<ul><li>DO NOT EAT THE FLESH OF MAN OR WOLF</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Breaking Point towards Flesh:<ul><li>Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Breaking Point towards Spirit:<ul><li>Hunting humans or wolves for food (\u20132)</li> <li>Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence (\u20133)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So basically, if you eat a human, you have to roll for a Breaking Point for both Flesh <i>and</i> Spirit? Or is the&quot;hunting&quot; Breaking Point rolled, and then the &quot;Oath Breaker&quot; Breaking Point rolled after? What about in the case of &quot;eating flesh for essence&quot;? Does that mean that you roll both? Or does is being &quot;for essence&quot; overrule the violation of the Oath (for some random reason)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:47:36-07:00","id":685920,"title":"","content":"I just roll against spirit. Breaking the Oath is a catch all term for all the other tenets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T11:09:02-07:00","id":685971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=685920#post685920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just roll against spirit. Breaking the Oath is a catch all term for all the other tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you get to ignore one tenet and not the rest? Where is it spelled out that this is just a catch-all term that excludes the consumption of human and wolf flesh as a violation of the Oath? I mean, I support your ruling for simplicity's sake, but it seems more like a personal interpretation than anything supported by the RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T11:57:04-07:00","id":686026,"title":"","content":"Breaking points pile up. You roll for all that are applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T11:58:55-07:00","id":686027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=685971#post685971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you get to ignore one tenet and not the rest? Where is it spelled out that this is just a catch-all term that excludes the consumption of human and wolf flesh as a violation of the Oath? I mean, I support your ruling for simplicity's sake, but it seems more like a personal interpretation than anything supported by the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really written anywhere specifically, it's just the Occam's razor interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T11:59:01-07:00","id":686028,"title":"","content":"It probably helps that there's no penalty to having the breaking points like there are for mortals, just potentially where you end up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:06:33-07:00","id":686098,"title":"","content":"Well, I always interpreted the line that says eating human flesh for essence is &quot;always a Harmony breaking point toward the spirit&quot; meant that in this case the very spirit-like nature of the practice trumped any ties to the flesh it may have due to the oath. <br /> <br /> Though I guess rolling for both ways means that there's always a slightly greater chance of it pulling you away from harmony than towards it, which may be appealing to those who wish to discourage the practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T02:37:00-07:00","id":688030,"title":"","content":"couple of questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1- Elemental gift (purity) : which pool do I have to use to inflict damage? Presence+ Empathy + Purity? or are there any rules about fire damage in the gmc?<br /> <br /> 2- Twilight: To damage/find/see a spirit in twilight the only way is to have the glory facet of the death gift ? The rules about twilight are a little bit chaotic.<br /> <br /> 3- When an uratha expel a spirit from a body/object, the spirit is blasted in the shadow or in the twilight?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T03:05:25-07:00","id":688035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688030#post688030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1- Elemental gift (purity) : which pool do I have to use to inflict damage? Presence+ Empathy + Purity? or are there any rules about fire damage in the gmc?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the right dice pool. There <i>are</i> rules for fire damage in GMC. In Vampire the Requiem second edition, because it's one of their main weaknesses. Why they didn't put it it werewolf with all the fire powers as well is beyond me.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688030#post688030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Twilight: To damage/find/see a spirit in twilight the only way is to have the glory facet of the death gift ? The rules about twilight are a little bit chaotic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gift of death doesn't even work on spirits. It only affects ghosts. Werewolves have so many ways of affecting spirits it's not even funny. Check the page of this thread before this one. We literally just listed every method we could think of. They can see spirits in twilight innately, and if they have a high enough rank they can hit them too without any help.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688030#post688030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- When an uratha expel a spirit from a body/object, the spirit is blasted in the shadow or in the twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight. Unless they actually banished it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-04-2015, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T04:17:28-07:00","id":688121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688035#post688035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like the right dice pool. There <i>are</i> rules for fire damage in GMC. In Vampire the Requiem second edition, because it's one of their main weaknesses. Why they didn't put it it werewolf with all the fire powers as well is beyond me.<br /> <br /> The gift of death doesn't even work on spirits. It only affects ghosts. Werewolves have so many ways of affecting spirits it's not even funny. Check the page of this thread before this one. We literally just listed every method we could think of. They can see spirits in twilight innately, and if they have a high enough rank they can hit them too without any help.<br /> <br /> Twilight. Unless they actually banished it.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:19:22-07:00","id":688672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688035#post688035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gift of death doesn't even work on spirits. It only affects ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, it affects, 'ghosts, other disembodied undead or death-infused beings in Twilight.' This would also work against vampires using the fifth dot of Auspex, which allows them to astrally project. I'd consider a death spirit to be a death-infused being as well, providing it was in Twilight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:26:06-07:00","id":688681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688672#post688672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to clarify, it affects, 'ghosts, other disembodied undead or death-infused beings in Twilight.' This would also work against vampires using the fifth dot of Auspex, which allows them to astrally project. I'd consider a death spirit to be a death-infused being as well, providing it was in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yup. It would also tag mages who have used the Death Arcanum to enter Twilight, etc.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T15:25:08-07:00","id":688910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=688672#post688672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would also work against vampires using the fifth dot of Auspex, which allows them to astrally project.</div> </div> </div> </div>More specifically, it allows them to project their consciousness beyond their body in a Twilight state, which might be described as astral projection in modern parlance, but has nothing to do with the part of the WoD cosmology that Mages call the Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T17:08:20-07:00","id":689037,"title":"","content":"Question: Do/Must Lunes have a specific Ban and Bane? If not, recommendation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T17:47:50-07:00","id":689041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=689037#post689037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Do/Must Lunes have a specific Ban and Bane? If not, recommendation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all spirits have them. In first edition they were sort of all compiled into bans and are now sort of divided amongst bans, referring to behaviors they have to follow or avoid, and banes, more of a physical thing that harms them. Here's a compilation of Lune bans from the Predators book, p50 to 53.<br /> <br /> 'Cahalunim are vulnerable to silence, and lose much of their power in an area without ambient sound. Elunim can be weakened by light so bright that it casts no shadow, or darkness so complete that there is no light. Most Glimmerings are bound under a ban not to appear on moonless nights. Others are bound only to appear under a certain phase of the moon. Some Irralunim are bound to silence. Others cannot abide the presence of Helions or affect the physical world during daylight hours. The Ithalunim are commonly bound against freely giving information. Many Ralunim are incapable of lies. Others are bound to accept any challenge made to them.'<br /> <br /> There are others, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-04-2015, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T18:04:54-07:00","id":689062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=689041#post689041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, all spirits have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Tabanese has worded their question awkwardly; they're asking if Lunes have specific <i>blanket</i> bans and banes rather than being variable or individualized stress fractures in their ephemera, if I'm reading it correctly.<br /> <br /> Tabanese, as nofather's collation should hopefully make clear, there's no fixed set of weaknesses for Lunes, though there's an ample body of suggestions available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T04:33:46-07:00","id":689550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=689062#post689062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Tabanese has worded their question awkwardly</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I never! :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=689062#post689062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're asking if Lunes have specific <i>blanket</i> bans and banes rather than being variable or individualized stress fractures in their ephemera, if I'm reading it correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are indeed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=689062#post689062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tabanese, as nofather's collation should hopefully make clear, there's no fixed set of weaknesses for Lunes, though there's an ample body of suggestions available.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thank you both for the prompt answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:16:44-07:00","id":691776,"title":"","content":"Are there any means for spirits and other ephemeral beings to deal aggravated damage? Would there be anything wrong with homebrewing a Numen that lets them spend additional Essence + 1 willpower point to deal aggravated damage with Blasts and a melee weapon Numen? Should this power have a Rank prerequisite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:20:48-07:00","id":691778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=691776#post691776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any means for spirits and other ephemeral beings to deal aggravated damage? Would there be anything wrong with homebrewing a Numen that lets them spend additional Essence + 1 willpower point to deal aggravated damage with Blasts and a melee weapon Numen? Should this power have a Rank prerequisite?</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't think of any ways to do it by default. The reason *not* to do it is the Bane system which is such a significant element of the ephemeral beings system. A power that gives ephemeral beings a shortcut round such a key part of their interactions with each other is not a great idea; on a personal note, I also find 'deals Aggravated damage' powers to *mostly* be interminably dull.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:55:24-07:00","id":691793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=691778#post691778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I can't think of any ways to do it by default. The reason *not* to do it is the Bane system which is such a significant element of the ephemeral beings system. A power that gives ephemeral beings a shortcut round such a key part of their interactions with each other is not a great idea; on a personal note, I also find 'deals Aggravated damage' powers to *mostly* be interminably dull.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed, not to mention the rule which says ephemeral beings automatically deal aggravated damage to others of their kind which are 2 or more Ranks below them.<br /> <br /> What I wonder is if Rank 6+ entities can mimic the Practice Of Unraveling that mages use to deal aggravated damage. Imperial Mysteries says these godlike beings can mimic any of the Common Practices of any Arcanum, as long as the effect fits with the being's purview. I assume this property does not transfer to Royal Avatars, since they are &quot;only&quot; Rank 5.<br /> <br /> That being said, if a Numen that only upgrades the damage type of other Numina is uncreative, we could try to include the Bane system somehow. How about a Numen that lets spirits and other ephemerals absorb the Essence of an instance of an enemy's Bane? That would upgrade each point of lethal damage into aggravated per success on the Power + Finesse roll (caps at Rank x 2 and improves only one future attack). That is seen as subverting the hierarchy of spirits, and has a chance of turning the offender into a magath with a second purview based on the Bane it absorbed Essence from. So, a spirit would need to have ready access to said Bane and use this bad Numen repeatedly, thus increasing the chances that it will be caught and/or become a magath. A group of rebel spirits with this Numen could pose a threat to spirits of greater Rank, which adds a layer of suspense to spirit politics. Does this sound like a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-06-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T17:02:21-07:00","id":691799,"title":"","content":"Why would you want ephemeral entities to do aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not something you need to make a big deal about. 'Bam,' they do aggravated damage in your game. But why would you want that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T17:18:19-07:00","id":691806,"title":"","content":"Of course I forgot that I'm actually wrong - spirits do have one relatively easy source of Aggravated damage against other spirits, namely if they outrank the victim by at least 2 Ranks they are treated as the Bane of the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T17:29:36-07:00","id":691811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=691799#post691799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want ephemeral entities to do aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not something you need to make a big deal about. 'Bam,' they do aggravated damage in your game. But why would you want that?</div> </div> </div> </div> I just wanted some ephemerals to pose a threat to characters that easily protect themselves from or heal lethal damage (e.g. werewolves in Gauru form in 2ED and mages who stock up on Life spells and similar techniques). But that would cut through the rules as written in a way that disregards important parts of the setting. An easy way to mitigate this issue would be to rule that any power that deals aggravated damage cannot bypass Rank hierarchy. In other words, spirits could only use this hypothetical aggravated damage Numen on non spirits, but against others of their kind, it might give 9 Again on attack rolls. Is there anything potentially troublesome about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T18:09:03-07:00","id":691832,"title":"","content":"Considering the vast majority of ephemeral entities are only going to be having relevant combat with players, you're looking for a way to throw aggravated damage at player characters and potentially ending their lives because of one extra success or an exploding 10.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't even have to be high rank to easily push past the gauru health boxes and start chipping away at them with aggravated damage, and that's just doing lethal damage and relying on it wrapping around. Having them just dole out aggravated damage without using a bane like silver is going to lead to very short games and no one risking attacking spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T02:42:04-07:00","id":692171,"title":"","content":"Blast alone with sufficient essence expenditure is a losing proposition to most Uratha. Relatively minor spirits, in broods, all blasting a single target is equally deadly, if not more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:12:27-07:00","id":693912,"title":"","content":"Simple question: How do these Blood and Bone things work? It looks like they replaced Virtue and Vice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:16:08-07:00","id":693914,"title":"","content":"Yes. Although much like Mask and Dirge they can both function as either, depending on circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:32:04-07:00","id":693955,"title":"","content":"Blood is your basic instincts when you're incensed, what your first answer and attitude is when you switch to an active state.<br /> <br /> Bone is your calmer, more rational self, what you're inclined to do when you head reins everything else in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:15:18-07:00","id":693990,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Shaping Gift Facet, Perfection of Form. If it's used on a weapon, the equipment bonus is added to the attack roll, not as damage bonus, right? And it's still limited by the general rule that equipment bonuses don't get higher than 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-08-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:45:48-07:00","id":694013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=693990#post693990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Shaping Gift Facet, Perfection of Form. If it's used on a weapon, the equipment bonus is added to the attack roll, not as damage bonus, right? And it's still limited by the general rule that equipment bonuses don't get higher than 5?</div> </div> </div> </div> Re weapons: ...actually I'm not sure whether the damage of a weapon counts as an equipment bonus or not.<br /> <br /> Re equipment bonus cap: Correct.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T12:37:11-07:00","id":694143,"title":"","content":"The other mentions of equipment bonuses do seem to suggest it works for the attack roll, like with scopes and such, but there isn't a section that really describes equipment bonuses well. At least not in the core books.<br /> <br /> Another thing I wanted to ask, sort of gauging the waters opinion-wise.<br /> <br /> What would people think about a merit that allowed you to activate a Gift Facet for free? There would be a limit, probably it couldn't be more than 1 Essence. On one hand, Gifts seem to work a very clear way, you pour your Essence through them and out pops the effect, plus at least to me, the game has always been about the cost of things. Like, a really active wolf throwing around Gifts is going to in turn require more Essence, gained primarily through either draining loci or eating things. Both those things, as well as some of the other ways like devouring fetishes, have a sort of repercussion to them, and I could see 'free Gifts' as a sort of out with that. On the other hand I could see a werewolf focused to a certain degree sort of changing. The Firstborn aren't just spirits of wolves, they're spirits of other things. So I could see certain Gifts becoming extensions of a werewolf's natural ability.<br /> <br /> I really just ask because I enjoy permanent and passive Gifts a lot and find myself using Command Artifice all the time and was wondering what other people thought about the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T13:24:56-07:00","id":694162,"title":"","content":"All i can tell you is that if a st allowed me to get that merit i'd use it on berserkers might and i would be unstoppable. Its very exploitable when used on certain gifts, i think. Once per scene maybe? I dont have a problem conceptually though it seems very unnecessary when dedicated locus exists<br /> <br /> I also love the permanent facets, though so i feel you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 10-08-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T14:07:46-07:00","id":694186,"title":"","content":"I see what you mean. Though Berserker's Might already activates automatically and for free during death rages. Perhaps requiring an instant action for usage, rather than reflexive abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T14:30:29-07:00","id":694199,"title":"","content":"Re: weapons and equipment bonuses - I could have sworn I read somewhere that a weapon's damage rating can be used as an equipment bonus on appropriate rolls (like using a crowbar to open a door, or a machete to cut through brush). But I can't seem to find it in any of the core books. Maybe it was in Armory? Or one of the Hurt Locker previews?<br /> <br /> Anyway, a Crowbar is listed both as a weapon with a +2 damage rating and as physical equipment with a +2 equipment bonus. This bonus obviously doesn't apply to weaponry rolls made when you use the crowbar as a weapon. I don't know what the official RAI is, but my ruling would be that Perfection of Form on a crowbar would increase its equipment bonus on rolls like prying things open, but would not add to attack rolls or damage rating. I'd then apply that ruling consistently across all weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T14:39:51-07:00","id":694201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694199#post694199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: weapons and equipment bonuses - I could have sworn I read somewhere that a weapon's damage rating can be used as an equipment bonus on appropriate rolls (like using a crowbar to open a door, or a machete to cut through brush). But I can't seem to find it in any of the core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Werewolf it's on page 168.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:12:18-07:00","id":694295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694199#post694199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, a Crowbar is listed both as a weapon with a +2 damage rating and as physical equipment with a +2 equipment bonus. This bonus obviously doesn't apply to weaponry rolls made when you use the crowbar as a weapon. I don't know what the official RAI is, but my ruling would be that Perfection of Form on a crowbar would increase its equipment bonus on rolls like prying things open, but would not add to attack rolls or damage rating. I'd then apply that ruling consistently across all weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition, the 'damage' for weapons, which was really a part of your entire attack dicepool, was considered an equipment bonus. From World of Darkness, p160, 'So, if a small SMG (+2 equipment bonus) is used to fire a long burst (+3 bonus), a total of five extra dice is gained.' And in both editions, things like scopes could add an equipment bonus to the attack rolls of weapons that benefited from scopes. The God-Machine Chronicle, p199, ''If your character has a scope or similar that affects how likely he is to hit his target, add the equipment bonus of the scope to the attack pool. These modifiers are listed separately to the weapon\u2019s base damage.'<br /> <br /> But you suggest not allowing an equipment bonus on a weapon to have any affect on attack roll or damage? Would a gun gain an equipment bonus to intimidation but otherwise be the usual gun? And a sword the usual sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-08-2015, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:23:54-07:00","id":694308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694295#post694295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would a gun gain an equipment bonus to intimidation but otherwise be the usual gun? And a sword the usual sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are actually things I could genuinely see happening. Like if the sword or gun was really badass-looking but no more effective at actually killing stuff than a plain one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:57:07-07:00","id":694333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694308#post694308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are actually things I could genuinely see happening. Like if the sword or gun was really badass-looking but no more effective at actually killing stuff than a plain one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I got the intimidating gun thing from the section you pointed out. Alright, that's fair.<br /> <br /> The problem comes from the weapon I was referring to, however. Because it's a stake. I should have mentioned it in the first post but figured a weapon is a weapon and the specific weapon wouldn't matter. However, a stake exists to be shoved into something, that's about its only function. Whether it's holding down a tent or keeping a vampire paralyzed.<br /> <br /> So how does Perfection of Form affect a stake? Or is it still only usable to increase intimidation potential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-08-2015, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T23:06:28-07:00","id":694586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694333#post694333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I got the intimidating gun thing from the section you pointed out. Alright, that's fair.<br /> <br /> The problem comes from the weapon I was referring to, however. Because it's a stake. I should have mentioned it in the first post but figured a weapon is a weapon and the specific weapon wouldn't matter. However, a stake exists to be shoved into something, that's about its only function. Whether it's holding down a tent or keeping a vampire paralyzed.<br /> <br /> So how does Perfection of Form affect a stake? Or is it still only usable to increase intimidation potential?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things I would apply a Stakes equipment bonus to would include Intimidation rolls against Vampires, Survival rolls to create a shelter, Crafts rolls to prop or strut a structure or anything that might require driving a pilot hole... I'd be open to other suggestions from the player as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T04:58:10-07:00","id":694737,"title":"","content":"Wow, okay. Skip that facet then. Experience and Essence for a one time usage of a minor equipment bonus only applicable to things done better with other Gifts or a werewolf's natural abilities, no thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:05:02-07:00","id":694738,"title":"","content":"It can also be used to repair objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:09:21-07:00","id":694741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694738#post694738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can also be used to repair objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's definitely the way to go with it, though it seems like more of a secondary effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:16:08-07:00","id":694744,"title":"","content":"I actually see it the other way around. It is true that the way it is described seems like the repair part is a side effect, but I mostly see it a s the primary use (is very useful) and the increase in the tool bonus a nice additional thing fro when you use the power in an object that is already A-alrigth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:20:18-07:00","id":694745,"title":"","content":"I think if repairing items was meant to be its primary purpose it would probably mention that first, or have something like an Exceptional Success adds your Purity to the repair roll, instead of offering a 9 or 8 again for the item's usage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:58:34-07:00","id":694756,"title":"","content":"An exceptional success already has an enhanced effect for a repair - the greater number of points of damage fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:24:09-07:00","id":694785,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I didn't mean that the power's true main purpose was the repair and the bonus was a side effect. Is just why I would decide to get that Facet. There's a lot of tactical advantages to be able to repair something on the spot (keeping equipment at top function being the main one). Imagine holding a door shut to prevent some enemy to enter, they could attack the door, slowly damaging it to bring it down and then you just use the facet and make all their efforts be for naught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:39:43-07:00","id":694831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694737#post694737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, okay. Skip that facet then. Experience and Essence for a one time usage of a minor equipment bonus only applicable to things done better with other Gifts or a werewolf's natural abilities, no thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is just a case of the example item being a poor one. Imagine using it on cash, or contraband, or housing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:40:35-07:00","id":694833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694756#post694756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An exceptional success already has an enhanced effect for a repair - the greater number of points of damage fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but adding the relevant Renown as automatic successes seems like it would fit, and is a more 'common' bonus for them, like it is with Sculpt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694785#post694785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn't mean that the power's true main purpose was the repair and the bonus was a side effect. Is just why I would decide to get that Facet. There's a lot of tactical advantages to be able to repair something on the spot (keeping equipment at top function being the main one). Imagine holding a door shut to prevent some enemy to enter, they could attack the door, slowly damaging it to bring it down and then you just use the facet and make all their efforts be for naught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, yeah, I could see using it for repairs if I had, I guess, important fetishes people were trying to destroy. But considering how many ways werewolves have to easily destroy things you wouldn't be able to keep up repairing them against the force of another werewolf. Odds are if something isn't strong enough to break through a door, with its Durability of one and Structure of five, you're probably better off confronting it in combat rather than letting your Essence get chipped away through attrition. Plus with something like All Doors Locked you could just close all the doors with a thought except the ones leading you to wherever you want to go, while also closing and locking them securely behind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:40:50-07:00","id":694834,"title":"","content":"I ran into that issue once with a character trying to repair a door. The facet specifically targets &quot;single item that the Uratha is holding and which grants an equipment bonus.&quot; which unfortunately explicitly excludes repair to structure damage or a door or even a car, for example. Which is a shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:46:50-07:00","id":694847,"title":"","content":"The bonus is to keeping people out of a room. Think about it, if you were trying to keep people out just by standing in the door frame it would be much harder, wouldn't it? Ergo, equipment bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:48:05-07:00","id":694849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694831#post694831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is just a case of the example item being a poor one. Imagine using it on cash, or contraband, or housing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be an item you can hold which grants an equipment bonus, so housing is out. And since it's an object that requires an equipment bonus to begin with you're looking at, best case, turning a +1 bonus to a +5 for bribes, which can probably be done better with other Gifts, like Primal Allure.<br /> <br /> Oh right, and Amravanti just pointed out the door repair problem. But you could still use it to repair fetishes if someone was trying to break them for Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694847#post694847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bonus is to keeping people out of a room. Think about it, if you were trying to keep people out just by standing in the door frame it would be much harder, wouldn't it? Ergo, equipment bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emphasis was less on it requiring an equipment bonus and more on 'This Facet targets a single item that the Uratha is holding.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T06:52:04-07:00","id":694854,"title":"","content":"&quot;I <i>am </i>holding the door.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're holding it <i>shut.</i> That's not the same thing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:05:22-07:00","id":694871,"title":"","content":"Haha. Unfortunately my ST was not quite so liberal with his interpretations.<br /> <br /> I still like the facet, but it definitely is less broadly useful than a lot of other ones. The Shaping Gift in general has a lot of facets that reward creativity and outside the box thinking more than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:06:49-07:00","id":694876,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Moldywarp is surprisingly cool too. And I like Entropy's Howl because it lets you be Black Bolt. Or huff and puff and blow their house in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:18:01-07:00","id":694883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694876#post694876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or huff and puff and blow their house in.</div> </div> </div> </div> Entropy's Toll and Grasp of Howling Winds may in fact be references to the big bad wolf. May. I can neither confirm nor deny.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:23:11-07:00","id":694886,"title":"","content":"They're both great. I hope you don't see my commentary as bashing on the Gifts, I think I've made it clear I love the game, and the powers. But our pack is currently dealing with increasing numbers of vampires and we're going to hunt a bit and spend some Experience so I'm looking for an ability that can help deal with them. With my characters low Presence, Purity and Empathy and detachment to his spiritual side, Tongue of Flame doesn't seem like the best choice. Though he's been wildly erratic and impulsive, maybe fire would be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2015, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:15:42-07:00","id":694926,"title":"","content":"I'd increase the damage rating, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:17:36-07:00","id":694927,"title":"","content":"Deny Everything vs Scent Beneath the Surface:<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:29:55-07:00","id":694956,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. Scent Beneath lets you detect deceit, while Deny Everything lets you resist pressure and manipulation, they don't really act against each other.<br /> <br /> Context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:06:05-07:00","id":694972,"title":"","content":"I think he means during the activation roll for Scent Beneath? I don't think that facet in itself explicitly counts as &quot;A social maneuver or manipulation based action&quot; though as an ST I would probably allow it, but only because I think the facet (Deny Everything) is a bit weak and I'd be looking for ways to squeeze some use out of it for a player who chose it because of the spirit of the facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 10-09-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:17:53-07:00","id":694997,"title":"","content":"Scent Beneath The Surface is not a Social manouever and does not use Manipulation, so Deny Everything doesn't help against it by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:18:33-07:00","id":694998,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figure that if somebody activated Deny Everything against an Elodoth using Scent Beneath the Surface, it would prompt a Clash of Wills. I mean, it's not exactly a killer app. The Elodoth presumably would know something weird is happening when their truth sense &quot;bounced&quot; instead of returning a conclusive answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T14:29:25-07:00","id":695392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=694997#post694997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scent Beneath The Surface is not a Social manouever and does not use Manipulation, so Deny Everything doesn't help against it by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. But Deny Everything suffers already because Social Maneuvers have to abide by common sense already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T14:35:39-07:00","id":695394,"title":"","content":"I think it would work to defend against more overt mind control than just Social maneuvers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:54:16-07:00","id":695456,"title":"","content":"Quick question. How do you guys handle vampire abilities where resistance would usually be resolve with Lashing Out? Lashing out (From Requiem 2e) is pretty equivalent to werewolf's Hunter's Aspects and is sometimes the only way to resist a lot of effects of some powers. Should werewolves just be treated like humans in this regard?<br /> <br /> An example from the first dot of Majesty, Awe:<br /> <br /> &quot;With a word, he can summon anyone in the<br /> room to his side \u2014 not by any mystical compulsion, but by making<br /> her aware that he wants her to approach. Another vampire can<br /> fortify herself against Awe with her predatory aura (see Lashing<br /> Out, p. 92). If she succeeds, she is unaffected by Awe.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T18:19:02-07:00","id":695567,"title":"","content":"I believe Hunter's Aspect is meant to be the werewolf equivalent to Lashing Out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T18:26:32-07:00","id":695572,"title":"","content":"I do too, but I don't see it explicit anywhere as it is with Blood Potency/Primal Urge so I guess I just wanted to make sure other people saw it that way.<br /> <br /> Good to know I'm not the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 10-09-2015, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:12:25-07:00","id":696265,"title":"","content":"It seems thematically correct. I mean, power traits work cross-system with no clear justification other than that they are power traits. I'd endorse a motion to just use hunter aspects to full such a role in this case, even without an explicit ruling.<br /> <br /> QUESTION: How do animal spirits become a threat in the same way emotional ones do? If I understand it right, spirits feed off essence of a similar resonance and resonance is whatever is within their influence. So, while fear spirits could terrorize a school in order to feed, what can a cow spirit do? It can't make cows more cowish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:50:22-07:00","id":696345,"title":"","content":"Cow spirits? Over grazing. Damaging the ozone. I dont really know. Rat spirits for example, i can think of a lot negative fall out. Same for any predator or grazer in an eco system. Basically just upsetting balance. Domestic cattle might be a bit hard to find many major negative effects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:57:39-07:00","id":696358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=696265#post696265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">QUESTION: How do animal spirits become a threat in the same way emotional ones do? If I understand it right, spirits feed off essence of a similar resonance and resonance is whatever is within their influence. So, while fear spirits could terrorize a school in order to feed, what can a cow spirit do? It can't make cows more cowish.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a spirit of a cow claims or rides a cow it grants that cow supernatural backing. Millions are killed every year, this spirit may want to put an end to it, or speed up the process without concerning itself with the aftereffects, which are more for the human's benefit than the cows, and it has the numina and control to make that happen, at least on a smaller scale. On their own cows are docile creatures weighing over a thousand pounds. Put a spirit behind that and it's going to be doing whatever the spirit wants with that mass, including making it stronger and harder to destroy. Keep in mind a decent spirit would likely be able to influence a herd, and through the course of its rebellion may pick up some other attributes.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, do you have anyone you care about? Well, now they're lactating, eating grass, growing patchwork coloring and mooing all the time. Therapy and medication won't do anything and they're going to do it for the rest of their lives, which have been extended by magic. But they aren't killing anyone so who cares, right? It doesn't have to lead to the deaths of dozens to be bad.<br /> <br /> For other animals, see animal-related thrillers such as the Birds, Night of the Lepus, Willard or Ben, Frogs, Alligator one but not two, Razorback, Pig Hunt, and so on.<br /> <br /> All that said, many spirits are content just feeding off the Essence their physical reflection generates by merely existing. If the animal is associated with docility, like a cow, then the spirit will likely be a more docile one, content to graze at the cow Essence generated passively by the herd of cows in the real world being cows. So if it just wanted to feed, it would just stay parallel to a 'real' cow and eke out its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-10-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:10:28-07:00","id":696373,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's <i>cattle</i> spirits you need to watch out for. They've got a bit more bull in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:25:52-07:00","id":696384,"title":"","content":"In some places, the want of the cow may be considered more important. At the risk of making light of a horrible event, a cow spirit could really take advantage of <a href=\"http://www.aljazeera.com/news/2015/09/indian-mob-kills-man-cow-slaughter-rumour-150930193719666.html\" target=\"_blank\">this kind of situation</a>.<br /> <br /> I'm reading a story at the moment about the Heron King. Some man with a lackluster life decides to get away from it by bird watching. And after a while a heron sort of approaches him, gazes upon him with disdain, and announces it disapproves of his skulking by its lake, and if he wants to keep his eyes, he will show proper respect to the Heron King. He's torn between believing he's imagined it all or met a sort of bird god. The next time he comes he acts respectful, and asks if he can speak with it more. He makes a mistake of referring to the other herons at the lake as the King's servants or vassals, whereupon the Heron King grows angry and threatening, explaining that they are all a Heron King, and their kingdoms move with them, and insulting one by considering it 'lesser' insults them all and I'm getting off track.<br /> <br /> That sort of interaction I could see happening from a benign spirit and a human. They like their worship and adulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:35:42-07:00","id":696388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=696373#post696373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's <i>cattle</i> spirits you need to watch out for. They've got a bit more bull in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me more about these cattle spirits; is it a matter of rank?<br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> Thank you for the detailed answer nofather. Couple of follow up questions, mostly for clarity.<br /> <br /> 1) 'Millions are killed every year, this spirit may want to put an end to it, or speed up the process without concerning itself with the aftereffects, which are more for the human's benefit than the cows, and it has the numina and control to make that happen, at least on a smaller scale.' So animal spirits do have these sort of strategic interests then? I was wondering how/why a spirit would go from absorbing the essence of cows to upsetting the balance, and a factor of my confusion was that I supposed the spirit would be too self-interest to do actions that didn't give instant essence. I assumed you'd need a magath to overcome this; it gained some complexity from the combined resonant and thus formed more complex plans.<br /> <br /> 2) 'Alternatively, do you have anyone you care about? Well, now they're lactating, eating grass, growing patchwork coloring and mooing all the time.' Wait... so animal spirits might try to turn others into their resonant animal? Is that 'normal' or a story-hook?<br /> <br /> 3) 'So if it just wanted to feed, it would just stay parallel to a 'real' cow and eke out its existence.' Which is why I couldn't fathom animal spirits as antagonists. They seem the most natural, non-threatening spirits out there. What stops a spirit eking out an existence and down the path of creating it?<br /> <br /> Thank you again for the help and movie recommendations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:53:20-07:00","id":696404,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember is that spirits, especially the higher-ranked ones, are <i>individuals. </i>So yeah, most of them are harmless, they do their thing and werewolves leave them alone. But not all of them are content to do this. All it takes is one to come up with some harebrained scheme for extra essence and suddenly everything goes out of whack.<br /> <br /> Or maybe a cow spirit gets in a slaughterhouse and starts eating death and slaughter spirits and becomes a cow/death magath. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T13:18:59-07:00","id":696451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=696388#post696388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) 'Millions are killed every year, this spirit may want to put an end to it, or speed up the process without concerning itself with the aftereffects, which are more for the human's benefit than the cows, and it has the numina and control to make that happen, at least on a smaller scale.' So animal spirits do have these sort of strategic interests then? I was wondering how/why a spirit would go from absorbing the essence of cows to upsetting the balance, and a factor of my confusion was that I supposed the spirit would be too self-interest to do actions that didn't give instant essence. I assumed you'd need a magath to overcome this; it gained some complexity from the combined resonant and thus formed more complex plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor spirits, like ranks one and two, are more comparable to animals and children. So a rank two spirit might be more impulsive and thoughtless about what it wants, but it likely doesn't have much more of a base desire beyond 'more Essence now,' which keep in mind means it can be predatory, as a way of getting Essence is to rip it out of lesser cow spirits. Once you get higher ranks you have more intricacy of thought. It's still all about Essence, but they are more unique, likely have more than one source of Essence, get into the spirit politics, might even be a patron of a werewolf pack. I think they get coo. Using those two examples, you have a regular cow spirit, that wants 'cow Essence,' and doesn't like the slaughter of cows as it lessens its reservoir of Essence. It may attempt to do something to change that on its own, knock off some rival spirits so it has the feeding ground to itself, or demand a tithe from lesser spirits. The second one is a cow spirit more associated with the slaughter. Through its evolution it's become firmly entrenched in the idea that slaughter is the natural apex of the cow life cycle, granting it a dot of Slaughter Influence. I don't think this would be considered a magath, necessarily, as in its location that is how the world works. But, say, for whatever reason less cows are being slaughtered, not feeding that part of it. It could use its influence and power to make the cows slaughter each other, or to wander off into the road to get hit by passing vehicles, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) 'Alternatively, do you have anyone you care about? Well, now they're lactating, eating grass, growing patchwork coloring and mooing all the time.' Wait... so animal spirits might try to turn others into their resonant animal? Is that 'normal' or a story-hook? </div> </div> </div>Under Claimed, from the second edition book, p191, 'The host's physical form begins to mutate, taking on an appearance influenced by the original host and the spirit.'<br /> <br /> Most cow spirits are going to be near the cows they're associated with, but shit happens. I was imagining a cow spirit associated with milk that sort of wandered to the dairy and then found its way to a carton of milk in someone's fridge and, realizing it was going to lose its Essence once that carton was emptied, decided to do something about it. People being claimed is a normal story hook, but I and I imagine other storytellers would come up with something more striking than a cow Claiming. That actually seems like it would fit more in hunter, with them wondering what to do about it. Either way, the World of Darkness is pretty weird like that, and I figure there's a lot of small, sad stories going on being overshadowed by the cooler stuff Storytellers get their players involved with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) 'So if it just wanted to feed, it would just stay parallel to a 'real' cow and eke out its existence.' Which is why I couldn't fathom animal spirits as antagonists. They seem the most natural, non-threatening spirits out there. What stops a spirit eking out an existence and down the path of creating it? </div> </div> </div>Need. If its food source is running out. The desire for more, if there's too much competition. Most spirits want to cross over because in the Hisil they are more dependent on whatever happens in the real world. If they cross over, they can attempt to do something about it. Think of a fish in a fish tank. On the other side of the Gauntlet there's a fish spirit, maybe it has some residual power from when it was 'in the wild,' but now it's all alone, and it'll likely waste away once the physical version dies. So if it reaches across and throws around some influence, strengthening its owners enjoyment of fish whenever they look at the tank, it can try and get them to get more fish for the tank. Suddenly it has more Essence. But the Gauntlet is thick here and still very little Essence comes through. So it reaches across and fetters itself to the fish, reaping the Essence where it's fresh and using that to get more ways to get Essence.<br /> <br /> The real world offers more opportunities for unfiltered Essence, and riding, urging and claiming all offer opportunities to make more sources of unfiltered Essence, all with less competition than there is in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> You might check out the first edition Werewolf book, Predators. Mechanically it needs tweaks to fit in with the new mechanics of second edition, but the explanations for how everything works are great. It also has essentially a bestiary of a wide variety of spirits.<br /> <br /> Hope you like the movies. I particularly recommend Willard and the Birds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T13:36:58-07:00","id":696460,"title":"","content":"Once again, big thank you for the posts! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll be on my merry little way now. I need to figure out how to shoehorn a deadly cow spirit into my current chronicle, as there is no way I'm wasting the vivid imagery you've inspired. Or maybe a fish. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T14:21:29-07:00","id":696491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=696373#post696373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's <i>cattle</i> spirits you need to watch out for. They've got a bit more bull in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, cattle spirit... <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://classic.battle.net/images/battle/diablo2exp/images/animations/bestiary/hellbovine.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:08:49-07:00","id":696675,"title":"","content":"Oh god, the flashbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T20:30:02-07:00","id":696760,"title":"","content":"Re: cow spirits: I've said it before in a different context and I'll say it again in this one: magic <i>leaks.</i> It bleeds into its surroundings.<br /> <br /> That hart-spirit in Book of Spirits offers the example of local tree-spirits having branches that look like its horns, and broadly speaking the trouble with resonance is that it's not naturally self-regulating in fashions that aren't hazardous to the stuff you want kept a particular way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T15:57:15-07:00","id":698034,"title":"","content":"Thank God they released the essence shaper merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:39:57-07:00","id":698727,"title":"","content":"Hey, here's a question: Can Reflected Facets stack? Say a bunch of werewolves know both that facet and Primal Strength, and they all try to grant their strength bonus to the same target, what happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:53:03-07:00","id":698762,"title":"","content":"Since the gift says that a facet cannot be activated while it is already in use, I'd say no. <br /> <br /> So you can't buff a single guy multiple times. Because technically when one pack member uses his facet the next one can't use hers because that gift facet is already in effect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T11:15:03-07:00","id":698786,"title":"","content":"I read that as saying that a single <i>copy</i> of a facet can't buff more than one person at a time. You activate it for yourself, but then you displace the <i>effect.</i> And then you can't use it again because it's already &quot;on&quot;. <br /> <br /> It says nothing whatsoever about what <i>another</i> werewolf can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T11:23:27-07:00","id":698816,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would stack, I think it would overlap. The facet adds your Purity Renown to your Strength. If you just have 1 Purity, it only adds 1 Strength, no matter how many times it's used.<br /> <br /> If the Reflected facet works off the activator's scores, giving the contributor's Purity in Strength to the target, I think it would still only take the highest Purity value.<br /> <br /> I'll point out that for all the Gifts that can be used in one way but is limited in another, there's also a three dot fetish that can allow it to break past those limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-12-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T12:46:15-07:00","id":698894,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was what I was thinking the alternative would be. It's how mage works, after all. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like it. Werewolf is a game that heavily promotes teamwork, and the Pack gift is a crucial chunk of that. Nerfing the &quot;All your powers combined&quot; facet in such a way almost feels like a betrayal of concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T13:13:15-07:00","id":698904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=698894#post698894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nerfing the &quot;All your powers combined&quot; facet in such a way almost feels like a betrayal of concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't rightly call &quot;abuse the 'lend your powers to teammates who don't have the same powers' power to double up on tricks you all know&quot; something that's <i>within</i> concept for &quot;all your powers combined&quot; to begin with. The point of the pack is to cover your bases, not consolidate a giant beatstick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T13:19:23-07:00","id":698907,"title":"","content":"To be fair, one person getting all the power isn't exactly about teamwork, either.<br /> <br /> There is probably another ability that is worded in a way that would let it happen, but even without it, you could have the other members of the pack use Reflect give to give one member everything. Primal Strength, Predator's Unmatched Pursuit, Running Silent and the Hunter Waits can make one of those werewolves terrifying. If you had a locus or surfeit of essence each member could give those abilities to everyone else, making an already scary pack even moreso. Since it doesn't seem limited to Shadow gifts, you could even load up a team with Auspice gifts like Killer Instinct and Bloody-Handed Hunter, which would 'stack' with Primal Strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:18:30-07:00","id":698966,"title":"","content":"Alright, say instead of Primal Strength, it's an unusually Rahu-heavy pack trying to use multiple copies of Crimson Spasm on the same guy. Now, by the mage stacking rules, that should work so long as each contributor boosts a different attribute, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:35:38-07:00","id":698978,"title":"","content":"Yes. Though I think the single person would then have to pay the upkeep on the multiple versions of the Gift, costing 4 Essence per turn.<br /> <br /> And, obviously, if you have a group of four werewolves with Crimson Spasm you're better off having them use it on themselves, rather than beefing up one person. Economy of action, and all, no matter how powerful an individual is they have one attack. Four werewolves have four attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:51:43-07:00","id":698990,"title":"","content":"Yeah, admittedly that one was solidly into &quot;dumb thought experiment&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> Although I'm not entirely sure one person would need to pay all the upkeep. The facet very specifically says the <i>effect</i> of the gift is transferred. Nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T16:19:13-07:00","id":703929,"title":"","content":"Will Werewolf be getting a printable ST screen soon? (in the next few months)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","name":"ShadowJakkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T05:12:36-07:00","id":704694,"title":"","content":"How and when do the Tilts Leg or Arm Wrack resolve when inflicted through Facets that cause no damage, like Butchery that can apply the Tilt to an <i>attacker </i>when it hits the Rahu?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T06:19:41-07:00","id":704758,"title":"","content":"I'd go by the end of the scene. It's a good benchmark. Or, in the Rahu's case, a number of turns equal to his Purity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 10-17-2015, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:06:37-07:00","id":704906,"title":"","content":"Either of those sounds reasonable, thanks, Ephsy<br /> <br /> What about the Poison Tilt suffered as part of the Moon Taint Condition? Would it be considered Moderate or Grave? I err on the side of considering it Moderate, more like a mild malaise while you don't trigger the change than anything else, but what do other people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:57:31-07:00","id":705067,"title":"","content":"It probably should be moderate as the intended victim is likely a normal human. Grave would probably reduce the odds of anyone surviving the poison effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:29:29-07:00","id":705141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=705067#post705067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably should be moderate as the intended victim is likely a normal human. Grave would probably reduce the odds of anyone surviving the poison effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bigger concern comes with figuring out how to do poison outside of combat in 2E. There's no guideline for which poison/toxin to pick from the 1E core book, and no poisons at all in any of the 2E cores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:43:01-07:00","id":705161,"title":"","content":"As per the writting in the Tilt, you don't really need to worry about out of combat effects if you don't want to. I wouldn't. If I had to, Maybe Toxicity equal to Purity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:44:59-07:00","id":705169,"title":"","content":"Sounds fair!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T09:08:35-07:00","id":705198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=705161#post705161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the writting in the Tilt, you don't really need to worry about out of combat effects if you don't want to. I wouldn't. If I had to, Maybe Toxicity equal to Purity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I <i>do</i> want to. But Toxicity = Purity sounds like a great idea. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T06:53:59-07:00","id":706718,"title":"","content":"totem question:<br /> <br /> Totem Points Advantage<br /> 1-8 One Experiences<br /> 9-14 Three Experiences<br /> 15-20 Five Experiences<br /> 20+ Ten Experiences<br /> <br /> The pack start with a 21 point-totem.<br /> what happens if some characters adds dots to the totem merits with experience points reaching more than 20+ to the total?<br /> Only the totem will become more powerful? or they will gain new experience points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-18-2015, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T07:07:55-07:00","id":706744,"title":"","content":"Only the totem gets more attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T00:39:27-07:00","id":708324,"title":"","content":"So, in other thread people told me, that werewolves can inflict aggravated damage for some supernatural beings by devouring. But for whom exactly? As I get it: for mages and hunters - completely YES, for vampires, Prometheans and, may be changelings - completely NO. What about sin-eaters, beasts and demons?<br /> P.S. I'd really prefer that werewolves inflict aggrav to vampire and for no one else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T00:49:29-07:00","id":708328,"title":"","content":"Idle spirit ecology question for the room:<br /> <br /> At what point does a spirit start to get into politicking (Essence tithes, etc) over direct predation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:09:44-07:00","id":708367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=708324#post708324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in other thread people told me, that werewolves can inflict aggravated damage for some supernatural beings by devouring. But for whom exactly? As I get it: for mages and hunters - completely YES, for vampires, Prometheans and, may be changelings - completely NO. What about sin-eaters, beasts and demons?<br /> P.S. I'd really prefer that werewolves inflict aggrav to vampire and for no one else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves inflict aggravated damage when they devour flesh for Essence. According to the rules, this is possible on wolves, werewolves and humans. It doesn't say anything about other supernaturals, but some people agree that it should work on any supernatural that still has essentially human flesh. I'd say it doesn't work on vampires, prometheans and mummies. It would work on demons unless they fail to Spoof. I can't say whether it would work on Changelings, as that would depend on how the Mask and Mien interact in second edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=708328#post708328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle spirit ecology question for the room:<br /> <br /> At what point does a spirit start to get into politicking (Essence tithes, etc) over direct predation?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Werewolf 2nd Edition, p. 180, spirit politics starts at rank 3 for most spirits. Rank 1 and rank 2 spirits can participate, but aren't full participants, being the equivalents of animals and children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:29:01-07:00","id":708396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=708367#post708367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Werewolf 2nd Edition, p. 180, spirit politics starts at rank 3 for most spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the Rank-based tendency and was more curious about the environment or stimuli that prompt the shift from viewing lesser spirits as food to treating them as lackeys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T02:39:12-07:00","id":708459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=708396#post708396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of the Rank-based tendency and was more curious about the environment or stimuli that prompt the shift from viewing lesser spirits as food to treating them as lackeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have expected you to be aware of that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is a very good question.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I need to note that I think a spirit could still eat its lessers, while trying to engage politically with its superiors. Then, for a spirit to engage in political behavior, it has to be in a situation where political behavior has greater benefit than predatory behavior at least of of the time, and of course it has to realize this, which depends on rank and type of spirit.<br /> <br /> An environment where hunting for food is really dangerous could spur political interaction at an earlier rank, weeding out those who can't manage that. An environment with stronger political benefits than average could do the same. I'm not sure whether environment or stimuli would actually prompt this shift you mentioned, or whether they would just let those who don't make the shift be eaten by those who do, leaving only politically oriented spirits.<br /> <br /> If I have more time, I'll try to think about more circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T02:53:26-07:00","id":708466,"title":"","content":"At high rank, a spirit might be disinclined to kill another because they want to eat it, but they might still eat it because they want to kill it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T03:40:53-07:00","id":708480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=704906#post704906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either of those sounds reasonable, thanks, Ephsy<br /> <br /> What about the Poison Tilt suffered as part of the Moon Taint Condition? Would it be considered Moderate or Grave? I err on the side of considering it Moderate, more like a mild malaise while you don't trigger the change than anything else, but what do other people think?</div> </div> </div> </div> If I remember correctly, the original draft had it be the Sickened Tilt rather than Poisoned; Sick seems to have been cut from the final edit for some reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T03:57:37-07:00","id":708492,"title":"","content":"I suspected as much, but the wording was clear. Sickened makes more sense, but then again there's still two tiers of it. The moderate one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T04:11:41-07:00","id":708501,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the moderate one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:10:06-07:00","id":710850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=708459#post708459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should have expected you to be aware of that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is a very good question.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I need to note that I think a spirit could still eat its lessers, while trying to engage politically with its superiors. Then, for a spirit to engage in political behavior, it has to be in a situation where political behavior has greater benefit than predatory behavior at least of of the time, and of course it has to realize this, which depends on rank and type of spirit.<br /> <br /> An environment where hunting for food is really dangerous could spur political interaction at an earlier rank, weeding out those who can't manage that. An environment with stronger political benefits than average could do the same. I'm not sure whether environment or stimuli would actually prompt this shift you mentioned, or whether they would just let those who don't make the shift be eaten by those who do, leaving only politically oriented spirits.<br /> <br /> If I have more time, I'll try to think about more circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>One key thing of spirit politics that people seem to forget is the broods. Groups of spirits that do not correspond to the same Umia but that can compliment each other to feed themselves better without the worry of being eaten when you're no longer useful (exceptions may apply). A spirit of murder, another of terror and a death spirit, for example. Each other's activities feed upon them. A spirit court is basically this with dozens if not hundreds of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T14:51:15-07:00","id":711262,"title":"","content":"I'm in gauru form and I take 8 point of lethal damage.<br /> Do I have to roll stamina for unconsciousness even if the next turn I'll heal every damage?<br /> Or do I have to roll for basu im?<br /> <br /> Don't know if this rule is changed from the first ed to god machine. Maybe it was removed and the ''exceed size'' rule is only to cause tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-20-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:03:51-07:00","id":711297,"title":"","content":"The exact wording given in the book is: &quot;A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I'd say no. I think the roll is supposed to take place at the beginning of the turn you want to act on anyway, so the healing would happen first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:08:54-07:00","id":711313,"title":"","content":"but, a gauru could be stunned anyway right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:12:51-07:00","id":711323,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that should work. Of course, it goes off size and has to be a single attack, so it's not exactly <i>easy...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T06:33:42-07:00","id":712330,"title":"","content":"How can an Uratha learn a second Moon's Gift?<br /> <br /> The rule-book states on P.114: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift.</span></span></div> <br /> But there is only one Moon gift per Auspice .... besides when looking at Moon Gifts themselves, they each state that they are only available to their corresponding Auspice.<br /> So ... can you or can't you?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4151-zeruul","name":"Zeruul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T06:51:26-07:00","id":712340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeruul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=712330#post712330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can an Uratha learn a second Moon's Gift?<br /> <br /> The rule-book states on P.114:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift.</span></span></div><br /> But there is only one Moon gift per Auspice .... besides when looking at Moon Gifts themselves, they each state that they are only available to their corresponding Auspice.<br /> So ... can you or can't you?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably supplements will introduce more Moon Gifts associated with the auspices, like in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:00:32-07:00","id":712353,"title":"","content":"Future Proofing!<br /> <br /> Also the Renown gifts in Lore of the Forsaken (I think?) work almost exactly like 2e moon gifts so you could also use those if you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:18:08-07:00","id":712365,"title":"","content":"Yup, future proofing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:17:16-07:00","id":712565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=712365#post712365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, future proofing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah! good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4151-zeruul","name":"Zeruul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:20:35-07:00","id":713357,"title":"","content":"How much essence per turn can a spirit spend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:38:29-07:00","id":713384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=713357#post713357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much essence per turn can a spirit spend?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good question. My gut says to use Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T20:10:52-07:00","id":713578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=713357#post713357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much essence per turn can a spirit spend?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as is permitted by the action they're taking and their maximum capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T20:27:22-07:00","id":713606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=713578#post713578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as is permitted by the action they're taking and their maximum capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a spirit with 18 essence could spend all 18 in a turn, provided it's for something (Like Blast?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T20:46:47-07:00","id":713634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=713606#post713606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, a spirit with 18 essence could spend all 18 in a turn, provided it's for something (Like Blast?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, though Blast and Trait-boosting are the only two things I can think of with a variable Essence cost and both of those are capped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:49:09-07:00","id":714777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=713384#post713384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a good question. My gut says to use Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be Rank +2 Essence Expenditure in 1st Edition, if I remember correctly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:53:37-07:00","id":714785,"title":"","content":"In order for Blast to work as-written the 2e cap needs to be rank x 2 at the very least. I think it is indeed theoretically unlimited, but the available powers put a definite cap on how much a spirit can actually use at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:07:33-07:00","id":714797,"title":"","content":"Blast has always bothered me. My character got nailed with it a couple times for stupid reasons.<br /> <br /> So I just want to be clear. The activation roll is Power + Finesse. Successes are, effectively, Lethal damage, right? It acts as a +0L weapon.<br /> <br /> From there, you can spend 2 Essence to 'increase the lethality of its Blast,' that adds +1L to it, essentially adding successes to an already successful roll.<br /> <br /> But, 'The maximum weapon bonus is equal to the spirit's Rank.' This refers to the spending 2 Essence to add +1L to the blast, but not the activation roll-to-damage part, right?<br /> <br /> So the Sparkblood Seneschal, on page 202 has Power 12 and Finesse 10, giving its Blast a dicepool of 22. Once activated, if it wanted, it could add +1L 'successes' for 2 Essence a pop, but only 4 successes, as it is Rank 4.<br /> <br /> That's all correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-22-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:10:30-07:00","id":714802,"title":"","content":"Sounds right. But the lethal damage you pay for is a weapon bonus. It only counts if it hits, and I'm fairly sure you need to spend it before you roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:14:20-07:00","id":714806,"title":"","content":"Okay, that makes sense. It has the potential to be wicked powerful. My character was nailed upon entering a room and wasted a round using a Gift to turn on the lights, was half-full of aggravated damage before I even knew what was going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:04:56-07:00","id":715032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=714806#post714806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that makes sense. It has the potential to be wicked powerful. My character was nailed upon entering a room and wasted a round using a Gift to turn on the lights, was half-full of aggravated damage before I even knew what was going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but that Blasting for all it can takes 9 freakin' essence. That's a bit too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:43:57-07:00","id":715085,"title":"","content":"That's just if you add the weapon damage. If you have a hefty enough dicepool like the Seneschal, you can probably just bet on chance. I think you have a good chance to get at least seven successes, which is a lot of damage that can't be avoided, though it can be soaked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T13:38:44-07:00","id":715341,"title":"","content":"Hit &amp; Run and Chase-Down begs to differ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T14:00:04-07:00","id":715403,"title":"","content":"Those don't so much avoid it as interrupt or delay it.. But okay. It's a lot of damage that require a specific set of circumstances to be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T17:22:18-07:00","id":716326,"title":"","content":"You know that the interrupt can go like &quot;I move out of the way before that shit owns me&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T18:21:12-07:00","id":716582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=716326#post716326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that the interrupt can go like &quot;I move out of the way before that shit owns me&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss the part where the range is in Power x 10 yards, and the Seneschal's Blast has a range of 120 yards? It is well beyond the distance most werewolves will be able to travel in a round in which they activate those abilities.<br /> <br /> In case you want to point out that the character might be 119 yards away, file that under 'specific set of circumstances.' In case you want to point out that werewolves can use that time to activate a gift that allows them to teleport, file that under 'specific set of circumstances.' In case you want to repeat, again, your belief that these interrupts act to avoid it, file the idea that the werewolf has Hit and Run under, 'a specific set of circumstances.' If you want to point out the fact that every werewolf can use urhan's interrupt in case a spirit uses this, keep in mind that it does nothing to stop the ability from activating unless the werewolf is able to, somehow, destroy the spirit in that one attack they get that turn. Which you can consider a 'specific set of circumstances.' In case you want to point out that, if they use a certain fighting style and aren't limited to one attack in a turn, fine, in 'the one attack they <i>likely</i> get that turn.'<br /> <br /> I'm surprised you didn't mention Fog of War. That could be used to actively avoid the attack. Though it requires the specific set of circumstances where there is chaos enough that the attack could conceivably hit someone else.<br /> <br /> Should I make it simpler, then?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">'That's just if you add the weapon damage. If you have a hefty enough dicepool like the Seneschal, you can probably just bet on chance. I think you have a good chance to get at least seven successes, which is a lot of damage in an attack where your Defense, Ephsy, doesn't mean anything, though it can be soaked.'</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T20:15:05-07:00","id":717042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=716582#post716582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you miss the part where the range is in Power x 10 yards, and the Seneschal's Blast has a range of 120 yards? It is well beyond the distance most werewolves will be able to travel in a round in which they activate those abilities.<br /> <br /> In case you want to point out that the character might be 119 yards away, file that under 'specific set of circumstances.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Calling foul on this because cover is a thing and even the most physically incompetent werewolf can run 24 yards per turn in Urhan.<br /> <br /> Unless you care to make the claim that &quot;the confrontation takes place in a featureless white void&quot; is not a specific set of circumstances, but I think it's safe to conclude that if that is the case nobody wants anything to do with that discussion.<br /> <br /> The Blast Numen is extremely powerful in the hands of the highest Rank of spirit that is not an Incarna or a Celestine. In other news, water is wet and fire is hot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T21:12:47-07:00","id":717178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=716582#post716582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you miss the part where the range is in Power x 10 yards, and the Seneschal's Blast has a range of 120 yards? It is well beyond the distance most werewolves will be able to travel in a round in which they activate those abilities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OneDimensionalThinking\" target=\"_blank\">I see you went to the Prometheus School for running away from things.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T21:32:48-07:00","id":717254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=717042#post717042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling foul on this because cover is a thing and even the most physically incompetent werewolf can run 24 yards per turn in Urhan.<br /> <br /> Unless you care to make the claim that &quot;the confrontation takes place in a featureless white void&quot; is not a specific set of circumstances, but I think it's safe to conclude that if that is the case nobody wants anything to do with that discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be ridiculous, both you and Ephsy would eagerly respond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Blast Numen is extremely powerful in the hands of the highest Rank of spirit that is not an Incarna or a Celestine. In other news, water is wet and fire is hot. </div> </div> </div>Which was my point to begin with, when making sure I had the mechanics were right. Yet, it still drags on.<br /> <br /> It's as if the Grammar Nazi has been replaced with the Pedantic Nitpicker. I'm guilty as anyone, but it's so stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2015, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T00:24:54-07:00","id":717812,"title":"","content":"Everyone just knock it off, please. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:23:08-07:00","id":725766,"title":"","content":"What's the definition of &quot;Technology&quot; as far as some Facets of the namesake Gift are concerned, like Command Artifice? Moving parts or running on some kind of energy? Just being manufacturated? Will a switchblade count but not a regular knife, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:39:33-07:00","id":725791,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think you could make a switchblade jam shut or something. Nothing too complex, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T01:56:29-07:00","id":737385,"title":"","content":"Question- If I gain a dot in my auspice renown, I gain only my moon gift or, my moon gift <i>and</i> another facet of one of my affinity gift list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T03:27:32-07:00","id":737501,"title":"","content":"I'm almost certain it's both, but I can't find the post where the devs clarify this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T04:19:51-07:00","id":737637,"title":"","content":"The rules are a little bit chaotic about it and my english is far from perfect.<br /> If a player gains both, well, looks like npc and pc will have a <i><b>lot </b></i>of gifts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T04:48:18-07:00","id":737676,"title":"","content":"You get both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T06:43:14-07:00","id":737931,"title":"","content":"then.. when I gain a dot of renown can I gain a facet from an affinity gift list if I have no facet in that list?<br /> Can I use it to unlock for free a list? Or it's necessary to unlock a facet with experience <i>before </i>I can gain another facet from that list with a renown increase?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T06:50:52-07:00","id":737977,"title":"","content":"You need to unlock a Gift before you can get a facet free with renown. Except Wolf Gifts. Those are always open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T07:07:33-07:00","id":738065,"title":"","content":"This is covered in the book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When you get a dot of Renown you get a free Facet for that Renown in a Shadow Gift you have already unlocked. If you have all the Facets for that Renown in the Shadow Gifts you've unlocked, then the free Facet gets banked until it can be spent (ie until you unlock a new Shadow Gift).\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T07:15:48-07:00","id":738111,"title":"","content":"Oh, is it just shadow gifts? I mean, it makes sense that you'd pick them over wolf gifts because they cost more, but I was under the impression that that was still an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T07:26:44-07:00","id":738133,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think anything's gonna break if you pick a Wolf Gift Facet with it, but by default I wrote it with the intention of it applying to Shadow Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T08:00:06-07:00","id":738296,"title":"","content":"Of course, this doesn't explain what happens pre-chargen, because no matter how you slice it a character with three renown and two shadow gifts ends up with six facets (including the moon gift) if you follow those rules from a blank slate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-29-2015, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:09:43-07:00","id":738732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=738296#post738296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this doesn't explain what happens pre-chargen, because no matter how you slice it a character with three renown and two shadow gifts ends up with six facets (including the moon gift) if you follow those rules from a blank slate...</div> </div> </div> </div>You explicitly can't dump all three of your starting Renown dots into the same category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:19:56-07:00","id":738807,"title":"","content":"Do Klaives still exist in second edition? I just noticed none of the Fetishes listed in the book are Klaives, nor is it mentioned in text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" 