chet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:48:09-07:00","id":738917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=738847#post738847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's no longer a special term for fetish weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, they dropped the term altogether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:56:10-07:00","id":738940,"title":"","content":"Yes, I specifically asked Stew if we could drop the term altogether. Klaive is a holdover word from Werewolf: the Apocalypse and there didn't seem much reason to have a random sore-thumb word just for fetish weapons kicking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:58:05-07:00","id":738946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=738732#post738732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You explicitly can't dump all three of your starting Renown dots into the same category.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would actually result in less facets, because you wouldn't be able to spend the free ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:07:26-07:00","id":738993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=738940#post738940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I specifically asked Stew if we could drop the term altogether. Klaive is a holdover word from Werewolf: the Apocalypse and there didn't seem much reason to have a random sore-thumb word just for fetish weapons kicking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. I liked the term. I'll probably re-add it to my games then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:19:44-07:00","id":741840,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves no longer have penalties for social interactions with ordinary humans? I know it's no longer on the Primal Urge table, so I'm thinking it was removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:37:48-07:00","id":741916,"title":"","content":"Nope, higher Primal Urge even gives werewolves in <i>hishu </i>a bonus to hiding in groups of humans. Can't do that if everybody around you is sidling away and giving you the stink eye.<br /> <br /> Higher Primal Urge does penalize Lunacy checks though, so that's still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T12:25:42-08:00","id":749699,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. Does, RAW, Primal Urge apply &quot;twice&quot; to supernatural disease and poisons dealt to the werewolf? As in, say against a disease that allows a resistance or contested roll involving Primal urge and usually stamina... but then a second time applying to the &quot;rating&quot; of the disease or poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:25:22-08:00","id":750311,"title":"","content":"Yeah, stuff like toxicity is subtracted and then you add Primal Urge to resisting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:05:05-08:00","id":753503,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> in 2nd edition, have Totem the manifestation trait or only Infuence and Numen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:16:01-08:00","id":753513,"title":"","content":"Like any spirit, Totems get Twilight Form and a number of manifestations equal to their rank, plus any numina you exchange for additional manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:29:00-08:00","id":756161,"title":"","content":"Another Totem question,<br /> The Pack must uphold the totem's Ban, but they have any problem with the totem's Bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:55:45-08:00","id":756267,"title":"","content":"No, not without Totemic Empowerment active or the Shadow Masquerade facet. There's probably a few other ways and it's possible a spirit has a bane of silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:12:06-08:00","id":756580,"title":"","content":"Human Senses are the default in Hishu and Dalu while Wolf Senses are the default in Urshul and Urhan, but what about Gauru? Both? Either?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:13:37-08:00","id":756582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=756580#post756580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human Senses are the default in Hishu and Dalu while Wolf Senses are the default in Urshul and Urhan, but what about Gauru? Both? Either?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume &quot;Best available&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:47:41-08:00","id":756631,"title":"","content":"So basically wolf senses but with better colour vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:31:45-08:00","id":756990,"title":"","content":"Can't you reflexively switch between those, even without shape-shifting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:46:00-08:00","id":757001,"title":"","content":"Yes, though you seem to get a penalty for using wolf senses the farther from wolf form you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:47:36-08:00","id":757129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=757001#post757001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, though you seem to get a penalty for using wolf senses the farther from wolf form you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or less of a bonus, depending on how you want to spin it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with the ability to switch senses reflexively, the default sense for a particular form is functionally irrelevant most of the time. But if it came up for what ever reason, I'd rule that Gauru form's default sense is which ever sense they were using prior to shifting to the form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-05-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:18:15-08:00","id":757164,"title":"","content":"The third type, Spirit Senses only let's you proyect your current form default senses across the Gauntlet, so you can't, for example, use wolf senses in Dalu. Hence why I ask which ones Gauru defaults to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:57:57-08:00","id":757205,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised we don't have an 'official' faq by now, it would be easier than searching through the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T15:44:50-08:00","id":757404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=757164#post757164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third type, Spirit Senses only let's you proyect your current form default senses across the Gauntlet, so you can't, for example, use wolf senses in Dalu. Hence why I ask which ones Gauru defaults to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... For some reason I had thought you could send any senses across in any form. In that case, I guess Gauru could probably send either form's senses, since it's the midway point between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T15:52:44-08:00","id":757411,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose it comes up very often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:18:09-08:00","id":757441,"title":"","content":"I have an end game and Totem related question: Primal Urge 10 Uratha, went full spirit and joined a Firstborn pack. Can this now spirit werewolf be taken as a Totem by another werewolf pack? And if so, what would its rank be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9109-sidhehound","name":"sidhehound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:59:59-08:00","id":757499,"title":"","content":"On equal power to a Firstborn? That's rank 7 or 8, so no. Physical World doesn't supports it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:23:32-08:00","id":757539,"title":"","content":"That's what I'm not sure about. Does the endgame werewolf, so to speak, that ends up becoming a spirit, is in the rank of a common Wolf Brother spirit or something more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9109-sidhehound","name":"sidhehound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:39:07-08:00","id":757560,"title":"","content":"For simplicity's sake I'd rank according to renown and leave it at that. So rank 5, likely. I'd allow it to become a pack's totem. Higher than rank 5 is beyond any in game mechanics and I'd argue is unattainable or at the very least would take many centuries for an Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:18:10-08:00","id":757619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=757164#post757164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third type, Spirit Senses only let's you proyect your current form default senses across the Gauntlet, so you can't, for example, use wolf senses in Dalu. Hence why I ask which ones Gauru defaults to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're in Gauru and trying to fight something on the other side of the Gauntlet then you're kind of boned regardless. If you're using the Father's Form to put the shape to a more nuanced use, though, I'd say treat it as Urshul in the same way that the Lunacy adjustment does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:57:36-08:00","id":758923,"title":"","content":"How would the spilling of vitae on land effected by the facet &quot;Black earth, red hunger&quot; effect the user? Would they still heal a lethal point instead of a bashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:56:07-08:00","id":759111,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if it has already been asked but... what is the link between the Werewolves and the other Changing Breed, at least on a mythological level ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:00:01-08:00","id":759114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=758923#post758923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the spilling of vitae on land effected by the facet &quot;Black earth, red hunger&quot; effect the user? Would they still heal a lethal point instead of a bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't bleed Vitae, or at all, except under special circumstances. If one had Blush of Life active and you cut them, they would 'bleed' inert blood and it would work as normal. If you managed to sever limbs with aggravated damage, Vitae would come out with blood as the limb decayed, activating the effect. If you just clawed or bit them with lethal damage, nothing.<br /> <br /> If a vampire just decided to pour out some Vitae, I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=759111#post759111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if it has already been asked but... what is the link between the Werewolves and the other Changing Breed, at least on a mythological level ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which changing breed you mean. In first edition there wasn't really much of a connection other than being overseen by Luna, patron of change and shapechangers, but there were some exceptions. In second edition you could probably link them to Pangaea, the lost world, but we don't know much about the standard changing breeds. The hosts, the azlu spiders and beshilu rats, are shards of a slain progenitor beast from Pangaea, trying to resurrect them or fulfill its work.<br /> <br /> It's nothing like Werewolf the Apocalypse, if that's why you were asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-06-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:35:21-08:00","id":762258,"title":"","content":"What do you guys and gals think about these additional uses of <b>Quicksilver Flesh</b> (<i>Wolf Gift of Changing, Wisdom facet</i>):<br /> <br /> -<b>Improved Reflexes</b>: Keeps Defense against firearms (<i>Hishu, Urhan</i>)<br /> <br /> -<b>Wolf Maw</b>: Bite does +1 damage, doesn't require a grapple and can initiate one. Speaking becomes difficult or imposible. (<i>Hishu, Dalu</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:38:53-08:00","id":762260,"title":"","content":"Wolf Maw sounds entirely legit, but I'm not sure how Improved reflexes would work. What are you changing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T07:28:12-08:00","id":762291,"title":"","content":"How do multiple opponents work in a grapple situation? Lets say Player A decides to bite and grapple Enemy. Player B also wants to bite and aid Player A in Grapple. I didn't see any rules regarding this, although I may have missed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T07:42:40-08:00","id":762303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762291#post762291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do multiple opponents work in a grapple situation? Lets say Player A decides to bite and grapple Enemy. Player B also wants to bite and aid Player A in Grapple. I didn't see any rules regarding this, although I may have missed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Player B goes first, then Enemy's Defense will be 1 lower when Player A tries to grapple (or Enemy will elect not to use Defense against Player B's attack and will more likely get hit). After the grapple has initiated, there's nothing stopping Player B from attacking Enemy (though unless Player A is Holding Enemy, Enemy still gets their Defense against Player B).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:03:24-08:00","id":762321,"title":"","content":"I think when it comes to the roll for continuing to grapple all 3 would go on the highest initiative and the dogpilee would need to beat both of them to get free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T09:19:01-08:00","id":762357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sidhehound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=757441#post757441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an end game and Totem related question: Primal Urge 10 Uratha, went full spirit and joined a Firstborn pack. Can this now spirit werewolf be taken as a Totem by another werewolf pack? And if so, what would its rank be?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a suitably unique event to be up to the individual Storyteller rather than something we've done any mapping for on a general mechanical level. In general, the answer given 'this werewolf is now a spirit' is that yes, as a spirit they could be taken by a werewolf pack if that pack could muster enough Totem dots to afford them. Rank would depend hugely on the hows and whys of the werewolf and their ascension. I know in my own games, a predator bodhisattva (ie going past PU10) surpassing their Flesh entirely to become a spirit would be <i>minimum </i>Rank\u200b 4, more likely Rank 5+, and with additional unique capabilities/aspects of existence on top of that of a usual spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=758923#post758923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the spilling of vitae on land effected by the facet &quot;Black earth, red hunger&quot; effect the user? Would they still heal a lethal point instead of a bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div> It just counts as blood for BE, RH.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:20:18-08:00","id":762497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762260#post762260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf Maw sounds entirely legit, but I'm not sure how Improved reflexes would work. What are you changing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, normally only the three intermediate forms (Dalu, Gauru and Urshul) can use Defense against firearms like guns and rifles. Yeah, it seems more an internal change than the others (save perhaps the improved Perception bonus), but I figured it wouldn't be broken. Too much, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:30:58-08:00","id":762506,"title":"","content":"It doesn't sound unbalanced or anything, I just can't figure out what's supposed to be happening in-universe to cause it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:32:55-08:00","id":762508,"title":"","content":"Wolven muscles and tendons, as well as probably eyes so you can see danger fast enough to react to. The eyes might not be necessary, the human eyes are astonishingly fast, having saccades of up to 900 degrees per second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:35:08-08:00","id":762512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762357#post762357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a suitably unique event to be up to the individual Storyteller rather than something we've done any mapping for on a general mechanical level. In general, the answer given 'this werewolf is now a spirit' is that yes, as a spirit they could be taken by a werewolf pack if that pack could muster enough Totem dots to afford them. Rank would depend hugely on the hows and whys of the werewolf and their ascension. I know in my own games, a predator bodhisattva (ie going past PU10) surpassing their Flesh entirely to become a spirit would be <i>minimum </i>Rank\u200b 4, more likely Rank 5+, and with additional unique capabilities/aspects of existence on top of that of a usual spirit.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let me take this opportunity to ask if there are any plans of introducing special gifts or abilities for high PU werewolves, maybe things like milestone facets and the secondary Auspice gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:38:11-08:00","id":762515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762508#post762508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolven muscles and tendons, as well as probably eyes so you can see danger fast enough to react to. The eyes might not be necessary, the human eyes are astonishingly fast, having saccades of up to 900 degrees per second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works. Whatever it makes the three intermediate forms do it, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me take this opportunity to ask if there are any plans of introducing special gifts or abilities for high PU werewolves, maybe things like milestone facets and the secondary Auspice gifts. </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the first but additional Auspice Gifts (now Moon Gifts) are a certain posibility contemplated in the new core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:04:02-08:00","id":762541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762512#post762512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me take this opportunity to ask if there are any plans of introducing special gifts or abilities for high PU werewolves, maybe things like milestone facets and the secondary Auspice gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be another set of auspice gifts, there's already rules in the corebook about how to purchase them. Other than that, I think you're confusing Aspects with Milestone gifts there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:12:34-08:00","id":762547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=759111#post759111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if it has already been asked but... what is the link between the Werewolves and the other Changing Breed, at least on a mythological level ?</div> </div> </div> </div> None that I am aware of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762512#post762512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me take this opportunity to ask if there are any plans of introducing special gifts or abilities for high PU werewolves, maybe things like milestone facets and the secondary Auspice gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div> No idea about plans for special abilities for high-PU werewolves as yet. New Moon Gifts won't be limited to high-PU.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:25:52-08:00","id":762600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762541#post762541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There will be another set of auspice gifts, there's already rules in the corebook about how to purchase them. Other than that, I think you're confusing Aspects with Milestone gifts there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is entirely possible, I meant the abilities that you could get after you had all facets of a particular gift. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762547#post762547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No idea about plans for special abilities for high-PU werewolves as yet. New Moon Gifts won't be limited to high-PU.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for your answer Chris. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:18:13-08:00","id":763131,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, once a spirit unlocks a gift within you, attaining new Facets it's more like an epiphany, reaching within yourself than hunting another spirit for the new power, correct? That's what I'm reading between the lines here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-11-2015, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:29:47-08:00","id":763140,"title":"","content":"Something like that. It's as much the literal, spiritual power of your Renown and your nature wriggling and coursing through your spirit and flesh to forge new channels through which Essence can flow. You definitely don't hunt a spirit for a new Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T02:50:11-08:00","id":763899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=759114#post759114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires don't bleed Vitae, or at all, except under special circumstances. If one had Blush of Life active and you cut them, they would 'bleed' inert blood and it would work as normal. If you managed to sever limbs with aggravated damage, Vitae would come out with blood as the limb decayed, activating the effect. If you just clawed or bit them with lethal damage, nothing.<br /> <br /> If a vampire just decided to pour out some Vitae, I'd say yes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the Kindred Dueling style in Blood and Smoke! You can deal Vitae damage instead of Health damage (but that's only with the 5 dot).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T03:43:26-08:00","id":763922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=763899#post763899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the Kindred Dueling style in Blood and Smoke! You can deal Vitae damage instead of Health damage (but that's only with the 5 dot).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an special circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:37:58-08:00","id":764004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=762291#post762291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do multiple opponents work in a grapple situation? Lets say Player A decides to bite and grapple Enemy. Player B also wants to bite and aid Player A in Grapple. I didn't see any rules regarding this, although I may have missed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If more than one person tries to grapple the same victim, count the attempt as a teamwork action. On the team side, both primary and secondary actors roll Strength + Brawl \u2013 Defense to engage, but the victim\u2019s Defense is unaffected by how many people are involved \u2014 even if five people try to grab him, he treats it as one attack. In the grapple, both primary and secondary actors roll Strength + Brawl in a contested action with the victim. If the defender wins, any chosen moves only affect the primary actor.&quot;<br /> - God-Machine Chronicle, page 200","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:50:18-08:00","id":764014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=763140#post763140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like that. It's as much the literal, spiritual power of your Renown and your nature wriggling and coursing through your spirit and flesh to forge new channels through which Essence can flow. You definitely don't hunt a spirit for a new Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got some players who want to learn the Gift of the Elementals, and they just so happen to have a friendly River Spirit nearby. Assuming they could provide the proper <i>gathra</i>, do the players really need to call a hunt on it to get it to bestow the Gift upon them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:58:58-08:00","id":764023,"title":"","content":"Depends how you want to play it, I guess. On the one hand, they need to use the rite to gain essence from a spirit, so that implies that siskur-dah somehow aligns their nature to the hisil in such a way as to make that possible. It may well be that the ability to bestow shadow gifts is also dependent on the siskur-dah condition to be present on the recipient. <br /> <br /> If that is the case then the river spirit would simply see the ritual as a necessary formality. It could even be there during the rite. <br /> <br /> &quot;I declare a sacred hunt on... that dude over there. Ok guys, well done, we got him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or you could just not bother and have it work fine without any pomp or ceremony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T07:10:47-08:00","id":764028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=764014#post764014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got some players who want to learn the Gift of the Elementals, and they just so happen to have a friendly River Spirit nearby. Assuming they could provide the proper <i>gathra</i>, do the players really need to call a hunt on it to get it to bestow the Gift upon them?</div> </div> </div> </div> They don't need to, no. As the Gifts section of 2e indicates, you can convince a spirit to inflict a Gift through negotiating etc - it doesn't have to be a hunt, but a hunt allows you to force the issue with a spirit that is noncompliant.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether the spirit is convinced or coerced, it still has to rend the Uratha's flesh and spirit to inflict the Gift on them, of course. This always hurts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:44:32-08:00","id":764717,"title":"","content":"Does Trained Observer apply to Tracking rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T00:46:42-08:00","id":764764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=764717#post764717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Trained Observer apply to Tracking rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically no (Tracking rolls aren't Perception rolls), but it's a simple house rule to apply it if you want. Personally, I think it would work okay with Tracking, and shouldn't break anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:56:14-08:00","id":764854,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, I just noticed you're writing for the Dark Eras Companion, can you tell us what era?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:10:55-08:00","id":764860,"title":"","content":"Forsaken By Rome. <br /> <br /> I'm excited for its release <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:15:23-08:00","id":764862,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:23:21-08:00","id":764869,"title":"","content":"I think Forsaken fans are gonna be pretty pleased with the Dark Eras offerings the line is getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:30:30-08:00","id":764874,"title":"","content":"It inspired me to re-back after backing out so definitely. That first round of votes Werewolf kept falling in second place almost every time, it was pretty brutal. Vampire and hunter didn't win at all, so not having any of my three favorite games really bummed me out on the whole thing. Werewolf came back with a vengeance, though, and some of the backer choices helped too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:38:12-08:00","id":764880,"title":"","content":"There's a lot to look forward to.<br /> <br /> Initially I was a\u200bnnoyed I didn't get to write the Viking-Era Forsaken, since I have what I still think is The Best Idea Evar (tm) for it, but then I got offered Neolithic instead and am so, so happy I did <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There will be some interesting setting details that should set the cat amongst the pigeons, as it were. There's also some <i>great </i>mechanical stuff coming through the Werewolf Eras.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T13:05:45-08:00","id":765109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=764880#post764880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There will be some interesting setting details that should set the cat amongst the pigeons, as it were. There's also some <i>great </i>mechanical stuff coming through the Werewolf Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Skinchangers was originally a Werewolf book, and most of it's rules are related to it, might me see some stuff in the Aztec Era that tie to WtF? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T13:17:30-08:00","id":765122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=764880#post764880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nitially I was a\u200bnnoyed I didn't get to write the Viking-Era Forsaken, since I have what I still think is The Best Idea Evar (tm) for it</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose you could share?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T13:47:11-08:00","id":765139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=765109#post765109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Skinchangers was originally a Werewolf book, and most of it's rules are related to it, might me see some stuff in the Aztec Era that tie to WtF? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not familiar enough with the era in question to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=765122#post765122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't suppose you could share?</div> </div> </div> </div> Definitely not before the book's out. Once it's out, I might write my idea up as a 'and here's a potential bit of setting/plot to run with your shiny new Viking Dark Era'.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:21:45-08:00","id":765241,"title":"","content":"Do you guys allow specialties to apply to gifts and/or rites? A specialty in Storms to apply to rolls for Heavens Unleashed or Raiment of the Storm, for example.<br /> <br /> Another question, is Lies or Lying too broad a specialty for the Subterfuge skill? I know Subterfuge includes many other kinds of deception, but I'm feeling a little guilty having it on my character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T18:05:32-08:00","id":765263,"title":"","content":"I do, and I know the vampire rules allow for it. I think generally you'd want something more specific than, 'Gifts' though, maybe a specific Gift you've specialized in.<br /> <br /> Lying is allowed, and in fact is one of the example specialties from the original core book, along with Con Jobs, Hiding Emotions, Misdirection, Spotting Lies, and the second edition's Detecting Lies, Doublespeak, Hiding Emotion, Little White Lies, and Misdirection. Most of them are pretty broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T00:03:25-08:00","id":765408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=765241#post765241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, is Lies or Lying too broad a specialty for the Subterfuge skill? I know Subterfuge includes many other kinds of deception, but I'm feeling a little guilty having it on my character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Subterfuge can be used to keep your mouth shut, to be taciturn or to for another example, fake a tell on a poker game. None of which is specifically lying. To lie effectively you gotta be able to craft credible stories, and then stick by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:57:34-08:00","id":767356,"title":"","content":"Are Totems or Pack spirits &quot;supposed&quot; to be on the side of material side of the Gauntlet? Does this opinion differ with the Pure? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:41:32-08:00","id":767384,"title":"","content":"Generally everything from the Hisil is 'supposed' to stay on the spirit side, but exceptions are made on a case by case basis and I'd expect some packs would be fine with it.<br /> <br /> The problem mostly comes from the fact that spirits bleed Essence fast when in the material realm. The most common ways to avoid this are to fetter yourself to someone, which makes them a spirit-urged, or claim them, which makes them a Claimed. Either way this can severely wreck peoples lives and draw a lot of attention. But, again, I'm sure it happens. Packs having a sort of assigned 'horse' like in Voodoo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:53:33-08:00","id":767395,"title":"","content":"There's a rite for it: Totemic Empowerment.<br /> <br /> Some spirits are better at doing their thing from one side of the gauntlet than the other. Others can materialize and fight alongside their packs for a brief moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:34:11-08:00","id":767565,"title":"","content":"What rank are a pack's Totem spirit? Are each Tier on the Totem table for Exp a rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:38:42-08:00","id":767566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=767565#post767565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rank are a pack's Totem spirit? Are each Tier on the Totem table for Exp a rank?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF2e Core, p92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For each Totem point, the totem receives one Attribute dot. [\u2026] The Attributes also determine the totem\u2019s Rank, determined by the chart on p. 183[.]</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:42:09-08:00","id":767567,"title":"","content":"Huh. Well in the game we have two wolves. So our Totem spirit IS Rank 1. I guess I always assumed that the spirit had to be sapient for you to take it as a Totem (IE Rank 2+, where as Rank 1 is basically an animal)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T22:07:09-08:00","id":767577,"title":"","content":"Well two wolves would have a hard time wrangling anything but a low level spirit to join their &quot;pack.&quot; At that point it's just a mascot really that they're hoping to build into something more. They could always put in a 3-4 additional dots (each) in the totem merit to make it a rank 2 spirit, however. It'd be worth roughly the same amount in totem bonuses so I guess that'd be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T22:27:49-08:00","id":767587,"title":"","content":"They have 3 and 2 in Totem, with 1 from a Wolf-Blood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T23:32:39-08:00","id":767601,"title":"","content":"Three more would do it. I've never run a game where the pack had a rank 1 totem, and it's not exactly something a pack would be proud of I don't imagine. I don't think packs trade out totems for bigger ones once they've outgrown them, so the plan would have to be to raise a spirit up in ranks themselves - which is not entirely unreasonable.<br /> <br /> But three merit dots is all it would take, and a rank 2 totem gives 3 xp worth in bonuses so it's not a huge sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:57:12-08:00","id":767746,"title":"","content":"Two werewolves is a really small pack, not many totems would flock to patron them and they would have trouble impressing spirits as well.<br /> <br /> But if you want to fiddle with the rules, we won't tell and get your ST certification revoked.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind during pack creation players are offered the opportunity to make wolf-blooded NPCs for support characters who can have a totem dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:09:27-08:00","id":767751,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for a two werewolf pack I'd have filled out the numbers a bit with extra wolfbloods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:54:56-08:00","id":767772,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind some settings show packs covering entire regions and with 40 to 50 members. Imagine that totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:50:17-08:00","id":768070,"title":"","content":"So I can't find anywhere in the book that says that werewolves can upgrade their bites to aggravated to consume the flesh of other werewolves. Under regaining Essence on page 100, it explicitly only mentions wolves and humans, but not werewolves. And the rest of the document seems somewhat mum on the subject.<br /> <br /> Was this intentional, or just an oversight mistake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:02:23-08:00","id":768081,"title":"","content":"Where it says wolves, it refers to werewolves. I believe the writers have confirmed that they can do it as well and there's a couple off-handed mentions of it in the book, like on page 285..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:06:50-08:00","id":768086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=768070#post768070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can't find anywhere in the book that says that werewolves can upgrade their bites to aggravated to consume the flesh of other werewolves. Under regaining Essence on page 100, it explicitly only mentions wolves and humans, but not werewolves. And the rest of the document seems somewhat mum on the subject.<br /> <br /> Was this intentional, or just an oversight mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ohXKK2O.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:12:03-08:00","id":768090,"title":"","content":"I was in a sufficiently self-doubting headspace that I wasn't sure what that was saying, but I could tell it was definitely &quot;pro&quot;-eating werewolves for essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:14:16-08:00","id":768093,"title":"","content":"Well, Essence is Essence, and unless you finish them off they'll grow back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T20:36:03-08:00","id":770490,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the thread! Here's some of my questions that I've not seen addressed so far.<br /> <br /> 1) How are new members added to the pack?<br /> <br /> I think it seems likely there'd be at least two different ways: a) negotiation or a ritual with the totem (which may not require the new member to be present, especially in the case of an unaware human), and b) at the whim of the totem.<br /> <br /> 2) Is there a way, for Uratha at least, to recognise Wolf-Blooded as such outside of observing the presence of a Tell?<br /> <br /> 3) Is there any way for one pack member to identify another? Something visible in the Hisil or to spirit senses? A scent? A companionly feeling?<br /> <br /> 4) What is a territory &quot;supposed&quot; to produce?<br /> <br /> 5) When should you gain Essence by seeing your auspice moon? The text says &quot;The first time an Uratha sees her auspice moon at night, she gains an Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> a) Must it be at night? Irraka are a little out of luck in this case, as the new moon is rarely visible after sunset.<br /> <br /> b) Do you gain an Essence on every different night/24-hour period you see your auspice moon, or just once a lunar month? If on every night, then Irraka and Rahu are a bit shafted, as they would only gain about three or four Essence a lunar month, as opposed to about six or seven for Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith. I have a first-draft suggestion, in this case: for Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith, the Essence gain only happens in the same half-cycle as their First Change, i.e. waxing or waning.<br /> <br /> 6) Do we have to uphold our totem's ban exactly as they do? Or is it sometimes modified slightly to reflect the not-wholly-spirit nature of Uratha? Do Wolf-Blooded need to uphold the totem's ban too?<br /> <br /> 7) Unihar don't exist anymore, true, but is a werewolf-werewolf mating still unable to produce viable offspring?<br /> <br /> 8) Can Uratha get drunk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9534-fivetomidnight","name":"fivetomidnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T21:21:28-08:00","id":770512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the thread! Here's some of my questions that I've not seen addressed so far.<br /> <br /> 1) How are new members added to the pack?<br /> <br /> I think it seems likely there'd be at least two different ways: a) negotiation or a ritual with the totem (which may not require the new member to be present, especially in the case of an unaware human), and b) at the whim of the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>These would be correct. The Totem/Uratha bond is mutual. The Uratha needs to be aware of it. Sing the dotted line as it were, in my opinion. Humans? They only need to belong to the group. A fire spirit brands it's Uratha, a spirit of fear embraces them with a shadowy tendril that is only apparent thru their peripheral vision, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Is there a way, for Uratha at least, to recognise Wolf-Blooded as such outside of observing the presence of a Tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can sniff them out with at Wits+Primal Urge roll, in second edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Is there any way for one pack member to identify another? Something visible in the Hisil or to spirit senses? A scent? A companionly feeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>The pack awareness gift would tell you precisely, otherwise, their senses can convene that familiar packmate scent just fine, unless there are attempts at disguise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) What is a territory &quot;supposed&quot; to produce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Security? Why do you own a house? It's a statement: it's your hunting ground, and of serious consequence to at least Hunters in Darkness and Iron Masters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) When should you gain Essence by seeing your auspice moon? The text says &quot;The first time an Uratha sees her auspice moon at night, she gains an Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> a) Must it be at night? Irraka are a little out of luck in this case, as the new moon is rarely visible after sunset.<br /> <br /> b) Do you gain an Essence on every different night/24-hour period you see your auspice moon, or just once a lunar month? If on every night, then Irraka and Rahu are a bit shafted, as they would only gain about three or four Essence a lunar month, as opposed to about six or seven for Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith. I have a first-draft suggestion, in this case: for Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith, the Essence gain only happens in the same half-cycle as their First Change, i.e. waxing or waning.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Even the New Moon emits luminosity. Shouldn't be an issue for Irraka's senses to perceive. Alternately, the notion that the night lacks a moon would count.<br /> <br /> B) I rule every night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Do we have to uphold our totem's ban exactly as they do? Or is it sometimes modified slightly to reflect the not-wholly-spirit nature of Uratha? Do Wolf-Blooded need to uphold the totem's ban too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I modify it, it makes for better gameplay. Like in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) Unihar don't exist anymore, true, but is a werewolf-werewolf mating still unable to produce viable offspring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha mating amongst themselves do produce viable offspring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8) Can Uratha get drunk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the Primal Urge and the quality of the beverage. American beer would be toxicity 1, so it wouldn't do the trick on Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T21:30:40-08:00","id":770517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=770490#post770490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If on every night, then Irraka and Rahu are a bit shafted, as they would only gain about three or four Essence a lunar month, as opposed to about six or seven for Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's five consecutive nights of recovery versus two batches of three consecutive nights of recovery. The Elodoth have eleven days of drought between each of theirs, and while the Cahalith and the Ithaeur only have five days' wait on one hand, the longer leg of their recovery time is seventeen days. The Rahu and Irraka only lose out in the very long term by a very slight margin \u2014 remember that Essence capacity doesn't vary all that much until a character reaches superhuman levels of Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T16:35:33-08:00","id":773501,"title":"","content":"I have a few more questions:<br /> <br /> 9) Do all of the Wolf-Blooded pack members need to uphold the totem's ban? None of them? Only those who have a dot in the Totem Merit? Or would it depend on the totem?<br /> <br /> 10) A Wolf-Blooded loses their Tell when they undergo the First Change, or recognise that their Tell was simply one aspect of what they've become (example: A Wolf's Meat). There's a few Tells, though, that involve entities beyond the Wolf-Blooded. What happens to them?<br /> <br /> a) The animal or spirit companion from &quot;Familiar&quot;<br /> b) The pack of spirit wolves from &quot;Phantom Pack&quot;<br /> c) The living wolf pelt from &quot;Second Skin&quot;<br /> d) The spirit twin from &quot;Shadow Twin&quot;<br /> <br /> As I see it, a character could spend one or more of their four unallocated Totem points in order to make the spirit companion or the spirit twin a personal totem (at the cost of weakening the character's possible bond to their pack totem), and I could see the character's pack totem possibly accepting the animal companion or the pack of spirit wolves into the pack.<br /> <br /> 11) Is there typically just one locus in a pack's territory, or can there be more? Is there some sort of points cost to add more, or is there just the added responsibility of handling multiple loci?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9534-fivetomidnight","name":"fivetomidnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T16:36:17-08:00","id":773502,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know the dice roll for Claimed or werewolf under the effects of totemic empowerment to use influences and/or numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:02:30-08:00","id":773518,"title":"","content":"For influences I would use the pool given for accessing them via a Talen. That is, Presence + Wits. I guess that works for numina too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:36:05-08:00","id":773532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=773501#post773501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few more questions:<br /> <br /> 9) Do all of the Wolf-Blooded pack members need to uphold the totem's ban? None of them? Only those who have a dot in the Totem Merit? Or would it depend on the totem?<br /> <br /> 10) A Wolf-Blooded loses their Tell when they undergo the First Change, or recognise that their Tell was simply one aspect of what they've become (example: A Wolf's Meat). There's a few Tells, though, that involve entities beyond the Wolf-Blooded. What happens to them?<br /> <br /> a) The animal or spirit companion from &quot;Familiar&quot;<br /> b) The pack of spirit wolves from &quot;Phantom Pack&quot;<br /> c) The living wolf pelt from &quot;Second Skin&quot;<br /> d) The spirit twin from &quot;Shadow Twin&quot;<br /> <br /> As I see it, a character could spend one or more of their four unallocated Totem points in order to make the spirit companion or the spirit twin a personal totem (at the cost of weakening the character's possible bond to their pack totem), and I could see the character's pack totem possibly accepting the animal companion or the pack of spirit wolves into the pack.<br /> <br /> 11) Is there typically just one locus in a pack's territory, or can there be more? Is there some sort of points cost to add more, or is there just the added responsibility of handling multiple loci?</div> </div> </div> </div>9) I go with only Uratha having to uphold the ban. It makes having not-in-the-know human packmates work better.<br /> <br /> 10) <br /> <br /> A) Sounds like a touchstone potential.<br /> B) Spirit Touchstone.<br /> C) Normal pelt, likely dead.<br /> D) Spirit touchstone.<br /> <br /> 11) There can be more, and you can have several instances of the locus merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:00:00-08:00","id":773574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=773518#post773518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For influences I would use the pool given for accessing them via a Talen. That is, Presence + Wits. I guess that works for numina too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Thanks. I knew there was a thing <i>somewhere</i> but I couldn't find it. <br /> <br /> Couple more questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Is there a roleplaying aspect to the Isolated condition? Because in my experience NPCs don't benefit from teamwork rolls very often and the defense reduction reduction is negligible at best. Do you guys run that condition as also making the a gang member's allies less likely to get involved in his argument with the PC, for example? Or less likely to defend him if he's threatened? Or maybe conversely, the gang member to at least believe he's less likely to get help (and thus less confident). Just curious because it feels a bit underwhelming as is to me. (As does the Cahalith's, since my NPCs don't spend willpower that often)<br /> <br /> 2. I have always assumed Human characters don't respond to the flaring of renown, but is it Uratha specific? Do Spirits respond? Claimed? Do Wolfbloods? Azlu (assuming you would ever not just try to kill them), etc. Does it apply to anything that can see it? Anything with a spiritual nature/side? Everything?<br /> <br /> 3. Brawling Dodge in wolf forms, yea or nay? I'm probably going to rule yea, but I just want to know what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:15:57-08:00","id":773580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=773574#post773574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is there a roleplaying aspect to the Isolated condition? Because in my experience NPCs don't benefit from teamwork rolls very often and the defense reduction reduction is negligible at best. Do you guys run that condition as also making the a gang member's allies less likely to get involved in his argument with the PC, for example? Or less likely to defend him if he's threatened? Or maybe conversely, the gang member to at least believe he's less likely to get help (and thus less confident). Just curious because it feels a bit underwhelming as is to me. (As does the Cahalith's, since my NPCs don't spend willpower that often)</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been running it with the idea that bystanders won't help at all and allies are just less likely to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I have always assumed Human characters don't respond to the flaring of renown, but is it Uratha specific? Do Spirits respond? Claimed? Do Wolfbloods? Azlu (assuming you would ever not just try to kill them), etc. Does it apply to anything that can see it? Anything with a spiritual nature/side? Everything? </div> </div> </div>We had a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446639#post446639\">brief discussion about this</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447972#post447972\">in another thread</a>. Keep in mind no one is forced to respond to your flaring, they just get a bonus if they do. I'm of the mind that anything can take advantage of it, but due to its essentially 'letting the herd know' it's something you'd be careful of when dealing with regular mortals, and since it could give enemies a serious advantage, not something you'd necessarily want to do with something willing to kill you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Brawling Dodge in wolf forms, yea or nay? I'm probably going to rule yea, but I just want to know what you guys think. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't make a rule against it, but I'd point out that it's not been updated to second edition rules and, as is, isn't that great unless you've got really good Brawl. The rules for dodge have changed in second edition, instead of adding to your Defense it turns it into a roll detracting from successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-24-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:29:34-08:00","id":773587,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm sorry, I meant Defensive Combat: Brawl.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks.<br /> <br /> I never thought for a second that flaring would work on Humans but I like it because I intend to use it more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 11-24-2015, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T20:16:29-08:00","id":773608,"title":"","content":"Oh, then sure yeah.<br /> <br /> I could understand an argument for the Brawl skill not adding to Defense against Firearms, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:58:56-08:00","id":774289,"title":"","content":"What are the top speeds of a werewolf in miles per hours?<br /> Assuming pu 1 and then put 10. In different forms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 11-25-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:20:03-08:00","id":774307,"title":"","content":"Can you share what you're comparing it against, or are you going to wait for an answer then let us know how horrible it is that it didn't work out the way you wanted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:26:20-08:00","id":774313,"title":"","content":"Curiosity.<br /> No real reason other than maybe it'll be handy for when I compare it with vehicles. I mean I don't really expect it to be too extreme without buffing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there a way to figure out the speed conversion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:39:48-08:00","id":774326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774313#post774313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiosity.<br /> No real reason other than maybe it'll be handy for when I compare it with vehicles. I mean I don't really expect it to be too extreme without buffing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there a way to figure out the speed conversion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Speed is how many yards the character can travel in one turn. A turn is 3 seconds. 1760 yards in a mile. 3600 seconds in an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:46:20-08:00","id":774332,"title":"","content":"I have 28.3 MPH for a Primal Urge 1 werewolf. And 35.8 for Primal Urge 10. Not allowing for essence expenditure, which would vary amounts for a bit, especially with the Primal Urge 10 wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Forgot some stuff, better results below. 11-25-2015, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:50:57-08:00","id":774335,"title":"","content":"It's feet per second. This handily puts the speed of light at a nice round 1 billion. Ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:58:47-08:00","id":774341,"title":"","content":"You get some vagaries there, as it can be either meters or yards per turn, and a turn is 'about' three seconds, giving every measurement a sort of 'ish' to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:07:50-08:00","id":774345,"title":"","content":"Well alright thanks then.<br /> <br /> Where's the line of text that says meters or feet for speed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:10:14-08:00","id":774349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774345#post774345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well alright thanks then.<br /> <br /> Where's the line of text that says meters or feet for speed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 158. Turn speed on page 162.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:29:20-08:00","id":774368,"title":"","content":"How does PU factors in the speed instead of other attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:32:48-08:00","id":774374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774368#post774368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does PU factors in the speed instead of other attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, it's the cap of attributes. It also adds more speed by allowing you to activate buffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:35:51-08:00","id":774376,"title":"","content":"Yes, that was the only difference Primal Urge had. Renown had a big impact through Predator's Unmatched Pursuit. The rest was merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:41:13-08:00","id":774382,"title":"","content":"This is of course ignoring crimson spasm, which renders the true limit theoretically infinite with an exponentially decaying probability of getting to a given value as you approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:00:28-08:00","id":774387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774382#post774382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is of course ignoring crimson spasm, which renders the true limit theoretically infinite with an exponentially decaying probability of getting to a given value as you approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... how does that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:02:36-08:00","id":774390,"title":"","content":"You roll to see how many points of strength you get. Statistically speaking, there's nothing stopping you rolling 10 after 10 after 10, it's just <i>really unlikely.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:25:32-08:00","id":774403,"title":"","content":"Keeping with the Primal Urge 10 werewolf, using Essence, you have a max dicepool of 25 for Crimson Spasm not counting Willpower, and if those are all successes, not counting possible extra successes from 10s, you end up with a speed of 196, sustainable for slightly over a minute but round it down to a minute and you have 3920 meters in a minute.<br /> <br /> I just realized I forgot to factor in Primal Strength to this and previous estimates, it would add a speed of 5 for a maximized werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-25-2015, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:28:18-08:00","id":774404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774390#post774390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You roll to see how many points of strength you get. Statistically speaking, there's nothing stopping you rolling 10 after 10 after 10, it's just <i>really unlikely.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You only have to roll once, and you only need 5 successes to get 10 bonus strength, which if you're rolling at least 15 die (5 Stamina, 5 Survival, 5 Purity) is very likely. More if you're capping at 10 and you're using a different form to power the gift. Still let's just go with 5 successes.<br /> <br /> With that I have a speed of at least 80<sup> (primal urge 1)</sup> - 110<sup>(10)</sup> for a Rahu in Urshul using Crimson Spasm with Predator's Unmatched Pursuit and 3 dots in Fleet of Foot.<br /> <br /> Whatever that translates to in mph, I dunno. Armory says 90 is about 60 mph. Bit more than that. Don't know if that's an outdated metric at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:59:33-08:00","id":774426,"title":"","content":"I'm not a min/maxer, but these things have gotten me interested lately. My wife is a scientist and we've had very different outlooks on math, and she's sort of winning me over to her side so I'm trying to practice it more and gaming keeps me interested.<br /> <br /> Anyways, breaking it down, maximizing everything but not really taking advantage of Essence except for Predator's Unmatched Pursuit and Primal Strength, which allows for 1 Essence a pop to work for the entire scene.<br /> <br /> Speed = Strength and Dexterity + 5.<br /> PU1 = 15 Speed<br /> PU10 = 25 Speed<br /> Embodiment of the Firstborn to give +1 Strength or Dexterity.<br /> Favored Form, Urshul, for +1 Strength and +1 Dexterity.<br /> Fleet of Foot 3 for +3 Speed.<br /> Urshul for +7 Speed. I'm reasonably sure this is already factoring in the Strength and Dexterity bonuses.<br /> Predator's Unmatched Pursuit for +5 Speed.<br /> Primal Strength for +5 Strength.<br /> PU1 = 38 Speed<br /> PU10 = 48 Speed<br /> <br /> First time around I threw in Springboarding, as I was trying to just throw anything that increased Speed, despite the ridiculousness of the imagery. But doing so I completely forgot about Run, which doubles your speed for the turn and presumably they're running for this. You can't run and do things at the same time, so Springboarding is out completely, as would some other options.<br /> <br /> PU1 = 76<br /> PU10 = 96<br /> <br /> Speed is meters or yards per 'about' three seconds. Meters are longer, though, so we'll use those.<br /> <br /> PU1 translates to 1520 in a minute, 91200 meters in an hour, converts to 56.7 miles per hour.<br /> PU10 translates to 1920 in a minute, 115200 meters in an hour, converts to 71.6 miles per hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:40:18-08:00","id":774614,"title":"","content":"You can't take favoured form at primal urge 1. Fortunately you also forgot about totem bonuses, so that leaves the PU1 max at 38, and bumps the PU10 max to 50.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T02:29:43-08:00","id":774630,"title":"","content":"And Predator's Unmatched Pursuit lets you double your Speed for an Essence for the turn in any form, that would be on top of the doubling for running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:27:18-08:00","id":774734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774426#post774426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urshul for +7 Speed. I'm reasonably sure this is already factoring in the Strength and Dexterity bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the species factor of Urhan, would be 10; Urshul is 12. So that's on top of Strength and Dexterity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:41:05-08:00","id":774748,"title":"","content":"The species factor of both is 8. That's why the bonus is +7 for urshul (+3 species, +2 strength, + 2 dexterity) and +5 for urhan (+3 species, + 2 dexterity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:32:37-08:00","id":774828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774630#post774630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Predator's Unmatched Pursuit lets you double your Speed for an Essence for the turn in any form, that would be on top of the doubling for running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's for the turn, and not something either Uratha can keep up for an hour, so I didn't count it. Plus, while running, you can't perform other actions without special merits to do so, and I believe spending extra Essence to double-up PUP would count for that. And I couldn't find the special merit anyways.<br /> <br /> Technically you could also use Totemic Empowerment which gives some Speed too but I discounted it for Basu-Im reasons. But yes, I forgot about the lack of Favored Form at Primal Urge 1 and totem bonuses but maxed out they are basically the same. Fortunately factoring the 50 from PU10 gets way easy when you double for 100, multiply by 20 for 2000, then 60 for 120,000, converting via google to 74.56 mph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:44:06-08:00","id":774869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=774748#post774748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The species factor of both is 8. That's why the bonus is +7 for urshul (+3 species, +2 strength, + 2 dexterity) and +5 for urhan (+3 species, + 2 dexterity).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agan, no. The speed is on top of Hishu's, Hishu's species factor is 5, so is Dalu.<br /> <br /> 12-5=7; 10-5=5.<br /> <br /> Why on Earth would a wolf have a species factor comparable to a prehistoric beast the size of a horse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:58:02-08:00","id":774881,"title":"","content":"Just... just read the forms section again. In fact, here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Traits: Strength +2, Dexterity +2, Stamina +2, Manipulation<br /> \u20131, Size +1, <b>Species speed factor +3</b> (Health +3,<br /> Initiative +2, Speed +7). </div> </div> </div>and<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Traits: Dexterity +2, Stamina +1, Manipulation \u20131, Size<br /> \u20131, <b>Species speed factor +3</b> (Initiative +2, Speed +5). </div> </div> </div>The +5 and +7 are <i>derived traits. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-26-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T17:11:00-08:00","id":775103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=773532#post773532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 11) There can be more, and you can have several instances of the locus merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Locus a first edition merit? I can't find in my copy of the second ed core; the closest I can find is Dedicated Locus.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Even more questions!<br /> <br /> 12) If Lunes give the Forsaken their Renown brands, what gives them to the Pure? They do have Renown brands, you can see them glowing &quot;fiery red&quot; if a Blood Talon leads the Siskur-Dah rite.<br /> <br /> 13) When you gain a level of Renown, you get a free Facet for that Renown in a Gift you have. What if you don't want that Facet for any Gift you already have - can you store it voluntarily?<br /> <br /> 14) Do you get your first dot in your auspice Renown when you undergo your First Change? I heard this is true, but I can't find it in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9534-fivetomidnight","name":"fivetomidnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T21:29:29-08:00","id":775233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fivetomidnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=775103#post775103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Locus a first edition merit? I can't find in my copy of the second ed core; the closest I can find is Dedicated Locus.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Even more questions!<br /> <br /> 12) If Lunes give the Forsaken their Renown brands, what gives them to the Pure? They do have Renown brands, you can see them glowing &quot;fiery red&quot; if a Blood Talon leads the Siskur-Dah rite.<br /> <br /> 13) When you gain a level of Renown, you get a free Facet for that Renown in a Gift you have. What if you don't want that Facet for any Gift you already have - can you store it voluntarily?<br /> <br /> 14) Do you get your first dot in your auspice Renown when you undergo your First Change? I heard this is true, but I can't find it in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a territorial merit for loci in 1e, but it's pretty handily replaced by Dedicated Locus.<br /> <br /> 12) Their totems recognize it, and their ritual is sanctioned by their Firstborns.<br /> <br /> 13) I believe the book says you can.<br /> <br /> 14) Yes, it's what identifies you as of that auspice. And why you generally behave in a specific fashion during the First Changes. Cahaliths trample and destroy, Irraka hide, Ithaeur face spirits machinations, Rahu slaughter, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T01:04:10-08:00","id":775318,"title":"","content":"In first edition the Pure would give each other their brands via a Rite. That may still be the case in second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:01:09-08:00","id":776279,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\">Claimed Animals<br /> <br /> So specifically, I want to know what would happen if an animal spirit claimed an animal of its species. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">So if a coyote spirit claimed a coyote, what would the problem be? Wouldn't it act just like a really </span><i>good (effective?) </i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">coyote? What kind of damage could it do? Would Werewolves feel obligated to hunt it? If not, could it be an ally? </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:22:31-08:00","id":776293,"title":"","content":"Once a spirit has decided to cross the Gauntlet and Claim a being, it has decided to no longer act by the restraints of its concepts. This would be a coyote that would be not just a really good and effective coyote, but be able to control and possibly even create other coyotes. And since it no longer holds back, it has no reason to fit into the 'natural' cycle of things, so it wouldn't stick to being just an ordinary coyote that would run from man, it would act erratically, attack pets and use its Dread Powers to expand its influence.<br /> <br /> If you've ever seen a 'when animals attack' type horror movie, that's basically the situation you have at hand. An animal makes the particularly un-animal-like decision to not take it anymore and organizes action against the status quo. They don't always have to go out and attack small towns with a massive horde of other animals, but they're likely to supplement their Essence needs with some flesh of man. Some werewolves might ally themselves with them, but if it was with the Forsaken it would always be an uneasy alliance, as werewolves are generally going to be more powerful than any animal, even spirit-enhanced ones, that you would find in your standard territory and the Claimed would always know that it's only surviving as long as the werewolves let it, which wouldn't put it in a comfortable position. Something like that is probably more common in the other groups like the Pure or Ghost Wolves, as well as humanity. The sample K-9 Officer in Tales from the 13th Precinct has a dog, Kita, that is claimed by a dog-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:23:48-08:00","id":776294,"title":"","content":"Would they hunt it? Yes. Why? Because it would become an apex creator. Because it's example would be followed, thus spawning even more claimed down the line. Beyond all that? It Broke the Great Wolf's edict, and The Wolf Must Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:00:26-08:00","id":776318,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that spirits eat their own kind as part of the Shadow's natural order of survival. So a coyote claimed isn't just going to be hunting normal coyote prey, it's also likely to prey on other coyotes for their delicious coyote flesh that tastes so right to it.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what animal, plant, or concept a spirit resonates with, all spirits are predators whose primary instinct is survival. More powerful spirits gain nuance, but the core remains. For 99.9% of spirits, this instinct translates into some variation of 'consume the weak, bring low the strong, gain strength and power'. Some ally themselves with Uratha to gain this power. Others live the laws of the Shadow and take their chances. And some break the rules and take their chances with the soft, fleshy creatures on the other side of the barrier. <br /> <br /> Plus, once a spirit has broken a couple of rules (being on the wrong side of the Gauntlet and possessing flesh), breaking subsequent and greater rules becomes easier, and more damaging to everything around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T21:16:02-08:00","id":776413,"title":"","content":"Well, I have made a new pack, and im starting a new game. Question is this: Are any valid stats for animal have been made in the Nwod 2.0 ? I mean, in the pack there is a wolf blood with a tell that grants him a dog. What would be the stats of that said dog ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:18:39-08:00","id":776425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=776413#post776413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I have made a new pack, and im starting a new game. Question is this: Are any valid stats for animal have been made in the Nwod 2.0 ? I mean, in the pack there is a wolf blood with a tell that grants him a dog. What would be the stats of that said dog ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There will likely be something similar in the second edition core book, but in the meantime the writers have put up <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">this file,</a> containing stats for large and small dogs and a number of other animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T13:18:31-08:00","id":777327,"title":"","content":"Another Quick question.<br /> <br /> In the Nwod first edition, there was some rituals like banish spirits, and exorcism that where explained. Now, in the nWoD 2.0 is the same stuff to exorcice and abjure spirits are still avalaible. I do not have my book with me now. And, since im in the Werewolf forum, the question is clearly about them. Do they have a gift, or a ritual that can do the same ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T13:31:35-08:00","id":777331,"title":"","content":"Yes. Banish and Expel rites do those things. There's about 23 rites in total, and you can see a glimpse of them <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ritualistic/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-30-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:06:40-08:00","id":777877,"title":"","content":"Without the Resonance Shaper merit, could a werewolf change the nature of a spirit by giving them certain flavors of essence? Seems like it could be a fun plot for a crazy werewolf to try out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:33:24-08:00","id":777894,"title":"","content":"It would be up to the spirit to eat said flavors, and would possibly create a magath. I'm not sure how a werewolf could 'give' flavored Essence to a spirit, other than just making it available, as the Essence they offer up in gathra seems to be unrefined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-01-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:13:35-08:00","id":777913,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was wondering about the Essence stored in a werewolf. I figured it was &quot;neutral&quot; flavored. But since the books don't say one way or the other, seems like the sort of thing a weird player could have fun managing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:47:51-08:00","id":777947,"title":"","content":"That seems like a lot of work to keep track of...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:53:42-08:00","id":777950,"title":"","content":"If I were going to bother with that at all, I'd say it's neutral &quot;raw&quot; essence a couple minutes after being ingested by a werewolf. Maybe a number of minutes equal to the rank of the locus/spirit you took it from. That's just what I'd do. <br /> <br /> Or increase that to hours if you want that to be a major factor in spirit dealing or whatever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:09:16-08:00","id":777978,"title":"","content":"One of the ways you could do it would be to use Shadowbind to lock a spirit in a location overflowing with a certain kind of Essence or a locus. It would probably be easier to make a lower Rank, like 1 or 2, spirit give in than a more sophisticated one.<br /> <br /> In our last game I had thought a lot about this stuff. Encouraging certain spirits to Claim otherwise comatose people, maybe even brain dead. Things like Cray from the Book of Spirits would be a powerful ally for packs willing to put up with the risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T18:28:21-08:00","id":778015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=777913#post777913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was wondering about the Essence stored in a werewolf. I figured it was &quot;neutral&quot; flavored. But since the books don't say one way or the other, seems like the sort of thing a weird player could have fun managing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's bits and pieces throughout 1e prior to the Spirit Predation hack in the FCG that indicate the resonance of Essence a werewolf takes in flavors their behavior a bit; I'd say it's less &quot;neutral&quot; and more &quot;a bit of a mishmash of your most recent and/or frequent sources of Essence&quot; and suggest that the effects become more pronounced at the extreme ends of Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T18:51:46-08:00","id":778026,"title":"","content":"There's something about that in Changeling, too, when describing werewolves eating changeling flesh, it mentions it's resonance is tainted with madness. I believe the idea was that that was supposed to affect the werewolf somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-01-2015, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:55:56-08:00","id":784205,"title":"","content":"Which is the point of the BOUNDARY WARD and PREDATOR\u2019S CLAIM Facets? I mean you are really can't use it on the start (cuz your character should have at least PU 5 to spend 5 essence as Instant action. And Boundary Ward really isn't so useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T09:03:09-08:00","id":784208,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536407-question-about-maximum-energy-usage-per-turn\">You can spend turns 'charging' powers that require more Essence than you can spend in an individual turn.</a><br /> <br /> Boundary Ward allows complete and remote detection of a template of your choice for a month, that's incredibly useful. Especially considering you can sit there watching a single entrance and still not detect many of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T19:00:21-08:00","id":784484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=784208#post784208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536407-question-about-maximum-energy-usage-per-turn\">You can spend turns 'charging' powers that require more Essence than you can spend in an individual turn.</a><br /> <br /> Boundary Ward allows complete and remote detection of a template of your choice for a month, that's incredibly useful. Especially considering you can sit there watching a single entrance and still not detect many of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Instant knowledge about trespassing Uratha, Sharta, spirits crossing over the material side... It's invaluable. You can also get a Dedicated Locus and activate it in a single turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T08:46:27-08:00","id":784772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Boundary Ward is potentially the most vital of the Warding gifts. Predator's Claim is very useful in combating spirits if you don't have their Bane or Ban on hand.<br /> <br /> I have a couple questions.<br /> <br /> Any tips on making the Cahalith Predatory Aspect more useful? Aside from &quot;make your NPCs use willpower more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, a Cahalith with Song in Your Heart (merit), War Howl (Gibbous Moon 1), Thousand Throat Howl (Gibbous Moon 4) and War Cry (Merit) spends one turn howling to inspire his pack, another turn howling to make his pack more lethal, yet another turn howling to demoralize his opponents, and another turn still, howling to weaken his opponent. I feel like 4 turns of howling is really silly and it sort of isn't worth being out of the combat for that long, despite the benefits. Meaning some of those abilities are gonna fall into irrelevancy for a Cahalith that has them all if only because of time spent.<br /> <br /> Yes, Song in Your Heart can be done before a battle so that one is situational, but even still. Would you guys allow combining War Cry and Song in Your Heart in your games? Maybe even also War Howl. Maybe allowing one or (both) of the effects to apply during the Facet? Thinking of asking my ST. <br /> <br /> Or am I wrong and is this a normal price to pay for these abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T09:51:08-08:00","id":784816,"title":"","content":"It says Song In Your Heart works like Inspiring does and I don't see them putting down a time frame more than, 'a few words,' though a Song In Your Heart lets you do it while howling, so coupling it with Warcry seems fine. I'd say you could couple Song with any of the howling gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T09:56:38-08:00","id":785448,"title":"","content":"In your games, if your clothes get absorbed into you when you shapeshift is it possible for them to get damaged? For instance, if you get stabbed is there going to be a hole in them when you shift back?<br /> <br /> One of the things that always struck me while reading Mr. Shopping's excellent AP is how utterly filthy and destroyed all of their clothes got over and over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:20:57-08:00","id":785483,"title":"","content":"My character's clothes tend to get drenched in blood but not really torn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:24:53-08:00","id":785487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=785483#post785483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My character's clothes tend to get drenched in blood but not really torn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, if you're bleeding or covered in blood, you'll drench them. Same if you're covered in dust. It gets dirty, but doesn't suffers damage unless they're there to be torn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T04:32:03-08:00","id":785891,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember is that they're not really merging with your skin so much as being shunted off to the weird personal twilight frequency werewolves store their other bodies in when they aren't using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:51:29-08:00","id":786461,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:49:53-08:00","id":796970,"title":"","content":"If I understand it right, the uratha can cause aggravated damage at will with a bite to humans and wolves, provided they are ready to face a breaking point. And want some extra essence.<br /> <br /> Can human include other supernatural creatures? Or is it up to storyteller? I think Vampire, Mages, Sin-Eaters and Changelings are probably included, perhaps with the essence they ingest having some applicable resonance. Promethean, Demon, Mummy are off, I guess. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T13:01:57-08:00","id":796985,"title":"","content":"We've been having it work on mages, sin-eaters, changelings and demons in human guise, though that's based on first edition sin-eaters and changelings. Vampires, mummies and prometheans don't count because they're essentially dead or inorganic.<br /> <br /> Plus our game involves a lot of vampires so we don't want to make it too easy. Ghouls count for humans, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-30-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:15:34-08:00","id":797014,"title":"","content":"What would it take for there to be a new Tribe? Would they have to find a currently unknown Firstborn, or are there other roads to legitimacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:12:02-08:00","id":797035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797014#post797014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would it take for there to be a new Tribe? Would they have to find a currently unknown Firstborn, or are there other roads to legitimacy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You need a powerful spirit both aligned with the hunt and the nature of the Uratha. The Firstborn are best bets for that, and the second edition corebook points out a few that are being sought to create new tribes, but you could conceivably find another spirit to manage it. It would just be very rare to find something so unique that wasn't one of the Firstborn to begin with. Or the Secondborn. Conceivably a werewolf who managed to become a spirit might be able to do it, like the Maeladar from Blasphemies.<br /> <br /> Presumably you'd need a minimum number of werewolves, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-30-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:30:13-08:00","id":797046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797035#post797035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You need a powerful spirit both aligned with the hunt and the nature of the Uratha. The Firstborn are best bets for that, and the second edition corebook points out a few that are being sought to create new tribes, but you could conceivably find another spirit to manage it. It would just be very rare to find something so unique that wasn't one of the Firstborn to begin with. Or the Secondborn. Conceivably a werewolf who managed to become a spirit might be able to do it, like the Maeladar from Blasphemies.<br /> <br /> Presumably you'd need a minimum number of werewolves, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, there are Secondborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:35:42-08:00","id":797048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797046#post797046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, there are Secondborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. They are 'detailed' in a sidebar in Lodges: the Faithful on p18, but they are the children of the Firstborn. Garm, of the Lodge of Garm, for instance, is the son of Fenris.<br /> <br /> The sidebar points out that their true number is unknown and it's not uncommon for spirits seeking to curry werewolf favor to simply claim to be a Secondborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:36:03-08:00","id":797050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797046#post797046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, there are Secondborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is that the Firstborn have spiritual &quot;children&quot; of their own. See the sidebar on pages 18-19 of Lodges: the Faithful for more details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T11:55:01-08:00","id":797447,"title":"","content":"That's also why I'm waiting for &quot;The Pack&quot; and hoping there will be some more content on Danu-Ur, the Creator Wolf (and secret revelation that God-Machine == Danu-Ur)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T18:34:41-08:00","id":797578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797447#post797447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's also why I'm waiting for &quot;The Pack&quot; and hoping there will be some more content on Danu-Ur, the Creator Wolf (and secret revelation that God-Machine == Danu-Ur)</div> </div> </div> </div>I severely doubt we will see any connection with an element of the CofD that is not determining or vital to Werewolf unambiguously exposed like that. It's not in the spirit or established paradigms of the writing going forward. At most, maybe it will be an implied answer... Out of several.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:34:41-08:00","id":798311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797447#post797447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's also why I'm waiting for &quot;The Pack&quot; and hoping there will be some more content on Danu-Ur, the Creator Wolf (and secret revelation that God-Machine == Danu-Ur)</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bO.o Do you have a source where the devs stated this? Has far as I know the so far the only future thing that's going to be expanded on are the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771946#post771946\">Eaters of the Dead</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:18:02-08:00","id":803409,"title":"","content":"This came up in the Werewolf Crossover Questions in the Requiem Forum: Is the &quot;<i>(she) may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn</i>&quot; part of the Glory Facet of the Gift of Strength a one time deal (meaning you can only spend 1 Essence tops on that effect) or you can pay multiple Essence to further multiply your Speed?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:47:10-08:00","id":803420,"title":"","content":"Hah, nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:59:04-08:00","id":803423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803409#post803409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in the Werewolf Crossover Questions in the Requiem Forum: Is the &amp;quot;<i>(she) may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn</i>&amp;quot; part of the Glory Facet of the Gift of Strength a one time deal (meaning you can only spend 1 Essence tops on that effect) or you can pay multiple Essence to further multiply your Speed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think just the once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T04:47:36-08:00","id":803660,"title":"","content":"That was my thought, I read it exactly as the Essence cost of Healing, say you can pay 1 Essence to do x and that's it. But other posters seemed so sure about the incremental thing that tehy made me doubt it, so looking for people's opinion on the matter. It changes things a damm lot if you can pay more essence to keep doubling your Speed.<br /> <br /> If I allow that reading I probably made the multiplication similar to that of celerity (1 + Essence) and/or limiting the Essence you can pay by your Glory dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:00:21-08:00","id":803664,"title":"","content":"It's already pretty limited by Primal Urge. Plus spending a load of Essence to boost your speed for one turn isn't exactly breaking the game, considering the low impact Speed has on things.<br /> <br /> You move from one place to another faster. You could do the same by taking a car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:30:55-08:00","id":803696,"title":"","content":"I have a different vision, I consider Speed does have a great impact, but that varies by playstyle, like any other Trait. It is less a matter of any inbalance and more that I cannot understand how it could be read that other way without really trying to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:31:58-08:00","id":803697,"title":"","content":"The maths had them going supersonic. That's a little game-breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:35:27-08:00","id":803700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803696#post803696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a different vision, I consider Speed does have a great impact, but that varies by playstyle, like any other Trait. It is less a matter of any inbalance and more that I cannot understand how it could be read that other way without really trying to.</div> </div> </div> </div>'By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn.'<br /> <br /> 'and may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn.'<br /> <br /> The first is from a vampire power that allows you to use as much Vitae as you can, the second is the relevant quote from Predator's Unmatched Pursuit. The ability doesn't offer a limit beyond how much you can spend per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803697#post803697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The maths had them going supersonic. That's a little game-breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see them. Going with our previous estimate, though, at Primal Urge 1 you can cap out at 56 mph, already including the doubling effect. Double that at Primal Urge 2 and you have 112 mph, that for 224, that to 448, then finally managing super sonicspeeds at Primal Urge 5, with 896 mph. Since it's only for the turn, though, you're getting about 7 and a half miles of travel.<br /> <br /> I could see it breaking a race, but I still don't think it would have much of an effect on the game in general.<br /> <br /> Still, if you really think it's game breaking, I'd suggest just limiting it to only being able to use it once, but using Elfive's idea, where other uses of Essence can double your speed further with a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:46:08-08:00","id":803709,"title":"","content":"I mean, on one hand, it's not really deserving of the name &quot;Predator's Unmatched Pursuit&quot; if a vampire can outclass it. On the other, I've seen at least one dev indicate that the automatically activating in Kuruth thing includes the speed boost, which if it's unlimited would allow such a werewolf to effectively teleport. On the third hand, teleporting werewolves in death rage are fucking terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:49:39-08:00","id":803710,"title":"","content":"While that's true, death raging werewolves aren't likely to teleport miles away, since they just go directly from potential victim to potential victim. Coupling it with their extreme sensory powers, and if you had a really isolated biome without animals or pollution you could have a gauru in death rage 'teleport' to a prey they see a couple miles away but it would just appear like they charged up on them really fast. Which is what would likely happen even without the speed post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:54:10-08:00","id":803712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=797447#post797447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's also why I'm waiting for &quot;The Pack&quot; and hoping there will be some more content on Danu-Ur, the Creator Wolf (and secret revelation that God-Machine == Danu-Ur)</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't hold your breath while waiting for Forsaken to establish that Creator Wolf is the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Pack has all sorts of tidbits in it but I can't recall whether Danu-Ur gets mentioned anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803409#post803409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in the Werewolf Crossover Questions in the Requiem Forum: Is the &quot;<i>(she) may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn</i>&quot; part of the Glory Facet of the Gift of Strength a one time deal (meaning you can only spend 1 Essence tops on that effect) or you can pay multiple Essence to further multiply your Speed?</div> </div> </div> </div> Er, I *think* my intention when writing it was that it was a singular effect - ie spend 1 Essence, double your speed, that's it - but hypersonic thunderwolves are entertaining so I am not going to condemn the ST who decides otherwise as a heretic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:15:49-08:00","id":804351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803660#post803660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MY MASTER PLAN: SPEED PORTION.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm. Interesting. Good to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:17:15-08:00","id":804352,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Basically it went from Celerity Lite to Celerity Plus. Costly, sure, but insane too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=803700#post803700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn.'<br /> <br /> 'and may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn.'<br /> <br /> The first is from a vampire power that allows you to use as much Vitae as you can, the second is the relevant quote from Predator's Unmatched Pursuit. The ability doesn't offer a limit beyond how much you can spend per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, that is indeed a good precedent...<br /> <br /> Only thing is that as the power may be activated for free, and to avoid time-traveling werewolves Flashpoint Style, maybe limit even the free activation but your max Essence per Turn. So a Primal Urge 3 Uratha in Kuruth could multiply their Speed by 8 (2*2*2).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-09-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T05:27:06-08:00","id":804386,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a fair limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:53:16-08:00","id":804425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=804352#post804352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Basically it went from Celerity Lite to Celerity Plus. Costly, sure, but insane too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmmm, that is indeed a good precedent...<br /> <br /> Only thing is that as the power may be activated for free, and to avoid time-traveling werewolves Flashpoint Style, maybe limit even the free activation but your max Essence per Turn. So a Primal Urge 3 Uratha in Kuruth could multiply their Speed by 8 (2*2*2).</div> </div> </div> </div> As I noted above, the intent of the Facet is that it offers a single doubler, not a stacking one; a Death Raging Uratha gets the doubler for free. However if you want to go with the unofficial hypersonic thunderwolf variant, yours is not a bad way to handle it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:01:38-08:00","id":806737,"title":"","content":"Does Helios have any servants?<br /> <br /> Is there anything about space spirits other than that star idigam in the 2e core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:04:34-08:00","id":806739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806737#post806737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Helios have any servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I should hope so, else that bit about Helions in the rundown of spirit-types is going to be really fucking awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:08:00-08:00","id":806742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806739#post806739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should hope so, else that bit about Helions in the rundown of spirit-types is going to be really fucking awkward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase; does Helios have any mortal or shapechanging servants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:57:21-08:00","id":806768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806742#post806742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me rephrase; does Helios have any mortal or shapechanging servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Baal-Hadad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">s there anything about space spirits other than that star idigam in the 2e core?</span> </div> </div> </div>There's also their call void spirit ability. The books seem to go back and forth about the existence of spirits outside of Earth, but there's nothing I know of in it in Werewolf, what with them being Earthbound. It is explored some in Mage, notably in the Thrice-Great legacy and their write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:05:30-08:00","id":806778,"title":"","content":"The werebulls from War Against the Pure, mind, it's 1e. Also completely optional there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:49:09-08:00","id":806789,"title":"","content":"Given that Luna favors the Forsaken and the Pure rebuke her, is there anything about the Pure searching for patronage from Helios?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T01:50:42-08:00","id":806849,"title":"","content":"Helios is still Luna's brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:19:02-08:00","id":806873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806768#post806768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's the Baal-Hadad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I keep having this nagging feeling that their name is a pun on bull-headed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:11:00-08:00","id":806921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806737#post806737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Helios have any servants?<br /> <br /> Is there anything about space spirits other than that star idigam in the 2e core?</div> </div> </div> </div> We haven't delved much into Helios and what direct influence he may have on the world in 2nd edition as yet, so there's not much to draw on thus far. It will get very, very briefly touched on in the Sundered World but exploring Helios and its agenda further is something I'd like to give more detail on at some stage.<br /> <br /> There is some other info but it's sparse due to lack of space - basic rules for the void spirits that idigam can call, for example, and descriptions of the Warden Moon alluding to its orbit being a guarded boundary that it strides to keep <i>sgnihtthings </i>out. Again (and with a higher priority) Luna and the Moon Courts are things I'd like to give more detail on at some stage, ideally going into depth over what exactly the Warden Moon <i>does </i>a\u200bnd how the Lunes rope Uratha into their schemes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806768#post806768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's the Baal-Hadad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, the <i>gudthabak </i>of the modern age are sun-worshippers and seek advice, aid and totemic blessings from hellions, although what agenda Helios may be pursuing through them isn't detailed. However, it's also indicated that the <i>gudthabak\u200b </i>were not always sun-worshippers, and there isn't much info at all about their origins beyond that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:12:11-08:00","id":806922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806789#post806789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Luna favors the Forsaken and the Pure rebuke her, is there anything about the Pure searching for patronage from Helios?</div> </div> </div> </div> Modern sun-worshipping werewolf sects are mostly dirty, dirty heretics as far as both Forsaken and Pure are concerned.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:47:53-08:00","id":806970,"title":"","content":"I want to point out that we just got confirmation that a future second edition supplement is going to be called &quot;Sundered World.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:18:53-08:00","id":806991,"title":"","content":"Sundered World is the Neolithic chapter of Dark Eras, not a whole supplement in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:19:57-08:00","id":806993,"title":"","content":"I thought Sundered World was the name of Werewolf's Neolithic Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:36:18-08:00","id":807010,"title":"","content":"What stage is Dark Eras at right now, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:27:10-08:00","id":807257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806993#post806993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Sundered World was the name of Werewolf's Neolithic Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was &quot;The Bull and the Bird&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:46:09-08:00","id":807269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=807257#post807257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was &quot;The Bull and the Bird&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think that's the Mage Neolithic, the Werewolf one apparently has a different name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:27:53-08:00","id":807300,"title":"","content":"It was originally called The Bull and the Bird, the name shifted to the Sundered World to better reflect the content due to the addition of Werewolf to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:41:41-08:00","id":807317,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, though I like the Bull and the Bird as a title for its fancifulness. And, of course, you can't delete posts anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:57:20-08:00","id":807381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=806873#post806873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep having this nagging feeling that their name is a pun on bull-headed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hadad\" target=\"_blank\">Nope!</a><br /> <br /> I know nothing about them in Werewolf but I recognise that name. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:50:15-08:00","id":807423,"title":"","content":"Despite the mythological reference, it could still be a pun. I could imagine a young Uratha hearing about them for the first time and someone mumbles through the proper name and they're going: &quot;Wait wait wait, they're all minotaurs, and their name is 'The Bull Headed'? Wow- that's dumb.&quot; &quot;Better than us being called 'People of the Wolf'?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:52:47-08:00","id":807428,"title":"","content":"The best puns are like that. It's a totally legit term that <i>also </i>happens to sound like &quot;bull headed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T13:06:03-08:00","id":810330,"title":"","content":"When and how do spirits increase Rank? I know it involves draining compatible spirits of their Essence and spreading their Influences over our other side of the Gauntlet, but beyond that, it seems kinda nebulous. Could a sufficiently high Rank spirit have a Numen that lets it choose a handful of similar spirits to be its vassals, granting them +1 Rank as long as they follow orders, with all that an increased Rank entails? Or is this somehow a built-in feature of their hierarchies, like the fact they become the Bane of those who are two Ranks or more below them? Likewise, what can make a spirit lose Rank?<br /> <br /> Is the Essence used by spirits somehow different from the one used by G-M Angels and ghosts? I'm asking this because Aether, the Fuel of the Unchained, is defined as a byproduct of the Essence that is processed in Infrastructures. Could a Demon create an unusual Gadget or hi-jack some kind of Infrastructure that harvests Aether from spirits placed in a sort of suspended animation and fed Essence &quot;intravenously&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T13:29:20-08:00","id":810337,"title":"","content":"Spirit, Ghost and Angel essence is <i>slightly</i> different to each other. Sufficiently so that a numen is required to take it from beings of the wrong type. On the other hand, it's sufficiently similar that ''only'' a numen is needed. They're closer to each other than they are to Vitae or Mana. <br /> <br /> As for how they increase in rank, well since it's generally mentioned to occur when gorging on essence, maybe you could say that if a spirit manages to fill its essence pool then any extra it builds up past that can be traded for attribute dots at some rate of exchange, and if it amasses enough of those that it exceeds the maximum dots for it's current rank it gets promoted to a weak example of the rank above, at which point it begins the process all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:13:19-08:00","id":810351,"title":"","content":"IIRC they've deliberately not been specific about mechanics for spirits increasing in rank; it's through some combination of consuming Essence and consuming other spirits. Spreading their Influences on the other side of the gauntlet is just a way to make more Essence they can safely consume be generated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:07:09-08:00","id":810427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=810330#post810330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When and how do spirits increase Rank? I know it involves draining compatible spirits of their Essence and spreading their Influences over our other side of the Gauntlet, but beyond that, it seems kinda nebulous.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's bits of spirit-resonant mechanics spread throughout the gamelines that you can draw inspiration from (Vampire, Mage, and Beast come to mind most directly), but generally speaking Rank Equals Significance. If a spirit has established itself as powerful, old, dangerous, well-connected, or otherwise exemplary on the strong points of its own contextual framework within the spiritual ecology, it's going to be high-Rank. If it can afford to only act directly every once in a while and has numerous and/or powerful subordinates who do most of its day-to-day heavy-lifting, it's probably higher-Rank than a similar spirit that's spread itself thin doing everything on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T03:18:01-08:00","id":810558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=810330#post810330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When and how do spirits increase Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, this is exactly something a group of us Werewolf writers are discussing backstage right now. (We don't have a definitive answer yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:14:19-08:00","id":810594,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've been looking for a system for this as early as Lore of the Forsaken. I usually treat essence spent on boosting attributes like experience on said attribute. Once the spirit spent three times it's current rating, it gets a new dot there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:18:34-08:00","id":818776,"title":"","content":"What qualifies as &quot;having an anatomy&quot; for purposes of the merit Efficient Killer?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing anyone moved to or native to the spirit world is off limits? What about vampires? Claimed in the real world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:23:26-08:00","id":819062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=818776#post818776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What qualifies as &quot;having an anatomy&quot; for purposes of the merit Efficient Killer?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing anyone moved to or native to the spirit world is off limits? What about vampires? Claimed in the real world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that doesn't has the consistency of an ooze. Spirits can be attacked by efficient killer if their forms aren't like, for example, elementals. And even then they probably have a head a Gauru can rip off. Ditto for vampires, ditto for claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T03:07:28-08:00","id":819078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819062#post819062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything that doesn't has the consistency of an ooze. Spirits can be attacked by efficient killer if their forms aren't like, for example, elementals. And even then they probably have a head a Gauru can rip off. Ditto for vampires, ditto for claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that is pretty crazy and really powerful. I always thought most spirits by default were kind of semi-formless, but I guess the Shadow is a lot more like the real world than I thought. I'll have to go back and re-read the Hisil sections.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have a similar interpretation? I'm clarifying this ahead of time for my GM and I because I have a feeling it's going to be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T04:46:55-08:00","id":819113,"title":"","content":"Did something change about Efficient Killer, was there an update or something? AFAIK in sourcebook it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Drawback: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points. Additionally, this immediately sends the character into <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>Wasu-Im</i><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">.</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So it's not really overpowered, there are lots of creatures that technically don't live or seem to have very well-hidden weak points. Plus you don't want to go <i>Wasu-Im </i>at the beginning of the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:27:11-08:00","id":819173,"title":"","content":"Well, you do seem to be using the first version. The current one reads<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Drawback: This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points. Additionally, this is a common kuruth trigger. </div> </div> </div>But the living target bit remains intact. The only thing they changed was to make it more usable for very harmony-balanced werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:24:12-08:00","id":819213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819078#post819078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that is pretty crazy and really powerful. I always thought most spirits by default were kind of semi-formless, but I guess the Shadow is a lot more like the real world than I thought. I'll have to go back and re-read the Hisil sections.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have a similar interpretation? I'm clarifying this ahead of time for my GM and I because I have a feeling it's going to be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if Ephsy's interpretation is absolutelly right. Spirits do not have an anatomy that 's easy to understand or even standardized. Two Murder Spirits won't have the same bodily construction. That's also the reason Medicine is a prerequisite for the Merit. I would say that it is pretty hard, if not impossible, to use Efficient Killer versus Spirits, unless you know the specific creature very well. However, ripping the head of a Vampire instantly kills them, so this should work on most of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:01:53-08:00","id":819253,"title":"","content":"Efficient Killer explicitly does not work on vampires because they are not living targets.<br /> <br /> Need to track down where my hard copy of the book has gotten to in order to check exact wording.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:05:02-08:00","id":819256,"title":"","content":"Here you go.<br /> <br /> Efficient Killer<br /> Prerequisites: Purity \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022\u2022, Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022, may only be used in Gauru form<br /> Effect: Your character is a master of immediate, merciful killing. She knows exactly where to clamp down to end a life in one swift blow. When in Gauru form, any time an opponent is completely denied her Defense \u2014 for example, if she\u2019s sacrificed it for an all-out attack, during a successful ambush, or when activating certain Merits \u2014 you can use Efficient Killer. Sacrifice your Defense for the turn, and you can deal a Killing Blow (see p. 168).<br /> Drawback: This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points. Additionally, this is a common kuruth trigger.<br /> <br /> Killing Blow<br /> When performing a killing blow, you deal damage equal to your full dice pool plus your weapon modifier. You\u2019ve time enough to line up your attack so it avoids your victim\u2019s armor.<br /> While people who kill in combat can justify their actions based on the heat of the moment, performing a killing blow is a premeditated attempt to end a human life without the target having a chance to do anything about it. Going through with a killing blow is a breaking point for humans whether the victim survives or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:18:49-08:00","id":819265,"title":"","content":"And regarding using it on spirits.<br /> <br /> From p186, 'Physical attacks on a Manifest spirit, or one in the Hisil, that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane. Even a spirit that\u2019s solid to its attacker doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:22:49-08:00","id":819268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819213#post819213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if Ephsy's interpretation is absolutelly right. Spirits do not have an anatomy that 's easy to understand or even standardized. Two Murder Spirits won't have the same bodily construction. That's also the reason Medicine is a prerequisite for the Merit. I would say that it is pretty hard, if not impossible, to use Efficient Killer versus Spirits, unless you know the specific creature very well. However, ripping the head of a Vampire instantly kills them, so this should work on most of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me any spirit and I can likely discern on my own where to chew it to kill it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:49:00-08:00","id":819287,"title":"","content":"You can't locate a weak spot that doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:24:00-08:00","id":819357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819268#post819268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Show me any spirit and I can likely discern on my own where to chew it to kill it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with nofather on this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819268#post819268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From p186, 'Physical attacks on a Manifest spirit, or one in the Hisil, that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane. Even a spirit that\u2019s solid to its attacker doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits weaknesses, their &quot;exposed throat and beating heart&quot;, are their Bane and Ban.<br /> <br /> On a side note: By stating that this is a Common Kuruth Trigger, does this mean that only Werewolves at the extreme spectrum of Harmony suffer the Wasu-Im state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:45:35-08:00","id":819369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819357#post819357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note: By stating that this is a Common Kuruth Trigger, does this mean that only Werewolves at the extreme spectrum of Harmony suffer the Wasu-Im state?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so, it's certainly how I'd rule it. 8-10, 2-0.<br /> <br /> The hard part is that you have to be in gauru form to do it, in which case you're likely attacking things already, every round. It doesn't seem like something you could do consistently. I could see someone, at the back of a group, reflexively shifting to gauru and doing it with their first attack. Gauru doesn't really seem like the sneaking-up-on-you form, so ambushing people feels like it would be hard to do.<br /> <br /> The two big ways to take advantage of it would be to influence people with Atavism Lunacy, which causes them to make all-out attacks, resulting in a loss of their Defenses and an easy way to mow them down. The other would be the Father's Form Gift, but once you attack you follow the usual rules for gauru form and presumably that involves the 'once per scene' rule. Still, it would allow you to start some easy ambushes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:56:08-08:00","id":819373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819369#post819369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe so, it's certainly how I'd rule it. 8-10, 2-0.<br /> <br /> The hard part is that you have to be in gauru form to do it, in which case you're likely attacking things already, every round. It doesn't seem like something you could do consistently. I could see someone, at the back of a group, reflexively shifting to gauru and doing it with their first attack. Gauru doesn't really seem like the sneaking-up-on-you form, so ambushing people feels like it would be hard to do.<br /> <br /> The two big ways to take advantage of it would be to influence people with Atavism Lunacy, which causes them to make all-out attacks, resulting in a loss of their Defenses and an easy way to mow them down. The other would be the Father's Form Gift, but once you attack you follow the usual rules for gauru form and presumably that involves the 'once per scene' rule. Still, it would allow you to start some easy ambushes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As shapeshifting is reflexive, you can remain in Urhan, and as soon you detect someone sacrificing their defense, spend 1 Essence to cut their action and efficiently kill them. As written, you can even be back at Urhan at the end of your turn to be prepared for the next target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:01:04-08:00","id":819375,"title":"","content":"That's true, but it's still limited to the once per scene thing. But odds are if they're going to be affected by Atavism Lunacy, they'd probably just fit under gauru's Down &amp; Dirty Combat, too.<br /> <br /> To get a lot of use out of it, at least. There's always the chance some other werewolf or changeling or hive-claimed or mage is going to use an all-out attack and it's certainly a nice card to have up your sleeves in those opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:08:15-08:00","id":819450,"title":"","content":"I had a question regarding death rage; the books says all packmates near a raging Wolf have to check or enter rage themselves. It also talks about a raging wolf attacking packmates and wolf-blooded if they don't join in. Is there a mechanic outside of individual tells for the blooded to rage or would their raging packmate leave them be once they joined in the frenzy by attacking enemies? Just wondering how that all works or if any blooded near a wolf in basu-im is just toast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:31:13-08:00","id":819466,"title":"","content":"The book says all <i>werewolf </i>packmates check to enter rage.<br /> <br /> 'Werewolf packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell the raging werewolf fall into Basu-Im after a turn.'<br /> <br /> The only ones free from attack are other werewolves in Basu-Im. Humans and wolf-blooded, spirits and vampires, cars and buildings, they're all free game. I might make an exception for a Wolf-Blooded with the Anger Issues Tell, but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:31:45-08:00","id":819467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819375#post819375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>That's true, but it's still limited to the once per scene thing.</b> But odds are if they're going to be affected by Atavism Lunacy, they'd probably just fit under gauru's Down &amp; Dirty Combat, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're referring to Chase Down, no, it doesn't seems to be the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:44:25-08:00","id":819479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819467#post819467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're referring to Chase Down, no, it doesn't seems to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to the ability to shift into gauru form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:37:30-08:00","id":820427,"title":"","content":"So my players went to war with local vampires and one is using the merit Nowhere to Hide on one of the Kindred. Problem is, the main haven of the Kindred is shrouded in Obfuscate 5. Not sure how I should resolve this. I though clash of wills, but I don't know if a Merit like that could trump a powerful discipline. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:43:05-08:00","id":820430,"title":"","content":"I'd say it would allow them to pinpoint the location of the safe place, but then there wouldn't appear to be anything there when they get there. <br /> <br /> Like, &quot;I <i>know</i> it's around here, where the fuck is it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:49:51-08:00","id":820435,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I like that idea!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T00:57:11-08:00","id":822187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=819466#post819466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says all <i>werewolf </i>packmates check to enter rage.<br /> <br /> 'Werewolf packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell the raging werewolf fall into Basu-Im after a turn.'<br /> <br /> The only ones free from attack are other werewolves in Basu-Im. Humans and wolf-blooded, spirits and vampires, cars and buildings, they're all free game. I might make an exception for a Wolf-Blooded with the Anger Issues Tell, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't forget that basu-im WWs <i>won't </i>attack their <i>packmates</i> that are also in basu-im. This means two packs of werewolves fighting can have 1 entire pack raging while the other keeps their shit together.<br /> <br /> Also, when you rage, you choose targets (randomly?) which could include packmates, until they fall into Basu-im.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:18:23-08:00","id":825244,"title":"","content":"I have been looking in the 2E werewolf books trying to find some implication to werewolf population. While I know that a population are not directly stated I was wondering if there was a generally agreed population ratio?<br /> <br /> Also do pack in a city form up by Alpha/Beta/Omega order or was that thrown out in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:22:48-08:00","id":825246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=825244#post825244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been looking in the 2E werewolf books trying to find some implication to werewolf population. While I know that a population are not directly stated I was wondering if there was a generally agreed population ratio?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. It's all up to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also do pack in a city form up by Alpha/Beta/Omega order or was that thrown out in 2E? </div> </div> </div>They can, but it's not a requirement. It's one of the pack creation questions, actually, whether or not your pack hunts like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:00:42-08:00","id":825265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=825246#post825246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah. It's all up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They can, but it's not a requirement. It's one of the pack creation questions, actually, whether or not your pack hunts like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that. But that does not answer my second question. I may have not explained clearly, what I meant was are some parks larger and more important then others such as what they have in Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:14:04-08:00","id":825272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=825265#post825265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for that. But that does not answer my second question. I may have not explained clearly, what I meant was are some parks larger and more important then others such as what they have in Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, pack formation, not pack formation.<br /> <br /> We haven't seen any example packs to know. While some packs are larger or more influential than others, presumably they aren't strictly ranked on an alpha-to-omega system. Unless you want them to be. There's a lot of packless werewolves in the example settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:19:47-08:00","id":825277,"title":"","content":"Well glade I was not missing something. Thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:18:41-08:00","id":828462,"title":"","content":"So, at some of the higher Primal Urge scores the werewolf has to eat the flesh of carnivores. At first I thought this meant freaky stuff like Lion, but couldn't they just eat most fish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:30:09-08:00","id":828470,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the intent of it was to make it a meat of predatory mammals or stuff like sharks. You know, that whole progression - you need to sustain yourself on meat, switch to raw stuff and then to a bloody chunks of bear you maul and end up with chewing on all those death and violence spirits at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T16:00:05-08:00","id":828482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828462#post828462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, at some of the higher Primal Urge scores the werewolf has to eat the flesh of carnivores. At first I thought this meant freaky stuff like Lion, but couldn't they just eat most fish?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Old Iron Masters love themselves some sushi.<br /> <br /> You can also transition higher on the foodchain. Essence taken from a Siskur Dah will always prove nutritious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:45:14-08:00","id":828564,"title":"","content":"1. How have people handled in character knowledge of Kuruth triggers? Does your character just know somehow? Do you work it out in character? I guess by default you don't start right after your first change, so you could have figured it out off screen before the start of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> 2. If I'm reading the kuruth rules correctly, if some forsaken and pure are fighting and everybody winds up in kuruth they just stop fighting each other and go on a rampage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T21:54:50-08:00","id":828605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828564#post828564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. How have people handled in character knowledge of Kuruth triggers? Does your character just know somehow? Do you work it out in character? I guess by default you don't start right after your first change, so you could have figured it out off screen before the start of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say most werewolves figure it out within the early days after their first change. For most starting characters it will have happened in their backstories, but those who start out Wolf-Blooded and First Change in play will have to sort it out (unless it carries over from a Tell like Anger Issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828564#post828564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If I'm reading the kuruth rules correctly, if some forsaken and pure are fighting and everybody winds up in kuruth they just stop fighting each other and go on a rampage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T01:11:34-08:00","id":828660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828470#post828470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the intent of it was to make it a meat of predatory mammals or stuff like sharks.</div> </div> </div> </div>A predator is a predator. Don't go disrespecting Cod. Some species of those things will eat each other given the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:18:54-08:00","id":828738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828564#post828564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If I'm reading the kuruth rules correctly, if some forsaken and pure are fighting and everybody winds up in kuruth they just stop fighting each other and go on a rampage?</div> </div> </div> </div>A developer amended that you only show mercy for your packmates, so two packs in Kuruth still try to rip each other apart, inefficiently at it may end up being. Good luck if someone's Kuruth last longer than yours, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:13:25-08:00","id":828769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828738#post828738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A developer amended that you only show mercy for your packmates, so two packs in Kuruth still try to rip each other apart, inefficiently at it may end up being. Good luck if someone's Kuruth last longer than yours, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only inefficient if the werewolves don't start taking bites and swallows of each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T08:28:35-08:00","id":828803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828769#post828769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's only inefficient if the werewolves don't start taking bites and swallows of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated Damage through eating is only done to Humans and Wolves, as far as I know. You can't do it to Werewolves, can you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:08:08-08:00","id":828818,"title":"","content":"P285. 'Another important time cannibalism can come up is in a battle between werewolves. If two Uratha face off in Gauru form, they\u2019re highly unlikely to cause any lasting harm, until one of them can no longer maintain the form. The first to fall out of Gauru loses. Cannibalism offers a trump in that argument. Since eating from another Uratha causes potentially deadly aggravated damage, that\u2019s one way to stop a rampaging Gauru. Particularly for the less potent Uratha, taking a bite out of her enemy could turn the tide of battle completely.'<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438246-eating-for-essence\">This question has come up</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage\">and been answered</a>, a lot. While the Essence section does say, 'They can eat the flesh of wolves and humans.' I believe 'wolves' was referring to 'werewolves,' not just the mundane wolves that aren't in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:20:26-08:00","id":828822,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves in death rage inherently avoid consuming (i.e. aggravated damage) other wolves and humans? Or is this just Forsaken propaganda?<br /> <br /> I'd personally run it on a case-by-case basis; most Forsaken and Ivory Claws wouldn't but a reckless Predator King or someone with the Hunger Kuruth trigger would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:24:09-08:00","id":828824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828822#post828822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves in death rage inherently avoid consuming (i.e. aggravated damage) other wolves and humans? Or is this just Forsaken propaganda?<br /> <br /> I'd personally run it on a case-by-case basis; most Forsaken and Ivory Claws wouldn't but a reckless Predator King or someone with the Hunger Kuruth trigger would.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were letting a character do it, if they decided to consume based on their Blood I'd give them a full Willpower refresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:29:10-08:00","id":828828,"title":"","content":"A case by case basis is probably a good way to do it, level of hunger and Essence, difficulty of opponent can have a big impact on whether it happens or not. I don't think tribe would have much sway in the matter. But it doesn't seem like the kind of thing you would suffer the 'normal' problems with, as once Kuruth is active you're not really making decisions anymore. A character who falls to Kuruth a lot would be seen as a loose cannon, of course, but I imagine all but the most uptight of packs would see things that happen <i>during</i> Death Rage as a horrible accident. You could blame someone for letting it happen, but the actual act would be hard to really pin on, and Kuruth is something all werewolves can at least understand.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth noting that the shartha seem to be the only 'common' antagonists werewolves have no natural ability to inflict aggravated damage on. They do not have banes, and unless they're riding a human I wouldn't count them as human. While in shard forms they are easy enough to kill without aggravated damage, there are the monstrous beshilu rokhan and azlu azaraths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:48:39-08:00","id":828838,"title":"","content":"It feels kind of strange, though. If I bite a chunk out of you and spit, it is lethal. If I bite it and swallow, it is aggravated? The intention is the trigger? I don't remember reading indeep information about this in the book. It seems a little confusing, no wonder a lot of people are not sure how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T10:01:54-08:00","id":828844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828838#post828838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels kind of strange, though. If I bite a chunk out of you and spit, it is lethal. If I bite it and swallow, it is aggravated? The intention is the trigger? I don't remember reading indeep information about this in the book. It seems a little confusing, no wonder a lot of people are not sure how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not strange when you consider you're a living scion to the Great Wolf, who ate gods away in this same fashion. Ate them, not bit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T10:47:51-08:00","id":828860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828838#post828838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels kind of strange, though. If I bite a chunk out of you and spit, it is lethal. If I bite it and swallow, it is aggravated? The intention is the trigger? I don't remember reading indeep information about this in the book. It seems a little confusing, no wonder a lot of people are not sure how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you bite them to take Essence from them it's aggravated, and that requires eating the flesh. If you've ever been bit by animals they don't always rip flesh off with every bite.<br /> <br /> Also try and keep in mind a single attack roll does not have to represent a single bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:26:05-08:00","id":828883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828844#post828844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not strange when you consider you're a living scion to the Great Wolf, who ate gods away in this same fashion. Ate them, not bit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the lore that bugs me, it is the way the choice is presented to the player. As it is written, you simple change the damage type by deciding to swallow the meat, which feels strange. If I decide to swallow the meat from Shartha, sharks, werebears, Vampires, I won't deal Aggravated damage, even though the same attack was used. I know we can change descriptions to compensate for the unintuitiveness of it, but it seems like a &quot;band-aid&quot; instead of a proper fix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828844#post828844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you bite them to take Essence from them it's aggravated, and that requires eating the flesh. If you've ever been bit by animals they don't always rip flesh off with every bite.<br /> <br /> Also try and keep in mind a single attack roll does not have to represent a single bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the thing that is hard to accept is the fact the very same attack, ripping as much flesh as you want and swalloing it, won't do aggravated to a Vampire or a shark or a bear. The thing that makes it unintuitive is that swallowing happens AFTER the attack, not before. Suppose Mary, a wolfblooded packmate, rips some flesh from the leg of a man, which is lethal damage, and then give it to her Uratha packmate to eat. He eats it to recover Essence, and suddenly the wounds become aggravated? Obviously not, and it is that strangeness that bothers me.<br /> <br /> Hell, it even works with the very same Werewolf: Turn into Gauru, rip some flesh from the victim (lethal), and then eat it later...<br /> <br /> This feature was probably added to increase the temptation of chosing to cannibalize, which wasn't as present as the developers wanted in the 1ed, however, it feels forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:47:09-08:00","id":828896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828883#post828883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the thing that is hard to accept is the fact the very same attack, ripping as much flesh as you want and swalloing it, won't do aggravated to a Vampire or a shark or a bear. The thing that makes it unintuitive is that swallowing happens AFTER the attack, not before. Suppose Mary, a wolfblooded packmate, rips some flesh from the leg of a man, which is lethal damage, and then give it to her Uratha packmate to eat. He eats it to recover Essence, and suddenly the wounds become aggravated? Obviously not, and it is that strangeness that bothers me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could shoot a vampire in the chest with a shotgun and it wouldn't necessarily cause aggravated damage. They reduce Lethal damage to Bashing, except with supernatural attacks like werewolf bites, and it takes special magic attacks or banes like sunlight to do aggravated damage to begin with. In regards to bears and sharks, Lethal damage is more than enough to kill. It's Lethal. In Gauru form your claws do +2 Lethal, and you've got a +3 to Strength. All you need is 5 successes to do 7 Lethal and basically kill your average person in one roll.<br /> <br /> The biting for Essence isn't something that you do after, it's something you do at the time. While the metaphysics of it are scattered across books, the Essence a person has in them is basically some part of their soul and life energy. Even if you cut a person's arm off, it's still there, because the body is just flesh. But the teeth of the Great Hunter are more than that, they're weapons that were used to kill gods. So when you unleash that, and take a part of your victim's flesh and spirit, you do more than Lethal damage. But no, obviously you don't do voodoo damage by eating already separated flesh, though there may be a Gift or rite for that somewhere. It's the attack that does it, a specific attack that's targeting not just flesh. It's not just because you decided to swallow.<br /> <br /> I thought people's problems were because it referred to 'wolves and humans,' not that people thought you could save someone's flesh, eat it later, and their wounds would turn from Lethal to Aggravated, which isn't how it works. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, it even works with the very same Werewolf: Turn into Gauru, rip some flesh from the victim (lethal), and then eat it later...<br /> <br /> This feature was probably added to increase the temptation of chosing to cannibalize, which wasn't as present as the developers wanted in the 1ed, however, it feels forced. </div> </div> </div>You could always get Essence from eating flesh in first edition. It didn't do extra damage.<br /> <br /> But, again, the only 'later' is immediately when the attack is done. 'They can eat the flesh of wolves and humans. For every point of damage caused by an Uratha\u2019s bite, they can choose to ingest the flesh and gain a point of Essence. This is a stark violation of the Oath of the Moon, and always a Harmony breaking point toward the spirit. When devouring flesh for Essence, the Uratha causes aggravated wounds. '","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:11:16-08:00","id":828906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828883#post828883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the lore that bugs me, it is the way the choice is presented to the player. As it is written, you simple change the damage type by deciding to swallow the meat, which feels strange. If I decide to swallow the meat from Shartha, sharks, werebears, Vampires, I won't deal Aggravated damage, even though the same attack was used.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game? They do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:12:57-08:00","id":828907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828896#post828896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always get Essence from eating flesh in first edition. It didn't do extra damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the point. Now they added the ability to cause Aggravated Damage to Werewolves by doing it, which is an incentive to use it more. I remember reading on the blog posts that they wanted to emphasize cannibalism in 2ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828896#post828896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought people's problems were because it referred to 'wolves and humans,' not that people thought you could save someone's flesh, eat it later, and their wounds would turn from Lethal to Aggravated, which isn't how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm having a hard time being able to express my self. The mechanic just feels a bit forced, by a Game Design point of view. Why not allow Werewolf bites to deal aggravated to other werewolves and humans anyway? Claws if you want Lethal, Jaws if you want Aggravated. Seems more intuitive to the player. I guess it is just a matter of my view about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:14:00-08:00","id":828908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828906#post828906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my game? They do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels more consistent to me this way, I will probably rule something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:20:02-08:00","id":828916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828907#post828907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm having a hard time being able to express my self. The mechanic just feels a bit forced, by a Game Design point of view. Why not allow Werewolf bites to deal aggravated to other werewolves and humans anyway? Claws if you want Lethal, Jaws if you want Aggravated. Seems more intuitive to the player. I guess it is just a matter of my view about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The different attacks all work pretty differently. In human form you're going to have a harder time biting someone, likely needing a grapple. In certain other forms, you can use them to establish grapples, or while grappling, or without needing to grapple, just as in certain forms they do more or less damage. Then you get special modifiers from merits and one form has a bite that does +3L with armor piercing.<br /> <br /> Add to the fact that some people don't want to play up the cannibalism part of the game and suddenly they could never use their bite attacks without deeming their character as a failure that should be tossed because they made a bite attack.<br /> <br /> It's just a choice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:26:35-08:00","id":828918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I bite a chunk out of you and spit, it is lethal. If I bite it and swallow, it is aggravated? The intention is the trigger? </div> </div> </div>I would go more into direction of &quot;I rip the flesh of his body!&quot; vs &quot;I devour him whole!&quot;. You know, canniballising someone being more savage act and whatnot while even in the most vicious fight you are actually fighting and not focus solely on dat delicious gluteus. Also it's a spirit magic symbollic thing, makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:52:55-08:00","id":828960,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say that the aggravated damage bite <i>is</i> noticeably different to a normal one. You're sort of pulling their life force out with your teeth. (Which I would probably represent as requiring less actual meat to get the same amount of essence than if you eat a corpse or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:58:07-08:00","id":828967,"title":"","content":"Does it say werewolves get Essence for eating dead or separated flesh? I suppose if you look at its structure as damage can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T16:06:00-08:00","id":829004,"title":"","content":"It was certainly the case in first edition, but I'm honestly not sure about second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T16:51:32-08:00","id":829024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=828967#post828967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it say werewolves get Essence for eating dead or separated flesh? I suppose if you look at its structure as damage can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of the Field seems to eat corpses exhumed from graveyards primarily, with the occasional ritualistic feast of living flesh. I'm not sure if that means they get anything out of it besides a meal, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T17:10:49-08:00","id":829030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=829024#post829024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lodge of the Field seems to eat corpses exhumed from graveyards primarily, with the occasional ritualistic feast of living flesh. I'm not sure if that means they get anything out of it besides a meal, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might also be due to his Gluttony Touch. Something he might encourage others to do due to his benefiting from the Devourer ability, as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Devourer:</b> Lycaon-Ur gains twice as much Essence as normal from consuming human flesh. Doing so also heals him for a single point of lethal or bashing damage per point of Essence gained in this way, and he can remove a Tilt after consuming an entire body in this way (even a persistent Tilt). Whenever a member of the Lodge of the Field consumes human flesh, Lycaon-Ur gains a single point of Essence from the feeding. Lycaon-Ur can consume anything and draw sustenance from it without suffering any sort of detrimental effects, toxicity or the like. Anything he consumes is annihilated utterly, and his bite attack deals aggravated rather than lethal damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Hungerer: </b>Lycaon-Ur is continually hungry and must spend a point of Essence every day that he goes without consuming human flesh. Simply by touching another character, he can cause them to gain the Gluttony Vice. A character so affected can be subject to the Claim manifestation by hunger spirits without needing to be Controlled first.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:19:28-08:00","id":835861,"title":"","content":"What exactly counts as a &quot;supernatural creature&quot; for the purposes of &quot;The Other&quot; Kuruth trigger? I would describe werewolves and spirits both as supernatural creatures, but I imagine if either of those counted you'd have a character that literally fell to Wasu-Im every scene at Passive, most scenes at Common, and at least every combat at Specific. Is it only supposed to count non-werewolf major splats? Anything supernatural that isn't covered in W:tF? Are you supposed to pick one kind of supernatural creature that sets it off for your character (so you might be Triggered by vampires but not prometheans, for example)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:57:00-08:00","id":835879,"title":"","content":"It's possible the Other is meant for more lone wolf and denier types.<br /> <br /> For a more 'normal' trigger of the unnatural, I'd use the list under Scent the Unnatural on p126. Spirits and werewolves don't count being 'natural' to werewolves, not something 'Other.' But Ridden, Hosts, vampires, ghouls, mages and so forth would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T12:36:12-08:00","id":835937,"title":"","content":"I partly agree with nofather - no spirits and no werewolves, but &quot;Other&quot; stuff - Ridden, Hosts, vampires, other minor and major templates, Horrors of different types, Idigam, Strix etc.<br /> <br /> I would rule though that it's applicable when the encounter is truly &quot;alien&quot;. If the Uratha is for the first time a target of strange powers of worm-things cult worshipping dead god, it is a Kuruth trigger. If he keeps fighting them in a chronicle and hunts cult members one by one, he isn't triggered every time he sees them. On the other hand, if the dead god (Idigam? big Horror template?) is summoned into this reality, it will trigger him again.<br /> Same with, say, Hosts. Seeing horrors of disease-ridden Beshilu for the first time will trigger Kuruth, but for n-th - not. On the other hand, if new strain of Beshilu will be encountered (those mole-mutant burrowing hybrids) it will trigger poor werewolf again.<br /> <br /> Though I agree - Kuruth triggers and rules around them need a bit more description and clarification. Some players don't know how many should they pick or if they can pick from different categories, some triggers seem a lot more broad (tasting blood vs being in area of a Wound vs pack member suffering lethal wound) than others or not applicable to every chronicle etc.<br /> <br /> So, to sum up - look at the intent of why player chooses specific Kuruth trigger. If he chooses &quot;Wounds&quot;, they should appear in chronicle. If &quot;Blood&quot;, eating or not eating people should be a theme in it. If &quot;Other&quot;, you should focus on challenging player with unknown, strange dangers that they don't know about/never previously encountered. In the chronicle it might be established that player pack is fighting Azlu on their territory for 10 years now, but if PC encounter never seen before tunnels/Azlu colonies in Gauntlet or mutated Azlu bloated with Blightings and their essence, then yeah, there should be some heavy Death Raging over the new horrors and travesties that happened and defy previously known rules/order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","user":"Miriander","date":". 02-23-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:54:27-08:00","id":836005,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, depends on what the character has experienced before and what they're used to thinking of as natural vs. unnatural. Thanks for the ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T16:35:37-08:00","id":836093,"title":"","content":"Can a Spirit see across the Gauntlet similar to how Uratha do? If not, how could one achieve this, Numina, Influence or Manifestation?<br /> <br /> Could Spirits in concert with their Umia or a powerful patron become a very capable information/spy network for not just the Shadow, but the Material as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T16:59:07-08:00","id":836102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836093#post836093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Spirit see across the Gauntlet similar to how Uratha do? If not, how could one achieve this, Numina, Influence or Manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha seem to be able to do it because they belong to both sides of the Gauntlet. Spirit perception seems to be based around their Influence. From p184, 'Spirits can sense sources of Essenec appropriate for their needs from up to a mile away, even across the Gauntlet without penalty.' I believe that, while in a locus' zone of influence they are able to peek across at will, as well, based on p179, 'No spirits require the Reaching Manifestation effect to use their powers across the Gauntlet in a locus' zone of influence.' Which, combined with the mentions that a locus is 'especially close to the Hisil' suggests to me some sort of permeability that extends beyond Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could Spirits in concert with their Umia or a powerful patron become a very capable information/spy network for not just the Shadow, but the Material as well? </div> </div> </div>Sure. Though one problem I can think of off the top of my head would be that a spirit of information isn't really capable of parsing information to determine whether it is useful or not. A network of security camera spirits throughout the city could watch everything for you, but I would imagine they would for the most part have trouble picking out a specific person or act out for you. It's not an insurmountable obstacle, but one of the bumps you might find.<br /> <br /> One might have more luck with an individually powerful spirit, like a high ranking spirit of secrets, who would likely know most if not all of the secrets of an area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-23-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:04:53-08:00","id":836107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836093#post836093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Spirit see across the Gauntlet similar to how Uratha do? If not, how could one achieve this, Numina, Influence or Manifestation?<br /> <br /> Could Spirits in concert with their Umia or a powerful patron become a very capable information/spy network for not just the Shadow, but the Material as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best way to model Material Vision would be with a Manifestation, because it's a way for the spirit to interact with the world. I usually let spirits with something of their purview in the vicinity to be able to perceive it instinctively, even on the other side of the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T22:31:14-08:00","id":836249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836107#post836107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best way to model Material Vision would be with a Manifestation, because it's a way for the spirit to interact with the world. I usually let spirits with something of their purview in the vicinity to be able to perceive it instinctively, even on the other side of the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836102#post836102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One might have more luck with an individually powerful spirit, like a high ranking spirit of secrets, who would likely know most if not all of the secrets of an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both excellent clarifications and suggestions. So if an Uratha asked a tree/dog/car Spirit what it witnessed about the material side of things, it could give an answers (from the Spirits perspective), just ones you would expect from a Shadow predator.<br /> <br /> However, if you wanted to keep tabs on everything, creating a spiritual surveillance network, you are better off with a powerful Spirit of that type who can use its Influence or Numina to come up with those answers.<br /> <br /> I ask these questions because I'm considering angles for how to run a more espionage kind of game in Werewolf, any other suggestions would be appreciated if available. I realize the idea is a bit out of theme, but with Hunters, Cults, Spirits, Hosts, and Pure I think there's a lot of reasons for Uratha to be secretive and cautious enough to evoke an espionage feel, they just have the best survivable 'going loud' option built in and conversely the most dangerous to start a larger war or set off tenuous chains of events.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T01:08:22-08:00","id":836292,"title":"","content":"The ability to peek across the gauntlet is described in the book as &quot;The senses of a spirit&quot;. Not a &quot;half-spirit&quot;, just a &quot;spirit&quot;. So it seems logical that spirits can do everything described in that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T07:14:41-08:00","id":836392,"title":"","content":"Elfive brings up a good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836249#post836249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask these questions because I'm considering angles for how to run a more espionage kind of game in Werewolf, any other suggestions would be appreciated if available. I realize the idea is a bit out of theme, but with Hunters, Cults, Spirits, Hosts, and Pure I think there's a lot of reasons for Uratha to be secretive and cautious enough to evoke an espionage feel, they just have the best survivable 'going loud' option built in and conversely the most dangerous to start a larger war or set off tenuous chains of events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bale Hounds are good for it, but you could also have a rite that allows Pure or Forsaken to seem like members of the other faction. Alternatively give things like Hosts more dominance in the territory, so that one might always be being watched. Spiders are basically everywhere, and any city can have a huge population of rats, all acting as practically invisible spies for more powerful masters. While part of the problem might be all the excellent sensory powers of werewolves that really give them a lot of tactical awareness, Shadow Gifts are available to any werewolf, and a Pure can use Iron Slave to drive around a city, spying on people through the windshield of a car they 'possess.' And of course there's Skin Thief, letting you impersonate someone else, or Beast Talker allowing you to strike up conversations with animal spies.<br /> <br /> There's a lot you can do with the espionage angle. I've mentioned this a lot but our first game, based on the first edition core book, had the Pure and Forsaken looking the same, without the visual difference later brought up where one has glowing silver renown and the other has glaring red. 'Everyone' had thought the Pure were defeated and driven out of the city years ago, but once we found out one prominent pack was Pure it sort of led to a ripple effect that revealed half a dozen others as Pure as well and we didn't know who to trust. If you want to go rules as written that's not something that can be done, but you still can do it with Bale Hounds or Ghost Wolves, and nothing's keeping a protectorate of Forsaken from being an oppressive and tyrannical regime. If you throw an idigam into the mix you can have werewolves controlled by spirits or ghosts or basically whatever they want to shove in there.<br /> <br /> And regarding the spirit network thing, a pro for that angle is that a more powerful spirit might be able to recognize things as more important or relevant to what werewolves might want to know. It could also be a higher up in an umia, which would give it access to those further down the food chain who would offer it tithe of Essence and information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T13:12:02-08:00","id":836626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=836392#post836392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive brings up a good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are good for it, but you could also have a rite that allows Pure or Forsaken to seem like members of the other faction. Alternatively give things like Hosts more dominance in the territory, so that one might always be being watched. Spiders are basically everywhere, and any city can have a huge population of rats, all acting as practically invisible spies for more powerful masters. While part of the problem might be all the excellent sensory powers of werewolves that really give them a lot of tactical awareness, Shadow Gifts are available to any werewolf, and a Pure can use Iron Slave to drive around a city, spying on people through the windshield of a car they 'possess.' And of course there's Skin Thief, letting you impersonate someone else, or Beast Talker allowing you to strike up conversations with animal spies.<br /> <br /> There's a lot you can do with the espionage angle. I've mentioned this a lot but our first game, based on the first edition core book, had the Pure and Forsaken looking the same, without the visual difference later brought up where one has glowing silver renown and the other has glaring red. 'Everyone' had thought the Pure were defeated and driven out of the city years ago, but once we found out one prominent pack was Pure it sort of led to a ripple effect that revealed half a dozen others as Pure as well and we didn't know who to trust. If you want to go rules as written that's not something that can be done, but you still can do it with Bale Hounds or Ghost Wolves, and nothing's keeping a protectorate of Forsaken from being an oppressive and tyrannical regime. If you throw an idigam into the mix you can have werewolves controlled by spirits or ghosts or basically whatever they want to shove in there.<br /> <br /> And regarding the spirit network thing, a pro for that angle is that a more powerful spirit might be able to recognize things as more important or relevant to what werewolves might want to know. It could also be a higher up in an umia, which would give it access to those further down the food chain who would offer it tithe of Essence and information.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all fantastic story hooks and clarifications. Thanks again so much.<br /> <br /> There's not a lot of info released on Bale Hounds in 2e yet, but Idigam and Hosts are covered well enough. Maybe something where you don't know who to trust because you don't know whose been converted to the Idigams service?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Hosts are closing in on Herd side of things, trying to set up lairs and regular food sources through a... dare I say... web of information networks and spies?<br /> <br /> Yeah, those can hook people pretty well and still capture the bloody beating heart of Forsaken. Thanks again developers and writers of Werewolf!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T13:20:33-08:00","id":836631,"title":"","content":"Nothing says the Host couldn't have been converted to the Idigam's service first, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:47:25-08:00","id":839211,"title":"","content":"Is a fetish rifle that lets an Irraka use the gift Eviscerate with firearms reasonable? Is that even something a fetish could do? It seems like it might be a little powerful. How many dots do you think it should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:52:26-08:00","id":839217,"title":"","content":"A 3 dot Fetish can have, 'a modification to a specific Facet that allows it to be used in new ways.' So you can do it. It certainly would be a little powerful but Eviscerate is powerful on its own. It has a nice limitation in that it can only be used against unaware or surprised opponents, though, so it's not something you can use in a running gunfight. Seems the staple of snipers, I'd be surprised if it wasn't commonplace in the Lodge of Gargoyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:58:03-08:00","id":839222,"title":"","content":"The description for the three dot level of Fetish mentions it can modify a Facet to work in a new way, so that seems like a good baseline if the effect is acceptable.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:20:38-08:00","id":839281,"title":"","content":"How do you describe the spirit/shadow world and how dangerous do you believe it should be for werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11379-mrimperator","name":"MrImperator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:38:46-08:00","id":839291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrImperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=839281#post839281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you describe the spirit/shadow world and how dangerous do you believe it should be for werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acrozatarim, a writer for Werewolf, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\">wrote up this great description of the Hisil of a hospital.</a> There's obviously a few examples in the books, as well.<br /> <br /> As for how dangerous, mild-to-very. Spirits are naturally not going to like new werewolves, as a werewolf means basically an outsider is there and they're going to start kicking ass. So any loci spirits might want, any plans they might have, are likely to be taken or disrupted by their presence. However, if the werewolf's made himself known and gained the respect of some spirits, word can spread and it can be less dangerous, especially if the werewolf has shown that he's not going to be a tyrant or bully. The more powerful a werewolf is, specifically with their Honorary Spirit Rank, the less likely it's going to be dangerous. Even more powerful spirits will likely pause before trying to wipe you out, as sending a bunch of minions at you is pointless if you can go through them faster than you would a human.<br /> <br /> It should always be dangerous, though. Even a territory where every spirit's been tied down in alliances or sworn to this or that has the chance of exploding into chaos and bloodshed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:27:40-08:00","id":839392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrImperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=839281#post839281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you describe the spirit/shadow world and how dangerous do you believe it should be for werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr. Shopping's AP Detroit Rock City was hugely inspirational for me when it comes to describing the shadow. He seriously knocks it out of the park almost every time. It is long, but really good.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...Rock-City-quot</a><br /> <br /> I'll quote some of my favorite descriptions from the prologue.<br /> <br /> Here is his description of the Ithalunim's lair, the Detroit public library:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The circular chamber you enter is massive, maybe a hundred feet in diameter, marble tile broken here and there, trails of faint silvery light wisping from the cracks, drawn upwards in waterfall trails. Around the perimeter are bookshelves that rise into the heavens, pitching forward and bent under their own weight, like some kind of Salvatore Dali imagining, sloping to form a roof, for there is nothing else overhead but a starry void. Flapping books use their covers as fluttering wings to fly. They are like insects, swarming, hundreds of them, moving here and there, hovering in front of bookshelves before worming into place against the rustling protest of their fellows. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The center of the chamber is sunken in, broken like a massive boulder was dropped from the sky directly below. Silvery white light caresses a card-catalog cabinet the height of a skyscraper. It too is swarming with spirits - tiny bifocals with white gloves that constantly 'Shhh!' at each other to be quiet. Drawers open and close, cards moved to and fro in an eternal test of spiritual bureaucracy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A massive presence is here too, were all that you've seen not enough to rob you of your sanity. It rises nearly 30 feet high, a being that radiates argent light, silvery wings spanning from its back and rustling down to form something of a trailing robe, body crooked and hobbled like a vulture's, dressed in a robe of white. It is hazy and indistinct, with arms like a man that end in hooked claws, bent legs that end in sharp talons, a craned neck and head of a carrion bird. It shimmers and chimes, and when you look at it, you can hear Mother Luna's song, ever so faintly. It walks with the aid of a silvery staff, waving its claw and coaxing books into proper order, a great ring of tomes circling around it.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You keep pace with Jack at first, underneath the gaze of broken, blasted buildings scorched by the fire of some unknown cataclysm, crumbling and gutted, buried and choked by rubble. Flitting eyes peer out from yawning corpse-mouth windows, hateful in their watchfulness. You can hear chittersqueals in the savage First Tongue, warnings and curses against your kind, before it fades into silence, black ooze dripping from cracks and holes in the wall. Rattling chains dangle in the place of clotheslines, bits of flesh hanging and flapping grotesquely in the breeze, dripping pinkish liquid against the ground. The ground undulates under your feet, rusty fanblades and fingernails, some catching your pants, tearing at your skin. Jack negotiates these easily, as the two of you run through the twisted streets of Detroit's Shadow. </div> </div> </div>Party Town descriptions:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ziggurats loom large in the distance, their outline bigger than any man-made building ever could be, stretching towards the strange Hisil sky. They sit like giant black shadows, covered in throbbing multicolored neon lights that pulse as veins would, making you wonder if they might be somehow partly organic. The neon covers their smooth geometric faces like overgrown vines. As you negotiate the broken Shadow streets with Jack, you can see dancing lights on the horizon, like a wash of phosphorescent wave. </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And then there's the music. It's faint on the air, but you can hear it, harmonics below the level of a man's, but not a wolf's. The closer you get, the louder it becomes. Even at this distance, you can feel your ribs pound at the spectral base.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The music is somehow familiar, like it were halfway human. Jack seems to be enjoying it, and as you reach an archway made of two buildings that have fallen together, windows blown out and blackened, he stops. The Elodoth looks to you with a grin. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You notice the ground begin to change under your feet. All this time it was desolate and bare, cracked asphalt like desert mud, scorched pavement, rubbled concrete. But now you notice growth everywhere. Wires, dead television screens that stare up like tiles, posters of a splash of writhing limbs and color, subtitled in a strange, block-letter language that makes no sense to you. The both of you emerge into an open courtyard that is lit by a dim red haze, filled with narrow, crooked alleyways and shop faces that have no windows. The openings yawn like corpse mouths, wrinkled and misshapen. Signs printed in the block-letter script hang askew everywhere, while billboards form a crude ceiling, stacked like a steepled church roof. Openings here and there let you see the massive buildings in the distance, and the hint of Luna's shining light.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You are not alone. There are spirits everywhere, motes of colored lights bobbing and weaving, squirming and shaping themselves like soundwaves to each beat of the ever-changing music. The sound seems to come from everywhere - the ground, the air, the creatures themselves. Stranger still, you see that the alleyways and shop fronts are occupied by mannequin legs, walking here and there with a hooker's gait, swinging plastic hips, feet clad in high heels. Some are more complete than others, but all are missing their heads.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As you step over the television tiles, they begin to light up, one by one, displaying black and white images that look like they're from the 1950s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Bastard-wolves...&quot; A television announcer sneers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;...Don't belong...&quot; A chef stirring a pot warns.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;...In this place...&quot; A homemaker frowns.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The images quickly turn to scenes from a flickering bondage film, where you're strapped on a table, cherry ball tied in your mouth, silver knives flashing all around. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Jack spits on one of the screens. &quot;FUCK OFF.&quot; he growls, stamping his foot on one of them so hard that the glass cracks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A pair of spinning, levitating vinyl records begin to float curiously around you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;[Why is she here</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">incantrix, vilatrex</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">lookin' or finding</span></span><br /> <i>mezmiderix</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Spin spin baby...]&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They crackle, a weird lyrical jumble of First Tongue that sounds similar to hip-hop, but garbled and distorted.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>The Wastewander, a barrens:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Partytown slowly transitions to somewhere else entirely. From smooth obsidian floors and massive ziggurats, vibrant lights, colors, sound and motion to rust and crude industrial shapes. Pipes, coiled rivets and corroded rebar stick out of the ground like the orange spines of bodies picked clean by scavengers and time. Your feet clank against metal planks that have been lain haphazardly, the walls high and tight, like compacted trash, all manner of rust-covered junk sticking out in a broken tangle. It is strangely, eerily quiet here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You feel like you're walking through a maze, Partytown swiftly disappearing behind high walls of rust and junk many times larger than you. There is the uncomfortable feeling of being watched.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Sounds, scrabbling from above, from the walls that obstruct everything, even as Jack leads you through unerringly, the monotony broken only by the glimpse of a great black sea beyond.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Something just ran up along the top of the wall, skittering.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pipes that should be hissing and gurgling steam lay dormant, your breathing sharp and too loud in the still air. You can hear Jack's heartbeat, the terse breath that moves from his lungs.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You see it crouching there as you round a corner. A long, slinking black catlike thing with the face of a little girl and long, matted black hair. The teats that hang down from its body look thin and withered. The grotesque thing lets out a plaintive mewling that sounds like a little girl's sob before it slinks off, leaping away. Jack pays the creature no heed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Eventually you come to a dead end. The rusty walls seem to have welded together recently and form an ugly, tattered seal, like a newly formed suture. The joint rises with the wall up about thirty feet.<br /> <br /> ...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The two of you get to your feet and survey that which is the edge of Wastewander - like out of a bad dream, the darkened vault of the sky is framed by pollution, Luna's edge barely shining through, weakly illuminating this place. Like a coastline, a vast labyrinth of rusty walls stretch from horizon to horizon, a hedge maze grown wild and dead for a hundred thousand years. Ahead is a great black sea of inky black oil. Pipes of all sizes protrude from this carpet of sludge, sticking out in crazy angles that form no complete structure or system. There are some as tiny as spiderwebs and others as large as smokestacks.<br /> </span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:32:25-08:00","id":839396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=839291#post839291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Acrozatarim, a writer for Werewolf, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\">wrote up this great description of the Hisil of a hospital.</a> There's obviously a few examples in the books, as well.<br /> <br /> As for how dangerous, mild-to-very. Spirits are naturally not going to like new werewolves, as a werewolf means basically an outsider is there and they're going to start kicking ass. So any loci spirits might want, any plans they might have, are likely to be taken or disrupted by their presence. However, if the werewolf's made himself known and gained the respect of some spirits, word can spread and it can be less dangerous, especially if the werewolf has shown that he's not going to be a tyrant or bully. The more powerful a werewolf is, specifically with their Honorary Spirit Rank, the less likely it's going to be dangerous. Even more powerful spirits will likely pause before trying to wipe you out, as sending a bunch of minions at you is pointless if you can go through them faster than you would a human.<br /> <br /> It should always be dangerous, though. Even a territory where every spirit's been tied down in alliances or sworn to this or that has the chance of exploding into chaos and bloodshed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also why joining a tribe is an advantage: During the period you're being groomed to join one, your mentor is vouching for you. If they mess with you, they're messing with him, and their pack. It's also why less powerful spirits with a vendetta go after your not-so-ferocious packmates, loved ones or other associates. Spirits are predators, and predators usually go for the infant, the frail and the elderly after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:00:32-08:00","id":840257,"title":"","content":"Can you take a merit if you don't meet the prerequisite for it in all of your forms? For example, could a character take the Relentless Assault Fighting style to use in Dalu/Gauru/Urshul even if they lacked the strength to use it in Hishu and Urhan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:06:05-08:00","id":840259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=840257#post840257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take a merit if you don't meet the prerequisite for it in all of your forms? For example, could a character take the Relentless Assault Fighting style to use in Dalu/Gauru/Urshul even if they lacked the strength to use it in Hishu and Urhan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a shadow of a doubt: No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:09:33-08:00","id":840263,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the Prerequisites are based on your standard, Hishu form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:11:47-08:00","id":840267,"title":"","content":"Yeah, was thinking that was the case. Thank you kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:05:57-08:00","id":840563,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing though: Why not? A werewolf can spend as long as they like in Dalu, so what's stopping them learning the fighting style in Dalu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:00:43-08:00","id":840584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=840563#post840563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing though: Why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's for a second look at Urshul and not Dalu for simplicity sake. It's also a form that you can theoretically spend as long as you want. <br /> <br /> So you get +2 to all Physical attributes from Urshul in addition to your 1 that you have to have as minimum. It means that every werewolf character that knows how to lay punches (Brawl 2) can take this fighting style. <br /> <br /> For me it's totally opposite of what Merits should be, quoting CofD: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Merits represent a character\u2019s <b>unique</b> abilities and assets. They can cover anything from her wealth to her <b>uncanny </b><b>ability </b>to knock out her opponents.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Easy accessibility of that merit would diminish its value for players and storyteller, they will feel obliged to take it and GM to give it to every other opponent. It's better to build up PCs with merits to make them feel unique - &quot;Oooh, Mark is a very smart and sly wolf, you can't catch him in a fight, he always slips away from your claws&quot; (Tactical Shifting), &quot;Brenda has this presence in herself, you have to hear her once, her howls come deep from her heart and pierce your soul&quot; (Warcry). <br /> <br /> Seriously, I would save &quot;Relentless Assault&quot; for those situations where PC pack stands encircled in Fire Touched wolfblooded village and the crowd splits and calls to itself in fear and awe &quot;Mad Eye! Mad Eye! Mad Eye is coming!&quot; and the half-naked viking giant from 80s heavy metal magazine cover with oily torso ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) emerges from the crowd and goes absolutely ballistic on the pack's Rahu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:43:28-08:00","id":840608,"title":"","content":"Aside from the fact that strength 3 and stamina 3 are probably common as shit among werewolves, and thus would not make the merit even remotely as rare as you suggest, you missed the point of my question.<br /> <br /> I don't give a crap about storytelling value right now. What I'm trying to figure out is a satisfactory <i>in-universe</i> reason that a character couldn't learn it when they can spend as long as they like in a form that is, by the rules, strong and tough enough to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:11:49-08:00","id":840626,"title":"","content":"I can't see any reason not too. Thing is, they would only have access to the Merit in the shapes that meet the prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:17:25-08:00","id":840629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=840608#post840608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't give a crap about storytelling value right now. What I'm trying to figure out is a satisfactory <i>in-universe</i> reason that a character couldn't learn it when they can spend as long as they like in a form that is, by the rules, strong and tough enough to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the prerequisites are directed at human form. Dalu prereqs might be higher, proportionate to the modifications the form offers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:19:47-08:00","id":840630,"title":"","content":"I did consider that possibility, but on the whole I think it just raises further questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:21:42-08:00","id":840632,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's because Hishu is the Uratha's first (if not true) form, and that somehow affects how they learn things? Probably not, but it's the best I can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:00:02-08:00","id":840657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=840608#post840608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the fact that strength 3 and stamina 3 are probably common as shit among werewolves, and thus would not make the merit even remotely as rare as you suggest, you missed the point of my question.<br /> <br /> I don't give a crap about storytelling value right now. What I'm trying to figure out is a satisfactory <i>in-universe</i> reason that a character couldn't learn it when they can spend as long as they like in a form that is, by the rules, strong and tough enough to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok Mr. Rudepants. Hishu is always referred as base form and all other mechanics refer to it directly. Example: if you hear about skill/attribute cap, you always look at the Hishu. Hell, other forms are defined as sort of template you put on Hishu form with change to attributes, size and additional stuff. Specifically if we think about &quot;Relentless Assault&quot;, it doesn't make sense for character to be less vicious fighter in different forms. Being ferocious should be his style of fighting per default to gain him merit advantages. Seriously, whole thing looks like min maxing for its own sake. We wouldn't have argued if say, Urshul gave you +1 to Wits and suddenly werewolf would be able to flank in this form and in other wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:35:20-08:00","id":840676,"title":"","content":"Elfive does have a point, though. I think part of it is just standard game thought. Human is 'standard' form, prerequisites are meant for it.<br /> <br /> You can have Striking Looks in hishu form, but does it work in urshul or gauru? You already have other merits that only work in certain forms, maybe because they require hands or talking.<br /> <br /> I suppose part of the problem would be you are paying for a merit you will not always be able to use. But as I just noted it's not exactly unique for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:57:21-08:00","id":840694,"title":"","content":"To look at it another way, what if you start off meeting the prerequisites in Hishu, but then lose a dot of strength in the form to the drawback of Favoured Form? Do you lose the merit then? That would seem strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:02:37-08:00","id":840696,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it would make more sense for you to just not be able to use the merit in that form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:56:23-08:00","id":844184,"title":"","content":"how do spirits cross the gauntlet outside of using a verge?<br /> <br /> Can they cross the gauntlet soley through the use of the gauntlet breach manifestation or can spirits also use locuses as the Uratha do and if so what is the mechanic for a spirit doing so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T17:00:56-08:00","id":844214,"title":"","content":"Well there's Verges, and then there's Loci. Loci are focal points and wells of Essence that influence the Shadow around them for a certain radius, but they're also miniature <i>axis mundi</i> that enable easy travel between Flesh and <i>Hisil</i>. I don't have my book with me at the moment, but they <i>can </i>cross using a Locus. Verges, on the other hand, are regions where the Gauntlet (or other appropriate spiritual barrier) simply doesn't exist for one reason or another, so obviously those are <i>much</i> easier to use when they're open.<br /> <br /> That being said- hitch a ride on a lost mortal? Fetter themselves to a Gauntlet-breaching Wolfblooded? Encourage someone with the Medium Merit to prepare the way for them using the Reaching Manifestation? I know Medium is traditionally a ghost thing, but there's nothing stopping the Merit from applying to Spirits, God-Machine Angels, or other Ephemeral Beings either. Pretty sure the Merit explicitly calls those Ephemeral Beings out as other things the Merit can affect.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Question I thought of- what's with Loci now? I was under the impression that in 1E they were usually places, but the 2E fluff (and a Wolfblooded Tell) implies that potentially mobile objects or even people can become a Locus now. Firstly, that means the <i>Hisil </i>can get pretty screwed by someone or something moving, and secondly, my god that poor person. <i>Especially </i>if they aren't Wolfblooded. Fast track to being Claimed right there.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about, wasn't there a 1E Spirit that was, itself, a Locus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:06:40-08:00","id":844244,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"865\" data-vbnamecard=\"865\">WelshBoi</a><br /> <br /> \u200bVerges don't seem to exist in Werewolf in second edition. Instead it's a Mage thing, with Supernal and Abyssal verges.<br /> <br /> Arcanist has it pretty on the dot. It's all in the Chronicles rules update, which you can get for free <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. But they need the right Condition to get things Open, basically giving them some air to breathe on the other side once they cross. They start with something Resonant on the other side, and they either Strengthen it or something else occurs so that it's Open. At that point they can Reach across. To actually cross they need either Gauntlet Breach or Shadow Gateway. Then when they do cross they're in Twilight, which is a state of existence and not a place, and from there they can Materialize, giving themselves a physical form, or Fetter themselves to a nice source of Essence. <br /> <br /> A locus allows you to Reach without needing the Reach Manifestation, so basically any spirit could act across the Gauntlet around a locus.<br /> <br /> @Arcanist<br /> <br /> While loci were limited, in the default setting, to places or at least parts of places, such as a certain painting in a high-rise lobby, there was an optional rule to allow them to be more mobile objects and even people, ghosts and fetishes. There was even theoretical people who were walking Wounds or Shoals. This is all detailed in Lore of the Forsaken. Second edition seems to have said, 'Screw it, let's have fun,' with a lot of the default setting. Yes, it does mean that the Hisil can get screwed by someone or something moving, and that's part of the fun of the game, things are always happening. You've set up your rows of dominos, there wouldn't be much of a game if there wasn't a chance for them to be knocked over. If you really want to get rid of it, you can just not have any of them in your story, but by the rules it's still part of the 'default' setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Erring on the side of caution until we get word from writers. 03-09-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:08:08-08:00","id":844302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844184#post844184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do spirits cross the gauntlet outside of using a verge?<br /> <br /> Can they cross the gauntlet soley through the use of the gauntlet breach manifestation or can spirits also use locuses as the Uratha do and if so what is the mechanic for a spirit doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can thru loci attuned to their natures, and there's manifestations that allow them to reach or materialize as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:51:49-08:00","id":844327,"title":"","content":"Oh, I by no means dislike the development of that being the default setting- in fact it adds a lot of serious potential to a story.<br /> <br /> If I remember the Locus rules correctly, in order to track as a permanent Locus Essence has to collect at about 50 Essence per dot and gain triple their dot rating in Essence per day. A person!Locus would have an utterly absurd Essence pool if they could just access it, and if they were Claimed... well, they'd basically become a Shadow god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T05:53:28-08:00","id":844464,"title":"","content":"So a spirit needs to find a locus that is resonance with it, use its influence to shift it to open and then it can cross the gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:06:20-08:00","id":844465,"title":"","content":"No, loci just make things easier. And I don't believe you need to be Resonant with it, they exist as places close to the other world, so presumably any spirit could use it to come across, but spirits and others who use loci tend to protect them. You also get a +2 bonus to cross if you are Resonant with the Influence of the locus,<br /> <br /> But the rest is right, they use their Influence to Strengthen existing Resonances and then cross over. In order to use their Influences across the Gauntlet they need to use Reaching. But in an area of a locus they don't need to use Reaching, it's applied automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2016, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:41:20-08:00","id":844638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844464#post844464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a spirit needs to find a locus that is resonance with it, use its influence to shift it to open and then it can cross the gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in 1e this was the case, which meant sudden spiritual upheval could be tracked to a new locus having been formed. Now every locus is basically an infestation zone. Makes no sense humanity hasn't been overwhelmed by sheer spiritual possessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:42:06-08:00","id":844639,"title":"","content":"Nofather, where are you seeing that spirits can cross the Gauntlet at an Open location? Cause I can't seem to find that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:54:19-08:00","id":844648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844638#post844638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back in 1e this was the case, which meant sudden spiritual upheval could be tracked to a new locus having been formed. Now every locus is basically an infestation zone. Makes no sense humanity hasn't been overwhelmed by sheer spiritual possessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, back in 1e it was even worse, because there was no Manifestation Condition system to limit where spirits could exert their influence, Gauntlet Breach had no spatial constraints, and Materialize could be used from the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:57:13-08:00","id":844651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844648#post844648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, back in 1e it was even worse, because there was no Manifestation Condition system to limit where spirits could exert their influence, Gauntlet Breach had no spatial constraints, and Materialize could be used from the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both gauntlet breach and materialize remain present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:04:14-08:00","id":844655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844651#post844651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both gauntlet breach and materialize remain present.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they are tied to a system that limits where and when they can be used, which was my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:05:12-08:00","id":844657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844655#post844655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they are tied to a system that limits where and when they can be used, which was my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: Spirit thieves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:06:44-08:00","id":844659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844651#post844651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both gauntlet breach and materialize remain present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but now Gauntlet Breach requires the Resonant Condition and Materialize requires the Open Condition and for the entity to be in Twilight Form (which itself requires them to be on the Flesh side of the Gauntlet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:07:32-08:00","id":844660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844657#post844657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two words: Spirit thieves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see in what way this is an argument that things were not worse in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:36:00-08:00","id":844675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844639#post844639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nofather, where are you seeing that spirits can cross the Gauntlet at an Open location? Cause I can't seem to find that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I thought it was an error on my part, now I'm not entirely sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844659#post844659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Materialize requires the Open Condition and for the entity to be in Twilight Form (which itself requires them to be on the Flesh side of the Gauntlet).</div> </div> </div> </div>How sure are we that this is the case? It does say it within the descriptive text on p187, 'By spending three Essence, the spirit may shift from Twilight Form into the Materialized Condition.' but it only says it 'Requires Open Condition' and it doesn't say it's further required in the Materialize Manifestation entry on p190.<br /> <br /> I've previously stated that Gauntlet Breach and Shadow Gateway are the only way to get across, but double-checking to answer Welshboi's question made me think you could just use the other Manifestations to do it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't look like this has been tackled by any of the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:00:12-08:00","id":844826,"title":"","content":"I think my assumption would be that some spirits (like ghosts) simply live on the flesh side of the Gauntlet. I might also point out that spirits can easily slip through holes in the Gauntlet like those chewed open by the rat hosts. Finally, CofD is a world that is simple full of cults. Spirits can be summoned across the Gauntlet by cultists using the proper rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:08:14-08:00","id":844834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844826#post844826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my assumption would be that some spirits (like ghosts) simply live on the flesh side of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... Ghosts aren't spirits, they're a completely different kind of ephemeral entity. Spirits are the only ephemeral entities that live in the Shadow, outside of exceptional circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:30:47-08:00","id":844850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844834#post844834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhh... Ghosts aren't spirits, they're a completely different kind of ephemeral entity. Spirits are the only ephemeral entities that live in the Shadow, outside of exceptional circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you're reading the wrong sense of &quot;like&quot;.<br /> <br /> To clarify the rest of your point though, are we to understand that numena with reach (R) can be used from places like the Underworld, the Shadow, the Astral, the Hedge, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:39:56-08:00","id":844853,"title":"","content":"True Fae and hobgoblins aren't ephemeral, so wouldn't have numina.<br /> <br /> But presumably the reason you can Reach across the Gauntlet is because the Hisil is a reflection of the gurihal. If you had the ability, you could jump across the Gauntlet, walk ten feet in a direction, then jump back and be ten feet from your starting point. The Underworld and Astral don't seem to act like that, and the Hedge, at least in first edition, had some attitudes from the real world but wasn't as intimately connected as the Hisil. So even a spirit or werewolf couldn't reach from those places, except perhaps in special circumstances.<br /> <br /> While spirits can live in the gurihal, they are created in the Hisil and had to move across at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:03:49-08:00","id":844859,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, so we should understand that the Shadow is basically twilight+. Works for me. Although I have no problem with rank 1 spirits occurring naturally (kinda like rank 1 or 2 ghosts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:08:52-08:00","id":844861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844850#post844850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry you're reading the wrong sense of &amp;quot;like&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said &quot;other kinds of spirits.&quot; Ghosts aren't a kind of spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844850#post844850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify the rest of your point though, are we to understand that numena with reach (R) can be used from places like the Underworld, the Shadow, the Astral, the Hedge, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean can they affect the physical world from those places? No, they can't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844859#post844859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh, so we should understand that the Shadow is basically twilight+. Works for me. Although I have no problem with rank 1 spirits occurring naturally (kinda like rank 1 or 2 ghosts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... The shadow is a place that's like a spiritual reflection of the physical world. Twilight is a state of matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:12:03-08:00","id":844865,"title":"","content":"Twilight isn't a place, it's a state of being.<br /> <br /> And spirits do occur naturally, in the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T20:57:57-08:00","id":844896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844861#post844861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said &quot;other kinds of spirits.&quot; Ghosts aren't a kind of spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> You mean can they affect the physical world from those places? No, they can't.<br /> <br /> <br /> Err... The shadow is a place that's like a spiritual reflection of the physical world. Twilight is a state of matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, you're still reading things you want to but that I didn't write. I'm saying some spirits live in the real world, like, and by like I mean 'similar to how', some ghosts do.<br /> <br /> Also I'm a bit confused. Either Spirits can use Numena with the (R) to affect the real world from the Shadow or they can't. If they can't then I'm back to being of the inclination that some Spirits exist in the flesh world (in Twilight States).<br /> <br /> Also Twilight is not a state of matter. It's an immaterial state of Ephemera (aka spirits, ghosts, angels, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 03-10-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T21:07:22-08:00","id":844902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844896#post844896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the wrong sense of &quot;spirit&quot;. Trust me if I had meant Spirit, I would have capitalized that s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roger that. That would have been the source of the confusion. I didn't assume you capitalized spirit, since it's not capitalized in Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844896#post844896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm a bit confused. Either Spirits can use Numena with the (R) to affect the real world from the Shadow or they can't. If they can't then I'm back to being of the inclination that some Spirits exist in the flesh world (in Twilight States).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what you asked. You asked if other ephemeral entities could use numena with the {R} tag to affect the physical world from places like the Underworld and the Astral. The answer is no, they can't. Spirits can use numena with the {R} tag to affect the physical world from the Shadow, (or the Shadow from the spirit world) if they have the Reaching Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844896#post844896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Twilight is not a state of matter. It's an immaterial state of Ephemera (aka spirits, spirity-things, apparitions, or whatever you want to call them).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I mistyped. And ephemeral entities is what they're called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T21:08:24-08:00","id":844903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=844896#post844896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm a bit confused. Either Spirits can use Numena with the (R) to affect the real world from the Shadow or they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Hisil, yes. From the Underworld, the Astral and the Hedge, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they can't then I'm back to being of the inclination that some Spirits exist in the flesh world (in Twilight States). </div> </div> </div>Some do, but they've come from the Hisil. Gauntlet Breach, Shadow Gateway, other methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:42:27-08:00","id":845244,"title":"","content":"This may not be as simple of a question as it sounds but I'm wondering how others deal with large pack battles between werewolves. I&quot;m pretty familiar with down and dirty combat, but I just don't find it to be fitting when facing off against a pack of pure nemeses. From what I've been able to tell, it seems that whomever runs out of Gauru turns first loses. I've experimented with turning points in combat, (a specific pack member goes down, 3/4 health lost, NPC in trouble) and also placed objectives but for a knockout drag out brawl is there anyway to streamline the conflict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","name":"Handriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4590_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:07:43-08:00","id":845258,"title":"","content":"I think Down and Dirty might work in a situation like that, since it isn't necessarily balanced for the player, especially against a pack of werewolves. Just give the NPCs the teamwork bonus the same way the players have. You might have the first few rounds just be standard battle then shift to Down and Dirty if things look like there's not going to be a way out of combat. <br /> <br /> You might also factor in the Beaten Down &amp; Surrender rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T02:26:27-08:00","id":845534,"title":"","content":"Beaten Down and Surrender aren't a factor in hybrid forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:58:46-08:00","id":845562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=845534#post845534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beaten Down and Surrender aren't a factor in hybrid forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be a factor in gauru, but can you reference anything where it says this?<br /> <br /> It was something in alpha but seems to have been dropped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-11-2016, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:38:46-08:00","id":845600,"title":"","content":"Beaten Down isn't a factor for werewolves in general. Fuckers can shrug off getting shot, they don't give a shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:34:35-08:00","id":845627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=845562#post845562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It shouldn't be a factor in gauru, but can you reference anything where it says this?<br /> <br /> It was something in alpha but seems to have been dropped.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on page 166<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These rules only apply to people who would incur a breaking point for committing (or attempting) \u201cmurder.\u201d Most Uratha \u2014 along with other creatures that don\u2019t have a problem killing people \u2014 can ignore surrender without penalty and don\u2019t get Beaten Down. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:43:02-08:00","id":845632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=845627#post845627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's on page 166</div> </div> </div> </div>There we go. Fall back to Down &amp; Dirty, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T10:05:36-08:00","id":846162,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies guys. I'll give this a shot in my upcoming game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","name":"Handriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4590_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:35:23-08:00","id":846327,"title":"","content":"Ironically, if there are any humans or wolves partaking in the struggle the Beaten Down and Surrender rules totally apply to them. I guess killing werewolves that aren't your packmates is a social norm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:19:26-08:00","id":846361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846327#post846327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, if there are any humans or wolves partaking in the struggle the Beaten Down and Surrender rules totally apply to them. I guess killing werewolves that aren't your packmates is a social norm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... I'm guessing since it's not worded as &quot;murder&quot; it must not count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T20:47:52-08:00","id":846419,"title":"","content":"I'm just like unlike packmates, humans, and wolves, it's not listed as a breaking point (towards spirit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T21:11:19-08:00","id":846425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846419#post846419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just like unlike packmates, humans, and wolves, it's not listed as a breaking point (towards spirit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oath of the Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:30:45-07:00","id":846536,"title":"","content":"Humans can totally surrender if they want. Werewolves just don't need to pay anything to ignore it. Against other werewolves the same can happen, it's just not mechanically enforced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:58:33-07:00","id":846543,"title":"","content":"Integrity-equivalents aren't about morality or social taboo. They don't reflect anything about what is normal or not in a given society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-13-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:11:51-07:00","id":846554,"title":"","content":"What Jacob is pointing out is that Beaten Down and Surrender says it doesn't apply to characters that don't incur a breaking point for murder, and lists werewolves as an example of such characters. But yet &quot;killing a human or wolf&quot; and &quot;killing a packmate&quot; are both Harmony Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:16:04-07:00","id":846571,"title":"","content":"I'd say they don't count because werewolf breaking points are not human breaking points in any way but name. For a werewolf, killing someone can actually make them <i>more </i>balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:30:51-07:00","id":846579,"title":"","content":"Beaten Down and Surrender generally don't apply to major templates in the first place. Unless we're talking about a high Rank wolf, that is, where the average Uratha doesn't stand a chance. Even then, I'm leery. BD/S are generally meant for mooks. So, the entire situation is kinda moot to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:07:37-07:00","id":846589,"title":"","content":"Honestly this is one of those areas where the individual storytellers and troupes have to decide for themselves. Personally I'd just use the quick and dirty combat but afterwards the survivors suffer from breaking points with some pretty big minuses (reduced to chance die sounds about right for the breaking point rolls). Nothing is as brutally gruesome as two werewolf packs tearing into one another. It isn't that they killed other werewolves as much as the scope of the carnage.<br /> <br /> IMO, this kind of fight is also going to degenerate into one last man standing as everyone falls into Kuruth and no one even considers surrendering. Whichever side wins, they're going to start in on themselves as soon as the other side is wiped. There are good reasons why Werewolves should fear Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:12:13-07:00","id":846590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846571#post846571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say they don't count because werewolf breaking points are not human breaking points in any way but name. For a werewolf, killing someone can actually make them <i>more </i>balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but that's actually a breaking point. I think you're probably imagining breaking points as too related to human conceptions of morality. That isn't how they work at all. They indicate state changes of one's soul. Low Integrity isn't a bad thing per se (ditto Humanity). For Werewolves it's much clearer that breaking points work in both directions. In this case wholesale slaughter of humans is &quot;bad&quot; not because it's evil or immoral by someone's standards. It simply drives the Werewolf's soul towards Spirit (which is accomplished through the mechanism of breaking points). What is experienced isn't a moral crisis in as much as it is a loss of physical substance. The call of the Shadow and its denizens grow louder as the call of the mortal world grows weaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:16:06-07:00","id":846593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846589#post846589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this is one of those areas where the individual storytellers and troupes have to decide for themselves. Personally I'd just use the quick and dirty combat but afterwards the survivors suffer from breaking points with some pretty big minuses (reduced to chance die sounds about right for the breaking point rolls). Nothing is as brutally gruesome as two werewolf packs tearing into one another. It isn't that they killed other werewolves as much as the scope of the carnage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the scope of the carnage do you feel would pull a werewolf so strongly towards flesh or spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:28:20-07:00","id":846603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846579#post846579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BD/S are generally meant for mooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>Down and Dirty </i>is meant for mooks. Beaten down is a step up from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:30:32-07:00","id":846605,"title":"","content":"You'll definitely have killed packmembers (or they'll have died). Everyone slipping into Kuruth virtually assures it (and gods forbid that wolf-blooded or human pack members were participating on either side). Also, I still think that you're linking breaking points too closely to morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:32:15-07:00","id":846606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846593#post846593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the scope of the carnage do you feel would pull a werewolf so strongly towards flesh or spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I've given penalties such as -3 to the breaking point for basically committing mass slaughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:46:13-07:00","id":846611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846606#post846606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I've given penalties such as -3 to the breaking point for basically committing mass slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get penalties to the breaking point for extremely gruesome murder or a high death toll. But if it's pack vs. pack, there probably aren't many human or wolf deaths, and unless there is a lot of confusion, not many characters are likely to be killing their own packmates. There's nothing going on, then, that would trigger one of the sample Breaking Points. The samples are of course not exhaustive, so it's certainly possible such a thing could cause a Breaking point, but I was curious what about such a battle Jacob (or anyone who wants to share their take on it, for that matter) thought would pull a werewolf in one direction or the other, and which way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:02:23-07:00","id":846635,"title":"","content":"Eh, killing Uratha, even when they aren't of your pack is still breaking the Oath, and has an according Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:13:15-07:00","id":846643,"title":"","content":"If it's pack versus pack once Death Rage comes into the picture the fight is over, since it's infectious and gauru don't target gauru. Humans and wolf-blooded and wolves and bears and vampires and other pack members are likely to die, which is why they don't usually come on hunts like that in the first place.<br /> <br /> Suggesting Down and Dirty was simply a solution to the problem in the first place, which was that fights with multiple packs can be a long and drawn out process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:18:45-07:00","id":846645,"title":"","content":"It's an epic battle, the climax of the story. In good stories the characters do not come out of such things unchanged. As a storyteller I would not be above simply raising or lowering a character's Harmony based on the things they did in that battle. Resisted Kuruth for as long as you could? +1 Harmony because the &quot;man&quot; likes control. Entered Kuruth as soon as you possibly could? -1 Harmony because spirits like it when you let the monster out to play.<br /> <br /> It's about the narrative growth (in either direction) of the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:27:37-07:00","id":846646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846635#post846635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, killing Uratha, even when they aren't of your pack is still breaking the Oath, and has an according Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846645#post846645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an epic battle, the climax of the story. In good stories the characters do not come out of such things unchanged. As a storyteller I would not be above simply raising or lowering a character's Harmony based on the things they did in that battle. Resisted Kuruth for as long as you could? +1 Harmony because the &amp;quot;man&amp;quot; likes control. Entered Kuruth as soon as you possibly could? -1 Harmony because spirits like it when you let the monster out to play.<br /> <br /> It's about the narrative growth (in either direction) of the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. I get what you mean now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T02:04:55-07:00","id":846977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846643#post846643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's pack versus pack once Death Rage comes into the picture the fight is over, since it's infectious and gauru don't target gauru. Humans and wolf-blooded and wolves and bears and vampires and other pack members are likely to die, which is why they don't usually come on hunts like that in the first place.<br /> <br /> Suggesting Down and Dirty was simply a solution to the problem in the first place, which was that fights with multiple packs can be a long and drawn out process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, a developer said, when inquired, that they only ignore other death raging packmates, so they would still try to kill each other, likely featuring cannibalism in order to do it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it Death Rage, otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-14-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:00:33-07:00","id":847014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846977#post846977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, a developer said, when inquired, that they only ignore other death raging packmates, so they would still try to kill each other, likely featuring cannibalism in order to do it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it Death Rage, otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I prefer the RAW for that. They kill everyone else, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T07:54:36-07:00","id":847068,"title":"","content":"It's called death rage because you either kill or die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:06:00-07:00","id":847076,"title":"","content":"The name is acknowledged to be a little hyperbolic though. Someone is <i>likely </i>to die, not <i>guaranteed.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:40:51-07:00","id":847139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=846977#post846977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, a developer said, when inquired, that they only ignore other death raging packmates, so they would still try to kill each other, likely featuring cannibalism in order to do it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it Death Rage, otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that conversation. It was actually two writers, (specifically, Bunyip and Chris) and they argued about whether or not Death Raging werewolves that weren't part of the pack should be valid targets. According to Chris, it was Stu who suggested during development that other werewolves in Death Rage should be treated as pack mates. Bunyip checked with Stu, and apparently he had changed his mind, because he responded that other non-packmate wolves in Death Rage should be valid targets. Then Bunyip said he thought both interpretations were good for different reasons, and implied that they might explore the matter further in future books (though not in The Pack because it didn't have enough space to do it well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:57:48-07:00","id":847435,"title":"","content":"So, question I thought up having let the concepts of weird and wonderful Loci stew for a few days. How would you handle a Locus that happened to be a person in your game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:24:59-07:00","id":847446,"title":"","content":"I'd either have it be a very important person, at least important regarding the locus' resonance, or someone utterly unassuming who just happens to have been born at the right time with the right stuff or lived the right life and happens to be full of Essence for no easily identifiable reason.<br /> <br /> The former would probably be urged on and off by spirits that matched its resonance. They would gather around the locus and protect them zealously and try their best to keep it motivated and doing whatever it is to amplify the locus aspect of the person. For more rare or dangerous resonances this could be a wrecking ball to the spirit. A walking Wound would basically spawn demons everywhere and have them constantly around it, protecting the locus like the dark forces protected Damien Thorn.<br /> <br /> An unassuming sort seems like it would be more openly manipulated and taken advantage of. If for whatever reason they aren't doing something that creates the Resonance, they just 'are' then spirits and other forces would do what they could to take advantage of it. With the 'important person' more aware spirits might guess that by Claiming they would lose access to the locus, as it would alter whatever they're doing, and the merging with the soul might damage whatever connection they had. With a random locus-person what they do doesn't matter. You could throw them in the trunk of your car and drive them wherever you go, as long as you kept them healthy. They would probably be either hostages or specially cared for people in Bale and Ghost Wolf cults, they might be strong-armed or otherwise forced into being a part of a Forsaken or Pure territory. I imagine they would probably be targets of other supernaturals, perhaps beshilu, since a locus is a thin point between worlds, it would probably give them a leg-up on their wrecking the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:33:24-07:00","id":847451,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that about fits what I was thinking. Except for maybe a third option- someone who's aware of what they are and what that means, and has a few supernatural abilities that enable them to interact with Spirits and/or use Essence. In such a case, they might become powerful enough to actually rule the local Shadow, having accumulated a stockpile of Essence that not even the local <i>Diharim</i> could match, and possessing a relatively loyal retinue of Spirits they keep happy and fed. That would make a pretty cool backstory for one of the Purified, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T00:44:13-07:00","id":847572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=847139#post847139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that conversation. It was actually two writers, (specifically, Bunyip and Chris) and they argued about whether or not Death Raging werewolves that weren't part of the pack should be valid targets. According to Chris, it was Stu who suggested during development that other werewolves in Death Rage should be treated as pack mates. Bunyip checked with Stu, and apparently he had changed his mind, because he responded that other non-packmate wolves in Death Rage should be valid targets. Then Bunyip said he thought both interpretations were good for different reasons, and implied that they might explore the matter further in future books (though not in The Pack because it didn't have enough space to do it well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty. I actually have two [redacted] to post - one each for 'Kuruth only spares pack in Kuruth' and 'Kuruth spares all Kuruth'. I'm just waiting on <i>The Pack</i> to be released (or spoiled by Stew) so you guys can see/know about [redacted] and I can share the relevant bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T00:47:02-07:00","id":847573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=847435#post847435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question I thought up having let the concepts of weird and wonderful Loci stew for a few days. How would you handle a Locus that happened to be a person in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* 2nd edition, p267 *cough*<br /> <br /> Edit: And p268","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-15-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T03:42:36-07:00","id":847603,"title":"","content":"I can picture quite a few saints having been living loci, of positive resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:29:31-07:00","id":848145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=847603#post847603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can picture quite a few saints having been living loci, of positive resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That word &quot;positive&quot; really doesn't need to be there.<br /> <br /> Take <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olga_of_Kiev\" target=\"_blank\">Olga of Kiev</a>, for example. Vengeance is not what most people would think of as positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:13:27-07:00","id":848250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=848145#post848145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That word &quot;positive&quot; really doesn't need to be there.<br /> <br /> Take <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olga_of_Kiev\" target=\"_blank\">Olga of Kiev</a>, for example. Vengeance is not what most people would think of as positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>TL;DR version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:48:12-07:00","id":848273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=848250#post848250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TL;DR version?</div> </div> </div> </div> Another tribe, the Drevlians, assassinated her husband and wanted her to marry their prince so they could take over the tribal federation.<br /> <br /> Olga welcomed the delegates from that tribe and buried them alive.<br /> <br /> She then sent a message back to the rest of the Drevlians saying she accepted the proposal. The prince and his retainers thus turned up. She invited them into a bath-house, then shut it and set it on fire.<br /> <br /> She then invited a load of the Drevlians to a funeral feast to mourn her dead 'husband'. They got very drunk, and she managed to have 5000 of them slaughtered.<br /> <br /> She *then* went to the Drevlians' city and besieged it. She offered them what seemed to be very merciful peace terms - her price was three sparrows and three pigeons from each household. They happily sent out cages and boxes full of the birds. She then had her soldiers attach slow-burning matches to the legs of the birds and let them all loose. They predictably all flew straight home to the city. The result was almost the entire place catching fire simultaneously, so there was no way to meaningfully firefight. The city burned and the survivors fled.<br /> <br /> She then captured them and killed some, enslaved others and left the last portion alive to pay her tribute.<br /> <br /> Olga did not do vengeance half-heartedly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:42:10-07:00","id":848445,"title":"","content":"Well, wow. Just. Wow. *slow, fearful clap*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T17:19:01-07:00","id":848495,"title":"","content":"Are deed names not really a thing in 2e? I'm re-reading the Territories section I noticed that they rarely come up when characters are named.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T17:57:46-07:00","id":848515,"title":"","content":"It still seems to be a thing. I think it was just skimmed over for word space and to keep the Territories section on-topic. I could see it getting some words in the upcoming Pack book, as it seems like something that would bind newcomers to packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T03:31:30-07:00","id":848703,"title":"","content":"At the very least, they probably have nicknames for pack members based on cool stuff they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T02:55:23-07:00","id":849660,"title":"","content":"While werewolves aren't human, they're all the product of human cultures for most of their formative years. The extent to which they'd give each other nicknames or deed names will largely depend on the culture they were raised in. Part of the thing we moved away from in 2nd ed is the notion that Uratha society is homogeneous. Storm Lords from Australia will (probably) have different practices to Storm Lords in Germany, who in turn will have different practices to Storm Lords in India (to grab three random countries). They're all still recognisably Storm Lords (or Hunters in Darkness, or Blood Talons etc.), but they're all different.<br /> <br /> Take a look at the Hunting Grounds in 2nd ed. Basra has Fatima 'Ahlaam al-Dam (Dreams of Blood), Hassan ibn al-Ab al-Dh'ib (Easter egg - Hassan <i>Who is Like Father Wolf)</i> and Nat Dory, who comes from a very different background. Belfast has Nathan Herron and Laura Fitzpatrick. Central Australia has Barbara Perrurle Petyarre, Nick 'Wildfire' May, Crow, and Simon Weir, aka Deathtrap.<br /> <br /> tl;dr - The world is a big place. Packs absorb a lot from their human societies. Use nicknames and deed names as much or as little as makes sense to your game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T03:57:08-07:00","id":849674,"title":"","content":"I certainly can't see a werewolf with the surname &quot;Butcher&quot; ever being called anything else by his packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:47:27-07:00","id":849792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=849674#post849674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly can't see a werewolf with the surname &quot;Butcher&quot; ever being called anything else by his packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call him Buck, for shorties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T10:53:55-07:00","id":851228,"title":"","content":"Do you let melee weapon klaives resize for use in gauru in 2e? I'm pretty sure they did this in 1e (I am 100% sure they did in Mr. Shopping's APs, but it may have been a house rule).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:38:19-07:00","id":851253,"title":"","content":"Not unless that's a specific feature you want from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:47:50-07:00","id":851260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=851228#post851228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you let melee weapon klaives resize for use in gauru in 2e? I'm pretty sure they did this in 1e (I am 100% sure they did in Mr. Shopping's APs, but it may have been a house rule).</div> </div> </div> </div> Fetish weapons don't resize as a standard feature in 2e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T23:09:16-07:00","id":851600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=851228#post851228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you let melee weapon klaives resize for use in gauru in 2e? I'm pretty sure they did this in 1e (I am 100% sure they did in Mr. Shopping's APs, but it may have been a house rule).</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Klaives aren't a thing in 2e. Fetish weapons are a thing, but there is no longer a vaguely-defined subset of them with a different name. Second of all, resizing based on form is not a standard feature for Fetish weapons, but that is a feature one could theoretically have. I'd say such a feature is worth a dot, maybe two dots at the absolute most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:46:41-07:00","id":852517,"title":"","content":"I want to thank anyone for helping answer my questions. Heres another: can you use Scent Beneath the Surface (the Elodloth Gift that lets you tell if someone is lying) over the phone? If not, it seems like a reasonable fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:01:53-07:00","id":852527,"title":"","content":"My gut says no, you need to be there with them in the room. Mostly because the gift seems to rely on using the other senses as clues. It wouldn't work on a recording, which is technically what the voice you hear on the phone is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:35:15-07:00","id":852540,"title":"","content":"That does seem like a neat Fetish, though. A cell phone with spirit bound to it that tells you if the person on the other end is lying? Very cool concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:20:55-07:00","id":852596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=852527#post852527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...recording, which is technically what the voice you hear on the phone is.</div> </div> </div> </div>OT tangent...<br /> <br /> Actually, putting my EE hat on, this is simply incorrect unless you're of the opinion that all utterances are recordings. That's a different debate altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:35:51-07:00","id":852608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=852517#post852517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to thank anyone for helping answer my questions. Heres another: can you use Scent Beneath the Surface (the Elodloth Gift that lets you tell if someone is lying) over the phone? If not, it seems like a reasonable fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the proviso that this is my personal opinion and not a definitive answer (unless Stew backs it up, mind), I would say no. As the Facet relies on (in my view) non-visual and non-audible clues such as scent and the like, you'd have to be in their physical presence. At least, that's how I'd run it.<br /> <br /> That <i>does</i> sound like a nifty fetish, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:44:54-07:00","id":852614,"title":"","content":"What do y'all think about using gifts while using Beast Ride or Iron Slave? Using the ridden body, of course. Yea or Nay?<br /> <br /> Also, does one use their own attributes or skills? Like, a rabbit might not have high Occult, but surely my Ithaeur can interpret the writings on the wall of the Cultists' hideout, right? Maybe Mental skills but not Physical ones are retained? What about Social? What about attributes? If I'm resisting mindcontrol as a rabbit, I use my own Resolve + Primal Urge, surely.. right?<br /> <br /> Curious about how you guys run this stuff or what you all think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:51:12-07:00","id":852617,"title":"","content":"Offhand I think using gifts would be possible. It's not just a remote viewing, it seems to be basically a variant of the Possession Manifestation, with your soul in the animal or vehicle, and so your Gift marks with it, I think. Though spirits can't use their Numina and Influences while Possessing. I'd say you use your own Skills and Mental and Social Attributes. If your werewolf body dies, perhaps the Physical Attributes would rise to meet yours, or if they were higher, just grow on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-24-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:01:24-07:00","id":852621,"title":"","content":"I'd say a general yes, but with the Storyteller having veto rights over whether individual facets can be used.<br /> <br /> For example, Pack Triumphs Together wouldn't work unless the animal/device in question has the ability to speak as it relies on the Uratha's voice to work. (Mainly parrots and similar - or machines with loud enough sound systems.) Slaughterer wouldn't work because the werewolf can't take Gauru form in another body (likewise with The Father's Form).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:03:16-07:00","id":852623,"title":"","content":"That's a good point, I suppose you would need a Storyteller to say no to keep you from using Beast Ride on a bird then Iron Slave from that bird to a plane and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:23:20-07:00","id":852691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=852623#post852623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point, I suppose you would need a Storyteller to say no to keep you from using Beast Ride on a bird then Iron Slave from that bird to a plane and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>See that sounds like a great reason to allow it for me! Why not?<br /> <br /> I agree with Slaughterer and Pack Triumphs, however.<br /> <br /> Good to know that I'm not aberrant for wanting it in my game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:38:23-07:00","id":852697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=852517#post852517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to thank anyone for helping answer my questions. Heres another: can you use Scent Beneath the Surface (the Elodloth Gift that lets you tell if someone is lying) over the phone? If not, it seems like a reasonable fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it like in the show Lie To Me. It allows the Elodoth to catch those micro-expressions that bypass conscious thought to 100% effectiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:46:01-07:00","id":852699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=852691#post852691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See that sounds like a great reason to allow it for me! Why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really just ease of use and not needing to spend a lot of time dealing with one character away from the pack and the issues that might come up. In that chain, what if the bird dies or the plane is destroyed? Do they count as your source body even if you're six or seven links away? It's intriguing in fluff, giving you essentially a werewolf body hopper with limited choice bodies. But thinking of all the drawbacks could give you a headache. Werewolf Gladys Crabtree decides she doesn't want to go with the rest of the pack, so she possesses a car and goes with them that way, she runs over the target and it ends up good so maybe she uses her engineering to add a gun to the car. Mechanically it's sound, but it can be a real drag on the game.<br /> <br /> That's just thinking extremes, of course. Gladys might make an entire fleet of cars-with-guns but maybe Captain Manzini just uses Beast Ride to find her secret stash and Iron Slave to steal one. There's no good reason to disallow these things in your own games if you're prepared for some odd ideas coming up now and again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good to know that I'm not aberrant for wanting it in my game. </div> </div> </div>I should have thought more about my first post on the subject. Usually I get a lot of edits in but it's been a busy day with Easter parties at pre-school. It's certainly not aberrant, gifts are a really cool part of the game and it's hard to look at most of them and not see really cool things that could be done with them, even if you don't think that's what they seem like they're for. It's a Chronicles of Darkness game, second edition has done a lot to open it up to us, we'd be doing a disservice if we look at or think of things and hold back, or worse just say, 'No.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:55:56-07:00","id":853308,"title":"","content":"So, the Merit Code of Honor notes Harmony 8+ as a requirement to have it; what happens if you drop below it? Do you keep it? Do you subject it to Sanctity of Merits? I'm partial to the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:09:11-07:00","id":853314,"title":"","content":"I'd probably have you keep it, just don't gain the benefits until you're back up. It would become eligible for turning in via Sanctity if you've spend a significant time under the pre-req and, more importantly, have decided to abandon your code.<br /> <br /> On second thought, the merit doesn't suggest you have to stay above Harmony 8. So I suppose I wouldn't take the benefits away. I guess Sanctity would still come into play only when you've officially renounced your vows, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T22:17:02-07:00","id":853339,"title":"","content":"I'd refund it with Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T23:01:27-07:00","id":853352,"title":"","content":"I'd put the choice in the player's hands. By default they keep the merit, and can strive to bring their character back above Harmony 8 if they wish. If they don't want to do this, or have developed a new path for their character, remove the merit and apply Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T00:27:40-07:00","id":853372,"title":"","content":"So, question. Can Fetishes be used by non-Werewolves in 2nd edition? The roll is Resolve + Composure, which, yes, doesn't inherently mean it's not a template specific thing, but does at least leave it open since it doesn't explicitly say, at least not that I could find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T02:42:25-07:00","id":853408,"title":"","content":"They're not really supposed to, but I guess it depends on whether the spirit in it feels like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:02:53-07:00","id":853478,"title":"","content":"Mages will almost certainly be able to use them somehow. As for what they roll or if they have to rely on feeding it essence via a spell, who knows. That also doesn't mean that just anyone can use them, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:24:44-07:00","id":853490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853478#post853478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages will almost certainly be able to use them somehow. As for what they roll or if they have to rely on feeding it essence via a spell, who knows. That also doesn't mean that just anyone can use them, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:48:51-07:00","id":853506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853372#post853372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question. Can Fetishes be used by non-Werewolves in 2nd edition? The roll is Resolve + Composure, which, yes, doesn't inherently mean it's not a template specific thing, but does at least leave it open since it doesn't explicitly say, at least not that I could find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a non-spiritual template even attune to the fetish? Unless the fetish is specifically constructed to function on a ban-like behavior, to activate upon a specific action (which is how Wolfblooded use them) then no. Spirit Mages can actually provide essence to rouse the spirit within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:42:21-07:00","id":853541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853490#post853490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you say that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, they could make Fetishes in 1e. I assume that means they could use them.<br /> I'm not super strong in how Forsaken 1e worked, so maybe something about fetishes changed considerably between 1e and 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","user":"solidork","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:15:39-07:00","id":853549,"title":"","content":"I would expect Spirit to remain capable of creating fetishes. It's a big part of the Thyrsus thing, being all shaman-y and shit.<br /> <br /> Plus, being able to use a fetish makes for an obvious tell or merit for a wolf blood. They all get a small slice of werewolf pie, and this one just happened to get the bit that lets werewolves use fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:38:10-07:00","id":853561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853541#post853541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they could make Fetishes in 1e. I assume that means they could use them.<br /> I'm not super strong in how Forsaken 1e worked, so maybe something about fetishes changed considerably between 1e and 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well in that case you're probably right. I never got into Mage in 1e, so I didn't realize that was a thing they could do. No reason to assume that would change in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:44:41-07:00","id":853599,"title":"","content":"The Gift Facet City Eyes.<br /> <br /> 'The werewolf touches a single building or structure and transfers her senses into it. For the duration of the effect, as long as she is touching the building, she can project her senses through any of the structure\u2019s windows or other apertures, both inwards and outwards. She can project through up to her Cunning in windows at a given time, which may be anywhere on the building; as such, the werewolf could well be able to survey several different areas at the same time. She can immediately sense whether any person she sees is an inhabitant of the building or an intruder, and adds her Cunning to Empathy dice pools targeting inhabitants and to perception dice pools targeting intruders.'<br /> <br /> Do you think by 'other apertures' it allows doors, vents, and so forth? What about secret or trapdoors?<br /> <br /> Also, sources of Essence include seeing your Auspice moon in the sky, eating certain things, Sacred Prey, rite of Harness the Cycle, benefiting from someone with a Gift of Essence, loci, and destroying fetishes. Are there any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-26-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:04:48-07:00","id":853636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853506#post853506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can a non-spiritual template even attune to the fetish? Unless the fetish is specifically constructed to function on a ban-like behavior, to activate upon a specific action (which is how Wolfblooded use them) then no. Spirit Mages can actually provide essence to rouse the spirit within.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how it worked in 1st edition, but there's no mention of that need anymore. You're essentially 'willing' the bound spirit into action, according to it, and that doesn't sound like something inherently needing the werewolf template, is why it's questionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:27:58-07:00","id":853648,"title":"","content":"I think it's at least strongly implied to be only werewolf usable, not counting mages and other spirit sensitives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:48:12-07:00","id":853689,"title":"","content":"It's not in the books. I asked the same question a while back and one of the devs said &quot;ehh... not really&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T04:00:01-07:00","id":853965,"title":"","content":"Hello :-) <br /> <br /> Making sure I'm reading this right, but it looks like the following is theoretically possible... <br /> <br /> Step 1: Normal human going about their day<br /> <br /> Step 2: Normal human encounters Delerium from a Werewolf <br /> <br /> Step 3: Normal human has a really bad day an gets a dramatic failure<br /> <br /> Step 4: Normal human becomes Wolf-blooded <br /> <br /> Step 5: Newly wolf-blooded human goes about their day<br /> <br /> Step 6: Newly wolf-blooded human encounters stuff that stresses them out and increases their Tension Pool<br /> <br /> Step 7: Wolf-blooded human fails the resistance on the Tension roll and undergoes the first change<br /> <br /> Thus, normal human with no genetic predisposition is literally scared into becoming a Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T04:23:35-07:00","id":853969,"title":"","content":"Also possible: Normal human with no werewolf heritage randomly becomes a werewolf because Luna felt like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T04:46:31-07:00","id":853972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853969#post853969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also possible: Normal human with no werewolf heritage randomly becomes a werewolf because Luna felt like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alrighty then. That answers that, lol. So genetics flat out don't matter, at least on occasion. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T04:49:53-07:00","id":853974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853965#post853965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Step 4: Normal human becomes Wolf-blooded<br /> <br /> Step 5: Newly wolf-blooded human goes about their day<br /> <br /> Step 6: Newly wolf-blooded human encounters stuff that stresses them out and increases their Tension Pool</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tension pool is a part of character creation, it's not a mechanic NPCs or even most PCs use. It's a fun way to incorporate the First Change into a story, if you don't want to start as a werewolf.<br /> <br /> And Elfive's explanation.<br /> <br /> But any mortal can become a wolf-blooded for a variety of reasons, and any of them can turn into a werewolf at random or stay a wolf-blooded for life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:15:51-07:00","id":853979,"title":"","content":"In CoD the classic trope of getting bitten by a werewolf and then turning into a big wolf monster the following full moon is a thing that can happen. It's rare, and a bunch of other stuff can happen instead but the possibility is nonetheless there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:56:56-07:00","id":853991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853974#post853974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tension pool is a part of character creation, it's not a mechanic NPCs or even most PCs use. It's a fun way to incorporate the First Change into a story, if you don't want to start as a werewolf.<br /> <br /> And Elfive's explanation.<br /> <br /> But any mortal can become a wolf-blooded for a variety of reasons, and any of them can turn into a werewolf at random or stay a wolf-blooded for life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Granted, in regards to the tension pool, but I guess what I'm getting at is, should I desire to do so, I could in theory introduce a mortal npc who undergoes a series of dramatically unfortunate events in response to carelessness on behalf of the PCs, which eventually turns into an Uratha with a deep grudge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T06:37:11-07:00","id":854000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853991#post853991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, in regards to the tension pool, but I guess what I'm getting at is, should I desire to do so, I could in theory introduce a mortal npc who undergoes a series of dramatically unfortunate events in response to carelessness on behalf of the PCs, which eventually turns into an Uratha with a deep grudge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:46:16-07:00","id":854023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=853372#post853372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question. Can Fetishes be used by non-Werewolves in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBy the rules for fetishes in the corebook, no. It requires the user to be an Uratha, and various fetish effects wouldn't even work with anything other than an Uratha anyway (like the Facet alteration ones).<br /> <br /> Awakening has always had Spirit-Arcanum-related fetishes as well, but they work differently to werewolf fetishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 03-27-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:55:20-07:00","id":854030,"title":"","content":"What Awakening calls a Fetish is an object with a spirit magically bound into it with a spell, that uses one of the spirit's Influences or Numina as a power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:56:49-07:00","id":854034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=854023#post854023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf can't use an Awakened-made Spirit fetish and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely pissed off at least one mage, I just know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:02:49-07:00","id":854037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=854034#post854034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's definitely pissed off at least one mage, I just know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI could see the nature and more varied effects of werewolf fetishes being very *interesting* to a mage and it seems like it'd be a really good Mystery for one to pursue and investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 03-27-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:13:44-07:00","id":854042,"title":"","content":"'Course, none of this will stop an unwitting mortal from activating a dangerous fetish by accident if they find it. Because Plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:23:11-07:00","id":854051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=854042#post854042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Course, none of this will stop an unwitting mortal from activating a dangerous fetish by accident if they find it. Because Plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell yes. Your game, your rules, etc. Under those circumstances I'd be more inclined to make the mortal actually an unwitting Wolf-Blooded with a new Tell that lets them use fetishes but that has no particular outward physical indications of their nature, so that they don't truly know what they are or why they can use the strange, occult bag they found to call up wailing things of fear, or to use the charred key of bone to make the fire dance and spread with nothing but a laugh. That in turn means that when the pack discover the problem and have to figure out how to deal with it, it's not as simple as 'kill the unwitting human who is wielding a dangerous fetish' but that the actual human themselves is potentially a useful asset, a factor that now needs to be considered when acting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:26:52-07:00","id":854055,"title":"","content":"All of that is super interesting, thanks Dave and Acr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:11:52-07:00","id":854208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=854023#post854023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBy the rules for fetishes in the corebook, no. It requires the user to be an Uratha, and various fetish effects wouldn't even work with anything other than an Uratha anyway (like the Facet alteration ones).<br /> <br /> Awakening has always had Spirit-Arcanum-related fetishes as well, but they work differently to werewolf fetishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, makes sense.<br /> <br /> That being said, can it be assumed 'Outsider/Wolfblood' Fetishes are still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for 