signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;...and then we discovered it wasn't the Robot King after all, it was the real one. Fortunately I was able to reattach the head.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/644-mcbaine","name":"McBaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:11:16-07:00","id":855077,"title":"","content":"Well, I can tell you that it is indeed in colour, At least for the most part. There are bits recycled from first edition and a few new ones in black (well, brown) and white.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/articles/view/tabletop/reviews/13858-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-2nd-Edition-Review-Onyx-Path-Delivers-2E-W#&amp;gid=gallery_4110&amp;pid=6\" target=\"_blank\">The escapist review of the book has a few pictures from it included.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-29-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:59:45-07:00","id":855639,"title":"","content":"Hello :-)<br /> <br /> Does anyone know what exactly this means? For the life of me I can't seem to find any other &quot;Moon&quot; gifts that could apply...<br /> <br /> &quot;A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:48:49-07:00","id":855658,"title":"","content":"It means nothing! For now. New Moon Gifts will be written one day*, all else goes well, and then that rule will be important. But for now it's just prep, baring homebrew.<br /> <br /> *And to be fair, a not official but written by a writer Moon Gift exists <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">here, alongside the design principles if you want to make your own.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:43:44-07:00","id":855693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=855639#post855639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello :-)<br /> <br /> Does anyone know what exactly this means? For the life of me I can't seem to find any other &amp;quot;Moon&amp;quot; gifts that could apply...<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It means they plan to add more Moon Gifts in later books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:27:53-07:00","id":855775,"title":"","content":"Righty-o, thanks :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:20:34-07:00","id":856000,"title":"","content":"Would you let All Doors Locked open a bank vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:26:56-07:00","id":856006,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's no different from any other door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:27:51-07:00","id":856009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=856000#post856000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you let All Doors Locked open a bank vault?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you would need something else for the alarm, though. Like Shutdown.<br /> <br /> All Doors Locked wouldn't open the safe deposit boxes. You would use Command Artifice for the locks on them.<br /> <br /> Really you could just tear it apart with your claws if you had the right Merits and Gifts.<br /> <br /> As an aside, check this vault door out, it's the biggest one in the world.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Cleveland_FRB_Vault_Door.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It weighs 100 tons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:44:49-07:00","id":856411,"title":"","content":"Hello :-)<br /> <br /> Perhaps I'm just not understanding Conditions properly (this is entirely plausible), but I'm a bit confused when reading the Awestruck condition. (My apologies if this isn't the right place to ask this... the condition is listed in the Forsaken book). Anyway, my question is &quot;Why is this a Persistent condition, if the only thing needed for its Resolution is for the source of the Awe to leave the character's presence?&quot; Am I missing something? Does the condition just keep being Resolved and character reconditioned every time the Awe-striking source comes and goes? That seems like an awful lot of Condition-Resolution Beats being gained, on top of the Beats gained from taking actions that serve the demands of the source...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:54:18-07:00","id":856440,"title":"","content":"I think it might be because only persistent conditions allow you to get beats for reasons other than resolving them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once per game session, a character can gain a Beat when a Persistent Condition impacts her life. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:09:13-07:00","id":856449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=856440#post856440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might be because only persistent conditions allow you to get beats for reasons other than resolving them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I totally get that. But Awestruck lists both a Resolution and a Beat. My understanding is that Resolving a Condition (permanent or otherwise) grans a Beat, as well as doing whatever is listed next to &quot;Beat:&quot; on the Condition card. But if Awestruck is a Persistent Condition, why is resolving it so transiently simple? All that needs to happen is for the source of the Awe to leave the room. I'm certain I'm somehow misreading this... It can't possibly be that easy, can it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":11526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","user":"lasellj","date":".  typo 03-31-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:09:07-07:00","id":856517,"title":"","content":"I don't recall writing it with the Persistent tag, to be honest, so I'm gonna assume that got added later; or I mucked up with the draft and *did* write Persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:14:14-07:00","id":856522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=856517#post856517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall writing it with the Persistent tag, to be honest, so I'm gonna assume that got added later; or I mucked up with the draft and *did* write Persistent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, cool, thanks. :-) That makes more sense to me, lol. I ordered the Print on Demand cards from Drivethrurpg, and it's listed as Persistent, with both a Resolution (the awe-striking source leaves) and a beat (do something for the source of awe, essentially).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":