dition?p=856589#post856589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the crimson Falx Fetish. It says that it removes a limb permanently. I was wondering if this circumvents regeneration rules for supernaturals</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it a (persistent) condition, but Uratha would largely be capable of regenerating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T10:53:20-07:00","id":857192,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... I'm trying to find where in the book it talks about how fast or slow Uratha age, but for the life of me I cannot seem to find it. Could anyone happen to please point me in the right direction? Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T10:57:36-07:00","id":857194,"title":"","content":"It's not really spelled out. They generally don't die of old age, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:35:40-07:00","id":857210,"title":"","content":"Granted, violent life is violent, but I mean, is it normal human age? Older than human age? Crazy centuries old werewolf npc likely to show up at some point age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:36:45-07:00","id":857212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=856517#post856517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall writing it with the Persistent tag, to be honest, so I'm gonna assume that got added later; or I mucked up with the draft and *did* write Persistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was added in the Errata stage because it has Beat criteria.<br /> <br /> The Persistent tag is kind of misleadingly named, because there are plenty of Persistent Conditions that are very easy to resolve and plenty of non-Persistent Conditions that are very difficult to resolve. What the tag actually means is that you can get Beats for it without resolving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-01-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:40:57-07:00","id":857216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=857210#post857210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, violent life is violent, but I mean, is it normal human age? Older than human age? Crazy centuries old werewolf npc likely to show up at some point age?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not specified. In fact, 2e doesn't actuall say anything about them having longer life spans than humans, so I would expect the answer to be &quot;the same as humans&quot;. But then there <i>are</i> crazy centuries old NPCs. So really the answer is &quot;they live as long as the story needs them to&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:15:54-07:00","id":857283,"title":"","content":"An elder werewolf can just shrug off most of the stuff that actually kills old people. Heart problems? Illness? &quot;Sprightly&quot; doesn't even begin to describe them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:07:52-07:00","id":859800,"title":"","content":"Hmm... how does one go about summoning a spirit? I can't seem to locate a &quot;Call Gaffling / Jaggling&quot; rite; am I missing it somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:13:02-07:00","id":859803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=859800#post859800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... how does one go about summoning a spirit? I can't seem to locate a &amp;quot;Call Gaffling / Jaggling&amp;quot; rite; am I missing it somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadowcall Rite. Page 145.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:22:55-07:00","id":859808,"title":"","content":"Aha! Thank you! I knew it had to be there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:05:08-07:00","id":861281,"title":"","content":"Hi, i missed the correct rule for the gauru with kuruth / without kuruth: my pc had 11 health levels. On 2\u00b0 turn take 11 Lethal damage... now.<br /> <br /> 1) My PC is in Gauru, no Kuruth. Does he fall unconscious? Does he fall unconscious for a turn and then reawaken?<br /> 2) As above, but with Kuruth. Does He fall unconscious at all?<br /> 3) Damage from Extreme Environment, is it regenerable with Essence or natural healing?<br /> <br /> Thanks to all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:00:36-07:00","id":861346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=861281#post861281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, i missed the correct rule for the gauru with kuruth / without kuruth: my pc had 11 health levels. On 2\u00b0 turn take 11 Lethal damage... now.<br /> <br /> 1) My PC is in Gauru, no Kuruth. Does he fall unconscious? Does he fall unconscious for a turn and then reawaken?<br /> 2) As above, but with Kuruth. Does He fall unconscious at all?<br /> 3) Damage from Extreme Environment, is it regenerable with Essence or natural healing?<br /> <br /> Thanks to all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - Your Werewolf will fall unconscious until she can regenerate, which will be at the START of her turn. So, she is blocked from taking any actions that could happen in another player's turn, but once she reaches her turn, she can Regenerate and act. Remember that time when you got up too fast and your vision went black for a brief second, leaving you a little bit confused? Like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Which means NO DEFENSE while her turn doesnt arrive, the main problem for her.<br /> <br /> 2 - Same as above, no real difference.<br /> <br /> 3 - Unless the Extreme Environment especifically says it blocks Essence Regeneration, it will occur. Natural Regeneration might be blocked by Environments that do that normaly. For example, suffocation blocks Regeneration until breathing can happen, which will block natural regeneration, but not Essence Regeneration.<br /> <br /> OBS: However, suffocation only blocks Natural Regeneration from suffocation specific damage, meaning wounds delivered by that angry shark will still regenerate normally. It might be easier to just count the turns you can still breath. For example, if you have 11 Health, you will be able to suffer 22 bashing suffocation damage before dying, so, 22 turns (Bash, then Lethal, which then make you unconscious). Plenty of time to use your Gauru and destroy whatever is blocking you from breathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 04-07-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:24:37-07:00","id":861369,"title":"","content":"I don't believe he'd fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> P169. 'If a character's Health track is filled with bashing damage, his player must make a reflexive Stamina roll each turn for him to remain conscious. If it fills with lethal damage, then each minute thereafter in which he receives no medical attention - mundane or supernatural - he suffers one more injury.'<br /> <br /> And the next paragraph. 'A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out.'<br /> <br /> You can get the Knocked Down Tilt if you're hit with a strong enough weapon, or someone makes a called shot against your legs and presumably some other ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:33:16-07:00","id":861375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=861369#post861369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe he'd fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out.'<br /> <br /> You can get the Knocked Down Tilt if you're hit with a strong enough weapon, or someone makes a called shot against your legs and presumably some other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf in Gauru dont roll for remain conscious (all bashing damage over healt points) ; nor does bleed out.<br /> No bleed out, meaning that dont take an extra damage over one minute, they have natural regeneration too.<br /> But...an all lethal scenario...what about? Can i take this as a turn of &quot;stunt&quot; tilt?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:38:00-07:00","id":861377,"title":"","content":"Gauru is rage incarnate. It Just. Keeps. Going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:48:34-07:00","id":861386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=861369#post861369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe he'd fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> P169. 'If a character's Health track is filled with bashing damage, his player must make a reflexive Stamina roll each turn for him to remain conscious. If it fills with lethal damage, then each minute thereafter in which he receives no medical attention - mundane or supernatural - he suffers one more injury.'<br /> <br /> And the next paragraph. 'A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out.'<br /> <br /> You can get the Knocked Down Tilt if you're hit with a strong enough weapon, or someone makes a called shot against your legs and presumably some other ways.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I got first edition mixed up in my head. So, Gauru can't be made uncounscious, just plain dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:51:06-07:00","id":861387,"title":"","content":"Oh, ok. Dead or nothing also.<br /> Thanks again ^__^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:55:47-07:00","id":861389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=861387#post861387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, ok. Dead or nothing also.<br /> Thanks again ^__^</div> </div> </div> </div>But it can be Stunned, which might be usefull if you can manage to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:41:00-07:00","id":863835,"title":"","content":"There's a couple mentions of it in the book, mostly in the Hunting Grounds sections, but what kind of effect does human sacrifice have regarding spirits?<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem to be something only murder and death spirits can take, I notice it's been tied up with river spirits a lot. Is a human sacrifice worth the equivalent of the sacrifice's health in Essence? Or is there more involved, providing the sacrifice is dedicated to the spirit and considering the emotions and gravity of the act? In comparison, it suggests 'a small amount of' Essence as bare minimum gathra for a soft leverage, to get past that first impression. Is it the kind of thing that 'taints' spirits? If included in a rite, what kind of modifier would it allow?<br /> <br /> I feel like it's been covered in first edition but I can't think of where, so a book name perhaps with page number would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:32:07-07:00","id":863869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=863835#post863835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple mentions of it in the book, mostly in the Hunting Grounds sections, but what kind of effect does human sacrifice have regarding spirits?<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem to be something only murder and death spirits can take, I notice it's been tied up with river spirits a lot. Is a human sacrifice worth the equivalent of the sacrifice's health in Essence? Or is there more involved, providing the sacrifice is dedicated to the spirit and considering the emotions and gravity of the act? In comparison, it suggests 'a small amount of' Essence as bare minimum gathra for a soft leverage, to get past that first impression. Is it the kind of thing that 'taints' spirits? If included in a rite, what kind of modifier would it allow?<br /> <br /> I feel like it's been covered in first edition but I can't think of where, so a book name perhaps with page number would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always considered that a being with a soul may be sacrificed, allowing any Spirit in the area to consume the Essence generated by the soul. First edition had some Indigam powers that allowed soul consumption, so I've loosely based on that. Roughly, each Integrity Dot translated to three Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:57:03-07:00","id":864086,"title":"","content":"If it's been answered please link me to it. <br /> <br /> How exactly are triggers applied? Is the list on of 103 the only ones to use. Are they set In Stone? When you go down to harmony 4 does that same trigger return that was there last time? <br /> <br /> Abs what about bans that the forsaken get. Is there alistvirviscit just like a spirits? Do the forsaken respond the same was as spirits do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:13:09-07:00","id":864218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=864086#post864086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's been answered please link me to it.<br /> <br /> How exactly are triggers applied? Is the list on of 103 the only ones to use. Are they set In Stone? When you go down to harmony 4 does that same trigger return that was there last time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every werewolf shares the General Triggers. Beyond that, you pick one 'set' of triggers for your character, like Pack or Territory or Wound triggers. You can make your own, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers\">there's a thread that has some custom ones</a>. You could probably change them if your character changes enough in-game, but there's no special rules for that as far as I know. At Harmony 4 or 6 you will have only the General Triggers and the Specific Trigger for your 'set,' even if you jump back and forth between 4 and 5 and 6, unless you decide they can change them. At Harmony 5, you don't suffer from the personal triggers and instead only the General Triggers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abs what about bans that the forsaken get. Is there alistvirviscit just like a spirits? Do the forsaken respond the same was as spirits do? </div> </div> </div>The bans are just like a spirit, you can tailor them to the situation. You get the Ban Condition, on p306, with the compulsion related to the Ban. If you go to low Harmony and then high, then low again, it's possible to have the same bans you had last time. But as a Storyteller, you probably want to tailor them to the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T19:43:01-07:00","id":864673,"title":"","content":"Okay. So the chart in 2e has no triggers at 5 harmony. So then nothing sets him off? <br /> 6-7 have specific triggers just like 4-3 are these triggers different based on harmony rating? Do they stack? If a werewolf has harmony 8 is he affected by one common trigger and two specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T20:54:24-07:00","id":864690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=864673#post864673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So the chart in 2e has no triggers at 5 harmony. So then nothing sets him off?</div> </div> </div> </div>General Triggers do, in the lower right of the triggers sidebar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6-7 have specific triggers just like 4-3 are these triggers different based on harmony rating? Do they stack? If a werewolf has harmony 8 is he affected by one common trigger and two specific? </div> </div> </div>Like I said, you only pick one set of triggers for your personal triggers, like Blood Triggers. Every werewolf has the general triggers automatically, but you pick a personal set of triggers for your own character in character creation. For this example, lets use Blood. If you're at Harmony 9, 8, 2, or 1, you have the Common Trigger, 'Tasting Someone's Blood.' You aren't affected by the Wound trigger, 'Interacting with a Wound-born spirit.' because you didn't pick the Wound triggers for your character. You can still be triggered by General triggers, however, as they affect you always and at every Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T20:56:46-07:00","id":864692,"title":"","content":"Well, because you're supposed to choose from a set, being triggered by your common is usually exactly the same as being triggered by your specific.<br /> <br /> If you're picking and choosing from different sets of triggers as a houserule (common one, I think) I'd rule that they all apply, probably. Not sure. Would be weird to become immune to your specific Wound trigger when your harmony was out of whack.<br /> <br /> And yes, no triggers at 5. Blessed be those that strive for true harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T21:46:01-07:00","id":864706,"title":"","content":"Okay. I was getting general triggers confused with common triggers. Harmony plays s much bigger role than Cover. <br /> Okay next. <br /> <br /> Is there a roll to resist your trigger? <br /> <br /> And what roll gets you out of wasu-Im or is that the resolve + composure roll used to do anything other than killing stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T22:24:29-07:00","id":864714,"title":"","content":"No roll to resist <i>a </i>trigger sending you into <i>Wasu-Im</i>. Once in the soft rage, either attack someone or roll Resolve + Composure to do something else. Each success on this roll gives one turn of doing something besides attacking. Exceptional Success pulls you back out of rage. If you enter Gauru form, you go straight into <i>Basu-Im</i>. If you fail the Resolve + Composure roll, you enter <i>Basu-Im</i>.<br /> <br /> If you reach the end of your <i>Wasu-Im</i> time (determined by Harmony) without achieving Exceptional Success (or other powers that can help), you enter <i>Basu-Im</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T22:55:48-07:00","id":864723,"title":"","content":"Well. Isn't death rage brutal? <br /> I appreciate the answers. A lot of this stuff wasn't hitting me on the head obvious. But I think I have what I need to run my first werewolf game. <br /> <br /> Last question. <br /> I know it will be in 1e but any more info on balehounds? They're the antagonist is like to spend some time on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T01:42:09-07:00","id":864777,"title":"","content":"Only in 1E. Nothing 2E yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:46:23-07:00","id":864892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=864723#post864723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Isn't death rage brutal?<br /> I appreciate the answers. A lot of this stuff wasn't hitting me on the head obvious. But I think I have what I need to run my first werewolf game.<br /> <br /> Last question.<br /> I know it will be in 1e but any more info on balehounds? They're the antagonist is like to spend some time on.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we do have a thread dedicated to talking about them: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...he-bale-hounds</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:48:29-07:00","id":864893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=864714#post864714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No roll to resist <i>a </i>trigger sending you into <i>Wasu-Im</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not technically a 'trigger', but you do get a Resolve+Composure to resist when you are potentially entering kuruth because a packmate goes into Basu-Im. I only bring it up because I totally missed that aspect of the kuruth rules on my first read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:13:06-07:00","id":865028,"title":"","content":"So on gifts. The book says you. Can unlock other moon gifts with what 3 or 5 exp. but there are no other moon gifts. Only shadow gifts tied to auspice other than the ones directly related to that moon phase. Is that what the book is referring? <br /> Do the shadow gifts associated with your auspice still have the restrictions with facets requiring a specific renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:23:34-07:00","id":865031,"title":"","content":"There aren't any other Moon Gifts <i>yet.</i> All going well, there should be more in future supplements. Heck, if you want you could always use <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">official guidelines</a> to make some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:26:03-07:00","id":865032,"title":"","content":"And yes, you can only get a facet for which you have at least one dot in the associated renown, even for affinity gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:11:32-07:00","id":865049,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much guys. This has been a big help. With running my first game Saturday in trying to cover all the things system wise that may come up. <br /> <br /> <br /> Is there any chance of a auspice realated to the blood moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:32:43-07:00","id":865089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865049#post865049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much guys. This has been a big help. With running my first game Saturday in trying to cover all the things system wise that may come up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there any chance of a auspice realated to the blood moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing official, but several people discussed this during the past years. It would probably be a Rahu that has a quirk, not a fully new Auspice, at least that's what makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:41:26-07:00","id":865097,"title":"","content":"There was stuff for it in first edition, in the Signs of the Moon book. They were Gishtahu, the Feasting Killer, and they're viewed as cannibals.<br /> <br /> They could have any Renown as their Auspice Renown except Purity, had Brawl, Intimidation and Survival as Specialty skills, their Gift List involved Full Moon, Rage and Strength, and their Auspice Ability was the Hunger, which allowed them to gain twice as much Essence when eating people, and in a turn when they've fed on someone can spend an addition Essence, on top of their max allowed by Primal Urge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:46:44-07:00","id":865191,"title":"","content":"Is there any real line between &quot;large, powerful Lodge&quot; and &quot;Tribe&quot; other than a sense of historicity and having a Firstborn as a totem? Would a group that could find one of the Firstborn that isn't currently aligned to an existing Tribe be recognized as one?<br /> <br /> Does anything terribly exciting happen at high Primal Urge ratings? I've always liked that Changeling's Wyrd warped their lifespan and precipitated a change into one of the Fae, so I'm curious if anything similar happens in Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T17:10:27-07:00","id":865203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865191#post865191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any real line between &quot;large, powerful Lodge&quot; and &quot;Tribe&quot; other than a sense of historicity and having a Firstborn as a totem? Would a group that could find one of the Firstborn that isn't currently aligned to an existing Tribe be recognized as one?<br /> <br /> Does anything terribly exciting happen at high Primal Urge ratings? I've always liked that Changeling's Wyrd warped their lifespan and precipitated a change into one of the Fae, so I'm curious if anything similar happens in Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, none of your questions are even mentioned in the core book. Developers hinted that we might get more information in the future books, but in second edition, is all up to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> However, first edition had some base rules on high Primal Urge and aging, which roughly translated to the werewolf becoming an immortal slumbering spirit demi-god at the end of the road.<br /> <br /> As for your lodge question, the common answer here in the forums is that yes, the difference between Tribe and Lodge is the number of members and the power of their Totem. Not every Spirit is capable of bestowing blessings to that much members, only above Rank 5, which the First Born happen to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T17:34:33-07:00","id":865216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865191#post865191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any real line between &quot;large, powerful Lodge&quot; and &quot;Tribe&quot; other than a sense of historicity and having a Firstborn as a totem? Would a group that could find one of the Firstborn that isn't currently aligned to an existing Tribe be recognized as one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Size is a factor, and Tribes have their own Renown they offer and a tendency towards certain gifts and a broad idea of a sacred prey. There's also the fact that you can be a member of a Tribe and a Lodge, but not two Lodges. And it's strongly suggested by the one book we have that, yes, a Lodge can become a tribe and the upcoming Pure book should get into that further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anything terribly exciting happen at high Primal Urge ratings? I've always liked that Changeling's Wyrd warped their lifespan and precipitated a change into one of the Fae, so I'm curious if anything similar happens in Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>It seems so, it just hasn't been expanded upon mechanically. 'As her Primal Urge increases, a werewolf sheds her human upbringing. She becomes closer to the Goddess of the Hunt, the ultimate predator. A few werewolves, those who follow the raging beast within, feel the drive to become something more \u2014 akin to the Firstborn, or even to Father Wolf himself.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T18:21:29-07:00","id":865241,"title":"","content":"At the least, Mr. Acrozatarim posted a hint of what he thought an Elder Wolf would be like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\">here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:36:39-07:00","id":865392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865191#post865191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any real line between &quot;large, powerful Lodge&quot; and &quot;Tribe&quot; other than a sense of historicity and having a Firstborn as a totem? Would a group that could find one of the Firstborn that isn't currently aligned to an existing Tribe be recognized as one?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMaybe. People aren't entirely sure because it's not something that's commonly happened. There *is* a difference in the nature of the totem bond between a tribe and a lodge but it's not exactly easy to test where the difference occurs, or why. There's a little bit more on this issue in the Eaters of the Dead write-up in The Pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anything terribly exciting happen at high Primal Urge ratings? I've always liked that Changeling's Wyrd warped their lifespan and precipitated a change into one of the Fae, so I'm curious if anything similar happens in Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>\u200bWe've laid down some hints in 2e that *something* starts to happen once an Uratha hits PU10, but just hints and ideas thus far. And yes, then there's my Lycaon-Ur write-up based on a few notions kicking around my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:11:41-07:00","id":865406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865392#post865392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWe've laid down some hints in 2e that *something* starts to happen once an Uratha hits PU10, but just hints and ideas thus far. And yes, then there's my Lycaon-Ur write-up based on a few notions kicking around my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Lycaon-Ur write-up definitely brings a lot of very awesome things to the metaphorical table, even if it isn't 'canon'. My favourite parts are the implication that uratha can be the totem to a group without becoming a full spirit like some theorize as what happens after PU10 and the idea of uratha getting different versions of auspice from patrons other than Luna. Brings up ideas like strange packs where one of the members has taken the role of totem or an idea I've tossed around where Helios took the role of the 'patron' of the pure in place of Luna and grants solar auspices to replace the luna ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T05:31:25-07:00","id":865436,"title":"","content":"So, when increasing your Auspice Renown, you get the corresponding dot of your Moon Gift. When increasing -any- Renown, you get a facet of Shadow gift you've already unlocked, of the corresponding Renown. As your Auspice Renown is indeed -any- Renown, does that mean when you increase your Auspice Renown that you get both a Moon Gift and a Shadow Gift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T05:36:18-07:00","id":865437,"title":"","content":"Yes. That's exactly right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T05:56:38-07:00","id":865447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865437#post865437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. That's exactly right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you :-)<br /> <br /> Unrelated question... Am I correct that 1s no longer subtract from successes? I was reading through the Dice Rolling section, and I don't seem to see that particular rule anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:03:58-07:00","id":865448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865447#post865447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you :-)<br /> <br /> Unrelated question... Am I correct that 1s no longer subtract from successes? I was reading through the Dice Rolling section, and I don't seem to see that particular rule anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat's never been a rule in the nWoD/ChroD; it's from Masquerade/Apocalypse/etc. So indeed, 1s do not subtract from successes in Forsaken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:14:09-07:00","id":865454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865448#post865448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat's never been a rule in the nWoD/ChroD; it's from Masquerade/Apocalypse/etc. So indeed, 1s do not subtract from successes in Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, duh... &gt;.&lt; Sorry, getting my game lines confused.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:33:07-07:00","id":865467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=865447#post865447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you :-)<br /> <br /> Unrelated question... Am I correct that 1s no longer subtract from successes? I was reading through the Dice Rolling section, and I don't seem to see that particular rule anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are correct. The only way to botch is rolling &quot;1&quot; in a Chance Die. You can also choose to turn a normal Failure into a Dramatic Failure to acquire a Beat.<br /> <br /> Edit: Acrozatarim as faster, probably used Urhan to jump Initiatives...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:18:03-07:00","id":866675,"title":"","content":"Did character creation tonight with my group and did a pre game to. <br /> I'm having a real hard time with starting gifts. Nothing I read is clicking for me. <br /> <br /> So I have a rahu storm-lord <br /> One purity, one honor. <br /> <br /> Character gains moon gift full moon 1st dot. <br /> 2 facets, 1 in two shadow gifts. <br /> 1 wolf gift. <br /> (He can take any of those that resonate with either renown and for the shadow gifts they have to be from auspice or tribe) <br /> So far 3 facets. <br /> <br /> Character gains a 3rd point of renown at creation. If he goes purity he's at his 2nd level moon gift. If he chooses another renown he unlocks a facet of any shadow gift that was previously applicable, or another wild gift facet. <br /> <br /> Starting character would have 5 facets, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:22:36-07:00","id":866676,"title":"","content":"4 Facets.<br /> <br /> 2 Shadow gifts always. <br /> <br /> An additional 1 Moon Gift and 1 Wolf Gift if he starts with his auspice renown at 1.<br /> <br /> Or an additional 2 Moon Gifts (and no Wolf Gift) if he starts with his auspice renown at 2.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:31:56-07:00","id":866679,"title":"","content":"So what about my players who managed to take 3 points in their auspice renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:38:38-07:00","id":866683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=866679#post866679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what about my players who managed to take 3 points in their auspice renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess they skipped over the rule on p83 under Renown in character creation that says, 'By this stage, you should already have two dots of Renown; one for your character\u2019s auspice, and one for her tribe. Choose another dot in a Renown of your choice, <i>but note that you cannot take a third dot in a single Renown at this point</i>.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:43:13-07:00","id":866685,"title":"","content":"I must have skipped that myself. That makes a lot more sense. Thank you. <br /> <br /> I'm going to get this game's systems down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:53:57-07:00","id":866687,"title":"","content":"No problem.<br /> <br /> I usually find a solid read through helps more than jumping back and forth to parts I may find more interesting, something better served for later. I try to do it before sessions, too, just going over what is most likely to happen, what rolls are most likely to come up and ensure I know the modifiers placed on them by NPCs or situations, that I have names for the characters that need them. Obviously you can't predict it all, and there's a lot to be said for ad libbing, but getting a good start in your head helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:04:07-07:00","id":866688,"title":"","content":"I've done one read through of werewolf. I tried to do another one in the time this game was starting. But beast came out. <br /> Anyways. I really do appreciate everyone's help with this game. It's the first CofD game that's given me trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T07:08:25-07:00","id":866810,"title":"","content":"Do Moon Gifts create any sort of mark that could be outlined and made into a tattoo in the same manner as Shadow Gifts? Granted, I understand that Moon Gifts aren't carved physically into the Uratha the same as Shadow Gifts are, but is there any sort of visible indication?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:23:41-07:00","id":866846,"title":"","content":"While there isn't any definitive affirmation, wouldn't the corresponding auspice renown qualify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:47:21-07:00","id":866859,"title":"","content":"That was my thought as well, though I was hoping for of definitive affirmation. Ah well. Thanks :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:03:32-07:00","id":866933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=866810#post866810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Moon Gifts create any sort of mark that could be outlined and made into a tattoo in the same manner as Shadow Gifts? Granted, I understand that Moon Gifts aren't carved physically into the Uratha the same as Shadow Gifts are, but is there any sort of visible indication?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. Generally you can see the gifts in the Hisil. The idea is you can see all the gift and renown marks and sort of see a 'story' of what the werewolf is. It's like forging your spirit, from a spirit of the hunt to something more specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:54:59-07:00","id":866963,"title":"","content":"Hey are spirits in a werewolves territory like fleshed out npc's that they may deal with on a regular basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:03:41-07:00","id":866973,"title":"","content":"Often, yes. You can probably skimp on it if the players aren't too active in the Hisil. And Rank one and two spirits don't have much of a unique personality on their own, though that doesn't keep them from resembling memorable pet, child or animal characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T02:10:55-07:00","id":867443,"title":"","content":"You could think of it like a caricature of a gangland sort of thing - the generic mooks don't have a lot of personality, but the boss sure as hell does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:28:57-07:00","id":869535,"title":"","content":"This might not be the right place to ask this. If that's the case, I offer my apologies, but I'm not really sure where else to ask...<br /> <br /> What would classify as circumstances under which a Forsaken would leave their pack and go elsewhere? I've read that the pack essentially seems to be the single most important aspect of an Uratha character's identity, and yet, how are new characters coming into the game explained? Unless they experienced their First Change either in play or very recently ago, they have to have come from somewhere else - and very likely from another pack. If the pack unit is closer than family, and more devoted than a cult, what on earth would prompt someone to say &quot;Y'know what guys, we've been tight for years, but I'm gonna check out. Peace!&quot; ? Aside from the &quot;my entire pack is dead&quot; trope, or an antisocial character that rejects the concept of pack, are there any legit reasons for a character to strike out for different pastures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:38:01-07:00","id":869547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=869535#post869535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might not be the right place to ask this. If that's the case, I offer my apologies, but I'm not really sure where else to ask...<br /> <br /> What would classify as circumstances under which a Forsaken would leave their pack and go elsewhere? I've read that the pack essentially seems to be the single most important aspect of an Uratha character's identity, and yet, how are new characters coming into the game explained? Unless they experienced their First Change either in play or very recently ago, they have to have come from somewhere else - and very likely from another pack. If the pack unit is closer than family, and more devoted than a cult, what on earth would prompt someone to say &amp;quot;Y'know what guys, we've been tight for years, but I'm gonna check out. Peace!&amp;quot; ? Aside from the &amp;quot;my entire pack is dead&amp;quot; trope, or an antisocial character that rejects the concept of pack, are there any legit reasons for a character to strike out for different pastures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves still have a human side. They could move away for any reason anyone else would; following work, love, family, cheap rent, etc. Then there's also the fact that while the pack is everything, nothing stops your packmates from being raging assholes; it doesn't matter how good the Rahu is in combat if he keeps belittling you. There could be issues of affiliation, like being a younger Uratha that doesn't really &quot;get&quot; the whole Bone Shadows thing but none of the other Tribes have any power locally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:51:48-07:00","id":869565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=869535#post869535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would classify as circumstances under which a Forsaken would leave their pack and go elsewhere? I've read that the pack essentially seems to be the single most important aspect of an Uratha character's identity, and yet, how are new characters coming into the game explained? Unless they experienced their First Change either in play or very recently ago, they have to have come from somewhere else - and very likely from another pack. If the pack unit is closer than family, and more devoted than a cult, what on earth would prompt someone to say &quot;Y'know what guys, we've been tight for years, but I'm gonna check out. Peace!&quot; ? Aside from the &quot;my entire pack is dead&quot; trope, or an antisocial character that rejects the concept of pack, are there any legit reasons for a character to strike out for different pastures?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be closer than family because there's a spiritual link between them all, and they're all keeping a secret that other members are the only ones who can understand, at least compared to the rest of humanity. It's still not a guarantee, plenty of packs are probably on edge with each other. But more devoted than a cult is a bit much. I don't doubt there would be some packs like that but most of them wouldn't reach that level of devotion among packmembers.<br /> <br /> The reasons for leaving are potentially infinite. A pack dying is appropriate, but sometimes a werewolf might just believe they need to be doing something else with their lives, perhaps as a personal decision or inspired by a hazy dream or missive from a spirit. They might never have truly felt like they fit in with their pack, or held close to their human life which requires a location change.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the upcoming Pack book will be offering a lot of answers for these questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:57:52-07:00","id":869576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=869565#post869565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">more devoted than a cult is a bit much</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. I was quoting the Purity facet of the Inspiration Gift. &quot;The pack is tighter than a family and more devoted than a cult. With this Facet, those bonds are almost unbreakable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both excellent thoughts though. Thank you guys :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:11:48-07:00","id":872335,"title":"","content":"When using Feet of Mist, would it block or fail to block automated drone cameras or satellite imaging from tracking them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-