peg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:20:34-07:00","id":885701,"title":"","content":"All such rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:31:10-07:00","id":888557,"title":"","content":"When a spirit uses Aggressive Meme, it is resisted by Resolve+Composure. Do people it spreads to after the initial use get a roll to resist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:16:03-07:00","id":888756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=888557#post888557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a spirit uses Aggressive Meme, it is resisted by Resolve+Composure. Do people it spreads to after the initial use get a roll to resist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it but more often than not, by the time it becomes endemic it's left to ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:34:32-07:00","id":889775,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not entirely across Harmony loss (and it's up come up surprisingly little in-game). How do people read the minuses to the Breakpoint roll working? The book says that for breaks towards Flesh, you get a -1 for each Harmony dot above 5, and the other way for breaks towards Spirit.<br /> <br /> Sooooo, does that mean that a Harmony 7 Uratha breaking towards Flesh rolls Comp + Res - 2 (+2 because of their Spirit Touchstone)?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, will they then roll Comp + Res (+2 for the Spirit Touchstone) when breaking towards Spirit? As in, no minuses because their Harmony ISN'T below 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:41:18-07:00","id":889776,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It's easier to slide down the side you're already on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:18:59-07:00","id":889998,"title":"","content":"Could a group other than an uratha pack have a totem and buy the totem merit? Like say, a cabal of mages with a spirit user or a coterie of vampires who have blood tenebrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:27:03-07:00","id":890000,"title":"","content":"Sure, let's give Werewolves countermagic and dispelation too.<br /> <br /> RAW wise? Nope. You won't see another line with a published totem merit. But really, you can do whatever you want in your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:58:27-07:00","id":890025,"title":"","content":"To be fair, nothing in the Moon's Grace merit forbids <i>non-uratha </i>supernaturals from being in a pack with it. And Magnanimous Totem can boost the buying power of wolf blooded, which other supernaturals count as in regular packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:35:23-07:00","id":890043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890025#post890025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, nothing in the Moon's Grace merit forbids <i>non-uratha </i>supernaturals from being in a pack with it. And Magnanimous Totem can boost the buying power of wolf blooded, which other supernaturals count as in regular packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would still need actual Blooded in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:44:00-07:00","id":890050,"title":"","content":"Would mages with tells count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:44:23-07:00","id":890051,"title":"","content":"And the game is pretty modular. The developer in particular seems enthused about letting players try new things. It's not something I'd go for, but nothing is keeping you from taking the Wolf-Blooded only restriction off and putting on a Vampire only or Sin-Eater only or whatever you want for your game. Just like people can have Daywalker vampire-Beast hybrids and Awakened Prometheans and Were-Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:05:30-07:00","id":890064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890050#post890050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would mages with tells count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in my games. Spirits have an understanding, hell, something of a tradition with werewolves and their descendants. Mages would be seen as more prone to dominate the shadow than co-existing with spirits. Look at their familiars. Even spirits within packs, apart from the totem would be getting a fairer treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:20:38-07:00","id":890130,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to have a pack with a mage in it whose backstory is that the totem used to be their familiar (but is now too powerful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:19:55-07:00","id":890228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890130#post890130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting to have a pack with a mage in it whose backstory is that the totem used to be their familiar (but is now too powerful).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an excellent backstory to explain a mage pack member.<br /> <br /> Chris needs to get right on it...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:30:05-07:00","id":890457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=889776#post889776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It's easier to slide down the side you're already on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification! Interesting that it doesn't give any minuses for Uratha at Harmony 5. That means that it's not *really* that hard to maintain, once you get there, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:19:11-07:00","id":890605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890000#post890000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, let's give Werewolves countermagic and dispelation too.<br /> <br /> RAW wise? Nope. You won't see another line with a published totem merit. But really, you can do whatever you want in your table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So... you think they could, yes?<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously though, I'm aware there's not likely going to be a fully canon ruling on this (unless Bunyip or Acrozatarim or Stew himself steps in and makes one). Personally I rule it that a non-uratha group who have a tie to the hisil in some fashion (like a coterie of vampires where at least one member has blood tenebrous or a mage cabal where at least on member has a tie to the hisil such that they'd accept a totem rather than a familiar) would be able to take a totem, but I was curious about the opinions of people here.<br /> <br /> My personal view is that the totem isn't a unique part of being an uratha, it's simply a natural part of flesh based things joining the hisil ecology, a binding that draws the group together but at the same time being an ambassador to the hisil at large. I mean, the purified are able to get personal totems as well, as much as 1e is a valid influence on the conversation here. I personally would 100% allow a mage cabal or vampire coterie or some other group to take a totem from the hisil, if they were able to convince me that they have actually formed a bond with a spirit. My limitation would be on roleplay, requiring that the non-uratha groups<br /> <br /> 1. Have a tie to the hisil / spirits to start: and<br /> 2. Are able to convince / force a spirit to act as totem for their group (which is going to be naturally harder than an uratha pack will find, unless they're at the point where spirits consider the group part of the ecology, like a mage cabal with an adept of spirit, or a group of vampires with Claire Redfield's 2e version of Blood Tenebrous at the right level.)<br /> <br /> Whereas your typical uratha containing pack could just go and find a spirit and either convince them or force them to be totem.<br /> <br /> Good to know your view though, clearly you think of the totem as a far more integral part of the uratha template than I do, my friend who GM's for me would probably agree with you that allowing on-uratha groups to take a totem is cribbing too much on their proprietary stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:37:14-07:00","id":890623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890228#post890228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's an excellent backstory to explain a mage pack member.<br /> <br /> Chris needs to get right on it...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's similar to something I've thought of doing, but the totem didn't used to be a familiar in my version of it, it still is one. My idea is a thyrsus who joins an uratha pack once they hit 4 dots of spirit (and have gained an honorary rank and the ability to create familiars) and turns the totem of their pack into a familiar, resulting in them having both the familiar and totem bond. I'm going to use it as an NPC in my upcoming mage game if any of my players focus on the hisil at all (one of them looks like he might be with one of the two characters he has prepped for this game (godamn exams ruining my CoD gaming)). I will admit I skipped to the lodges section of the Pack as soon as I opened it and haven't read the crossover section any deeper than a skimming, but I doubt there's much if anything on mages screwing with the totem of a pack they belong to by using the spirit arcana, so I'm going to make my own conclusions with regards to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:41:11-07:00","id":890624,"title":"","content":"It would make hunting hard, since the totem would have to stay within five yards of whatever object or person you attuned it to. The hardest part might be getting the totem to be willing to do it. Or surviving after the werewolves find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-14-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:15:07-07:00","id":890640,"title":"","content":"The way totems and familiars work now there's really no point in being both. Familiar just protects the spirit from essence bleed in twilight, which being a totem also does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:54:10-07:00","id":890729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=890623#post890623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's similar to something I've thought of doing, but the totem didn't used to be a familiar in my version of it, it still is one. My idea is a thyrsus who joins an uratha pack once they hit 4 dots of spirit (and have gained an honorary rank and the ability to create familiars) and turns the totem of their pack into a familiar, resulting in them having both the familiar and totem bond. I'm going to use it as an NPC in my upcoming mage game if any of my players focus on the hisil at all (one of them looks like he might be with one of the two characters he has prepped for this game (godamn exams ruining my CoD gaming)). I will admit I skipped to the lodges section of the Pack as soon as I opened it and haven't read the crossover section any deeper than a skimming, but I doubt there's much if anything on mages screwing with the totem of a pack they belong to by using the spirit arcana, so I'm going to make my own conclusions with regards to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages that take totems have to prove they have the spirit's interest at heart, which is considerably more difficult with their burning obsessions. Could they device a spell to do it? Sure they could. Then they have to deal with having an alien creature applying bans on their behaviors and aspirations that will likely conflict with what polite mage society thinks as wise, and that can be exploited. How hard do you think it would be for the local Pylon to figure out your bans? Then what happens when this spell runs out? To relinquish it safely at an indefinite duration is a life-long bond. Can they make that commitment? Even some Uratha are incapable of doing so.<br /> <br /> The case of a singular mage who joins in a pack is clearly spelled out in The Pack's Other section. The same complications arise, without the pack finding out that the mage is attempting to exert undue manipulation on their literal spirit. That could turn ugly, fast.<br /> <br /> Vampires? They usually have more pressing matters at hand rather than to appease some shadow entity and running the risk of being labelled demonologists by the Second and First States.<br /> <br /> If you want to explore all that, go ahead. I'm not going to send ninjas at your table to stop you. I'm just enumerating the complications such a thing creates, which should be considered for a greater experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:48:34-07:00","id":900784,"title":"","content":"If a Wolf-Blooded has picked up additional Tells via merit, do they also keep these when acquiring another supernatural template, or only their original Tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:19:42-07:00","id":900840,"title":"","content":"If a wolf blooded was born with the merit, what <i>is </i>their original Tell? <br /> <br /> I'd say they keep both/all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:22:48-07:00","id":901260,"title":"","content":"The spirits are very hard to be killed because you have to drain the essence first and then damage the corpus and most of then are hostile/afraid to the very nature of Uratha. Assuming that, any or most of the changes in the spiritual realm has to start from the material world.<br /> <br /> Exemple: You have a crime/drug problem in the territory. Its kinda big and now after a while you have defeated the cause of everything &quot;the boss&quot;.<br /> Now you know is temporary until other criminals try to revenge on you. Now you have peace, but you have to act fast because you know if you weak their spiritual crime/drug counterparts in the hisil you will mantain a safer Terriotry. and then what? What should you do in the spirit realm? How did your actions eliminating by force the crime in the material realm reflected in the Hisil? Claws and fangs to destroy the spirits? but if you do that they will return. Should you enter blindly in the crime lord spirit lair and try to talk to him? You want to eliminate crime in your territory why reason with crime spirit?<br /> <br /> So thats my &quot;simple question&quot; i hope im being simple enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:32:00-07:00","id":901268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901260#post901260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirits are very hard to be killed because you have to drain the essence first and then damage the corpus and most of then are hostile/afraid to the very nature of Uratha. Assuming that, any or most of the changes in the spiritual realm has to start from the material world.<br /> <br /> Exemple: You have a crime/drug problem in the territory. Its kinda big and now after a while you have defeated the cause of everything &quot;the boss&quot;.<br /> Now you know is temporary until other criminals try to revenge on you. Now you have peace, but you have to act fast because you know if you weak their spiritual crime/drug counterparts in the hisil you will mantain a safer Terriotry. and then what? What should you do in the spirit realm? How did your actions eliminating by force the crime in the material realm reflected in the Hisil? Claws and fangs to destroy the spirits? but if you do that they will return. Should you enter blindly in the crime lord spirit lair and try to talk to him? You want to eliminate crime in your territory why reason with crime spirit?<br /> <br /> So thats my &quot;simple question&quot; i hope im being simple enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also interested in what someone else has to say on this, but as I understand it so far, Spirits really hate being discorporated. Even if they're smart enough to know they can survive it or have that discorporate manifestation, the pain and vulnerability that such a &quot;death&quot; incurs makes a Spirit want to avoid it as much as possible. They also need to reform in a place of appropriate resonance, which makes them vulnerable to a repeat attack. If the Urathra doesn't destroy the spirit, another spirit trying to eat them certainly will if they've been weakened from discorporation..<br /> <br /> edit: on that note, how do spirits eat each other, just the essence stealing trick to their lesser template? How should that look when you roleplay it, do they take bites out of each other? How would it look for say, a cellphone looking Communication Spirit trying to eat another of its kind?<br /> Also, do werewolves <i>eat</i> spirits, and how does that look mechanically? Does it require a gift? Does the werewolf take essence from chomping the spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-27-2016, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:02:49-07:00","id":901299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901268#post901268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: on that note, how do spirits eat each other, just the essence stealing trick to their lesser template? How should that look when you roleplay it, do they take bites out of each other? How would it look for say, a cellphone looking Communication Spirit trying to eat another of its kind?</div> </div> </div> </div>The baseline metaphor of greatest utility, I think, is amoebas \u2014 regardless of what form the consumption takes, a spirit consumes bits of other spirits by engulfing and incorporating them; a spirit is wholly consumed when the last of its directive portions have been subverted.<br /> <br /> There aren't really mechanics for the threshold of total consumption because it's kind of an inherently narrative turning point, but it's important to remember that spirits imbue some of their nature into their Essence by dint of having it and that spirits are what they eat; part of the reason spirit lords set up tithing systems is because it lets them cycle their personal subtype of Essence back into the court and hungry spirits are less likely to turn down Essence that fits their basic nature.<br /> <br /> Feeding is a means of establishing dominance in Shadow ecology, because making other spirits dependent upon you and/or having them continue to exist at your mercy effectively turns them into extensions of yourself in a means that is only made more literal by total incorporation. Keeping that in mind, recognizable-spirit predation tends to be illustrated in fashions that demonstrate the superiority of the predator or mark the prey as subordinate to the predator when successful. Depending on type, a cell-phone spirit might overwhelm its lessers with chatter or force them to give up their secrets; a spirit of graffiti makes an abandoned building its own by tagging its spirit over and other until the walls run over with cheap paint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:31:18-07:00","id":901321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901260#post901260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exemple: You have a crime/drug problem in the territory. Its kinda big and now after a while you have defeated the cause of everything &quot;the boss&quot;.<br /> Now you know is temporary until other criminals try to revenge on you. Now you have peace, but you have to act fast because you know if you weak their spiritual crime/drug counterparts in the hisil you will mantain a safer Terriotry. and then what? What should you do in the spirit realm? How did your actions eliminating by force the crime in the material realm reflected in the Hisil? Claws and fangs to destroy the spirits? but if you do that they will return. Should you enter blindly in the crime lord spirit lair and try to talk to him? You want to eliminate crime in your territory why reason with crime spirit?<br /> <br /> So thats my &quot;simple question&quot; i hope im being simple enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could have been more directly asked.<br /> <br /> There's no one way, or even a right way, to deal with problems like this.<br /> <br /> An obvious way is to kill 'the boss.' But if you're restricting it to actions in the spirit world you can limit and weaken the spirits of crime. They would just come back later if it was a white room or something, but it's not. It's an ecosystem and it hates a vacuum just like the real world so something else is going to take advantage. Weakened crime spirits are easy prey for police or law spirits, for instance. The police or law spirits can get stronger, and influence the gurihal that way. They're out there using Strengthen on the detective trying to solve a case, Control or Manipulation to make sure the officer sees the evidence.<br /> <br /> 'You want to eliminate crime in your territory' is a bit of a leap. Werewolves break laws routinely, and if you have an authoritarian Hisil full of mirror-shaded cop spirits you're going to find it just as hostile as one full of empty-hooded thug spirits lurking in dark alleys to gank you. It's about balance, not extremism, you deal with spirits because killing them is going to upset that balance, while encouraging them to act more moderately is 'safer.' Not that you <i>can't </i>try to eliminate certain aspects of things you don't like, but it's the kind of thing a Storyteller should take advantage of. Someone on the forums pointed out that Forsaken is all about unintended consequences, from the death of Father Wolf to landing on the moon. It's a good thing to keep in mind when Storytelling spirit shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:11:32-07:00","id":901595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901260#post901260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirits are very hard to be killed because you have to drain the essence first and then damage the corpus and most of then are hostile/afraid to the very nature of Uratha. Assuming that, any or most of the changes in the spiritual realm has to start from the material world.<br /> <br /> Exemple: You have a crime/drug problem in the territory. Its kinda big and now after a while you have defeated the cause of everything &quot;the boss&quot;.<br /> Now you know is temporary until other criminals try to revenge on you. Now you have peace, but you have to act fast because you know if you weak their spiritual crime/drug counterparts in the hisil you will mantain a safer Terriotry. and then what? What should you do in the spirit realm? How did your actions eliminating by force the crime in the material realm reflected in the Hisil? Claws and fangs to destroy the spirits? but if you do that they will return. Should you enter blindly in the crime lord spirit lair and try to talk to him? You want to eliminate crime in your territory why reason with crime spirit?<br /> <br /> So thats my &quot;simple question&quot; i hope im being simple enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated damage drains essence, so indeed, using the spirit's bane will eventually destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T19:38:32-07:00","id":901660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=900784#post900784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Wolf-Blooded has picked up additional Tells via merit, do they also keep these when acquiring another supernatural template, or only their original Tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>St fiat but if the st allows you would keep all. They may rule that some no longer apply however so it could be a case by case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T04:07:19-07:00","id":901937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901321#post901321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no one way, or even a right way, to deal with problems like this.<br /> <br /> An obvious way is to kill 'the boss.' But if you're restricting it to actions in the spirit world you can limit and weaken the spirits of crime.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The idea is that we dont have justice spirits at all, its a forgotten neighborhood</b>. We have only<b> strong spirits of </b><u>crime/violence/drug/prostitution</u> - /<u>poverty/demotivation/fear </u>- And the few good old people who live there for a long time their grandchildren and children come visit thinking in their minds how great is to visit gramma etc attracts <u>Love/Confort/Nostalgia/</u><br /> <br /> <b>The pack</b> has a dream of turning the territory into a safer place. The alpha has a crime trauma and tends to imagine that the spirits that cause this are also something to be fought.<br /> <b>The pack </b>created a secret club(made of humans) that focuses on ideals that justice can be done if we take some actions.<br /> We have a pack formed by two Urathas and a Wolf-blooded.<br /> The common most important people we have a police detective a patrol officer, directly related to the player characters. And we have half a dozen people who are motivated by alpha speeches that feeds the thirst for justice.<br /> <br /> Players began taking action with a very specific rule &quot;Do not kill if it is absolutely necessary&quot;: They created specific days of the month to send their people associated with the club to find criminals in the act crime and punish them there. They tied most of them and left to deliver to the police. Criminals seeking redemption are watched carefully and when they are ready can even join the group.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Trying to imagine the reflection of this is extremely difficult. I've read a lot of nwod lines and even comparing with Awakening that has plenty of little rules to be aware is not so hard to build campaigns and understand causes and consequences. Still Werewolf is the most difficult game to GM because is abstract. (Actualy even Apocalypse from the older releases is easier) </b></span>I'm really impressed with the monstrous difficulty I'm having to imagine the spiritual world without taking references directly from books or forum and how hard is to conceive the spiritual changes by player actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 05-28-2016, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:05:59-07:00","id":902021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901937#post901937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]The idea is that we dont have justice spirits at all</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901937#post901937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The pack </b>created a secret club(made of humans) that focuses on ideals that justice can be done if we take some actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. You have justice spirits (for whatever you want 'justice spirits' to be). They're likely weak and need protection from the various 'crime spirits' (who'd love to feast on justice), but they exist somewhere important to the club - where the humans meet and talk about bringing justice to the neighbourhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901937#post901937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to imagine the reflection of this is extremely difficult. I've read a lot of nwod lines and even comparing with Awakening that has plenty of little rules to be aware is not so hard to build campaigns and understand causes and consequences. Still Werewolf is the most difficult game to GM because is abstract.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way of doing it is to picture the physical world territory. If possible, sketch out a rough map - it doesn't need to be too detailed, just include some of the major locations within the neighbourhood, such as the pack's den, the place where the humans meet to talk about justice, the crime boss's place, the drug dealing areas etc. (Maybe even the police station.)<br /> <br /> Around these key points, draw a circle reflecting how strong an influence each point has on the <i>Hisil</i>. Don't worry if they overlap.The justice club is likely to be very small, the pack maybe bigger, drug hot spots may not be circles, they may be oblongs along certain roads, the kingpin's circle may overlap several others.<br /> <br /> Now, within these circles are the spirit ecologies. The justice spirits stay close to the human clubhouse. Spirits of addiction, pain, greed and death stick close to the drug dens. Spirits of wealth, greed and power are close to the kingpin. Where the circles overlap, the different spirits mingle and prey on each other. The justice spirits will probably be consumed as fast as they can spawn unless the Uratha help. The zone around the den is probably a somewhat safe haven as those spirits allowed by the pack and the totem linger for long.<br /> <br /> Take your zones, imagine what you think they look like in the physical world (and I'm sure you can find a bunch of images from movies and TV to help here), then stick a twisted 'Silent Hill' filter over them. As one example, for drug-heavy streets, think <i>The Wire.</i> Roughly humanoid substance spirits hang out on corners, using their Numen and Influences to draw prospective 'customers' in, offering them the fix they need. Sometimes they'll just take a little piece of Essence for the trade, but they'll snatch up the smaller spirits and consume them whole. Spirits of withdrawal pain and addiction sidle up to the pusher spirits, their natures simultaneously needing to approach but wanting to stay away and survive. Spirits of greed and power cruise the addiction places, demanding tithes of Essence to take to bigger power spirits closer to the (human) kingpin. If they don't get what they want, they take the pusher spirits instead to be consumed - this opens up a vacancy in the drug court.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:19:40-07:00","id":902033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=901937#post901937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The idea is that we dont have justice spirits at all, its a forgotten neighborhood</b>. We have only<b> strong spirits of </b><u>crime/violence/drug/prostitution</u> - /<u>poverty/demotivation/fear </u>- And the few good old people who live there for a long time their grandchildren and children come visit thinking in their minds how great is to visit gramma etc attracts <u>Love/Confort/Nostalgia/</u><br /> <br /> <b>The pack</b> has a dream of turning the territory into a safer place. The alpha has a crime trauma and tends to imagine that the spirits that cause this are also something to be fought.<br /> <b>The pack </b>created a secret club(made of humans) that focuses on ideals that justice can be done if we take some actions.<br /> We have a pack formed by two Urathas and a Wolf-blooded.<br /> The common most important people we have a police detective a patrol officer, directly related to the player characters. And we have half a dozen people who are motivated by alpha speeches that feeds the thirst for justice.<br /> <br /> Players began taking action with a very specific rule &quot;Do not kill if it is absolutely necessary&quot;: They created specific days of the month to send their people associated with the club to find criminals in the act crime and punish them there. They tied most of them and left to deliver to the police. Criminals seeking redemption are watched carefully and when they are ready can even join the group.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Trying to imagine the reflection of this is extremely difficult. I've read a lot of nwod lines and even comparing with Awakening that has plenty of little rules to be aware is not so hard to build campaigns and understand causes and consequences. Still Werewolf is the most difficult game to GM because is abstract. (Actualy even Apocalypse from the older releases is easier) </b></span>I'm really impressed with the monstrous difficulty I'm having to imagine the spiritual world without taking references directly from books or forum and how hard is to conceive the spiritual changes by player actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the existence of police and the speeches about justice it's at least a little surprising you don't have any police or punishment spirits. You basically have a gang of vigilantes. Granted it's small but they should have an impact.<br /> <br /> Changing the Hisil isn't something that can usually be done overnight, if you want to make things safer you will probably want to work at it more than a few days a month. Form a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neighborhood_watch\" target=\"_blank\">neighborhood watch</a>. Get some cameras out there or police presence. You're really limiting yourself with the no kill rule, which is valid but as a pack of werewolves you have the ability to do a lot more than 'tie up' occasional criminals. Our pack went after drug dealers in our first couple hunts and they were far too easy, almost laughably so, even with hit squads and guns, and most of us aren't built for combat at all. Having a totem would probably help too, give your pack some spiritual weight to throw around, even when your pack isn't doing things. But if your hisil is just overrun and you want to change it you're going to have to do more, especially if you want to make it safer. Though, again,unintended consequences, I could see this place spawning a new fascist movement. Why are there so many criminals, anyways? Are there opportunities for regular jobs?<br /> <br /> It's not a Wound, is it?<br /> <br /> It's worth noting it's not all abstracts. If there's stores and businesses, parks and cars or other notable things they would be representative in the Hisil as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T09:53:15-07:00","id":902113,"title":"","content":"The Hisil is an ecosystem, I've had Ithaeur characters use the Science and Animal Ken skills to better discern how to influence it. The thing you have to do is first deal with the general aura of disregard around the neighborhood, squash the bystander effect, unite the decent folk under righteousness, make visible manifestations, and eventually you'll get a martyr to ignite the fires of change.<br /> <br /> It'll get messy afterwards. People is going to start taking justice by their own hand, they'll be persecuted, and then you'll have to get more subtle, influencing the outcome of the trials that come. Eventually it'll be too much trouble to pursue profit in that neighborhood.<br /> <br /> A spirit of outrage sounds amazing for such an endeavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:16:13-07:00","id":902827,"title":"","content":"Do the teeth of Uratha inflict lethal damage to spirits or bashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:49:44-07:00","id":902920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=902827#post902827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the teeth of Uratha inflict lethal damage to spirits or bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its does at least Lethal to everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:03:31-07:00","id":902929,"title":"","content":"Can you use Gifts in Kuruth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:04:30-07:00","id":902930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=902920#post902920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its does at least Lethal to everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that confirmed anywhere? I know they count as mystical sources of damage (so it does lethal to vampires who only have a blanket 'physical' protection), but Spirits downgrade all damage from physical sources to Bashing. Does it not count as a physical source because it's mystical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:56:12-07:00","id":902954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=902930#post902930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that confirmed anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sidebar in the book, The gifts that you can use while in Kuruth are used reflexively and without any expenditure of essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T01:53:59-07:00","id":903339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=902930#post902930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that confirmed anywhere? I know they count as mystical sources of damage (so it does lethal to vampires who only have a blanket 'physical' protection), but Spirits downgrade all damage from physical sources to Bashing. Does it not count as a physical source because it's mystical?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought spirits lacked internal organs would mean that they take bashing even from mystical sources depending on what the effect precisely is. I can understand how the sidebar works on spirits since its the resonance of Father Wolf... but I also figured that if you were playing, oh say Mage, and threw a fireball at a spirit it would still do bashing even if it was powerful enough to do lethal.<br /> <br /> I'd like to repeat my ask from earlier about whether werewolves can get essence from spirits when they eat them? I don't recall getting an answer for that, can't find one at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T03:05:15-07:00","id":903365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=903339#post903339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to repeat my ask from earlier about whether werewolves can get essence from spirits when they eat them? I don't recall getting an answer for that, can't find one at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>p.100, second dot point under 'Essence'. Short version - no, unless covered by the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-30-2016, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T03:45:01-07:00","id":903378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=903339#post903339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought spirits lacked internal organs would mean that they take bashing even from mystical sources depending on what the effect precisely is. I can understand how the sidebar works on spirits since its the resonance of Father Wolf... but I also figured that if you were playing, oh say Mage, and threw a fireball at a spirit it would still do bashing even if it was powerful enough to do lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits do lack internal organs but corpus is considerably less substancial than meat. This is to say, if you chew off a piece of a spirit, it has usually little recourse than to wait until it is whole again. That's because it's ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:01:24-07:00","id":904024,"title":"","content":"I was hoping The Pack would answer this, but it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Can other supernaturals that are part of a pack (Vampires, Beasts, etc) purchase Totem dots? If so, can they purchase up to 5, like Uratha? Or are they limited to the amount Wolf-Blooded can purchase? Or Humans?<br /> <br /> What if they were wolf-blooded before they changed into something stranger? Does that impact the equation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:41:35-07:00","id":904056,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they're considered wolf-blooded for this purpose specifically because they might actually be a former wolf-blooded, so they need at least that level of totem otherwise it gets weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":".  typo 05-31-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:33:36-07:00","id":904179,"title":"","content":"<b>All Uratha see clearly spirits in twilight or it should activate something? Spirits are turning the person to Claimed they can be seen in the twilight?<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Since I've never find anything about buying &quot;merit: loci&quot; to begin the game I assume that the locus you start in the territory is purely narrative decided by the players in the territory creation or the gm. For me that was a big problem because its really strange that you are not given any criterion to have a loci to start your game since they are clearly an advantage and needed such as the totem. (Any information about starter locus?)<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b><br /> <br /> Ignoring all spirits and narratives results: <br /> <b>What are the rules for consuming essence in the loci? You can consume their essence until your essence pool is full? Could not find any dicepool for that too.<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:03:06-07:00","id":904206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=904179#post904179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All Uratha see clearly spirits in twilight or it should activate something? Spirits are turning the person to Claimed they can be seen in the twilight?<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>P95, 'The werewolf does not need to focus in order to sense spirits in Twilight. Unless the spirit is intentionally trying to hide, Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested.' A Claimed doesn't have a Twilight presence unless it had a power that gave itself one. Either the spirit is Influencing the target, or it has Possessed or Claimed them, in which case you wouldn't see them. If a Claimed had an ability to go Twilight, I'd suggest you'd see it providing it was a spirit-claimed and not a ghost or something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Since I've never find anything about buying &quot;merit: loci&quot; to begin the game I assume that the locus you start in the territory is purely narrative decided by the players in the territory creation or the gm. For me that was a big problem because its really strange that you are not given any criterion to have a loci to start your game since they are clearly an advantage and needed such as the totem. (Any information about starter locus?)<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b> </div> </div> </div>P106, 'Dedicated Locus' Merit. Aside from that they are part of the setting and the Storyteller's domain. It's also worth noting that upon gaining a totem the pack is considered Resonant to that totem, and a lot of the things they do are likely to shed Essence to it. Totems don't struggle with Essence the way normal spirits might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ignoring all spirits and narratives results:<br /> <b>What are the rules for consuming essence in the loci? You can consume their essence until your essence pool is full? Could not find any dicepool for that too.<br /> <i>Answer:</i></b> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there's no dicepool and you take as much as you need. If you have a way to quickly vent off Essence you can use it to drain loci dry. As far as I can tell they tried to get rid of useless dice rolls like that, since if you didn't get however much you needed, you could just do it again and it's the kind of thing you would most likely not do under pressure like in the middle of a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/ava