div class=\"message\">I see there are very specific ways of dealing with spirits who have passed to the physical realm.<br /> If the player knows all the ways described in the books how can I come with creative new ways for the players?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what banes and bans are for. They're generally hard to figure out, though there's a Moon Gift that can let one auspice find them, it's not a guarantee. Even then, knowing the ban or bane is a lot different from being able to use it, 'a weapon smeared in the blood of a virgin who killed a werewolf' can make for an awkward scavenger hunt. Spirits tend to have high Defense too, as well as being capable of things like flight that can make it harder for a group of werewolves to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:20:15-07:00","id":905657,"title":"","content":"Is there a version of scar- or tattoo-fetishes in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:49:10-07:00","id":905725,"title":"","content":"In many ways, that's what Gifts are now. <br /> <br /> But no, I don't recall any mention of embedding spirits in your own flesh. It's probably a bad idea anyway, tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:30:00-07:00","id":905752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=905725#post905725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's probably a bad idea anyway, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it would be so entertaining to watch characters figure that out for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:01:17-07:00","id":905775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=905657#post905657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a version of scar- or tattoo-fetishes in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing explicitly stating they are or not in the setting, I generally use them for the 3 facet modification fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:06:48-07:00","id":906357,"title":"","content":"On Pack Tactics... each Theme give a +2... or a flat +2 if all the themes are incorporated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:54:45-07:00","id":906962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=906357#post906357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Pack Tactics... each Theme give a +2... or a flat +2 if all the themes are incorporated?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an excellent and interesting question.<br /> <br /> The new Pack Tactics system went through *a lot* of iterations. The earliest didn't look anything like what we ended up with. (They looked more like 1st edition's tactics system.)<br /> <br /> In an earlier iteration of the Pack Tactics system than the one that ended up being published, Tactics had a lot fewer themes (maybe one or two per Tactic), and if you incorporated them you got the +2.<br /> <br /> In a later version, I added more themes per Tactic, and gave +1 for each, but you subtracted the dot rating of the Tactic from the dice roll. The idea being that higher rated Tactics are more difficult to use, but if you can make conditions favorable for the pack you could overcome the penalty and even turn it into a bonus.<br /> <br /> Stew and I went back and forth fine tuning Pack Tactics, so some elements of earlier versions slipped through to publication. (Like the paragraph saying humans and Wolf-Blooded can use Tactics, then later saying they were restricted to Uratha.)<br /> <br /> So, by RAW, the primary actor's dice pool is Attribute + Skill +2 (if you incorporate all the Themes) + Secondary actor successes. (Attribute + Skill for secondary actors.)<br /> <br /> By the errata that I've sent to Stew (that he's said he'll include) the dice pool for the primary actor should be Attribute + Skill - Tactic Dot Rating + 1/Theme + Secondary actor successes. (Attribute + Skill - Tactic Dot rating for secondary actors.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully that's helped clear it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:19:05-07:00","id":906968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=906962#post906962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stew and I went back and forth fine tuning Pack Tactics, so some elements of earlier versions slipped through to publication. (Like the paragraph saying humans and Wolf-Blooded can use Tactics, then later saying they were restricted to Uratha.)<br /> <br /> So, by RAW, the primary actor's dice pool is Attribute + Skill +2 (if you incorporate all the Themes) + Secondary actor successes. (Attribute + Skill for secondary actors.)<br /> <br /> By the errata that I've sent to Stew (that he's said he'll include) the dice pool for the primary actor should be Attribute + Skill - Tactic Dot Rating + 1/Theme + Secondary actor successes. (Attribute + Skill - Tactic Dot rating for secondary actors.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully that's helped clear it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderfull, thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","