g","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:10:32-07:00","id":910797,"title":"","content":"I meant there is no more Damage that Indicates the number of bonus dice added. Now is if the damage is 2 and you got any sucess you got the number of sucess plus 2 damage. <br /> And the\b\u0002\u0010 Armor no longer subtract the number of dices from the enemie attack now it subtracts the amount of damage/sucess he had. Is that right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:22:09-07:00","id":910813,"title":"","content":"Oh, Yeah, that's right.<br /> <br /> It basically works in two stages now. Attributes, skills and specialities matter before the dice roll. Weapons and armour matter after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:08:14-07:00","id":920394,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, just finished reading <b>The Pack</b> and there are a lot of spiritual goodies in there that could make some interesting plot hooks. Figured I'd ask opinions on them here, since some of the implications aren't totally clear to me.<br /> <br /> 1) Totems probably shouldn't teach Gifts because it runs the risk of disrupting the totem bond, but if they <i>do </i>teach Gifts they can always sense the general distance and direction of the individual they have marked. Is this something exclusive to the unique nature of Totems or is this true of all Spirits? Because if it's true of all Spirits you had better be careful about declaring <i>Siskur-Dah </i>to force a Spirit to teach you a Gift.<br /> <br /> 2) Totems are protected from Essence Bleed by their bond with a pack and regain Essence by hanging around their pack. If I'm understanding this correctly, a Totem is always Resonant with their pack, and the totem bond acts sort of like the Familiar Condition from Mage 2E but supported across multiple people enabling it to sustain a larger Spirit. Uratha can also smell or otherwise sense this pack bond on a totem, which makes them tend to give the spirit a pass for being on the wrong side of the Gauntlet. Could a Mage with Active Mage Sight attuned to Spirit also be able to sense the totem bond?<br /> <br /> 3) How far can you push a Totem Spirit's Influences? Could you, conceivably, give them Influences normally reserved for Rank 6+ if you're willing to pump the Experiences into it?<br /> <br /> 4) If an Idigam used Forge Fleshbound Spirit on a Totem, would that sever the totem bond, or would the pack now have a slightly more powerful patron? Would the Totem still regain Essence from the bond, or would it still need to feed exclusively on living flesh?<br /> <br /> 5) The Magnanimous Totem Merit indicates that because this Spirit is more accepting, it expects more attention, and now packmates need to offer chiminage/<i>gathra</i> for a number of hours a week equal to their dots in the Totem Merit. What form of <i>gathra</i> would you consider acceptable? Would it just involve praying to/paying homage to the Totem for up to five hours a week? Slip a prayer here, a minor sacrifice there, until it all adds up?<br /> <br /> 6) How does a large pack go from being just a large pack to being a Lodge? What metaphysical/spiritual changes need to be wrought to change a Pack Totem to a Lodge Totem? Because, in my view, a Lodge Totem of equal Rank to a Pack Totem has significantly more spiritual heft. This makes sense, but I'm wondering how that shift occurs. Do packmates who contributed dots of the Totem Merit to the Pack Totem before it became a Lodge Totem get those Merit dots restored?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T12:36:36-07:00","id":920505,"title":"","content":"How exactly do Totems exist in the material realm, can they only manifest in certain places (do not factor in a ban or Bane) or can they freely move about the Physical realm and the Shadow. Do they have to expend essence to do so or not? Totems have always confused me even when I read the rules for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T12:44:00-07:00","id":920507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=920505#post920505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly do Totems exist in the material realm, can they only manifest in certain places (do not factor in a ban or Bane) or can they freely move about the Physical realm and the Shadow. Do they have to expend essence to do so or not? Totems have always confused me even when I read the rules for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A pack totem treats every member of its pack as Resonant, which affords it a great deal of added sustainability and mobility but does not allow it to wander about the material realm with impunity without using Manifestations like any other spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T12:48:57-07:00","id":920509,"title":"","content":"Like Satchel said, they need Manifestations, and only get Twilight Form for free. But being a member of a pack sort of staunches the Essence bleed for acting within the gurihal, and while they still have to pay the 1 Essence per day to stay active, they don't have to pay more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T12:56:16-07:00","id":920514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=920507#post920507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A pack totem treats every member of its pack as Resonant, which affords it a great deal of added sustainability and mobility but does not allow it to wander about the material realm with impunity without using Manifestations like any other spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks, I just needed to know for a upcoming requiem game I am doing Saturday where a pack of Predator Kings attack and I need the Totem to get involved with the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:33:23-07:00","id":920530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=920394#post920394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Totems probably shouldn't teach Gifts because it runs the risk of disrupting the totem bond, but if they do teach Gifts they can always sense the general distance and direction of the individual they have marked. Is this something exclusive to the unique nature of Totems or is this true of all Spirits? Because if it's true of all Spirits you had better be careful about declaring Siskur-Dah to force a Spirit to teach you a Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is just a totem thing, perhaps due to their already-close link to Uratha. But I wouldn't be adverse to having some spirits have access to a similar ability. The thing with the Siskur-Dah is that, like most rituals, providing you're going by the rules and playing fair, it's an accepted part of the spirit world rules. A spirit might resent being on the losing end of the hunt, but they don't seem like they would hold a grudge afterwards for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a Mage with Active Mage Sight attuned to Spirit also be able to sense the totem bond? </div> </div> </div>Probably. They might not know what it meant without focused sight or prior experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) How far can you push a Totem Spirit's Influences? Could you, conceivably, give them Influences normally reserved for Rank 6+ if you're willing to pump the Experiences into it? </div> </div> </div>I think that just means a Rank 3 totem can have 3 dots of Influence: Fire and 3 dots of Influence: Passion.<br /> <br /> From the core book, p186, 'Although a spirit's Rank is also the Maximum rating for an Influence, a spirit can split its dots to have more than one Influence...Spirits may reduce their number of Numina granted by Rank to increase Influence dots at a cost of one Numen per dot.'<br /> <br /> As you can see on p64 in The Pack, you can purchase additional Numina and Influences for the totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) If an Idigam used Forge Fleshbound Spirit on a Totem, would that sever the totem bond, or would the pack now have a slightly more powerful patron? Would the Totem still regain Essence from the bond, or would it still need to feed exclusively on living flesh? </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind it's also a lot more vulnerable, as it can now be killed and probably won't come back. It lacks the ability to shift into Twilight as well.<br /> <br /> I'd say the totem's protection from essence bleed keeps them from the double Essence-bleed effect of the ability but I could see Storytellers deciding that it would now bleed 'normally.'<br /> <br /> It's really in the werewolf's best interest to bring it back. Grabbing onto it and Reaching shouldn't be too hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What form of gathra would you consider acceptable? Would it just involve praying to/paying homage to the Totem for up to five hours a week? Slip a prayer here, a minor sacrifice there, until it all adds up? </div> </div> </div>The form is going to depend on the individual spirit. Odds are it is going to require a specific act, more than simple prayer unless it's something associated with prayer. You might look at the core book for it, p182 'a change to the material world that will produce a small amount of Essence are the bare minimum.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What metaphysical/spiritual changes need to be wrought to change a Pack Totem to a Lodge Totem? </div> </div> </div>Arguably the spirits' ambition has a lot to do with it. Pack totems are a member of the pack. They do get benefits from it, but they're just one of the pack, even if they may be a revered one. Lodge totems are the bosses. They are not part of the lodge like everyone else, they are at the top of it. Lodge members are called <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/adherent\" target=\"_blank\">adherents</a> for a reason, and dedicate their Siskur-Dah, and often the rest of their lives, to the lodge totem.<br /> <br /> A pack totem is like an alien in your group of friends. A lodge totem is like a cult leader in a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T03:25:46-07:00","id":920896,"title":"","content":"Depeding on the spirit and his &quot;powers&quot;, he can cross the gauntlet anywhere?<br /> The loci area usually is full with spirits with the same resonance? They treat uratha like invaders?<br /> In a meeting of protectorate if someone enter kuruth this will activate wasu-im for everybody?<br /> rank 3 spirits are already bizarre enough, how can I differentiate these from a Magath?<br /> <br /> One last question: I'm in trouble in the shadow. I want to kill a spirit and I know he will ressurrect later in some place that resonates his type, so whats the point on combat in that case if the cicle will never end? (I know there is ways to end his essence and corpus at the same time but It isnt too much specific?) Siskur-dah can help in something?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-25-2016, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T03:47:29-07:00","id":920899,"title":"","content":"Spirits lose essence if they take aggravated damage. Get their bane into play and they can die permanently pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T04:43:18-07:00","id":920908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=920899#post920899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits lose essence if they take aggravated damage. Get their bane into play and they can die permanently pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you do that the spirit Umia will be less friendly to Uratha right? In terms of gaming how can I aproach that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T06:19:41-07:00","id":920931,"title":"","content":"The umia isn't going to take you murdering one of them lightly no matter how you do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T09:40:03-07:00","id":920995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=920896#post920896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depeding on the spirit and his &quot;powers&quot;, he can cross the gauntlet anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. There are powers that would let them cross anywhere. We're trying to get an answer out of the writers as to whether a locus allows spirits to cross over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The loci area usually is full with spirits with the same resonance? They treat uratha like invaders? </div> </div> </div>It depends on everyone involved. If the spirits are a bunch of Rank 1 and 2, they'll probably scatter if a high Ranked werewolf saunters by, but might swarm if it's a pack of werewolves with barely a glimmer of Renown. If the werewolves are on good terms and respectful to the spirits, for instance using the Supplication rite, they might just make way for them, even if they were more powerful. If the territory is properly claimed and the werewolves are on good terms with them, things are likely to go better. Otherwise it's easy to imagine spirits fending werewolves away from a locus. The spirit-side, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a meeting of protectorate if someone enter kuruth this will activate wasu-im for everybody? </div> </div> </div>Yes. This is why protectorates do not have a capitol building where every werewolf who's part of it will be tightly confined. There's a wide variety of methods to avoid or resist kuruth. I imagine when a lot of protectorates have meetings, it will be in glades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> rank 3 spirits are already bizarre enough, how can I differentiate these from a Magath? </div> </div> </div>Pick two resonances that aren't connected. Give it the attitude of a spirit that has been exiled and exists alone, hated by all other spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One last question: I'm in trouble in the shadow. I want to kill a spirit and I know he will ressurrect later in some place that resonates his type, so whats the point on combat in that case if the cicle will never end? (I know there is ways to end his essence and corpus at the same time but It isnt too much specific?) Siskur-dah can help in something? </div> </div> </div>Elfive got the main thrust. Alternatively you can eliminate nearby sources of resonance. It won't work for all spirits but it might work for some. Or you could use Shadowbind and lock the spirit away somewhere, or Fetish and bind it to an object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-25-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:01:57-07:00","id":921039,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>! changing the subject just a little:<br /> Is common knowledge that everything has a spirit, right? (Except humans) With that in mind, it can be understandable that every single spoon in my kitchen has a spirit reflection. (Sleeping spirits &quot;faded, weak, nothing more than a transparent spoon, subsisting as a fruit for other spirits that feed on this)<br /> Now imagine that I'am a law professor and I have a justice statue in the size of a cup. I always bring this little marble statue with me because my father gave me and I always tell the stories of my father with this statue for students but no1 really cares.<br /> Meanwhile in the hisil, this statue has its own reflection? If it were a sleeping spirit momentarily he appeared on the teacher's desk in college because of the teachers routine? And when the professor goes home and left him on the nightstand the sleeping spirit would be there in the hisil as a normal statue reflection?<br /> Or spirits &quot;insignificant&quot; as these doesnt have a reflection yet?<br /> <br /> When narrating the interior of a home in the spiritual realm is a little tricky to understand what really reflects so things are exactly as they are? If so what happens to objects that move in the material realm? Cars, bags, phones, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-25-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:22:30-07:00","id":921118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=921039#post921039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile in the hisil, this statue has its own reflection? If it were a sleeping spirit momentarily he appeared on the teacher's desk in college because of the teachers routine? And when the professor goes home and left him on the nightstand the sleeping spirit would be there in the hisil as a normal statue reflection?<br /> Or spirits &quot;insignificant&quot; as these doesnt have a reflection yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably one of the more significant spirit reflections in their house, considering the thought and care that goes into it, but yes it would move. How often do you really think about the spoon you mentioned? You probably can't tell it from any other spoon in your house, if it fell behind a counter you might never even notice. But this thing is carried with the professor every day. The spirit would probably feast on memory spirits, going dormant or just slinking along when the professor moves it. It would depend more about the statue and stories told, the emotion involved that would spawn the spirit in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When narrating the interior of a home in the spiritual realm is a little tricky to understand what really reflects so things are exactly as they are? If so what happens to objects that move in the material realm? Cars, bags, phones, etc. </div> </div> </div>While it's easy to imagine a Disney scenario where every item has some animated feature that runs around singing its virtues, it's important to remember that things aren't inherently friendly there, they're predatory. Odds are most of the silverware has been fed upon by Kitchen and Gluttony spirits to the point that they would need to be awakened or something. A lot is going to depend on the situation. In a bachelor pad maybe only the tv and the bed are really active, everything else being drowned out by spirits of loneliness. In a family house it might appear as a chaotic whirling storm of objects flying around as trinkets and toys are constantly moved, with a stable 'eye' in the family room and a dark presence in one of the bedrooms. The Hisil is an opportunity to show, not tell. In a house you can imply what is important to the occupants by having it be a centerpiece.<br /> <br /> But even in a 'stable' home, the Hisil isn't a perfect reflection. Everything is going to be slightly off, tainted by the resonance it collects. A phone used for phone sex might appear phallic, beaded with sweat and emit heavy breathing sounds when you listen to the receiver, or the voice of an old flame. A kitchen might seem to have an inordinate amount of knives, beckoning you to use them, and blood across the floor, as it's where the previous owner slashed their family to death. A television emits a constant stream of hypnotic sounds and sights, and if you just look at it a minute you can find yourself trapped on the couch, staring into it for hours and days as it feeds off your mindless attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T14:04:17-07:00","id":921146,"title":"","content":"The best analogy I've ever read of the shadow is that it's like a drawing done from memory. Things that stand out, things that are important to the artist, are going to be more defined and things that are subtle or unimportant will be less detailed, or forgotten alltogether. The way the artist feels about the things he's drawing often has more impact on how the drawing turns out than what those things are actually like. And, it's a self-reenforcing process as the artist draws and re-draws the same picture from memory over and over again. The things he remembers better, he draws more consistently, and every time he draws them they stick in his memory more and become easier to keep drawing consistently. The things he forgets to draw get harder and harder to remember. Then keep in mind that it's not just one artist, but a collaboration between everyone and everything in the space, putting it together from the collective influence of all of their memories. Some of the collaborators are probably more abstract or impressionistic artists, so some things will be more symbolic than literal representations, and those differences will be further compounded by the constant reproduction-from-memory.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if this actually answers your questions at all, but it's how I think about spirits working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-25-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T04:16:25-07:00","id":921426,"title":"","content":"You both gave me interesting ways to understand the Hisil. The lack of artistic work in relation to the spiritual world always left me quite puzzled in how it can be absurd and alive.Or how little things that move can actually move.<br /> It is strange and alien enough making it very hard to understand. It is more dificult in the sense that: Everything you put you have create a literal visual explanation of the elements in play. Therefore it is extremely difficult to improvise locations or think quickly without thinking of the reflection in the material world.<br /> I've read and re-read the first edition and the second related to the spiritual world. But the lack of direction still leaves me completely lost.<br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> said <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=921118#post921118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably one of the more significant spirit reflections in their house, considering the thought and care that goes into it, but yes it would move..</div> </div> </div> </div>So when i'm in the Hisil at the same time the spirit goes to the collage. I can see the statue floating around on street? If this is possible then it is valid for all the smaller items that people carry with themselves.<br /> In that case the spiritual world is a world with so much information that it becomes overwhelming and inconceivable for its strangeness.<br /> Or the hisil is a pure and modified reflection of everything that is happening in <i><b>real time </b></i>in the physical world. (Except for places that happen memorable and different things)<br /> I think that the spiritual world in the things that really matter are all well explained in the book, but it does not have any explanation for these details so simple. If a player wants to search for a cell spirit in the spiritual world, he just complicated my life haha.<br /> What would I do: Should I say &quot;Oh people cross this street all the time. You see cellphones floating around like flies going to their destinations.&quot;<br /> Or should I say: 'You cant see the phones on the streets like its a easy thing to remember, but you know where is a phone store'<br /> \u200b<br /> I believe that a way to train the imagination to HiSil has been imagining places on my routine in the other side.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> You both can easlly capture your own house in the hisil?<br /> Sorry for so many questions, but I think I'm the only one snowflake that has such difficulty with this part of the scenario. (And strangely it is my favorite part)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-26-2016, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:52:55-07:00","id":921527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=921426#post921426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when i'm in the Hisil at the same time the spirit goes to the collage. I can see the statue floating around on street? If this is possible then it is valid for all the smaller items that people carry with themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might see the spirit pass by, not necessarily the statue. The spirit reflection doesn't have to look like the object it's derived from. It might be a spirit of 'memory' in which case it might only linger around the statue long enough to get to school and leave it to go to study hall. If this is the case, the spirit might just stay at the university, and wait for the statue to come to it for a snack while it travels among students studying and devours their memory.<br /> <br /> For smaller items, there's not likely to be a reflection, or much of one. They're inconsequential. A t-shirt spirit has the same problem as your spoon spirit, it's been gobbled up by bigger things, if it even managed to form a spirit in the first place. The fact that these things move makes them even more likely to get eaten up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the hisil is a pure and modified reflection of everything that is happening in <i><b>real time </b></i>in the physical world. (Except for places that happen memorable and different things)<br /> I think that the spiritual world in the things that really matter are all well explained in the book, but it does not have any explanation for these details so simple. If a player wants to search for a cell spirit in the spiritual world, he just complicated my life haha.<br /> What would I do: Should I say &quot;Oh people cross this street all the time. You see cellphones floating around like flies going to their destinations.&quot;<br /> Or should I say: 'You cant see the phones on the streets like its a easy thing to remember, but you know where is a phone store' </div> </div> </div>'These objects haven't been momentous enough to create a spirit reflection, or if they had, it's been devoured by something bigger.' In your previous description the statue seemed like a very special object. For most people their phones and t-shirts and so forth are easily replaced and don't concern much thought.<br /> <br /> Even if they've awakened, cell phone spirits are probably absorbed by larger communication spirits, or electronic spirits, or distraction spirits. While your phone might mean something to you, every day for the past 40 years thousands of people have been driving by those phone lines on the road outside that stretch across the city. Objects on the move are less likely to generate spirits. <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a> gets into this. Basically, very basically as there's more to it, Noun in the real world creates Noun-Resonant Essence in the spirit. For some things, it's an inconsequentially small amount of Essence, that spoon doesn't matter to you, to your family, not to anyone else in the world, there's no animals seeing it, it's just part of a larger group of things. But if it is special, like the statue, once enough Essence gathers, a muthra develops, a Rank 0 spirit. You should be able to see the problem already. If you're moving Noun around, Noun-Resonant Essence isn't gathering in one place, instead it's being dragged around where anyone can eat said Essence, so nothing can really coalesce. There's already more powerful spirits in your house, getting one of a dozen of the same shirts at the store and putting it 'with the others' isn't going to make enough of an impact to really help that spirit form, or keep that dormant spirit from being eaten if it already did.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> You both can easlly capture your own house in the hisil?<br /> Sorry for so many questions, but I think I'm the only one snowflake that has such difficulty with this part of the scenario. (And strangely it is my favorite part) </div> </div> </div>It's no problem, its one of my favorite parts of the game and the information is scattered across a couple books.<br /> <br /> Chaos and ruin and rampant nature spirits all around it. The previous owners didn't keep the house up very well and eventually filed for bankruptcy. Now it's the home of a family with a child, which is often a chaotic thing. I can probably tell you the most significant objects in each room, and which rooms aren't significant enough to have a reflection, many of the closets for instance. We always use the side door so the front door on the house in the Hisil might just be the image of a door, or not exist at all. This room I'm in would probably be the most active or spiritually significant. The tv is probably bigger in the hisil due to the focus placed on it, the desk I'm at might be its own little tesseract. The room would probably look similar, but mostly sun lit through the skylights, as we keep moving the lights around from different rooms. The skylights might be bigger, as they let in the brightest light and we tend to nap in the sunbeams. Toy spirits would probably wander from room to room, scrounging up little entertainment Essence, cannibalizing each other, and trying to avoid being eaten by the television.<br /> <br /> There's a good example. My kid has toys, we move them from room to room while playing or putting them away. The 'entertainment' Essence they develop is probably weak, and some of the special ones probably develop more direct 'toy' spirits. But they might get eaten up by others, empowered by the fact that they're the favorite toy of the moment. When he's not playing with them, they're not really generating much Essence. So they go dormant and get eaten up by something larger, or just become forgotten. Alternatively, maybe they go scouting around for more Essence, things related to toys like entertainment, but they risk being devoured by the television in here, which likely harbors a more powerful spirit, as we use it for Netflix, movies and video games, it being the only tv in the house.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The 'gravity' of Helios, from Werewolf the Forsaken p73, is a new factor added in second edition and probably keeps a lot of spirits that might otherwise be created or active during the daytime from existing, or keeps them dormant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:20:32-07:00","id":921546,"title":"","content":"You mean, describe what my house would look like in the Hisil? Haha... Not a pleasent place, to be honest. The house itself would be a scarred, dilapidated warden of the countless clutter spirits within. It hoards Essence, giving them just enough to keep them from leaving, but little enough to insure none are powerful enough to challenge it. <br /> <br /> The clutter spirits are lathsome, skittering things that crawl over everything, concealing anything one of the human essence batteries on the other side of the gauntlet are looking for, lest their attentions feed it essence that could be theirs. There are two or three larger clutter spirits that have grown by cannibalizing smaller, weaker ones, which have made them more resilient to the humans' constant efforts to shift the resonance within the house by cleaning on the Flesh side. They command the lesser members of their miniature courts to scuttle underfoot at inoportune times. The walls are are lined with shelves, packed with spirits of books and knowledge, though most of them have gone dormant. Drawers upon drawers are stuffed with spirits of creativity and art, although many are tainted with clutter resonance and may soon become magath if they haven't already.<br /> <br /> One of the rooms in the house is a complete spiritual dead zone, where starved spirits (especially clutter spirits) go to slip into dormancy. The room itself has no clearly defined shape or size in the Hisil, just a nebulous void of a sprit graveyard.<br /> <br /> The bed is a power unto itself in this spirtual ecosystem, largely stationary, but grown enormous feeding on essence of lethargy and sex. Some clutter spirits take refuge beneath it, in hopes of escaping the tyranny of the larger of their kind and stealing any essence the bed spirit doesn't immediately devour.<br /> <br /> The television lords over the entertainment center, demanding a tithe from any of the various spirits of technology and entertainment that reside there, in exchange for access to a steady and regular stream of essence that flows to that area every day. The chords and wires have taken on a life of their own, like a slithering, tentacled beast, its long and tangled tendrils touching everything in the area, and sliding in and out of outlets on a whim. Next to this small kingdom is an oasis of positive essence, a terrarium housing the young spirit of a leopard geko, lovingly tended by the humans on the flesh side. The tank itself is permitted to stay there by the graces of the spirit of power chords just nearby, and the geko spirit is developing a diplomatic relationship with the television spirit.<br /> <br /> (By the way, I am aware that a great deal of this discription makes my house sound pretty depressing, but it's really not. Chalk it up to the nature of CofD as a horror game, I think just about any place described with everything personified and defined by hunger would end up sounding pretty unpleasent.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-26-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:25:17-07:00","id":921620,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> These explanations will help me a lot. I will try to practice creating places posting on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow\">Grab-bag of Shadow Thread</a>.<br /> My biggest fear is to play the game the wrong way. (I know that each group plays their ways) But I'd rather stick to the default concepts of the game. So for me its top priority to understand how things work in the most basic way first. I will practice writing some Spiritual Places there. Thanks to you both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:13:03-07:00","id":922213,"title":"","content":"Ok I may just be being dumb here but I cannot find any information in the 2nd edition book explaining what protectorates are. What are they and how exactly do they work? And if you could let me know where Protectorates are in the books I would be much obliged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:17:27-07:00","id":922215,"title":"","content":"Protectorates are briefly described on p66, under 'Packs and Protectorates.' There's a sample one in the Bristol Hunting Ground that starts on p255.<br /> <br /> They are more fleshed out in the supplement, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/181760/The-Pack\" target=\"_blank\">The Pack</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:50:52-07:00","id":923915,"title":"","content":"Can you pick shadow gifts in any order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:00:14-07:00","id":923920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xizzicks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=923915#post923915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you pick shadow gifts in any order?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean Facets of Shadow Gifts? They don't really have an order, they're associated with Renown. You can buy any Facet of any Gift that you have unlocked, as long as you have at least one dot the associated Renown. You also get one free Facet every time you increase your Renown, which must be associated with the same Renown and come from a Gift you have unlocked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:02:53-07:00","id":923968,"title":"","content":"Yeah, only Moon Gifts have an order to go into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:49:16-07:00","id":924653,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:07:44-07:00","id":930342,"title":"","content":"An easy way to understand how the new lunacy system works? <br /> I'm so used to the 1e so is even harder to memorize.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:22:19-07:00","id":930350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=930342#post930342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An easy way to understand how the new lunacy system works?<br /> I'm so used to the 1e so is even harder to memorize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roll Resolve + Composure as with other Integrity breaking points. Anything but exceptional success renders the character's memory of the scene hazy, indistinct, or unreliable. Success applies the normal Conditions for a successful breaking point roll, and penalizes all actions for the rest of the scene by two dice. Failure removes a dot of Integrity as normal for failed breaking points and applies a Lunacy Condition. Dramatic failure makes the character wolf-blooded. Being in the presence of a group adds dice to the roll based on the size of the group, while other factors like what form the witnessed werewolf is in and how powerful they are subtract dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:31:35-07:00","id":930354,"title":"","content":"Mortals suffer Breaking Points for witnessing the supernatural.<br /> <br /> If they suffer a Breaking Point for witnessing a supernatural werewolf, they're afflicted by Lunacy, which is a supernaturally-enhanced primal fear.<br /> <br /> They roll the usual roll, with modifiers depending on the situation. Dramatic Failure, they're a wolf-blooded and forget. Failure, one of three Conditions is a Lunacy Condition instead of a normal Breaking Point Condition, and they forget and lose a point of Integrity. Success, they suffer a regular Breaking Point Condition, try to rationalize it, and suffer a -2 penalty for the scene. Exceptional Success you remember everything and regain all Willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:13:06-07:00","id":930816,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys.<br /> The denver setting in 1e fits well enough to incorporate in the 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:39:10-07:00","id":930870,"title":"","content":"You mean the Rockies? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:12:21-07:00","id":934793,"title":"","content":"Couple questions. In The Pack, The 5th dot of the Garmir fighting style reads:&quot;The Garmir may use Jaws of Garm when dealing damage in a grapple to prey that has already taken at least 1 point of aggravated damage. The Garmir spends 1 point of Essence and adds half the prey\u2019s Primal Urge to the damage she deals that turn.&quot; Anyone have any official indication on whether that should be rounded up or down? What are your thoughts?<br /> <br /> Second, what is the landscape of the Shadow made up of? Hardened ephemera (oxymoron)? Like what is the earth in the Shadow made of, is it the spirit of the earth? What about the ocean? What happens if you burrow through the earth or go walking on the floor of the ocean? Is there even an ocean? Do fish spirits just swim around where the ocean would be in the Shadow? What are the features of these environments? Would you even have to swim, or hold your breath? How closely does it mimic it's real life counterpart?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:22:15-07:00","id":934900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=934793#post934793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, what is the landscape of the Shadow made up of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every natural part of the Shadow is a spirit or the stuff that becomes one. The place isn't considered generally crowded for nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hardened ephemera (oxymoron)? </div> </div> </div>In what sense could this possibly be an oxymoron, given that you're talking about a dimension where everything is made of ephemera and the state of reality in which ephemera is intangible does not exist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like what is the earth in the Shadow made of, is it the spirit of the earth? What about the ocean? </div> </div> </div>Varying quantities of elemental motes or chunks of a location spirit or Gaia or the outer skin of some bound or slumbering terrorbeast or take your pick, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens if you burrow through the earth or go walking on the floor of the ocean? </div> </div> </div>Possibly nothing. Possibly you've trespassed in a spirit's domain. Possibly you've woken something up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there even an ocean? </div> </div> </div>Mother Ocean is spoken of with similar hushed tones and dread as Mother Luna. The sea is narratively, mechanically, metaphysically, and politically one of the most potent symbols that exists. There is absolutely an ocean in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do fish spirits just swim around where the ocean would be in the Shadow? </div> </div> </div>Depending on the coastline, maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are the features of these environments? </div> </div> </div>The depths of the ocean and the underground are Mysterious almost as a matter of course. Could be there's a bunch of elemental courts fighting for supremacy. Could be there's a brood of nature spirits messing around with what wildlife spawned them. Could be there's nothing there at all. It's variable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you even have to swim, or hold your breath? </div> </div> </div>You've immersed yourself in the liquid flesh of a being whose nature is broadly known to be pitiless and fickle. I wouldn't put money on the experience being easier than its material counterpart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How closely does it mimic it's real life counterpart? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the chunk of the Shadow you're dealing with, but if the Gauntlet is fairly thin I'd expect a reasonable level of fidelity to Earthly geography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T02:28:48-07:00","id":934968,"title":"","content":"Query: Wolf Senses - Do you gain the bonus dice of Urhan to perception rolls with wolf senses while being in a humanoid form, or it merely allows you the ability to roll for things that Urhan would be allowed to roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T02:49:40-07:00","id":934970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=934793#post934793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple questions. In The Pack, The 5th dot of the Garmir fighting style reads:&quot;The Garmir may use Jaws of Garm when dealing damage in a grapple to prey that has already taken at least 1 point of aggravated damage. The Garmir spends 1 point of Essence and adds half the prey\u2019s Primal Urge to the damage she deals that turn.&quot; Anyone have any official indication on whether that should be rounded up or down? What are your thoughts?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRound up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T03:21:10-07:00","id":934978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=934968#post934968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: Wolf Senses - Do you gain the bonus dice of Urhan to perception rolls with wolf senses while being in a humanoid form, or it merely allows you the ability to roll for things that Urhan would be allowed to roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The perception bonus of each form is for using wolf senses in that form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:46:37-07:00","id":935653,"title":"","content":"It's been asked before on these forums but I wanted clarification: Does Gauru regeneration happen at the start of a 'CofD turn' (i.e. at the top of a global 'turn,' initiative count 99+) or at the start of that player's turn? (i.e. initiative &lt;99+) <br /> <br /> Another way of wording this is: When exactly in a turn do Gauru regeneration and conditions/tilts like Poisoned take place?<br /> <br /> Note that CofD calls a turn what some other systems call rounds. A turn is 3-second period where actions take place in CofD.<br /> <br /> Here's a follow-up question: If Gauru regeneration happens at the top of a turn (basically, initiative 99+ count) and not in the middle of it (after the top of the turn), and a character goes Gauru in the middle of the previous turn... how should that previous Gauru turn be counted? Should it be counted towards total Gauru turns, or just ignored?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:05:21-07:00","id":935658,"title":"","content":"I always ran it as the beginning of your turn. As you noted, CofD does things differently than d20 systems, and I can't think of anything off the top of my head that really activates at Initiative 99+, even environmental damaging Tilts operate on the characters turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:13:57-07:00","id":935663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=935653#post935653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been asked before on these forums but I wanted clarification: Does Gauru regeneration happen at the start of a 'CofD turn' (i.e. at the top of a global 'turn,' initiative count 99+) or at the start of that player's turn? (i.e. initiative &lt;99+)<br /> <br /> Another way of wording this is: When exactly in a turn do Gauru regeneration and conditions/tilts like Poisoned take place?<br /> <br /> Note that CofD calls a turn what some other systems call rounds. A turn is 3-second period where actions take place in CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regeneration happens at the time the character gets to act, delayed action non-withstanding (not that Gauru is usually able to delay them, mind). In fact, the first thing that happens when you go Gauru is that you heal completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:36:09-07:00","id":937299,"title":"","content":"Two-World Eyes. I can't seem to find a reference in 2E that covers peering from one side of the gauntlet to the other. Can anyone help point me in the right direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:03:50-07:00","id":937316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrimsonOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=937299#post937299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two-World Eyes. I can't seem to find a reference in 2E that covers peering from one side of the gauntlet to the other. Can anyone help point me in the right direction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit Senses. Starts on page 94 and continues onto 95.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:18:42-07:00","id":937426,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if there's something (numina, influence, dread power) a spirit or a claimed can do that would make a drug more addicting? Maybe make people more resonant to certain spirits of it's brood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6533-gingerkid88","name":"Gingerkid88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T00:37:17-07:00","id":937506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gingerkid88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=937426#post937426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm wondering if there's something (numina, influence, dread power) a spirit or a claimed can do that would make a drug more addicting? Maybe make people more resonant to certain spirits of it's brood?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Influence (addiction) 1, easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T05:21:28-07:00","id":937555,"title":"","content":"Yeah. And if there wasn't something like that available as a Dread Power, the system for those is meant to allow you to whip up ones you want that are appropriate for whatever monster you're making.<br /> <br /> You could go the Vitae Addiction route for some sort of 'enhanced addiction' of a substance, where if the spirit or claimed has imbued it with the ability anyone who uses it requires a Resolve + Composure roll -1 per dot of Essence spent enhancing it or resist getting the Addicted Condition.<br /> <br /> Arguably the Aggressive Meme Numina could help spread addiction, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:23:54-07:00","id":937663,"title":"","content":"Say a spirit Claims a creature that has supernatural abilities: either merits, or Gifts, or Tells, or whatever. Can the Claimed use the host's supernatural powers?<br /> <br /> I can't see anything in the Claimed Condition that says they can, and since it says &quot;Claimed may use the spirit's Influences, but not Numina or Manifestation Effects. They may develop unique Dread Powers.&quot; I've got a plot wherein a Spirit of Rage has been feeding off of a captured Uratha, but that may end up with the spirit Claiming the Uratha once the PCs threaten to rescue them. Just trying to decide if I want to let the Claimed Uratha keep its Gifts or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:49:39-07:00","id":937680,"title":"","content":"You might take a cue from the Forge Servant ability of the idigam. An Empty Wolf, whose soul has been swapped for a spirit, retains its regeneration, shapeshifting, and senses. It also keeps its Gifts, Facets, and Renown brands, but can no longer gain any new ones. It retains the ability to perform rites, use fetishes and talens, but no longer treats silver as a bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:52:20-07:00","id":937682,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought of that. 'swhat I get for not reading the idigam section as closely as everything else (gotta keep them secret for the big encounters).<br /> <br /> Thanks, nofather!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:53:58-07:00","id":937683,"title":"","content":"No problem, I was going to do that too but their powers are very weird and unique. You could probably wrap an entire story around a herald or hive-claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T04:02:05-07:00","id":938014,"title":"","content":"Aren't uratha normally immune to claiming from regular spirits? Like, that's why it takes an idigam dread power to force it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T04:45:35-07:00","id":938023,"title":"","content":"P32, 'Uratha are not immune to being Claimed, and the greatest fear of any Iminir Rahu is becoming one of the Su\u2019ur.' Being supernatural and aware of spirits they are, of course, more able to resist than the standard mortal.<br /> <br /> In first edition I believe the rules kept them and other supernaturals from being Claimed, but it was brought up as a story hook at least once. In second edition there is no such restriction, any supernatural may be Claimed, or the other types of things like what idigam and strix do.<br /> <br /> The idigam isn't technically Claiming the werewolf with Forge Empty Wolf. It's ripping the werewolf's soul from its body and replacing it with a spirit. A spirit Claiming a werewolf, or anything else, instead sort of merges with and subsumes the existing soul. Though an idigam can likely also do that, taking a spirit or human or other supernatural soul and shoving it into a werewolf without removing said werewolf's soul. Likely one has even gathered the souls of werewolves of four other auspices and tribes and shoved them into the body of a werewolf with the fifth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:39:10-07:00","id":939090,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this is explained somewhere, but how has the first change fluff changed between editions? Are all potential werewolves Wolf-Blooded before the change now? And if so, don't they know something's wrong with them because of their tells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6533-gingerkid88","name":"Gingerkid88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:59:56-07:00","id":939119,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's explicitly stated that all werewolves were wolfblooded before the change, but it seems implied in every reference to the First Change that I can remember.<br /> <br /> And generally yes, a wolfblood does get the sense that there is something different about them. Though I think some Tells are subtle enough that it might not always be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:33:55-07:00","id":939143,"title":"","content":"There is no set minimum of time between one becomes wolf-blooded and then a werewolf. So when Luna chooses you, or you have your Lunacy-induced-Change, it might have taken course over a matter of seconds or minutes.<br /> <br /> Plus while someone experienced in the supernatural might recognize a Tell, they're not something everyone else would, even the Wolf-blooded. Clever Fingers, for instance, don't show any true differences unless you're participating in a Rite. Also, I've known many Fuck Ugly people and never once thought they were going to become a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:39:19-07:00","id":939393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gingerkid88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=939090#post939090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are all potential werewolves Wolf-Blooded before the change now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gingerkid88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=939090#post939090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if so, don't they know something's wrong with them because of their tells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf-blooded know they have Tells. Doesn't mean they automatically know what that means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:49:22-07:00","id":942384,"title":"","content":"I just realized since there's a Pure template and a Forsaken template, werewolves are one of the few major templates that can switch over immediately to another major template.<br /> <br /> If anyone happens to be going to Gencon, would you be kind enough to inform us of werewolfish updates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:35:13-07:00","id":943448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=939393#post939393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that, with the exception of Wolf-Blooded who become so due to Lunacy or Luna's whims, wolf-blooded are born as such, even if their Tells don't always manifest until later in life. Is this not the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T01:50:08-07:00","id":943487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=943448#post943448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that, with the exception of Wolf-Blooded who become so due to Lunacy or Luna's whims, wolf-blooded are born as such, even if their Tells don't always manifest until later in life. Is this not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBunyip was commenting that not all people who become werewolves are Wolf-Blooded, rather than on the origins of Wolf-Blooded <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:38:48-07:00","id":943537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=943448#post943448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that, with the exception of Wolf-Blooded who become so due to Lunacy or Luna's whims, wolf-blooded are born as such, even if their Tells don't always manifest until later in life. Is this not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I was being too flippantly brief in replying.<br /> <br /> Let me be clearer with the reasoning. All werewolves may come from wolf-blooded (lower case, don't have Tells, and don't get a separate mention in the 2nd ed book, because they're glossed over as not really existing, but by definition must), but they definitely don't all come from Wolf-Blooded (the upper case, with the Tells).<br /> <br /> How do we know? Let's look at basic character creation (pp 81-88, not the narrative versions later in the book), and Wolf-Blooded (p. 296+).<br /> <br /> <i>Step One: Concept</i> says 'Express concept as a few words, a short epithet. Think about your character as the protagonist of a novel. How would a reviewer describe your character\u2019s role in the story? Is she the Disgruntled Ex-Cop? Is he the Penitent Thug? Is she the Startup CEO With A Heart of Gold? Keep it simple, but unique enough that your character doesn\u2019t sound like just anyone from off the streets. This should imply some identity, some individuality. Your concept doesn\u2019t need to have anything to do with your character\u2019s identity as Forsaken, though. It can, if that\u2019s core to her very being.'<br /> <br /> No mention of being a Wolf-Blooded. No mention of formative years in a pack. Apparently being a Wolf-Blooded has quite an impact on a character's life.<br /> From p. 296:<br /> - <i>From birth onward, wolf children see things no one else can. Their wide, pale eyes trace movements over their mother\u2019s shoulder while nursing, like someone is walking by, and send chills down mother\u2019s spine. They\u2019ll speak to no one at all before they\u2019ll speak to other people, and sometimes they whisper things in words that sound so foreign to human ears that they must be possessed or demonic.</i><br /> - <i>As these Wolf-Blooded grow, even if they find homes with packs and territories, family and friends, they never cease to be strange. They remain off-putting in ways that are hard to put a finger on. They talk to themselves, they twitch, they eat their meals strangely or eat things not food and it\u2019s always as if they\u2019re in on some cosmic joke no one around them knows about, let alone gets the punch line to.</i><br /> - <i>A baby Wolf-Blooded, rejected by his mother because he was born with a full set of teeth. A child who kills another on the playground when she simply doesn\u2019t understand her own strength. A teenager who flies into a rage and wakes days later, in another town, covered in human blood and little else. These special, suffering souls are the bastard and beloved children of Luna.<br /> - They find ways to cope, and often, revel in their condition. Some spend their lives aching to be Forsaken so that at least they have something like control \u2014 that is, if they know that the Forsaken exist. Those who never find a pack to join have the worst, most tragic stories to tell.</i><br /> - <i>On occasion, Luna or Father Wolf adopts a perfectly normal person. A run-in with the world of the Forsaken or the spirit changes a perfectly mundane human being, turning her into a<br /> Wolf-Blooded. This is always traumatic; no one is adopted into the world of wolves without blood and screaming, and it is a miracle that any of these fresh-born Wolf-Blooded survive with<br /> anything like their lives and minds intact. </i><br /> <br /> I could grab more, but that's illustrative. Whether a Wolf-Blooded grows up knowing what Uratha are, or grows up without knowing, it's a big f'ing deal.<br /> <br /> Go back to Concept. Is she an ex-cop? A startup CEO? Not, what did she think of the fact she always healed faster than anyone else but developed hives when her family pulled out the silverware? (A Wolf's Meat) Not, how did she cover that wound that never healed right, or explain the strangers who would come from miles away to experience visions after tasting blood from the scar? (Bitten). Or, did she think she was going crazy from the constant whispers before she underwent the First Change and discovered spirits were real? (Horse)<br /> <br /> Tells are pretty important. Tells are pretty noticeable to the Wolf-Blooded. Every Wolf-Blooded has at least one Tell. (p. 300 tells us that <i>Having a Tell is what, essentially, makes a Wolf-Blooded a Wolf-Blooded</i>.) Yet Tells rate zero mention in basic character creation.<br /> <br /> While we're talking Tells, there's no 'What did your character think when she lost her Tell while undergoing the First Change? Relief, or was she disappointed that her unborn twin abandoned the werewolf she became?' (Shadow Twin) Tells are a big deal. She loses it if she becomes Uratha. That would probably be something that the character would find noteworthy in her existence.<br /> <br /> On the First Change, 'Sometimes Wolf-Blooded Change. Late in life, early on, with no rhyme or reason, some Wolf-Blooded just become werewolves.' (p. 297) The wording suggests Wolf-Blooded becoming Uratha is relatively uncommon. Uncommon enough that there's never any mention of the social dynamic between the 'successful' Uratha who came from Wolf-Blooded, and the 'failure' Wolf-Blooded who never underwent the First Change. The implication is that Wolf-Blooded are a state of existence, that sometimes change, but never with enough frequency that it's something anyone expects.<br /> <br /> So, summarising - players character Uratha have no mention of Tells or their existence as Wolf-Blooded. Very few (if any) NPC Uratha have any consideration of their early years as Wolf-Blooded, and how that shaped their werewolf experience. Wolf-Blooded characters have no real expectation of every becoming Uratha. It's theoretically possible, but so is winning the lottery, so you might as well buy tickets and hope for that.<br /> <br /> *But*, werewolves aren't human, and apart from the rare cases of Luna just being fickle on some poor bastard, never were human. Putting that all together, yes, <b>all werewolves come from wolf-blooded</b> (meaning somewhere way back when in the family, they had some kind of werewolf relative, minus that tiny percentage of 'moon-gifted/cursed' that means not really *all*), but actually <b>very few werewolves come from Wolf-Blooded</b> (which was the original question, but I had to unpack a lot of thinking that really wasn't captured in my thumb-typed phone-posted 'No'.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:40:57-07:00","id":943538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=943487#post943487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBunyip was commenting that not all people who become werewolves are Wolf-Blooded, rather than on the origins of Wolf-Blooded <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>... or I could just wait for Acrozatarim to cross-post in a much more succinct fashion while I compose a thesis! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What he said. Thanks buddy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:07:44-07:00","id":943629,"title":"","content":"I get it. But I can understand why people might be confused. The Wolf-Blooded section muddies it a little on p296.<br /> <br /> 'Where do Werewolves come from? Not in the grand scheme, but in the immediate, visceral, bodily sense?<br /> Short and sweet, they come from Wolf-Blooded.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2016, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:19:46-07:00","id":943635,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I never really drew a mental distinction between wolf-blooded and Wolf-Blooded, I just saw Wolf-Blooded who had manifested Tells and Wolf-Blooded who hadn't, and I figured either could go on to experience First Change. Saying that not all werewolves are Wolf-Blooded before the First Change just confused me because I was pretty sure ordinary humans never went through First Change. But if you're just talking about people with werewolf ancestry vs. people with Tells, I got you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:18:00-07:00","id":944391,"title":"","content":"My apologies if this has already been covered. I tried searching for this but didn't have much luck.<br /> <br /> I'm having a good deal of difficulty understanding how Spirit Influence works. Especially in the context of Gift of Elementals.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say I have a character with Purity 4 and Tongue of Flame. The character then has Influence (Fire) 4, which allows them to create fire... to what end? How much fire is created? What is the size of the fire? The intensity of the fire? Where are the mechanics determining the boundaries of what can be created?<br /> <br /> On that same token, once the fire is created, does it then start burning things and become natural fire? Or does the whole thing vanish once the duration of the influence has expired? At Influence (Fire) 4, creating fire from nothing could only be done for one minute per success (which, granted, is a lot of rounds), but during that minute does the manifested fire behave like normal fire? Igniting things and spreading like fire would?<br /> <br /> To that end, what happens if said character then used further manifestations of Influence (Fire) after initially creating it? What does adding ten minutes per success do, for instance, on Control? Or one day per success on Strengthen? Or are these effects ultimately limited by the initial duration of the Creation effect?<br /> <br /> If a character had Purity 5, and thus Influence (Fire) 5, could they presumably make a &quot;Permanent&quot; fire? An everliving flame that will never extinguish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:02:06-07:00","id":944446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lasellj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=944391#post944391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a good deal of difficulty understanding how Spirit Influence works. Especially in the context of Gift of Elementals.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say I have a character with Purity 4 and Tongue of Flame. The character then has Influence (Fire) 4, which allows them to create fire... to what end? How much fire is created? What is the size of the fire? The intensity of the fire? Where are the mechanics determining the boundaries of what can be created?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics are on page 186, under Influence. A fire can do whatever a fire can do. They're good for killing vampires and Prometheans and mummies. You can use further Influences to Manipulate or Control or Strengthen said fire. As for how much, size and intensity, keeping in mind you're only creating one fire it would likely be based on your successes, with 1 success granting you the equivalent of a torch or small campfire. If you were creating a fire on someone, successes would correlate to damage.<br /> <br /> There should be a scale chart somewhere but I think they only put it up in Mage.<br /> <br /> 'The spirit pays the listed cost in Essence and rolls Power + Finesse, with success creating the desired effect. If the Influence is altering the thoughts or emotions of a sentient being, the roll is contested by Resolve or Composure (whichever is higher) + Primal Urge.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On that same token, once the fire is created, does it then start burning things and become natural fire? Or does the whole thing vanish once the duration of the influence has expired? At Influence (Fire) 4, creating fire from nothing could only be done for one minute per success (which, granted, is a lot of rounds), but during that minute does the manifested fire behave like normal fire? Igniting things and spreading like fire would? </div> </div> </div>Fire would behave like normal fire. Whatever fire 'spread' from it would probably be normal, but the 'base' fire would disappear when the duration ran out.<br /> <br /> The durations are also on p186.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To that end, what happens if said character then used further manifestations of Influence (Fire) after initially creating it? What does adding ten minutes per success do, for instance, on Control? Or one day per success on Strengthen? Or are these effects ultimately limited by the initial duration of the Creation effect? </div> </div> </div>If you add Duration onto Create, the starting point of the fire lasts longer. If you add it to Control, whatever Control you use lasts longer, with that fire always doing that particular thing as long as the Duration lasts. Strengthening a fire would have it burn more viciously or be harder to put out depending on how you used it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a character had Purity 5, and thus Influence (Fire) 5, could they presumably make a &quot;Permanent&quot; fire? An everliving flame that will never extinguish? </div> </div> </div>Indefinite would probably be a better word. The fire would last unnaturally long, it would not run out of fuel, but I imagine it could be extinguished by external forces working against it. Fire is delicate that way, but I don't think anyone would crucify you for deciding the other way, that the fire was an everliving one that would never extinguish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-05-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:34:01-07:00","id":947717,"title":"","content":"Could someone just help explaining the sacred hunt to me? Like how does it work and why is it so vital to every single uratha on the planet. Like what time is the right time to call one? How does it work if you call it on a concept like let's say death or dishonesty as that also seems to be possible based on posts here. What effect does ghost wolves that go on a sacred hunt have compared to the effects the different tribe memberships give when they go on a sacred hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:04:43-07:00","id":947738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=947717#post947717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone just help explaining the sacred hunt to me? Like how does it work and why is it so vital to every single uratha on the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're part spirit of the hunt. Part of their soul demands the hunt. They are also part human, however, and can't 'eat' hunt Resonance the way a spirit might. They were able to in Pangaea, but it no longer exists. So they need the Siskur-Dah ritual to fulfill that part of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like what time is the right time to call one? </div> </div> </div>Arguably whenever you need. Werewolves can't go without hunting for long or they start losing Essence and making Harmony checks towards the Flesh, which makes further hunts harder.<br /> <br /> Each tribe has a favored prey of sorts that is likely to spur them into hunting it. There's also the demands of the territory which can require action in the form of a hunt. Sometimes there's a glorious prey, sometimes a vicious enemy. Sometimes there's a personal issue, sometimes it's an existential threat. The hunt means something, but it's up to the individual werewolf, or their pack, to decide what needs to be hunted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does it work if you call it on a concept like let's say death or dishonesty as that also seems to be possible based on posts here. </div> </div> </div>They hunt spirits, spirits can be of concepts. If you were going to defeat death or dishonesty in their highest form you would be going up against high-ranking conceptuals like Pseulak himself. Generally you wouldn't start a Siskur-Dah against something like that unless you had at least a basic idea of how to go about it, or were planning on spending all your time working on a way to go about it.<br /> <br /> A hunt against death or dishonesty from a group of scientist-werewolves could be an attempt to create a death vaccine, or a working lie detector. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What effect does ghost wolves that go on a sacred hunt have compared to the effects the different tribe memberships give when they go on a sacred hunt? </div> </div> </div>None. It seems to be granted by a tribal totem. No tribal totem? No Siskur-Dah blessing. However if you are part of a lodge you might gain a special benefit that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-10-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:22:17-07:00","id":956374,"title":"","content":"Is a werewolf in Gauru form able to shift out of Gauru form before their turns are up, or would that count as &quot;doing something other than attacking&quot; and send them into Kuruth? What if they attacked, and then shifted reflexively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:14:56-07:00","id":956395,"title":"","content":"They're allowed to shift out, providing they have the ability to, as in some cases it requires Essence. When you shift out of gauru, however, you're unable to go back in for the rest of the scene as you can only shift into gauru once per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:22:56-07:00","id":956546,"title":"","content":"Think of it as the Rage being the last thing to come and the first to go. You can take a turn to shift in without going nuts, so you can takes as long to get out as well for the same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:18:50-07:00","id":956807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=956546#post956546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it as the Rage being the last thing to come and the first to go. You can take a turn to shift in without going nuts, so you can takes as long to get out as well for the same reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't parse what you're saying here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T02:43:48-07:00","id":956862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=956807#post956807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't parse what you're saying here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, take 2: A werewolf can shift to Gauru form without falling into Kuruth, even if they take a whole turn to do it. Therefore the &quot;attack each turn or Kuruth&quot; rule must show up at the end of the transformation and only apply to the next turn. If we assume that shifting out of Gauru is simply the whole process running in reverse, that means the rule is the first to go and therefore they can shift down safely, even if they take an entire turn to do it. <br /> <br /> I mean sure, you could also say it doesn't cause Kuruth because that would be annoying for players, but I'm getting Watsonian here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","