Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=961497#post961497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dinosaur era is firmly in the region of &quot;got retconned into reality by the fall of Atlantis&quot; so it's a bit fuzzy how it interacts with the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I hadn't read that. First edition had dinosaur spirits, so there was at least a Hisil way back when. Unless that was retconned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:13:53-07:00","id":961585,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean if you want to totally ignore Mage here, that's fine, but I was just noting that pre-human history is a bit hard to nail down because at some undetermined no-longer-existent point a bunch of humans broke reality and made the world what it is today.<br /> <br /> Anything before that has always really existed, but it hasn't always always really existed so what connection it has to the more fantastic aspects of reality is a bit uncertain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:49:00-07:00","id":961682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=961585#post961585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean if you want to totally ignore Mage here, that's fine, but I was just noting that pre-human history is a bit hard to nail down because at some undetermined no-longer-existent point a bunch of humans broke reality and made the world what it is today.<br /> <br /> Anything before that has always really existed, but it hasn't always always really existed so what connection it has to the more fantastic aspects of reality is a bit uncertain.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/503363-exarchs-as-nonhumans?p=503468#post503468\">As Dave has pointed out</a>, the belief that the Exarchs were human is an in-world view the Awakened believe not backed up by the books. It's possible they were even Pangaean.<br /> <br /> So your answer is, 'No,' or 'Unsure, leaning towards no?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-01-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:51:12-07:00","id":961684,"title":"","content":"*shrug* I guess it depends if you think Father Wolf could pre-date wolves somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:02:58-07:00","id":961693,"title":"","content":"Mage's Time Before has no bearing on pangaean dinosaurs - so what if the world broke and pre-Fallen World time line was messed up? Father Wolf and dinosaurs exists in the current (broken?) timeline, and clearly have a before-after stage. Can't have Father Wolf before there are wolves, after all - spirits need to reflect reality to some extent, and there were no wolves in the age of dinosaurs. <br /> <br /> So, my personal answer is that &quot;Yes, dinosaurs had Pangaea before Father Wolf even existed.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:05:29-07:00","id":961695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=961682#post961682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/503363-exarchs-as-nonhumans?p=503468#post503468\">As Dave has pointed out</a>, the belief that the Exarchs were human is an in-world view the Awakened believe not backed up by the books. It's possible they were even Pangaean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or fully unfettered Old Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:30:23-07:00","id":961836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=961693#post961693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't have Father Wolf before there are wolves, after all - spirits need to reflect reality to some extent, and there were no wolves in the age of dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Father Wolf was not a spirit, it was a Pangaean.<br /> <br /> 'They are powerful symbols of natural cycles and forces, the gods of weather, the seasons, and the animals. Unlike spirits, they are not reflections of the world but pillars of it \u2014 primeval divinities born in this rift between worlds.'<br /> <br /> While we call it Father or Mother Wolf, it's also known as the Great Predator, and seems to have more of a bent towards Predation and the Hunt, not just Wolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=961695#post961695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or fully unfettered Old Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though given their appearances and powers and alienness, it's possible to lump Pangaeans under that label.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-01-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:34:49-07:00","id":962099,"title":"","content":"I don't think <i>Urfarah</i> is any more a wolf than Stephen King's It is a giant spider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pennywise</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly boy! You still think you can see &quot;me&quot;. Ha ha. You can never see me, you can only see what your little mind can allow!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:53:00-07:00","id":962182,"title":"","content":"That's being overly pendantic, y'all. Spirit, pangaean, Father, Mother, whatever. Wolfy Prime has its roots in modern day canine pack predators. Even if you want to argue that somehow we're dealing with an ancient spiritual being that evolved over time (which I doubt - predation between animal species is too varied for the Big Bad Wolf to embody close to a fraction of them to survive; we're looking at very narrow concepts outside of &quot;wolf&quot;), that would be a vastly different being that really would have no relationship to the modern figure. <br /> <br /> Futhermore, just because its a pangaean doesn't remove the necessity of having a tie to actual mundane and physical wolves. In order to be a symbol of something (and Wolfy absolutely has ties to wolves specifically over any other form of predator), that something has to exist, same as modern spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:54:34-07:00","id":962238,"title":"","content":"I would argue that <i>Urfarah</i> wasn't a pack predator. He hunted alone for Milennia before the First Pack formed, and from Sundered Workd's description of the First Pack, it sounds more like they followed in his wake rather than actually hunting with him.<br /> <br /> I don't think he was ever really the symbol of wolves, but rather that of predation. As long as there have been predators, there has been <i>Urfarah</i> (or perhaps, as long as there has been <i>Urfarah</i>, there have been predators). What form those predators have taken has changed over the centuries, and he eventually had children that took after the apex predators of their time, wolves. But that doesn't mean he has to have actually been a symbol of wolves himself.<br /> <br /> Not many people, including werewolves, got to see him and lived, and those that did usually only saw brief flashes as he ran through the Hunter's Paradise in pursuit of his prey. But if the description of Fox is any indication, he can't have looked <i>that much</i> like an actual wolf, and it's entirely possible that his association with wolves was a result of some combination of not having a better point of comparison and an assumption that if his children were wolves, he must have been a wolf as well. By modern times the story has gotten so distorted that the <i>Uratha</i> remember him as a spirit, so that's definitely not a reliable indicator. We really don't have much hard evidence that he was actually a wolf at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:22:27-07:00","id":962263,"title":"","content":"I have seen several mentions of that the Siskur-dah generates a lot of beats for players, but I am a little confused. Can someone elaborate on this? I'm worried that I'm not utilizing the beat system correctly in relation to Werewolf specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:41:45-07:00","id":962364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=962263#post962263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen several mentions of that the Siskur-dah generates a lot of beats for players, but I am a little confused. Can someone elaborate on this? I'm worried that I'm not utilizing the beat system correctly in relation to Werewolf specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Siskur-Dah rite gives those involved the Siskur-Dah Persistent Condition, which in turn offers Beats for achieving an exceptional success on an action involving the prey, or 'bringing down' the prey.<br /> <br /> It's not a Beat farm like certain other inherent gameline Conditions but providing you perform Sacred Hunts often, you are looking at many Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T03:49:10-07:00","id":963148,"title":"","content":"Are spirits solid when they're in the shadow, or always intangible without the manifestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:55:44-07:00","id":963202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963148#post963148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spirits solid when they're in the shadow, or always intangible without the manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritual intangibility is a function of the state of Twilight, which normally does not exist in most worlds beyond the material realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:24:18-07:00","id":963210,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Basu-im. My friend say that the line &quot;any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means&quot; means that a Werewolf gets this resistance to ANY Mage spell that influences the Werewolf in any way. Such as casting Control Gravity to suspend him in the air for duration of his rage.<br /> <br /> I believe it is meant as a defense against mental or social coercion. They've gone so far as to say anyone would suffer this penalty against an action like Grappling, since it's a mundane action attempting to change the Urathas course of action. His course of action being &quot;going after someome&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is there anything in the book at all that would support my argument? Hes saying the line is incredibly ambiguous and cites outside fantasy books as the intent of the rule. That the books are meant to be balanced and without resistance to any action by a Mage would allow a beginner Mage to effectively remove an elder Werewolf. We're all very good at rules lawyering and he is adamant about this and has convinced everyone else.<br /> <br /> We're playing a mixed game and if we can't effectively neutralize the Uratha then we could all die when he rages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T08:16:50-07:00","id":963229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Basu-im. My friend say that the line &quot;any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means&quot; means that a Werewolf gets this resistance to ANY Mage spell that influences the Werewolf in any way. Such as casting Control Gravity to suspend him in the air for duration of his rage.<br /> <br /> I believe it is meant as a defense against mental or social coercion. They've gone so far as to say anyone would suffer this penalty against an action like Grappling, since it's a mundane action attempting to change the Urathas course of action. His course of action being &quot;going after someome&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is there anything in the book at all that would support my argument? Hes saying the line is incredibly ambiguous and cites outside fantasy books as the intent of the rule. That the books are meant to be balanced and without resistance to any action by a Mage would allow a beginner Mage to effectively remove an elder Werewolf. We're all very good at rules lawyering and he is adamant about this and has convinced everyone else.<br /> <br /> We're playing a mixed game and if we can't effectively neutralize the Uratha then we could all die when he rages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's only against mental or social attempts. For that I point to the rules of interpretation that you use when interpreting law, the relevant rule of interpretation here is that you have to look to existing items in a list when trying to determine if new items would belong to it (a law which says it is illegal to use a skateboard or bike or other things can be interpreted to also apply to banning rollerskates and those weird hoverboard things, but it couldn't extend further and ban the use of cellphones as they're a thing which doesn't fit with the existing members of the list). So the existing things are attempts to influence or intimidate the raging werewolf. This list is all about socially or mentally manipulating a thing. Pointing a shotgun at them, trying to talk them down, hiding behind someone else and making the other person look more appetizing. Grappling or using a spell to immobilize them doesn't fit within the list, if it did then fighting back against the werewolf in any fashion or running away from them would also fit in that list, since those are changing the werewolf's course of action as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T08:17:01-07:00","id":963230,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure your friend is talking bullshit. You grapple or restrain a werewolf, their course of action isn't going to change. They're just going to have a lot more trouble doing it. By your friends logic they'd also get a resistance to being shot, because you can't chase after people when you're dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T08:36:02-07:00","id":963234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963229#post963229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's only against mental or social attempts. For that I point to the rules of interpretation that you use when interpreting law, the relevant rule of interpretation here is that you have to look to existing items in a list when trying to determine if new items would belong to it (a law which says it is illegal to use a skateboard or bike or other things can be interpreted to also apply to banning rollerskates and those weird hoverboard things, but it couldn't extend further and ban the use of cellphones as they're a thing which doesn't fit with the existing members of the list). So the existing things are attempts to influence or intimidate the raging werewolf. This list is all about socially or mentally manipulating a thing. Pointing a shotgun at them, trying to talk them down, hiding behind someone else and making the other person look more appetizing. Grappling or using a spell to immobilize them doesn't fit within the list, if it did then fighting back against the werewolf in any fashion or running away from them would also fit in that list, since those are changing the werewolf's course of action as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely understand that, but was looking for a concrete entry in the book that would contradict his &quot;fairness resistance&quot;. He'll, I had to point out to them that it was stupid for a Mage wanting to cast a worldwide spell to fail because somewhere in the world there was a death raging Werewolf.<br /> <br /> They finally broke down and created a house rules that the Werewolf himself gets a contested roll and if he succeeds then only he is unaffected. So in the case of Control Gravity he would stand in the middle while the world turns upside down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T08:57:18-07:00","id":963236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Basu-im. My friend say that the line &quot;any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means&quot; means that a Werewolf gets this resistance to ANY Mage spell that influences the Werewolf in any way. Such as casting Control Gravity to suspend him in the air for duration of his rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your friend is trying to get away with something that is obviously beyond the intent of the rules by citing a technical reading of rules that are not written in technical language. Tell him Chronicles of Darkness is written in natural language and to knock that rules lawyering bullshit off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it is meant as a defense against mental or social coercion. They've gone so far as to say anyone would suffer this penalty against an action like Grappling, since it's a mundane action attempting to change the Urathas course of action. His course of action being &quot;going after someome&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct, the intent is supposed to be for it to apply against mental and social coercion. As Elfive pointed out, grappling a werewolf (or using a gravity spell or whatever) doesn't <i>change</i> the werewolf's course of action. It presents an <i>obstacle</i> to their course of action, but they're still free to pursue any course of action they choose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything in the book at all that would support my argument? Hes saying the line is incredibly ambiguous and cites outside fantasy books as the intent of the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, natural language, not technical language. The intent should be clear to anyone who isn't trying to exploit wording to eek extra value out of their abilities. That shit doesn't work in Chronicles of Darkness, and if your players are going to insist on this kind of thing, they're gonna have a bad time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the books are meant to be balanced and without resistance to any action by a Mage would allow a beginner Mage to effectively remove an elder Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>HAHAHAHAHA!!!!!! Oh man, I have some baaaaaaaaaad news for your friend...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're all very good at rules lawyering and he is adamant about this and has convinced everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys are going to want to break yourselves of this habit, quick. The Chronicles of Darkness books are written with the assumption that the players are playing in good faith, can interpret natural language, and are invested in cooperative storytelling. Technical readings with intent towards gaining a competitive edge are antithetical to the buy-in of the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963210#post963210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're playing a mixed game and if we can't effectively neutralize the Uratha then we could all die when he rages.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I hinted at earlier, you're going to have balance issues in a mixed-template party. The game lines may be compatible, but they are designed as individual games - supbsplats within a template are more or less balanced against each other, but templates are not created equal. An analogy I've seen used before is that even though elves and dragons use the same rules in D&amp;D doesn't mean they work well in the same party.<br /> <br /> That's not to say you can't do a crossover group, but you should know that it is <i>not</i> going to be balanced in the way that, say, a D&amp;D party is balanced. You need to create your own &quot;balance&quot; by finding narrative niches each character fits into. Your werewolf can be the combat guy, or the scout/tracker, or the spirit medium, or all of the above, really. If you've got a vampire, they can be the face guy, the social networker, the mind controller, or all of the above. You might want to consider banning Mages, because while their primary niche is the investigator, they are so versatile they can easily step on everyone else's niche. Playing a Mage in a mixed template group requires a lot of discipline to avoid spotlight-hogging and let other players shine, even when you have a spell that could totally work in this situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T09:46:30-07:00","id":963254,"title":"","content":"You should direct your friend towards the Unchained Facet, in the Gifts of Strength. That would allow their character to break free from a magical or mundane attempt to 'hold' them, including giving a bonus to grapple.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, it is free and automatic in Basu-Im.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:03:29-07:00","id":963377,"title":"","content":"Probably a dumb question, but how is damage calculated? Is it weapon rating plus successes? That would mean our Werewolf during death rage has strength 6 plus 3 brawl so he rolls 9 dice and adds +2L for claw. But one Mage has 9 Defense with his spell and would knock the WW down to a chance die each attack. Then if he manages to hit he'd do 3L damage, but the Mage also has 3 armor and would make the WW completely unable to hurt him.<br /> <br /> This seems to make death rage go from scary to annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:28:23-07:00","id":963387,"title":"","content":"Yes, weapon rating plus successes. Your werewolf rolls 9 dice, any successes grant an extra 2 Lethal.<br /> <br /> In gauru form an opponent only goes by their Dexterity or Wits to determine their Defense, the usual skill like Athletics doesn't count. But keep in mind a werewolf in gauru has a great advantage to grappling. And if you can hit a target, you can initiate a grapple. To initiate a grapple you need to get over the target's Defense, but once in a grapple it comes down to contesting Strength + Brawl vs Strength + Brawl.<br /> <br /> That's not counting the various Gifts and fetishes that may be available, and often become free and automatic during death rage, or the fact that other wolves can be triggered by the presence of a werewolf in death rage, and each character attacking a target in a round lowers that target's Defense by 1. Or Merits that grant Armor Piercing or increased damage.<br /> <br /> But if you're dealing with a single werewolf who isn't inclined towards combat, and a mage who is very inclined towards avoiding it, that mage is going to still be good at avoiding combat. Though when you're taking Lethal damage, with armor you always take at least 1 Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> If you offered more details, like the specifics of the mage's Defense, the werewolf's abilities, or the source of this armor, we might be able to point out some other things you've missed.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, providing your werewolf is at a level of Harmony that allows for reflexive shapeshifting, a good maneuver to start with against humanoid opponents is to open up in urshul with an attack that causes Leg Wrack to lower Defense, or Arm Wrack if they have a dangerous weapon, Knocked Down only if they seem like they can run or your pack is with you. Then shift into gauru. Against dangerous opponents, I strongly suggest one eats the flesh, causing Aggravated damage whenever possible. But that doesn't fit the personality of all player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-04-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:47:44-07:00","id":963398,"title":"","content":"Also, werewolf in death rage not making all-out attacks? Pull the other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:54:48-07:00","id":963403,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Willpower expenditure can also add +3 dice to the attack roll. So, with Willpower and an all-out attack, you're looking at a dice pool of 5, which gives you a pretty good chance to land the first hit in Urshul, dealing Leg Wrack automatically to halve their Defense. Then next round if they're not already Beaten Down from the damage you can go Gauru to further reduce their Defense. With another All-Out and Willpower you can either just roll with a huge dice pool or take a small penalty for a targeted attack to try and slam them with yet another Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:06:35-07:00","id":963429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963387#post963387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, weapon rating plus successes. Your werewolf rolls 9 dice, any successes grant an extra 2 Lethal.<br /> <br /> In gauru form an opponent only goes by their Dexterity or Wits to determine their Defense, the usual skill like Athletics doesn't count. But keep in mind a werewolf in gauru has a great advantage to grappling. And if you can hit a target, you can initiate a grapple. To initiate a grapple you need to get over the target's Defense, but once in a grapple it comes down to contesting Strength + Brawl vs Strength + Brawl.<br /> <br /> That's not counting the various Gifts and fetishes that may be available, and often become free and automatic during death rage, or the fact that other wolves can be triggered by the presence of a werewolf in death rage, and each character attacking a target in a round lowers that target's Defense by 1. Or Merits that grant Armor Piercing or increased damage.<br /> <br /> But if you're dealing with a single werewolf who isn't inclined towards combat, and a mage who is very inclined towards avoiding it, that mage is going to still be good at avoiding combat. Though when you're taking Lethal damage, with armor you always take at least 1 Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> If you offered more details, like the specifics of the mage's Defense, the werewolf's abilities, or the source of this armor, we might be able to point out some other things you've missed.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, providing your werewolf is at a level of Harmony that allows for reflexive shapeshifting, a good maneuver to start with against humanoid opponents is to open up in urshul with an attack that causes Leg Wrack to lower Defense, or Arm Wrack if they have a dangerous weapon, Knocked Down only if they seem like they can run or your pack is with you. Then shift into gauru. Against dangerous opponents, I strongly suggest one eats the flesh, causing Aggravated damage whenever possible. But that doesn't fit the personality of all player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the rule you only get dex/wits and not Ath? I know the WW is not combat focuser and the Mage has 3 Life so he uses the higher of Dex/Wits and adds half Life to armor and defense.<br /> <br /> I suppose against others he'd want to all out attack, but this is a scenario if we are left with our WW out of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:27:57-07:00","id":963436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963429#post963429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the rule you only get dex/wits and not Ath? I know the WW is not combat focuser and the Mage has 3 Life so he uses the higher of Dex/Wits and adds half Life to armor and defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 97 of the Werewolf second edition core book, under Gauru and further under Primal Fear. 'In normal combat, opponents count only their Dexterity or Wits to their Defense; they may not add the appropriate Skill (normally Athletics).'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose against others he'd want to all out attack, but this is a scenario if we are left with our WW out of control. </div> </div> </div>A werewolf in gauru, and more specifically death raging, is only going to attack or move closer to something to attack. All Out Attacking should at least be on the table, 'out of control' or not. Considering the healing ability of a werewolf and whole concept of Kuruth, overextending oneself may not be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Edited: For reasons stated below. 09-05-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:42:46-07:00","id":963536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963436#post963436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf in gauru, and more specifically death raging, is only going to attack or move closer to something to attack. There is no reason it wouldn't All-Out Attack, as that's basically what it's doing to begin with. Normally characters wouldn't All-Out Attack because they risk overextending themselves and getting hurt, but that's not something a werewolf in Kuruth is concerned with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this may be an unpopular opinion, but I don't think werewolves are obligated to make all-out attacks in Basu-Im. As you cite, it specifies that the werewolf can only attack or move closer to a target to attack. I would think if they could only make all-out attacks it would specify that as well.<br /> <br /> Not that a Death Raging werewolf wouldn't be inclined to make all-out attacks, but I also think they have enough natural fighting instinct to know when to go all-out and when to defend themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:03:43-07:00","id":963547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963536#post963536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this may be an unpopular opinion, but I don't think werewolves are obligated to make all-out attacks in Basu-Im. As you cite, it specifies that the werewolf can only attack or move closer to a target to attack. I would think if they could only make all-out attacks it would specify that as well.<br /> <br /> Not that a Death Raging werewolf wouldn't be inclined to make all-out attacks, but I also think they have enough natural fighting instinct to know when to go all-out and when to defend themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're right. Probably inclined to but it's not a guarantee, depends a lot on the character and situation. I'd understand if some Storytellers insisted it happened that way, with them all using All-Out Attacks in Kuruth, but it's not how I would run it so shouldn't expect others to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2016, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T01:43:30-07:00","id":963598,"title":"","content":"Well, in general, no, but I think he'd start doing it after the first time he missed the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:04:32-07:00","id":963757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963547#post963547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you're right. Probably inclined to but it's not a guarantee, depends a lot on the character and situation. I'd understand if some Storytellers insisted it happened that way, with them all using All-Out Attacks in Kuruth, but it's not how I would run it so shouldn't expect others to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm conflicted as well because it states that a WW in Basu-im will use Rage gifts automatically for no cost, but says they're also aware of their own safety and will run if fighting a foe stronger than them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:28:22-07:00","id":963774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963757#post963757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm conflicted as well because it states that a WW in Basu-im will use Rage gifts automatically for no cost, but says they're also aware of their own safety and will run if fighting a foe stronger than them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't state that, do you have a page number? In Wasu-Im, before you've fully succumbed to Kuruth, you can run and find a 'safe place' to do it, but in Basu-Im you aren't aware of your own safety and won't run if fighting a foe stronger than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:48:25-07:00","id":963791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963774#post963774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It shouldn't state that, do you have a page number? In Wasu-Im, before you've fully succumbed to Kuruth, you can run and find a 'safe place' to do it, but in Basu-Im you aren't aware of your own safety and won't run if fighting a foe stronger than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>May have been 1st Ed or even WTA. I might rule they must All-out attack as Rage and certain Strength Gift automatically turn on.<br /> Although what about Fighting Styles? Relentless Assault can be used in Kuruth but isn't forced...so maybe not.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It doesn't specifically stated you must use all out attack, so I think it would not be forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","user":"Grimbli","date":". 09-05-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:19:16-07:00","id":963960,"title":"","content":"How serious is breaking the Oath of the Moon by consuming flesh for essence? It says the Pack and Totem get pissed, but no concrete answers as far as I can tell. <br /> <br /> And if eating flesh is off the table, else does a WW regain Essence if they won't have access to a Hallow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T17:13:00-07:00","id":963981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963960#post963960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How serious is breaking the Oath of the Moon by consuming flesh for essence? It says the Pack and Totem get pissed, but no concrete answers as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its a breaking point on the Harmony scale. The totems tend to demand some kind of penance, or action by the wolf to repay the act.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if eating flesh is off the table, else does a WW regain Essence if they won't have access to a Hallow? </div> </div> </div> Locus. Hallows are for mages. <br /> <br /> And there's several ways, primarily the sacred hunt, seeing your Moon, and trading.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T20:15:56-07:00","id":964036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=963960#post963960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How serious is breaking the Oath of the Moon by consuming flesh for essence? It says the Pack and Totem get pissed, but no concrete answers as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> And if eating flesh is off the table, else does a WW regain Essence if they won't have access to a Hallow?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so serious that it's entirely off the table. Generally if there's a specific rule about something, it's something that has a tendency to happen, if not to you, then somewhere.<br /> <br /> It is taboo, and some wolves are going to get up in arms about it, while some may shrug it off as a matter of necessity. But just like the other Oaths it's going to depend on your world and characters within it to decide how serious it's taken. There's an entire tribe focused on breaking, 'The People Do Not Murder The People,' while most wolves will agree that it's a line that can be crossed in times of 'great need.' And most packs aren't entirely going to stick to honoring the high and respecting the low. From a Storyteller's standpoint, these rules exist to be tested, if not outright broken. They're all strings you can pull.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to get Essence is from a locus. They have an abundant amount, usually, and as much can be taken as one wants. Performing the Sacred Hunt against other spirits is a way to do it too, but at that point you're risking danger and you might not get much. From there you can get drips and drops from breaking open fetishes, seeing your Auspice moon, and the occasional Rite like Harness the Cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:36:49-07:00","id":964242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964036#post964036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The easiest way to get Essence is from a locus. They have an abundant amount, usually, and as much can be taken as one wants. Performing the Sacred Hunt against other spirits is a way to do it too, but at that point you're risking danger and you might not get much. From there you can get drips and drops from breaking open fetishes, seeing your Auspice moon, and the occasional Rite like Harness the Cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt we'll have Fetishes in the beginning and the Hunt will take a while. Auspices only gives one point a night for 5 (?) nights.<br /> <br /> The only Locus we'll have is any purchased with Dedicated Locus merit and can I even access that if I don't spend dots?<br /> <br /> We may end up doing a nomadic game and I'm just wondering if I'll have options other than devouring spirits or eating people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:49:10-07:00","id":964246,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is a game of predation and the hunt. You get your main source of essence by acting like a territorial predator. If you're breaking away from the predation and territory grooming, then yes, essence is going to be scarce. The game is designed with that in mind on purpose - you're encouraged into the werewolf mindset by getting essence for acting like one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-06-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T06:25:31-07:00","id":964257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964246#post964246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf is a game of predation and the hunt. You get your main source of essence by acting like a territorial predator. If you're breaking away from the predation and territory grooming, then yes, essence is going to be scarce. The game is designed with that in mind on purpose - you're encouraged into the werewolf mindset by getting essence for acting like one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. We may start with people buying Dedicated Locus, can I use it as a normal Locus and just not use the extra benefits? Or is considered reserved for only those that spend points?<br /> <br /> Also, would it be worth it starting at Primal Urge 2? It's a lot of points, but I feel like my character would have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:52:04-07:00","id":964293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964257#post964257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. We may start with people buying Dedicated Locus, can I use it as a normal Locus and just not use the extra benefits? Or is considered reserved for only those that spend points?<br /> <br /> Also, would it be worth it starting at Primal Urge 2? It's a lot of points, but I feel like my character would have it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A dedicated locus can be used as a locus by anyone in the pack, but only the ability to spend more essence per-turn can be used by those that invest the points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:49:50-07:00","id":964396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964257#post964257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would it be worth it starting at Primal Urge 2? It's a lot of points, but I feel like my character would have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found that the first levels of Primal Urge amped up in power very slowly so I made a point to increase them fast, considering my werewolf was a very werewolfy werewolf. But really there's not much different mechanically between 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> Nomads are meant to have a harder time of it, you don't know when your next 'meal' will come from, or whether there will be something to hunt at the next town. You might look at the Pack, and a lodge like the Thousand Steel Teeth, who can act nomadic and have some road-based prey to hunt. You can find loci, but they may be claimed by other werewolves or spirits or worse, and you might be running through the territory of other werewolves who won't like it. But that's the fun of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:59:55-07:00","id":964399,"title":"","content":"I am new to the forum and am running my first game of WtF 2e, but I had a lot of experience with 1e.<br /> <br /> One of the characters is coming from another pack to join the current pack of characters. What is the process for leaving a pack/joining a pack? How do the totemic benefits change? Thanks for any input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12325-iamspoonman","name":"iamspoonman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:42:14-07:00","id":964434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamspoonman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964399#post964399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am new to the forum and am running my first game of WtF 2e, but I had a lot of experience with 1e.<br /> <br /> One of the characters is coming from another pack to join the current pack of characters. What is the process for leaving a pack/joining a pack? How do the totemic benefits change? Thanks for any input!</div> </div> </div> </div>The totem will naturally increase in power as more uratha join the pack as they provide more totem merit dots. If the new dot rating of the totem exceeds the threshold for the totemic benefit xp pool increasing then the totemic benefit xp pool increases.<br /> <br /> As for how to leave / join. Up to the pack. Some packs will let you leave as you like, not wanting to keep others around who don't want to be there, some will hunt down and eat any who would dare to try to leave. Joining wise, some packs just let anyone in who wants in, some are super strict and require massively difficult trials for newbies to prove their worth. Pretty much all that happens mechanically is the uratha breaks their bond with the old totem and puts at least 1 dot towards the new totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:47:38-07:00","id":965136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=964434#post964434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...some will hunt down and eat any who would dare to try to leave. Joining wise, some packs just let anyone in who wants in...</div> </div> </div> </div> They might hunt you down, but only the most debased packs will eat other werewolves as it's a violation of the Oath of the Moon (and a good way to create a Harmony imbalance).<br /> <br /> No pack is just going to let anyone join on a whim either, these are the closest and most trusted individuals you will ever associate with as a werewolf, and with how dangerous werewolf existence is you don't just let anyone watch your back or learn your secrets. Not if you want to live for too long.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:12:16-07:00","id":965416,"title":"","content":"Can anything be targeted with Siskur-dah? Or is it used for spirits only?<br /> <br /> I only ask because it usually mentions spirits but the third Rahu Gift says you gain attack bonus against anything protecting prey and mentions humans. But nothing I've found has come out and said humans or other supernaturals can be the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:17:03-07:00","id":965417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=965416#post965416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anything be targeted with Siskur-dah? Or is it used for spirits only?<br /> <br /> I only ask because it usually mentions spirits but the third Rahu Gift says you gain attack bonus against anything protecting prey and mentions humans. But nothing I've found has come out and said humans or other supernaturals can be the target.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I don't have the rules with my and thus can't cite a specific page, considering that four out of the five Tribes have beings other than Spirits as their Sacred Prey, then I would certainly think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:26:22-07:00","id":965425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=965416#post965416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anything be targeted with Siskur-dah? Or is it used for spirits only?<br /> <br /> I only ask because it usually mentions spirits but the third Rahu Gift says you gain attack bonus against anything protecting prey and mentions humans. But nothing I've found has come out and said humans or other supernaturals can be the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything. Even concepts, jobs, territories. The Sacred Hunt is often used for, but not limited to, the kill. One can hunt to find a lost fetish or rite, the ban of an idigam, the spirit of a lost packmate, and so forth. Though obviously you limit some of your abilities in this regard, as being able to use a special damaging Gift against the Lost Land of Nar isn't going to be very useful.<br /> <br /> That specific Gift refers to anything serving as an obstacle to you pursuing the Sacred Hunt. Man, beast, werewolf, demon, Claimed, host, god. Any obstacle.<br /> <br /> If you want you can skip ahead to the Sacred Hunt rite, it's on page 140.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:06:51-07:00","id":965624,"title":"","content":"When I purchase Renown I get a free Shadow or Wolf Facet, does it have to be the Facet that shares the same Renown as the one you improved? Or can it be any one you choose?<br /> <br /> Also, when increasing your main Auspices Gift by buying Renown, do you also gain the free Facet in addition to your Auspice?<br /> <br /> And I think I know this one, but it says purchasing other Auspice Gifts allows you to buy the higher ones for 2xp, and you cannot have it above your current Auspice Renown. So that means if you have 1 Cunning but 3 Purity as a Rahu, you could buy New Moon up to 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:22:01-07:00","id":965633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=965624#post965624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I purchase Renown I get a free Shadow or Wolf Facet, does it have to be the Facet that shares the same Renown as the one you improved? Or can it be any one you choose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If you don't have one open, you can 'save' it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, when increasing your main Auspices Gift by buying Renown, do you also gain the free Facet in addition to your Auspice? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Moon Gift and a Shadow or Wolf Gift, just like any other increase in Renown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think I know this one, but it says purchasing other Auspice Gifts allows you to buy the higher ones for 2xp, and you cannot have it above your current Auspice Renown. So that means if you have 1 Cunning but 3 Purity as a Rahu, you could buy New Moon up to 3? </div> </div> </div>Ooh, close.<br /> <br /> You can only get the Auspice Gifts associated with your Auspice. That remark is 'future proofing' for when other Moon Gifts are created, such as the one in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a>, available to Cahalith. A Rahu could, without homebrewing your own Moon Gifts, only get Moon Gifts from the Full Moon. And only an Irraka can get Gifts from the New Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:51:12-07:00","id":965642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=965633#post965633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. If you don't have one open, you can 'save' it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Moon Gift and a Shadow or Wolf Gift, just like any other increase in Renown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ooh, close.<br /> <br /> You can only get the Auspice Gifts associated with your Auspice. That remark is 'future proofing' for when other Moon Gifts are created, such as the one in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/&amp;quot;]this</a> post[/URL], available to Cahalith. A Rahu could, without homebrewing your own Moon Gifts, only get Moon Gifts from the Full Moon. And only an Irraka can get Gifts from the New Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks for all the answers, my friends and I are starting a game and it's the first time we've run 2e.<br /> <br /> Guess I should've noticed the last one's &quot;associated with your Auspice&quot; but it's wonky they put that in when there's no supplements. Figure something like that would be detailed in the next books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:13:26-07:00","id":965862,"title":"","content":"I get it, it's probably put up the most questions. It's ironic because it was solely put in there to help future players. But I suppose without the context of 'there are no alternative Auspice Gifts for each Auspice in this book, but there may be in future supplements,' or having played the game in first edition it seems to have really caught a lot of peoples attention. I like it, but I appreciate why it might pop a question mark above the heads of newcomers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:34:47-07:00","id":966016,"title":"","content":"Can anyone explain Elemental Gifts to me? I'm confused about the five levels and what each of them can do.<br /> <br /> Does it scale in power with that of Mage's Arcanum?<br /> <br /> Is it purely story effects?<br /> <br /> Is there a list of what can be done in the book and I'm missing it?<br /> <br /> What is the purpose of the Catastrophic power if you can only light a candle?<br /> <br /> I have to be missing something. Usually I understand powers easily but this one is stumping me and I have a feeling it's staring me in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:35:44-07:00","id":966036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966016#post966016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone explain Elemental Gifts to me? I'm confused about the five levels and what each of them can do.<br /> <br /> Does it scale in power with that of Mage's Arcanum?<br /> <br /> Is it purely story effects?<br /> <br /> Is there a list of what can be done in the book and I'm missing it?<br /> <br /> What is the purpose of the Catastrophic power if you can only light a candle?<br /> <br /> I have to be missing something. Usually I understand powers easily but this one is stumping me and I have a feeling it's staring me in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've noticed it says the Uratha gains 'Influence' of an element but it doesn't go into it there.<br /> <br /> Influence is an ability of ephemerals, it is noted later in the book, more specifically on page 187. But it is heavily dependent on story for effect, though it has obvious practical applications as well.<br /> <br /> You can light a candle with no source of fire with Tongue of Flame and four dots of Purity. If you had Catastrophe, you can set fire to everything in a radius of miles equal to twice your Glory Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:06:14-07:00","id":966093,"title":"","content":"BTW this is also how some Talens such as Storm Coils work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T03:29:55-07:00","id":966127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966036#post966036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've noticed it says the Uratha gains 'Influence' of an element but it doesn't go into it there.<br /> <br /> Influence is an ability of ephemerals, it is noted later in the book, more specifically on page 187. But it is heavily dependent on story for effect, though it has obvious practical applications as well.<br /> <br /> You can light a candle with no source of fire with Tongue of Flame and four dots of Purity. If you had Catastrophe, you can set fire to everything in a radius of miles equal to twice your Glory Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how do you determine how strong the effect is or what you can do. At 4 Purity, lighting a candle seems extremely weak, but also it seems like you could create a floor of fire over an area.<br /> <br /> The language shares a lot with Mage, but the differing levels don't correlate. For instance, Disciple (3 Arcanum) allows Perfecting which can bolster something's durability or structure, but that can be done with Influence 1.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Influence 4 can create something from nothing, while Arcanum 5 is needed for Making.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean Influences are stronger because it takes Influence 2 to manipulate and that's the job of Arcanum 1. It also correlates evenly with Influences 3 controlling things that Arcanum 2 can do.<br /> <br /> Without charts to give examples I'm not sure how far you can reach. 4 Purity creates fire from nothing, but is that just the aforementioned candle or creating a pillar of fire to burn a Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T03:39:39-07:00","id":966130,"title":"","content":"Normally, Rank of the spirit determines the stregth of the effect. You could use the same for a werewolf, or Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:17:20-07:00","id":966145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966130#post966130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally, Rank of the spirit determines the stregth of the effect. You could use the same for a werewolf, or Primal Urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit I'm brand new to the spirit thing, never bothered with them before. Is there any reference for how they work? Even if it's 1e or WtA.<br /> <br /> I love your sig btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:26:15-07:00","id":966146,"title":"","content":"In the descriptions of the Influences. For example in Strengthen, is suggested to give a bonus to a given roll or heal a number of Health/Structure equal to Rank. Can't remeber if this was a flat amount or per success, I think the later.<br /> <br /> Oh, thanks. Can't remeber where I took it from, but I can't get credit for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:38:12-07:00","id":966180,"title":"","content":"Basically &quot;lighting candles&quot; is a deceptively advanced application of Influence (fire). At that point you can chuck around fireballs and create walls of flame and all sorts of crap. You ever see Pyro from X-Men? He's basically got Influence (fire) 3. He can do all sorts of crap but he needs a lighter to get started.<br /> <br /> This is why there's a numen that lets you start fires. Flame spirits would be a bit hobbled without it, so they can sort of cheat and get &quot;create fire&quot; early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:11:50-07:00","id":966195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966180#post966180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically &amp;quot;lighting candles&amp;quot; is a deceptively advanced application of Influence (fire). At that point you can chuck around fireballs and create walls of flame and all sorts of crap. You ever see Pyro from X-Men? He's basically got Influence (fire) 3. He can do all sorts of crap but he needs a lighter to get started.<br /> <br /> This is why there's a numen that lets you start fires. Flame spirits would be a bit hobbled without it, so they can sort of cheat and get &amp;quot;create fire&amp;quot; early.</div> </div> </div> </div>So with a high Renown and the Elemental Facets you can be like a Forces Mage but only relating to the element you have available? Seems fairly powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:21:51-07:00","id":966199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimbli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966195#post966195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with a high Renown and the Elemental Facets you can be like a Forces Mage but only relating to the element you have available? Seems fairly powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> You can also befriend spirits, in fact have one as a totem, and spirits always have Influences too. Later, you'll see the fetishes section, and you'll see that they can offer variants of existing Gifts, or offer their own Influence. One of the fetishes offers a limited Influence: Electricity. You could get another one to turn your Tongue of Flame Influence to Spiders, or Wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:23:52-07:00","id":966200,"title":"","content":"Some Lodges also give an influence as their membership perk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:28:44-07:00","id":966201,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for things like Scale and Potency, it's largely up to ST discretion. Influences are meant to be pretty narrative effects, so beyond the limits placed by the Influence levels, it's kind of just &quot;as the story demands.&quot; That said, if you want more hard and fast rules regarding how much fire your Purity 4 Werewolf can create (for example), I would suggest looking to Mage's Spell Factors.<br /> <br /> Influences are always activated Instantly, so we can assume Instant casting time. They don't generally require touch, so we can assume Sensory range. Duration is covered by the chart in the Epbemeral Entiries section. That leaves us with Potency and Scale. Scale is kind of covered by Rank but kind of not. For example, Influence 4 is Create, which allows creating a single example of the Inluence temporarily, where Influence 5 is Mass Create, which allows creating multiple examples of the Influence temporarily, or one example permanently. But Strengthen, Manupulate, and Control don't really tell us how many subjects or how large an area they can affect. So, let's assume Influences use the interaction between Create and Mass Create as our model. Use Standard Scale by default, and switching to Advanced Scale increases the Influence dot requirement by 1.<br /> <br /> We can use successes as a measure of Potency and/or steps up the Scale chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-09-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:55:45-07:00","id":966221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966201#post966201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for things like Scale and Potency, it's largely up to ST discretion. Influences are meant to be pretty narrative effects, so beyond the limits placed by the Influence levels, it's kind of just &amp;quot;as the story demands.&amp;quot; That said, if you want more hard and fast rules regarding how much fire your Purity 4 Werewolf can create (for example), I would suggest looking to Mage's Spell Factors.<br /> <br /> Influences are always activated Instantly, so we can assume Instant casting time. They don't generally require touch, so we can assume Sensory range. Duration is covered by the chart in the Epbemeral Entiries section. That leaves us with Potency and Scale. Scale is kind of covered by Rank but kind of not. For example, Influence 4 is Create, which allows creating a single example of the Inluence temporarily, where Influence 5 is Mass Create, which allows creating multiple examples of the Influence temporarily, or one example permanently. But Strengthen, Manupulate, and Control don't really tell us how many subjects or how large an area they can affect. So, let's assume Influences use the interaction between Create and Mass Create as our model. Use Standard Scale by default, and switching to Advanced Scale increases the Influence dot requirement by 1.<br /> <br /> We can use successes as a measure of Potency and/or steps up the Scale chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes a ton of sense. I'll bring that up with my group as we have two Bone Shadows. I'm a Rahu Hunter, but plan on getting it eventually. We have 2 Mages, buy neither have Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:57:18-07:00","id":966468,"title":"","content":"So how deep is the connection between any given spirit and it's physical counterpart? If you have a car and it's spirit in the shadow, what happens to the car if you kill the spirit? What happens to the spirit if the car gets hit, or even wrecked? Is there a way to do something to one side for a direct, meaningful effect on it's counterpart, like killing the spirit of a bomb to keep the real deal from going off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","user":"Gaius94","date":". 09-09-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","name":"Gaius94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T16:26:03-07:00","id":966476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966468#post966468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how deep is the connection between any given spirit and it's physical counterpart? If you have a car and it's spirit in the shadow, what happens to the car if you kill the spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It becomes 'less' of a car. It's still a car, but it's not as 'car' as another car might be. It's not as noteworthy, interesting, it doesn't have soul. But otherwise there's no mechanical effect other than the car spirit might not be there to give it a push every once and awhile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens to the spirit if the car gets hit, or even wrecked? </div> </div> </div>It might become a wrecked car spirit, opening up its feeding. Depending on the circumstances of the accident it might become a death and car spirit. Depending on the emotions of the driver it might become an alarmed or panicked or fearful car spirit, or an angry one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a way to do something to one side for a direct, meaningful effect on it's counterpart, like killing the spirit of a bomb to keep the real deal from going off? </div> </div> </div>Well, obviously a spirit of a bomb would have Influence over bombs. Depending on the dots of Influence it could Strengthen that bomb, or Manipulate or Control it. Or make a new one. Or make many new ones.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's specific mechanics for something's 'lack' of a spirit, but it's definitely something to play with in stories. Throughout the books there are warnings against things like spirit bombs or blocking off the Gauntlet, as without a spirit to access, everything becomes bland and emotionless and spiritually dead. I always pictured it similar to the planet Miranda in the movie Serenity.<br /> <br /> Throughout our games we've used it as a way to more easily deal with certain things, as they no longer have a sort of spiritual backing to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:34:12-07:00","id":966561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=966476#post966476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It becomes 'less' of a car. It's still a car, but it's not as 'car' as another car might be. It's not as noteworthy, interesting, it doesn't have soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Dave's clarifications are any indication, this might be an illusory correlation founded in the fact that destroying a spirit terminates the effects of its Influences and thus a car whose spirit is destroyed becomes &quot;less remarkable&quot; because there has ceased to be a spirit that is Strengthening its Car-quale. A car-spirit lacking a home and/or looking to expand might claim the unguarded resource, but that could very well have happened already thanks to the way discorporation normally works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:44:34-07:00","id":966563,"title":"","content":"I think one of the books somewhere, or perhaps a developer or writer, was talking about when a spirit awakens. The example was a knife or gun, and the spirit was awakened when the knife or gun was used as a knife or a gun. Before that it was unused and unawakened, presumably not in a 'shiny brand new' way. Perhaps on the other end of the scale, a powerful spirit reflects upon a powerful source. A shark is not 'just a shark' but the shark from Jaws. Its name was Bruce. The kind of ephemeral quality that makes something stand out, to be 'more' than the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eJkxxm68MZI\" data-code=\"eJkxxm68MZI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eJkxxm68MZI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But that was first edition, I could see the spirit Strengthening thing being a meta explanation for Durability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:31:17-07:00","id":967868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=904024#post904024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping The Pack would answer this, but it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Can other supernaturals that are part of a pack (Vampires, Beasts, etc) purchase Totem dots? If so, can they purchase up to 5, like Uratha? Or are they limited to the amount Wolf-Blooded can purchase? Or Humans?<br /> <br /> What if they were wolf-blooded before they changed into something stranger? Does that impact the equation?</div> </div> </div> </div>i searched for a lot of time this question: some writer can give a sentence &quot;officialized&quot; about this?<br /> Thanks a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:40:24-07:00","id":967988,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they're considered wolf blooded for most purposes, including totem dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:56:07-07:00","id":969013,"title":"","content":"Is it a correct that if a spirit has a shadow gift that it can teach, then that spirit can also use it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:03:29-07:00","id":969015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=969013#post969013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a correct that if a spirit has a shadow gift that it can teach, then that spirit can also use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there was something of the sort in first edition. <br /> <br /> Not in second. A Gift becomes a special aspect of the werewolf's hunter soul, then focused through a facet of their Renown.<br /> <br /> You could justify Numina as having similar powers, obviously a weather spirit can cause changes in weather similar to Weather Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:06:37-07:00","id":969017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=969015#post969015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe there was something of the sort in first edition.<br /> <br /> Not in second. A Gift becomes a special aspect of the werewolf's hunter soul, then focused through a facet of their Renown.<br /> <br /> You could justify Numina as having similar powers, obviously a weather spirit can cause changes in weather similar to Weather Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I mean, blast is badass but I might grab gift facets as numina to make a wider variety of spirit battles/dealings<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T02:08:23-07:00","id":969095,"title":"","content":"Gifts are distinctly werewolf-themed most of the time so just make sure you file those serial numbers off properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:40:47-07:00","id":972518,"title":"","content":"One of my friends said you can only gain a beat from Condition resolution once per scene, but I'm having trouble finding that rule.<br /> <br /> If you had multiple Conditions and somehow resolve them all at once, would you only gain 1 beat or would you get multiple beats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:49:30-07:00","id":972698,"title":"","content":"I think they're thinking of the rule about only getting beats from persistent conditions once per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:25:45-07:00","id":973017,"title":"","content":"So when you get an exceptional success it says you should gain a positive condition. What would be one for Brawl? Inspired is given as an example but then mentions it's for crafts or expression. And I don't think getting an ex success on 3 dice would be good for Brawl since you'd gain and resolve it every round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:01:22-07:00","id":973043,"title":"","content":"If you manage to get 5 successes on someone and then 3 successes on a continuous basis you're doing pretty damn good for yourself. Sadly, the dice are rarely that kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:57:12-07:00","id":973140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973043#post973043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you manage to get 5 successes on someone and then 3 successes on a continuous basis you're doing pretty damn good for yourself. Sadly, the dice are rarely that kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I am a high strength Rahu with Primal Strength, lots of Brawl, an Area of Expertise bite specialty, and 8-again from Killer Instinct. It comes up more than you think.<br /> <br /> Seemed that an Inspired loop would generate as many Beats as I had things to hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:23:27-07:00","id":973212,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, not saying you can't get your dice pool pretty high. A starting Rahu Werewolf can actually get reliable 17 dice bite attacks in Urshul Form with 8-Again, but due to the averages of the game you only get a 1-in-3 chance of getting a success in the first place. This goes along with your enemy also having their defense remove 2-6 of your dice on a regular basis means you'll have a tough time of it. <br /> <br /> But, oh boy, when you get it going that'll be some Dempsey Roll shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:04:59-07:00","id":973329,"title":"","content":"This happened on my game: A Steel elemental that &quot;nested&quot; on an old abandoned car shop made a deal with a pack. It has the possession charm. It asks for the pack to help it find a human body to inhabit, that is not a &quot;softie.&quot; It\u00b4s a rank 3 spirit (the elemental presented in Predators). The players are discussing it, as it is interesting to have a thing like that in good terms.<br /> So given that.<br /> - Is it a violation of the oath of the moon (The wolf must hunt) to indulge in such a pact?<br /> - Is it badly seen by the other packs (I assume so).<br /> - How long the conditions (open, possessed, etc) must exist for it to Claim the human?<br /> - Would the local storm lords become the enemy of the pack for such an action?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11882-bernagarou","name":"Bernagarou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:40:03-07:00","id":973441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernagarou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973329#post973329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Would the local storm lords become the enemy of the pack for such an action?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on two things.<br /> <br /> 1. If they ever found out about it.<br /> 2. If they believed strongly that such a thing was wrong, which is likely but isn't always true, especially given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> You know more about the other storm lords in the area than us. There's none in the pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-20-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:19:53-07:00","id":973472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernagarou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973329#post973329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This happened on my game: A Steel elemental that &quot;nested&quot; on an old abandoned car shop made a deal with a pack. It has the possession charm. It asks for the pack to help it find a human body to inhabit, that is not a &quot;softie.&quot; It\u00b4s a rank 3 spirit (the elemental presented in Predators). The players are discussing it, as it is interesting to have a thing like that in good terms.<br /> So given that.<br /> - Is it a violation of the oath of the moon (The wolf must hunt) to indulge in such a pact?<br /> - Is it badly seen by the other packs (I assume so).<br /> - How long the conditions (open, possessed, etc) must exist for it to Claim the human?<br /> - Would the local storm lords become the enemy of the pack for such an action?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's akin to allowing a spirit to operate in the material realm, but with a clear victim, so it's even more of a sin.<br /> <br /> The condition must exist at a number of nights it would take for the spirit to override the mortal's will.<br /> <br /> Most Storm Lords would put you in the same bag as the claimed, what's worse? Some spirit breaching the gauntlet or the assholes that allowed it knowingly in the first place? The later could have re-occurrences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:56:36-07:00","id":973698,"title":"","content":"I think there's either a breaking point or oath of the moon that mentions &quot;willingly allowing spirits through the Gauntlet&quot;<br /> <br /> It's definitely not a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:54:40-07:00","id":973877,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> I have an Irraka Storm Lord in my game and the player keeps trying this combat maneuver where they run out of combat and try to &quot;hide&quot; to be able to use the New Moon Gift Eviscerate to maximize their damage rolls. I don't really like this and don't think RAW supports the idea of &quot;hiding&quot; after being in combat.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think of this? How would the Gift of Evasion Hit and Run Facet affect this plan? On a success, can Eviscerate be used again? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12325-iamspoonman","name":"iamspoonman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:08:55-07:00","id":973886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973441#post973441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on two things.<br /> <br /> 1. If they ever found out about it.<br /> 2. If they believed strongly that such a thing was wrong, which is likely but isn't always true, especially given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> You know more about the other storm lords in the area than us. There's none in the pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one, but he is a new player in the game and does may not be aware of the repercurssions of his actions. Also, he is not really allowed to ask for help (Show Weakness is against the storm lord code, isn\u00b4t it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11882-bernagarou","name":"Bernagarou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:22:19-07:00","id":973892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamspoonman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973877#post973877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> I have an Irraka Storm Lord in my game and the player keeps trying this combat maneuver where they run out of combat and try to &quot;hide&quot; to be able to use the New Moon Gift Eviscerate to maximize their damage rolls. I don't really like this and don't think RAW supports the idea of &quot;hiding&quot; after being in combat.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think of this? How would the Gift of Evasion Hit and Run Facet affect this plan? On a success, can Eviscerate be used again? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, yeah, it sounds plausible. Werewolves in Forsaken aren't kitted out to all be in-your-face maulers; a repeated sequence of ambush, escape, and ambush again to harry the prey is very in tone for the New Moons.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't have it be as simple as succeeding on the Hit and Run roll. Hit and Run first requires you to have somewhere within the range of your dash away that can take you out of the line of sight. I'd then probably require the werewolf to repeat the contested Stealth versus Perception roll to ambush again, and if this tactic is getting disruptive, it wouldn't be unreasonable to rule that disengaging and reestablishing stealth might take more time than the three-second turn scale of combat makes feasible, making it impractical to be able to repeat an ambush while the rest of the pack is still engaged. Inflicting Shadow Paranoia will make this tactic easier.<br /> <br /> But the strategy is sound. Irraka don't fight fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:47:59-07:00","id":974043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernagarou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973886#post973886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one, but he is a new player in the game and does may not be aware of the repercurssions of his actions. Also, he is not really allowed to ask for help (Show Weakness is against the storm lord code, isn\u00b4t it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>His character would have been taught about the Storm Lords. Whoever initiated him into it may have told him what they think about it. If the character doesn't care, it could be because their mentor didn't either.<br /> <br /> And asking about rules and traditions you're unaware of isn't necessarily showing weakness, or really asking for help. One could certainly argue that seeking out someone wiser in matters you are ignorant of is a strong thing to do, and acting in willing ignorance due to fear of asking for guidance a weak thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-21-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:44:13-07:00","id":974074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamspoonman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=973877#post973877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of this? How would the Gift of Evasion Hit and Run Facet affect this plan? On a success, can Eviscerate be used again? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly how it works. Even more so with that merit that gives you cumulative bonus dice each time you slip unnoticed.<br /> <br /> It's also at least worth 2 essence per attack, not exactly cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:53:19-07:00","id":975495,"title":"","content":"I swear I heard someone say on this thread that WW in Gauru form can still attack with full dice pool even while blind, but can't find a mention in the rules. Anyone confirm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:37:24-07:00","id":975506,"title":"","content":"It's on page 94, and goes a bit further than just in Gauru:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolf senses offer a bonus to<br /> Perception-based rolls depending on her form. Further, if she<br /> would normally suffer penalties due to deprivation (blindness,<br /> strong scents, or deafness), her other senses compensate,<br /> negating those penalties entirely. </div> </div> </div>Basically, a werewolf can just flat-out ignore blindness or deafness or anything else, as long as they use their wolf senses. Which they can reflexively turn on whenever they like for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T02:38:33-07:00","id":975890,"title":"","content":"Ah, ok, awesome! I was just reading the upper part where it said they halve the penalty for Urshan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12291-grimbli","name":"Grimbli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:38:36-07:00","id":977942,"title":"","content":"1e used to have Location spirits as a spirit type, a sort of blend of artificial and nature spirit that wasn't considered Magath, but doesn't list them as a spirit type any longer. Is that still a spirit type in 2e, or did this edition purposefully get rid of it? If so, what type of spirit is something like the spirit of a city in 2e... Conceptual? Or just &quot;the biggest spirit in the region that can take and hold the title&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:48:21-07:00","id":977949,"title":"","content":"There are spitits of everything except humans. So, yeah, that includes locations. The biggest and most powerful spirit in a city should by all rights be the spirit of the city itself (unless it gets killed or something), as literally everything in the city is Resonant for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:56:05-07:00","id":977954,"title":"","content":"They're Artificial spirits, along with Information, Tool, Weapon, Vehicle, Structure, and Object spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:17:27-07:00","id":977966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=977949#post977949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest and most powerful spirit in a city should by all rights be the spirit of the city itself (unless it gets killed or something), as literally everything in the city is Resonant for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like it would be intuitively true (and potentially a &quot;boring&quot; enough answer that I thought they perhaps explicitly removed Location spirits because of it), and yet whenever they talk about example spirit courts for urban locations, I never see the spirit of the city mentioned as the lord of the court or even an important spirit. So far as I can tell in 2e, a &quot;spirit of the city&quot; is only explicitly mentioned in the Basra, Iraq hunting grounds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:25:59-07:00","id":977970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=977966#post977966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like it would be intuitively true (and potentially a &quot;boring&quot; enough answer that I thought they perhaps explicitly removed Location spirits because of it), and yet whenever they talk about example spirit courts for urban locations, I never see the spirit of the city mentioned as the lord of the court or even an important spirit. So far as I can tell in 2e, a &quot;spirit of the city&quot; is only explicitly mentioned in the Basra, Iraq hunting grounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a being so powerful is often going to be rather above the things werewolves deal with. It's not like they're a common antagonist.<br /> <br /> For instance in Basra, the only reason the city spirit is known is because Basra is being spiritually wrecked by Fenris-Ur. In a normal, large city, it would be much more above things, a Rank 5 or 6 spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:57:28-07:00","id":977983,"title":"","content":"Hi. Where can I find informations about Azlu? Besides corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:06:39-07:00","id":977991,"title":"","content":"The first edition book Predators has a substantial section on them. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They're really nasty. </div></div> </div> </div>Some of the mechanics would have to be converted, but not much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:10:13-07:00","id":977992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=977983#post977983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Where can I find informations about Azlu? Besides corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got to go to the 1e book <b>Predators</b> for more information of Azlu. Unfortunately there are no guidelines in 2e to building hosts at this point that i know of, though you can probably use the Horror rules in Chronicles of Darkness core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:33:43-07:00","id":978005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=977970#post977970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because a being so powerful is often going to be rather above the things werewolves deal with. It's not like they're a common antagonist.<br /> <br /> For instance in Basra, the only reason the city spirit is known is because Basra is being spiritually wrecked by Fenris-Ur. In a normal, large city, it would be much more above things, a Rank 5 or 6 spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your feeling is that city spirits of large metropolitan areas are too removed to take visible action or be in charge of the local spirit court?<br /> <br /> I suppose that would explain some things, but then again nearly all the hunting grounds talk about very powerful spirits that are impacting the spirit courts locally - they are just never city spirits. Spirits of Royalty and Government Authority for All of Thailand, spirits of Rivers, Indigam, weird oil and chain Demons etc. City spirits just seem incredibly conspicuous in their near complete absence (and unlike to be more powerful than the spirit of Royalty and Governmental Authority for an entire country) from talk about spirit court politics. Which was what was leading me to believe that either they mostly got axed in 2e, or that they are rarely the strongest spirit in the area for one reason or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:55:06-07:00","id":978047,"title":"","content":"Hi there.<br /> I want to know, if there is any abillity for an Idigam to use his power through one of its spawn/herald/slave/whatever without being at the place of the spawn.<br /> Exampel: the Idigam is in its Lair. It feels, its herald is in danger. It looks through his eyes (One Million Eyes) and decided to use the Shadow Warp essence shaping ability to save its herald.<br /> Is it possible? Is there a dread power, numina or essence shaping power I haven't seen?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:30:31-07:00","id":978061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=978005#post978005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your feeling is that city spirits of large metropolitan areas are too removed to take visible action or be in charge of the local spirit court?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part. As you can see in Basra, and the Night Horrors book, and the UK book, sometimes city spirits are going to do things that deserve a response. The second edition book says this, 'Dihim are potent spirits, fed on the Essence of wide-ranging phenomena and paid a steady stream of Essence from their lessers. Even the weakest Dihir dominates the Shadow around its lair, and Uratha with hunting grounds including those lairs have to take the Dihir into account as a central figure in Hisil predation. Uratha seek Dihim \u2014 or Diharim \u2014 for the most potent Gifts, or to use their influence among other spirits. When a Dihir breaks through the Gauntlet, it\u2019s cause for alarm and a call to the Siskur-dah.'<br /> <br /> When your pack is fighting over territory with another pack, it is creating violence spirits, death spirits, rage spirits, there's probably a lot of destruction going around. But the city itself is not suffering any existential threat over it, unless it's a small city. The city spirit isn't going to have to bow down and do anything about it until something big happens, and while that does happen, the book is presenting the game's core, not just 'high end' content, and in many of the Hunting Grounds the plot hooks aren't related to the possible destruction of the city like they are in Basra. Whether the Pure or the Forsaken rule, the city spirit is still there to get its Essence from everything in the city. And generally it's going to be too powerful a thing to wrangle into being a totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose that would explain some things, but then again nearly all the hunting grounds talk about very powerful spirits that are impacting the spirit courts locally - they are just never city spirits. Spirits of Royalty and Government Authority for All of Thailand, spirits of Rivers, Indigam, weird oil and chain Demons etc. City spirits just seem incredibly conspicuous in their near complete absence (and unlike to be more powerful than the spirit of Royalty and Governmental Authority for an entire country) from talk about spirit court politics. Which was what was leading me to believe that either they mostly got axed in 2e, or that they are rarely the strongest spirit in the area for one reason or another. </div> </div> </div>It's because there's one city spirit per city. Usually. Some divided cities probably have a few. The spirits you're talking about in Thailand are 'linked to royalty and governmental authority,' not spirits of those things. But even then, as Predators points out, the spirits of playground, sewers, and subways in a city are 'city spirits,' it's just not the spirit of the city.<br /> <br /> They're still there, I mean you've mentioned the one in Basra yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=978047#post978047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there.<br /> I want to know, if there is any abillity for an Idigam to use his power through one of its spawn/herald/slave/whatever without being at the place of the spawn.<br /> Exampel: the Idigam is in its Lair. It feels, its herald is in danger. It looks through his eyes (One Million Eyes) and decided to use the Shadow Warp essence shaping ability to save its herald.<br /> Is it possible? Is there a dread power, numina or essence shaping power I haven't seen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there's a power that does that in the book, but the book isn't meant to show all the abilities of the idigam and limit them. You're free to make an ability that does that, I think it would be very fitting, though perhaps cause some damage to the herald.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:21:32-07:00","id":980901,"title":"","content":"Hi Everyone,<br /> <br /> The Pure are shaping up to be playing a large role in my current campaign, from an Ivory Claw stealing wolf-blooded of the tribe and hiding them from Luna's mark, to a big pack of Predator Kings nurturing a baby Idigam they don't understand.<br /> <br /> I've been reading up more about the Pure from 1e to get some more information as my players are really compelled by them and I'm getting a bit confused. So Forsaken argue that the Pure should not be killed because &quot;The People do not Murder the People&quot;, but then in the 1e source The Pure, there is the Oath of the Wolf which <i>specifically </i>omits this interpretation of that rule, allowing the Pure to unabashedly murder the Forsaken. So then why are there any forsaken left? They don't have the awesome spirit totems of the Pure, they spend all their time fighting against all the litany of antagonists introduced, and in general there are just fewer Forsaken. There's also references in 2e to 'skirmishes' with the Pure. If the Pure see no issue in killing the Forsaken, why are these skirmishes not resulting in deaths all the time? And how do the Forsaken continue to justify their believe in the Oath of the Moon protecting the pure?<br /> <br /> I know that's a lot of questions, but I'm just so confused. At this point I really want my Pure to be a bit more sympathetic, more of the &quot;different interpretation&quot; that is so common in nWoD than the unrelatable &quot;evil guys&quot;. What do you guys think of having the Pure have the same debate about their oath of the wolf as to whether it applies to Forsaken? Thanks for your input, the forum and community here are truly amazing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12325-iamspoonman","name":"iamspoonman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:44:23-07:00","id":980913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamspoonman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=980901#post980901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading up more about the Pure from 1e to get some more information as my players are really compelled by them and I'm getting a bit confused. So Forsaken argue that the Pure should not be killed because &quot;The People do not Murder the People&quot;, but then in the 1e source The Pure, there is the Oath of the Wolf which <i>specifically </i>omits this interpretation of that rule, allowing the Pure to unabashedly murder the Forsaken. So then why are there any forsaken left? They don't have the awesome spirit totems of the Pure, they spend all their time fighting against all the litany of antagonists introduced, and in general there are just fewer Forsaken. There's also references in 2e to 'skirmishes' with the Pure. If the Pure see no issue in killing the Forsaken, why are these skirmishes not resulting in deaths all the time? And how do the Forsaken continue to justify their believe in the Oath of the Moon protecting the pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, as you can see, their Oath doesn't allow them to unabashedly murder the Forsaken. The Pure, p33. 'In seeing the Forsaken as lesser, the Pure theoretically believe it\u2019s perfectly acceptable to murder the Forsaken. Not just to kill in the heat of battle \u2014 but to outright execute them. (Note that this still constitutes a Harmony violation. The Oath to Urfarah and sins against nature are not in accord.) In fact, some grudgingly accept that murdering Forsaken is the only way that Pangaea and Father Wolf will be allowed to return. Still, killing Forsaken rattles many Pure, whether or not they admit it out loud.'<br /> <br /> Second, every werewolf is naturally borne with an auspice. It would be incredibly difficult to wipe out the Forsaken just by that basis, because if you kill every Forsaken in North America, there's going to be two going through their First Change the next day, and three more elsewhere across the world. It's impossible to tell when someone might change, who might change, and be there for every change that occurs before they become Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Third, the Forsaken have been decimated. There's something called the Brethren War, just before the 'modern day' in first edition where the Pure have wiped out most of North America's Forsaken. That was the situation the players were starting in. But in a number of other places it explains that the Brethren War is a two-sided, cyclical thing. At some point the Pure gets too comfortable, and starts weakening themselves with infighting, the Fire-Touched never leaving the Hisil, the Predator Kings never leaving the wilds, and the Ivory Claws too arrogant to see anything happening to them. Which is when the Forsaken, organized and having to train and fight tooth and claw just to survive against a superior number, cuts them down. Then the Forsaken get fat and happy, telling their pups the Pure are just an old threat they've already taken care of and nothing to worry about anymore. Maybe the Blood Talons are going to point out that the Pure are gaining numbers, angrily, in the dark corners of the world where the Forsaken don't abide, but the Forsaken have other things to deal with. And the cycle continues.<br /> <br /> Fourth, while this existed in first edition I don't think it's been as big an issue as it is now. There's other factions. Ghost Wolves can have lodges and faux protectorates, strange groups like the Cull and Lodge of the Field exist and would rabidly defend their right to in the face of the Pure coming to convert them for not having abandoned their auspice. And the Bale Hounds are always there to corrupt and sabotage any endeavor either side pursues.<br /> <br /> Fifth and finally, for this post, though I'm sure there's other reasons, it's just a matter of organization. It would be ridiculously hard to root out a group like the Forsaken, or the Pure across the world in their entirety. You would have to know where every one of the enemy is, while they have the capability to escape to other worlds and use magic to conceal themselves. These are both groups that have existed for thousands of years, being hunted by each other, spirits, and other supernatural beings. They're all very good hunters, but they're all very good at surviving, too. And tribes maintain some intra-tribal communication, but not usually to that a high level of organization, no one really has a database of peoples names and packs and totems. Once you get past Packs and Lodges, everyone is pretty much scattered and unaligned in mindset with others beyond what brought them into the tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that's a lot of questions, but I'm just so confused. At this point I really want my Pure to be a bit more sympathetic, more of the &quot;different interpretation&quot; that is so common in nWoD than the unrelatable &quot;evil guys&quot;. What do you guys think of having the Pure have the same debate about their oath of the wolf as to whether it applies to Forsaken? Thanks for your input, the forum and community here are truly amazing! </div> </div> </div>I think it would be hard to justify, as is, Pure arguing that they shouldn't kill the Forsaken, full stop. Some people might just need to get killed. It would be a good point for people to bring up that the Pure are created via recruitment, however, 'Why should we kill them when we can convert them?' is a valid argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:26:02-07:00","id":981340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=980913#post980913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, every werewolf is naturally borne with an auspice. It would be incredibly difficult to wipe out the Forsaken just by that basis, because if you kill every Forsaken in North America, there's going to be two going through their First Change the next day, and three more elsewhere across the world. It's impossible to tell when someone might change, who might change, and be there for every change that occurs before they become Forsaken.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was a 1e thing but the pure are able to detect nuzusul and perform a rite on them such that they never have an auspice and undergo their first change without ever being touched by Luna's blessing. I don't see any reason why that can't be the case for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:20:20-07:00","id":981395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=981340#post981340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a 1e thing but the pure are able to detect nuzusul and perform a rite on them such that they never have an auspice and undergo their first change without ever being touched by Luna's blessing. I don't see any reason why that can't be the case for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're rituals, but it would still involve using multiple rituals to cover everyone on the globe because each use of the rite only detects the first, closest nuzusul in 5 miles. Which would be difficult to arrange.<br /> <br /> It's one thing when you control a wolf-blooded town and someone's likely to change, it's another when you're trying to catch them all and they can pop up at random.<br /> <br /> Seems like the kind of rites that would cross over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:19:08-07:00","id":981424,"title":"","content":"You also have the point where Luna's involvement with their choirs of spirits, and the Forsaken Firstborn with their choirs of spirits. While its possible for them to get pushed into the gutter its all too easy for these great powers of the Shadow to get involved and turn things to their favor.<br /> <br /> Hell, nothing really seems to stop Luna from causing a Mass Change among Wolf-Blooded across the Globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:18:53-07:00","id":981453,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Another problem, with eradicating either side, is that it just takes one spirit to jumpstart it again. One ex-Pure totem or one of the Pure Firstborn initiating a new member, or a lune.<br /> <br /> That said you could still make significant gains with territory, and have a lot of personal, pack and possibly protectorate strength with your chosen side. I like to focus on the massive changes they want, with the Pure trying to bring back Pangaea or resurrect Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:01:28-07:00","id":993721,"title":"","content":"In which Umia belongs a shadow-spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:22:19-07:00","id":993731,"title":"","content":"It depends on the area and how the choirs are organized within. It's not always a system that follows human logic, and spirits of the same type can be in different choirs.<br /> <br /> A safe bet would be Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:47:25-07:00","id":997564,"title":"","content":"Not to backtrack too far, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=977992#post977992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to go to the 1e book <b>Predators</b> for more information of Azlu. Unfortunately there are no guidelines in 2e to building hosts at this point that i know of, though you can probably use the Horror rules in Chronicles of Darkness core.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are rules in the 2e core for making Hosts and Claimed. They're not incredibly in-depth, but they suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:24:41-08:00","id":1000461,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, i have a quick question regarding the hisil:<br /> is EVERYTHING there made of ephemera/spirit-stuff?<br /> <br /> Recently one of my players wanted to sharpen a rock to use as an improvised weapon while in the hisil which made me wonder about the implications. Is it actually a rock or maybe a dormant muthra? in which case, can it even be sharpened in the typical way? what if he brought it back through a locus? can the same be said for the vegetation of the hisil?<br /> <br /> I personally would think that it not everything would be a spirit, as there are still spirits of buildings that look entirely different (humanoid, for example).<br /> <br /> I'd love to know what you guys think, this thread has been a huge help to a new ST like myself in getting a better understanding of the werewolf setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12646-darkatom","name":"Darkatom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:29:22-08:00","id":1000464,"title":"","content":"I think it's all ephemera. Dormant spirits or dormant parts of larger spirits. A building may change to look humanoid but it might just have a part of it look humanoid, like drawing a face on your thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:57:32-08:00","id":1000555,"title":"","content":"Unlike in the Material World, in the Hisil eveything is composed of Ephemera. Raw ephemera is like unmolded clay: it is the stuff Spirits are maid of, but it is not active unless sufficient Essence has poured into it.<br /> <br /> Let's take your stone as an example:<br /> Unlike active ranked Spirits or even Muthra, the stone is just a raw ephemera that got it's shape by the minimum Essence of the symbolism acquired from its material counterpart. It will (most of the time) work exactly as a stone would work in the Material World, so sharpening it would be no problem at all. However, if that place has a particularly abundant sort of some kind of Resonance, like a big battlefield where people battled to death, the stone might acquire some different proprieties, still being a stone, but a little easier to use on violent purposes (allowing for combat bonuses, for example).<br /> <br /> The Hisil, is highly reactive to the Material World. Even if something is not a Spirit nor Muthra, Resonance will shape it's ephemera accordingly, making even inanimate objects very unpredictable by common knowledge standards. In resume, feel free to allow things to work normally in the Hisil, and then surprise your players by adding some nice twist to mundane activities now and then. The sharpened stone might bite back at its user, due to a betrayal having occurred on that place, or it might shatter to dust when used on combat, due to a promise of peace that was forged right over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:32:20-08:00","id":1000569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1000555#post1000555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's take your stone as an example:Unlike active ranked Spirits or even Muthra, the stone is just a raw ephemera that got it's shape by the minimum Essence of the symbolism acquired from its material counterpart.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is a spirit. This is why everything in the world has a spiritual reflection, except for humans. P179, 'Spirits come into being alongside the thing they're a reflection of, but they're dormant, barely-living, tiny lumps of ephemera at first.' P180, 'Muthra are barely formed, new-born spirits with no minds of their own and no rank in the umia. They aren't even powerful enough to awaken from dormancy, and simply settle in the Hisil close to a source of Essence. Other spirits feed on them with no more care than a human shows towards fruit.'<br /> <br /> If there's a spirit reflection of a thing and another, ephemeral reflection of things that is not a spirit, it's not mentioned in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:44:17-08:00","id":1000573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1000569#post1000569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, buy they are not ranked Spirits nor Muthra, that's what I was trying to explain. Everything in the Hisil is called &quot;spirit&quot; by the book, but the ranked ones are the ones and Muthra are the only ones active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:03:47-08:00","id":1000580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1000573#post1000573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, buy they are not ranked Spirits nor Muthra, that's what I was trying to explain. Everything in the Hisil is called &quot;spirit&quot; by the book, but the ranked ones are the ones and Muthra are the only ones active.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what I'm pointing out is that there is no space between nothing and muthra. If it has enough ephemera to have the outline of a form, it's muthra at least. 'They exist in the Hisil as faint outlines of the earthly phenomena they draw Essence from, but if they aren't consumed by other spirits, they eventually develop into dormant Hursihim with the capacity to awaken.' The step you're describing is just muthra, a Rank 0 spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:27:44-08:00","id":1000585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkatom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1000461#post1000461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, i have a quick question regarding the hisil:<br /> is EVERYTHING there made of ephemera/spirit-stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what others have said, according to Book of Spirits, when something that isn't ephemeral like a human goes to the Shadow they get converted into ephemera (which can make them look slightly off).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:40:10-08:00","id":1000961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1000580#post1000580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what I'm pointing out is that there is no space between nothing and muthra. If it has enough ephemera to have the outline of a form, it's muthra at least. 'They exist in the Hisil as faint outlines of the earthly phenomena they draw Essence from, but if they aren't consumed by other spirits, they eventually develop into dormant Hursihim with the capacity to awaken.' The step you're describing is just muthra, a Rank 0 spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. I was mixing concepts from first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:06:11-08:00","id":1001013,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for answering my question, this clarified a lot of questions I had.<br /> I do have one follow up question though, using my previous example of a stone muthra being sharpened into an improvised weapon.<br /> <br /> In short: what would happen to it when taken from its resting place?<br /> According to page 184, I would assume it would be able to keep up its essence reserves while in the proximity (several yards?) of other stones, even while in the material world. <br /> But it would also have turned into a weapon, so might therefore diversify its diet to also consuming weapon resonance? or does it actively have to try to steal essence (also described on page 184) of a different resonance for that to happen?<br /> If it did diversify somehow, what would be needed to keep its essence pool stable? it's a spirit, so it should not be able to generate resonance by simply existing like a normal sharpened stone would, so perhaps it would have to be held (or even used) as a weapon every couple of hours/days (depending on what side of the gauntlet you're on), or is the idea of it being a weapon in the user's mind enough, and will it survive indefinitely as long as the user doesn't lose it?<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the help, I gained a lot of insight into how the hisil functions from your answers so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12646-darkatom","name":"Darkatom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T16:09:43-08:00","id":1001536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkatom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1001013#post1001013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to page 184, I would assume it would be able to keep up its essence reserves while in the proximity (several yards?) of other stones, even while in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>A dormant Spirit, specially a Muthra, won't lose Essence. Spirits enter dormancy because they <b>lack</b> Essence. So, essentially, a Muthra is a dormant Spirit that may, one day, wake-up if it accumulates Essence enough. This means that your stone probably has not even sufficient Essence inside her to mechanically measure as an Essence Point. Active Stone Spirits eat thousands of little stones to be able to remain active. You would not be able to invoke the Siskur-Dah agains that stone to claim it's Essence, for example.<br /> <br /> That said, the book isn't much specific about this hole &quot;Spirit Awakening&quot; part, so I'm only giving you my own interpretation of how to treat the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkatom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1001013#post1001013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it would also have turned into a weapon, so might therefore diversify its diet to also consuming weapon resonance? or does it actively have to try to steal essence (also described on page 184) of a different resonance for that to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since your Stone Weapon isn't really active yet, it can't hunt for Essence on it's own, but with sufficient exposure to lots of Essence and Resonance, it might awaken as a Spirit of that Resonance. As written, Spirits gain 1 Essence per day when near their main Resonance. Since the lowest Hursih has a 10 Essence pool, I would say that it would take that amount of days for an Spirit to awaken, problem is, they are normally consumed by bigger Spirits. In your case, the stone is being protected by the Uratha, so it might have an easier time developing.<br /> I would say that after several exposures to really meaningful combat, it would certainly awaken as a Murder Stone Hursih.<br /> <br /> Just remember that Spirits eat Essence, and if the Uratha uses that stone against the wrong kind of Spirit, it will just gobble it up and gain more power in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkatom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1001013#post1001013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it did diversify somehow, what would be needed to keep its essence pool stable? it's a spirit, so it should not be able to generate resonance by simply existing like a normal sharpened stone would, so perhaps it would have to be held (or even used) as a weapon every couple of hours/days (depending on what side of the gauntlet you're on), or is the idea of it being a weapon in the user's mind enough, and will it survive indefinitely as long as the user doesn't lose it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely right on the first example. It will need to be exposed, daily, to a suitable Resonance Condition, gaining a minimum of 1 Essence Point. A material version of it will suffice to maintain it, but actions using it will also allow a chance for generating Essence. For example, using the spirit-weapon in combat would qualify as a Resonant Condition, allowing the Spirit to Gorge. As written:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits may attempt to gorge themselves on a source of appropriate Essence. Once per day, when in proximity (even if it\u2019s on the other side of the Gauntlet) to a suitable Condition, a spirit can roll Power + Finesse, regaining successes in Essence. If the spirit is still in the Hisil, the dice pool is penalized according to Gauntlet strength. <b>Page 184</b> </div> </div> </div>So, after the Spirit is active, it will use it's attributes to try and suck Essence from a Resonant Condition into itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T22:58:14-08:00","id":1001636,"title":"","content":"Thanks Binaly (and nofather and milo v3), thanks to you I'll be able to better understand and therefore portray the hisil. The quality of my games will most certainly improve because of you guys. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12646-darkatom","name":"Darkatom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T06:11:45-08:00","id":1001731,"title":"","content":"Does a Wolf-Blooded with a Tell that gives them access to a werewolf form gain Wolf Senses and/or Spirit Senses in that form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:00:31-08:00","id":1001744,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think so, since there seems to be other Tells that grant abilities like that, like Piercing Eyes. Also the senses aren't really attributable to a particular form, they're part of the werewolf that can be used in any form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:12:26-08:00","id":1001762,"title":"","content":"Spirit senses are more than just being able to see the spirit twilight. Spirit senses also include when you 'reach' across the gauntlet with one or more of the senses native to your current form, there isn't really any tell that grants that ability. So I'd say no to spirit senses. Wolf-senses yes, though only with tells that let you take urshul or urhan, dalu wouldn't grant wolf-senses, you gain all of the other bonuses from the form and the tells don't say you don't also get wolf-senses. I mean, if you cause lunacy when you are in urshul with shape-shifted I don't see why you wouldn't be able to use the perception bonuses as well. They wouldn't be able to just switch back to human senses though, they'd have to shift back to human form for it. I'd say they could only use the senses native to the form they're in (so no +2 perception for dalu).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:57:52-08:00","id":1001784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1001762#post1001762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit senses are more than just being able to see the spirit twilight. Spirit senses also include when you 'reach' across the gauntlet with one or more of the senses native to your current form, there isn't really any tell that grants that ability. So I'd say no to spirit senses. Wolf-senses yes, though only with tells that let you take urshul or urhan, dalu wouldn't grant wolf-senses, you gain all of the other bonuses from the form and the tells don't say you don't also get wolf-senses. I mean, if you cause lunacy when you are in urshul with shape-shifted I don't see why you wouldn't be able to use the perception bonuses as well. They wouldn't be able to just switch back to human senses though, they'd have to shift back to human form for it. I'd say they could only use the senses native to the form they're in (so no +2 perception for dalu).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about what I was thinking. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:32:05-08:00","id":1002053,"title":"","content":"<b>Wolf senses are considered the werewolf\u2019s default senses<br /> in Urhan and Urshul form</b>. Wolf senses offer a bonus to<br /> Perception-based rolls depending on her form. Further, if she<br /> would normally suffer penalties due to deprivation (blindness,<br /> strong scents, or deafness), her other senses compensate,<br /> negating those penalties entirely.<br /> <br /> \u200bFrom page 94 of the book it seems as if the senses are tied to form so I agree with Fumus' interpretation. Just in case you want a supporting opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:05:43-08:00","id":1006414,"title":"","content":"I know this has been asked elsewhere but I don't think a developer ever gave an answer to it. Can Totems grant their packs merits that bypass template-limitations or other prerequisites? Things like Supernatural merits or merits specific to other gamelines, for instance. I've been leaning towards bypassing prerequisites for merits werewolves (or whatever pack member type) can take otherwise, but not bypassing template restrictions, but want to know if there's been any official word on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 11-21-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:51:03-08:00","id":1006485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1006414#post1006414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this has been asked elsewhere but I don't think a developer ever gave an answer to it. Can Totems grant their packs merits that bypass template-limitations or other prerequisites? Things like Supernatural merits or merits specific to other gamelines, for instance. I've been leaning towards bypassing prerequisites for merits werewolves (or whatever pack member type) can take otherwise, but not bypassing template restrictions, but want to know if there's been any official word on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wind spirit giving telekinesis to it's pack seems thematic enough, since they can't give gift-facets or influences. Mundane merits are, in fact, harder to justify on average, like say, the resources merit. Or the contacts merit that isn't directly tied with some spirit court, etc - from a point of verisimilitude. How do you explain a mystic connection to suddenly know a given information broker?<br /> <br /> The corebook's seems to be left deliberately vague on those accounts, with only the outright exploitable traits being explicitly forbidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:32:12-08:00","id":1008078,"title":"","content":"Can werewolves use Fight Styles while they in Gauru-form (for 2ed)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:33:52-08:00","id":1008105,"title":"","content":"Relentless Assault and Tactical Shifting, yes. Anything else, I'd argue no. Maybe with some styles I'd consider on a successful control (Resolve + Composure) roll but I mean, neither the physical form nor the temperament of the Gauru is built for fine motor functions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:48:47-08:00","id":1008111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1008105#post1008105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relentless Assault and Tactical Shifting, yes. Anything else, I'd argue no. Maybe with some styles I'd consider on a successful control (Resolve + Composure) roll but I mean, neither the physical form nor the temperament of the Gauru is built <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">for fine motor functions.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds bad. Although, I disagree that they physically unable for<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> motor functions. After all, the\u043d have +1 to Dex and enhanced Defense. Is it described in book?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:53:33-08:00","id":1008114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1008105#post1008105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">neither the physical form nor the temperament of the Gauru is built for fine motor functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>They literally get a dexterity bonus. <br /> <br /> Anyway I'm pretty sure the &quot;no fighting styles in gauru&quot; was deliberately ditched because any restrictions that makes gauru worse in a fight are a no-no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:57:14-08:00","id":1008116,"title":"","content":"So, up to storyteller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:09:59-08:00","id":1008123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1008116#post1008116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, up to storyteller?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the sense that it's up to the storyteller if they want to house rule additional restrictions on the form. By the rules as written though, there is absolutely nothing stopping werewolves from using any fighting style they want in any form they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:43:55-08:00","id":1008148,"title":"","content":"I would probably say no if my players started trying to do boxing while they're in urhan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:51:06-08:00","id":1008152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1008148#post1008148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably say no if my players started trying to do boxing while they're in urhan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, fair point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> In any form with the necessary anatomy. No punching without fists, no holding weapons without opposable thumbs, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:57:19-08:00","id":1008158,"title":"","content":"Or martial arts, or light weapons style. I mean, there's no rules as written reason you can't use any fighting style in any form. Just feels like common sense to me. You get dexterity in Urhan too, but it's not a form meant for those kinds of maneuvers. Not so much about inherent dexterity as it is about how the body moves and how that translates to most fighting styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:27:58-08:00","id":1008173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1008158#post1008158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or martial arts, or light weapons style. I mean, there's no rules as written reason you can't use any fighting style in any form. Just feels like common sense to me. You get dexterity in Urhan too, but it's not a form meant for those kinds of maneuvers. Not so much about inherent dexterity as it is about how the body moves and how that translates to most fighting styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the styles Gauru stops make sense against enemies with styles. It will be like Underworld, where it wasn't a big deal for trained vampire to kill werewolf. I don't want them to be constantly humiliated in fight. And what actually changes in them so much? Their still have vertical body structure and prehensile limbs? OK, it couldn't works that way IRL, considering how they look on the arts, but... there is no special rules about their bodies, except of bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:28:08-08:00","id":1008174,"title":"","content":"At any rate, any style being available in Gauru is rules as intended. I think it was Azocazatrim who confirmed it shortly after release, I can dig up the quote if people want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:46:43-08:00","id":1008188,"title":"","content":"Nah I believe you. Doesn't square for me personally just based on optics on physiology, but like you said, definitely no rules written against it and as with all things, I can houserule it at my table. Hopefully the diversity of opinions have helped the question-asker find their own stance on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:54:19-08:00","id":1008196,"title":"","content":"Found the thread. It was a short one, but has a variety of opinions on the matter. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445934-fighting-style-in-gauru-ie-kung-fu-panda\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-kung-fu-panda</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T04:56:53-08:00","id":1008493,"title":"","content":"Yup. My answer now is the same as it was then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:35:56-08:00","id":1011297,"title":"","content":"How do Uratha actually get their deeds notices for renown?<br /> <br /> Do they have to summon a lune and tell them what they did? Or a Lune just descend from the sky when they do something worthy and after the werewolf explain it the lune says &quot;oh you cute little furry half-thing did good! Have some renown&quot;. Or it is like WoW and a beam of moonlight hits the player as soon a he does something renown worthy and renown is gained?<br /> <br /> I cant seem to find it on the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:25:03-08:00","id":1011310,"title":"","content":"I've always run it as the uratha has to go to a lune or a wolf spirit that follows the firstborn of their tribe and describe why that deed is worthy of a renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T21:13:50-08:00","id":1011363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1011297#post1011297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Uratha actually get their deeds notices for renown?<br /> <br /> Do they have to summon a lune and tell them what they did? Or a Lune just descend from the sky when they do something worthy and after the werewolf explain it the lune says &quot;oh you cute little furry half-thing did good! Have some renown&quot;. Or it is like WoW and a beam of moonlight hits the player as soon a he does something renown worthy and renown is gained?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can summon them to be sure, but odds are the lunes or Luna is going to hear about it, being the god of werewolves and spirits and nigh-omnipresent in their lives. I wouldn't expect it to happen instantly like in Warcraft. A lune would probably be more serious about carving the renown of the werewolf's deeds onto their soul. Or at least not as flippant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T20:12:11-08:00","id":1011807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1011297#post1011297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Uratha actually get their deeds notices for renown?<br /> <br /> Do they have to summon a lune and tell them what they did? Or a Lune just descend from the sky when they do something worthy and after the werewolf explain it the lune says &quot;oh you cute little furry half-thing did good! Have some renown&quot;. Or it is like WoW and a beam of moonlight hits the player as soon a he does something renown worthy and renown is gained?<br /> <br /> I cant seem to find it on the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunes tasked with granting renown have influences in that, and spirit senses can feel such things. A Rahulim can literally smell how pure you are, and if you're lacking recognition just as much as a fear spirit knows what phobias you have or had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:36:41-08:00","id":1012083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1011297#post1011297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Uratha actually get their deeds notices for renown?<br /> <br /> Do they have to summon a lune and tell them what they did? Or a Lune just descend from the sky when they do something worthy and after the werewolf explain it the lune says &quot;oh you cute little furry half-thing did good! Have some renown&quot;. Or it is like WoW and a beam of moonlight hits the player as soon a he does something renown worthy and renown is gained?<br /> <br /> I cant seem to find it on the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou can run it a few ways. I prefer the one where a Lune comes and stabs the character up with their new Renown carvings if it is particularly present in the area and notices them, but that otherwise you need to go call down a Lune - which you can do with Shadowcall, but you can also manage by a good bit of howling at the moon in the Shadow during the night, when at least a minor Lune may well come and have a look at who is trying to get their attention, then can pass a message up the chain to a heavy hitter with the ability to rewire the werewolf's Essence.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can just as viably run it that, when the werewolf buys the new Renown dot, the tendrils of the Renown brands coiling through their spirit just twist and dig further in a spasm of power, or even that it just gradually happens over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:34:00-08:00","id":1012133,"title":"","content":"I was toying with the idea that the first time the Urathas skin is touched by moonlight after doing something Renown-worthy, their brands update. The same thing happens to the Pure (much to their eternal irritation), except theirs come with searing pain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:34:12-08:00","id":1013386,"title":"","content":"Do wolf-blooded cause Lunacy when using Tells that allow for shapeshifting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:44:28-08:00","id":1013392,"title":"","content":"Yes. Not the one that turns them Urhan, but the others do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:24:11-08:00","id":1013424,"title":"","content":"Ok, because for Uratha, the simple act of shapeshifting itself, even to Urhan, causes Lunacy. Is this not the case with urhan-based wolf-blooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:28:18-08:00","id":1013428,"title":"","content":"Oh, you meant <i>as</i> they transform. Yeah, I think even the urhan one does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:44:59-08:00","id":1013478,"title":"","content":"Depending on how you run with it, it might cause a Breaking Point but not specifically Lunacy. Mortals often hit breaking points for witnessing the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:35:05-08:00","id":1017775,"title":"","content":"Even after reading through the corebook, I'm a little confused on the laws of spirits, how they come into being, eat and grow in power.<br /> <br /> From what I can tell, bigger emotional spirits devour smaller spirits generated from just people experiencing emotions, with the emotion they represent being the tastiest to them and branching out to concepts different from them being a product of desperation. Is that about right, or am I really misunderstanding it? And how do spirits of stuff that is not emotions - like spirits of Mountains - generate spirits to eat?<br /> <br /> And is it more likely to have an overall forest spirit representing all the animals and vegetation within a single grove or forest, a spirit for every single tree and bush, or both with the forest spirit being the leader of the latter? And what happens when you break apart a boulder big enough and important enough to the local mythology to have its own spirit? Does it just die, or does it becom a bunch of pebble spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:37:47-08:00","id":1017804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1017775#post1017775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even after reading through the corebook, I'm a little confused on the laws of spirits, how they come into being, eat and grow in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence flows through the Gauntlet. If it's not eaten, it becomes a spirit. Spirits devour more Essence with their Resonance and grow in power, providing they survive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I can tell, bigger emotional spirits devour smaller spirits generated from just people experiencing emotions, with the emotion they represent being the tastiest to them and branching out to concepts different from them being a product of desperation. Is that about right, or am I really misunderstanding it? And how do spirits of stuff that is not emotions - like spirits of Mountains - generate spirits to eat? </div> </div> </div>People experiencing emotions creates Essence of the Resonance of that emotion across the Gauntlet. Providing it's powerful enough. A moment's anger at noticing you accidentally tipped twenty instead of ten isn't necessarily going to be a feast for spirits. And they eat things more related to them. An anger spirit won't eat anything but anger Essence or spirits, unless it's crazed or being forced, as this will change its being. The exception is relative concepts. Anger can be associated with Fire, a spirit who is powerful enough that their Anger has tinges of that can also eat Fire Essence. 'Natural' spirits have an innate benefit with this. A fire spirit eats fire Essence, but it can also eat wood Essence, as fire devours wood, like a wolf spirit can eat a rabbit spirit. Emotion spirits don't usually have advantages like these, or at least they aren't as common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is it more likely to have an overall forest spirit representing all the animals and vegetation within a single grove or forest, a spirit for every single tree and bush, or both with the forest spirit being the leader of the latter? </div> </div> </div>The last, you'd generally have a hierarchy. A forest spirit of that forest, with individual animal, vegetation and even locational spirits that offer it tithes of Essence. Every tree and bush generates its own Essence, just not always enough to awaken its own spirit, so they would remain dormant or just weak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what happens when you break apart a boulder big enough and important enough to the local mythology to have its own spirit? Does it just die, or does it becom a bunch of pebble spirits? </div> </div> </div>Depending on how powerful it would be it might cling to one special shard of that boulder. It might find another way out. It might just wither and go dormant. It might not have survived the breaking process, as that might be reflected in the spirit as rock-breaking tool spirits destroying the boulder spirit. If the spirit is just a weak spirit of that boulder, it's not going to have that boulder Essence to survive, and will go dormant or get eaten up. But if it's important to local mythology it probably has more power to it and with that some agency.<br /> <br /> A lot of these are variable for plot elements. What happens if John goes out and kills someone? He goes to jail. But maybe he doesn't, and he kills another, and another. Maybe someone covers it up. Maybe that person comes back to life. Same with spirits. That broken boulder spirit might decide it's going to cross the Gauntlet and start haunting the place, or be captured by a human shaman and used to wreak vengeance on its destroyers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-15-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:27:04-08:00","id":1017943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1017804#post1017804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emotion spirits don't usually have advantages like these, or at least they aren't as common.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fear leads to anger, anger leads to hate, hate leads to suffering&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T23:35:23-08:00","id":1017982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1017775#post1017775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even after reading through the corebook, I'm a little confused on the laws of spirits, how they come into being, eat and grow in power.<br /> And what happens when you break apart a boulder big enough and important enough to the local mythology to have its own spirit? Does it just die, or does it becom a bunch of pebble spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some spirits are actually only awakened by the destruction of their earthly reflection so by destroying the boulder you could have wakened a dormant spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T04:49:00-08:00","id":1018025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1017982#post1017982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some spirits are actually only awakened by the destruction of their earthly reflection so by destroying the boulder you could have wakened a dormant spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ooooo, now that's cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:33:42-08:00","id":1020275,"title":"","content":"1. What is so &quot;dark&quot; about the Shadow? Seems like an innocuous enough ecosystem. What is it that makes spirits so desperate to leave, and so dangerous-feeling for visitors?<br /> 2. It seems that there are swarms of spirits crossing into the physical realm, not counting riding and claiming and all that. Riders and Claimers have obviously crossed a line, becoming monstrous, but what about unattached spirits? Are they just hunted when they become annoying or when they trespass, or is there a line they too can cross in which they become something fundamentally unnatural that werewolves would feel gut-level revulsion for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:16:48-08:00","id":1020303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020275#post1020275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What is so &quot;dark&quot; about the Shadow? Seems like an innocuous enough ecosystem. What is it that makes spirits so desperate to leave, and so dangerous-feeling for visitors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of Essence makes spirits want to leave. A source of anger is not always available, fires go out in the real world, seasons change, and sometimes spirits don't want to go dormant, sometimes they just want more, plus during the daytime Helios makes things oppressive and hard to go about your normal busniess. Visitors are a source of Essence, so it's like walking into a tiger den with a steak suit, alternatively you can be a new mode of travel as your soul is subdued and the spirit possesses you. As for what makes it 'dark' there's everything being an overt predator except the few things that aren't, which are manipulative enough to be slavers or just decide to wear you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. It seems that there are swarms of spirits crossing into the physical realm, not counting riding and claiming and all that. Riders and Claimers have obviously crossed a line, becoming monstrous, but what about unattached spirits? Are they just hunted when they become annoying or when they trespass, or is there a line they too can cross in which they become something fundamentally unnatural that werewolves would feel gut-level revulsion for? </div> </div> </div>Offhand I wouldn't say werewolves feel a gut-level revulsion to spirits outside of perhaps wound-spirits and maybe, maybe magath. Some spirits, even ones that Ride or Claim people, are left alone. But completely unattached spirits are unlikely, at least for a lengthy period of time, if only due to the fact that they need to attach themselves to something before they start bleeding Essence. If a spirit did decide to just jump across every day, eat some Essence, and jump back without actively harming people, it might point this out while werewolves are bearing down on it. Some might leave it alone, some might destroy it, some might make a bargain.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are individuals and have differing opinions about things and ways to handle them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:30:23-08:00","id":1020312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020303#post1020303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like walking into a tiger den with a steak suit, alternatively you can be a new mode of travel as your soul is subdued and the spirit possesses you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I feel the chill up my spine when thinking about it now that I thought should be there but wasn't<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020303#post1020303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But completely unattached spirits are unlikely, at least for a lengthy period of time, if only due to the fact that they need to attach themselves to something before they start bleeding Essence. If a spirit did decide to just jump across every day, eat some Essence.....</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm mistaken, and there are NOT swarms of unattached spirits in the physical world. Do the many opportunists that come across at thin places just hang around for awhile then go home then, for the most part?<br /> <br /> 3. How can I pass essence to a spirit? Do I just will it to happen, or carry around little ziplock bags of it, or do I have to bring them to a source or make a source for them to feed off of?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:38:44-08:00","id":1020317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020312#post1020312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I feel the chill up my spine when thinking about it now that I thought should be there but wasn't</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I'm mistaken, and there are NOT swarms of unattached spirits in the physical world. Do the many opportunists that come across at thin places just hang around for awhile then go home then, for the most part? </div> </div> </div>Most of them that come across know they don't belong, and are likely to find a source of Essence as fast as possible and make it last as long as they can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. How can I pass essence to a spirit? Do I just will it to happen, or carry around little ziplock bags of it, or do I have to bring them to a source or make a source for them to feed off of? </div> </div> </div>Will it to happen, or more exactly allow the spirit to reap the Essence. Sometimes you might be asked to make a source of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:59:33-08:00","id":1020366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020317#post1020317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of them that come across know they don't belong, and are likely to find a source of Essence as fast as possible and make it last as long as they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning someone to ride, urge or claim. Free-ranging breeze spirits, or babbling brook spirits getting essence from the environment would be vanishingly rare, then?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:02:01-08:00","id":1020423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1020366#post1020366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaning someone to ride, urge or claim. Free-ranging breeze spirits, or babbling brook spirits getting essence from the environment would be vanishingly rare, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, most of those would just be in the Shadow, eating Essence that's filtered through the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Once you cross the Gauntlet, you start losing Essence, and things like breezes won't always be there to feed you unless you start using Influences, which is even more of a drain on your power. So you would Fetter yourself to something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:30:40-08:00","id":1022372,"title":"","content":"auspice renown gives auspice gift dots<br /> what does tribe renown serve for?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:58:00-08:00","id":1022379,"title":"","content":"Nothing except to give some insight into a Tribe's priorities. There used to be a mechanic in place where you roll dice based on a werewolf's Tribal renown to see if you had heard of them or their reputation, which I've considered using but haven't actually put into action. I've been using the difference between Tribal renown as a flat bonus to interacting with Tribe mates, which I believe was also a 1e mechanic. (Ex: A Hunter in Darkness with 4 Purity would get a +2 bonus to social rolls against/with a HiD with 2 Purity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:21:08-08:00","id":1022621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1022372#post1022372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">auspice renown gives auspice gift dots<br /> what does tribe renown serve for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tribe renown aren't anything special mechanically after you finish character creation. Auspice renown give a dot of the moon gift and a shadow or wolf gift facet, any other renown gives a shadow or wolf gift facet. Whether or not it's a tribe renown doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T23:06:51-08:00","id":1022628,"title":"","content":"Yeah, mechanically it gives you starting Renown and, thus, Gifts. In-game it says something about the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T23:37:50-08:00","id":1022637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1022628#post1022628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, mechanically it gives you starting Renown and, thus, Gifts. In-game it says something about the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And these two things are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/491309-your-werewolf-starter-kit-2e-facet-baselines?p=491418#post491418\">not unrelated</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:02:21-08:00","id":1024097,"title":"","content":"I feel as though I'm struggling with some of the basics of being a werewolf. I've finished the sections of the book detailing the Uratha condition, but certain things are still a jumble.<br /> <br /> So, by following the character creation chapter word-for-word, I end up with a pack of Uratha that are a little more experienced than someone freshly Changed; they've got some training and cool abilities to go along with their turf.<br /> <br /> Given that, I've got some questions relating to how my character does his duty:<br /> <br /> <b>Scenario 1</b><br /> <br /> a. My werewolf is walking down the street, and approaches a spirit in Twilight (which means that the spirit is in the physical realm, but not manifested?); can he just <i>see</i> it, regardless of form or senses being used? Can he <i>do</i> anything to it without it manifesting or some special ability being activated? Does the spirit instantly know he is a werewolf?<br /> <br /> b. Same werewolf, same street, but this time he approaches a human who is being ridden (urged = influenced from across the Gauntlet, ridden = sort of possessed, but not fully claimed?); does he just <i>know</i>? If not, how does he go about verifying?<br /> <br /> c. The werewolf approaches a werewolf/vampire/mage; does he just <i>know </i>what they are? Do the latter two know what he is?<br /> <br /> <b>Scenario 2</b><br /> <br /> a. Something is causing trouble in my werewolf's territory; how does he find out about it? Without gifts/rites, does he just have to patrol around and ask questions?<br /> <br /> b. The thing is an Azlu/Beshilu; how does the werewolf find out? These enemies being what they are, I don't imagine they will do anything overt unless they have no choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12810-coronablue","name":"CoronaBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:25:46-08:00","id":1024104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoronaBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024097#post1024097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that, I've got some questions relating to how my character does his duty:</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a. My werewolf is walking down the street, and approaches a spirit in Twilight (which means that the spirit is in the physical realm, but not manifested?); </div> </div> </div>Technically it's Manifested, just in Twilight Form. This is covered in the Manifestations section down on p286. Every spirit has the Twilight Form Manifestation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can he just <i>see</i> it, regardless of form or senses being used? </div> </div> </div>Yes, unless it's hiding. P95, 'The werewolf does not need to focus in order to sense spirits in Twilight. Unless the spirit is intentionally trying to hide, Uratha sense spirits in Twilight as well as they would manifested.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can he <i>do</i> anything to it without it manifesting or some special ability being activated? </div> </div> </div>He could activate any sense abilities. An Ithaeur could use Shadow Gaze to learn the spirit's bane. A creature's bane will hurt them even in Twilight. Otherwise it's hard to hit things in Twilight, you generally need a special ability, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the spirit instantly know he is a werewolf?[ </div> </div> </div>Good question, I'd say no, offhand. Things in Twilight tend to notice when they're noticed, however, and that might get attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b. Same werewolf, same street, but this time he approaches a human who is being ridden (urged = influenced from across the Gauntlet, ridden = sort of possessed, but not fully claimed?); does he just <i>know</i>? If not, how does he go about verifying? </div> </div> </div>A Ridden has the spirit Fettered to someone or something, using the Fetter Manifestation. It's in Twilight in the real world and would be seen as the previous one, unless it made an attempt to hide. Urged seem to be a 'kind' of Ridden. The spirit is still outside, riding them. Claimed have them on the inside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> c. The werewolf approaches a werewolf/vampire/mage; does he just <i>know </i>what they are? Do the latter two know what he is? </div> </div> </div>Miles may vary. I'm pretty sure werewolves recognize werewolves. Vampires can be pretty distinctive unless they're using Blush of Life. They also tend to have a lot of identifiers a perceptive werewolf might note, for instance, their 'breath' smells of blood. But some werewolves might not know vampires exist and think they're some sort of zombie or revenant or host. I generally have werewolves notice vampires unless they go to great lengths to hide themselves, and vampires tend to notice werewolves as another predator but not necessarily what unless they have experience with werewolves. The vampire book says this on p92, 'When Kindred notice werewolves, they feel physiological responses they never otherwise experience, such as goose pimples along their arms, and chills down their backs. They feel the adrenaline surge in the pit of the stomach that humans associate with danger and tense excitement.' Mages look like normal people, I don't think they'd just recognize one off the bat. It's worth noting that there are Gifts werewolves have and spells Mages do that would let them identify or note something off about someone.<br /> <br /> But you can run it with everyone recognizing everyone else or not recognizing everyone else without the game being broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a. Something is causing trouble in my werewolf's territory; how does he find out about it? Without gifts/rites, does he just have to patrol around and ask questions? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Gifts and rites help, but if you don't have any of those, you just have enhanced senses and socializing. If you're on better term with spirits, some of them would likely have noticed trouble being caused. Otherwise you'd look to the human world, with the help of the werewolf's immediate and extended pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b. The thing is an Azlu/Beshilu; how does the werewolf find out? These enemies being what they are, I don't imagine they will do anything overt unless they have no choice. </div> </div> </div>They can generally only stay riding a human-looking body for so long before it starts mutating into a spider-monster or rat-man. In that time if they encountered a werewolf the werewolf might think they were the walking dead, like a vampire. Presumably some experienced werewolves would recognize the scent of rats or other little things that could point towards it, like blood from an ear.<br /> <br /> Azlu and Beshilu aren't stupid, but they are obsessed. They can't really help themselves when it comes to some things, similar to a werewolf and 'the hunt,' but taken up a notch. With that it's noting overly aggressive rats or deaths by spider bites, a fight or flight response, atmospheric changes like a thickening or hollowing of the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Obviously there's Gifts that help with these. Scent of the Unnatural, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:44:41-08:00","id":1024108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoronaBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024097#post1024097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a. My werewolf is walking down the street, and approaches a spirit in Twilight (which means that the spirit is in the physical realm, but not manifested?); can he just <i>see</i> it, regardless of form or senses being used? Can he <i>do</i> anything to it without it manifesting or some special ability being activated? Does the spirit instantly know he is a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>He can sense it regardless of form, but unless he's got an honorary Rank high enough to qualify as its bane he'll have to resort to Gifts or rites or fetishes to attack it without engaging with the same methods mortals use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b. Same werewolf, same street, but this time he approaches a human who is being ridden (urged = influenced from across the Gauntlet, ridden = sort of possessed, but not fully claimed?); does he just <i>know</i>? If not, how does he go about verifying? </div> </div> </div>Depending on how large the spirit is, he might be able to outright spot an urging or possessing spirit (urging is like constant low-level possession where the spirit is Fettered to the target and maintains some influence over their host, in contrast to the temporary overt takeover of full Possession; &quot;Ridden&quot; is a werewolf umbrella term for &quot;a spirit is manifesting through this creature&quot;) on the periphery of its host body, but otherwise you need to be hunting a target under the blessing of a Storm Lord's Sacred Hunt to be able to spot a spirit controlling somebody from within.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> c. The werewolf approaches a werewolf/vampire/mage; does he just <i>know </i>what they are? Do the latter two know what he is? </div> </div> </div>The vampire almost assuredly hasn't got the bit of insurance active that stops them from evincing signs of deadness to heightened senses \u2014 no heartbeat is a bit of a dead giveaway, and it normally costs to keep that up. The werewolf is going to need to be fairly close and it'll take wolf senses to be sure, but it's otherwise straightforward. The mage is going to require a Gift to spot unless they're actively magicking it up.<br /> <br /> As for the opposite direction, the mage is going to notice if he activates a Gift or changes shape anywhere near him and will certainly notice something's odd about him if they happen to look at him through the Sight, but nothing about just being a werewolf automatically pings the default supernatural senses of a mage. The vampire has no inherent benefit to spotting his magical nature, but unless he lives a weirdly bloodless life as a hunter between the worlds of spirit and flesh he's probably going to catch the interest of the monster that can smell any traces of his last kill that he missed during cleanup. The werewolf has the same limits as he does going the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a. Something is causing trouble in my werewolf's territory; how does he find out about it? Without gifts/rites, does he just have to patrol around and ask questions? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b. The thing is an Azlu/Beshilu; how does the werewolf find out? These enemies being what they are, I don't imagine they will do anything overt unless they have no choice. </div> </div> </div>Changes in Gauntlet density can be registered by their impact on spirit senses and can readily influence the spiritual ecosystem, particularly given that the archetypes of Host complications are &quot;rats chewing through the otherwise-solid wall between worlds in a city&quot; and &quot;spiderwebs gumming up the interface around a locus.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:51:19-08:00","id":1024141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024104#post1024104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Technically it's Manifested, just in Twilight Form. This is covered in the Manifestations section down on p286. Every spirit has the Twilight Form Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see my misconception about Manifestation, and being ridden now.<br /> <br /> In the section covering Influence and Manifestation, the book states that a spirit can cause the Open condition via Strengthen Influence, or an Extended Action. However, I can't find any mention of what roll that action requires, just the number of scenes that it takes. Does the spirit simply have to hang around the source of Resonance for a number of scenes, or have I missed something?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024104#post1024104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miles may vary. I'm pretty sure werewolves recognize werewolves. Vampires can be pretty distinctive unless they're using Blush of Life. They also tend to have a lot of identifiers a perceptive werewolf might note, for instance, their 'breath' smells of blood. But some werewolves might not know vampires exist and think they're some sort of zombie or revenant or host. I generally have werewolves notice vampires unless they go to great lengths to hide themselves, and vampires tend to notice werewolves as another predator but not necessarily what unless they have experience with werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024108#post1024108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vampire almost assuredly hasn't got the bit of insurance active that stops them from evincing signs of deadness to heightened senses \u2014 no heartbeat is a bit of a dead giveaway, and it normally costs to keep that up. The werewolf is going to need to be fairly close and it'll take wolf senses to be sure, but it's otherwise straightforward.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I take it that, like many things, whether or not the signs of vampirism are overt enough to be noticed in passing is determined by what else is going on in the scene? For example, would wolf senses automatically detect blood on the breath of a vampire who has just fed, assuming the vampire has not taken some precaution and there are no other intense smells in the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12810-coronablue","name":"CoronaBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:18:06-08:00","id":1024163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoronaBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1024141#post1024141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the section covering Influence and Manifestation, the book states that a spirit can cause the Open condition via Strengthen Influence, or an Extended Action. However, I can't find any mention of what roll that action requires, just the number of scenes that it takes. Does the spirit simply have to hang around the source of Resonance for a number of scenes, or have I missed something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence is Power + Finesse. I believe the extended action is talking about just hanging around and working in concert. Certain rituals would probably do it, I imagine that's what it's calling back to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I take it that, like many things, whether or not the signs of vampirism are overt enough to be noticed in passing is determined by what else is going on in the scene? For example, would wolf senses automatically detect blood on the breath of a vampire who has just fed, assuming the vampire has not taken some precaution and there are no other intense smells in the area? </div> </div> </div>Provided they were using their wolf senses, sure. That is something the player would have to note. In human form their senses are top notch but still human. Beyond that, it should depend on things. If your werewolf is walking into a busy club full of dancing people and there's a vampire who just drank on the other side of the room, they wouldn't exactly stick out like a sore thumb just based on the senses. There would probably be the scent of blood from various small cuts and other explanations. But if a werewolf and vampire met each other in an otherwise empty room and neither were distracted by anything else, they would probably notice something was up near instantly, though not necessarily what. Vampires look dead, without the use of Blush of Life. They don't have a heartbeat, they have no pulse, no sweat or other natural body odors. They're pale, they're slightly below room temperature. If the werewolf didn't know about vampires it would be easy to think it was a zombie. Blush of Life, an ability vampires in Requiem have that lets them fake life better, puts them at normal human levels. They gain a heartbeat, pulse, they fake all the bodily fluids and everything else. There's where you would have to rely on other things, and wolf senses are really powerful and could probably notice a vampire close to them who has just fed.<br /> <br /> I forget where in the fluff but Solomon Birch, a fairly powerful vampire, has remarked that a lot of vampires don't brush their teeth. While they wouldn't get gum disease or anything, it would probably lead to some nasty breath after years of putting nothing but blood into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:29:21-08:00","id":1028963,"title":"","content":"Hello All,<br /> <br /> I'm still on my first read through of WtF 2E and I've just looked through the section tackling the Pure. There's a passage spoken by an Uratha's on page 198 where they speak of the Pure Tribes various Ban's are these Ban's accurate or is it purely based on the narrators assumptions so could be misleading?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7354-monsieurcutts","name":"MonsieurCutts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:48:58-08:00","id":1028969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonsieurCutts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1028963#post1028963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello All,<br /> <br /> I'm still on my first read through of WtF 2E and I've just looked through the section tackling the Pure. There's a passage spoken by an Uratha's on page 198 where they speak of the Pure Tribes various Ban's are these Ban's accurate or is it purely based on the narrators assumptions so could be misleading?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fluff bits are interpretations of the bans, but you can interpret them differently with the actual wordings which we haven't gotten for 2e yet as far as I am aware (though they might not have changed at all), but the 1e bans are:<br /> Fire-touched - Let not a false statement lay unchallenged.<br /> Ivory Claws - Call no whelp of lesser blood your brother or sister.<br /> Predator Kings - Touch not a thing made by human hands, lest to destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T18:41:15-08:00","id":1031409,"title":"","content":"I can't remember the exact date, but maybe a year (?) or so back, one of the writers posted rules for converting lupus/wolfborn into Forsaken. Anyone have a link to said conversion? It was either on the forums or the blogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T19:26:46-08:00","id":1031423,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">This blog maybe?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T20:47:35-08:00","id":1031441,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that was it. Thank you!<br /> <br /> If anyone knows of other Forsaken lupus homebrews, please point me in their direction. Was always one of my favorite concepts to explore in WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:29:45-08:00","id":1031665,"title":"","content":"Some strange rule readings came up in my last game in regard to spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do Werewolves to lethal to spirits, and then agg if they're higher in honorary rank? Or is it bashing (as all other things do) and lethal if higher in honorary rank? I believe the passage in the book just says 'devastating damage' to spirits lower in rank, and never specifically mentions werewolves doing lethal to spirits normally.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, does the Ithaeur ability Spirit Howl force all spirits lower in rank to run? Or just lower ranked spirits that aren't hostile?<br /> <br /> My impression was that it made spirits lower in level run no matter what, and then it lowered the defense of those who stay around (due to being equal or higher in level, and hostile) by Wisdom. But my GM disagrees so I just want to make sure I've been running it right in my own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:53:06-08:00","id":1031679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1031665#post1031665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Werewolves to lethal to spirits, and then agg if they're higher in honorary rank? Or is it bashing (as all other things do) and lethal if higher in honorary rank? I believe the passage in the book just says 'devastating damage' to spirits lower in rank, and never specifically mentions werewolves doing lethal to spirits normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bashing with punches, guns, weapons, claws, and teeth. Their teeth normally do Lethal to things that reduce all but supernatural attacks to Lethal,but that doesn't seem to be the case in spirit's point, who don't reduce the damage or take Lethal from supernatural. Aggravated if they are sufficiently higher in rank. I believe the 'devastating' line is referring to the honorary rank bane aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, does the Ithaeur ability Spirit Howl force all spirits lower in rank to run? Or just lower ranked spirits that aren't hostile?<br /> <br /> My impression was that it made spirits lower in level run no matter what, and then it lowered the defense of those who stay around (due to being equal or higher in level, and hostile) by Wisdom. But my GM disagrees so I just want to make sure I've been running it right in my own games. </div> </div> </div>'Spirits of lower Rank than the werewolf flee the area, hide, or go dormant, while more powerful spirits avoid the werewolf out of deference. Spirits that are actively allied with the werewolf's pack or tribal totem might even come to his aid, though the Ithaeur shouldn't ever count on that. Only spirits that are outright hostile to the pack do not show deference, though their Defense is penalized by the werewolf's Wisdom Renown.'<br /> <br /> The last line, I imagine, refers to the higher ranked spirits that did not flee. It seems while it doesn't force all lower ranks to run, it would force them to react as if a really scary werewolf was coming into town. Allied ones might come to you, but, like it says, that's not a sure thing. I'd certainly have lower rank spirits run, hide or go dormant, as that's what it says they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Changed, Charlaquin's got it right. 01-14-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:56:48-08:00","id":1031680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1031665#post1031665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Werewolves to lethal to spirits, and then agg if they're higher in honorary rank? Or is it bashing (as all other things do) and lethal if higher in honorary rank? I believe the passage in the book just says 'devastating damage' to spirits lower in rank, and never specifically mentions werewolves doing lethal to spirits normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither. Werewolves' teeth and claws normally do lethal damage, so they do bashing damage to materialized spirits and spirits in the <i>hisil</i>, and can't damage spirits in Twilight. If the werewolf's Honorary Rank is at least 2 dots higher than the spirit's Rank, their teeth and claws are treated as a Bane to the spirit, and accordingly deal aggravated damage to it, and can even do so when it is in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T02:14:55-08:00","id":1032550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1031680#post1031680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither. Werewolves' teeth and claws normally do lethal damage, so they do bashing damage to materialized spirits and spirits in the <i>hisil</i>, and can't damage spirits in Twilight. If the werewolf's Honorary Rank is at least 2 dots higher than the spirit's Rank, their teeth and claws are treated as a Bane to the spirit, and accordingly deal aggravated damage to it, and can even do so when it is in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Keep in mind that even Bashing damage is capable of discorporating spirits, the difference between damages is how long they take to become active again, and specially with Aggravated, the loss of essence and the potential to outright destroy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T03:07:04-08:00","id":1033250,"title":"","content":"Don't banes only deal lethal to non-materialised twilight spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:53:53-08:00","id":1033329,"title":"","content":"Yes, Twilight seems to dull the pain a bit. Aggravated to Materialized beings or beings in their home plane. Lethal to Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:08:16-08:00","id":1033422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1032550#post1032550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. Keep in mind that even Bashing damage is capable of discorporating spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into bursts of ephemera stylized to their natures </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:21:52-08:00","id":1033434,"title":"","content":"Bashing damage would roll over. Once you're full of Bashing wounds, you start taking Lethal wounds, even from a Bashing weapon. The same as how an unarmed person can kill someone, even though they're only capable of inflicting Bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:31:29-08:00","id":1034289,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is a simple question, but it would at least have a short answer.<br /> <br /> Since going into the Shadow converts your body into Essence while you're there, what kind of Essence are Werewolves in the Shadow made of? Sacred Hunt essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:38:45-08:00","id":1034295,"title":"","content":"I think it's ephemera, not Essence.<br /> <br /> Edit: As in, you transform into ephemera, not Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:02:36-08:00","id":1034306,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ephemera. If you ate one it would be primarily Essence of the Hunt, though, with other Resonances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:47:55-08:00","id":1034322,"title":"","content":"Damn, now I want to start a thread to debate what kind of Essence different creatures and splats would provide if eaten by a Spirit in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> That said, does that mean that only Hunt and Hunt-related spirits would try to eat them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:03:34-08:00","id":1034399,"title":"","content":"No, there's plenty of other things that might. Death, rot, scavenger, rat, wolf, entropy, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Obviously werewolves benefit a lot from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-18-2017, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:55:16-08:00","id":1034540,"title":"","content":"why would rat spirits eat them? I mean, unless you're talking about the rat hosts<br /> <br /> (P.S. I wish there were some non-plague and greed-related rat beings in CoD. Like a Rat Spirit of Family Togetherness or Cleverness)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:52:21-08:00","id":1034601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1034540#post1034540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why would rat spirits eat them? I mean, unless you're talking about the rat hosts</div> </div> </div> </div>Scavengers who would eat the dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (P.S. I wish there were some non-plague and greed-related rat beings in CoD. Like a Rat Spirit of Family Togetherness or Cleverness) </div> </div> </div>There are. At least cleverness. Luck's probably common in the east. I can't imagine how a rat would symbolize family togetherness enough to warrant being a spirit of it without really stretching. The Lodge of the Grotto has Pale Rat, among others, as a potential totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-19-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:15:20-08:00","id":1034611,"title":"","content":"Rats in the wild outside cities have very loving, close and matriarchial families, plus pet rats are very empathetic to their owners (like, dog levels and above) if treated well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:05:34-08:00","id":1035224,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves 'purify' the essance they take in so that any spirit can consume it without risk of being altered by it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:41:35-08:00","id":1035246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1035224#post1035224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves 'purify' the essance they take in so that any spirit can consume it without risk of being altered by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so. This is why spirits, not counting totems, won't usually ask for Essence so much as ask for you to do something that creates Essence for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:46:53-08:00","id":1036064,"title":"","content":"Does the essence a werewolf is currently holding have an efffect on it's personality? Like, say a werewolf filled up on murder essence to give him the power to cleanse a harmful loci. Would he be more violent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:09:10-08:00","id":1036074,"title":"","content":"It's never really stated, but that sounds like a fun idea. <br /> <br /> Not that it's all that noticeable in the case of something like violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:50:36-08:00","id":1036093,"title":"","content":"yeah. but in the case of an Iron Master who usually hunts through exposing corruption, with murder when necessary, it might be noticable, as violence starts becoming Plan A more often until he gets more balanced Essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:00:20-08:00","id":1036098,"title":"","content":"It would only be temporary, I think. They'd be a bit quicker to anger for a couple of days but eventually the resonance would bleed off and they'd settle back to normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:22:09-08:00","id":1036149,"title":"","content":"that's reasonable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:31:35-08:00","id":1036191,"title":"","content":"There's an optional system in one of the Chronicles books that offers some mechanics for increasing the effect Essence has on werewolves, I recall mention of a werewolf who takes down the spirit of a bulldozer growing a yellowish complexion and a broader jaw. I believe these changes are just temporary, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:42:19-08:00","id":1036229,"title":"","content":"ooooooooooooh that is sooo cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:34:16-08:00","id":1036330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1036191#post1036191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an optional system in one of the Chronicles books that offers some mechanics for increasing the effect Essence has on werewolves, I recall mention of a werewolf who takes down the spirit of a bulldozer growing a yellowish complexion and a broader jaw. I believe these changes are just temporary, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the Spirit Predation hack, which notably also uses some of the same concepts that made it into the Sacred Hunt and provides a non-idigam-based origin for Su'ur.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Resonance can often be abstracted to the symbolic markers of like-attracts-like and you-are-what-you-eat. The special-effects and other narrative elements that signify the generation of Essence are themed in a manner appropriate to their Resonance \u2014 balanced Harmony can mitigate some of the more overt manifestations, but generally speaking a werewolf that gets most of their Essence from drawing it out of a particular variety of locus is going to be at least a little visibly different from less particular Uratha.<br /> <br /> That goes double for spirits, obviously, but the nature of Rank means most Shadow-nobles aren't too monofocused and tend to reorient themselves as part of regular ecological/economic activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T20:34:40-08:00","id":1036420,"title":"","content":"This might have been mentioned somewhere else but I couldn't find it on the forum. I was planning a host antagonist for my group but when I was looking up their rules it didn't say how much essence they should get. The examples the book gives has one with four essence and the other one has twenty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12379-zithpith","name":"Zithpith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T20:48:41-08:00","id":1036424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zithpith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1036420#post1036420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been mentioned somewhere else but I couldn't find it on the forum. I was planning a host antagonist for my group but when I was looking up their rules it didn't say how much essence they should get. The examples the book gives has one with four essence and the other one has twenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually seems about right, considering what first edition says.<br /> <br /> From Predators, 'Azarath begin with 3 to 5 Essence, but grew accordingly powerful (at the Storyteller's discretion) very quickly as they consume other Azlu. There's technically no upper limit to the amoutn of power an Azlu can have - a single, sufficiently old and scarred Spider Host can challenge an entire pack of werewolves. For such creatures, anywhere from 20 to 50 Essence is feasible, depending on just how monstrous the creature needs to be.'<br /> <br /> And, 'The Beshilu tend to have very high Essence scores, at least compared to the Uratha.'<br /> <br /> They seem to be made pretty fast and loose. I'd expect them to have more comprehensive rules if there was a new book about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-22-2017, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T00:19:36-08:00","id":1037073,"title":"","content":"Where does it say how many Gifts you have unlocked at character creation? I don't mean Facets, but actual Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:58:52-08:00","id":1037144,"title":"","content":"It's 3 if you have a tribe, 2 for ghost wolves. You get your moon gift, an affinity gift from your auspice and an affinity gift from your tribe if you have it. The third/fourth facet is either the second moon facet or a wolf facet, which don't need to be unlocked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:40:07-08:00","id":1037160,"title":"","content":"cahalith sleep for prophetic reasons but do werewolves require sleep for biological reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:45:10-08:00","id":1037164,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:46:53-08:00","id":1037167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037144#post1037144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's 3 if you have a tribe, 2 for ghost wolves. You get your moon gift, an affinity gift from your auspice and an affinity gift from your tribe if you have it. The third/fourth facet is either the second moon facet or a wolf facet, which don't need to be unlocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that? I can find where it says Wolf Gifts are unlocked, and your Auspice Gift is unlocked, but nothing about Shadow Gifts being unlocked at character creation. Just Facets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:52:17-08:00","id":1037170,"title":"","content":"Character Creation -&gt; Add Forsaken Template -&gt; Gifts and Rites (p. 83):<br /> <br /> &quot;Your character receives the first dot of a Moon Gift according to her auspice. She also receives a Facet of two Shadow Gifts from her tribe or auspice. If she has two dots in her auspice\u2019s Renown, she gains the second-dot Facet of that Moon Gift. Otherwise, she gains a facet of a Wolf Gift. Your character can\u2019t take a Facet of a Gift in which she has no dots of Renown.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:06:31-08:00","id":1037180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037170#post1037170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character Creation -&gt; Add Forsaken Template -&gt; Gifts and Rites (p. 83):<br /> <br /> &quot;Your character receives the first dot of a Moon Gift according to her auspice. She also receives a Facet of two Shadow Gifts from her tribe or auspice. If she has two dots in her auspice\u2019s Renown, she gains the second-dot Facet of that Moon Gift. Otherwise, she gains a facet of a Wolf Gift. Your character can\u2019t take a Facet of a Gift in which she has no dots of Renown.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That talks about how many Facets you get, but not how many Shadow Gifts are unlocked at character creation.<ul><li>No Shadow Gifts are unlocked, but you have two Facets in locked Gifts (extremely unlikely).</li> <li>All Tribe / Auspice Shadow Gifts are unlocked, but you only start with two Facets.</li> <li>Only Shadow Gifts you choose your starting Facets in are unlocked.</li> </ul>\u200bBut I... can't find anything that says which of those is true.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:09:18-08:00","id":1037181,"title":"","content":"If you have a facet of a shadow gift, it's unlocked.<br /> <br /> If you don't, it's locked. <br /> <br /> It's really not that complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:37:50-08:00","id":1037195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037181#post1037181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a facet of a shadow gift, it's unlocked.<br /> If you don't, it's locked.<br /> It's really not that complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>What page number did you find this on? I'm still trying to find it.<br /> Page 83 (Gift and Rites) talks about Facets, but not what Shadow Gifts are unlocked at character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:45:00-08:00","id":1037197,"title":"","content":"&quot;Unlocking a Shadow Gift costs 5 Experiences, or 3 if it is favored by auspice or tribe. Once it is acquired, the Uratha gains a single Facet within that Gift immediately.&quot;<br /> Page 115<br /> <br /> Since it's impossible to unlock Shadow Gifts without having Facets in them it stands to reason that Gifts without Facets are locked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:52:37-08:00","id":1037202,"title":"","content":"It's not actually stated anywhere. It's just that it not working that way would be unspeakably stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:04:36-08:00","id":1037212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037197#post1037197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Unlocking a Shadow Gift costs 5 Experiences, or 3 if it is favored by auspice or tribe. Once it is acquired, the Uratha gains a single Facet within that Gift immediately.&quot;<br /> Page 115<br /> <br /> Since it's impossible to unlock Shadow Gifts without having Facets in them it stands to reason that Gifts without Facets are locked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes logical sense, and gives me a page number to work with. Thank you, that helps a great deal!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:06:11-08:00","id":1037214,"title":"","content":"In character creation, mechanically if you are the type who worries about something possibly costing more Experiences later in the game, you would benefit from picking facets from two different Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:33:04-08:00","id":1037233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037214#post1037214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In character creation, mechanically if you are the type who worries about something possibly costing more Experiences later in the game, you would benefit from picking facets from two different Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have a choice. In two different places it specifies &quot;a facet of two shadow gifts&quot; (pg83), and 'choose one facet each of two shadow gifts&quot; (pg84).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:21:18-08:00","id":1037896,"title":"","content":"Can Werewolves damage Strix with their teeth when Strix are in their natural form which shrugs off almost all damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:31:14-08:00","id":1037901,"title":"","content":"Hard to say. The predator's bane usually goes through effects that lower damage. So if I'm a tough guy who reduces Lethal to Bashing, it still does Lethal. But for the strix, they don't really get injured without special powers.<br /> <br /> 'Injury is an extremely rare sensation for a Strix. They are completely immune to all physical and ephemeral attacks except for Disciplines and Devotions that inflict aggravated damage, which inflict Bashing wounds on them instead. Some banes inflict injury as well, notably sunlight and fire if the Strix is unable to escape.'<br /> <br /> Just based on the wording, I'd say no, but I imagine there would be a variety of alternative methods that would allow for it. Darkness Gifts, special fetishes, and so forth. Obviously you could use Tongue of Flame against them, and wolves of the Temple of Apollo sometimes emit light from their eyes and mouth, 'capturing' one in your mouth while that's active would probably count for capturing it within inescapable light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:21:42-08:00","id":1037927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037901#post1037901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to say. The predator's bane usually goes through effects that lower damage. So if I'm a tough guy who reduces Lethal to Bashing, it still does Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what the sidebar says...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:34:10-08:00","id":1037934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1037927#post1037927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't what the sidebar says...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay lets see what it says. 'Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources. Even in Hishu, a werewolf\u2019s bite causes lethal damage to vampires.'<br /> <br /> Still, they aren't inflicting Aggravated damage, which is the only way to do damage to the strix outside of banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:39:35-08:00","id":1038020,"title":"","content":"Their bites count as mystical sources. They're the scions of the embodiment of the hunt. They should be able to damage Strix through biting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:46:06-08:00","id":1038026,"title":"","content":"Alright, word of writer for the win. I'm still stuck in the 'toning down werewolf for other games' mindset, which sucks.<br /> <br /> I don't suppose there's any news on the book front?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:00:11-08:00","id":1038056,"title":"","content":"Yeah, intent from writing was that werewolves are the inheritors of the greatest predator ever. If they're hunting you, be worried. <br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't mean instant win or anything. They may end up doing the minimum damage against a particular foe. (The ST will have to exercise some judgement.) But their teeth will let them inflict some damage. <br /> <br /> Re: books, I've heard nothing, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:10:08-08:00","id":1038061,"title":"","content":"Anyone know if there's any word on if you can have both a personal AND pack totem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T16:15:51-08:00","id":1038098,"title":"","content":"I think considering it's an option given in the core and doesn't mention anything about not having a pack totem because of it, it's doable. I'd suggest using the Mentor Merit, as a personal totem doesn't seem be a sidekick, which would be more appropriate with a Retainer Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2017, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:37:35-08:00","id":1038126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038061#post1038061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know if there's any word on if you can have both a personal AND pack totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's allowable, and already covered by the Totem merit (p. 108) - <i>Your character has a relationship to a totem spirit, either personally or to a pack totem</i>.<br /> <br /> Purchase it separately from your pack totem - yes, this does mean that the personal totem is likely to be significantly weaker than the pack totem, but this is generally how it should be in the hierarchy of spirits and totems. A pack totem is okay with its pack having smaller personal totems, just like a lodge totem is okay with members having smaller pack totems (and/or personal totems), and tribal totems (aka Firstborn) are okay with lodges, packs and Uratha having lesser totems.<br /> <br /> As long as every spirit knows its place, everyone is happy.<br /> <br /> That said, you could certainly have scenarios (and tell stories) where the personal totem is more powerful than the pack totem. This will cause friction, and be a flashpoint for drama. Run with it and play it out, just expect that the pack will be pulling double-time on massaging its ego while the more powerful personal totem sits smugly and preens its little favourite werewolf.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit to add</i>: Don't forget that the more powerful a totem, the more (and greater) demands it's going to place on the werewolf for its patronage. Spirits, including totems, cannot cannot cannot give anything away for free. Their existence is transactional and they have to be paid/bribed/coerced/rendered favours etc if you want something from them. As covered in <i>The Pack</i>, the totem bond already gives them quite a bit, so you've got a reasonable amount of 'currency' banked with a totem because of the merit dots*, but bigger will ask for more - after all, they could be enjoying the services of a whole pack, why settle for just you?<br /> <br /> * Which is why I suggest using the Totem merit for a personal totem rather than Mentor or Retainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-25-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:53:14-08:00","id":1038131,"title":"","content":"Wow I need to read this book better. Otherwise, yeah, what Bunyip said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:01:57-08:00","id":1038135,"title":"","content":"Alright, cool, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T21:52:14-08:00","id":1038266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038020#post1038020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their bites count as mystical sources. They're the scions of the embodiment of the hunt. They should be able to damage Strix through biting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. That's definitely not the impression I got from the sidebar. Saying, &quot;their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources&quot; sounds like something that would only matter against foes that are explicitly vulnerable to mystical sources of damage, which the Strix are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T23:25:32-08:00","id":1038281,"title":"","content":"(Dammit, I had a longer, more eloquent response but computer crash ate it.)<br /> <br /> Vampire p. 202 - 'Some magic, though, including potent Cr\u00faac rites, the most devastating Disciplines and some banes can rend the shadows and actually injure a Strix'.<br /> <br /> Strix explicitly are vulnerable to 'some' mystical sources. Werewolf teeth count as those mystical sources. They can bite Strix.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T23:58:41-08:00","id":1038288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"> They are completely immune to all physical and ephemeral attacks except for Disciplines and Devotions that inflict aggravated damage, which inflict Bashing wounds on them instead</span> </div> </div> </div>Strix don't have any kind of resistance to <i>any </i>supernatural forms of damage except for Disciplines and Devotions as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T00:06:09-08:00","id":1038290,"title":"","content":"ST call. It's sometimes difficult to reconcile how something from one book interacts with something from another book. This is especially true when each core book writes from the point of view of that monster and the things it's likely to face. Vampire (and Strix) were written with Kindred in mind*, not werewolves. Werewolf was written with the 'if it bleeds we can kill it' mentality across the rest of the CofD, but it possibly wasn't phrased as clearly as that in the final product.<br /> <br /> I'm sure many of these questions will be answered in the Crossover Chronicles when they get under way.<br /> <br /> * Meaning Disciplines, Cruac etc, not Gifts, Atavisms, Awakened Magic, Contracts, Exploits etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T00:12:37-08:00","id":1038296,"title":"","content":"Werewolf teeth deal lethal damage to vampires. That is an <i>absolute </i>statement. Doesn't matter if they're in a form that doesn't deal lethal to anything else, doesn't matter if the vampire is an owl made of smoke.<br /> <br /> Werewolf teeth + Vampire = Lethal. At all times. No ifs, no buts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T00:28:39-08:00","id":1038298,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's because Vampire was the only other thing out at the time, and we wanted to be clear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T03:17:54-08:00","id":1038312,"title":"","content":"I think you're supposed to interpret that if a being has a weakness to a mystical source (not necessarily mystical sources in general) it is also vulnerable to werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T04:57:45-08:00","id":1038340,"title":"","content":"I dunno, maybe it's just me being salty about werewolves' bites dealing lethal damage to vampires, but the whole rule seems really strange and inconsistent to me. If they count as a source of whatever mystical vulnerability their prey may have, why do they need high enough Honorary Rank to count as Banes to spirits? Do they count as Banes for ghosts, angels, goetia, and other ephemeral beings? Why don't their bites count as silver against other werewolves without a Rite? Do they count as iron against Changelings and other Fae? Fire against Prometheans? Why do their bites in Hishu deal lethal damage to vampires when lethal damage bites isn't a benefit of the form and vampires don't have any weaknesses that upgrade damage from bashing to lethal? Why don't they count as sunlight?<br /> <br /> I remember during open development, Stew mentioned when the forms were previewed that the teeth and claws in hybrid forms (Dalu, Gauru, and Urshul), would be considered supernatural sources of damage, and therefore get around vampires' damage resistance. There was a big kerfuffle about that, and eventually someone (I think it might have been David?) said it would be changing to just the teeth, and that it had to do with the symbolism of the predator's jaws. It really looks to me like the rule exists because of a design goal that werewolves should be able to do lethal damage to vampires specifically, and that the specific reasoning being used to justify that is creating weird and inconsistent interactions with various other creatures damage resistances and vulnerabilities.<br /> <br /> If the intent is that werewolves' bites in any form always do lethal damage, bypassing any supernatural resistances or immunities their prey might have, that would be far more consistent, but that doesn't appear to be what it's saying. And again, Hishu form bites don't normally deal lethal damage in the first place. It seems like a better rule would just be to say that the damage from a werewolf's bite is never reduced by supernatural resistances, and let the type of damage be determined by the form and any Gifts, Rites, or other spirit magic enhancing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2017, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:13:13-08:00","id":1038346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038340#post1038340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a better rule would just be to say that the damage from a werewolf's bite is never reduced by supernatural resistances, and let the type of damage be determined by the form and any Gifts, Rites, or other spirit magic enhancing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be the intent, but it's how we run things.<br /> <br /> Re: Inconsistency with how they interact with spirits vs other supernaturals: Keep in mind that they don't do agg to vampires, just lethal. Acting as a bane to spirits does aggravated damage, they only do lethal by default. So that bit is internally consistent (kind of).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:26:58-08:00","id":1038355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038346#post1038346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not be the intent, but it's how we run things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably how I'll run it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038346#post1038346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Inconsistency with how they interact with spirits vs other supernaturals: Keep in mind that they don't do agg to vampires, just lethal. Acting as a bane to spirits does aggravated damage, they only do lethal by default. So that bit is internally consistent (kind of).</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, except that the justification given is that they count as mystical sources to creatures vulnerable to such sources. If that means that they count as anything their prey is mystically vulnerable to, then they really should do aggravated damage to vampires, because vampires are mystically vulnerable to sunlight and sunlight does aggravated damage to them. In fact, most supernatural vulnerabilities cause aggravated damage to the entities that have them.<br /> <br /> It really looks to me like the intent was just for werewolves to be able to do lethal damage to vampires, and that it says they count as &quot;mystical sources&quot; to explain why. And if that's the goal, that's fine. Vampires are the only creatures that currently have a damage resistance that explicitly applies only to mundane sources of damage (though arguably Death Mage Armor might work that way too). It's fine if that's what the Predator's Jaws does, it only starts getting weird when you try to apply it to things like Strix with the justification that they can be hurt by some supernatural sources, therefore werewolf teeth count as one of those sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:42:28-08:00","id":1038363,"title":"","content":"I don't think werewolf teeth are supposed to deal damage <i>as</i> one of those sources. Just that being vulnerable to one type of mystical damage means they also do damage, but unless you're also a Bane due to Honorary Rank or something like that they only deal normal damage.<br /> <br /> Also, sunlight deals bashing, lethal or aggravated damage to vampires based on Humanity. It's not always aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:48:07-08:00","id":1038366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038363#post1038363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think werewolf teeth are supposed to deal damage <i>as</i> one of those sources. Just that being vulnerable to one type of mystical damage means they also do damage, but unless you're also a Bane due to Honorary Rank or something like that they only deal normal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if a creature has a supernatural weakness, werewolf bites always deal lethal to them? I guess that would give you a consistent ruling, but it feels really awkward to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038363#post1038363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, sunlight deals bashing, lethal or aggravated damage to vampires based on Humanity. It's not always aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then go with fire. That's also a supernatural vulnerability vampires have and it does always cause aggravated wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:49:31-08:00","id":1038367,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's weird at all and seems like the spirit of the rule. I don't think they're supposed to count as banes of anything (except spirit, rank issues), they just count as mystical damage if the creature in question is vulnerable to mystical damages. Like the strix (which are vulnerable to a variety of such damages) and vampires, who are the same. Changelings are just as vulnerable to regular old gunshots as they are to werewolf teeth.<br /> <br /> If anything, Spirits, the exception to the rule, seems more because developers didn't want werewolf fucking up spirits without some kind of effort put in, as it would vastly uncomplicate their interactions, which are probably the most common interactions in the game beyond perhaps, humans.<br /> <br /> So it does sound a little like salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:58:23-08:00","id":1038368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, Spirits, the exception to the rule, seems more because developers didn't want werewolf fucking up spirits without some kind of effort put in </div> </div> </div>Wait - so do werewolf jaws only do <i>bashing</i> to spirits, like everything else?<br /> Or still lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:05:09-08:00","id":1038370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038367#post1038367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's weird at all and seems like the spirit of the rule. I don't think they're supposed to count as banes of anything (except spirit, rank issues), they just count as mystical damage if the creature in question is vulnerable to mystical damages. Like the strix (which are vulnerable to a variety of such damages) and vampires, who are the same. Changelings are just as vulnerable to regular old gunshots as they are to werewolf teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how do you know what type of damage their bites deal? Stirges only take bashing from mystical sources that normally deal aggravated damage, and werewolf teeth don't normally deal aggravated damage. Vampires explicitly take lethal damage from werewolf bites even in Hishu form, but bites in hishu normally do bashing damage and vampires don't have a weakness that causes them to take lethal damage from mystical sources that normally cause bashing damage. So do they just always do lethal to anything with a supernatural weakness? I guess that works, but I definitely think it's weird that a bite from a Hishu werewolf is more harmful to a Strix than an Unraveling spell with Reach but less harmful to a human than a smack with a baseball bat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038367#post1038367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, Spirits, the exception to the rule, seems more because developers didn't want werewolf fucking up spirits without some kind of effort put in, as it would vastly uncomplicate their interactions, which are probably the most common interactions in the game beyond perhaps, humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they the exception to the rule though? Do werewolf bites do bashing damage to spirits they don't outrank, or lethal? Do they deal lethal damage to ghosts? To Changelings? To Prometheans? To Horrors with the Unbreakable Dread Power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038367#post1038367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it does sound a little like salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, to be honest, that's probably where my concern over the internal consistency of the ability is coming from. I do genuinely think it's internally inconsistent though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2017, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T07:18:20-08:00","id":1038406,"title":"","content":"Werewolf bites specifically being something of a bane to vampires does show up here and there in fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:00:02-08:00","id":1038417,"title":"","content":"Would anyone have some advice or inspiration for statting out a Hurricane spirit and its entourage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:03:13-08:00","id":1038419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038370#post1038370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they the exception to the rule though? Do werewolf bites do bashing damage to spirits they don't outrank, or lethal? Do they deal lethal damage to ghosts? To Changelings? To Prometheans? To Horrors with the Unbreakable Dread Power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like the intent is that they do Lethal to everything. It upgrades to Aggravated against spirits of a certain rank, but that's about it. Lethal to ghosts, changelings, Prometheans. Unbreakable would probably do 1 Lethal, as there's nothing in there about Lethal and Armor-Piercing outside of the Living Weapon Merit.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to this Crossover book all of a sudden. It will clear up a lot of things nicely, I imagine. Everything I've heard about it beforehand has been Mage stuff, which is great since I'm playing mage but crossover hasn't been an issue there and werewolf's still my favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:10:38-08:00","id":1038424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038406#post1038406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf bites specifically being something of a bane to vampires does show up here and there in fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and I'm cool with that. I just find the text as-is unclear, and the interpretation with the most internal consistency (lethal damage to anything with a supernatural weakness) just feels wrong to me. I'd much rather the damage be by Form but bypass any supernatural resistances, or that it only do lethal to vampires and things with vampire-like damage resistance (i.e. Death Mage Armor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:16:40-08:00","id":1038425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thatxygirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038417#post1038417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone have some advice or inspiration for statting out a Hurricane spirit and its entourage?</div> </div> </div> </div>First major spirit we dealt with was a hurricane spirit, though I never dealt with the stats, really fun. I'd probably go big. Maybe Rank 4 or 5, depending on size or attention. I'd think dumping more dots into Power than Finesse would probably make sense, Hurricanes aren't particularly known for their smoothness. Predators suggests for storm spirits, 'Another common ban is a limit on how long a storm-spirit may remain in one area.' Which makes sense for hurricanes too, considering how they move.<br /> <br /> As for their entourage, you'd have wind, lightning, water and ocean spirits while over the ocean, probably lesser storm and tornado spirits. It would be a huge mess.<br /> <br /> One of the forum's creative types, Reighnhell,has written up stats for a 'regular' though powerful Storm Spirit <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993183#post993183\">here</a>, and a particular one, the Storm of Dread, known for killings, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993202#post993202\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:28:00-08:00","id":1038432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thatxygirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038417#post1038417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone have some advice or inspiration for statting out a Hurricane spirit and its entourage?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bStarting point is to think about narrative role and, off the back of that, Rank. What do you intend to do with the spirit? Small, local manifestation of a wider hurricane, or overarching spirit of the entire thing? 'Rampaging monster' causing havoc due to the real hurricane? Powerful spirit noble that must be negotiated with to minimise or exploit damage caused by the actual weather? Tormented victim being harnessed and used by sorcerers or Pure to direct the hurricane to the areas they want to devastate? Etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:38:42-08:00","id":1038435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038432#post1038432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bStarting point is to think about narrative role and, off the back of that, Rank. What do you intend to do with the spirit? Small, local manifestation of a wider hurricane, or overarching spirit of the entire thing? 'Rampaging monster' causing havoc due to the real hurricane? Powerful spirit noble that must be negotiated with to minimise or exploit damage caused by the actual weather? Tormented victim being harnessed and used by sorcerers or Pure to direct the hurricane to the areas they want to devastate? Etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The story I am working with is specifically Hurricane Matthew. What I want the group to deal with is the small local manifestation stirred up by the passing hurricane, the rampaging monster motif that must be calmed, redirected, or put down. The campaign takes place in St. Augustine, which sustained heavy damage and severe flooding from the storm. The idea of having to deal with an entity harnessing the storm to move in a specific direction intrigues me, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:39:57-08:00","id":1038436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038425#post1038425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First major spirit we dealt with was a hurricane spirit, though I never dealt with the stats, really fun. I'd probably go big. Maybe Rank 4 or 5, depending on size or attention. I'd think dumping more dots into Power than Finesse would probably make sense, Hurricanes aren't particularly known for their smoothness. Predators suggests for storm spirits, 'Another common ban is a limit on how long a storm-spirit may remain in one area.' Which makes sense for hurricanes too, considering how they move.<br /> <br /> As for their entourage, you'd have wind, lightning, water and ocean spirits while over the ocean, probably lesser storm and tornado spirits. It would be a huge mess.<br /> <br /> One of the forum's creative types, Reighnhell,has written up stats for a 'regular' though powerful Storm Spirit <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993183#post993183\">here</a>, and a particular one, the Storm of Dread, known for killings, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993202#post993202\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks! This really helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:37:24-08:00","id":1044729,"title":"","content":"Hope I'm not bogarting questions here so I'll shoot and if I'm off shoot me down... I'd prefer answers in an official capacity or strong non rhetorical statements as to why something does or does not work<br /> <br /> 1.) Do Merits like Striking Looks and/or Air of Menace stack with ALL Supernatural Abilities that incorporate their relevant mentioned skills unless otherwise noted?<br /> <br /> 2.) Do creatures that &quot;auto grapple&quot; as part of a natural attack get to utilize grappling fighting styles... Specifically Gauru form Bite + 2nd dot of Grappling Fighting Style Takedown? If so how would it work?<br /> <br /> 3.) Does Badass Motherfucker evoke fear based emotions? If so why does it not use Intimidate? <br /> <br /> I'm AFB now and perhaps it does use it however my ST stated it does not. Having a 3 Intimidate with a Specialty in Dominance a 2 Presence 1 Primal Urge and Air of Menace in Dalu using Badass Motherfucker seemed abundantly counterintuitive when I ended up with a 3 Dice Pool (was told to roll Presence + Primal Urge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","user":"WyrmWeaver","date":".  Rephrased first question. Also Thank you for addressing my plebian questions! 02-06-2017, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","name":"WyrmWeaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:32:04-08:00","id":1044747,"title":"","content":"1.) Generally yes, but looking at it case by case might reveal instances where it's not very logical. Striking Looks, for example, should probably not have an effect outside of Hishu.<br /> 2.) Takedown is a variation of the establish grapple action. Bite attacks is a different action that has establish grapple as a side effect. It's not possible to combine them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T17:18:57-08:00","id":1044779,"title":"","content":"Also for Badass Motherfucker, the ability is a natural extension of one of your forms, rather than a trained ability.<br /> <br /> If your Striking Looks tends towards the Intimidating or something similar, I would allow its bonus to work there. I'd disagree with Tessie about Striking Looks, but they may be thinking of first edition where Striking Looks was just 'you are remarkably good-looking,' and now it can be 'you are particularly terrifying-looking,' among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T00:35:27-08:00","id":1044950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1044747#post1044747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Generally yes, but looking at it case by case might reveal instances where it's not very logical. Striking Looks, for example, should probably not have an effect outside of Hishu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please! Striking Looks would totally allow you to be an extraordinarily magnificent wolf! Glossy fur, perky ears, haunting eyes, and a particularly fine scent!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T01:29:22-08:00","id":1044959,"title":"","content":"1 - Yes, but as Tessie said the ST may rule otherwise for situations where it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> 2 - No.<br /> <br /> 3 - It's an instinctive reaction of the prey to a literal inheritor of the predator god, it's not a skill. The human's lizard brains couldn't care less if your character presents as a blood-spattered biker or a meek librarian, they get out of the character's way. If you want your character to use her trained, practiced ability to scare people, take an Intimidate action instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-07-2017, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:39:46-08:00","id":1045716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1044959#post1044959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Yes, but as Tessie said the ST may rule otherwise for situations where it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> 2 - No.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a clarification of intent on the rules would help... Largely I realized this in retrospect. I apologize for my short coming in that regard.<br /> <br /> 1.) But you wouldn't rule that it doesn't apply under the pretense that the ability is supernatural? There would have to be more relevant context than that right?<br /> <br /> 2.) If you'd humor me though... I'm confused with the wording &quot;...with a normal roll you may render an opponent prone, instead of establishing a grapple...&quot; an attack that causes a grapple --whether bite, claw or hurricanrana doesn't require any sort of &quot;special roll&quot; or even modification to the roll itself. It is an attack roll (a normal roll) that if successful allows for a roll to establish a grapple (a normal roll) at which point you can choose to render an opponent prone rather than establish a grapple. Just because the circumstances aren't normal, there is no change to dice rolls themselves... So the clause &quot;normal roll&quot; stands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To summarize:<br /> Successful x/y/z attack+successful roll to establish grapple+Takedown=rendering prone instead of establishing grapple. Its a change to the function of establishing a grapple, not a change to the function of a dice roll.<br /> <br /> If Takedown were a maneuver I'd understand but it's effectively a substitute for successfully establishing a grapple. A clarification of intent would cast out any doubts. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Despite my long-winded Bite Slam Thesis I don't really have an attachment to it working or not so much as I care about my interpretation being technically correct.<br /> <br /> Do I think bite slams in the context of verisimilitude would work? Yes. Would I use it? No. It's effing broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","user":"WyrmWeaver","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","name":"WyrmWeaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:55:37-08:00","id":1045728,"title":"","content":"Normally a grapple is established when one character makes a roll to grab another character. Takedown is a move that modifies the outcome of the grabbing action. Biting (when in forms that allows it outside a grapple) is an attack roll that establishes grapple as a side effect. Takedown does not modify that action because it's not the <i>normal</i> grabbing action.<br /> And with the existence of specialties (and Area of Expertise) I can add that the roll for biting and the roll for grabbing does not necessarily have identical dice pools.<br /> <br /> Edit: I do not have a werewolf character, but my grappling focused vampire character would have 24 dice in Frenzy (before other activated abilities and situational modifiers) to grab and use the Takedown move and &quot;only&quot; 20 to bite unless my ST allows the grappling specialty to be applied since the bite will lead to a grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:01:50-08:00","id":1046041,"title":"","content":"Question, can a spirit be the target of a &quot;specified target&quot; attack?<br /> <br /> Like -2 to hit its &quot;arm&quot;, producing an arm wrack tilt? Rules says spirit dont suffer lethal from most attacks because they lack internal organs and they lack wound penalties but still havent caught a rule that says they cant suffer tilts like &quot;arm wrack&quot;<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:13:37-08:00","id":1046045,"title":"","content":"They're made of ephemera so they don't necessarily have joints that work the way humans do. Plus they don't usually look humanoid in appearance or shape.<br /> <br /> You could certainly do called shots, but they wouldn't cause specific Tilts unless the spirit had, for some reason, made themselves to be vulnerable to such, but the problem is it's not just hitting the part of the body, it's hitting it and doing more damage than their Stamina, which for a spirit would be represented by Resistance Trait, which could be ridiculously high. Depending on their form they might even be immune to Knocked Down.<br /> <br /> Had a surprisingly hard time re-finding this thread. I wanted to point out that sometimes spirits use weapons or objects, you could probably justify them becoming unable to use them if you somehow did the equivalent of inflicting Arm Wrack. Though you might just use Disarm for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-08-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T20:14:07-08:00","id":1046601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1046045#post1046045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could certainly do called shots, but they wouldn't cause specific Tilts unless the spirit had, for some reason, made themselves to be vulnerable to such, but the problem is it's not just hitting the part of the body, it's hitting it and doing more damage than their Stamina, which for a spirit would be represented by Resistance Trait, which could be ridiculously high. Depending on their form they might even be immune to Knocked Down.<br /> <br /> Had a surprisingly hard time re-finding this thread. I wanted to point out that sometimes spirits use weapons or objects, you could probably justify them becoming unable to use them if you somehow did the equivalent of inflicting Arm Wrack. Though you might just use Disarm for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does anybody remember a section in one of the books that had what favors out of spirits one could get and at what cost? I remember being in Lore of the Forsaken but i have been flipping through it and cant find it. I remember it was more geared towards artificial spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T20:22:35-08:00","id":1046603,"title":"","content":"Just a guess but perhaps Summoners? The last chapter, Otherworldly Compacts, deals with pacts with beings, including spirits, and guides you in designing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:20:21-08:00","id":1046781,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Can't find it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:23:22-08:00","id":1048539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1046781#post1046781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Can't find it either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Found it, it was on Blood of The Wolf page 58.<br /> <br /> Non related question. So on page 85 on Forsaken 2nd edition says that a player can earn a beat when among other sources.<ul><li>Persistent conditions provide beats for actions other than resolutions.</li> <li>If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost health boxes they take a beat.</li> </ul>So if say, a Werewolf in gauru form during a hunt condition in combat for 5 turns in during which he gets exceptional success on his attack rolls for all of them (5 successes) which is the condition to get a beat in &quot;the hunt condition&quot;, and eat his entire health track in damage each turn (which he regenerates next turn). Would he get 10 beats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-13-2017, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:43:47-08:00","id":1048542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048539#post1048539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non related question. So on page 85 on Forsaken 2nd edition says that a player can earn a beat when among other sources.<ul><li>Persistent conditions provide beats for actions other than resolutions.</li> <li>If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost health boxes they take a beat.</li> </ul>So if say, a Werewolf in gauru form during a hunt condition in combat for 5 turns in during which he gets exceptional success on his attack rolls for all of them (5 successes) which is the condition to get a beat in &quot;the hunt condition&quot;, and eat his entire health track in damage (which he regenerates next turn). Would he get 10 beats?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the storyteller you're able to limit the dispersion of Beats, just as you're able to dole them out for worthy ones not listed. The 'taking lethal damage' in one of her rightmost health boxes is meant to give a beat for the dramatic turn of the scene, as you are now truly badly hurt. Which may not be the case if you're biting yourself. Five exceptional successes in a row is pretty surprising, but the Condition only gives Beats when you're getting a roll in an action regarding the prey. But if you think it's worthy of ten Beats, feel free to give them out.<br /> <br /> As a cooperative storytelling game, it generally works best if players aren't trying to screw over the system and the storyteller isn't trying to screw over the player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:55:43-08:00","id":1048546,"title":"","content":"One of the general modifiers for rites is &quot;All participants are wearing or showing symbols that indicate their shared purpose.&quot; Is this per-rite or per-ritual-group? (i.e. Is this to encourage painting the entire set of ritual participants with the symbolism of the rite or is it to encourage packs to develop consistent ritual iconography of their own?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T20:10:50-08:00","id":1048550,"title":"","content":"Seems like it would be per rite. Especially with the existence of 'tribe only' rites that might have a different influence than rituals tailored by the pack.<br /> <br /> The other way seems like it would warrant a sort of 'Cabal Theme' type Merit for the pack.<br /> <br /> I have to ask, are you running a game of Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T20:38:02-08:00","id":1048563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048550#post1048550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to ask, are you running a game of Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not currently, but Yantra talk has the question of intended visuals on my mind and general forethought means I feel obligated to give some attention to how the inevitable reuse of my Chicago setting for other gamelines might best be approached; the city's existing iconography in my Changeling game suggests the local werewolf scene in particular is pretty fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T21:03:51-08:00","id":1048573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048563#post1048563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not currently, but Yantra talk has the question of intended visuals on my mind and general forethought means I feel obligated to give some attention to how the inevitable reuse of my Chicago setting for other gamelines might best be approached; the city's existing iconography in my Changeling game suggests the local werewolf scene in particular is pretty fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. It doesn't seem like an 'iconic focus' is necessary for packs. The same pack that has an Iron Master with rites adapted from 90s cyberpunk movies and things like <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0113243/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Hackers</a> might have a more reverential Bone Shadow who's spent more of his life in the Hisil than out.<br /> <br /> Lodges seem to be where a unified focus is more important, especially with overbearing totems. The Temple of Apollo, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-14-2017, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:41:13-08:00","id":1049001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048542#post1048542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As the storyteller you're able to limit the dispersion of Beats, just as you're able to dole them out for worthy ones not listed. The 'taking lethal damage' in one of her rightmost health boxes is meant to give a beat for the dramatic turn of the scene, as you are now truly badly hurt. Which may not be the case if you're biting yourself. Five exceptional successes in a row is pretty surprising, but the Condition only gives Beats when you're getting a roll in an action regarding the prey. But if you think it's worthy of ten Beats, feel free to give them out.<br /> <br /> As a cooperative storytelling game, it generally works best if players aren't trying to screw over the system and the storyteller isn't trying to screw over the player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>They werent try to cheat the game it just that both situations came pretty easily. It was a blood talon rahu hunting a fire touched backed up by a fire spirit both were fighting in garu (so none of them had defense agaisnt the other). The rahu rolled 11 dices for an attack roll pumped to 14 with wp and with 8s again for full moon so he landed 12 hits each turn (considering he had +1 automatix success for the claws). <br /> <br /> On the other hand the fire touched and fire spirit fill all the lethal health of the blood talon each turn but there was no overflow so the player regenerated all each turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:17:55-08:00","id":1049029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1049001#post1049001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They werent try to cheat the game it just that both situations came pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get one Beat per source per session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:36:07-08:00","id":1049042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1049001#post1049001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so none of them had defense agaisnt the other</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have Defense, it would just be the lesser of Wits or Dexterity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T02:38:56-08:00","id":1049199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048546#post1048546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the general modifiers for rites is &amp;quot;All participants are wearing or showing symbols that indicate their shared purpose.&amp;quot; Is this per-rite or per-ritual-group? (i.e. Is this to encourage painting the entire set of ritual participants with the symbolism of the rite or is it to encourage packs to develop consistent ritual iconography of their own?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a slightly tricksy answer, but I'd suggest that the symbolism is per rite, but nothing prevents a group from using the same dress/symbolism for multiple rites.<br /> <br /> To break this down further, a pack could have one style of dress they use as affirmation for all their rites, or they may modify the clothing/symbols based on the type of rite and its intended purpose. The modifier allows for both and doesn't punish either style of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:22:52-08:00","id":1049217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1049029#post1049029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can get one Beat per source per session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know where it says that? i am on the beat section on the book and i cant find that rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1049042#post1049042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would have Defense, it would just be the lesser of Wits or Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are right i miss that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T18:39:12-08:00","id":1049638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1049217#post1049217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know where it says that? i am on the beat section on the book and i cant find that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually 1 beat per source per scene, not session. It's not actually a rule in the werewolf core, the only place I remember seeing it is in the mage 2e core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:55:44-08:00","id":1050040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048539#post1048539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Found it, it was on Blood of The Wolf page 58.<br /> <br /> Non related question. So on page 85 on Forsaken 2nd edition says that a player can earn a beat when among other sources.<ul><li>Persistent conditions provide beats for actions other than resolutions.</li> <li>If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost health boxes they take a beat.</li> </ul><br /> So if say, a Werewolf in gauru form during a hunt condition in combat for 5 turns in during which he gets exceptional success on his attack rolls for all of them (5 successes) which is the condition to get a beat in &quot;the hunt condition&quot;, and eat his entire health track in damage each turn (which he regenerates next turn). Would he get 10 beats?</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally can't attack yourself in Gauru form. You're out for blood. Other's blood. Would you net a beat for exceptionally mauling someone/something in accordance to a sacred hunt? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:57:39-08:00","id":1050041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1048546#post1048546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the general modifiers for rites is &quot;All participants are wearing or showing symbols that indicate their shared purpose.&quot; Is this per-rite or per-ritual-group? (i.e. Is this to encourage painting the entire set of ritual participants with the symbolism of the rite or is it to encourage packs to develop consistent ritual iconography of their own?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I lean on the later. Making symbolic displays of their totem is a common method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T20:49:33-08:00","id":1050294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1050040#post1050040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You literally can't attack yourself in Gauru form. You're out for blood. Other's blood. Would you net a beat for exceptionally mauling someone/something in accordance to a sacred hunt? Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didnt attack himself. In 5 consecutive turns he got 5+ successes agaisnt his prey and said prey hit back filling all the lethal damage track of the pc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:16:34-08:00","id":1050604,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <br /> \u200bI think the word 'eat' caused some confusion. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> used that to mean 'took that amount of damage and kept going', not that the werewolf was performing the act of eating on his own body.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:47:59-08:00","id":1053884,"title":"","content":"That would cause aggravated damage, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:10:28-08:00","id":1054933,"title":"","content":"About how easy would it be to pass off the Mother Wolf/origin story as myth in 2e? I always liked the mystery &amp; toolbox aspect of the nWOD/ChroD, but Forsaken seems (or seemed) to make it's back lore more concrete than the other lines.<br /> <br /> Edit: And by myth, I mean 'one possibility among many.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:25:28-08:00","id":1054986,"title":"","content":"Very easy, there's other options available in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:00:19-08:00","id":1057694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1054933#post1054933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About how easy would it be to pass off the Mother Wolf/origin story as myth in 2e? I always liked the mystery &amp; toolbox aspect of the nWOD/ChroD, but Forsaken seems (or seemed) to make it's back lore more concrete than the other lines.<br /> <br /> Edit: And by myth, I mean 'one possibility among many.'</div> </div> </div> </div>It is canonically just one myth among many. And while Sundered World did give us a glimpse of the truth behind the myth, it also proved a great deal of the modern version of the myth to be false. And at any rate, there's no reason Sundered World needs to be accurate history in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:02:44-08:00","id":1059277,"title":"","content":"Are werewolves in gauru form immune to tilts and/or wound penalties like in first edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:18:05-08:00","id":1059281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1059277#post1059277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are werewolves in gauru form immune to tilts and/or wound penalties like in first edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, yes, unless those are inflicted by Aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T13:43:58-07:00","id":1061600,"title":"","content":"How does <b>The Hunter Waits</b> work?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Once I move, the gift is over?</li> <li>While I am moving I get no benefit. Each time I remain still again in the same scene, I get the benefit?</li> </ol>How does <b>Fading</b> work?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Every failed perception check adds -1 penalty to everyone who attempts to detect me in the scene?</li> <li>Every individual who fails a perception check adds -1 penalty. So 4 people can never exceed a -4 penalty (one for each individual that failed)?</li> <li>Each person counts their failed perception checks individually. So Guy 1 might have a -2 penalty, while Guy 4 might have a -4 penalty?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T21:08:18-07:00","id":1061720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1061600#post1061600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does <b>The Hunter Waits</b> work?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Once I move, the gift is over?</li> <li>While I am moving I get no benefit. Each time I remain still again in the same scene, I get the benefit?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>2. It lasts a scene. 'Duration: 1 scene.'<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does <b>Fading</b> work?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Every failed perception check adds -1 penalty to everyone who attempts to detect me in the scene?</li> <li>Every individual who fails a perception check adds -1 penalty. So 4 people can never exceed a -4 penalty (one for each individual that failed)?</li> <li>Each person counts their failed perception checks individually. So Guy 1 might have a -2 penalty, while Guy 4 might have a -4 penalty?</li> </ol> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's 1, based on the description, 'her ethereality compounds with each person who does not see her.' If you're stingy you might go with 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T05:47:36-07:00","id":1062250,"title":"","content":"does a werewolf suffer aggravated damage from a spirit two ranks higher than him? Or does it work only for spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T06:28:52-07:00","id":1062262,"title":"","content":"Honorary Rank does not come with that particular drawback. Only beings with actual Rank suffers aggravated damage from beings at least two Ranks higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:05:37-07:00","id":1062271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1062262#post1062262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honorary Rank does not come with that particular drawback. Only beings with actual Rank suffers aggravated damage from beings at least two Ranks higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>then can i assume that Honorary Rank only count for purpose of social interaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:13:51-07:00","id":1062277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1062271#post1062271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> then can i assume that Honorary Rank only count for purpose of social interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves still <i>benefit from </i>the &quot;natural attacks count as a bane&quot; quality of Honorary Rank, they just don't have the same <i>vulnerability to</i> higher-Ranking beings as spirits do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:18:50-07:00","id":1062280,"title":"","content":"Beings with actual Rank takes damage from beings with honorary Rank if they are at least two Ranks higher.<br /> The honorary Rank of a werewolf is just that; honorary. It does not affect the werewolf. But it's real enough for spirits and other beings that have Rank that they are affected by it.<br /> See the Tooth and Claw side bar on page 186.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:20:27-07:00","id":1062281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1062271#post1062271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> then can i assume that Honorary Rank only count for purpose of social interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, that's incorrect. Here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF pg 186</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">TOOTH AND CLAW<br /> Uratha have one great advantage in the Hunt against weaker spirits \u2014 the spiritual deference to Rank extends to the honorary Rank werewolves earn through Renown (see p. 99), but only against spirits. A werewolf who \u201coutranks\u201d a minor spirit will deal devastating wounds to it with his claws and bite,but a high-Rank spirit can\u2019t burn that werewolf by touching him. High-Ranking spirits have other ways to assert dominance over the half-fleshed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: Wow a lot of people replied very quickly to that misconception and my typing was a bit slow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-14-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:31:51-07:00","id":1062362,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this was asked before, there's a lot to read. When making a wolf-blooded to play do you have to purchase that first tell or is it free? Like if I wanted to play a wolf-blooded in a hunter game would I just say I'm wolf-blooded(ST approval obviously) and get a tell or do I have to put the 3 merit points in to purchase a tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:51:59-07:00","id":1062376,"title":"","content":"The Tell seems to be the 'buy in' aspect. If you're a Wolf-Blooded, you get a Tell. So a lot is going to depend on your storyteller, since it's basically a free 'power' at the cost of being Wolf-blooded, which might not be a cost at all. Some might make you pay for it but there doesn't seem to be a rule about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:03:33-07:00","id":1062380,"title":"","content":"When directly creating a Wolf-Blooded it should be free. When a human character spontaneously becomes Wolf-Blooded during the course of the story you would represent that by buying the Merit.<br /> However, if all other characters are regular humans the ST might rule that being Wolf-Blooded should come with an XP cost (i.e. you buy the Tell Merit) to make it a bit more fair for the other player characters. But that's something between you and your ST.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another possibility is to have the character become Wolf-Blooded in the game. You and your ST could engineer a situation your character might have to roll for Lunacy, and it'll be a Dramatic Failure (even if the roll would show a success). Or come up with another way to become Wolf-Blooded. I haven't read the entire book yet so I don't know about other ways that might happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-14-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:33:18-07:00","id":1062503,"title":"","content":"Normally, being Wolf-Blooded is something that happens at birth or as a result of Lunacy, and does not cost experiences. The Tell Merit has Wolf-Blooded as a prerequisite, and is primarily for giving characters who are <i>already</i> Wolf-Blooded a second Tell. However, at Storyteller discretion, a human character might be able to take the Tell Merit to spontaneously become Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T17:22:13-07:00","id":1062562,"title":"","content":"Tells also uniquely stick around if the wolf blooded becomes something else like a mage or a vampire. If someone wants to play such a character (maybe even outside a werewolf game), you can make them pay for it with merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:38:32-07:00","id":1062607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1062562#post1062562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tells also uniquely stick around if the wolf blooded becomes something else like a mage or a vampire. If someone wants to play such a character (maybe even outside a werewolf game), you can make them pay for it with merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was something that stuck with me. I rather liked a lot of the tells the book had, because many of them hearkened back to actual rumors and myths about werewolves. (like the one where you wear a living wolf-pelt to turn into a wolf) I wonder how that tell, for example, or the one that makes you take Dalu form when confronted with religious iconography would interact with being a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:52:19-07:00","id":1062618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1062607#post1062607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was something that stuck with me. I rather liked a lot of the tells the book had, because many of them hearkened back to actual rumors and myths about werewolves. (like the one where you wear a living wolf-pelt to turn into a wolf) I wonder how that tell, for example, or the one that makes you take Dalu form when confronted with religious iconography would interact with being a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I imagine the naive vampire hunter who tried it would really, really regret it.<br /> <br /> But it seems like the type of thing that would be first on the list for things to fiddle with once the vampire decided to 'take a bane' for a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> It's probably the neatest of the 'sub splat' offerings so far. I like ghouls but their power potential is very high and the drawback is obvious. The proximi are really tuned in to mages. Wolf-blooded seem to be really popular even outside of the Forsaken fandom. Their powers are interesting, well-balanced, and the option honestly seems right at home in a Hunter or mortal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-14-2017, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:17:30-07:00","id":1063129,"title":"","content":"Simple question: when you lose one of your Touchstones, you immediately slip in the opposite direction (physical Touchstone fades - automatic loss of Harmony; spiritual Touchstone is left behind - automatic increase of Harmony); but when you establish new relationship towards it you encounter breaking point in the <u><i>other</i></u> direction (WtF 2ed, p. 87). That means when my character lost his physical Touchstone (his Harmony slipped one dot towards Spirit), then he will have a breaking point towards Spirit for establishing new relationship with different physical Touchstone, yes?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf this is correct I would like to know why there is possibility of strengthening your spiritual side for establishing connections with something that exist for the purpose of rooting character in his human, physical and material nature? Either I'm not translating text correctly, or something isn't entirely right. I supposed that when my character lost his spiritual companion (one dot of Harmony up toward Flesh), he should encounter breaking point toward Spirit for establishing significant relationship with something that reminds him that he is partially Spirit as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10834-mictlantecuhtli","name":"Mictlantecuhtli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:31:29-07:00","id":1063132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1063129#post1063129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: when you lose one of your Touchstones, you immediately slip in the opposite direction (physical Touchstone fades - automatic loss of Harmony; spiritual Touchstone is left behind - automatic increase of Harmony); but when you establish new relationship towards it you encounter breaking point in the <u><i>other</i></u> direction (WtF 2ed, p. 87).</div> </div> </div> </div>The other direction from the one you slid in for losing the Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1063129#post1063129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means when my character lost his physical Touchstone (his Harmony slipped one dot towards Spirit), then he will have a breaking point towards Spirit for establishing new relationship with different physical Touchstone, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that would be in the same direction as you slipped for having lost the first Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1063129#post1063129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf this is correct I would like to know why there is possibility of strengthening your spiritual side for establishing connections with something that exist for the purpose of rooting character in his human, physical and material nature? Either I'm not translating text correctly, or something isn't entirely right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems you misinterpreted what &quot;the other direction&quot; was referring to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1063129#post1063129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I supposed that when my character lost his spiritual companion (one dot of Harmony up toward Flesh), he should encounter breaking point toward Spirit for establishing significant relationship with something that reminds him that he is partially Spirit as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You supposed correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T21:09:15-07:00","id":1065582,"title":"","content":"Can the Pure defect to the Forsaken? I've seen the stuff about Forsaken joining the Pure and getting their Auspice &quot;burned&quot; out of them, but can a Pure werewolf join the Forsaken and <i>gain </i>an Auspice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T21:18:25-07:00","id":1065586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065582#post1065582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Pure defect to the Forsaken? I've seen the stuff about Forsaken joining the Pure and getting their Auspice &quot;burned&quot; out of them, but can a Pure werewolf join the Forsaken and <i>gain </i>an Auspice?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's possible at all, it's the stuff of legend \u2014 wholesale conversion to the Pure state involves a process not entirely unlike getting a Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T21:26:06-07:00","id":1065588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065582#post1065582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Pure defect to the Forsaken? I've seen the stuff about Forsaken joining the Pure and getting their Auspice &quot;burned&quot; out of them, but can a Pure werewolf join the Forsaken and <i>gain </i>an Auspice?</div> </div> </div> </div>We talked about it in more detail <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice\">here</a>. It was possible, but rare, in first edition. There's no equivalent rite in second but it's still early in the game and the game has been more open about possibilities so I wouldn't expect it to be closed off, but like Satchel says it would be rare enough to be a thing of legends. The Pure would go far to kill anyone trying to leave them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:19:50-07:00","id":1065646,"title":"","content":"It's probably far more common (and that's still pretty damn rare) for a pure to defect and just stay auspiceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:45:10-07:00","id":1065719,"title":"","content":"Which Facets/Fetishes can be useful against vs vampire's Celerity? Into more or less open combat (only short-term ambushes are allowed).<br /> I can remember only HIT AND RUN","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:30:22-07:00","id":1065784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065719#post1065719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Facets/Fetishes can be useful against vs vampire's Celerity? Into more or less open combat (only short-term ambushes are allowed).<br /> I can remember only HIT AND RUN</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure what you mean but guessing it's the 'running away and running back' kind of thing. Werewolf senses would probably compensate enough for that, since they can follow very fast moving things with their eyes, so it wouldn't be 'the vampire disappeared!' so much as 'the vampire went over there.'.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Falx can lop off a leg with the first attack, which would severely hinder running away abilities. An opening attack with urshul can inflict knocked down, which would do the same. Hit and Run, One Step Ahead. Pack Triumphs Together can give everyone in the pack the same Initiative, so jumping one would potentially lead you into attacks by the others. Black Earth, Red Hunger brings up obstacles, Knotted Path makes escape impossible. Potentially Maze Ward or All Doors Locked, which lets you open and close any doors in the way. Heavens Unleashed would make moving around fast much more difficult. If you're of the right auspice, the Shrieking Moon Gifts can turn your opponent into a gibbering, soulless mess.<br /> <br /> Fetishes are hard, because there's infinite variations of them and you should be making some up yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:41:10-07:00","id":1065797,"title":"","content":"Urhan form lets you use an ability similar to the interrupt action thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:27:54-07:00","id":1065820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065784#post1065784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite sure what you mean but guessing it's the 'running away and running back' kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> This facet<br /> &quot;This Facet can be used to interrupt an attack action that is aimed at the Uratha. Before the action is taken, the Uratha may immediately disengage and move up to her full Speed away.&quot; And vampire's speed as is is not such a problem as the ability to interrupt any enemy's action he aware of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:35:45-07:00","id":1065823,"title":"","content":"I mean, in some face-to-face, HtH fight. It's quite hard to make bloodsucker spend the whole bloodpool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:52:31-07:00","id":1065828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065823#post1065823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, in some face-to-face, HtH fight. It's quite hard to make bloodsucker spend the whole bloodpool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just doing Lethal damage to them should be more than enough to help. They aren't able to use Celerity to both interrupt an action and move to the head of the Initiative Queue, and can't use more interrupts than they have Celerity in a scene, so they max out at five.<br /> <br /> And if you just Ready an Action, something like, 'I hold my action until the vampire comes near me,' you should be able to take advantage providing the vampire approaches, even if it means forgoing your normal turn.<br /> <br /> Simply Grappling would stop it dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-21-2017, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:57:19-07:00","id":1065830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065828#post1065828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just doing Lethal damage to them should be more than enough to help. They aren't able to use Celerity to both interrupt an action and move to the head of the Initiative Queue, and can't use more interrupts than they have Celerity in a scene, so they max out at five.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it. But everything that vampire need to do - just interrupt you attacks. While he actually can attack later in his turn. So, Hit and Run become completely 'musthave'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:12:04-07:00","id":1065836,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's fully possible for a vampire to both interrupt an action and move to the top of the initiative queue. They are able to use each active Celerity effect once per turn; not just one active Celerity effect per turn. However, since both effects are typically followed by an action it's rarely practical to do both during the same turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:31:58-07:00","id":1065841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1065830#post1065830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it. But everything that vampire need to do - just interrupt you attacks. While he actually can attack later in his turn. So, Hit and Run become completely 'musthave'.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just travel around with a pack, personal totem, or your totem.<br /> <br /> As Tessie pointed out, they can interrupt and move to the top if they have enough Blood Potency, but they still only have one action per turn and a werewolf or spirit is more than a match for a vampire unless you're talking pup-out-of-First Change versus some centuries-old-creep.<br /> <br /> Even alone, just land one shot and they're now torn between using Celerity twice or healing. And that's still Vitae they're not using for Physical Intensity or Resilience. Use Urhan to interrupt them, and Urshul to cripple them.<br /> <br /> Since standing up is an action, I'd argue you couldn't really interrupt an attack with 'standing up.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:40:08-07:00","id":1065845,"title":"","content":"Huh, I re-read the rules just now.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, using Celerity in this way is exhausting; a vampire may only interrupt as many actions <b>in a scene </b>as she has dots in Celerity </div> </div> </div> That's the thing. I thought, they can broke others' action <i>in a turn. </i>Untill Vitae will be change spent.<br /> Yep, i was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 03-21-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:36:06-07:00","id":1068770,"title":"","content":"Is there a way for a werewolf to force dramatic failures, so as to convert normal humans into Wolf-Blooded through judicious use of Lunacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:38:43-07:00","id":1068774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lackey Man Ren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068770#post1068770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for a werewolf to force dramatic failures, so as to convert normal humans into Wolf-Blooded through judicious use of Lunacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No<br /> 2. Werewolves don't know Lunacy can cause humans to become Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:34:02-07:00","id":1068799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068774#post1068774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Werewolves don't know Lunacy can cause humans to become Wolf-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I question this. Werewolves will have noticed that some people exposed to Lunacy become wolf-blooded. And the tribes do keep lore on such things.<br /> That the Iron Masters, Bone Shadows, and (especially) the Ivory Claws wouldn't be aware of that fact smacks me as highly unlikely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:09:44-07:00","id":1068819,"title":"","content":"Do you have to be Wolf-blooded to undergo the First Change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:31:09-07:00","id":1068836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068799#post1068799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I question this. Werewolves will have noticed that some people exposed to Lunacy become wolf-blooded. And the tribes do keep lore on such things.<br /> That the Iron Masters, Bone Shadows, and (especially) the Ivory Claws wouldn't be aware of that fact smacks me as highly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is always traumatic; no one is adopted into<br /> the world of wolves without blood and screaming, and it is a<br /> miracle that any of these fresh-born Wolf-Blooded survive with<br /> anything like their lives and minds intact. Lunacy, possession,<br /> sexually transmitted pseudo-lycanthropy, and sometimes a severe<br /> reaction to the bite of a werewolf can create a Wolf-Blooded<br /> where one did not exist before. Uratha who research these things<br /> have found no pattern, and the circumstances that cause this<br /> to happen can\u2019t be machinated. It just happens sometimes at<br /> random, or sometimes with a strange poetry of fate. This is why<br /> so many Forsaken blame their spiritual Father and Mother for<br /> the existence of these spontaneous Wolf-Blooded.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's a bit of dissonance between the rules and the setting. My impression is that werewolves are at least aware of the fact that humans having run ins with werewolves have a higher chance of becoming wolf-blooded. The circumstances are just not as reliable as the rules suggest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068819#post1068819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have to be Wolf-blooded to undergo the First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Where do Werewolves come from? Not in the grand<br /> scheme, but in the immediate, visceral, bodily sense?<br /> Short and sweet, they come from Wolf-Blooded.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both quotes are from page 296.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:33:36-07:00","id":1068838,"title":"","content":"To me this reads as general wolf-bloodedness, in more instances than just Lunacy affliction.<br /> That they have no pattern for the general instances, I accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:50:08-07:00","id":1068856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068819#post1068819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have to be Wolf-blooded to undergo the First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>We talked about this in another thread some time ago. I'll see if I can dig it up. <br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't have to be (capital letter) Wolf-Blooded with Tells. Most aren't. They do all have to be (lower case) wolf-blooded, since Uratha aren't human and never were. (Lower case) wolf-blooded never get discussed, because they just look and act like normal humans. They have no way of knowing they carry the blood of the wolf until they undergo some kind of Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T14:01:32-07:00","id":1068865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068856#post1068856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We talked about this in another thread some time ago. I'll see if I can dig it up.<br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't have to be (capital letter) Wolf-Blooded with Tells. Most aren't. They do all have to be (lower case) wolf-blooded, since Uratha aren't human and never were. (Lower case) wolf-blooded never get discussed, because they just look and act like normal humans. They have no way of knowing they carry the blood of the wolf until they undergo some kind of Change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Makes sense. But are they all Lunacy-proof pre-change? Also, what are the rules on supernatural creatures and empowered humans and Lunacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T14:44:25-07:00","id":1068883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068856#post1068856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We talked about this in another thread some time ago. I'll see if I can dig it up. <br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't have to be (capital letter) Wolf-Blooded with Tells. Most aren't. They do all have to be (lower case) wolf-blooded, since Uratha aren't human and never were. (Lower case) wolf-blooded never get discussed, because they just look and act like normal humans. They have no way of knowing they carry the blood of the wolf until they undergo some kind of Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still iffy about this. I do understand what you're getting at - not all werewolves develop Tells before their First Change, and a person with werewolf heritage but no Tell isn't what the book describes as Wolf-Blooded (pg 300, &quot;A Wolf-Blooded is a Wolf-Blooded because of her Tell.&quot;) But there's nothing in the book that suggests to me a distinction exists between wolf-blooded and Wolf-Blooded. And in fact, in many places the implication seems to be that a Wolf-Blooded who's Tell has not yet manifested is still a Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> One of the places this is most clear is in the First Change Story section of the Storytelling chapter. Page 291: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Run through character creation as normal. Since these characters are all pre-First Change, the players should create Wolf-Blooded, complete with Tells from p. 300. If you want to limit the Tells to the less obvious shape-changing sort, or remove any others that don\u2019t appeal to you as a Storyteller, let the players know up-front of any limitations. Limited choices can speed up character creation and reinforce the themes you want to bring forward as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> If you want to leave all Tells on the table, just make sure your players understand that most Tells don\u2019t manifest until early puberty. For your teenage characters in this story, anything particularly strange, like seeing spirits or speaking the First Tongue, should have just started happening. A Tell coming up in-scene should add to the Tension pool.<br /> <br /> While the players are having a good time discussing Tells and deciding which they want for their characters, ask them to write you a note in secret, telling you if you they plan on having their characters go through the First Change or would rather the character remained Wolf-Blooded. Encourage them to remain quiet about the choice. If your players are okay with the idea, make the choice yourself. Just remind them while they\u2019re choosing Tells that their characters lose their Tells if they Change. Be open to them changing their mind as the story progresses. </div> </div> </div>A big part of your argument in the previous thread hinged on the fact that character creation doesn't ask the player to consider what Tell they had before First Change, or how they felt about losing their Tell, or anything of that sort. But I would make the counter-argument that character creation assumes the PCs have been werewolves for a while - at least long enough to earn 3 dots of Renown, join a Tribe, join a pack, and gain a Totem. On the other hand, <i>This</i> character creation session, which focuses on characters just before the First Change, assumes that they all have Tells, although some may not have manifested yet. The strong implication seems to me to be that all Werewolves are in fact Wolf-Blooded prior to First Change, but that some may First Change before their Tells first manifest, and others may have Tells subtle enough that they're not fully aware of them before First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:19:53-07:00","id":1068896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068799#post1068799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I question this. Werewolves will have noticed that some people exposed to Lunacy become wolf-blooded. And the tribes do keep lore on such things.<br /> That the Iron Masters, Bone Shadows, and (especially) the Ivory Claws wouldn't be aware of that fact smacks me as highly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy, like Luna, follow no rhyme or reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:37:01-07:00","id":1068906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068838#post1068838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me this reads as general wolf-bloodedness, in more instances than just Lunacy affliction.<br /> That they have no pattern for the general instances, I accept.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But there is no way to tell that someone Changed because of Lunacy or for another reason. So the same lack of pattern always applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:58:53-07:00","id":1068917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068906#post1068906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is no way to tell that someone Changed because of Lunacy or for another reason. So the same lack of pattern always applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. They're certainly aware that some humans randomly become Wolf-Blooded, but they can't discern a pattern behind when or why. Lunacy in particular would be very difficult to establish a connection to Wolf-Blooded adoptions, because there are a ton of people exposed to Lunacy who don't become Wolf-Blooded, and those who do don't remember it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:04:11-07:00","id":1068921,"title":"","content":"Isn't the whole &quot;lack of pattern&quot; thing just to excuse to give more freedom to the storyteller and players? Like, take a different splat- vampires are unique in that they're one of the only supernatural creatures that can deliberately make more of themselves. By the mechanics, <i>any</i> human character can potentially be turned into a vampire with a reasonable chance of success. Siring another vampire is choice that can be made both by the player and by the character in-universe.<br /> <br /> With werewolves, in-character you can't really decide to &quot;make&quot; another werewolf using Lunacy. But, if I'm playing a mortal character and decide I'd like to upgrade to Uratha, the rules allow me to work something out with the storyteller where that could happen...it's just a little more indirect than asking a vampire for the Embrace. In-character, it's just assumed retroactively that my character was always &quot;supposed&quot; to undergo First Change at that point, courtesy of Mother Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:11:53-07:00","id":1068924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068921#post1068921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the whole &quot;lack of pattern&quot; thing just to excuse to give more freedom to the storyteller and players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With werewolves, in-character you can't really decide to &quot;make&quot; another werewolf using Lunacy. </div> </div> </div>And this.<br /> <br /> I believe it was the same week the book came out someone asked incredulously why they couldn't just have a farm of humans constantly exposed to Lunacy until they got a Dramatic Failure, and that since the Pure would do that 'they would win,' or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:52:52-07:00","id":1068996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068924#post1068924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And this.<br /> <br /> I believe it was the same week the book came out someone asked incredulously why they couldn't just have a farm of humans constantly exposed to Lunacy until they got a Dramatic Failure, and that since the Pure would do that 'they would win,' or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, THAT is something I'd totally have an NPC *try* to do...with spectacular(ly bad) results!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:52:39-07:00","id":1069677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1068924#post1068924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was the same week the book came out someone asked incredulously why they couldn't just have a farm of humans constantly exposed to Lunacy until they got a Dramatic Failure, and that since the Pure would do that 'they would win,' or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviously, this is a solid chunk of a story I'm running right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:39:31-07:00","id":1069833,"title":"","content":"Someone posted a rite that makes wolfblooded, which include inflicting the tell. Homebrew, but it's something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:18:02-07:00","id":1070761,"title":"","content":"Ok, question, would having the Familiar Merit as a Werewolf make no sense at all, only in certain circumstances (Werewolf clearly outranking the Rank1-2 spirit), or is totally kosher? Related to that, wich kind of Rite (type and rating) would create such a Familiar bond?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:24:54-07:00","id":1070763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1070761#post1070761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, question, would having the Familiar Merit as a Werewolf make no sense at all, only in certain circumstances (Werewolf clearly outranking the Rank1-2 spirit), or is totally kosher? Related to that, wich kind of Rite (type and rating) would create such a Familiar bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, it wouldn't make sense because the Familiar Merit represents an Ephemeral with the Familiar Manifestation, which can normally only be obtained via the Spirit 4 Spell, Familiar. That said, it's probably not a bad way to mechanically represent a personal Totem or a Wolf-Blooded with the Familiar Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:48:02-07:00","id":1070776,"title":"","content":"Totem seems like a better way to do it. We have personal totems. We have the Merit.<br /> <br /> The differences in a Familiar are mostly that it stops Essence bleed and allows for casting of spells through the familiar, the latter of which would never come up. Also sharing of senses.<br /> <br /> As a bonus with Totem, you're not limited to Ranks 1-2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2017, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:59:50-07:00","id":1070980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1070776#post1070776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a bonus with Totem, you're not limited to Ranks 1-2.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a personal Totem you kind of are, as 5 dots of Attributes isn't enough to get a Spirit above Rank 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:42:32-07:00","id":1070995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1070980#post1070980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a personal Totem you kind of are, as 5 dots of Attributes isn't enough to get a Spirit above Rank 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can raise them further using the mechanics in the Pack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T20:47:23-07:00","id":1071016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1070995#post1070995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can raise them further using the mechanics in the Pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. I haven't read that one in a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:00:05-07:00","id":1071046,"title":"","content":"It's a good one. That section jibes with the whole 'playing the totem' bit too in case you use the, uh, troupe? method. I forget the term. Where you or your group can play multiple characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T04:46:10-07:00","id":1073032,"title":"","content":"Ok, not sure if this counts as a simple question, but there it goes:<br /> <br /> I want to create a power that can deal Persistent Tilts like Leg/Arm Wrack, Blind and similar in a &quot;Voodoo doll&quot; kind of style, but I am undecided if making it a set of Fetish iron coffin nails or a Rite. What do you think is the best aproach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:14:12-07:00","id":1073042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1073032#post1073032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, not sure if this counts as a simple question, but there it goes:<br /> <br /> I want to create a power that can deal Persistent Tilts like Leg/Arm Wrack, Blind and similar in a &amp;quot;Voodoo doll&amp;quot; kind of style, but I am undecided if making it a set of Fetish iron coffin nails or a Rite. What do you think is the best aproach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knee jerk response is to make it a fetish based on that Full Moon's Gift Facet that inflicts those Tilts in combat, but Rahu aren't exactly known for employing voodoo dolls...<br /> <br /> Were there any other Facets that inflict such Tilts? If so, then fetish. If not, then a rite. (My Werewolf crunch is flimsy, though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:18:54-07:00","id":1073043,"title":"","content":"If it's an object, make it a fetish. If it's an arcane procedure, a rite. Keep in mind that fetishes tend to be highly personal, with rites the knowledge can be widespread, and if you want to make it exclusive you may have to consider tying it to a lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:11:04-07:00","id":1073132,"title":"","content":"Seems like mechanically it would be a four dot fetish, as it's basically the Crimson Falx. Maybe with a pain spirit, though it really seems like it would be a wounded spirit type thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:08:39-07:00","id":1076364,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to read this entire topic and am somewhere on page 20, so please forgive me of this has been asked a few times cuz when I wanted to ask it I only saw it about vampires.<br /> <br /> A werewolf's fangs do lethal to vampires. Does that count against spirits even if you're not 2 ranks above, like, your claws or your gun do bashing against spirits even if they would do lethal because spirits do not have internal organs... but do your teeth do lethal still because of the resonance of Father Wolf?<br /> <br /> I also presume this power works against mage armors like the death one.<br /> <br /> I also presume you still have basically nothing against a strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:48:29-07:00","id":1076425,"title":"","content":"They have fire. That'll work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:13:13-07:00","id":1078328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1076364#post1076364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to read this entire topic and am somewhere on page 20, so please forgive me of this has been asked a few times cuz when I wanted to ask it I only saw it about vampires.<br /> <br /> A werewolf's fangs do lethal to vampires. Does that count against spirits even if you're not 2 ranks above, like, your claws or your gun do bashing against spirits even if they would do lethal because spirits do not have internal organs... but do your teeth do lethal still because of the resonance of Father Wolf?<br /> <br /> I also presume this power works against mage armors like the death one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are pretty unclear about this, so it's ultimately an ST call. Personally, I would rule that werewolves bites don't do lethal against spirits unless the werewolf has enough honorary rank to count as a Bane for the spirit. I would rule that they do cause lethal to mages using Death armor but not against mages using Spirit armor. And not against Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:48:17-07:00","id":1078773,"title":"","content":"I personally ruled that they can interact with Strix, via the Barghest facet of the Death Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T07:18:23-07:00","id":1078876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1078773#post1078773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally ruled that they can interact with Strix, via the Barghest facet of the Death Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense but, wouldn't the facet need to target shadows to affect strix, not merely death? Strix do not exist in twilight, they're smoke but anyone can see them with mundane senses.<br /> Not that it would be hard to make a facet that will effect them. A Shadow Wraith would have a Gift like that waiting to be ripped out of it for sure. But I can see why you chose Barghest in a pinch. I'm guessing you thought of all of this already? Since you used &quot;personally&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:28:55-07:00","id":1079201,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Uratha behavior. Let's say that there is a Locus on a forest and a group of Urathas have taken that as territory. Now theres this strange little group of teenagers that seems to somehow ignore the protection Rites and is going straight to the Locus. What the wolves do? <br /> <br /> 1 - The forest is far from the civilization.<br /> 2 - Wolf senses detect that the are just that, teenagers.<br /> 3 - The Locus is Uratha territory and it is sacred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:33:56-07:00","id":1079221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1079201#post1079201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Uratha behavior. Let's say that there is a Locus on a forest and a group of Urathas have taken that as territory. Now theres this strange little group of teenagers that seems to somehow ignore the protection Rites and is going straight to the Locus. What the wolves do?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the werewolves in question. There's an entire Lodge dedicated to making up urban legends to scare people away from sacred places and to give some 'cause' for the bodies that pop up. But plenty of loci are going to be in places people will stumble upon. A big one in first edition was a painting on the ground floor basement of a tall building. People would be passing by it and watching it all the time. In a lot of cases constant human presence are why things become loci in the first place. There's some people here who balk at the idea of playing characters that kill humans, and some who play characters who enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Also I don't believe there's any protective Rites, in the core at least. Might be thinking of Wards, from the Warding Gifts, and having someone just ignore those would be a huge red flag.<br /> <br /> At the very least, the werewolves would take note and observe them, using their various powers and senses to pull apart their secrets and figure out what they are and why they're there. Hunters in Darkness, especially, would keep an eye out for any violation of their sacred places.<br /> <br /> My character was never particularly territorial but if he was he'd probably eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:36:07-07:00","id":1079223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1078876#post1078876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense but, wouldn't the facet need to target shadows to affect strix, not merely death? Strix do not exist in twilight, they're smoke but anyone can see them with mundane senses.<br /> Not that it would be hard to make a facet that will effect them. A Shadow Wraith would have a Gift like that waiting to be ripped out of it for sure. But I can see why you chose Barghest in a pinch. I'm guessing you thought of all of this already? Since you used &quot;personally&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought about it, and decided to go for the easy way -- Using something that already exist instead of making up something new. I'm lazy like that.<br /> And it isn't TOO far off, after all, the Facet allows special interaction with vampires, Strix are close enough.<br /> ...<br /> Though looking at it, I think I should have added a &quot;pay Willpower&quot; requirement for the damage part.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:45:27-07:00","id":1079227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1079221#post1079221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big one in first edition was a painting on the ground floor basement of a tall building. People would be passing by it and watching it all the time. In a lot of cases constant human presence are why things become loci in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite remember that one (though it's admittedly been a couple years since my Werewolf 1e readthrough), but I do remember that the necessary accumulation of Essence to form a locus tends to mean that most naturally-occurring loci form in low-traffic areas, likely because of the whole &quot;human activity tends to birth a lot of spirits&quot; thing \u2014 do you happen to recall which book it was in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T22:27:45-07:00","id":1079238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1079227#post1079227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite remember that one (though it's admittedly been a couple years since my Werewolf 1e readthrough), but I do remember that the necessary accumulation of Essence to form a locus tends to mean that most naturally-occurring loci form in low-traffic areas, likely because of the whole &quot;human activity tends to birth a lot of spirits&quot; thing \u2014 do you happen to recall which book it was in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good memory. Apparently I conflated the Architects of Steel Locus, a painting, with the Silver Syndicate's Argentum building.<br /> <br /> My example of a people-heavy locus is now the one in the middle of the Bullring Shopping Centre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T04:00:56-07:00","id":1079318,"title":"","content":"The rules are pretty explicit, bites do lethal damage to everything. Even if they say they downgrade damage it's still lethal. Strix are made of smoke and shadows, but they still track damage they take from banes that aren't fire or sunlight. This means there is something there to tear into if you can.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are the preeminent hunters of the setting, and part of that is always being a potential threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:20:33-07:00","id":1079484,"title":"","content":"Technically, the rules say they count as mystical sources if vulnerable to such sources. Strix are NOT vulnerable to mystical sources. They can be damaged with things that do aggravated damage, and they have banes, but they have no general 'mystical sources' vulnerability to their damage immunity/downgrading like vampires do.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And frankly, I absolutely despise venue antagonists whose biggest weaknesses are 'Get help from another splat type'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T15:37:00-07:00","id":1079539,"title":"","content":"Nope, in Vampire you get help from someone with Obtenebration.<br /> <br /> A bane is as much a mystical weakness as you get in c ChroD. And I'm of the opinion if you are playing Werewolf we go with how they rule on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:15:53-07:00","id":1079575,"title":"","content":"Anything that has banes probably qualifies as having &quot;weakness to mystical sources&quot;. I have to assume that &quot;weakness to mystical sources&quot; does not mean a generic weakness to <i>all</i> mystical sources. Just that some mystical sources of damage are extra potent. Otherwise it would make no sense for vampires to explicitly take lethal from werewolf bites since vampires <i>do not</i> have a generic weakness to all mystical sources. They have very specific vulnerabilities against sunlight, fire and personal banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:39:08-07:00","id":1079578,"title":"","content":"What I was referring to is that supernatural lethal damage sources hurt vampires regularly. That's what that sidebar is referring to, IMO, and strix have no equivalent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T04:25:46-07:00","id":1080241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1079578#post1079578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was referring to is that supernatural lethal damage sources hurt vampires regularly. That's what that sidebar is referring to, IMO, and strix have no equivalent</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyhow, the Elemental Gift is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:19:22-07:00","id":1086996,"title":"","content":"So question about the Gauntlet <br /> <br /> I understand that the Gauntlet isn't just a barrier between worlds, but more of a divide in which Uratha, Spirits, powerful sorcerers, etc can pass. My question is this:<br /> <br /> I'm running a crossover game, and potentially thought in the future that the PCs could have a chapter physically crossing into The Gauntlet as a pass to enter The Shadow. Is this realistic and does this make sense in terms of how the Gauntlet works? Correct me if this interpretation is totally off/ wouldn't make sense in the usage of the Gauntlet. I also know of Loci, but I thought if they couldn't find one this may work. Thanks in advance - Look forward to your opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T22:23:46-07:00","id":1087014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1086996#post1086996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a crossover game, and potentially thought in the future that the PCs could have a chapter physically crossing into The Gauntlet as a pass to enter The Shadow. Is this realistic and does this make sense in terms of how the Gauntlet works? Correct me if this interpretation is totally off/ wouldn't make sense in the usage of the Gauntlet. I also know of Loci, but I thought if they couldn't find one this may work. Thanks in advance - Look forward to your opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's more of a void. It only takes seconds, and there's generally nothing there but sometimes there's exceptions.<br /> <br /> 'The seconds of travel in-between are spent hanging in a gray, mist-like void, feeling a claustrophobic pressure all around. Travelers are safe from attack while crossing, and can't move until they emerge on the other side.<br /> Some Uratha tell tales about encountering bizarre entities inside the Gauntlet - ghostly &quot;spirits,&quot; unnatural corpses of no known creature, splashes of blood, and other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited, always just on the edge of the paralyzed traveler's senses.'<br /> <br /> So putting some vestiges of things or some 'area' inside is fine, but it wouldn't be the normal way to go about things, and likely represent something strange happening to the Gauntlet at that location. Though obviously you can just change the game so the Gauntlet is its own place, in which case you might make it a sort of 'dead' Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T00:59:08-07:00","id":1087042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1087014#post1087014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically it's more of a void. It only takes seconds, and there's generally nothing there but sometimes there's exceptions.<br /> <br /> 'The seconds of travel in-between are spent hanging in a gray, mist-like void, feeling a claustrophobic pressure all around. Travelers are safe from attack while crossing, and can't move until they emerge on the other side.<br /> Some Uratha tell tales about encountering bizarre entities inside the Gauntlet - ghostly &quot;spirits,&quot; unnatural corpses of no known creature, splashes of blood, and other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited, always just on the edge of the paralyzed traveler's senses.'<br /> <br /> So putting some vestiges of things or some 'area' inside is fine, but it wouldn't be the normal way to go about things, and likely represent something strange happening to the Gauntlet at that location. Though obviously you can just change the game so the Gauntlet is its own place, in which case you might make it a sort of 'dead' Pangaea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats exactly what I was thinking of - I appreciate the clarification Nofather <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Now that you mention it - is there a book that explains what Pangea looks like? I remember reading something brief under the Sundering World in the Dark Eras, but I wasn't sure if there were any others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:49:29-07:00","id":1087186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1087042#post1087042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats exactly what I was thinking of - I appreciate the clarification Nofather <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Now that you mention it - is there a book that explains what Pangea looks like? I remember reading something brief under the Sundering World in the Dark Eras, but I wasn't sure if there were any others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sundering World is the only one that depicts it accurately and with mechanics. Beyond that it was mostly described in myths, like how the Spinner Hag used to web up entire villages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:17:26-07:00","id":1092350,"title":"","content":"So I've been looking through &quot;The Pack&quot; again, and I noticed the Primal Instincts Tell (page 59). It gives the Wolf-Blooded Primal Urge, which they can raise like a Werewolf would with Experiences. But that's gotta have some weird interactions with the fact that people who acquire major templates keep their Wolf-Blooded Tells. Or, at least, Mages keep them after Awakening. Does this mean that you could theoretically have a character who has both Primal Urge and Gnosis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:49:11-07:00","id":1092405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1092350#post1092350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's gotta have some weird interactions with the fact that people who acquire major templates keep their Wolf-Blooded Tells. Or, at least, Mages keep them after Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>P300, 'Unless she goes through the First Change, a Wolf-Blooded character retains her Tell if she becomes another kind of supernatural creature.' It's not limited to Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this mean that you could theoretically have a character who has both Primal Urge and Gnosis? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though they probably wouldn't stack. It's like the Supernatural Resistance Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:22:04-07:00","id":1092752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1092405#post1092405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P300, 'Unless she goes through the First Change, a Wolf-Blooded character retains her Tell if she becomes another kind of supernatural creature.' It's not limited to Mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Though they probably wouldn't stack. It's like the Supernatural Resistance Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Primal Urge Wolf Blood, who is also a skin thief, out of spite and desire to be a Werewolf. Who is then Embraced!<br /> We can make Samuel Haight yet...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:35:12-07:00","id":1092754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1092752#post1092752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! Primal Urge Wolf Blood, who is also a skin thief, out of spite and desire to be a Werewolf. Who is then Embraced!<br /> We can make Samuel Haight yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal Insticts Tell (Primal Urge) + retroactive Demon-blood by a pact + Awakens as a mage + Legacy that replicates the Kindred condition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:54:45-07:00","id":1092831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1092754#post1092754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primal Insticts Tell (Primal Urge) + retroactive Demon-blood by a pact + Awakens as a mage + Legacy that replicates the Kindred condition</div> </div> </div> </div>Yees... A Tremere Lich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T10:44:10-07:00","id":1092864,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd just convert Primal Urge dots bought <i>into </i>dots of Gnosis if the Wolf-Blooded character with the Primal Instincts Tell ever Awakened. I'd be predisposed to making them a Thyrsus, though I suppose other Paths could potentially fit, but the Primal Urge, as a concept, would suggest to me Gnosis that fits the Thyrsus perspective of the world. Not sure I would do if the character <i>wasn't </i>going to be a Thyrsus though. Probably still have Primal Urge convert to Gnosis. Not very fun if the player sinks all that XP into their Supernatural Resistance Trait only for it to be rendered useless if they become anything other than a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To continue on the insanity, I'm pretty sure Unchained Offspring retain access to their Embeds, their Cipher, and their Stigmata if they convert to another being, so you could theoretically have a Wolf-Blooded Offspring without anything rules-breaking going on. I'd argue it would be in bad taste except in fairly specific games, but I can't think of anything it would conflict with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 05-15-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:15:13-07:00","id":1092874,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine any player taking that specific Tell knowing that their character will be turned into a different major splat later, and I can't imagine any ST allowing that specific Tell in case the turning to a different major splat was supposed to be a surprise. So the XP thing wouldn't be a problem except in extremely fringe cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T00:44:48-07:00","id":1093142,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to prevent a werewolf from changing, force them to stay in Hishu form?<br /> Is there a way to drain all their Essence away to prevent them using gifts?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens to a werewolf that has been bound tightly, let's say with ropes, chains or manacles, and they change into Gauru or wolf form? How strong is the shapeshift when it comes to breaking bonds? I feel most any restraints that are used on a mortal would be useless against most werewolves, if not all of them.<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm getting at is, I'm trying to keep a werewolf prisoner. When it comes to the Pure, I would assume they might have access to a Fetish or Spirits, or something that drains a werewolf, but what if the captors are a bunch of humans or maybe vampires?<br /> <br /> Trapping them in a bunker would hold them, but I want a way to have someone torture and interrogate them while in the same room, staring them in the face. Spitting distance. More dramatic that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:38:06-07:00","id":1093211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1093142#post1093142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to prevent a werewolf from changing, force them to stay in Hishu form?<br /> Is there a way to drain all their Essence away to prevent them using gifts?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens to a werewolf that has been bound tightly, let's say with ropes, chains or manacles, and they change into Gauru or wolf form? How strong is the shapeshift when it comes to breaking bonds? I feel most any restraints that are used on a mortal would be useless against most werewolves, if not all of them.<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm getting at is, I'm trying to keep a werewolf prisoner. When it comes to the Pure, I would assume they might have access to a Fetish or Spirits, or something that drains a werewolf, but what if the captors are a bunch of humans or maybe vampires?<br /> <br /> Trapping them in a bunker would hold them, but I want a way to have someone torture and interrogate them while in the same room, staring them in the face. Spitting distance. More dramatic that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Dominate. A subconscious command that prevents them to shapeshift. Would cause flesh breaking points. Just try not to trigger the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 05-16-2017, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:53:33-07:00","id":1093254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1093142#post1093142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to drain all their Essence away to prevent them using gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Gifts that would allow this, and Numen. Idigam and strange Tilts in the Shadow, too. I think most splats have an 'energy drain' of some sort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what happens to a werewolf that has been bound tightly, let's say with ropes, chains or manacles, and they change into Gauru or wolf form? How strong is the shapeshift when it comes to breaking bonds? I feel most any restraints that are used on a mortal would be useless against most werewolves, if not all of them. </div> </div> </div>A werewolf could shift down, granting them much smaller size and allowing them to escape. Shifting up would probably cause some damage. There's a Gift to break free from any restraint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically what I'm getting at is, I'm trying to keep a werewolf prisoner. When it comes to the Pure, I would assume they might have access to a Fetish or Spirits, or something that drains a werewolf, but what if the captors are a bunch of humans or maybe vampires? </div> </div> </div>The Pure would use totems, or bring them into the Shadow or someplace where there's no locus. Humans wouldn't have much luck with a werewolf of any real power, as they are basically walking Essence batteries. But weaker werewolves without many Gifts and with moral problems might just end up stuck. Werewolves can also be forced into a blood bond, though as noted above if you keep a werewolf from shapeshifting, eventually their Harmony is going to shift and they're going to start going into Death Rages at the drop of a hat, and a blood bond might not protect from that. Might take a long time, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trapping them in a bunker would hold them, but I want a way to have someone torture and interrogate them while in the same room, staring them in the face. Spitting distance. More dramatic that way. </div> </div> </div>Find a weak or new werewolf. They might not have the abilities to get themselves out, their pack might not be able to either, or be able to get help, or they might be new enough they don't have one. Of course in that case they might not be able to answer anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-16-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:16:34-07:00","id":1094205,"title":"","content":"This is tangential to WtF 2E, so I hope this question is still OK.<br /> <br /> Is it against the rules to create a topic looking for a WtF group here? Or is the &quot;Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play&quot; sub-forum the only place?<br /> <br /> I ask because that sub-forum does not seem to attract many people and it is hard to find a group as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T03:09:59-07:00","id":1094480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guiskj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1094205#post1094205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is tangential to WtF 2E, so I hope this question is still OK.<br /> <br /> Is it against the rules to create a topic looking for a WtF group here? Or is the &quot;Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play&quot; sub-forum the only place?<br /> <br /> I ask because that sub-forum does not seem to attract many people and it is hard to find a group as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you wanna try that other subforum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:26:11-07:00","id":1095221,"title":"","content":"This question might be a bit hard for this thread, but how would you, as a story teller, help newly changed Werewolves character, only changed a week ago in game, understand their duty to their Tribe, Auspice, and Uratha in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13466-wyverian","name":"Wyverian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13466_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:50:42-07:00","id":1095289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyverian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1095221#post1095221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question might be a bit hard for this thread, but how would you, as a story teller, help newly changed Werewolves character, only changed a week ago in game, understand their duty to their Tribe, Auspice, and Uratha in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have their Mentor, or another werewolf, teach them. There's not much duty to them, really, beyond the Oath of the Moon, which different werewolves take different priorities regarding, and the tribal ban. There's often an introductory character who explains the basics, a lot can be intuited through play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T03:04:29-07:00","id":1095418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyverian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1095221#post1095221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question might be a bit hard for this thread, but how would you, as a story teller, help newly changed Werewolves character, only changed a week ago in game, understand their duty to their Tribe, Auspice, and Uratha in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>My game recently introduced a 10 years old new changee. My character's goal with him will be hiding him away in the Shadow till I can figure out his triggers and erode his harmony at the same time. Few things can put a Forsaken's world into perspective as displaying the spirit wilds and telling him &quot;we keep those away from people&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T03:33:03-07:00","id":1095424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1095418#post1095418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My game recently introduced a 10 years old new changee. My character's goal with him will be hiding him away in the Shadow till I can figure out his triggers and erode his harmony at the same time. Few things can put a Forsaken's world into perspective as displaying the spirit wilds and telling him &quot;we keep those away from people&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a reminder: Werewolves have Harmony 5 directly after the First Change. Starting characters are assumed to have maintained much of their human life which drags Harmony up to 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:03:45-07:00","id":1095430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1095424#post1095424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a reminder: Werewolves have Harmony 5 directly after the First Change. Starting characters are assumed to have maintained much of their human life which drags Harmony up to 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect: right after first change, the Harmony is set at 9. Naked, bloody rampages are still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:13:27-07:00","id":1095433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1095430#post1095430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect: right after first change, the Harmony is set at 9. Naked, bloody rampages are still a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had misread. I can't find where it specifies Harmony 9, but you're correct about Harmony being higher at First Change than at start of normal play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:46:56-07:00","id":1095441,"title":"","content":"P. 104, third paragraph under Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T05:44:28-07:00","id":1095452,"title":"","content":"Ain't I glad I'm behind a computer screen and don't have to physically face any of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T09:01:34-07:00","id":1095505,"title":"","content":"You might've picked that up from the Dark Eras book? In the neolithic, Werewolf PC's did indeed start at Harmony 5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T09:42:21-07:00","id":1095518,"title":"","content":"Thank's for saving me. The only one I <i>do</i> have to face IRL. That is indeed where I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T02:51:04-07:00","id":1112020,"title":"","content":"Questions about equipment and the Hisil/Reaching:<br /> When a werewolf reaches over from the material world into the Hisil, what happens to all of their possessions? Do they get all the gear they were carrying with them, clothes, weapons, backpacks etc. or do they drop down on the ground where the disappeared from and they arrive naked through the gauntlet?<br /> <br /> If they do take their equipment, to what extent? Guns, backpacks, duffel bags, corpses you are carrying, vehicles they are in/on? Also, does the equipment still work? I think it would be safe to assume melee weapons work just fine, but what about guns, explosives, electronics?<br /> <br /> And what about the other way around? Do stuff picked up from the Hisil come with you?<br /> <br /> Are there any weapons you can pick up in the Hisil itself? If you go to an armory, can you pick up a gun that has a representation over there? Not enough to be an awakened spirit but maybe someones favorite gun so it still shows? And would it work like an actual gun, (with unlimited bullets?)?<br /> <br /> I'm just having a really hard time with the whole transition thing and what is there and what is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T03:02:54-07:00","id":1112024,"title":"","content":"1- Unless the Uratha's Harmony is 9 or higher, their possessions transition normally. Even things you hold in your hand.<br /> <br /> If you can wear it or carry it, I let you Reach with it.<br /> <br /> 2- Depends on the stuff. Is the stuff an unawakened spirit? Then no. Is it a piece of corpus which became a talen? then sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T03:06:07-07:00","id":1112025,"title":"","content":"You can carry over all personal equipment. Not sure if you can carry over someone else without having to read the book. Either way everything that works in the Flesh should work in the Shadow. However, anything that originates in the Shadow is made out of ephemera and will just enter Twilight, collapse on itself, and dissipate if you bring it over to the Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T03:16:40-07:00","id":1112026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1112024#post1112024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can wear it or carry it, I let you Reach with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I say there, Brian Whose-Strength-Is-As-Great-As-The-Rules-Permit, why do you have a motorcycle strapped to your back?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hisill road trip&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:08:00-07:00","id":1112053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1112026#post1112026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I say there, Brian Whose-Strength-Is-As-Great-As-The-Rules-Permit, why do you have a motorcycle strapped to your back?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hisill road trip&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Riding it probably counts enough. We have fetish cars after all, and lodges dedicated to killing via car. If as a ST you find it weird you have the obvious limitation of room, where a weak locus inside a broom closet in the basement of a building would be hard to reach with a car. You could probably further limit it by requiring loci to be a certain power to let bigger things in.<br /> <br /> Rather than the logistics of getting across, the more difficult aspect would be taking advantage of your vehicle. The roads are spirits, if they don't want you there you better hope you brought a bunch of spare tires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1112020#post1112020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do take their equipment, to what extent? Guns, backpacks, duffel bags, corpses you are carrying, vehicles they are in/on? Also, does the equipment still work? I think it would be safe to assume melee weapons work just fine, but what about guns, explosives, electronics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, bring it over. Most of it will still work, but you're dealing with the spirit now. So everything's going to have a spirit attached. One of the examples in the Book of Spirits is a cell phone spirit that, now having access to Essence-rich humanity, decides to eat the brain of the human who's using it. It can be seen as a way to 'dispose' of things, but that's the sort of thing that would lead to repercussions in the long run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about the other way around? Do stuff picked up from the Hisil come with you? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much everything in the Hisil is a spirit, so you could bring it over but it would likely drift back when it ran out of Essence. Or go crazy devouring things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any weapons you can pick up in the Hisil itself? If you go to an armory, can you pick up a gun that has a representation over there? Not enough to be an awakened spirit but maybe someones favorite gun so it still shows? And would it work like an actual gun, (with unlimited bullets?)? </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of dormant and active spirits. While the vast majority are going to dislike werewolves, spirits do what spirits do. So using a gun spirit for a gun that doesn't get much action might wake it up in a good mood. Wouldn't likely have unlimited bullets, though. Even spirits run out of energy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just having a really hard time with the whole transition thing and what is there and what is not. </div> </div> </div>When it comes down to it, ruleswise, Werewolf tends towards 'letting you have it if it's more awesome.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:10:50-07:00","id":1112518,"title":"","content":"Thanks all for the great answers!<br /> <br /> Tomorrow is the first time ever that I'm ST:ing a Werewolf session (done some Vampire and Mortal before) where the players get introduced to the Hisil, so I'm really gathering all the info I can get. The spirits are a difficult thing to wrap my head around, even after reading sections about them over and over again. Influence for some reason is difficult for me to understand, also Bans and Banes are hard to come up with.<br /> <br /> My players started regular Mortal and I always gave them a choice if they wanted to go the Hunter, Vampire, Mage or Werewolf route. During/after several sessions they chose Werewolf, and the previous session began when they woke up after their First Change. One of my players is still at Harmony 9, but the other shifted to 8 already.<br /> <br /> I know their clothes rip at Harmony 9-10 when they shift, but is what Malus said considered &quot;canon&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1112024#post1112024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Unless the Uratha's Harmony is 9 or higher, their possessions transition normally. Even things you hold in your hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when a Harmony 9 goes across the Gauntlet, their clothes stay behind and fall on the floor and they arrive naked?<br /> <br /> Also, if anyone has any specific tips for a new Werewolf ST/players, those are very welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:31:17-07:00","id":1112547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1112518#post1112518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if anyone has any specific tips for a new Werewolf ST/players, those are very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make another thread for that. Or look them up. The biggest hurdle is usually portraying the Shadow and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T04:40:43-07:00","id":1115470,"title":"","content":"How does a Werewolf in full on Kuruth act? What is it motivated by? Does it want to absolutely try to hunt and kill something/anything as fast as it can, or does it only run and kill everything that happens on its path? How intelligent is it?<br /> <br /> A Vampire's Frenzy seems easier to grasp, since it's usually motivated by a clear reason. Anger, hunger, fear.<br /> <br /> But a Werewolf trigger can be any number of things. Like seeing the moon. No clear motivation for the rage, not like you can attack the moon.<br /> <br /> Example scenario from a session:<br /> A Werewolf is driven to Wasu-Im by an enemy in combat. That enemy is killed right after that by a pack member. The Rager manages to roll for 3 turns of control. He screams at the others to run and then books is as fast as it can in the other direction, deeper into he woods. The others run away to their car, ready to drive away if needed. After a moment they hear a rage filled howl.<br /> <br /> Now, would the raging werewolf remember that it was just in the company of a pack mate and turn around and try to kill him, or would he just continue running in the direction it was going, maybe scent an animal to hunt and eat, or go into the first building it comes across and kill people?<br /> <br /> At PU 1 it has 10 minutes to accomplish something, would it use that intelligently to hunt for enemies, or just keep running until it finds something? Would it care about &quot;action economy&quot; as in try to make the most of it like a PC would in combat, or could it just walk around a house, stalking through the halls?<br /> <br /> Also, does it retain any of his usual &quot;sane&quot; personality, or is pretty much every Death Rage Werewolf the same as another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:19:32-07:00","id":1115481,"title":"","content":"A Gauru has better senses than your average human, so it wouldn't rely merely on it's sight. Kuruth means it'll try to kill anything on it's path, starting with the weakest prey available. If it encounters a house, it'll detect entry points by scent, and hear people inside. Packmates who aren't in Kuruth become valid targets, those that succumb to it begin to work together towards the mayhem and death toll. Given it's virtual invulnerability, going all out becomes costumary. <br /> <br /> Regarding MOs I usually color them by auspice and tribe in terms of preferred tactics and prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:28:37-07:00","id":1115484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115470#post1115470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a Werewolf in full on Kuruth act? What is it motivated by? Does it want to absolutely try to hunt and kill something/anything as fast as it can, or does it only run and kill everything that happens on its path? How intelligent is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunt and kill. It will break stuff if there's nothing to hunt and kill, but this is working off of gauru senses and can likely find someone. It's not dumb, it's still got the vicious cunning of a monster. It's just single-minded.<br /> <br /> [quote[A Vampire's Frenzy seems easier to grasp, since it's usually motivated by a clear reason. Anger, hunger, fear.[/quote]<br /> <br /> In second edition you can set your own motivation for it, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a Werewolf trigger can be any number of things. Like seeing the moon. No clear motivation for the rage, not like you can attack the moon. </div> </div> </div>Look at it like this. Take away everything that's borne of being raised by humans, except the knowledge of the immediate. It doesn't care that that's the woman that raised you, it does recognize the leader of the hunters has a gun. Then take away the spiritual Oath and bindings of that. It's not after a sacred hunt, it's not concerned with Harmony. It's pure predator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Example scenario from a session:<br /> A Werewolf is driven to Wasu-Im by an enemy in combat. That enemy is killed right after that by a pack member. The Rager manages to roll for 3 turns of control. He screams at the others to run and then books is as fast as it can in the other direction, deeper into he woods. The others run away to their car, ready to drive away if needed. After a moment they hear a rage filled howl. </div> </div> </div>A point to remember, providing the packmates are also werewolves, they would be urged by their rampaging fellow to join him. P104, 'When an Uratha falls to Kuruth, the fire of the hunt rouses his packmates to a frenzy as well. Werewolf packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell the raging werewolf fall into Basu-Im after a turn.' It can be resisted but it's a potential outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, would the raging werewolf remember that it was just in the company of a pack mate and turn around and try to kill him, or would he just continue running in the direction it was going, maybe scent an animal to hunt and eat, or go into the first building it comes across and kill people?<br /> <br /> At PU 1 it has 10 minutes to accomplish something, would it use that intelligently to hunt for enemies, or just keep running until it finds something? Would it care about &quot;action economy&quot; as in try to make the most of it like a PC would in combat, or could it just walk around a house, stalking through the halls?<br /> <br /> Also, does it retain any of his usual &quot;sane&quot; personality, or is pretty much every Death Rage Werewolf the same as another? </div> </div> </div>It would probably head towards the closest prey, which might be its former company. It likely wouldn't be lured out by the insects in the woods. A bunch of people in a car is just asking for it.<br /> <br /> The intelligence and personality thing? It's going to depend on the character a bit. Like I said, they're not stupid. But different characters are going to act differently. I might look to the Blood archetypes in the Blood and Bone section to decide how specifically it's going to act. A werewolf with the Destroyer archetype might just wreck their way through the house, while one with the Monster might jump over it just so it could land on the car and attack in the scariest way possible. Other things could factor in, like auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:07:12-07:00","id":1115568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115484#post1115484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A point to remember, providing the packmates are also werewolves, they would be urged by their rampaging fellow to join him. P104, 'When an Uratha falls to Kuruth, the fire of the hunt rouses his packmates to a frenzy as well. Werewolf packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell the raging werewolf fall into Basu-Im after a turn.' It can be resisted but it's a potential outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminded me of a question I had been pondering. Does encountering a trigger and going to Wasu-Im immediately trigger a possible Basu-Im in a packmate? I had interpreted that passage to mean that a packmate entering Basu-Im triggers that in packmates as well. Otherwise it would be possible that the packmates go into Basu-Im before the person that was &quot;triggered&quot;, which seems wrong to me. I think they should have time enough to react and get away before they too are sucked in the vortex of death.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also as a side note, these &quot;ask a simple question&quot; threads are the best idea ever. So much stuff I've learned just reading through them and searching. Also, you've all been great at answering (and asking), immensely useful for people like me just running their first games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 07-13-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:39:18-07:00","id":1115583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115568#post1115568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminded me of a question I had been pondering. Does encountering a trigger and going to Wasu-Im immediately trigger a possible Basu-Im in a packmate? I had interpreted that passage to mean that a packmate entering Basu-Im triggers that in packmates as well. Otherwise it would be possible that the packmates go into Basu-Im before the person that was &quot;triggered&quot;, which seems wrong to me. I think they should have time enough to react and get away before they too are sucked in the vortex of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the 'fire of the hunt' only happens when someone goes Basu-Im. It also has a range limit, 10 yards, and you have to be able to see and smell the werewolf in Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> One can resist with a Resolve + Composure roll to get a turn, which may be enough to do something like use the Elodoth Gift. Or just rush out of range.<br /> <br /> Yeah I forget who started them, I think it was when Vampire came out. Really useful. Honestly I prefer more people talking about their games, but [i am cynical] those just devolve into criticisms about things that happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-13-2017, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:45:12-07:00","id":1115682,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that while in first edition, being in a lodge offers some benefits like decreased experience costs and other benefits, by the second edition core book lodges do not seem to offer any benefits at all.<br /> <br /> Do they?<br /> <br /> If not, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","user":"HelloMyNameIs","date":". 07-13-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:57:01-07:00","id":1115686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115682#post1115682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that while in first edition, being in a lodge offers some benefits like decreased experience costs and other benefits, by the second edition core book lodges do not seem to offer any benefits at all.<br /> <br /> Do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, just not decreased Experience costs. It gets detailed in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/181760/The-Pack?\" target=\"_blank\">the Pack</a> book.<br /> <br /> You get a Blessing that is a natural power, for instance the Thousand Steel Teeth Blessing, 'When she spends Willpower to add dice to a Drive roll, a Crafts roll to repair or modify a vehicle, or an Athletics roll to move between moving vehicles, the Lodge member gains the rote quality on that roll.'<br /> <br /> You get a Lodge Aspiration, which works in addition to other aspirations and helps you get extra Beats for doing something aligned with the lodge's goal. The Lodge of the Screaming Moon has the extra Aspiration 'To rule through fear.'<br /> <br /> There's a special variant of the Sacred Hunt each lodge has, which gives different blessings to pack members, not just lodge members, than the tribal ones in the core book. For the Lodge of Garm, for instance, 'The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense if the prey has a Primal Urge of 6 or higher. Your character retains her full Defense when making an all-out attack against such prey.'<br /> <br /> In addition, 'A Lodge usually possesses at least one rite, merit, or other advantage that an adherent can learn or gain, acquired at the usual cost in Experiences.' <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/181760/The-Pack?\" target=\"_blank\">The Pack</a> has a Fighting Style, a few fetishes, and a few rites, Lastly there are Lodge-only Merits, including Lodge Armory, Lodge Connections, Lorehouse, Stronghold, and Lodge Sorcery, which grants the ability to use the lodge totem's Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-13-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:04:40-07:00","id":1115905,"title":"","content":"Forsaken are branded by Luna for their auspice. The Pure are marked by their totem. I want to remember that in 1e wolf-blooded can be adopted into a tribe, and doing so marks them as well. Is there some formal element to this? Or is it more like a dog-tag (haha) and their pack keeping tabs on them? How, in other words, would spirits or another tribe/pack know that they're &quot;taken&quot;?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:14:39-07:00","id":1115909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115905#post1115905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forsaken are branded by Luna for their auspice. The Pure are marked by their totem. I want to remember that in 1e wolf-blooded can be adopted into a tribe, and doing so marks them as well. Is there some formal element to this? Or is it more like a dog-tag (haha) and their pack keeping tabs on them? How, in other words, would spirits or another tribe/pack know that they're &quot;taken&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just another werewolf saying, 'They're mine.' In first edition, at least. I don't know if they really got into the tribal or moon-born thing too much.<br /> <br /> In second it starts on p304. There's Merits for Tribal Affiliation, which can be a genetic or lineage thing or just a spontaneous, and Moon Birth Merits, for those with a closeness to Luna. As for how spirits would know, it might be because due to being a member of a pack they would have a strange Resonance relating to their totem. In some cases it might seem normal like a pack whose totem is about Law and Order and the wolf-blooded being a cop, but other spirits and potentially werewolves might notice something strange in a wolf-blooded with a Shark resonance or something.<br /> <br /> Beyond that I don't think there would be an automatic way to tell if someone is a member of a pack beyond interacting with them or, at least, watching them to see if they interact with a pack. Certainly if they did have some sort of obvious marker it would make hiding among mankind much harder. I'm sure it happens that occasionally a wolf-blood who doesn't know they're a member of a pack might be taken by another werewolf who wants them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:16:51-07:00","id":1115911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115905#post1115905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to remember that in 1e wolf-blooded can be adopted into a tribe, and doing so marks them as well. Is there some formal element to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially? No. There's design space to come up with a rite for such purpose. In 1e, discovering someone was a wolfblood was harder than nowadays, and didn't add much play value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115905#post1115905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is it more like a dog-tag (haha) and their pack keeping tabs on them? How, in other words, would spirits or another tribe/pack know that they're &quot;taken&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could announce it down the spiritual grapevine, but my characters would silently watch over their charges and only involve themselves with the blooded if they were in trouble they couldn't get off on their own. Advertising who you watch out for in many respects would lead you down the path of Spiderman in Civil War. Poor, poor Aunt May.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:20:46-07:00","id":1115914,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, that makes sense: if they're &quot;human with wolf-spirit bits&quot; then representing ties with merits is a mechanically elegant way to go. Spirits would know quickly they're wolf-blooded, but otherwise the resonance clinging to them is the clue. And yeah, walking around with a big billboard brand is a good way of lowering the infiltration utility/painting a target on your junior packmates--be you Forsaken or Pure.<br /> <br /> Plus cuts down on drama around &quot;you're messing wit my humans!&quot; Which is a basic WtF trope.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:34:19-07:00","id":1116510,"title":"","content":"Are there rules for official challenges? How they're done, rules they go by? Anything like that? <br /> <br /> Maybe they're in a book I missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:52:50-07:00","id":1116545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1116510#post1116510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules for official challenges? How they're done, rules they go by? Anything like that?<br /> <br /> Maybe they're in a book I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, they're going to go on a pack by pack basis. One pack of martial-heavy wolves might due a standard duel, another pack with a broad territory might task a riddle spirit for a scavenger hunt, a spirit-heavy group might just put things up to the spirits.<br /> <br /> Further information is scattered throughout the books, like the Rage, which has a brief section on Conflicts and how they're resolved. More specific information can probably found in Signs of the Moon, which details what the various auspices tend to be like and how they act and deal with things, Tribes of the Moon, which does the same for the five Forsaken tribes, and the Pure, which does the same for the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:28:30-07:00","id":1116706,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is a silly question but looking in the book.. it seems like once you have a trigger (which you need specific ones written for your character?), you automatically fall into soft rage without a roll to resist it. From there, you have to roll res+comp in order to do any other action during your &quot;control time&quot; and if that fails, you go straight up Kuruth. Is this right? Is it really that automatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T22:06:30-07:00","id":1116725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1116706#post1116706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is a silly question but looking in the book.. it seems like once you have a trigger (which you need specific ones written for your character?), you automatically fall into soft rage without a roll to resist it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can either take the existing triggers on p103 or make three up. There's also general triggers. How you're affected by them will depend on your Harmony. At Harmony 5, for instance, you're only affected by your general triggers. The farther away, the more triggers you'll have, harder they are to avoid, and the less time you'll have to maintain your cool and find someplace safe to rage. A starting character at Harmony 7 is only affected by Specific Triggers, which are easier to avoid or prepare for, as well as giving you a few minutes to resist further raging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From there, you have to roll res+comp in order to do any other action during your &quot;control time&quot; and if that fails, you go straight up Kuruth. Is this right? Is it really that automatic? </div> </div> </div>Yes, with a caveat. There are other ways to deal with it, from Gifts like Still Small Voice which pulls Uratha out of Wasu-Im, or the Chain Rage rite, which gives you considerable breathing room. The Controlled Burn Merit works similarly, though is probably easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-16-2017, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:01:45-07:00","id":1116804,"title":"","content":"Also, each trigger only affects you once a day. If you see your auspice moon but somehow get to avoid Kuruth, you don't have to worry about that until next night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:44:28-07:00","id":1117328,"title":"","content":"Is being stripped of renown dots a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:50:37-07:00","id":1117334,"title":"","content":"No. I think it's in Apocalypse, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:26:23-07:00","id":1117405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117328#post1117328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is being stripped of renown dots a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so far, no. Such a rite would need to be at least rank 5, as you're tampering with something inherent to the character's spiritual make-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:46:58-07:00","id":1117481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117405#post1117405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so far, no. Such a rite would need to be at least rank 5, as you're tampering with something inherent to the character's spiritual make-up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the spirits never take away renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:48:43-07:00","id":1117483,"title":"","content":"Are there any stats in any of the books for Lunes or Firstborn (or advocates of the firstborn)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:05:59-07:00","id":1117489,"title":"","content":"For Lunes, yes, in Signs if the Moon I think. Firstborn are beyond stats","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:12:43-07:00","id":1117490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117481#post1117481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So the spirits never take away renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Renown in Forsaken, despite the name, is less about social recognition and more about personal growth. Renown is of the werewolf's own virtue, not something bestowed by the spirits, so the spirits cannot take it away.<br /> <br /> But then again, the world is filled with aberrations in the CoD. Nothing prevents you from introducing a powerful Big Bad who <i>can </i>strip Renown from the Uratha, in a blatant deviance against the order of the world. Probably an <i>idigam </i>or a crazed Rank 5+ lune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:13:23-07:00","id":1117491,"title":"","content":"There's one of the first primary types of lune in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a> book, along with the lesser glimmerings, and other special ones scattered throughout the rest of the books. Even with the change in edition, Predators is a really useful resource in regards to spirits and other werewolf antagonists. <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/27863/World-of-Darkness-Book-of-Spirits?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">The Book of Spirits</a> is good, too, but primarily for spirits, as it's more about the spirit world.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn and Secondborn are generally too powerful to be written up in stats, but Predators has powerful spirits that could be lesser messengers of them. Or if they show up in your games themselves you could use it as a plot element. Fenris-Ur, of the Blood Talons, is in Basra, and the affects of it are described in the core book in the Basra Hunting Ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:39:39-07:00","id":1117545,"title":"","content":"What have you guys done with 'create technology' in your stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:58:33-07:00","id":1117557,"title":"","content":"Do you mean Influence: Technology 4?<br /> <br /> I've never encountered one or built one, but it would be pretty nasty, depending on how it was Technologically bent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:03:55-07:00","id":1117580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117557#post1117557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean Influence: Technology 4?<br /> <br /> I've never encountered one or built one, but it would be pretty nasty, depending on how it was Technologically bent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Am i in the wrong place?<br /> <br /> I meant this. <br /> <br /> Create Technology (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> To a master of technological animism, complicated <br /> devices are simply another element to be conjured up at <br /> will. This Gift allows a werewolf to create sophisticated <br /> technology from the basest materials. <br /> Cost: 1 Essence + 1 Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Crafts + Cunning<br /> Action: Extended (5 to 50 successes required; one <br /> turn passes per roll)<br /> The character must have some foundation materials, <br /> such as metal or plastic, roughly equivalent in mass to the <br /> item she wishes to create. She must also either know how <br /> to build the item in question or have access to instructions <br /> on how to construct such a thing. A character cannot cre-<br /> ate a complicated bomb without either extensive knowl-<br /> edge of explosives or a manual or other set of instructions <br /> on how to create the object in question. Within these <br /> limitations, this Gift can quickly and efficiently replicate <br /> almost any technology imaginable. With a few pounds of <br /> scrap metal and sand, for example, she can create a rudi-<br /> mentary computer. Or a handful of glass could be trans-<br /> formed into a magnifying glass. The more complex the <br /> item is, the more successes are required. A dozen bullets <br /> may be formed with as few as five successes, a pistol 15, <br /> while a car or computer would take a total of 50.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:12:37-07:00","id":1117584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117580#post1117580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. Am i in the wrong place?<br /> <br /> I meant this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow, first edition. No, not in the wrong place. We just talk more about second lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:22:38-07:00","id":1117590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1117584#post1117584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, wow, first edition. No, not in the wrong place. We just talk more about second lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, i thought it looked pretty cool. <br /> <br /> And a nice shoutout to the dataprobe thing. <br /> <br /> So have you guys used it before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:38:35-07:00","id":1119503,"title":"","content":"So the 2e core rulebook states that &quot;Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha.&quot;<br /> <br /> What kind of thing deals agg through &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot;, and how do you tell the difference between that and something that merely causes enough lethal/bashing to wrap around and kill you? For example, if you drop a wrecking ball on a human, they obviously die. But do they die because the &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot; deals aggravated damage directly, or because they just took like 20 lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:50:36-07:00","id":1119507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1119503#post1119503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the 2e core rulebook states that &quot;Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha.&quot;<br /> <br /> What kind of thing deals agg through &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot;, and how do you tell the difference between that and something that merely causes enough lethal/bashing to wrap around and kill you? For example, if you drop a wrecking ball on a human, they obviously die. But do they die because the &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot; deals aggravated damage directly, or because they just took like 20 lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of explosives cause aggravated damage at their ground zero distance, this is an example of damage that would merely cause lethal damage to Uratha, off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> When I hear the phrase &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot; I picture actual loss of limb, not something like a neck snapping. I'd treat the wrecking ball like a car collision, indeed in this case, copious amounts of lethal damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:55:36-07:00","id":1119509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1119503#post1119503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the 2e core rulebook states that &quot;Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha.&quot;<br /> <br /> What kind of thing deals agg through &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot;, and how do you tell the difference between that and something that merely causes enough lethal/bashing to wrap around and kill you? For example, if you drop a wrecking ball on a human, they obviously die. But do they die because the &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot; deals aggravated damage directly, or because they just took like 20 lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In Chronicles of Darkness games,aggravated damage is a catch-all representing extremely serious injuries: the crushed bones, deep cuts, and other nasty things that toss characters at death\u2019s door.&quot;<br /> <br /> What comes to my mind first are explosives. If you are at ground zero of an explosive, it does aggravated instead of lethal. Pretty much stuff that you could rule do permanent damage to a mortal, like for example if your hand gets crushed to bits by a crusher, it might not be the best idea to have that damage represented by doing so much damage as to roll over, but for mortals an arm wrack caused by aggravated is permanent damage. So you would lose that hand completely, but might suffer only something like 2-3 aggravated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Another example that came to mind is let's say someone cuts a persons fingers off completely, that should likely be aggravated to represent permanent loss, but perhaps that could be downgraded to lethal if there is sufficient medical attention, such as someone is fast enough to reattach those fingers before the tissue dies completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 07-23-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T19:40:09-07:00","id":1120592,"title":"","content":"Is there any rules for swarms? I cant find any, like a swarm of a Host of rats. How does one handle them? I got the stats for a rat but little else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T20:17:53-07:00","id":1120605,"title":"","content":"Animals of Size 1 are generally best represented by swarms, flocks and other groupings of the animals. Swarms are measured by their radius in yards. A swarm inflicts one point of bashing damage to anyone within its radius. <br /> A swarm can inflict more damage by condensing. Every time the swarm condenses to cover half of its full area, it inflicts one additional point of damage per turn.<br /> Therefore, a swarm of eight yards in radius inflicts two bashing damage per turn if it constricts down to a fouryard radius, three bashing if it halves that again to a two-yard radius, and four bashing damage per turn it if condensed itself down to a one-yard radius. Though condensing doesn\u2019t usually happen all that often in nature (save in the case of creatures such as killer bees), it is an easy enough thing for a being with supernatural powers to command them to do so.<br /> Armor is effective against a swarm only if it covers one\u2019s full body, but even then it provides only half its rating. In addition, targets are distracted by the swarm, suffering \u20132 dice on all rolls while they are within the radius, even if they\u2019re not specifically attacked.<br /> Causing the Tilt: The Swarm Exploit can cause this Tilt, as can similar powers from non-demonic sources. The Tilt can occur naturally if someone disturbs a nest of bees. <br /> Ending the Tilt: The swarm cannot be attacked with fists, clubs, swords or guns. Only area-affect attacks such as a torch affect it. Each point of damage inflicted by a flame or other applicable attack halves the swarm\u2019s size. Once the swarm is reduced below a one-yard radius, either all insects are dead or the few remaining disperse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T20:46:58-07:00","id":1120619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1120592#post1120592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any rules for swarms? I cant find any, like a swarm of a Host of rats. How does one handle them? I got the stats for a rat but little else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, as an option if you want something perhaps simpler: On p.121 of CoD core culebook the stats for a trained guard dog are given. At the end of them it says they also double as stats for a &quot;swarm of vermin&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Attributes: Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 3,<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Presence 3,<br /> Manipulation 0, Composure 1<br /> General Dice Pools: Born Survivor 7, Marathon<br /> Runner 7, Aggressive Growl 5<br /> Combat Dice Pools: Bite 6, Tackle 6<br /> Initiative Modifier: +5<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 0<br /> Size: 4<br /> Speed: 12<br /> Doubles as: K-9 hound, wild animal, swarm of<br /> vermin, genetic experiment.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:21:20-07:00","id":1120766,"title":"","content":"Thanks both for the answers. I am gonna go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13318\" data-vbnamecard=\"13318\">Cainite</a> option as the other would require the pc to have a area of effect attacks to hit the beshilu swarm otherwise they would keep getting hit with 1 bashing per turn indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:44:27-07:00","id":1120775,"title":"","content":"The massive scything claws and crushings fists of Gauru could count as &quot;area-affect&quot; if you wanted them to. But imo a big part of what makes the Hosts scary is that you can't really solve a beshilu problem by picking a fight with a swarm of rats. Recall the between-chapter fiction of the pack dealing with rat hosts, in which the werewolves are forced to retreat because picking a fair fight with a billion rats isn't a feasible solution even in the short term. I know it's Werewolf, but sometimes it's okay to face the players with an encounter they have to escape from or prepare for. Also werewolves regenerate at least one bashing per turn, so it's more of a stalemate than an inevitably loss.<br /> <br /> 'course if you want to let your players just club 'em to death, do that. I'd personally still include the -2 penalty - no matter how they're represented mechanically, being covered in angry rats seems like it would be pretty distracting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:30:09-07:00","id":1120856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1120775#post1120775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The massive scything claws and crushings fists of Gauru could count as &quot;area-affect&quot; if you wanted them to. But imo a big part of what makes the Hosts scary is that you can't really solve a beshilu problem by picking a fight with a swarm of rats. Recall the between-chapter fiction of the pack dealing with rat hosts, in which the werewolves are forced to retreat because picking a fair fight with a billion rats isn't a feasible solution even in the short term. I know it's Werewolf, but sometimes it's okay to face the players with an encounter they have to escape from or prepare for. Also werewolves regenerate at least one bashing per turn, so it's more of a stalemate than an inevitably loss.<br /> <br /> 'course if you want to let your players just club 'em to death, do that. I'd personally still include the -2 penalty - no matter how they're represented mechanically, being covered in angry rats seems like it would be pretty distracting.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons Meninna (Hunters in Darkness) are so good at dealing with Hosts is the Elemental Gift, making their habitats suddenly deadly inhabitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:46:49-07:00","id":1120869,"title":"","content":"Plus even at Primal Urge 1, 1 Bashing per turn isn't a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:05:37-07:00","id":1121012,"title":"","content":"With the tilt my issue is also that it doesnt specify damage needed to end the tilt. I prefer hard mechanics like &quot;you need to deal X damage to kill Y thing&quot; specially for things that the PCs hunt. I will use part of the tilt however in the sense that once they kill the &quot;guarded dog&quot; it doesnt mean that the swarm dies but that they disperse with the AoE attack needed to finish the job once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:00:13-07:00","id":1121174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1120856#post1120856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons Meninna (Hunters in Darkness) are so good at dealing with Hosts is the Elemental Gift, making their habitats suddenly deadly inhabitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e's sole change to the core Gift affinities means it's not so much this as the Nature and Warding Gifts; Knotted Paths, Black Earth Red Hunger, and basically every Facet of Warding except Predator's Claim provides vital means of catching unobtrusive prey or locking down swarms. Elemental's gone to the Bone Shadows instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:15:07-07:00","id":1122031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1115909#post1115909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's just another werewolf saying, 'They're mine.' In first edition, at least. I don't know if they really got into the tribal or moon-born thing too much.<br /> <br /> In second it starts on p304. There's Merits for Tribal Affiliation, which can be a genetic or lineage thing or just a spontaneous, and Moon Birth Merits, for those with a closeness to Luna. As for how spirits would know, it might be because due to being a member of a pack they would have a strange Resonance relating to their totem. In some cases it might seem normal like a pack whose totem is about Law and Order and the wolf-blooded being a cop, but other spirits and potentially werewolves might notice something strange in a wolf-blooded with a Shark resonance or something.<br /> <br /> Beyond that I don't think there would be an automatic way to tell if someone is a member of a pack beyond interacting with them or, at least, watching them to see if they interact with a pack. Certainly if they did have some sort of obvious marker it would make hiding among mankind much harder. I'm sure it happens that occasionally a wolf-blood who doesn't know they're a member of a pack might be taken by another werewolf who wants them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forgive me, but I'd like to ask a set of follow-ups. Wolf-blooded are so often it seems just *assumed* to be around, already connected to packs, that I perceive a distinct gap between &quot;normal human herdling&quot;, &quot;unaligned (frequently unaware) wolf-blood&quot; and &quot;aligned and useful wolf-blood&quot;. <br /> <br /> As well we have several strong clues as to how Forsaken and Pure packs react to unknown werewolves in their territory (i.e. generally not favorably). But less I think regarding wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> If the pack has a way to identify wandering wolf-blooded, how could we expect them to react if:<br /> 1. There is some possibility the wolf-blooded are unaligned or do not know they are wolf-blooded; in other words, they are not knowingly under direction by a pack.<br /> 2. The pack is within their territory versus outside of it (either invited to a neighbor's territory or in unclaimed territory, hunting or no).<br /> <br /> Generally I would assume that a pack hunting within enemy territory encountering an unknown wolf-blooded would result in Action!--at least from the wolf-blood's perspective....<br /> <br /> Also, how might reactions vary between Forsaken and Pure? I assume this is where the rubber meets the roadkill for &quot;The High Respect the Low;&quot; the Pure don't do that bit.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> To frame the matter: I have PCs who have decided they want to be wolf-blooded, wandering around a medieval era under mundane orders and invitations. They signed up for this, but I'm trying to understand what is reasonable behavior by the inevitable packs they collide with, before said packs end up severely restricting said PCs' agency....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:06:24-07:00","id":1122047,"title":"","content":"Huge text dump, apologies ahead of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1122031#post1122031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me, but I'd like to ask a set of follow-ups. Wolf-blooded are so often it seems just *assumed* to be around, already connected to packs, that I perceive a distinct gap between &quot;normal human herdling&quot;, &quot;unaligned (frequently unaware) wolf-blood&quot; and &quot;aligned and useful wolf-blood&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty accurate way to look at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the pack has a way to identify wandering wolf-blooded, how could we expect them to react if:<br /> 1. There is some possibility the wolf-blooded are unaligned or do not know they are wolf-blooded; in other words, they are not knowingly under direction by a pack. </div> </div> </div>First remember that detecting wolf-blooded is possible but requires some closeness. From there, feeling them out might be different from one group to another. Suggesting something about wolves might get the wolf-blooded to react a certain way so you know they're 'in the know,' without necessarily overplaying your hand by, say, turning into a giant wolf and potentially scaring them. This actually happened to me in my game and it went about as bad as it could have.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of detective abilities werewolves have access to. Something like 'Know Thy Prey' might clue a werewolf in to whether they're part of a pack as it shows a lot of social Merits.<br /> <br /> A lot might depend on the atmosphere. If a pack is being besieged by the Pure, this wolf-blooded might be some sort of spy. If the wolf-blooded is a particularly nasty looking fellow, with the scent of gun oil and silver, you might watch out. But otherwise some casual questions might help you figure out what they're there for, and if they're up for grabs. 'Do you live nearby?' or 'I work down the street, how bout you?' can be asked in so many different ways, and if a wolf-blooded is just visiting it might not be worth attempting to recruit them. If they live in your territory it's worth keeping tabs on them, at the least. You can get to know them better and if they seem not entirely afraid of the werewolf life, like they aren't freaked out about their Tell and Boon, then bringing them in is likely to go smoother. It helps that there's some sort of inherent incentive for wolf-blooded, they feel better when part of a pack and with werewolves.<br /> <br /> 'Being pulled into a pack is as natural a thing as most Wolf-Blooded will ever feel in their lifetimes. This is why so many Wolf-Blooded are fiercely loyal to the pack. Not to any one member, but to the pack itself. It is a home and family and lifeline and sanity that some of them have never fully experienced before.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The pack is within their territory versus outside of it (either invited to a neighbor's territory or in unclaimed territory, hunting or no). </div> </div> </div>Inside your territory, if the wolf-blood is a permanent resident or works there, you're definitely going to want to do something about it. Just finding out if they're part of a larger pack and, if so, what that pack's relationship with yours is would be important. If your pack is outside their territory, or nomadic, you would probably be more reluctant to strike up any long term relationships, as any wolf-blooded potentially belongs to another pack, and it's quite likely they'll be angry if some stranger is sniffing around. This obviously leads to good plothooks and it's not always entirely up to the werewolf. Even aside from things like the Exciting Tell, there's plenty of ways for a wolf-blooded to just get wrapped up in your life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally I would assume that a pack hunting within enemy territory encountering an unknown wolf-blooded would result in Action!--at least from the wolf-blood's perspective.... </div> </div> </div>Likely. The wolf-blood might lead you right to your target, especially if it's a werewolf, human, or another wolf-blooded. If it's something unrelated you might just skip over the wolf-blooded. But they can act as hidey holes for spirits, heralds and servants to idigam, and hosts for hosts. They might even be able to tell you something useful about the neighborhood they know and no one else does. Interacting with them could be dangerous for other reasons, though. If the pack whose territory you're in is vicious you might want to keep your head down for the hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how might reactions vary between Forsaken and Pure? I assume this is where the rubber meets the roadkill for &quot;The High Respect the Low;&quot; the Pure don't do that bit. </div> </div> </div>Forsaken are more likely to negotiate and talk things through. Pure are more likely to just take. They're not stupid, though, so they might stalk a bit to see if they could get more, like if they go home and there's a whole house full of wolf-blooded. Or if the wolf-blooded is protected somehow, which wouldn't necessarily stop them but may give them pause to organize more. Ivory Claws are probably the most vampire-like, moving things around so that the wolf-blooded gets fired and has to work in their territory. Slaughtering a family and somehow the wolf-blooded finds out that there's a house for sale really cheap, they just have to move. Then once the wolf-blooded is all settled in the werewolf introduces himself. The Pure aren't the only ones who can do that, though, some Forsaken are going to be brutal and ghost wolves like the Temple of Apollo are probably really good at recruiting, being a cult and all.<br /> <br /> Something else I wanted to point out. There's a rite that hasn't been talked about much. Hunting Ground. The book doesn't say this outright but the way we rule it is that, unless you've used this rite, a Gift or Rite that works 'on your territory' doesn't have nearly as much range. In addition, and this is RAW, it definitively outlines your territory, so you wouldn't wander into someplace and not realize you were setting foot on another werewolf's territory unless you were being really unobservant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T19:03:56-07:00","id":1122164,"title":"","content":"Has anyone home-converted the Ananasi for Nwod or chronicles? Or homebrewed something similar? I've already looked at changing breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T19:13:40-07:00","id":1122165,"title":"","content":"Have you checked out the Azlu, in Predators? It's a more monstrous take but they are spiders and spider-people and giant spider monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T03:00:00-07:00","id":1122277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1122165#post1122165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you checked out the Azlu, in Predators? It's a more monstrous take but they are spiders and spider-people and giant spider monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was aware of them, but haven't actually read it. My ST was asking about playable werespiders and I think the Azlu might be too monstrous for a PC option, if there are even mechanics for it. It's a mixed chronicle, but would an Azlu be willing/able to cooperate with mortals and other supernaturals, including possibly a werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T09:38:52-07:00","id":1122371,"title":"","content":"Oh, as-written the Azlu are totally unplayable. <br /> <br /> But you <i>could</i> use some of their mechanics in a conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T10:48:56-07:00","id":1122392,"title":"","content":"Yeah port their different shapes over for shapeshifting, offer some of their mechanical powers in place of gifts or rites.<br /> <br /> You could just make a werewolf and give him spider forms instead of wolf ones, using the azlu as a template.<br /> <br /> Without the Weaver, do the Ananasi really have much to them, beyond being blood-drinking spider people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T13:16:12-07:00","id":1122454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1122392#post1122392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without the Weaver, do the Ananasi really have much to them, beyond being blood-drinking spider people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not, but they seem preferable to the Spinner- Kin for a lot of reasons. <br /> <br /> I'll mention the possibility of converting the Azlu to him, though, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T06:03:35-07:00","id":1122988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1122047#post1122047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huge text dump, apologies ahead of time.<br /> <br /> *snippity!*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, your experience is most welcome! It looks like the sum is: how packs behave is entirely dependent on their circumstances and characteristics, but they don't have a sure-fire way to finger an unknown wolf-blood (short of close contact, possibly extended and via interrogation). And how direct they may be in &quot;dealing with&quot; the problem will depend on how confident they feel at the time and other, specific circumstances and goals.<br /> <br /> In other words, packs (even Pure) are made of people, who just happen to turn into wolves and eat spirits....<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T06:19:52-07:00","id":1122993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1122988#post1122988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, your experience is most welcome! It looks like the sum is: how packs behave is entirely dependent on their circumstances and characteristics, but they don't have a sure-fire way to finger an unknown wolf-blood (short of close contact, possibly extended and via interrogation). And how direct they may be in &quot;dealing with&quot; the problem will depend on how confident they feel at the time and other, specific circumstances and goals.<br /> <br /> In other words, packs (even Pure) are made of people, who just happen to turn into wolves and eat spirits....</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that's a good way of looking at it.<br /> <br /> There are some tendencies and stuff you can see mentioned throughout the books like Tribes of the Moon and the Pure or War Against the Pure would obviously have some tactics of the various groups. But werewolves 'grow up' in different circumstances and place their emphasis on the hunt in different things, so their priorities and methods and so forth are more based on the individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:10:35-07:00","id":1127586,"title":"","content":"This is probably in the book but i can't seem to find it. <br /> How does new members get introduced in the packs? And how large is a pack? Im not really talking about the Uratha, but about woolf-blooded and normal humans. Mostly normal humans. Becouse as far as i know, they also get the Totem gift-thing and many gifts and such only applies to pack members<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:09:27-07:00","id":1127676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1127586#post1127586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]How does new members get introduced in the packs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any way the pack needs. Some might just stumble upon the secret and have to be informed, others might go through a ceremony or initiation of some sort. It's going to vary pack to pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And how large is a pack? Im not really talking about the Uratha, but about woolf-blooded and normal humans. Mostly normal humans. Becouse as far as i know, they also get the Totem gift-thing and many gifts and such only applies to pack members </div> </div> </div>The Totem Advantage isn't in the form of a Gift. The Totem gives you Merits, Skill Specialties, Skills, or Attributes. Packs can really be as small as four people, or as large as a hundred. Some might not have humans at all, while some in very close territories might consider everyone inside a member of the pack. Going by character creation, each werewolf has one wolf-blooded, then 1-3 humans. If you're working on creating some packs, that's a median you can go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:30:04-07:00","id":1127688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1127676#post1127676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any way the pack needs. Some might just stumble upon the secret and have to be informed, others might go through a ceremony or initiation of some sort. It's going to vary pack to pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Totem Advantage isn't in the form of a Gift. The Totem gives you Merits, Skill Specialties, Skills, or Attributes. Packs can really be as small as four people, or as large as a hundred. Some might not have humans at all, while some in very close territories might consider everyone inside a member of the pack. Going by character creation, each werewolf has one wolf-blooded, then 1-3 humans. If you're working on creating some packs, that's a median you can go by.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah but are there any formal ways of doing it, is it a Rite or just only narrative? <br /> And yeah, the Totem thing aint a Gift, i know that, but didn't remember what t was called, therefor Totem gift-thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:32:37-07:00","id":1127690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1127688#post1127688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but are there any formal ways of doing it, is it a Rite or just only narrative?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just a narrative. There are some abilities that can temporarily bring people into the pack that could be used as a first step, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:39:47-07:00","id":1127692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1127690#post1127690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, just a narrative. There are some abilities that can temporarily bring people into the pack that could be used as a first step, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lead the Lesser Pack, Wisdom facet of Dominance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T09:41:58-07:00","id":1130869,"title":"","content":"What happens if a werewolf becomes Soulless? In the book the main context of Soullessness for werewolves is immediately followed by an idigam shoving a spirit or a soul in its place and creating an Empty Wolf, but what happens if that <i>doesn't</i> happen? I imagine the werewolf would be unable to gain additional Renown or unlock Gifts and Gift Facets, as per an Empty Wolf, but what impact would it have on Harmony?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T09:57:36-07:00","id":1130872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1130869#post1130869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a werewolf becomes Soulless? In the book the main context of Soullessness for werewolves is immediately followed by an idigam shoving a spirit or a soul in its place and creating an Empty Wolf, but what happens if that <i>doesn't</i> happen? I imagine the werewolf would be unable to gain additional Renown or unlock Gifts and Gift Facets, as per an Empty Wolf, but what impact would it have on Harmony?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no content discussing such an outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:47:13-07:00","id":1130956,"title":"","content":"Can a human have a First Change without his soul? (removed with Death 3)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 08-18-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:11:41-07:00","id":1130999,"title":"","content":"Probably not. Though Luna can just give you a new soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T02:51:56-07:00","id":1131170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1130999#post1130999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not. Though Luna can just give you a new soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean &quot;take something and shove it in AS a soul&quot;, then I agree. I doubt she can create souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T04:51:49-07:00","id":1131186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1127688#post1127688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but are there any formal ways of doing it, is it a Rite or just only narrative?<br /> And yeah, the Totem thing aint a Gift, i know that, but didn't remember what t was called, therefor Totem gift-thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narrative. I don't know if any specific regulations around how it works were written into 2e, but my preferences align towards there being a symbolic element to the joining - and that the new pack member is made aware they are becoming part of *something* larger, even though the pack may obfuscate its true nature as having an inner circle of no-shit, actual shapeshifters from the inductee. You want that cult or gang or family element of feeling and aesthetic to it, I feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1130869#post1130869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a werewolf becomes Soulless? In the book the main context of Soullessness for werewolves is immediately followed by an idigam shoving a spirit or a soul in its place and creating an Empty Wolf, but what happens if that <i>doesn't</i> happen? I imagine the werewolf would be unable to gain additional Renown or unlock Gifts and Gift Facets, as per an Empty Wolf, but what impact would it have on Harmony?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing beyond the usual Soulless effects in the core rules, as far as I am aware. Stuff like 'no additional Renown/Gifts/etc' seems a reasonable direction to take it, if that's what you want to do. IIIRC, in my own games I've had Soulless werewolves become horrifically prone to Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1130956#post1130956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a human have a First Change without his soul? (removed with Death 3)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a sufficiently edge-case scenario that my personal answer is 'I dunno really, what do you think works best for your particular story?'. I don't think there's any official info on it. I broadly lean towards 'yes, they Change anyway, but maybe something interesting happens like they need to commit a Sacred Hunt to hunt down their own soul and get it back' or whatnot.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:58:40-07:00","id":1131783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1131186#post1131186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing beyond the usual Soulless effects in the core rules, as far as I am aware. Stuff like 'no additional Renown/Gifts/etc' seems a reasonable direction to take it, if that's what you want to do. IIIRC, in my own games I've had Soulless werewolves become horrifically prone to Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you for the response! Any suggestions about how to handle the Breaking Points that can be brought on by Soulless? Werewolves obviously don't have a Virtue or Vice and they can have Breaking Points &quot;up&quot; or &quot;down&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:05:12-07:00","id":1131786,"title":"","content":"5 is the ideal Harmony. Any penalty that makes you more likely to get Breaking Points is disruptive to Harmony. 'The centre can not hold' kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:47:20-07:00","id":1132555,"title":"","content":"Do First Changes always happen at night? The Tension system in the appendix doesn't mention this so I hadn't considered that that might be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T04:06:47-07:00","id":1132559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1132555#post1132555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do First Changes always happen at night? The Tension system in the appendix doesn't mention this so I hadn't considered that that might be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say so, no. Just that they are more likely, since the moon presumably has to be visible for 4/5 Auspices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T04:17:46-07:00","id":1132562,"title":"","content":"Full Moons usually would. At other times of the cycle the moon can be visible during the day. <br /> <br /> Technically an eclipse happens at peak New Moon. Which is always during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T13:50:23-07:00","id":1133152,"title":"","content":"What would happen if a Rahu while under the effect of &quot;Killer Instinct&quot; facet (meaning 8s again on all the Brawl &amp; weaponry rolls) is hit with the Mystified condition (which if 6 - gauntlet strength equals more than his resolve, then he looses the 10-again on all his roll)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-23-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:27:44-07:00","id":1133162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133152#post1133152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would happen if a Rahu while under the effect of &quot;Killer Instinct&quot; face, meaning 8s again on all the Brawl &amp; weaponry rolls is hit with the Mystified condition, which if 6 - gauntlet strength equals more than his resolve, then he looses the 10-again on all his rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule his dicepool can't explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:32:20-07:00","id":1133165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133162#post1133162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rule his dicepool can't explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, but since Mystified results from a supernatural ability I think a Clash of Wills is apropriate. If the Rahu loses, her dice don't explode at all. If she wins, she has 8-again but still suffers the dice penalty from Mystified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:38:46-07:00","id":1133168,"title":"","content":"Or you could rule that removing 10 Again is equated to removing a level of X Again, meaning 8 Again would instead become 9 Again.<br /> <br /> Edit: That would grant both Killer Instinct and Mystified their effects. Killer Instinct adds two levels of X Again while Mystified removes one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-23-2017, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T17:02:32-07:00","id":1133214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133165#post1133165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, but since Mystified results from a supernatural ability I think a Clash of Wills is apropriate. If the Rahu loses, her dice don't explode at all. If she wins, she has 8-again but still suffers the dice penalty from Mystified.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133168#post1133168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could rule that removing 10 Again is equated to removing a level of X Again, meaning 8 Again would instead become 9 Again.<br /> <br /> Edit: That would grant both Killer Instinct and Mystified their effects. Killer Instinct adds two levels of X Again while Mystified removes one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newp, he's prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:23:44-07:00","id":1133386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133214#post1133214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Newp, he's prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does that have to do with anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:56:43-07:00","id":1133399,"title":"","content":"If a werewolf has already used Gauru in a scene, can she intentionally enter Death Rage by trying to take Gauru again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:48:39-07:00","id":1133427,"title":"","content":"I think the last time this came up the official answer was &quot;no&quot;. <br /> <br /> I guess so the Elodoth have more reasons to use their &quot;induce death rage&quot; power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:24:42-07:00","id":1133437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133399#post1133399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf has already used Gauru in a scene, can she intentionally enter Death Rage by trying to take Gauru again?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can only enter gauru once a scene. Staying too long in gauru can lead to death rage, not trying to take gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:32:19-07:00","id":1133442,"title":"","content":"Taking Gauru can cause death rage outside a fight, but yeah in this case once it's done it won't come if you call. You need to provoke it to come out on it's own some other way.<br /> <br /> Like, stabbing yourself in the leg with a silver knife, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:27:58-07:00","id":1133497,"title":"","content":"One of the side benefits of Chain Rage is that it effectively gives you a Rage button, as if you destroy the object the rage is chained to you automatically go into Wasu-Im.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:58:32-07:00","id":1133516,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks. I suspected that was the case because of the Elodoth thing, but best not assume.<br /> <br /> On a tangent, is it just me or is it a little weird the no amount of non-silver damage can trigger kuruth? It seems odd that a werewolf could let a bunch of thugs beat him to death without even risking going berserk and killing them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:04:17-07:00","id":1133517,"title":"","content":"You can make that as your own set of triggers, if you want. Passive for Common, Lethal for Common, Aggravated for Specific.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if you had it as a general trigger, you would always go berserk in combat. Unconscious from Bashing, but you'd heal that. Lethal only kills you if you're full and don't get medical attention, or have nice regeneration. If you had 'regular' aggravated damage do it, gauru would be an 'I win/I lose' switch. Because if anything can get past your healing, you would jump into rage and lose agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:06:22-07:00","id":1133518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133516#post1133516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks. I suspected that was the case because of the Elodoth thing, but best not assume.<br /> <br /> On a tangent, is it just me or is it a little weird the no amount of non-silver damage can trigger kuruth? It seems odd that a werewolf could let a bunch of thugs beat him to death without even risking going berserk and killing them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can easily be a custom Death Rage trigger: Passive: Suffering Lethal Damage; Common: Enduring a wound on the last three health boxes (where wound penalties start); Specific: Suffering an aggravated wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:26:42-07:00","id":1133528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133517#post1133517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make that as your own set of triggers, if you want. Passive for Common, Lethal for Common, Aggravated for Specific.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if you had it as a general trigger, you would always go berserk in combat. Unconscious from Bashing, but you'd heal that. Lethal only kills you if you're full and don't get medical attention, or have nice regeneration. If you had 'regular' aggravated damage do it, gauru would be an 'I win/I lose' switch. Because if anything can get past your healing, you would jump into rage and lose agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I would expect it to work. If there's one point where you'd think a werewolf would lose control, it's suffering massive damage while already in Gauru. I guess it makes mechanical sense since you don't want every fight with a credible threat to end in kuruth and it's only exploitable in the niche circumstance where you've already taken gauru and the bad guys aren't dead, but it still feels unintuitive that literally dying isn't enough to stir the death rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:29:09-07:00","id":1133881,"title":"","content":"At character creation, a werewolf starts with one dot in his Auspice Renown. Does this dot have to be earned, or does e.g. just being a Rahu automatically entitle you to a dot of Purity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:33:32-07:00","id":1133886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1133881#post1133881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At character creation, a werewolf starts with one dot in his Auspice Renown. Does this dot have to be earned, or does e.g. just being a Rahu automatically entitle you to a dot of Purity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna bestows their auspice with that first dot of renown, so that would be your later assumption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:51:09-07:00","id":1134624,"title":"","content":"Can a spirit be Totem to multiple packs, or is it only ever the Totem to one and only one pack at a time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:56:43-07:00","id":1134626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134624#post1134624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a spirit be Totem to multiple packs, or is it only ever the Totem to one and only one pack at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Same pack, different tiers or squads. Given that packs have no limit on actual membership.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:01:07-07:00","id":1134629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134626#post1134626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Same pack, different tiers or squads. Given that packs have no limit on actual membership.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by &quot;different tiers or squads&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:26:56-07:00","id":1134637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134629#post1134629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by &quot;different tiers or squads&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Packs have no upper limit on membership or maximum distance apart. Thus, some packs are huge and divided - a canonical example is 36LOVE, a Japanese pack containing 36 werewolves split into several &quot;sub-packs&quot; containing either 8 or 4 werewolves spread throughout Japan.<br /> <br /> Such a pack may or may not have a tiered structure, e.g. having a central &quot;leader pack&quot; that makes decisions on big-scale strategy and gives orders to the leaders of each subservient pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:30:28-07:00","id":1134639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134629#post1134629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by &quot;different tiers or squads&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you organize a pack numbering in the dozens? Mountain's Proud Children have 5 different core groups; Not to mention periphery and wolfblooded. The Few Against Many literally number in the 50 active members spread across several metropolitan areas of Tokyo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:18:44-07:00","id":1134746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134637#post1134637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packs have no upper limit on membership or maximum distance apart. Thus, some packs are huge and divided - a canonical example is 36LOVE, a Japanese pack containing 36 werewolves split into several &quot;sub-packs&quot; containing either 8 or 4 werewolves spread throughout Japan.<br /> <br /> Such a pack may or may not have a tiered structure, e.g. having a central &quot;leader pack&quot; that makes decisions on big-scale strategy and gives orders to the leaders of each subservient pack.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134639#post1134639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you organize a pack numbering in the dozens? Mountain's Proud Children have 5 different core groups; Not to mention periphery and wolfblooded. The Few Against Many literally number in the 50 active members spread across several metropolitan areas of Tokyo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, got it.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I...completely forgot the 36LOVE and Few Against Many packs were a thing. Whoops. Although one giant pack wasn't quite what I had in mind...<br /> <br /> And I presume what separates a large pack like this from protectorates is that in a protectorate it's a bunch of packs that (in theory) follow different Totem spirits?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:52:03-07:00","id":1134766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1134746#post1134746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I presume what separates a large pack like this from protectorates is that in a protectorate it's a bunch of packs that (in theory) follow different Totem spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or none at all. But yes, different packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:39:14-07:00","id":1136662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1131783#post1131783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank-you for the response! Any suggestions about how to handle the Breaking Points that can be brought on by Soulless? Werewolves obviously don't have a Virtue or Vice and they can have Breaking Points &quot;up&quot; or &quot;down&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd suggest always breaking away from 5, so if the character is already slanted towards Flesh, breaking towards Flesh, etc. I don't think being Soulless should ever be a help towards balancing Harmony :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:53:15-07:00","id":1136667,"title":"","content":"What if they're <i>at</i> 5? Do they stay precariously balanced there until they break one way or the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T10:30:07-07:00","id":1138349,"title":"","content":"Does the Auspice of werewolf always correspond to his temperament? To me the core book makes it sound that way in the &quot;Who was he/she before the First Change?&quot; which indicates that the werewolf already exhibited characteristics of his future auspice before the first change. This would mean that no werewolf is struggling with his auspice because it runs counter to her natural temperament e.g. an aggressive and confrontational character finding herself in role of a mediator due to her Elodoth auspice. It would also mean that Mother Luna is fairly benevolent and attentive ensuring that all of her children receive a blessing they can benefit from.<br /> Is this a correct interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T11:29:15-07:00","id":1138358,"title":"","content":"I took it that it was common, but not mandatory. Most werewolves find themselves in a role they could have guessed they would before they changed, but some don't.<br /> <br /> Maybe the change was a traumatic event that altered their worldview. Maybe luna sees something in them that they never did. Whatever the reason, it's never 100% certain that you'll get what you expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T11:31:26-07:00","id":1138359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1138349#post1138349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Auspice of werewolf always correspond to his temperament? To me the core book makes it sound that way in the &quot;Who was he/she before the First Change?&quot; which indicates that the werewolf already exhibited characteristics of his future auspice before the first change. This would mean that no werewolf is struggling with his auspice because it runs counter to her natural temperament e.g. an aggressive and confrontational character finding herself in role of a mediator due to her Elodoth auspice. It would also mean that Mother Luna is fairly benevolent and attentive ensuring that all of her children receive a blessing they can benefit from.<br /> Is this a correct interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what the book says, but keep in mind there's a lot of room for interpretation. No one Rahu is going to fulfill <i>every</i> Rahu stereotype. Temperament also doesn't necessarily translate to skill or comfort - consider for example an Elodoth who's a natural mediator, but grew up under circumstances where honesty and compromise were seen as weakness. That guy probably won't find debate and negotiation particularly easy, even if it's what he <i>wants</i> to do.<br /> <br /> Plus, Luna is infamously fickle. Even if temperament matching auspice was supposed to be an ironclad rule, a serious mismatch would absolutely be the sort of thing that could happen with no better explanation than &quot;because Luna&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T14:42:42-07:00","id":1138403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1138349#post1138349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Auspice of werewolf always correspond to his temperament? To me the core book makes it sound that way in the &quot;Who was he/she before the First Change?&quot; which indicates that the werewolf already exhibited characteristics of his future auspice before the first change. This would mean that no werewolf is struggling with his auspice because it runs counter to her natural temperament e.g. an aggressive and confrontational character finding herself in role of a mediator due to her Elodoth auspice. It would also mean that Mother Luna is fairly benevolent and attentive ensuring that all of her children receive a blessing they can benefit from.<br /> Is this a correct interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, Luna is fucking crazy. There's no rhyme or reason to whichever Auspice you might end up. Sure, some people are born Rahu, but sometimes the born killer got blessed by the Half Moon (Or any other Auspice). Many a Pure switched sides because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:13:04-07:00","id":1144051,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this question was discussed in some way but still - what about Uratha aging in 2ED? Is there any World of God about how long they can live, and is there any ways for them to become long-living/immortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:00:07-07:00","id":1144067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1144051#post1144051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this question was discussed in some way but still - what about Uratha aging in 2ED? Is there any World of God about how long they can live, and is there any ways for them to become long-living/immortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>No word of god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T01:28:19-07:00","id":1144310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1144067#post1144067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No word of god.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. In this case - what is more &quot;fair&quot;: 1) their get old as normal people or<br /> 2) they stop after PU5+?<br /> For me that's important since any other splats are (can be)long-livers. Is there <i>canonical</i> options for werewolves? (Right now I see only one - find Health (Life, Healing, etc.) spirit with Influence 3-5 and make him to increase your lifespan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","u