:"","content":"At least they CAN become long-livers if they'll try hard enough. As for Mages or Changelings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-27-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:47:50-07:00","id":1144440,"title":"","content":"Changeling's had their life extended by Wyrd too, and could make goblin pacts for more. Mages have a dozen ways to extend their lifespan, and have more potential for bargaining..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T16:49:09-07:00","id":1144560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1144421#post1144421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second, I think. 1st ED PU-description was about Essence-management. It was not explicitly about aging<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kbUrJtflv1M?t=89\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/kbUrJtflv1M?t=89</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The video isn't wanting to load properly on my phone, and I never watched True Blood. Can you give me the gist of the video, and its significance to the discussion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T17:38:29-07:00","id":1144571,"title":"","content":"An Uratha would eat a True Blood werewolf for breakfast. Any ChroD vamp trying that would be torn to bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T00:24:34-07:00","id":1144660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1144440#post1144440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling's had their life extended by Wyrd too, and could make goblin pacts for more. Mages have a dozen ways to extend their lifespan, and have more potential for bargaining..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's the point. Any other splat can extend the lifespan, why werewolves are inferior? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">An Uratha would eat a True Blood werewolf for breakfast. Any ChroD vamp trying that would be torn to bits.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> Ofc they can, since TB wers are just shapeshifters without any other abilities. (Btw, it would be interesting to make a build of ChroD-werewolfe able to fight TB vampire).Anyway, Chro vampires still can degrade werewolves for their lifespan, if they can't extend one. But... they can))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T04:29:28-07:00","id":1144699,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4950\" data-vbnamecard=\"4950\">Lashet</a> your question was answered, make another thread to discuss it further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T09:26:11-07:00","id":1144810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1144660#post1144660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, that's the point. Any other splat can extend the lifespan, why werewolves are inferior?</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't? If you want to go by first edition rules, then they have extended lifespans the same as changelings and can make bargains like everyone else.<br /> <br /> In second edition it just hasn't been written about. This does not mean it's been erased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T00:31:12-07:00","id":1147946,"title":"","content":"An idigam's Soul Slaves are statted as spirits and receive +3 to using the Possess Manifestation on regular humans, but have no Influences; given that Lunacy removes the ability of a character to resist Possession and Wolf-Blooded with Tells that make them Open are not normal humans, neither of the primary means of making a character susceptible to Possession get much benefit out of the extra dice. How does a Soul Slave manage to steal a body without assistance from a secondary entity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-08-2017, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T05:47:32-07:00","id":1147980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1147946#post1147946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idigam's Soul Slaves are statted as spirits and receive +3 to using the Possess Manifestation on regular humans, but have no Influences; given that Lunacy removes the ability of a character to resist Possession and Wolf-Blooded with Tells that make them Open are not normal humans, neither of the primary means of making a character susceptible to Possession get much benefit out of the extra dice. How does a Soul Slave manage to steal a body without assistance from a secondary entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Influences and Lunacy are just the quick and dirty ways to hijack a body. The more typical way is to gently massage the subject until it becomes sufficiently aligned with the entity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;WtF p. 189</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Causing the Condition:</b> [The Open Condition] is usually the result of fine-tuning the Resonant Condition as part of an extended action, involving the subject and spirit acting in concert for a number of scenes equal to Rank or a living subject\u2019s Resolve, whichever is higher. Using a Strengthen Influence allows a spirit to temporarily upgrade Resonant to Open as an instant action. </div> </div> </div> </div>So a Soul Slave can use its Manifestations and Numina to do things the hard (but more permanent) way. Though I guess what exactly constitutes being &quot;Resonant&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to a Soul Slave remains an exercise for the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T09:18:23-07:00","id":1148033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1147980#post1147980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Soul Slave can use its Manifestations and Numina to do things the hard (but more permanent) way. Though I guess what exactly constitutes being &quot;Resonant&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to a Soul Slave remains an exercise for the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>My approach, and bad news for the average mortal, is that \u200b'being a human' is enough to be resonant for a soul slave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T22:03:39-07:00","id":1151211,"title":"","content":"Is the breaking point toward Flesh from exceeding the Primal Urge-based window for Sacred Hunt once per interval or once per day-past-interval? The writeup seems clear that the consequent Essence bleed is per-day, but the breaking point's inclusion in the same sentence seems like it has some room for confusion.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, is there any consequence to dietary- or Hunt-aversion-induced Essence loss on an empty tank besides running on empty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T00:59:21-07:00","id":1152135,"title":"","content":"well:<br /> <br /> 1- I was eating a human with my predator king yesterday and I was thinking: I do aggravated damages with my bite when I want to eat someone who is ''human''.<br /> Is a mage, considered human?<br /> <br /> 2- To regenerate aggravated damages without waiting 4 damn days for one health box, is to create a oooo or ooooo fetish with a healing spirit inside?<br /> <br /> 2.1- or a spirit ally with at least influence ooo (healing) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-23-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:33:18-07:00","id":1152153,"title":"","content":"1- Yes, they are considered human for all intents and purposes, including a nice meal<br /> <br /> 2- Depending on how you or your Storyteller rule the way Influence: Healing works it could require as little as O (Strengthen) or as much as OOOO (Create). In the first case it could improve upon the natural regeneration of the Werewolf, maybe reducing the time interval by 12 hours or a day per success, letting you eventually to be able to heal 1 or more Aggravated per day. In the second case it would be a more direct healing application, just eliminating Aggravated wounds equal to successes, or if that is too much,maybe downgrading them to Lethal, wich should be trivially easy to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:14:49-07:00","id":1152295,"title":"","content":"There's an explicit heal numina from 2e sources, in, I believe, the Chronicles of Darkness book, and it can heal Aggravated damage for a hefty amount of essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T07:56:23-07:00","id":1153734,"title":"","content":"So, killing blows (efficient killer).<br /> It's only my full dicepool of strength + brawl + weapon(claws or bite), or I can add all out + willpower + gift ( slaughterer or primal strength for example..) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T08:23:05-07:00","id":1153741,"title":"","content":"You can't All Out because Efficient Killer already requires sacrificing your Defense, but anything else that adds to the dice pool is a-okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-28-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:13:35-07:00","id":1154197,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans to produce a Storyteller Screen for Forsaken 2nd edition? If not, are there any community-made resources that serve as such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15848-volkspanzer","name":"Volkspanzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:15:53-07:00","id":1154776,"title":"","content":"Okay, simple question; I heard a lot about the Bale Hounds, but 2e has very little mention of them and zero rules to play them, so I would like to ask: are there special rules to play them? Like unique Gifts or something? Or are they just Forsaken and Pure Werewolves who happens to worship demon-like spirits, and get no special rules from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:26:07-07:00","id":1154780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1154776#post1154776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, simple question; I heard a lot about the Bale Hounds, but 2e has very little mention of them and zero rules to play them, so I would like to ask: are there special rules to play them? Like unique Gifts or something? Or are they just Forsaken and Pure Werewolves who happens to worship demon-like spirits, and get no special rules from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't be detailed in second edition until Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon, which isn't likely to come out soon. Werewolf is currently without a developer.<br /> <br /> For first edition's rules, which can be converted fairly easily, you can check out <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3418/Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">Blasphemies</a>. First edition offers a few ways to handle them, either as lodges dedicated to specific Maeljin (we have examples of this in things like the Lodge of Mammon), as a Ninth Tribe serving Soulless Wolf, herald of the Maeljin. Or as a sort of Dark Pantheism, with the Bale Hounds as an evil horde following all the Maeljin. While they don't get specific rules for just being a Bale Hound, they tend to have rites that are only traded among themselves. Most noteworthy is the Rite of Dead Light, which grants access to Flayed Lunes Merit, which in turn gives access to the Tainted Moon Gift. If second edition updates these I imagine there would be less of an Experience tax involved.<br /> <br /> Power wise, based on what we know of werewolf so far, going the Lodge route would probably be an easy way to go. Lodges grant access to powers and offer fittingly cultlike behavior. Ideally there will be new stuff in Shunned by the Moon but only time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-01-2017, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:34:05-07:00","id":1154802,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T01:36:16-07:00","id":1155327,"title":"","content":"Using Tongue of Flame with Purity 3 --&gt; Influence level 3. Able to control fire. How would you use this in combat? I'm imagining it basically being like a firebender from Avatar, being able to move existing fire along flammable materials and even probably short distances over air to spread the fire. I assume the fire that is directly under your control will not burn the user, but stuff that has previously caught fire will have normal fire on it and will burn you.<br /> <br /> What would you use as a limit in combat for how far/much fire you can control? Maybe base it on Willpower (Resolve+Composure) and Purity Renown? Those combined in yards in a turn, or maybe WP*Purity yards? Also, need to have line of sight to it and each turn spend your action to control the fire?<br /> <br /> Could a packmate use Catastrophe at level 1 to strengthen that fire, add like +1 damage to it? Would it only strengthen the fire being controlled or even the stuff caught on fire?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:50:46-07:00","id":1155412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1155327#post1155327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Tongue of Flame with Purity 3 --&gt; Influence level 3. Able to control fire. How would you use this in combat? I'm imagining it basically being like a firebender from Avatar, being able to move existing fire along flammable materials and even probably short distances over air to spread the fire. I assume the fire that is directly under your control will not burn the user, but stuff that has previously caught fire will have normal fire on it and will burn you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Control can probably let you move it over longer distances. Might add a penalty, if you want. But basically it seems like it would be a damaging effect. You can look to Fire in the Chronicles core book to see how fire causes damage, because it's not like clubbing someone over the head with a crowbar. It 'automatically inflicts lethal damage per turn of exposure.' Said damage depends on the size and intensity of the flame, with Size going from Torch (1 Damage) to Bonfire (2) to Inferno (3). Then the heat of the fire adds to that damage, with a candle not adding any, a torch adding +1, bunsen burner +2, chemical fire or molten metal +3. 'So, a fire the size of a bonfire (2) and with the Intensity of a torch (+1) inflicts three damage per turn of contact.' Heat of fire would probably rely on the source of the fire, but keep in mind with Control you can make it burn hotter. There's also some rules for combustion, to keep the fire burning.<br /> <br /> Hurt Locker adds a 'Burning' Condition, which represents you being on fire, how much damage you take per turn, and adds the Blinded tilt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would you use as a limit in combat for how far/much fire you can control? Maybe base it on Willpower (Resolve+Composure) and Purity Renown? Those combined in yards in a turn, or maybe WP*Purity yards? Also, need to have line of sight to it and each turn spend your action to control the fire? </div> </div> </div>I'd probably break it up among the successes for the Influence roll, with successes letting you change it further, either adding to the heat level or moving it more than ten feet from its source or do something intricate like spell out a warning in the air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a packmate use Catastrophe at level 1 to strengthen that fire, add like +1 damage to it? Would it only strengthen the fire being controlled or even the stuff caught on fire? </div> </div> </div>I think Catastrophe affects the users Influences, not those of others, even packmates. Though a simple fetish could solve that problem. That said, what Catastrophe does is pretty clear, it would allow you to use the Influence without any line of sight and drastically expand range limitations (to a radius in miles equal to twice their Glory). Basically all fires in that area could be affected by Control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:05:48-07:00","id":1155435,"title":"","content":"First, you don't need Catastrophe to Strengthen a flame, you already have that influence at Purity 1, but you may need it if you want to be actually impervious to immolation.<br /> <br /> Attack wise? Roll for the influence, substract defense. Add a bonus depending on how large (or a penalty depending how little) fire is in the vicinity. Inferno? +5. Bonfire? +3. Torch? +2. Range on what you can affect? Make it sensory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T06:41:09-08:00","id":1156032,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm new to WtF 2e, and more or less new to nWoD/CoD in general. My group is relatively new as a whole, but some of our members seem to have at least been familiar with either WtA or 1e WtF, and there was some confusion last game over some specifics, so I thought I'd ask here with some specific questions that *should* be yes or no questions. If possible, I'd like book / page references if you have them, simply because most of us like to be able to check out relevant sections for anything else we missed.<br /> <br /> 1. Are Claimed and / or Spirit-Ridden supposed affected by the banes or bans of the spirits possessing them? Our ST wasn't sure, but he noted that the entry he was using (some kind of glass spirit our of a 1e book) didn't have anything mentioned there, nor did the example Ridden in WtF2e have them listed. My suspicion is that its because each spirit may have different ones even if they're the same ilthum.<br /> <br /> 2. If they are, are there any changes to how that's supposed to work from spirits that are in Twilight or simply Fettered to something? What happens when you wield a bane against them?<br /> <br /> 3. When paying gathra to a spirit, does the essence the werewolf is giving up need to be Resonant to the spirit somehow, since spirits seem to be supposed to consume only essence (and other spirits) of kinds similar to their natures?<br /> <br /> 4. Can werewolves transport prepared essence somehow to a spirit for the purposes of paying gathra? (Like say, using Resonance Shaping when you know you're going to talk to a fire spirit to bring it a gift of fire-resonant essence).<br /> <br /> 5. When performing the Sacred Hunt ritual, are spirits aware that it is being enacted, particularly the targets? I vaguely remember it being mentioned at least somewhere that spirits aware of the ritual 'tremble and pray they arent the targets' or somesuch, but when I went back to find it, I could see anything. This came up as a question because since my Ithaeur Boneshadow has a a reliably high chance of quick successes and can enact the ritual in only 304 minutes, when we come across prey it is our duty to put down, it seems like I should quickly perform the rite. At the the time there was a question of whether the Spirit-Ridden in question would know they were being targeted.<br /> <br /> 6. As a followup to that, are there any requirements for location or presence of a totem to conduct a Sacred Hunt ritual? We are a VERY newly minted pack, don't even have our totem yet, that's going to be part of our prelude, more or less. All we have is an assigned (by other packs) home, which we havent even gotten to yet, and instructions to form whatever territory we can control, since the region is largely empty.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> On a separate possibly-too-complicated-for-this-thread question: (So skip it if it is)<br /> <br /> 1. Are there any mechanic merits that relate to the Buddy Spirit touchstone? There seem to be some options here and there that mention spirit companions, like Buddy Spirit or the Wolf-Blooded Familiar, or Ambitious Totem, but nothing about any kind of mechanics involved, like 'How do they follow me around at all times if they bleed essence every day?' or 'Do I need to invest merit points in this?'. Or is that just handwaved since CoD is more freeform and cares more about the story than mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","user":"Chandrak","date":". 11-05-2017, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:44:29-08:00","id":1156129,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% certain of a few of the others, so I'll leave them to people more in the know, but for number 6, I'm pretty sure you don't need a totem to use the Sacred Hunt rite. In fact I'm pretty sure you don't need a <i>pack. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T13:36:07-08:00","id":1156150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chandrak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1156032#post1156032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are Claimed and / or Spirit-Ridden supposed affected by the banes or bans of the spirits possessing them? Our ST wasn't sure, but he noted that the entry he was using (some kind of glass spirit our of a 1e book) didn't have anything mentioned there, nor did the example Ridden in WtF2e have them listed. My suspicion is that its because each spirit may have different ones even if they're the same ilthum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is first edition didn't have banes and bans, it just had bans. And yes, they weren't put into the spirit-ridden example antagonists.<br /> <br /> Also, Claimed are a type of spirit-ridden, where the spirit has used the Claim Manifestation, described on page 191. The entry also has the following quote, 'The hybrid being that results has the spirit\u2019s Essence trait, ban, and bane, but is a material being.' For an Urged or Fettered spirit, which first edition would call a Ridden or Urged, the person the spirit is connected to doesn't have the ban or bane, however, on p185 where it describes how bans and banes interaction with entities it says, 'If the bane comes into contact with an item or person linked to a Fettered spirit, the spirit suffers one point of lethal damage per turn as long as contact holds. The spirit must use the Unfetter Manifestation Effect to escape.' and 'If the bane is used as a weapon against the spirit, the spirit suffers aggravated wounds if both bane and spirit are in the Hisil or the bane is in the physical world and the spirit is using a Manifestation. The wounds are lethal for spirits still in Twilight when the bane is physical.' So a spirit would want to be careful around these banes, as they're sort of hazard areas for them as long as they're in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. If they are, are there any changes to how that's supposed to work from spirits that are in Twilight or simply Fettered to something? What happens when you wield a bane against them? </div> </div> </div>I think the above quote answered these questions, but you can check the referenced pages for more details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. When paying gathra to a spirit, does the essence the werewolf is giving up need to be Resonant to the spirit somehow, since spirits seem to be supposed to consume only essence (and other spirits) of kinds similar to their natures? </div> </div> </div>They would likely only accept gathra Resonant to them. A fire spirit would probably just not accept a gift of a portable icemaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Can werewolves transport prepared essence somehow to a spirit for the purposes of paying gathra? (Like say, using Resonance Shaping when you know you're going to talk to a fire spirit to bring it a gift of fire-resonant essence). </div> </div> </div>I think the spirit would need to take the Essence. Werewolves don't have much control over their own Essence, and there's <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">a Gift to transfer it</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. When performing the Sacred Hunt ritual, are spirits aware that it is being enacted, particularly the targets? I vaguely remember it being mentioned at least somewhere that spirits aware of the ritual 'tremble and pray they arent the targets' or somesuch, but when I went back to find it, I could see anything. This came up as a question because since my Ithaeur Boneshadow has a a reliably high chance of quick successes and can enact the ritual in only 304 minutes, when we come across prey it is our duty to put down, it seems like I should quickly perform the rite. At the the time there was a question of whether the Spirit-Ridden in question would know they were being targeted. </div> </div> </div>No, unless they're informed of it through other means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. As a followup to that, are there any requirements for location or presence of a totem to conduct a Sacred Hunt ritual? We are a VERY newly minted pack, don't even have our totem yet, that's going to be part of our prelude, more or less. All we have is an assigned (by other packs) home, which we havent even gotten to yet, and instructions to form whatever territory we can control, since the region is largely empty. </div> </div> </div>No. First edition did require a spirit to be part of things, but second edition, like Elfive says, just requires someone who knows how to do the rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Are there any mechanic merits that relate to the Buddy Spirit touchstone? There seem to be some options here and there that mention spirit companions, like Buddy Spirit or the Wolf-Blooded Familiar, or Ambitious Totem, but nothing about any kind of mechanics involved, like 'How do they follow me around at all times if they bleed essence every day?' or 'Do I need to invest merit points in this?'. Or is that just handwaved since CoD is more freeform and cares more about the story than mechanics? </div> </div> </div>I prefer to do it freeform. However, mechanically for a totem, you can just use the Totem Merit (which specifically says can be used for a personal totem, as well as a pack totem), and for a familiar of some sort, you can use the Retainer Merit (or Mage's Familiar Merit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-05-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T01:36:13-08:00","id":1156257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1156150#post1156150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (snipped)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a ton, that pretty much clears up everything we needed to know. I\u2019ll pass it on to our ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:52:12-08:00","id":1158059,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to disable a Uratha in Gauru? Knock them down? Hit them so much they are force to change form? Or once a Uratha enters Gauru is either they get filled with aggravated and die or they choose to change form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:02:13-08:00","id":1158062,"title":"","content":"They can't stay in gauru forever without getting into Kuruth. You could avoid them until time is up. Or use other disabling abilities or tools, like a bear trap or pit trap or magic holding spell.<br /> <br /> There's always ways to get out of them but not every werewolf will have access to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:04:42-08:00","id":1158064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1158062#post1158062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't stay in gauru forever without getting into Kuruth. You could avoid them until time is up. Or use other disabling abilities or tools, like a bear trap or pit trap or magic holding spell.<br /> <br /> There's always ways to get out of them but not every werewolf will have access to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I ask because i was reading Detroit Rock city in which 2 Uratha fight each other in Gauru until one falls defeated (not by his own choice) and i was wondering if that was possible in 2nd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:10:26-08:00","id":1158065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1158064#post1158064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask because i was reading Detroit Rock city in which 2 Uratha fight each other in Gauru until one falls defeated (not by his own choice) and i was wondering if that was possible in 2nd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. You can just hit them hard enough to roll over into Aggravated. It's easier with something with Lethal damage like claws and teeth. There's things like Flense Shape which can sort of force you to choose between shifting and Kuruth.<br /> <br /> But since Detroit Rock City was in first edition, it would have been easier then, you just need to fill them with Lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2017, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:20:44-08:00","id":1158066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1158065#post1158065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. You can just hit them hard enough to roll over into Aggravated. It's easier with something with Lethal damage like claws and teeth. <br /> <br /> But since Detroit Rock City was in first edition, it would have been easier then, you just need to fill them with Lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there is nothing mechanically take &quot;the fight out of a Uratha in Gauru&quot; beyond him choosing to give up. Thats a shame, i was looking for a way for duels one on one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:27:01-08:00","id":1158067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1158066#post1158066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there is nothing mechanically take &quot;the fight out of a Uratha in Gauru&quot; beyond him choosing to give up. Thats a shame, i was looking for a way for duels one on one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sort of calming spirit, of course. Then where there's a spirit there's a Gift, there's a fetish. One could also easily make a rite.<br /> <br /> But gauru isn't meant to be used for non-lethal duels, or non-lethal anything really. It's the killing form. 'Gauru is a form to take and to dodge killing blows, and to end a hunt or a battle quickly and efficiently. The Gauru form only communicates to help with the kill.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Having to specify non-lethal. 11-12-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:18:16-08:00","id":1159178,"title":"","content":"Back with some more newbie questions - the last round was really helpful for us, but ofc as always with these things we ran into some more:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you cast spells that need extra essence than you can spend in a turn? Some Gift facets, like Warding, can cost up to 5 Essence, which without dedicated locus would seem to be impossible for a Primal urge 1 new werewolf to cast at all. Is this correct, or can you spend multiple turns drawing out the essence?<br /> <br /> 2. Uratha know other Uratha on sight, but do they know if someone is Wolfblooded by anything other than Tells?<br /> <br /> (Moved three to the end since it\u2019s more complex)<br /> <br /> 4. If shifting into gauru, does shifting as an instant and not attacking in the same action lead to kuruth because you didn\u2019t try to move/attack?<br /> <br /> 5. Does shifting out of Gauru when not yet in Kuruth require a roll?<br /> <br /> 6. Can Uratha who do not know the Sacred Hunt rite participate in it? Sacred Hunt is a Wolf Rite, but only Pack Rites are mentioned as being joinable by those who do not know it, but that seems weird to me.<br /> <br /> 7. (Complex): There are a lot of various things that are implied can happen during Siskur-Dah, from forcing spirits to teach gifts and rites, to consuming their essence, to completely destroying them, and even forcing them back across the guantlet. How is this supposed to actually happen, given what is supposed to happen when you deal full corpus damage to spirits, or should they generally surrender when facing defeat at the hands of a sacred hunt? Do they need to somehow be forced to capitulate first, or can something be done with a dormant spirit? Especially in werewolf, it seems odd to me to have someone standing around in the middle of combat trying to make social rolls to intimidate or make demands while the rest of the pack is fighting (and while other players are just trying to do as much damage as they can). Also it seems like once a Spirit is dormant it would be difficult to move them across the Guantlet (though it just occurred to me I have Bottled Spirit, so I could just ferry dormant ones across personally)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:27:28-08:00","id":1159227,"title":"","content":"1) If you can only spend 1 essence per turn, you'll be 5 turns trying to power that gift.<br /> <br /> 2) Wolfblooded can be scented for what they are.<br /> <br /> 3/7) All of what the spirit may offer a pack that is by all means about to consume it generally comes out of the spirit own determination to save it's neck. No need to pause combat for social rolls unless the prey surrenders. Then you give your terms.<br /> <br /> 4) No. Same if the Gauru was somehow restrained.<br /> <br /> 5) Shapeshifting no longer requires dicerolls.<br /> <br /> 6) Yes. The ritualist usually has to anoint the Hunting party, bonus if this is done to signal packhood, bonus if this is done honoring a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T16:23:51-08:00","id":1159248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159227#post1159227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Yes. The ritualist usually has to anoint the Hunting party, bonus if this is done to signal packhood, bonus if this is done honoring a totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide some sort of rules page I can check up on for this? Because while I was going over your answers, it seems to directly contradict the rules on Rites. Sacred Hunt is a Wolf Rite, and only Pack Rites are spelled out as not needing the participants to know the Rite. Also i think you may be confusing Hunting Grounds with Sacred Hunt - Hunting Grounds is a pack rite while Sacred Hunt is a wolf rite. Also I\u2019m not sure about the parts about bonuses for honoring things - definitely don\u2019t recall seeing that anywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, some clarification in number 4 would be helpful. I\u2019m still stuck on the \u2018if you do anything else, roll composure\u2019, and shifting and then not immediately attacking seems like that counts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","user":"Chandrak","date":".  Followup question added 11-15-2017, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T16:24:44-08:00","id":1159249,"title":"","content":"Just for some references.<br /> <br /> 1. P100. 'Uratha use Essence for numerous purposes. How much Essence a werewolf can spend in a turn is dictated by her Primal Urge score, as detailed on p. 93. If a Gift or other effect would require she spend more Essence than she may in a turn, she can spend the required Essence over a number of turns, with the ability activating once she has spent the total needed.'<br /> <br /> 2. P94. 'Werewolves can also identify each other and Wolf-Blooded by smell. Doing so requires a Wits + Primal Urge roll, though this takes an instant action and she has to get in close to the character to be sure. Whether she uses the close press of a nightclub crowd or a tight-knit mob at a riot, she has to invade her suspect\u2019s personal space.'<br /> <br /> 6. P140. ' All werewolves present are cast as the hunters....All participating werewolves gain the Siskur-Dah Condition.' Only the ritemaster has to know the rite, everyone who participates is a participant and it doesn't require any mechanical investment. Though if others do know the rite they can assist with a teamwork roll.<br /> <br /> 7. 'If the Uratha chase down spirit-prey that knows the symbols of a rite or can carve the secret of a Gift, any Uratha hunter present can expend the necessary Experiences to be marked with the Gift or learn the rite from the spirit. If this is done, the hunters do not get any Essence if they then bring the spirit down, and doing so is a breaking point toward Spirit.'<br /> <br /> Like you said, this is complex. A big thing, it's important to remember the sacred hunt, even when being done to a spirit, is not necessarily to the death. You can perform the sacred hunt solely to get a Gift. Often spirits will have bans that can be used against them, such as 'Must give safe audience to anyone wearing red,' which can be used in the course of a hunt after tracking the spirit down, without necessarily having to get into combat. Alternatively, demanding a spirit submit in combat (or, potentially, refuse and die) wouldn't necessarily take an extra turn to do and can be done as a Reflex action without hindering combat. So they do need to be forced to capitulate (and mind that the Sacred Hunt binds its target just as much as it binds its hunter) but it's nothing that requires standing around making social rolls, as spirits are sort of contractually obligated to respond to the rite, you can just determine how that's handled (for example a roadrunner spirit migh require you to just catch up to it, while a bull spirit might require you to knock it down, or any of them you can decide need to be brought 'down' as in horribly wounded).<br /> <br /> As for sending them back across the Gauntlet. P184, 'Spirits must spend a point of Essence per day to remain active, even when in the Hisil . If they have run out of Essence, they fall into hibernation until something happens to let them regain at least one point, which they can then spend on returning to activity. Such dormancy is dangerous \u2014 the spirit remains in Twilight and can be destroyed if it loses all Corpus and Essence at the same time (see p. 186). <i>When spirits enter hibernation in the physical world, they slowly move back across the Gauntlet into the Shadow, crossing over in the local Gauntlet\u2019s dice penalty in hours.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-15-2017, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T18:46:11-08:00","id":1159292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159249#post1159249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for all the page references! I\u2019d actually managed to find a handful after the previous reply, but you have a few that were slightly different, which helps reinforce the answers we were looking for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On number 6, i\u2019d sort of taken that \u2018all participating\u2019 to refer to to those performing it, but between that quote and rereading it, I see where we went wrong; The section on Wolf Rites I guess refers to other Uratha aiding in conducting it, not specifically participating, which I\u2019d misinterpreted. It makes a lot more sense that way (especially when looking at some of the wolfblooded participant rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T19:48:29-08:00","id":1159309,"title":"","content":"It's no problem, Malus got it I just figured some page references could help, I know the info is spread out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T20:03:49-08:00","id":1159316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159309#post1159309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's no problem, Malus got it I just figured some page references could help, I know the info is spread out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha yeah, the books are a bit disorganized. And I thought games like Pathfinder were bad ;p.<br /> <br /> Well, maybe CoD is sitll better than those ... at least its all in the same book as a general rule, haha.<br /> <br /> Anyway, two last questions, that I'd apparently missed (we're keeping a list as we play, haha)<br /> <br /> 1. How does an Uratha actually go about gifting appropriately-resonant essence? Can they even carry around to give away? That was never clear to me. Or do they just escort the spirit somewhere? (This is related to me wanting to take Resonance Shaping with the hopes that it would help me bargain with spirits for lots of reasons, so I can easilly have the right kinds... but even though we have a locus, im unclear on how to actually get the right kinds of essence to the spirits I want to talk to)<br /> <br /> 2. How do chases / running down prey work? (Or rather, is there somewhere you can point me to that we can read about it?) Specifically in this case, we had been fighting some manifested disease-spirits who decided to up and run after we dispersed one of them. We'd also had them surrounded and were more or less all in melee with them, and weren't sure how it would work with us trying to stop them from running (or even if we could, if they were first in the initiative order), or how to try and run them down (again, or even if we could, since they had a good 4 speed over the fastest of us)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T21:54:57-08:00","id":1159345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chandrak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159316#post1159316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. How does an Uratha actually go about gifting appropriately-resonant essence? Can they even carry around to give away? That was never clear to me. Or do they just escort the spirit somewhere? (This is related to me wanting to take Resonance Shaping with the hopes that it would help me bargain with spirits for lots of reasons, so I can easilly have the right kinds... but even though we have a locus, im unclear on how to actually get the right kinds of essence to the spirits I want to talk to)</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually doing something, but it can be a matter of a physical offering, both can create appropriate Essence, but generally you don't just 'hold' weird Essence unless you're weird. One of the writers wrote up a description of a hospital, ruled by the Pain Angel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel#post794977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sovereign is only interested in a couple of forms of payment for such healing. It mostly demands that the bargainers pay five Essence per point of damaged healed <i>and</i> hospitalise a number of mortal victims equal to the points of damage healed; the precise nature of the hospitalisation is flexible, but the victims must be genuinely harmed so that the spirit can draw Essence from their healing. The easiest way is to break a few limbs but the spirit will be intrigued by and well inclined to packs that get creative and start trying to infect victims with serious diseases or the like. This payment <i>must</i> happen within the week of the service or the healed flesh will fester and blight, turning necrotic and foul. The Sovereign is also interested in nearby rival hospitals being sabotaged, on the rough and irrational basis that they are stealing its \u2018congregation\u2019 from it. For this sort of service, the spirit will want a significant act of sabotage or damage \u2013 actually permanently killing the spirit of healing in one of the rival hospitals will buy a huge amount of favour with it and gain not only payment for the service but also a number of dots of the Ally (Sovereign of Blood and Gold) merit. The Sovereign <i>cannot</i> be forced to heal without payment, whether through intimidation or domination \u2013 it is literally incapable of doing so without <i>gathra</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fire spirit might want you to set fires, an ancient river spirit might want drowned human sacrifice, a pain spirit might want a certain amount of Aggravated damage inflicted, a violence spirit a few unprovoked attacks. More static spirits might want attention, or a diversion of attention, like a store spirit wanting customers scared from the competitor across the street.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. How do chases / running down prey work? (Or rather, is there somewhere you can point me to that we can read about it?) Specifically in this case, we had been fighting some manifested disease-spirits who decided to up and run after we dispersed one of them. We'd also had them surrounded and were more or less all in melee with them, and weren't sure how it would work with us trying to stop them from running (or even if we could, if they were first in the initiative order), or how to try and run them down (again, or even if we could, since they had a good 4 speed over the fastest of us) </div> </div> </div>An easy way to do it is Speed. But the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness book</a> has a set of Chase Rules that offer some more of a chance for RP. They start on p84 in the Chronicles book. Basically you have a goal to reach, usually starting at 5 successes, over the other character. If they succeed, pursuer gets an Instant Action, then Initiative starts, or pursued gets away. One character or side has Edge, and is basically able to lead the hunt, like a spirit that knows or is of the area, or a werewolf who's got a taste of blood and reflexive shifting so is able to easily get through obstacles. They throw up obstacles ideally suited to their skillset, like a member of the Thousand Steel Teeth might steer you into the open road where its Drive can play out, or a beshilu through a sewer full of rabid rats that it has some natural Animal Ken to stir them up with. There's more to it, allowing for Seizing the Edge, and characters being able to use their other dice pools but with a penalty, like a werewolf hunting said beshilu attempting Intimidate to keep the rats away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T22:51:53-08:00","id":1159351,"title":"","content":"Ahh yeah, that part in CoD is what we were wondering about for Chase rules, perfect.<br /> <br /> The other part though didn't quite answer my question, though that was pretty interesting for an example, and is some good examples of other methods of payment a spirit might want.<br /> <br /> But the part that's getting us is that second line:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159345#post1159345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>It mostly demands that the bargainers pay five Essence per point of damaged healed </i><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The question the best I can think of to word it is 'how does this actually happen in-game?' I'd already asked previously about whether they needed to be paid in appropriate essence - there's all sorts of mentions of paying spirits essence, including paying them to even begin talking to them in the first place, but how does that actually occur if you can't just give them some or they need the right kinds?<br /> <br /> In the example, the Pain Angel seems to require a gift of essence AND the creation of additional essence both - but how do you bring it that first essence in the first place? If it just sucks essence right out of you (which doesn't seem like an ability that spirits can have), then it wouldn't be the right kind unless you were Resonant; In this specific case its probably simple, because if you need healing you're probably already Resonant to a degree with Pain, but what if we're talking about other kinds of spirits? The example seems to pretty well mirror the book, which talks about needing to bring a gift of Essence to even open negotiations, but how would that even work if you were approaching say, a Computer Spirit? How would you 'bring' computer-resonant essence to it?<br /> <br /> If on the other hand the idea is you're only supposed offer to go make some somewhere, the language they use all the time about offering gifts before being able to bargain doesn't really make much sense to me - it makes more sense that you're bringing an already-existant gift to give them in order put them at ease or show respect so you can begin making an offer in the first place. This implies to me, somehow, that either you are able to transport essence, or they can draw it directly from you somehow. (Also, it should be noted that essence 'grows' in the form of weird stuff around loci that Uratha can eat to regain essence, so I'd imagine it CAN be transported, at least in the Hisil, if not in the flesh assuming you can see it / touch it.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully that communicates where our confusion is; not sure how else to explain, really. Basically, there's all this language about gifting or paying essence to spirits for things, but no explanation anywhere I can find about how exactly this is supposed to happen, and the language used (to me) seems separate from going out and doing things to deliberately make essence or otherwise drive it to where the spirit is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T05:56:14-08:00","id":1159394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chandrak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159351#post1159351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully that communicates where our confusion is; not sure how else to explain, really. Basically, there's all this language about gifting or paying essence to spirits for things, but no explanation anywhere I can find about how exactly this is supposed to happen, and the language used (to me) seems separate from going out and doing things to deliberately make essence or otherwise drive it to where the spirit is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I have a direct, easy answer to your question, however there are ways to draw out and store essence so it can be used later. Also, there is an excellent AP on RPG.net, <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal\" target=\"_blank\">The Seventh Seal</a>, that illustrates spirit-dealing very well. It's been an inspiration for me at least.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T08:38:24-08:00","id":1159432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chandrak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1159351#post1159351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question the best I can think of to word it is 'how does this actually happen in-game?' I'd already asked previously about whether they needed to be paid in appropriate essence - there's all sorts of mentions of paying spirits essence, including paying them to even begin talking to them in the first place, but how does that actually occur if you can't just give them some or they need the right kinds?<br /> <br /> In the example, the Pain Angel seems to require a gift of essence AND the creation of additional essence both - but how do you bring it that first essence in the first place? If it just sucks essence right out of you (which doesn't seem like an ability that spirits can have), then it wouldn't be the right kind unless you were Resonant; In this specific case its probably simple, because if you need healing you're probably already Resonant to a degree with Pain, but what if we're talking about other kinds of spirits? The example seems to pretty well mirror the book, which talks about needing to bring a gift of Essence to even open negotiations, but how would that even work if you were approaching say, a Computer Spirit? How would you 'bring' computer-resonant essence to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviating here. Healing-Resonant Essence is created from the act of Healing. What it looks like, if anything, depends.<br /> <br /> Lore of the Forsaken p129, 'Essence cannot be perceived as a thing in and of itself, but as a series of phenomena. Uratha have to use all of their senses to \ufb01nd free Essence as it bleeds through the Gauntlet and \ufb02ickers into and out of existence in the spirit world \u2014 brie\ufb02y appearing as sensations related to its resonance. Essence \ufb02avored with joy might appear as a whirlwind of \ufb02ower petals, the sound of laughter, the scent of ice cream, the touch of satin.'<br /> <br /> This is why werewolves are bombarded by sensory information in the Hisil, because it's practically made of a wide variety of experiences that they can feel, smell, hear, see, or taste or any combination of these. A spirit can take it in a variety of different ways. Smaller spirits might 'eat' the physical representations, while a larger one might just bathe in it, their ephemeral essence just absorbing it. One that resembles a human or animal might 'breathe' it in.<br /> <br /> <b><i>This is more what you're asking. </i></b>As a straight offering of Essence, it looks like through the rules of the Shadow a spirit can just 'take' Essence from a werewolf, if offered. This is how lesser spirits offer up tithes of Essence to greater ones in their feudal system. It should be represented by some sort of act specific to the spirit, of course, not just holding out your hand full of glowing energy and tossing it to the spirit. Werewolf Essence seems to undergo some 'processing' in the werewolf, and it's not all 'Essence of the hunt.' On their own, werewolves can't just 'let out' Essence, without a special <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Gift</a> that only allows it to transfer between packmates..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If on the other hand the idea is you're only supposed offer to go make some somewhere, the language they use all the time about offering gifts before being able to bargain doesn't really make much sense to me - it makes more sense that you're bringing an already-existant gift to give them in order put them at ease or show respect so you can begin making an offer in the first place. This implies to me, somehow, that either you are able to transport essence, or they can draw it directly from you somehow. (Also, it should be noted that essence 'grows' in the form of weird stuff around loci that Uratha can eat to regain essence, so I'd imagine it CAN be transported, at least in the Hisil, if not in the flesh assuming you can see it / touch it.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully that communicates where our confusion is; not sure how else to explain, really. Basically, there's all this language about gifting or paying essence to spirits for things, but no explanation anywhere I can find about how exactly this is supposed to happen, and the language used (to me) seems separate from going out and doing things to deliberately make essence or otherwise drive it to where the spirit is. </div> </div> </div>I think the bits and pieces around loci can't really be transferred, or if they can, it doesn't equate to any real Essence outside of the locus. The same book mentioned above, Lore of the Forsaken, points out that when you get to visible representations you aren't meant to get too mechanically solid, and that 'one glowing light' doesn't equal one Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T12:30:48-08:00","id":1164599,"title":"","content":"Got more questions haha - thanks for the continued patience and answers! We\u2019re getting there with our understanding of the rules - last session we managed to answer several before deciding to post. <br /> <br /> As an aside beforehand, we did find a way to carry essence, sort of - apparently in one of the 1e books there\u2019s a Fetish called the Cup of Life that is intended for just that. While obviously 1e, we decided it\u2019s worth converting it for our use, seeing as my Boneshadow has the fetish rite.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, on to questions:<br /> <br /> 1. If something has multiple types of attacks, like a Magath with special attacks, bites, and claws, can it use all of them at once or mist select one per turn? (We\u2019re kind of assuming only one, but figured we\u2019d ask).<br /> <br /> 2. We figured out the roll forncrossing the Gauntlet, but what, if any, is the penalty for failing that roll? In 1e there was, our ST thinks, but we didn\u2019t see anything in 2e.<br /> <br /> 3. What constitutes unarmed attacks? Namely, can things like claws be counted as unarmed for the purposes of merits? One of our Uratha has a merit that affects unarmed opponents, he wanted to know if spirits with only claws counted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21246-chandrak","name":"Chandrak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T13:00:41-08:00","id":1164607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chandrak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1164599#post1164599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If something has multiple types of attacks, like a Magath with special attacks, bites, and claws, can it use all of them at once or mist select one per turn? (We\u2019re kind of assuming only one, but figured we\u2019d ask).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the vast majority of cases each one of those attacks will require one instant action, and for the most part things can only take one of those per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. We figured out the roll forncrossing the Gauntlet, but what, if any, is the penalty for failing that roll? In 1e there was, our ST thinks, but we didn\u2019t see anything in 2e. </div> </div> </div>Two turns per Gauntlet level. You could have other things happen but they seem to want to get rid of extraneous penalties for using your natural abilities like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. What constitutes unarmed attacks? Namely, can things like claws be counted as unarmed for the purposes of merits? One of our Uratha has a merit that affects unarmed opponents, he wanted to know if spirits with only claws counted. </div> </div> </div>Yes, claws and teeth count as unarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T16:39:33-08:00","id":1164922,"title":"","content":"Clarification on the third question: Claws and teeth are unarmed, but many Fighting Styles are incompatible with that type of natural weaponry. Teeth are naturally only used when biting, and claws can be impossible to combine with Fighting Styles that rely on closed fists, kicks, or throws. Simply put, use your own common sense.<br /> In your example, however, the Merit would definitely work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-03-2017, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T20:59:47-08:00","id":1166599,"title":"","content":"Can the benefits available from a successful use of Crimson Spasm be reassigned from turn to turn? The description of the effect and the consequence of the dramatic failure lead me to suspect that would be thematically appropriate, at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T02:01:47-08:00","id":1166661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1166599#post1166599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the benefits available from a successful use of Crimson Spasm be reassigned from turn to turn? The description of the effect and the consequence of the dramatic failure lead me to suspect that would be thematically appropriate, at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is exactly the way I play it, in my humble mind the gift should have been like to alocate successes and have them as buff up in strength, stamina, natural weaponry, and or armor for the rest of the scene, which would have been quite logical. But the word ''spasm'' that needs to be fueled with essence every turn makes me think of constantly violent shapeshifting which indeed supports the ''reassigned every turn successes'' version you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T07:45:00-08:00","id":1167298,"title":"","content":"Did we ever get an official answer as to whether Uratha deals lethal or bashing to spirits that they don't outrank by 2?<br /> <br /> If not, would a reasonable rule be If Uratha ranks lower than the spirit then bashing, if both rank the same lethal and if the Uratha outrank the spirit by 2 aggravated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T08:16:15-08:00","id":1167308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167298#post1167298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever get an official answer as to whether Uratha deals lethal or bashing to spirits that they don't outrank by 2?<br /> <br /> If not, would a reasonable rule be If Uratha ranks lower than the spirit then bashing, if both rank the same lethal and if the Uratha outrank the spirit by 2 aggravated?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038056#post1038056\">some</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038290#post1038290\">comments</a> by Bunyip that didn't explicitly answer this question, but came down pretty solidly on the side of &quot;if it bleeds, [werewolves] can kill it&quot;, which to me rather suggests the intention is that they deal lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T10:22:43-08:00","id":1167348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167298#post1167298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever get an official answer as to whether Uratha deals lethal or bashing to spirits that they don't outrank by 2?<br /> <br /> If not, would a reasonable rule be If Uratha ranks lower than the spirit then bashing, if both rank the same lethal and if the Uratha outrank the spirit by 2 aggravated?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is written in the book Uratha do lethal damage with fangs/teeth in all forms to all enemies, super or not, gauru does lethal with claws as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T12:37:42-08:00","id":1167385,"title":"","content":"Only their fangs have the mystical endowment of Lethal. Claws will do Lethal to humans, but not pierce a vampire's undead-numbness.<br /> <br /> I think it was a compromise. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/122291-uratha-teeth-and-claws\">The vampire forum blew up for a little bit</a> when <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\">it was suggested werewolves might be able to do Lethal to them with all their attacks</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-13-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T14:12:29-08:00","id":1167412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167348#post1167348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it is written in the book Uratha do lethal damage with fangs/teeth in all forms to all enemies, super or not, gauru does lethal with claws as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not what the book says at all. What it says is that &quot;[Uratha] bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources&quot; and names vampires as an example. There is no clarification as to what it means for a foe to be &quot;vulnerable to mystical sources&quot;, a statement which is only further muddled by the fact that Vampire itself has a passing mention of vampires only taking bashing from &quot;most non-supernatural weapons&quot; with no clarification of that statement, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T02:49:09-08:00","id":1167553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167412#post1167412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's not what the book says at all. What it says is that &quot;[Uratha] bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources&quot; and names vampires as an example. There is no clarification as to what it means for a foe to be &quot;vulnerable to mystical sources&quot;, a statement which is only further muddled by the fact that Vampire itself has a passing mention of vampires only taking bashing from &quot;most non-supernatural weapons&quot; with no clarification of that statement, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary the book supports me:<br /> <br /> <u><b>GAURU</b></u> <i>Teeth and Claws: Claw attacks deal +2 lethal damage.</i><br /> <i>Bites deal +2 lethal damage and do not require a grapple</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>DALU</b></u><br /> <i>Teeth and Claws: Unarmed attacks with the werewolf\u2019s</i><br /> <i>claws deal lethal damage to humans. While in a grapple,</i><br /> <i>successful bite attacks (see p. 167) deal lethal damage</i><br /> <br /> The answer to this issue is specified in every form, gauru does lethal with fang and claw to all targets, end of story, since there are no other mentionings, this is how it works.<br /> Dalu does lethal with fangs and bashing to all except humans to take lethal from dalu claws, <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">uratha also do lethal to spirits (and vampires) with Urshul claws as well as described in the same teeth and claw section.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>THE PREDATOR\u2019S JAWS</b></u><br /> <i>''Their teeth carry the deadly</i><br /> <i>resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As</i><br /> <i>such, their bites in every form count as mystical</i><br /> <i>sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources.''</i><br /> <br /> <br /> This is a side note that specifies that uratha jaws in all forms do lethal damage, even in hishu, it has nothing to do with the ability of uratha to do lethal with gauru claws,<br /> <br /> Now the ''if'' and ''what'' is vulnerable to such damage its up to the ST, but in general anything that can take the role of predator and prey is vulnerable to such mystical sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-14-2017, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:17:00-08:00","id":1167555,"title":"","content":"Back in Vampire, I remember one reason people being opposed to werewolf bites dealing lethal to vampires and Strix was because it \u201ccheapens\u201d vampires and Strix. While it\u2019s something I don\u2019t agree with, I do hope that the upcoming Contagion Chronicles (or any other crossover source) do address that concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T04:17:11-08:00","id":1167564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167553#post1167553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the contrary the book supports me:<br /> <br /> The answer to this issue is specified in every form, gauru does lethal with fang and claw to all targets, end of story, since there are no other mentionings, this is how it works.<br /> Dalu does lethal with fangs and bashing to all except humans to take lethal from dalu claws, <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">uratha also do lethal to spirits (and vampires) with Urshul claws as well as described in the same teeth and claw section.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> This is a side note that specifies that uratha jaws in all forms do lethal damage, even in hishu, it has nothing to do with the ability of uratha to do lethal with gauru claws,<br /> <br /> Now the ''if'' and ''what'' is vulnerable to such damage its up to the ST, but in general anything that can take the role of predator and prey is vulnerable to such mystical sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>All weapons are said to deal lethal damage as well so that is no different from how WW claws and teeth work. The thing is, vampires (and many undead I believe) are specifically said to take bashing damage from lethal damage sources. The exception is WW teeth since for some inexplicable reason they are special. (Even as a WW storyteller I don't like this).<br /> <br /> Now spirits I believe only take bashing from WW that don't outrank them, they only take lethal from their banes. But spirits are &quot;killed&quot; as soon as they fill up on lethal so it is kind of the same as aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The one issue also have with the whole teeth=lethal to vamps is it has trained my players to never attack with anything else. They always go for the bite. It tends to get tedious to describe for the 20th time in a single fight how they bite their foe this particular time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T04:40:09-08:00","id":1167570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167564#post1167564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All weapons are said to deal lethal damage as well so that is no different from how WW claws and teeth work. The thing is, vampires (and many undead I believe) are specifically said to take bashing damage from lethal damage sources. The exception is WW teeth since for some inexplicable reason they are special. (Even as a WW storyteller I don't like this).<br /> <br /> Now spirits I believe only take bashing from WW that don't outrank them, they only take lethal from their banes. But spirits are &amp;quot;killed&amp;quot; as soon as they fill up on lethal so it is kind of the same as aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The one issue also have with the whole teeth=lethal to vamps is it has trained my players to never attack with anything else. They always go for the bite. It tends to get tedious to describe for the 20th time in a single fight how they bite their foe this particular time.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a sidebar in the corebook of 2e as to why Uratha, which literally means Slayer in First Tongue bypass mystical damage imperviousness. Nevermind their whole original deal was to be able to shepherd the most fundamental aspects of reality.<br /> <br /> Regarding spirits, that's only if the spirit is in twilight. Materialized or Hisil poluling spirits take lethal.<br /> <br /> Maybe stop tossing vampiric antagonists to werewolves? Poisoned blood Sharta should get in vogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T07:23:17-08:00","id":1167604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167564#post1167564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All weapons are said to deal lethal damage as well so that is no different from how WW claws and teeth work. The thing is, vampires (and many undead I believe) are specifically said to take bashing damage from lethal damage sources. The exception is WW teeth since for some inexplicable reason they are special. (Even as a WW storyteller I don't like this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural damage.<br /> <br /> From Blood &amp; Smoke, 'Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This includes most non-supernatural weapons.' Rose has stated exceptions from non-supernatural weapons can include devastating things like a shotgun blast to the head or face. But it does imply that supernatural weapons (such as the mystical fangs of the thing that created Predators in the first place) would pierce the defense. If people didn't make such a fuss the first time around, they would probably have more options as it's likely claws would count too.<br /> <br /> This seems like if it's something you had a problem with would be the simplest thing in the world to house rule. 'They cause bashing.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-14-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:08:37-08:00","id":1167620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167564#post1167564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All weapons are said to deal lethal damage as well so that is no different from how WW claws and teeth work. The thing is, vampires (and many undead I believe) are specifically said to take bashing damage from lethal damage sources. The exception is WW teeth since for some inexplicable reason they are special. (Even as a WW storyteller I don't like this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not lethaal damage sources, but mundane lethal damage sources, there is quite the difference. Anything that does lethal and is part of the mystical does lethal to vampires, for instance a mountain lion spirit will do lethal to a vampire while a normal mountain lion will do bashing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167564#post1167564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now spirits I believe only take bashing from WW that don't outrank them, they only take lethal from their banes. But spirits are &quot;killed&quot; as soon as they fill up on lethal so it is kind of the same as aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Spirits take lethal from all uratha natural weapons that do lethal, except dalu and urhan claws, now if a werewolf hits a spirit with a normal sword it will do bashing, but if the sword is a fetish weapon it will do lethal.</span></span></span><br /> No spirits take aggravated damage from their banes, aggravated damage also makes them lose essence. Spirits fear and respect uratha, appart froma hating them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167564#post1167564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one issue also have with the whole teeth=lethal to vamps is it has trained my players to never attack with anything else. They always go for the bite. It tends to get tedious to describe for the 20th time in a single fight how they bite their foe this particular time.</div> </div> </div> </div>See? The only teeth thing created a story mood issue, let your players have flexibility in order to have more fun. If you are troubled in what to follow, in order to be right in a campaign, follow the road of good mood and atmosphere. Not like:<br /> -Player: I bite him<br /> -Story Teller: Not again *facepalm*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-14-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:20:08-08:00","id":1167631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167570#post1167570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding spirits, that's only if the spirit is in twilight. Materialized or Hisil poluling spirits take lethal.<br /> <br /> Maybe stop tossing vampiric antagonists to werewolves? Poisoned blood Sharta should get in vogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf in Hisil deals lethal to spirits in Hisil? Oh. I had this idea from somewhere that something like a rank 3 spirit should be a challenge to several werewolves, but even a rank 3 spirit is almost as easy to kill as a tough human? They do of course have high defence but they don't have armor and such right in the Hisil, since they are formed of spirit stuff? Or can they?<br /> <br /> I have stopped giving them vampires to feed on so they probably won't fight them much anymore, but your idea of giving the enemies a highly poisonous blood is a great idea. Will need to try that soonish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167604#post1167604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like if it's something you had a problem with would be the simplest thing in the world to house rule. 'They cause bashing.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was really considering of house ruling it but they had faced vampires a few times by then and I didn't want to go and change the rules around during the same &quot;game&quot;. Never played any nWoD stuff really before starting this campaign so didn't realize beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:25:09-08:00","id":1167636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167553#post1167553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer to this issue is specified in every form, gauru does lethal with fang and claw to all targets, end of story, since there are no other mentionings, this is how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no. It's specified that werewolf teeth and claws deal lethal damage, but all weapons do that. The only thing that specifically mentions any kind of ability to bypass damage resistance is the Predator's Jaws sidebar, which is very vague. To me it sounds like they should count as the Bane of any entity they fight, but that is clearly not the intention. It could also be interpreted as werewolf teeth counting as &quot;supernatural&quot; for things that care about that, which is pretty much just vampires. Maybe. That rule is pretty vague in itself.<br /> <br /> From the developer commentary though it seems that the intention was that they deal lethal to pretty much everything, but the problem is that's not actually stated in the book. Hence this recurring debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:30:03-08:00","id":1167637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167631#post1167631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf in Hisil deals lethal to spirits in Hisil? Oh. I had this idea from somewhere that something like a rank 3 spirit should be a challenge to several werewolves, but even a rank 3 spirit is almost as easy to kill as a tough human? They do of course have high defence but they don't have armor and such right in the Hisil, since they are formed of spirit stuff? Or can they?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can. They can also have weapons. They're far tougher than humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:30:52-08:00","id":1167638,"title":"","content":"Any tips on how to make fights in Werewolf exiting and challenging to the players? I have 3 players regularly and am having a tough time keeping them on their toes. The only thing that seems to work is having more enemies than there are players, but I find it hard to keep track of combat when there are 3-4 good guys against 4-5 bad guys. Especially with tracking initiatives with different weapons and the werewolves changing forms from turn to turn. Do you maybe have a good system of how to keep track of health and initiative?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167637#post1167637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can. They can also have weapons. They're far tougher than humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I always thought that while in the Hisil the spirits can't have armor, that they don't really have seperate 'parts' if that makes any sense. I thought things like armor would be represented by having high Resistance, hence more Corpus and Defence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 12-14-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:53:11-08:00","id":1167657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167638#post1167638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any tips on how to make fights in Werewolf exiting and challenging to the players? I have 3 players regularly and am having a tough time keeping them on their toes. The only thing that seems to work is having more enemies than there are players, but I find it hard to keep track of combat when there are 3-4 good guys against 4-5 bad guys. Especially with tracking initiatives with different weapons and the werewolves changing forms from turn to turn. Do you maybe have a good system of how to keep track of health and initiative?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the way action economy works, multiple antagonists are probably one of the best ways to deal with it. I don't have any particularly good system but I've never had trouble just writing down their Health and Initiative orders.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, you can have fewer antagonists but load them up with Numina or Dread Powers and extra Health to make them last longer. Or play more 'guile' like and have them be harder to actually get at, as werewolves are not as good at range. That could involve flying spirits, or something like a Mountain spirit who can create obstacles at a whim.<br /> <br /> A big part of making things more exciting or challenging is knowing what your players are capable of. Checking out their sheets you can see that, if you have an Ithaeur with the first auspice Gift you probably won't be able to throw a spirit at them and leave its bane a mystery, as the first Gift can let you know what a spirits bane is. Look at how much damage your players are likely to do in one round, individually and as a group, so you can see what you should do for Health. See how good their combat pools and Defense are. And if you want to keep things interesting, don't fall into the 'tank' game, it's not an MMO and spirits shouldn't be treated like monsters with Threat, uselessly flailing at the toughest character while others act to lower its Defense and plink away its Health.<br /> <br /> The Hurt Locker would probably help. One of the aspects of the first chapter is about making dangerous areas, like fighting on top of a speeding semi-truck trailer. Scenery is really important if you want to make things interesting and exciting. The Batman the Animated Series creator's bible specifically points out that, at the climax of each episode, the confrontation with antagonists should appear in an interesting fashion. 'Each episode will also feature a big set piece, an incredible visual action visual that will be a looked-forward-to element in each show. This will be the climax, centerpiece or show-stopper of each episode.' Things like fights on the top of skyscrapers or massive clocktowers, or hunt-and-kills in a House of Mirrors or dark sewer. Not only does this allow you to use the environment (the spirit winds almost blow you off the top of the cathedral, though you manage to keep your ground, but your packmate is clinging feebly to a gargoyle at the lip of the roof, do you help them or continue fighting the Bird of Pray?), but allows a spirits aspects come into play in force, even in Claimed, providing you've tailored the situation to the spirit's advantage. A spirit of water might have Influences that never come into play in the parking lot next to the dock, but why would it fight there, instead have the fight occur on a boat in storm-tossed waters. This doesn't mean spirits can't be lured out of their comfort zone but there's no reason to play them like lambs to the slaughter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1167638#post1167638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason I always thought that while in the Hisil the spirits can't have armor, that they don't really have seperate 'parts' if that makes any sense. I thought things like armor would be represented by having high Resistance, hence more Corpus and Defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ephemera, at least usually, like their weapons. They can also have Numina that do it, I think it was called Rage Armor, with successes granting Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-14-2017, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:30:17-08:00","id":1167676,"title":"","content":"Other is lethal and other is lethal to humans, as stated in dalu. I know that the book descriptions are a bit enigmatic, I think you should see things with werewolf in the center and leave aside other games and keep an eye on where you find something, not only what it says. And I will say it for second and last time, a bane does aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T01:13:59-08:00","id":1168741,"title":"","content":"A Werewolf in Gauru forces humans to use Down and Dirty combat. So all attacks are resolved with 1 contested roll each?<br /> Let's say a group of 10 mind controlled humans attack a lone Werewolf in a single round. The Werewolf is out to kill them all and so are the humans. So, there are 10 rolls in a row, and let's say that in all of them the attacking humans roll less successes than the Werewolf. Does that mean, that even without taking any actions, the Werewolf has just managed to kill 10 humans?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Any penalty for the WW because of the extra attacks?<br /> Also, does Down and Dirty apply to ranged attacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 12-19-2017, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:43:30-08:00","id":1168753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1168741#post1168741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Werewolf in Gauru forces humans to use Down and Dirty combat. So all attacks are resolved with 1 contested roll each?<br /> Let's say a group of 10 mind controlled humans attack a lone Werewolf in a single round. The Werewolf is out to kill them all and so are the humans. So, there are 10 rolls in a row, and let's say that in all of them the attacking humans roll less successes than the Werewolf. Does that mean, that even without taking any actions, the Werewolf has just managed to kill 10 humans?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Any penalty for the WW because of the extra attacks?<br /> Also, does Down and Dirty apply to ranged attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe the entire thing is resolved with one roll for everyone. So, onewolf roll, one mob roll.* if the werewolf wins, yes, everyone dies. The whole point of down and dirty is to gloss over all those unnecessary details like what actions are taken.<br /> <br /> No penalty for the wolf - defense isn't subtracted. This is a pure contested roll.<br /> Yes, ranged attacks count for D&amp;D combat. Uhh.. down and dirty. You know what I mean!<br /> <br /> * I use teamwork rolls here. So, still 10 rolls, but the successes add up differently, and only one primary actor.<br /> <br /> EDIT - if the point of mind controlled humans is that they can act in a coordinated manner and ignore fear, then don't use Down and Dirty combat rules. Or at least call for a clash of wills first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-19-2017, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T08:44:34-08:00","id":1168808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1168741#post1168741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Any penalty for the WW because of the extra attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>To add some clarity here, there is no penalty because there is no 'extra attacks' Down and Dirty Combat isn't an Action, it's not taking a Turn to accomplish. It is an out of character way of resolving the outcome of the scene quickly. You would want to narrate the combat a bit to explain how it happens (I imagine good fight scenes like John Wick vs. some mooks or that church scene in Kingsman).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T23:41:36-08:00","id":1169019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1168753#post1168753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the entire thing is resolved with one roll for everyone. So, one wolf roll, one mob roll.* if the werewolf wins, yes, everyone dies. The whole point of down and dirty is to gloss over all those unnecessary details like what actions are taken.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1168808#post1168808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To add some clarity here, there is no penalty because there is no 'extra attacks' Down and Dirty Combat isn't an Action, it's not taking a Turn to accomplish. It is an out of character way of resolving the outcome of the scene quickly. You would want to narrate the combat a bit to explain how it happens (I imagine good fight scenes like John Wick vs. some mooks or that church scene in Kingsman).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarifications, I think I get it now. It's more a roll for the whole scene and not turn-by-turn combat.<br /> <br /> The point of using D&amp;D combat (yes I will call it that) for when facing weak threats in Gauru is just to skip the dice rolls and just narrate how everyone is killed or driven away since the WW regenerates all non-aggravated damage anyway, so there is really no point.<br /> <br /> Using teamwork rolls might be a good idea if there are so many enemies that you might not be able to kill them all before Gauru is expended. Perhaps if the WW loses the roll, they only eliminate as many enemies as they got successes and still face the rest of them without instant regeneration.<br /> <br /> But if the humans are using silver weapons or there are supernatural enemies in the mix, then it should be resolved as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T02:14:02-08:00","id":1169033,"title":"","content":"Personally, even if the humans have silver weapons, I would say that they can use D&amp;D combat. I believe that the Primal Fear ability is the result of Lunacy affecting the minds of the mortals and making them unable to fight properly. Sure, the silver will hurt more, but shots will be going wild, there will be friendly fire, etc. Supernaturals have a bit of resistance, and I would say that hunters should count as supernaturals for this kind of fight and be able to fight back, but average mortals, even if armed with silver, should get down and dirty.<br /> <br /> EDIT - And don't forget that, in down and dirty combat, both sides still take damage from the fight. Its entirely possible for a werewolf to kill all the humans, but then die of wounds after the fight ends and she loses the extra health from the form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-20-2017, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T04:38:45-08:00","id":1169048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1169033#post1169033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT - And don't forget that, in down and dirty combat, both sides still take damage from the fight. Its entirely possible for a werewolf to kill all the humans, but then die of wounds after the fight ends and she loses the extra health from the form.</div> </div> </div> </div>But only the side that loses the D&amp;D roll takes any damage. A WW (especially Rahu) almost definitely has mode dice to use for the roll than humans so it's fairly likely they will take no damage.<br /> <br /> Actually that brings another question to my mind. When a WW &quot;runs out&quot; of turn in Gauru, do they have to change back at the end of the last turn, or at the start of a next one? Or maybe I should rather ask what is the &quot;turn order&quot; when regeneration happens? Only at the start of the players turn?<br /> <br /> Let's say a player takes 6 Lethal damage before his turn. At the start of that turn He decides to change into Gauru. Does he automatically heal all of that 6 damage? So changing reflexively let's them heal fully and then take their normal now-Gauru turn? So when they run out of Gauru, the damage done after their last turn does not get fully healed, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:49:21-08:00","id":1169059,"title":"","content":"Yes, Yes, No. If you are in Gauru and it's your turn, you regen. Regen subsides if you're not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T02:22:48-08:00","id":1175397,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, <br /> <br /> I'm looking for some suggestions to this dilemma (last minute I know) but I'm playing a Werewolf 1 on 1 game within the next day or so. The GM is looking to introduce my Werewolf to the pack so I can join them in later games. The problem is the character I'm meeting is the not so people person combat focused Werewolf. My character is an antisocial Ithaeur (more lone shaman based), how can we smoothly intergrate my character into their pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T07:54:03-08:00","id":1175459,"title":"","content":"Without knowing what the pack is about, the basic requirements tend to be: be useful, be loyal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T17:16:27-08:00","id":1176864,"title":"","content":"Ok so I'm having a dispute over the teeth and claw abilities of the wolf forms.<br /> Some friend's of mine are saying that it can do the bite attack and as the same instant action begin a grapple.<br /> I'm saying the rules say you can either do damage or grapple. Not both at the same time.<br /> Which is right?<br /> Rules below<br /> Teeth and Claws: Claw attacks deal +1 lethal damage. Bites deal +2 lethal damage and do not require a grapple. Bite attacks can establish grapples as well as cause damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T18:33:24-08:00","id":1176873,"title":"","content":"RAI has to be that once you bite you're automatically in a grapple (if you wish to), since the grappling part of it is that you just bite down rather than letting go after the bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T21:51:14-08:00","id":1176886,"title":"","content":"Indeed, when a werewolf or something with such jaws bite, they apply the bite damage and hold the opponent in a grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T22:01:41-08:00","id":1176887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176864#post1176864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I'm having a dispute over the teeth and claw abilities of the wolf forms.<br /> Some friend's of mine are saying that it can do the bite attack and as the same instant action begin a grapple.<br /> I'm saying the rules say you can either do damage or grapple. Not both at the same time.<br /> Which is right?<br /> Rules below<br /> Teeth and Claws: Claw attacks deal +1 lethal damage. Bites deal +2 lethal damage and do not require a grapple. Bite attacks can establish grapples as well as cause damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yes, you can initiate a grapple on a successful bite action (claws also if in Gauru). If your victim is later in the initiative, they basically lose their turn. When it comes back around to the higher of the initiative of the grappling characters, the first contested Strength+Brawl vs Strength+Brawl roll is made to figure out which gets to act.<br /> <br /> Now, this actually reminded me of a question I had:<br /> If a werewolf in a non-human form wins a grapple contest and chooses to do damage, that damage is lethal instead of bashing, right? (Unless they want to do bashing in Dalu.)<br /> <br /> Now, would the damage bonus from teeth be applied to this damage roll as extra damage, or would it already be &quot;included&quot; in the amount of successes for the damage maneuver?t<br /> <br /> Also, what about specialties. If a WW has a brawl specialty in bite, would that grant extra die in a grapple situation? Then what about a grappling specialty? Could both then apply (or was there a rule about only one specialty per roll)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T00:18:11-08:00","id":1176906,"title":"","content":"There's a sidebar in the 2e corebook regarding Uratha teeth regarding your first question; Yes, the damage modifiers to teeth apply; in 2e you apply all the relevant specs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T03:56:04-08:00","id":1176917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176864#post1176864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I'm having a dispute over the teeth and claw abilities of the wolf forms.<br /> Some friend's of mine are saying that it can do the bite attack and as the same instant action begin a grapple.<br /> I'm saying the rules say you can either do damage or grapple. Not both at the same time.<br /> Which is right?<br /> Rules below<br /> Teeth and Claws: Claw attacks deal +1 lethal damage. Bites deal +2 lethal damage and do not require a grapple. Bite attacks can establish grapples as well as cause damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'll be honest - it can be read both ways, and I'm not entirely sure myself of the intended reading. I lean towards reading it as the bite attack can be used for grapples and for inflicting damage, but not both simultaneously, as the Chronicles of Darkness system tends to veer away hard from anything that tampers with the action economy by stacking actions or offering multiple actions in one go. I wouldn't lay claim to my reading being a one true interpretation, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T08:51:12-08:00","id":1176962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176917#post1176917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'll be honest - it can be read both ways, and I'm not entirely sure myself of the intended reading. I lean towards reading it as the bite attack can be used for grapples and for inflicting damage, but not both simultaneously, as the Chronicles of Darkness system tends to veer away hard from anything that tampers with the action economy by stacking actions or offering multiple actions in one go. I wouldn't lay claim to my reading being a one true interpretation, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that vampires in Frenzy explicitly both deal damage and establish a grapple with the same action when biting. I can also point out that Clinch Strike is a one dot Merit that allows <i>regular mortals</i> to both deal damage and establish a grapple with the same action. I find it harder to believe that werewolves wouldn't be able to do both when in a form that grants them fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T08:57:21-08:00","id":1176965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176962#post1176962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that vampires in Frenzy explicitly both deal damage and establish a grapple with the same action when biting. I can also point out that Clinch Strike is a one dot Merit that allows <i>regular mortals</i> to both deal damage and establish a grapple with the same action. I find it harder to believe that werewolves wouldn't be able to do both when in a form that grants them fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSure, and I'm not trying to tell you how to do things in your own games - just indicating which direction my preferences lie. The rules you've mentioned don't change my inclination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T09:24:33-08:00","id":1176976,"title":"","content":"Preferences are preferences, of course, but my intention was providing examples that clearly state that's a part of the action economy that CofD quite clearly doesn't mind tampering with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T20:11:11-08:00","id":1177499,"title":"","content":"Is there a way (1st or 2nd edition) to close a Spiritual wound area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T21:48:21-08:00","id":1177518,"title":"","content":"Seems to be time and work, like in first edition. Resonance Shaping would go a long way towards it in second and there's a variety of 'lock down' the area type abilities that might help, but also might make things worse. We haven't had any special updated rules on them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T15:40:02-08:00","id":1177699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176864#post1176864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some friend's of mine are saying that it can do the bite attack and as the same instant action begin a grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm like 98% sure that's the intent. If the intent was to say you could either choose to do damage <b>or</b> start a grapple, it would simply point out that the teeth can be used to grapple someone, since being able to use them to damage someone is a 'duh' since they have a weapon modifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T16:04:28-08:00","id":1177704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1176864#post1176864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I'm having a dispute over the teeth and claw abilities of the wolf forms.<br /> Some friend's of mine are saying that it can do the bite attack and as the same instant action begin a grapple.<br /> I'm saying the rules say you can either do damage or grapple. Not both at the same time.<br /> Which is right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first one. You attack with a bite, succeed and deal damage. If you choose to not let go, you\u2019re in a grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:40:49-08:00","id":1180254,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've got a handful of werewolf questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Can Uratha carry spirits across the gauntlet while reaching? I assume this would probably at least require Harmony below 9.<br /> <br /> 2) In Apocalypse (old world of darkness) there was a ritual to change one's auspice. Has there been an equivalent in Forsaken?<br /> <br /> 3) A weird one: how much clothing damage should a high-harmony werewolf expect when shifting into Dalu? Are we talking straining of seams, or hulking out? <br /> <br /> 4) A bit more subjective: would you allow a wolf-blooded with the Anger Issues Tell to voluntarily &quot;trigger&quot; themselves with an instant action and a willpower point (a bit like a high-harmony Uratha shifting)? <br /> <br /> 5) How would you deal with another supernatural power trying to interfere with Kuruth? For example, a mage using Mind to calm down someone currently in Wasu-Im. A Clash of Wills? Versus the Uratha's Renown+Primal Urge, maybe? What if the raging individual is wolf-blooded (no renown, effective primal urge of 1)?<br /> <br /> 6) The Shape Shifted Tell has the wolf-blooded going Urhsul during the full moon. Classic werewolf lore would suggest they would enter Kuruth, but the Tell doesn't specify this. Bug or feature?<br /> <br /> 7) How many Tells do you reckon it would take before a wolf-blooded would register as Uratha to supernatural senses? And is this before or after the Storyteller has a fit and tells you to just play an actual werewolf already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:01:05-08:00","id":1180256,"title":"","content":"2. Not to change Auspice, as far as I know. There is, however, a ritual for tearing out a werewolf's Auspice that is used by the Pure.<br /> <br /> 3. I believe many clothes would rip, but not necessarily shred. Dalu adds one Size, and at least some of that Size comes through muscles and fur.<br /> <br /> 5. Clash of Wills is the rule created just for such occasions, and page 115 says Clash of Wills for a werewolf would be Primal Urge + Auspice Renown (so who knows what Pure would roll) when not using Gifts. A Wolf-Blooded would use the same dice pool, which would start at chance die before any bonuses such as from Willpower. (There is one Tell that does increase a Wolf-Blooded's Primal Urge that would help in this situation.)<br /> <br /> 7. I don't think Wolf-Blooded are supposed to have more than two Tells considering that the Tell Merit is for developing a &quot;<i>second tell</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:22:15-08:00","id":1180264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180256#post1180256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clash of Wills for a werewolf would be Primal Urge + Auspice Renown (so who knows what Pure would roll) when not using Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanical requirements being what they are, I'd posit that a Pure werewolf uses their tribe's primary Renown for generalized Clash rolls, since that's the one they'll all have a dot in. (Tribeless Pure are, as in everything else, kind of up in the air.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:57:40-08:00","id":1180288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180254#post1180254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can Uratha carry spirits across the gauntlet while reaching? I assume this would probably at least require Harmony below 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it's been answered in second edition. If it is possible, the spirit would shift into Twilight Form when it crossed over, and therefore be generally out of reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) In Apocalypse (old world of darkness) there was a ritual to change one's auspice. Has there been an equivalent in Forsaken? </div> </div> </div>No, like Tessie said, you can remove your Auspice, and potentially gain it back, but that's mostly it, and half of it is storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) A weird one: how much clothing damage should a high-harmony werewolf expect when shifting into Dalu? Are we talking straining of seams, or hulking out? </div> </div> </div>A lot would depend on the clothes, eh? Straining, maybe bursting some seams. Definitely not hulking out level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) A bit more subjective: would you allow a wolf-blooded with the Anger Issues Tell to voluntarily &quot;trigger&quot; themselves with an instant action and a willpower point (a bit like a high-harmony Uratha shifting)? </div> </div> </div>They would have to have a good reason for it, some sort of Merit that allows them to achieve a meditative state or a worthy memory to fall back on. That's just my personal ST decision, though, I could see others allowing it or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) How would you deal with another supernatural power trying to interfere with Kuruth? For example, a mage using Mind to calm down someone currently in Wasu-Im. A Clash of Wills? Versus the Uratha's Renown+Primal Urge, maybe? What if the raging individual is wolf-blooded (no renown, effective primal urge of 1)? </div> </div> </div>For Basu-Im the answer's on page 103. Clash of Wills is generally reserved for two vying powers, so it doesn't seem to be warranted unless someone was forcing Kuruth on the werewolf at the same time someone else was trying to nullify it (two elodoth using their abilities on the same werewolf, for instance). It would just be a resistance roll, likely based on Resolve+Primal Urge, though it would depend on the ability used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) The Shape Shifted Tell has the wolf-blooded going Urhsul during the full moon. Classic werewolf lore would suggest they would enter Kuruth, but the Tell doesn't specify this. Bug or feature? </div> </div> </div>Feature. Urshul doesn't go Kuruth, anyways, that's Gauru. You could easily tack on a variant rule that had the wolf be uncontrollably raging or doing things based on the character's subconscious desires, or controlled by the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) How many Tells do you reckon it would take before a wolf-blooded would register as Uratha to supernatural senses? And is this before or after the Storyteller has a fit and tells you to just play an actual werewolf already? </div> </div> </div>If you mean a werewolf's supernatural senses, never, though you could have a Tell that gives false positives. Going outward it would depend on whatever ability was being used to sense the supernatural and how knowledgeable the user is about werewolves or wolf-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-28-2018, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:11:17-08:00","id":1180318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180288#post1180288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Basu-Im the answer's on page 103. Clash of Wills is generally reserved for two vying powers, so it doesn't seem to be warranted unless someone was forcing Kuruth on the werewolf at the same time someone else was trying to nullify it (two elodoth using their abilities on the same werewolf, for instance). It would just be a resistance roll, likely based on Resolve+Primal Urge, though it would depend on the ability used.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you adjudicate it if the werewolf <i>wanted</i> to be pulled out of rage? The Still Small Voice facet uses the same die pool, but it seems wrong that calming effects would be less helpful to a werewolf with high resolve. Maybe I'm just thinking about this too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think Wolf-Blooded are supposed to have more than two Tells considering that the Tell Merit is for developing a &quot;<i>second tell</i>&quot;. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/glee/images/b/b4/Maleficent_telling_you_to_shhh.gif/revision/latest?cb=20140413214350\" target=\"_blank\">Shhhhh...</a><br /> <br /> That particular question was mostly in jest. I have what, I think, is a decent metaphysical reason for multiple Tells. The short version is that the character was literally in the middle of his First Change but took a hard left into the Primal Wilds and Awakened instead. Luna said &quot;it's okay i love you anyway&quot; and dumped a pile of Tells on him that essentially come down to having all the rage and shapeshifting (minus Gauru form) of a true werewolf but none of the control. Angst ensues (as an example, I'm picturing a scenario where he tries Goetic magic to &quot;cast out&quot; his wolf-blooded-ness, which ends precisely as poorly and bloodily as you might expect). In case it isn't obvious, I'm trying to gauge how effective his magic should be at mitigating the Kuruth problem: I don't want it to be easy (a chance-die to &quot;resist&quot; a calming effect would qualify as &quot;too easy&quot;), but there should be <i>some</i> recourse. Hopefully the fact that this is all a problem for the character to overcome should make it clear that I'm not just trying to get around the template stacking-rules. Of course, I could change my mind again and have him just be a high-harmony werewolf that's good with rites (*whinny voice* But rites are <i>boring)</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd comment that it took me far too long to write this post, but if I did that, I would have to do it on all of my posts, making them take even longer and...dang it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":".  typos 01-28-2018, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:54:29-08:00","id":1180328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180318#post1180318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you adjudicate it if the werewolf <i>wanted</i> to be pulled out of rage? The Still Small Voice facet uses the same die pool, but it seems wrong that calming effects would be less helpful to a werewolf with high resolve. Maybe I'm just thinking about this too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow it to have much of an impact unless the werewolf also had some other ability to affect that, like Controlled Burn, where maybe you could cut out the Resolve but not the Primal Urge part. Even then, if there is a trigger occurring it might just be triggered again in the next few moments.<br /> <br /> It's one of the drawbacks of being a werewolf, arguably part of their 'curse' and not wanting it to happen is something most werewolves would experience, at least consciously. Like Sunlight for vampires or Disquiet for Prometheans. It's something magic can help you get around but it shouldn't be made easy. And, while I'm not saying this is your intent, if people want to excise it from the game, they can just do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-28-2018, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:40:38-08:00","id":1180343,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23730_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23730\" data-vbnamecard=\"23730\">Scriptorian</a> Keep in mind influencing an Uratha's Kuruth is penalized by twice the werewolf's Primal Urge if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T22:38:51-08:00","id":1180351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180328#post1180328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of the drawbacks of being a werewolf, arguably part of their 'curse' and not wanting it to happen is something most werewolves would experience, at least consciously. Like Sunlight for vampires or Disquiet for Prometheans. It's something magic can help you get around but it shouldn't be made easy. And, while I'm not saying this is your intent, if people want to excise it from the game, they can just do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you on all that. I mean, I find the whole idea compelling enough that I'm trying to shoehorn it into a mage character. It's just weird that normally high Resolve helps a werewolf get out of rage (Composure+Resolve roll to do non-aggressive stuff in Wasu-im), but when a friend tries to pull you out it becomes a liability, apparently. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180343#post1180343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23730_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23730\" data-vbnamecard=\"23730\">Scriptorian</a> Keep in mind influencing an Uratha's Kuruth is penalized by twice the werewolf's Primal Urge if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but in my case that's only two dice (assuming an effective Primal Urge of 1. Which I assume, because the Anger Issues Tell says you get regeneration while in Dalu, which, based on the Wolf's Meat Tell, assumes a effective Primal Urge 1. Aaaand... now I have to go to the mage forum and figure out how the magic rules would deal with that minus 2.) Gosh, it's so weird to spend all this effort making sure my character's weaknesses are enough of a liability. I used to be an unapologetic power-gamer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T23:03:11-08:00","id":1180353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1180351#post1180351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gosh, it's so weird to spend all this effort making sure my character's weaknesses are enough of a liability. I used to be an unapologetic power-gamer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as a wolf-blooded your weaknesses aren't going to be built off of Kuruth, more your overall squishiness and vulnerability in relation to the things that are antagonistic to wolf-blooded. The Pure, spirits, Claimed, hosts, Forsaken and ghost wolves. If a werewolf can pull a spirit across by Reaching, they may not be able to grab it in Twilight Form, but they can at least see it. Unless a wolf-blooded has Piercing Eyes, a spirit can just hang around them getting them ready to Claim.<br /> <br /> It's not really played up much, presumably due to people not expecting them to be the main aspect of play, but being a wolf-blooded combines the horror of all the enemies and revelation of Werewolf, with a massive lacking in ability to deal with it. They may not be corralled for breeding pens or whatever anymore but they're still really vulnerable.<br /> <br /> That said, look at the tenth storytelling commandment, 'Celebrate the Awesome.' This character seems to have some interesting blessings, embrace it. There's no need to try to weaken or balance out your character, your storyteller has more than enough ammunition to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-29-2018, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T03:56:32-08:00","id":1181069,"title":"","content":"Are there any restrictions/downsides to having a mobile Locus and moving it?<br /> <br /> Let's say you have an object as a Locus, perhaps a serial killers favorite weapon or some such. Can a werewolf just carry it around and have pack members be able to pop in and out of the Hisil at will? I would imagine a reason for not moving your Locus outside of a well maintained territory is that it would attract all kinds of nasty attention from the spirits you go near, but the essence pooling that makes a Locus is contained &quot;inside&quot; the object itself, not around it, so that it can be carried around?<br /> <br /> Just a scenario that popped into my head. Let's say a bad guy is telling a PC to come alone to a remote desert meeting and if he sees anyone else approach, he will kill their loved one. Could he just carry a Locus in his pocket and have all of his pack in the Hisil then pop out and surprise slaughter everyone at the meeting?<br /> <br /> Or an Irraka sneaks into a building carrying a Locus and lets his pack in that way.<br /> Having the ability to basically move through wall/fences seems kinda nice too, since not all of them might be there on the other side.<br /> <br /> Loci can't be picked up and moved from the Hisil side, right? Only fed from?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could the Pure just carry a Locus and have an army of spirits on the other side, ready to be unleashed when they want to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 01-31-2018, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T04:26:57-08:00","id":1181074,"title":"","content":"Are moving Locus a thing? I need to look it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T04:52:11-08:00","id":1181080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1181074#post1181074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are moving Locus a thing? I need to look it up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At first I didn't think they were, but in the Loci section on p.179 it does say &quot;Loci are individual objects or creatures&quot; so I would assume they can move. Most (if not all) examples of loci I have seen are stuff that is pretty much stationary, like places, trees, buildings and rooms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 01-31-2018, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:49:54-08:00","id":1181100,"title":"","content":"There's no written rules for them in 2e, so up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T07:43:12-08:00","id":1181123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1181069#post1181069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any restrictions/downsides to having a mobile Locus and moving it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance being what it is, you're likely going to be looking at an effective reduction in dot rating for the purposes of crossing area if you just move the focus of a locus somewhere completely separate from its normal resting place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:25:57-08:00","id":1181134,"title":"","content":"There's rules for mobile loci (and living loci) in first edition's Lore of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> It boils down to, they can happen if you want, and are a tremendous advantage for the reason you mentioned (a movable Reaching portal) but reminds you to keep in mind that a mobile one doesn't really help solidify territory and the same advantage can turn into a drastic negative, as werewolves aren't the only ones who can empower themselves via loci and moving it around guarantees a lack of control over its location and who happens to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:19:32-08:00","id":1181837,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been asked and I'm not about to search through over 120 pages to check, but here it goes. What happens when a werewolf fulfills it's totems Aspiration? Does it go away and get replaced like a normal Aspiration or is it something you can milk over time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:33:35-08:00","id":1181846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1181837#post1181837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been asked and I'm not about to search through over 120 pages to check, but here it goes. What happens when a werewolf fulfills it's totems Aspiration? Does it go away and get replaced like a normal Aspiration or is it something you can milk over time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to make my totem's aspiration something recurring. For example, I have a totem of revenge, it's pack given aspiration is 'avenge packmates'. For any given slight. A spirit of fear's aspiration could be as simple.<br /> <br /> In the case of less spiritual aspirations, you could change it. Forsaken totemic aspiration aren't nearly as self-aggrandizing as Pure ones, with things like &quot;get to the top of the hisil food chain&quot;, IE maximize it's rank in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:51:13-08:00","id":1181850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1181837#post1181837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been asked and I'm not about to search through over 120 pages to check, but here it goes. What happens when a werewolf fulfills it's totems Aspiration? Does it go away and get replaced like a normal Aspiration or is it something you can milk over time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not something that would change without a change to the spirit, which is possible if it grows more powerful or picks up new Influences. Like Glabna the Unyielding Stone's totem aspiration is 'To remain strong despite all challenges.' But if the pack gets a lot of members, or it gets wounded by a demon, or the pack just gets bloodthirsty in their hunger for power, it might start aspiring to have a human sacrificed upon it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T19:39:16-08:00","id":1181894,"title":"","content":"So can a regular mortal or even a werewolf be in multiple packs at once?<br /> And get the benefit of all their totems? Or only one of their choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 02-02-2018, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T20:00:07-08:00","id":1181898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1181894#post1181894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can a regular mortal or even a werewolf be in multiple packs at once?<br /> And get the benefit of all their totems? Or only one of their choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a mention of it in one of the books, but it's the kind of thing that would rarely work out and usually be easy to find out, in game. Providing you're using the setting, spirits have an innate connection and bond to all packmates, and unless there was something magical happening it would likely notice if a member had an alien Resonance, which isn't getting into the ways a werewolf could do it. But there are soon-to-be Pure who would go 'undercover' in Forsaken packs to prove themselves by luring the Forsaken into a trap or feeding the Pure information about them. It's also a way the Bale Hounds could turn a pack out from the inside while still being part of another Bale Hound group that isn't a lodge or tribe. But these would imply some sort of magical deception or subterfuge.<br /> <br /> You would probably get all the benefits, though it's possible a spirit might just block you from being a part if you didn't fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T14:25:15-08:00","id":1182066,"title":"","content":"Hey all, first post here. I am just getting into WW/OP games and am trying to whip up some friends to play WTF, so I'm diving into this game pretty hard here. I wasn't able to find the answer to my question in a search so I apologize if this is commonly asked.<br /> <br /> My question is on Harmony, specifically Breaking Points, and the way the section in the 2nd ed. rulebook is phrased.<br /> <br /> Refer to page 104:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a character hits a breaking point towards Spirit,<br /> he subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Harmony<br /> below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Harmony. When he<br /> hits a breaking point towards Flesh, he gets a penalty for each<br /> point of Harmony above 5. If the roll is a failure, the character<br /> gains a point of Harmony. This means an Uratha\u2019s Harmony<br /> can fluctuate wildly over the course of play. </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm not sure if the text is phrased poorly, if I'm completely misunderstanding how harmony dots are allocated, or if I'm misunderstanding how the mechanic works, but based on this it sounds like it's very easy to break toward a werewolf of spirit and difficult to break toward a werewolf of flesh. But it sounds like the rules strongly favor breaking downward rather than upward, unless you have a high humanity stat already in which case you'd be entrenched toward the flesh. In this way it seems thematically similar to the way you'd play, I dunno, an addict who has just one drink or something. As the book mentions, it's generally ideal to maintain balance between the two extremes. Am I misreading this somehow or are werewolves meant to gradually slip toward the spiritual?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23815-sieranthefox","name":"SieranTheFox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T15:01:13-08:00","id":1182079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182066#post1182066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it sounds like the rules strongly favor breaking downward rather than upward, unless you have a high humanity stat already in which case you'd be entrenched toward the flesh. In this way it seems thematically similar to the way you'd play, I dunno, an addict who has just one drink or something. As the book mentions, it's generally ideal to maintain balance between the two extremes. Am I misreading this somehow or are werewolves meant to gradually slip toward the spiritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about 'strongly,' but yes a slide towards the spirit is the natural inclination of werewolves. Though keep in mind you do start with 7 Harmony and you get Touchstones, giving you a bonus to either side, and extra Breaking Points at lower than 4 or higher than 7 Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T15:21:47-08:00","id":1182087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182066#post1182066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not sure if the text is phrased poorly, if I'm completely misunderstanding how harmony dots are allocated, or if I'm misunderstanding how the mechanic works, but based on this it sounds like it's very easy to break toward a werewolf of spirit and difficult to break toward a werewolf of flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you got that reading from &quot;Rolls for breaking points away from the middle of the Harmony scale suffer a penalty for every point of Harmony away from 5 in that direction&quot; on its own, but yes, it's supposed to get increasingly easier to fall farther up or down the scale as you gain or lose Harmony, particularly given that your counterbalancing Touchstone stops providing its benefit if you're far enough out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T16:32:51-08:00","id":1182109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182066#post1182066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not sure if the text is phrased poorly, if I'm completely misunderstanding how harmony dots are allocated, or if I'm misunderstanding how the mechanic works, but based on this it sounds like it's very easy to break toward a werewolf of spirit and difficult to break toward a werewolf of flesh. But it sounds like the rules strongly favor breaking downward rather than upward, unless you have a high humanity stat already in which case you'd be entrenched toward the flesh. In this way it seems thematically similar to the way you'd play, I dunno, an addict who has just one drink or something. As the book mentions, it's generally ideal to maintain balance between the two extremes. Am I misreading this somehow or are werewolves meant to gradually slip toward the spiritual?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give you an example:<br /> <br /> Say your character has Harmony 7, and he spends a whole month without venturing to the shadow. That's a breaking point toward Flesh (base -2), and given he's 2 points above perfect balance and breaking toward that end, he gets another -2. Those modifiers are usually countered by touchstones, at least negating from 1 to 4 points assuming you've taken a merit such as Anchored (normally it'll be a flat +2).<br /> <br /> Consequently, if my character is in Harmony 4, he gets a ban, and killing people is a spirit breaking point at (-1) because of the touchstones and state of harmony.<br /> <br /> All of this is alleviated by the point you're at harmony 8 and above, or 3 and below, because then you get much more easier breaking points toward the other end of the harmony chart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 02-03-2018, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T16:35:43-08:00","id":1182110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182087#post1182087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you got that reading from &quot;Rolls for breaking points away from the middle of the Harmony scale suffer a penalty for every point of Harmony away from 5 in that direction&quot; on its own</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that reading of the rules was how I thought it would work, but it seems like there is meant to be a bit of a bias toward the spiritual, which is fine. Also, as nofather pointed out, I am ignoring the presence of touchstones and your starting harmony when interpreting these rules. I'll err on the side of interpreting the text literally, it just seemed interesting to me that the ideal would be balance between the opposing extremes and yet, the rules would slightly bias a slide toward one end rather than another. But it makes sense thematically and allows for some interesting spirit world interaction so I'm all for it.<br /> <br /> Thanks again guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23815-sieranthefox","name":"SieranTheFox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:21:06-08:00","id":1182125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182110#post1182110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that reading of the rules was how I thought it would work, but it seems like there is meant to be a bit of a bias toward the spiritual, which is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not seeing where you got this from the quoted portion, is what's confusing me. The mechanics of low Harmony incentivize it more than high Harmony's mechanics incentivize it and Forsaken culture is set up in such a way that you'll more likely shift towards the middle of the scale than stabilize around the First Change's starting point of Harmony 9, but I'm not sure what about &quot;the more unstable your Harmony is, the easier it is to further destabilize it&quot; suggests the mechanics &quot;strongly favor&quot; low Harmony. Care to clarify your initial train of thought?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T23:55:31-08:00","id":1182191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182125#post1182125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not seeing where you got this from the quoted portion, is what's confusing me. The mechanics of low Harmony incentivize it more than high Harmony's mechanics incentivize it and Forsaken culture is set up in such a way that you'll more likely shift towards the middle of the scale than stabilize around the First Change's starting point of Harmony 9, but I'm not sure what about &quot;the more unstable your Harmony is, the easier it is to further destabilize it&quot; suggests the mechanics &quot;strongly favor&quot; low Harmony. Care to clarify your initial train of thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. This is reading the rules of how breaking point rolls work in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a character hits a breaking point towards Spirit,<br /> he subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Harmony<br /> below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Harmony. </div> </div> </div>So if you have, I dunno, 9 harmony, you take a penalty to a breaking point roll of 4. This make you -4 more likely to fail the roll, which would slide you toward the spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When he<br /> hits a breaking point towards Flesh, he gets a penalty for each<br /> point of Harmony above 5. If the roll is a failure, the character<br /> gains a point of Harmony. </div> </div> </div>So if your harmony is two, you receive no penalty toward your roll since you have zero harmony above 5 and the roll is disproportionately more likely to entrench a spirit-oriented character to remain in the spirit, rather than a flesh-oriented character, who is more likely to fail a roll and slide toward the spirit.<br /> <br /> Again, I recognize that this ignores a lot of balancing mechanics that have an existing presence in the game but in the absence of everything else, swinging from the high extreme to the other is more favored than its opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say your character has Harmony 7, and he spends a whole month without venturing to the shadow. That's a breaking point toward Flesh (base -2), <b>and given he's 2 points above perfect balance and breaking toward that end, he gets another -2</b>. Those modifiers are usually countered by touchstones, at least negating from 1 to 4 points assuming you've taken a merit such as Anchored (normally it'll be a flat +2). </div> </div> </div>I am so very confused. Please clarify the bolded portion. Because from my reading of the rules, being two points above perfect balance does not penalize toward the spirit. It appears that the penalty would be -4 because of the four dots that exist <i>below</i> 5, per the second quote in this post. I still feel like I might be fundamentally misunderstanding the rules...<br /> <br /> NB: I have a nasty habit of proofreading after I post. I may make small edits here and there to clarify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23815-sieranthefox","name":"SieranTheFox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T03:09:32-08:00","id":1182210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182191#post1182191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am so very confused. Please clarify the bolded portion. Because from my reading of the rules, being two points above perfect balance does not penalize toward the spirit. It appears that the penalty would be -4 because of the four dots that exist <i>below</i> 5, per the second quote in this post. I still feel like I might be fundamentally misunderstanding the rules...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think the problem here is you're thinking that harmony should be filled as dots. I think it might help you if you think of the Harmony track more as like a sliding scale. If you have Harmony 7, that does not mean you should fill in all the dots from 1 to 7 so that the points are almost fully colored in. Rather, fill in only 1 dot and put it in where 7 would be. So you don't have any points &quot;towards&quot; spirit if you are over 5. Under 5 you have points towards spirit. Maybe putting a permanent inked dot at 5 and filling in 6 and 7 would be easier to see how many points you are towards flesh (2 points). Then if you go to 6, you are 1 dot towards flesh, none to spirit. Harmony at 3 would be 2 points towards spirit, none towards flesh.<br /> <br /> So basically, it's counted from 5. 5 is kinda like 0, it is the balanced state.The further you go from that the easier it's to keep sliding to that end. Works kinda like a non-electric celcius thermometer. 0 it where water freezes. The rest are either - degrees or + degrees.<br /> <br /> At least that has been my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-04-2018, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T04:40:24-08:00","id":1182228,"title":"","content":"Cainite has it right: Harmony is a scale from 0-10, with 5 sitting as the balance point in the perfect middle, having 5 dots above and below.<br /> <br /> Is those dots towards each side which act as penalties to slide further in that direction. If you have Harmony 7 you don't have any points towards spirit, you just have 2 steps towards Flesh away from the point of Balance, and so a -2 penalty to Flesh related Harmony Breaking Points. If you suffered a Breaking point towards Spirit at Harmony 3 your roll would be similarly penalized, as Harmony 3 is two steps &quot;unbalanced&quot; towards Spirit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For ease of visualization you could fill out only the dots from 5 to either direction, so for Harmony 7 you would only fill out the 5th 6th and 7th dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-04-2018, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:16:17-08:00","id":1182406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SieranTheFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182191#post1182191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you have, I dunno, 9 harmony, you take a penalty to a breaking point roll of 4. This make you -4 more likely to fail the roll, which would slide you toward the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. If you have Harmony 9 you have a baseline -4 penalty to the Resolve + Composure roll to avoid <i>gaining</i> Harmony from breaking points toward Flesh. You have <i>no</i> baseline penalty for rolls to avoid <i>losing</i> Harmony from breaking points toward Spirit, because 9 is not below 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if your harmony is two, you receive no penalty toward your roll since you have zero harmony above 5 and the roll is disproportionately more likely to entrench a spirit-oriented character to remain in the spirit, rather than a flesh-oriented character, who is more likely to fail a roll and slide toward the spirit. </div> </div> </div>This is the reverse of the reading problem above \u2014 if your Harmony is 2, you're three points below Harmony 5 and therefore suffer a -3 penalty to the Resolve + Composure roll to avoid <i>losing</i> Harmony, but since 2 is not above 5 you have no inherent penalty for rolls to avoid <i>gaining</i> Harmony from breaking points toward Flesh. A Flesh-oriented character is not <i>more likely</i> to lose Harmony.<br /> <br /> You've grasped <i>parts</i> of the dynamic, but what you're missing is that the dynamic goes in both directions \u2014 once your Harmony destabilizes from 5, you have a cumulatively harder time resisting gaining Harmony at higher Harmony or losing it at lower Harmony while receiving no such added difficulty in the opposite direction. You have to <i>fail rolls</i> to alter your Harmony in either direction, and it's harder to flip from one end of the scale to the other because the middle is more desirable and exists along the way up or down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T23:46:36-08:00","id":1182514,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys for the input.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182210#post1182210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I think the problem here is you're thinking that harmony should be filled as dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book straight up says you should do this on the very same page. &quot;The ideal point, the balance, is five dots.&quot; &quot;Humans who go through the First Change replace Integrity with Harmony, and start with nine dots regardless of their Integrity.&quot; It's full of verbiage suggesting that Harmony should be counted from zero and &quot;filled up&quot; rather than a track.<br /> <br /> The interpretation you guys are presenting makes more sense and is how I prefer to interpret the mechanic, but it does contradict what's on the page, and at least is inconsistent with about every other filled-dot mechanic in the game from what I've read so far. So this is something that could really use a wording update, if I may make a suggestion to the writers. I mean, I trust you guys, but I just can't wrap my head around the wording. I've been staring at paragraphs 2 through 5 in the Harmony section on pp. 104 for literal <i>days</i> and I cannot interpret the text in the way you're all presenting it to me, and that's turning out to be a rather severe hangup. :&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23815-sieranthefox","name":"SieranTheFox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T23:57:18-08:00","id":1182515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182406#post1182406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the reverse of the reading problem above \u2014 if your Harmony is 2, you're three points below Harmony 5 and therefore suffer a -3 penalty to the Resolve + Composure roll to avoid <i>losing</i> Harmony, but since 2 is not above 5 you have no inherent penalty for rolls to avoid <i>gaining</i> Harmony from breaking points toward Flesh. A Flesh-oriented character is not <i>more likely</i> to lose Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's this. When the text says &quot;for each point of Harmony below 5,&quot; it is simply using less than ideal diction to explain the concept. This happens; writers are human. The writer's intent could be more clearly conveyed as something like &quot;for each point <i>by which</i> your Harmony is below 5.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T23:59:36-08:00","id":1182516,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m curious, did the book never use the concept of absolute values to explain Harmony? Such as, 2 in absolute values away from 5? I was sure the book was worded that way, but my memory\u2019s hazy and now I\u2019m not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T00:05:12-08:00","id":1182517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182515#post1182515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's this. When the text says &quot;for each point of Harmony below 5,&quot; it is simply using less than ideal diction to explain the concept. This happens; writers are human. The writer's intent could be more clearly conveyed as something like &quot;for each point <i>by which</i> your Harmony is below 5.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know, but the tricky thing is stuff like this makes me think that <i>I'm</i> going crazy. This has definitely cleared it up though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23815-sieranthefox","name":"SieranTheFox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T03:12:40-08:00","id":1182530,"title":"","content":"Yes, the wording is quite unclear, once you see it one way, it's kind of hard to see why it should be interpreted the other way. The words &quot;harmony track&quot; should have been used or something. In my initial read through of the book I thought the same way as you did, but after trying to figure out what it meant by &quot;for every point above...below&quot; I came to that conclusion. Probably a legacy of the fact of how Integrity and humanity are tracked, and how Harmony was in 1st edition. It's different than pretty much anything else, except for The Pack book where the packs Hunting Nature is shown on a sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T08:27:01-08:00","id":1182611,"title":"","content":"Guys the rules are simple:<br /> <i>''When a character hits a breaking point towards Spirit, he subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Harmony below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Harmony. When he<br /> hits a breaking point towards Flesh, he gets a penalty for each point of Harmony above 5. If the roll is a failure, the character gains a point of Harmony.''</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T08:50:02-08:00","id":1182618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1182611#post1182611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys the rules are simple:<br /> <i>''When a character hits a breaking point towards Spirit, he subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Harmony below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Harmony. When he<br /> hits a breaking point towards Flesh, he gets a penalty for each point of Harmony above 5. If the roll is a failure, the character gains a point of Harmony.''</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The problem is that a literal reading will make anyone with 4+ Harmony always have 4 filled dots of Harmony below 5 ranging from 1 to 4. Fortunately this misconception has been explained and cleared now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T08:12:51-08:00","id":1182935,"title":"","content":"Quick question. It's awkward, but I'll ask it here: <br /> <br /> Is anyone aware of powers among werewolves or other splats that would force a shapeshifter (default assumption: werewolf) to return to base human form? Essentially in most useful application, to knock him out of Gauru by forcing a change.<br /> <br /> There were a variety of such powers scattered around WoD lines, but I've not spotted any in CofD yet.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T08:36:52-08:00","id":1182939,"title":"","content":"In first edition the Wolfslayer Gift set had Return to Birth which changed a werewolf back to human. In first the Horn of Munin and Waters of Songkran fetishes (the latter would be more of a talen in second edition). In second, the Garmir have Flense Shape. There's also a variety of 'command' powers, like Lay Low the Challenger or Dominate, that would probably help for this.<br /> <br /> Just as an addition, first edition werewolf was pretty insular, and did not really have abilities that targeted things outside the lines. So most targets would be Uratha, mortals, spirits, and occasionally ghosts. I don't think there are werewolf powers called out to affect other shapeshifters, like those from Changing Breeds, Skinchangers, or War Against the Pure, or shapeshifters among other gamelines. Second edition has expanded on it a little, but not nearly as much as other lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2018, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T08:42:43-08:00","id":1182942,"title":"","content":"A demon using the Wave Function Collapse Embed from Flowers of Hell couldn't collapse a werewolf from Gauru back to Hishu, but could prevent a werewolf who is not yet in Gauru from being able to shift into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T11:51:06-08:00","id":1183002,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> that's a useful place for my understanding to start. It seems as though there is precedent for such abilities (whether in item form or no), which means that if homebrew 2e is needed a benchmark on power/expense exists. I'm also going to assume that anything forcing a werewolf change would key of spiritual energies as much as &quot;shape flesh&quot;--to use very imprecise language.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> the very fact Demon has a power with that name is <i>almost</i> enough to make me look at the game. (Sadly, spy stories have never been my thing.) Noted however is the &quot;prevent shapeshift&quot; benchmark. Thanks!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T21:12:46-08:00","id":1183155,"title":"","content":"To add to those, the Elodoth werewolf auspice ability Darkness Into Light can force a Death Raging werewolf out of it, which would make them fall back to human form and be stunned for a round. Since they can only go Gauru once per scene voluntarily, that would prevent that at least. Can shift to other forms still, so....<br /> <br /> For my game sort-of off screen I had this medical research company facility that was run by a spirit-ridden/claimed person do some experiments on werewolves that were using some sort of cocktail of drugs and weird spirit &quot;things&quot; to have their werewolf guinea-pig be unable to control their change, forcing them to either stay human or go into gauru death rage for their demonstrations/experiments. Didn't really have any support in the rules for that but since it didn't happen to a player character, it was OK in my mind to use some BS storyteller reason.<br /> <br /> It's OK if I have my imaginary characters torture another of my imaginary characters. Some not-GM people might think it's strange to stay up at night and think of all the ways imaginary creatures are torturing others, even if no one will ever know of what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-07-2018, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T22:50:21-08:00","id":1183482,"title":"","content":"Do Spirits roll two attributes for perception? Finesse+Resistance? That would mean a Rank 3 spirit would be hard to ambush, Rank 4 almost impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T23:02:40-08:00","id":1183485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1183482#post1183482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Spirits roll two attributes for perception? Finesse+Resistance? That would mean a Rank 3 spirit would be hard to ambush, Rank 4 almost impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> P184, 'Attribute + Attribute for actions like surprise and perception.' Finesse from Wits, Resistance from Composure.<br /> <br /> They sense things, any eyes they have are inconsequential, at least for perceiving things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T07:49:18-08:00","id":1183587,"title":"","content":"You can easily incorporate disadvantages in such rolls as forms of bans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T08:09:56-08:00","id":1183594,"title":"","content":"Thanks nofather for the reply, I recalled reading that but could not seem to find it for some reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1183587#post1183587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can easily incorporate disadvantages in such rolls as forms of bans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that did occur to me. My players are wanting to do some sort of assault on a Pure held territory (one the Pure took from them months ago) and I was thinking they most likely have some Spirits watching the place. Was thinking of some observation spirits that maybe have a ban that they can't see those that are themselves unable to see. Maybe the players have to blind themselves (stab out their eyes) or something gnarly like that if they want to move past them without notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T20:11:52-08:00","id":1183809,"title":"","content":"Or a specific time or phenomena makes their perception an automatic failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T22:00:14-08:00","id":1185018,"title":"","content":"Rage Gift: Berserker's Might (Glory facet): Reflexive &quot;...can be used once per turn when in Dalu, Gauru or Urshul.... may immediately heal a single Tilt that is a physical injury such as Arm Wrack, Blind, or Leg Wrack....&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean it would heal any of the damage that caused the tilt, since it says heal, or does it mean that it just removes the tilt without touching the health damage you have? I'm assuming the latter. Also, if you had Leg Wrack in both legs, it would heal only one of them, right?<br /> <br /> How would this work in narration if someone uses let's say Crimson Falx fetish to chop that leg clean off, if it doesn't heal the damage? What about a tilt caused aggravated damage? Maybe someone uses that gift to heal a chopped of leg 5 turns later, the leg just magically reappears, or reattaches regardless of the distance?<br /> <br /> The Rahu Auspice benefit Tenacious to me seems like you just ignore the fact that you have no legs for example and launch yourself at your foe by just pure grit, since it ignores the tilt for just 2 turns. But this gift heals the tilt completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T23:13:04-08:00","id":1185030,"title":"","content":"With the Crimson Falx specifically, I'd just argue that it shouldn't work, personally. Unless your Glory is enough to prevent the damage entirely.<br /> <br /> But if you think it should, and since it clearly doesn't heal the damage, if you just choose to remove the tilt specifically, I would assume that the facet just prevents the leg from being cut off. For the sake of convenience, I would ask that it be used reflexively, and the leg just hangs on, injured but usable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T23:53:22-08:00","id":1185039,"title":"","content":"Yes, while technically the Tilt you would use for Crimson Falx is Leg Wrack, more realistically you would want a Leg Gone Condition. Same penalties, limited resolution.<br /> <br /> I believe the ability (Berserker's Might) just removes the Tilt, does not touch the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2018, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T00:35:29-08:00","id":1185045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185039#post1185039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, while technically the Tilt you would use for Crimson Falx is Leg Wrack, more realistically you would want a Leg Gone Condition. Same penalties, limited resolution.<br /> <br /> I believe the ability (Berserker's Might) just removes the Tilt, does not touch the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't reconcile in my head that the Crimson Falx is not said to deal aggravated damage, but still removes a limb completely. Permanent damage in a non-supernatural is reflected with aggravated damage, so removing a limb should have at least 1 agg damage associated with it.<br /> <br /> With werewolves, lethal heals so fast that it seems comical to me that you remove a limb completely and a new one sprouts before your next turn if in Gauru. I think I might personally rule that it does cause at least 1 aggravated, unless for example as a werewolf you spend an action to hold the neatly severed limb to the stump, then it would be lethal and you can heal the Wrack as if it was lethal damage.<br /> <br /> In my head, regrowing a limb completely as a Werewolf should be more akin to how Deadpool does it in the movie, and not like Piccolo in Dragonball Z.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:09:56-08:00","id":1185186,"title":"","content":"What's the minimum size of an area a Shadow Court has to control before its leaders can be considered Nobles? Or is it not a matter of size, but importance to the surrounding area? Basically, I'm asking if a building or complex like an asylum could support its own court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:49:06-08:00","id":1185203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185045#post1185045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't reconcile in my head that the Crimson Falx is not said to deal aggravated damage, but still removes a limb completely. Permanent damage in a non-supernatural is reflected with aggravated damage, so removing a limb should have at least 1 agg damage associated with it.<br /> <br /> With werewolves, lethal heals so fast that it seems comical to me that you remove a limb completely and a new one sprouts before your next turn if in Gauru. I think I might personally rule that it does cause at least 1 aggravated, unless for example as a werewolf you spend an action to hold the neatly severed limb to the stump, then it would be lethal and you can heal the Wrack as if it was lethal damage.<br /> <br /> In my head, regrowing a limb completely as a Werewolf should be more akin to how Deadpool does it in the movie, and not like Piccolo in Dragonball Z.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its ability to sever limbs is really limited. It's not lopping them off every attack, it only does it once per scene to the first enemy attacked. If it did flat Aggravated damage, it might as well not have any magical power at all as that is wildly powerful on its own. And, mechanically, there is no representation for one limb equalling a certain amount of damage, but I don't think anyone's going to care if you decide to apply one at your table. It would just be a clunky system to add to the fetish section.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone has said that a new limb grows in their next turn, but they do have powers to allow things to be more like Piccolo than Deadpool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T09:08:12-08:00","id":1185217,"title":"","content":"While aggravated damage is the kind of damage that can easily result in a loss of a limb, losing limbs does not require that you've taken aggravated damage. The fact that your arm is missing isn't killing you. It's the bleeding wound that does (and infections), and blood loss is represented through lethal damage.<br /> I think loss of limbs should be best represented by Conditions that can be resolved by healing it as if you were healing a number of aggravated damage, but it doesn't take up space on your health track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-12-2018, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T11:25:32-08:00","id":1185282,"title":"","content":"Aggravated damage does implies to cause persistent limb wrack. Mutilation does fit the bill for catastrophic bodily destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:37:31-08:00","id":1186002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185282#post1185282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aggravated damage does implies to cause persistent limb wrack. Mutilation does fit the bill for catastrophic bodily destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps untreated Mutilation. Eventually, even a paraplegic Uratha wont be rolling around with 4 points of persistent aggradam. Phantom Limb and Pain Conditions perhaps, but it wont be lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T11:02:48-08:00","id":1186014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186002#post1186002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps untreated Mutilation. Eventually, even a paraplegic Uratha wont be rolling around with 4 points of persistent aggradam. Phantom Limb and Pain Conditions perhaps, but it wont be lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha are usually immune to Aggravated damage outside their bane of silver, treating things like explosives as lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T11:54:52-08:00","id":1186028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186014#post1186014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uratha are usually immune to Aggravated damage outside their bane of silver, treating things like explosives as lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>To direct aggravated damage, yes. Indirect aggravated damage is a different story.<br /> <br /> And as to the above, regarding having trouble considering limb loss as not aggravated. There are lots of in game examples that consider Arm and Leg Wrack without Aggravated damage. They aren't mutually exclusive. In fact, you could suffer these tilts without taking any Lethal damage but bashing damage. Sprains and dislocations are not Lethal, and in some cases only arguably qualify as Bashing.<br /> <br /> Regarding Wracks as being Damage at all:<br /> If a PC has just had all their limbs dislocated at all joints, and I try and represent that with 4 wrack tilts and 2 bashing damage for each joint (shoulders, elbows, wrists, hips, knees, heels) each, with a result that rolls over to Lethal, it doesn't mean she is actually bleeding out, though penalties may still apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:30:10-08:00","id":1186037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185186#post1185186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the minimum size of an area a Shadow Court has to control before its leaders can be considered Nobles? Or is it not a matter of size, but importance to the surrounding area? Basically, I'm asking if a building or complex like an asylum could support its own court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure this is supposed to be a Changeling the Dreaming question. Might get more mileage in that forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:39:23-08:00","id":1186040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186037#post1186037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure this is supposed to be a Changeling the Dreaming question. Might get more mileage in that forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I mean like, the leader of a Choir of Spirits in the <i>Hisil. </i>You know, Bloodyclaws, Spirit of Big Cats and Hunting, commanding the loyalty of all the Jungle's hunting and big cat spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-14-2018, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:50:56-08:00","id":1186045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185186#post1185186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the minimum size of an area a Shadow Court has to control before its leaders can be considered Nobles? Or is it not a matter of size, but importance to the surrounding area? Basically, I'm asking if a building or complex like an asylum could support its own court.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186040#post1186040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, I mean like, the leader of a Choir of Spirits in the <i>Hisil. </i>You know, Bloodyclaws, Spirit of Big Cats and Hunting, commanding the loyalty of all the Jungle's hunting and big cat spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is a warped reflection, not an exact reflection. Time (and Space) don't follow the same rules. A long demolished hospital can still appear in the Shadow decades later, provided that the essence resonated from the hospital was not overwhelmed by newer essences. Inversely, a tiny hovel, which provided strong emotions of security and wellbeing, might look to appear as a fortified palace in the shadow. It's all about the spirits that the essence attracts and feeds. In your case, an asylum could be perfectly fitting provided that the essences of the asylum could support them. A very large asylum which was shut down early in its age and didn't see much particular use would probably not even have a reflection in the Hisil, but one that was used for particularly nasty practices, or that saw decades of persistent use, could easily have reached well beyond its physical grounds, turning a small town (based around the asylum) into one large madhouse.<br /> <br /> An example of a feudal court is given in the Book of Spirits, p 100, where a court (Called the Harvest Carnival) is established for only a short time every year, only to rest again till next year. Regardless of the other domains present while it's hibernating, it springs up and lays claim to its domain for only a short time, exerting its rule of law. It even extends beyond its place (the Carnival) and into the township to get the people in town excited about returning to the Carnival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","user":"TriCitiesLodge","date":". 02-14-2018, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T13:01:11-08:00","id":1186049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1185186#post1185186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the minimum size of an area a Shadow Court has to control before its leaders can be considered Nobles? Or is it not a matter of size, but importance to the surrounding area? Basically, I'm asking if a building or complex like an asylum could support its own court.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more of a matter of importance. Location helps if it's isolated, and it sounds like an asylum would be, with basically a lot going on inside and separate from the outside, unless you have breakouts.<br /> <br /> An asylum could have its own court, and it may in turn answer to a higher court in the city. That could be a really engaging affair, where the boss of the asylum court deals with the city spirit personally, or they just put aside a tithe of essence and the city drains it away remotely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-14-2018, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:05:10-08:00","id":1186064,"title":"","content":"Related note. Can a Spirit, even with Numina Traded out for extra Influence, have an influence higher than their Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:12:59-08:00","id":1186067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186064#post1186064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related note. Can a Spirit, even with Numina Traded out for extra Influence, have an influence higher than their Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1184626-stronger-totems?p=1184659#post1184659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. It\u2019s part of what makes being a totem attractive to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably there are some rare ways for non-totems to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T21:22:04-08:00","id":1186174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186028#post1186028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as to the above, regarding having trouble considering limb loss as not aggravated. There are lots of in game examples that consider Arm and Leg Wrack without Aggravated damage. They aren't mutually exclusive. In fact, you could suffer these tilts without taking any Lethal damage but bashing damage. Sprains and dislocations are not Lethal, and in some cases only arguably qualify as Bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know there are. That is what causes the issue in my mind.<br /> A character gets hit by a baseball bat to their arm, causing more lethal damage than their stamina. An Arm Wrack caused by lethal, most likely a break.<br /> <br /> Now, this damage would heal in several days time, healing the Wrack as the last damage is healed. Takes an hour at most for a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Now let's say you use a Crimson Falx that is specifically said to chop off the limb permanently. Not just break the bone. Let's say they wear some armor and only receive one lethal damage. The arm goes flying off, with only 1 damage. If mortal, it takes a few days to heal it. But unlike every other Wrack caused by lethal, it never gets removed even if at full health. In the case of a Werewolf, the damage is healed in a turn or 15 minutes. I try for some sense of realism in my game, arms just growing back without supernatural means does not fit it.<br /> <br /> Now, werewolves are supposed to be able to recover all losses of limbs at some point, just need to remember that they grow a new arm eventually, keep track of it somewhere on the character sheet. I think in my games I might just rule that always the first 1-2 points of damage it deals is aggravated. That way mortals never heal it and takes longer for WW. I also think your overall &quot;health&quot; might be lower if you have chopped off limbs. No offense to any amputees out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T22:07:33-08:00","id":1186181,"title":"","content":"I don't think it makes much sense to make it do aggravated damage. The fetish is balanced around operating as is. Just have it <i>heal </i>as though it were a single (or equivalent) point of aggravated damage, would be my suggestion.<br /> <br /> I'd actually consider have it not healing, but that's just me, and I like weird effects that require spirit magic to undo.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Falx is spirit magic. It isn't doing aggravated damage to chop the leg off, it's just cutting it off clean. Besides, it's not as though 1-3 lethal damage is a negligible amount of damage (even if werewolf do heal these things quickly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 02-15-2018, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T23:46:52-08:00","id":1186197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186181#post1186181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it makes much sense to make it do aggravated damage. The fetish is balanced around operating as is. Just have it <i>heal </i>as though it were a single (or equivalent) point of aggravated damage, would be my suggestion.<br /> <br /> I'd actually consider have it not healing, but that's just me, and I like weird effects that require spirit magic to undo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda regretting having my players getting that particular Fetish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It might be for the best to have this particular thing be represented by a longer lasting Condition rather than damage. But weirdness happens now also because the character who has the fetish, also has the Berserker's Might gift. He was planning on going against some Pure in a session soon. What happens now if a Pure WW takes the weapon from the player and uses it against the player?<br /> <br /> Berserker's lets you instantly heal a physical tilt.<br /> Now, which is stronger, a 4 point fetish or a gift?<br /> <br /> I'm okay with permanently mutilation NPC's, not keen on doing that to a player. Guess we'll need to do some talking at the table and come up with a resolution that the players are happy with as well.<br /> <br /> Thank all of you for the input, you gave me some possible ideas I never considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T04:39:38-08:00","id":1186244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186181#post1186181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it makes much sense to make it do aggravated damage. The fetish is balanced around operating as is. Just have it <i>heal </i>as though it were a single (or equivalent) point of aggravated damage, would be my suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which... is the mechanical equivalent of striking another line over lethal to depict aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186181#post1186181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually consider have it not healing, but that's just me, and I like weird effects that require spirit magic to undo.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Falx is spirit magic. It isn't doing aggravated damage to chop the leg off, it's just cutting it off clean. Besides, it's not as though 1-3 lethal damage is a negligible amount of damage (even if werewolf do heal these things quickly).</div> </div> </div> </div>This would make record keeping a nightmare. Are you suggesting we make some new standard of damage &quot;spiritual damage&quot; with completely random healing times?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:24:10-08:00","id":1186314,"title":"","content":"Just make a condition, I don\u2019t see why it would be a record keeping nightmare more than any other condition, especially improvised ones. Or keeping track of how long the Charmed condition lasts on an exceptional success, for example (1 night per user BP). It\u2019s par for the course, no need to overthink it. If variable times bother you, 4 days (1 agg) can be the standard.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13318\" data-vbnamecard=\"13318\">Cainite</a> I\u2019d say that the fetish supersedes Berseker\u2019s might, just for sanity\u2019s sake, but it\u2019s definitely arguable. Unless it was used to prevent the Falx damage entirely.<br /> <br /> If a PC had his leg permanently lopped off, I\u2019d just lead them to search for a rite or a spirit that could heal it. But yeah, I see why that would be worrying on PCs and might derail the plot, as that\u2019s a pressing issue that they\u2019d have to deal with. Maybe not a good idea after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:16:09-08:00","id":1186363,"title":"","content":"A quick question: in page 82 of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition, on Auspice reference, third paragraph, it says &quot;Also note your character\u2019s Instincts, Hunter\u2019s Aspect, and Auspice Ability.&quot;. What it refers to with &quot;Instincts&quot;? It refers to the section &quot;Individuals: faces&quot; of each auspice? <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:25:47-08:00","id":1186366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186363#post1186363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question: in page 82 of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition, on Auspice reference, third paragraph, it says &quot;Also note your character\u2019s Instincts, Hunter\u2019s Aspect, and Auspice Ability.&quot;. What it refers to with &quot;Instincts&quot;? It refers to the section &quot;Individuals: faces&quot; of each auspice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's an artifact of an older edition. If you download the final copy of the book, it only says 'Also note your character\u2019s Auspice Ability and hunter\u2019s aspect.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T18:06:21-08:00","id":1186500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186363#post1186363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question: in page 82 of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition, on Auspice reference, third paragraph, it says &quot;Also note your character\u2019s Instincts, Hunter\u2019s Aspect, and Auspice Ability.&quot;. What it refers to with &quot;Instincts&quot;? It refers to the section &quot;Individuals: faces&quot; of each auspice?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>As nofather stated, I believe it's an artifact, but not of the original editions, but the transition drafts from 1E to 2E. It's my belief that since Tribes didn't really have a staple Prey in 1E that they were meant to target, and since Werewolves Must Hunt is the natural instinct, the Instincts in that draft would ultimately become The Prey outlined in the Tribe sections in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T00:43:16-08:00","id":1187483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1186500#post1186500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As nofather stated, I believe it's an artifact, but not of the original editions, but the transition drafts from 1E to 2E. It's my belief that since Tribes didn't really have a staple Prey in 1E that they were meant to target, and since Werewolves Must Hunt is the natural instinct, the Instincts in that draft would ultimately become The Prey outlined in the Tribe sections in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T22:34:40-08:00","id":1187750,"title":"","content":"Is there a Tell related to eating meat? Like, eat raw meat you hunted yourself for some sort of bonus or healing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:15:19-08:00","id":1188893,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for one of the Uratha to identify another as Pure or Forsaken on sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:31:28-08:00","id":1188898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1188893#post1188893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for one of the Uratha to identify another as Pure or Forsaken on sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some Gifts that could do it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you would have to be in the Hisil, or have one flaring their renown. Forsaken glow silver, Pure glow red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:39:37-08:00","id":1188901,"title":"","content":"The Blood Talon Sacred Hunt makes identifying Pure more viable, as it reveals Renown Brands on the prey - which glow fiery red to the Blood Talon's eyes if the target is Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:06:30-08:00","id":1188934,"title":"","content":"Are there any physical marking of Auspice, or are they all spiritual brands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:18:07-08:00","id":1188937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1188934#post1188934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any physical marking of Auspice, or are they all spiritual brands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not naturally. Sometimes werewolves get actual tattoos over them, so they have a more physical representation. I suppose a lune with a quirk could give you some physical evidence, like scars or paler flesh where they were.<br /> <br /> And keep in mind when the Pure rip out your Auspice brands, they do so with fire and hate, and sometimes silver. It tends to leave great scars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:17:03-08:00","id":1189006,"title":"","content":"So...this has come up a few times in this thread (raised once by myself) but I'm still not seeing meaningful consensus anywhere.<br /> <br /> Werewolf bites a materialized spirit, and isn't strong enough to count as a bane: Does it do bashing (because spirits downgrade all lethal to bashing) or lethal (because The Predators Jaws)? Spirit/Uratha conflict is so central to this game that I find myself kind of blown away that this isn't made utterly clear in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:25:50-08:00","id":1189010,"title":"","content":"Definitely lethal. The Predators Jaws explicitly always deal lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T03:30:20-08:00","id":1189376,"title":"","content":"I, on the other hand, say they cause bashing damage. Predator's Jaws just seems to me to be just a way to try make vampires less dangerous to werewolves since they can use blood to heal bashing damage so easily (lethal less so).<br /> <br /> Page 98:<br /> Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources. Even in Hishu, a werewolf\u2019s bite causes lethal damage to vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, in fact it does not say explicitly they always cause lethal. It only says that it does so with vampires. The sentences before it are just flavor fluff to justify this vampire bit.<br /> <br /> Page 186:<br /> &quot;Physical attacks on a Manifest spirit, or one in the Hisil, that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane. Even a spirit that\u2019s solid to its attacker doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure. Spirits record and heal from wounds the same way as human characters, but in addition lose one point of Essence for every aggravated wound they suffer. Spirits that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into bursts of ephemera stylized to their natures.&quot;<br /> <br /> That would meant that even a Rank 3 Spirit, which is specifically said to be a challenge to werewolves, would be &quot;killed&quot; faster than a normal human would. Since humans need to be filled with aggravated to truly die they can take pretty much twice the damage that a usual Rank 2 spirit would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-25-2018, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T05:01:12-08:00","id":1189386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189376#post1189376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, say they cause bashing damage. Predator's Jaws just seems to me to be just a way to try make vampires less dangerous to werewolves since they can use blood to heal bashing damage so easily (lethal less so).</div> </div> </div> </div>Manifested spirits are doing so from twilight, being in a twilight state downgrades even damage suffered from their bane. Materialized spirits get no such protection, an is in fact the purpose of rites that force the spirit's to become corporeal, to be more easily dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:26:43-08:00","id":1189428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189386#post1189386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manifested spirits are doing so from twilight, being in a twilight state downgrades even damage suffered from their bane. Materialized spirits get no such protection, an is in fact the purpose of rites that force the spirit's to become corporeal, to be more easily dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I see now. The two words Manifested and Materialized were too similar and got mixed together in my head. Didn't register that they were not in fact the same thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> But it says &quot;Physical attacks on a Manifest spirit, or one in the Hisil, that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane.&quot; and Materialize is a Manifestations, doesn't that mean it is Manifest if it is Materialized?<br /> <br /> &quot;Even a spirit that\u2019s solid to its attacker doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.&quot; Still not seeing how Materialized spirits take lethal damage. They just lose the twilight mode protection that makes them normally impossible to damage, so even a human can shoot a Materialized spirit and it causes bashing.<br /> <br /> Materialized p.190:<br /> &quot;The spirit has shifted from ephemeral to material substance, Manifesting in physical form. <b>All the rules for ephemeral spirit\u2019s traits still apply except for the effects of being in Twilight.</b> This Condition protects the spirit from Essence bleed for its duration..&quot;<br /> <br /> And the effect of twilight is &quot;Spirits in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other spirits, unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane.&quot;<br /> Nothing about Twilight that makes them take bashing only<br /> <br /> <u>Specifically the effect of twilight which are the ones Materialize manifestation removes:</u><br /> &quot;To beings in Twilight, physical objects appear pale and semi-transparent, light appears dimmed, and sound is distorted as though underwater... When in Twilight, only items, creatures, and phenomena that are also in Twilight and comprised of the same kind of ephemera can touch an ephemeral being. Attacks simply pass through the Twilight being; solid concrete and steel are no more hindrance than fog.<br /> <br /> Spirits in Twilight can move at walking pace in any direction. Gravity has no sway, though a spirit can only truly \u201cfly\u201d if it\u2019s appropriate for its form \u2014 most hug the material terrain.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-25-2018, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:35:45-08:00","id":1189443,"title":"","content":"The whole rationale for Bashing damage against vampires also involve their lack of functional internal organs, yet Predator's Jaws works all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:24:39-08:00","id":1189467,"title":"","content":"Yes, spirits naturally enjoy all that protection. It\u2019s a rule of ephemera and the Shadow. <br /> <br /> Werewolves cheat. Or more precisely, trump it as their right of Urfarah\u2019s children. That\u2019s one of the reasons why spirits hate them so much. They\u2019re afraid of the beings that can truly kill them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I highly doubt the Predator\u2019s Jaws was implemented with vampiric endurance in mind. This isn\u2019t WoD, or Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-25-2018, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:53:31-08:00","id":1189473,"title":"","content":"Sort of. When it was originally declared that werewolf natural weapons would always do lethal always, the vampire fans really got loud and angry about it, and it was limited to just werewolf fangs. The threads are still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T15:18:39-08:00","id":1189478,"title":"","content":"The intent of The Predator's Jaws is probably something like this:<br /> &quot;Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites deal lethal damage to all foes that are vulnerable to banes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because nothing (that I know of) has a weakness to &quot;mystical sources of damage&quot; in CofD. That's what really bugs me. (Of the current iteration, I mean. I wasn't involved in the all natural weapons thing.) The natural reading of the rule says one thing, but the example another. Hence we have to reverse engineer the intent of the rule.<br /> <br /> And if you agree with my interpretation of what The Predator's Jaws should be, then werewolf bites will deal lethal damage to spirits (and other ephemerals) despite them normally downgrading lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T21:05:39-08:00","id":1189526,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know how this worked in First Edition? Was just wondering if it was the same there of if it was something different.<br /> <br /> I find it weird that something as integral to the whole game, Spirits and how threatening they are to werewolves, has been left to a throwaway line in a sidebar text that is open to all kinds of interpretation. The only thing that is specifically said, without interpretation clouding it, is that WW deal lethal to vampires and spirits downgrade lethal to bashing.<br /> <br /> The books talk about humans how they are weak individually, threat in numbers (that's the whole basis of all of WoD IMO) but a werewolf is more likely to destroy a rank 4 Spirit in one hit than an old lady walking her dog at night.<br /> <br /> I don't really see the point of trying to find Banes for spirits that have been created using the default rules. None of the Spirit examples have armor (Gagh Azur is an exception) so I assume most (if any) don't. Spirits just seem like goblins in a higher level DnD game, die with one roll and only a threat when there are dozens of them.<br /> <br /> It's a good thing my players haven't read the rules so I can keep house ruling it that they only take bashing, but since this whole thread should probably be about RAW it would be nice to have some confirmation for other ST's. <b>Would it be possible to get some kind of confirmation from a Werewolf developer?</b><br /> <br /> The Predator Jaws interpretation does make sense for the whole ultimate hunter thing, but it does devalue stuff like figuring out banes, unless all spirits are stacked with Armor and Regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-26-2018, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T21:48:55-08:00","id":1189528,"title":"","content":"First edition worked entirely different.<br /> <br /> You can look at the Sparkblood Seneschal for a 'regular' example of a Rank 4 spirit, with 18 Corpus and a variety of abilities that would make it more durable than 'an old lady walking her dog at night,' and its lair full of elementals and other minion servants would probably do a better job of assisting it than a dog might.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem may be you seem to be coming at the game from the wrong angle. For one thing, figuring out banes is not meant to be the hard part. Literally the first Gift an Ithaeur gets is going to help them figure out what a spirits ban is. Being able to use them, and doing so smartly is. For another, while in DnD you're meant to slaughter goblins, it's not the point of Werewolf any more than mowing down people in a mall with an M50 is for Vampire. It' something you can do, providing the spirits are low Ranked and there's some sort of motivation, or death rage is pushing you like frenzy might, or just regular anger and annoyance, but it's the kind of action that would draw consequences, and thus plot (I know some people don't like consequences, but it's good enough for the Newton, physics, and every story ever, it's good enough for a tabletop game).<br /> <br /> There is no Werewolf developer anymore, but the writers have posted about this before.<br /> <br /> You're free to have it not work against spirits, it will just make all spirit battles substantially more difficult, especially the ones with packs of low Rank spirits. Until Down &amp; Dirty gets used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2018, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T22:42:37-08:00","id":1189532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189528#post1189528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can look at the Sparkblood Seneschal for a 'regular' example of a Rank 4 spirit, with 18 Corpus and a variety of abilities that would make it more durable than 'an old lady walking her dog at night,' and its lair full of elementals and other minion servants would probably do a better job of assisting it than a dog might.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem may be you seem to be coming at the game from the wrong angle. For one thing, figuring out banes is not meant to be the hard part. Literally the first Gift an Ithaeur gets is going to help them figure out what a spirits ban is. Being able to use them, and doing so smartly is.<br /> <br /> There is no Werewolf developer anymore, but the writers have posted about this before.<br /> <br /> You're free to have it not work against spirits, it will just make all spirit battles substantially more difficult, especially the ones with packs of low Rank spirits. Until Down &amp; Dirty gets used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do admit that the way my group plays Werewolf is most likely very different than how it's &quot;supposed&quot; to be played, it's more combat focused and the horror tends to come from threats to the player characters themselves, since they are more the &quot;murder hobo&quot; stereotype, with having no one they care about other than each other. So for this kind of game, downgrading to lethal seems to work better.<br /> <br /> Since Spirits have Corpus of Resistance+Size and size can be anything, even a high ranking spirit might only have 10 Corpus. Average human has 7, which could translate to 14 if they always succeed in their Stamina roll to not go down. (Yeah I know no-one sticks around to fight that long, but in theory).<br /> Also, they might have guns and armor and those are pretty scary.<br /> <br /> I know that figuring out a Bane is not the hard part, the hard part is finding a reason to bother using it. Especially for Spirits of Rank 4 and 5 it often seems to be extremely hard to find it. If a Spirit has a Bane of &quot;The ashes of a human that burned in a volcanic eruption&quot; why would you bother? I feel that there should be a temptation to actually manufacture the Bane, to kill a person to get a Bane for a strong spirit.<br /> <br /> I had actual questions as well:<br /> EDIT<br /> <b>1. Magath Spirits are usually shunned by other Spirits so that a high ranking Magath might not have any Spirit allies, making them easy prey for werewolves?</b><br /> <br /> <b>2. Is there a limit to how much Essence a Spirit can use in one turn? I haven't seen it anywhere.<br /> <br /> 3. Siskur-Dah lets WW &quot;eat&quot; the remaining essence from a Spirit they defeat, but what if the Spirit has already used almost all of it on Regenerate to stay alive? (If there is no limit to Essence per turn, why not burn it all just to spite the werewolves.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-26-2018, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T23:12:51-08:00","id":1189535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189532#post1189532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Spirits have Corpus of Resistance+Size and size can be anything, even a high ranking spirit might only have 10 Corpus. Average human has 7, which could translate to 14 if they always succeed in their Stamina roll to not go down. (Yeah I know no-one sticks around to fight that long, but in theory).<br /> Also, they might have guns and armor and those are pretty scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't underestimate Blast, or simple combat attacks. Once you're dealing with Rank 3 or above spirits they're going to have a hefty dicepool. And a spirit's going to have substantially more Defense than puny humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that figuring out a Bane is not the hard part, the hard part is finding a reason to bother using it. Especially for Spirits of Rank 4 and 5 it often seems to be extremely hard to find it. If a Spirit has a Bane of &quot;The ashes of a human that burned in a volcanic eruption&quot; why would you bother? I feel that there should be a temptation to actually manufacture the Bane, to kill a person to get a Bane for a strong spirit. </div> </div> </div>Because they're difficult to truly kill without it, even if you are murderhobos. If you just damage a spirit with tooth, claw, and gun, it can have Essence at the end and discorporate, and reform elsewhere. Sacred Hunt is an option but it's not always there when you're fighting a spirit. Also banes can keep spirits from touching you (they require Willpower expenditure and a roll to succeed), banes can be used to remove Manifestations and 'exorcise' a spirit from an area or person,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Are Magath Spirits usually shunned by other Spirits' so that a high ranking Magath might not have any Spirit allies? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though they can have other magath as allies, like if a bunch of dog spirits ended up eating a bunch of computer spirits you could have a pack of cyberdogs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Is there a limit to how much Essence a Spirit can use in one turn? I haven't seen it anywhere? </div> </div> </div>No. Sometimes abilities will have limits, like Blast limits Essence use for it by 2xRank, or their being able to boost only one Attribute per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Siskur-Dah lets WW &quot;eat&quot; the remaining essence from a Spirit they defeat, but what if the Spirit has already used almost all of it on Regenerate to stay alive? </div> </div> </div>Then they don't get much Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T00:22:06-08:00","id":1189548,"title":"","content":"Do any of you have a house rule / rule-of-thumb for how much time has to go by for a werewolf to be able to take Gauru form again? It's once per scene, but of course a Scene can last from anywhere between 1 minute to 10 hours and also, what if the Scene changes 1 minute after they already took Gauru form?<br /> <br /> I had this come up in our game on Saturday where they fought a tough enemy and after it was defeated, the Rahu of the group dove in to the water alone and started swimming outside the cave they were in. The rest stayed behind to investigate and loot while he arrived on the Ocean shore outside. We felt that outside was a different scene, and immediately after arriving there he was under attack by 2 Claimed.<br /> <br /> Under 5 min had gone by and so I had him roll Stamina + Primal Urge to see if he was able to transform, but it was pretty much a given he would succeed. So he was able to transform again.<br /> <br /> I feel like it should perhaps be similar to the &quot;Short rest&quot; concept that is in DnD, so 45min-1h between voluntary Gauru, since Gauru form pretty much makes you invincible unless swarmed by enemies. Having it too often removes the should-I-risk-using-Gauru-now-or-save-it-for-later aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 02-26-2018, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T01:31:38-08:00","id":1189555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189526#post1189526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that is specifically said, without interpretation clouding it, is that WW deal lethal to vampires and spirits downgrade lethal to bashing</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing that is said (albeit in Vampire) is that vampires also downgrade to bashing since they also don't have any need for functional internal organs.<br /> <br /> The official rule of thumb for how long a scene is (when it isn't arbitrarily long) is an hour. Therefor it's easy to say that any powers that lasts for a scene instead lasts for an hour if you need consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T02:24:45-08:00","id":1189561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189555#post1189555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official rule of thumb for how long a scene is (when it isn't arbitrarily long) is an hour. Therefor it's easy to say that any powers that lasts for a scene instead lasts for an hour if you need consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is good to know, so my gut feeling that it should take close to an hours interval before you can go into Gauru voluntarily was not without merit.<br /> <br /> If you have used Gauru in a Scene already, you can't go into Gauru again no matter how much you want to, right? The exception would be going into Basu-Im, which you don't have conscious control over, you need a trigger for it to happen?<br /> <br /> What about the Wolf Gift Father's Form? Would you be unable to use it, or could you use it and instantly be forced into Kuruth if you attack or suffer Purity amount in Lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T04:02:24-08:00","id":1189570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1189532#post1189532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Siskur-Dah lets WW &quot;eat&quot; the remaining essence from a Spirit they defeat, but what if the Spirit has already used almost all of it on Regenerate to stay alive? (If there is no limit to Essence per turn, why not burn it all just to spite the werewolves.[/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if they die without any Essence in their pool they die for good, so even if they can assume that is going to happen anyway (and werewolves that do that without good reason suffer the consequences) their own survival instinct goes against that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-26-2018, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:34:15-08:00","id":1190283,"title":"","content":"1. Are there Claimed by wolf spirits?<br /> 2. How do the Forsaken do their job in regions where wolves are not endemic, as to blending in and ecology?<br /> 3. Which tribe hunts shapeshifters like Balam-Colop, Suthanu-Sua, Werefalcons, Brineborn and do they even bother with Skinthieves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:40:12-08:00","id":1190308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1190283#post1190283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are there Claimed by wolf spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. How do the Forsaken do their job in regions where wolves are not endemic, as to blending in and ecology? </div> </div> </div>Either use the Skin Thief Gift, which lets them turn into animals comparable in size, or don't rely overly on wolf form. Or just hunt as normal and let people believe you might be a wild dog or escapee from a zoo. Strictly speaking, using wolf-form is not something werewolves have to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Which tribe hunts shapeshifters like Balam-Colop, Suthanu-Sua, Werefalcons, Brineborn and do they even bother with Skinthieves? </div> </div> </div>Any of them can. Sacred Prey is just something they focus on, not something they can only hunt. Hunting a Skinthief is a matter of whether it's worth it, if one is causing trouble for you or your territory, go for it, if they're helpful and friendly, maybe avoid it. Blood Talons, Storm Lords, and Iron Masters are probably most likely. Maybe Hunters in Darkness if you thought they might be a host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:40:16-08:00","id":1193620,"title":"","content":"Can werewolves smell cancer? And what would a cancer spirt be like? Shudder!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:21:03-08:00","id":1193637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1193620#post1193620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can werewolves smell cancer? And what would a cancer spirt be like? Shudder!</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, though I imagine most wouldn't really recognize it for what it was. Silver, too, has a distinct smell that people who work a lot with silver notice but your average person doesn't get much exposure to pure silver. So a werewolf can likely scent out both, but unless they train themselves to they likely wouldn't stand out in terms of all the smells that surround people.<br /> <br /> It might look like a forboding dark spot that seeps through its surroundings like an infection. Or something that seems alive but grows strange gaping holes and pseudopods at random full of teeth and eyes and hairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2018, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:38:03-08:00","id":1193646,"title":"","content":"Cancer spirits are kind of an interesting thought, because the typical MO of a spirit is actually pretty similar to that of a malignant tumor - propagate yourself, even if you end up killing your only food source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:56:26-08:00","id":1193660,"title":"","content":"What would a spirt of Hematophagy be like in specifics vampire bats spirt my head cannon is that they\u2019re suprisengly \u2018nice\u2019 and would work well as a totem spirt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:34:58-08:00","id":1193674,"title":"","con