n what many elders of the tribe would view as a particularly intricate lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T17:47:36-08:00","id":1194100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194098#post1194098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, more like Fire-Touched packs encouraging and inciting otakus to fight over things like that. I doubt a follower of Rabid Wolf would be so deeply immersed in what many elders of the tribe would view as a particularly intricate lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that\u2019s hilarious it\u2019s still Hilarious to imagine fire touched starting waifu wars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T20:29:10-08:00","id":1194126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194093#post1194093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can spirits steal Essence from Uratha the same way as from each other? If not then how do you go about paying any of your own Essence as gathra?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can apparently be traded, but there's some wolf gifts that let you offer essence. Essence from gathra isn't always 'raw' essence as much as it is an activity or material that offers Essence. But there's still things like talens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Essence collected in a receptacle consumable by any spirit or only those matching the resonance it originally came from? </div> </div> </div>A spirit can take any Essence but they generally only eat corresponding Essence. Keep in mind that it doesn't have to be 'their' Essence as much as it could be something appropriate for them. A fire spirit can eat wood spirits, for instance, representing fire's consumption of wood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T22:10:38-08:00","id":1194137,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit to how much Essence can be extracted from a given source (either in total or per unit time)? How many fire spirits could theoretically share the same bonfire, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T22:25:45-08:00","id":1194138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194137#post1194137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit to how much Essence can be extracted from a given source (either in total or per unit time)? How many fire spirits could theoretically share the same bonfire, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on the source. Loci have limits, it's in the locus section, though they get pretty big. You seem to be able to take as much as possible when you feed, but you can only hold as much as your Max Essence.<br /> <br /> There isn't a set Essence or spirit calculator (though as noted, loci are pretty thoroughly explained), anywhere between 1 and 'a reasonable amount depending on the bonfire.' Which probably wouldn't get too high, though bonfires can be pretty massive, and if it was something like at burning man or about to spread like a wildfire it could get a lot more than that. Providing some party or something and not a repetitive ritual or magic involvement you would be fine with having 1-12, though when you have more it's going to have more extras to deal with, while if you have 1, it might point at them being a 'special' spirit that might linger from a narrative point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-11-2018, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:24:51-07:00","id":1194583,"title":"","content":"What are the mechanics of joining a Lodge in 2nd Edition? Do you need to be at a certain level of Primal Urge or Renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:31:45-07:00","id":1194587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194583#post1194583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the mechanics of joining a Lodge in 2nd Edition? Do you need to be at a certain level of Primal Urge or Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, though some lodges might have individual preferences they probably wouldn't be prohibitive. You just get recruited, either there's a grueling initiation you join or a sort of apprenticeship or both.<br /> <br /> It's all in <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/181760/The-Pack\" target=\"_blank\">the Pack</a>, starting on p79. Five sample lodges and a bunch of referenced ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T15:54:27-07:00","id":1194656,"title":"","content":"What would the hisil of a avegange middle school be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T16:01:19-07:00","id":1194658,"title":"","content":"These things depend on the circumstances. But a confined area full of raging emotion spirits and some base knowledge and discipline ones. Bentley Little's book the Academy had a good depiction of it, with what was effectively a spirit of discipline being harnessed and empowered to take control of the school and everything going downhill in a supernaturally fascistic way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T17:47:44-07:00","id":1194679,"title":"","content":"Like a normal middle class run what types of spirt would thrive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T20:29:39-07:00","id":1194716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194679#post1194679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like a normal middle class run what types of spirt would thrive</div> </div> </div> </div>What's normal? Nothing has happened there? Or an average amount of things have happened there?<br /> <br /> You have the obvious physical spirits, houses, roads, trees, cars, and so forth then more conceptual things, community, monotony, banality, and so on. Then down to the individuals, you have your usual emotion spirits but likely confined to indoors.<br /> <br /> There's one of these in <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/64270/Night-Horrors-Wolfsbane\" target=\"_blank\">Wolfsbane</a>, but the entire town has been claimed by itself.<br /> <br /> Since you're interested you might want to look at the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/3771/Territories\" target=\"_blank\">Territories</a> book, which gets into what werewolf territories might be like and what spirits might live in them. Or <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a>, which gets into different kinds of spirits there are. <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/27863/World-of-Darkness-Book-of-Spirits\" target=\"_blank\">The Book of Spirits</a> does that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-12-2018, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:58:34-07:00","id":1194837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194658#post1194658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These things depend on the circumstances. But a confined area full of raging emotion spirits and some base knowledge and discipline ones. Bentley Little's book the Academy had a good depiction of it, with what was effectively a spirit of discipline being harnessed and empowered to take control of the school and everything going downhill in a supernaturally fascistic way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hisil of a American Indian residential school while it was in use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-13-2018, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:21:54-07:00","id":1194879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194837#post1194837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hisil of a American Indian residential school while it was in use</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you come up with things that have defined the school over the years. From student customs, be it a nasty and generalized displays of bullying or general care for students with disabilities, to achievements, to tragedies that may have marked it and stuff it's shadow with representation of those.<br /> <br /> Think about it in this way: if ghosts are ephemeral representation of long gone people, the shadow and it's inhabitants are ephemeral representations of events and phenomenons, their causes and consequences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:54:52-07:00","id":1194891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194879#post1194879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest you come up with things that have defined the school over the years. From student customs, be it a nasty and generalized displays of bullying or general care for students with disabilities, to achievements, to tragedies that may have marked it and stuff it's shadow with representation of those.<br /> <br /> Think about it in this way: if ghosts are ephemeral representation of long gone people, the shadow and it's inhabitants are ephemeral representations of events and phenomenons, their causes and consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought it would be best to leave details vague so other people can fill in the blanks and it\u2019s an American Indian residential school just be that description you should know it wasn\u2019t a good place of learning but when children where stolen from the parents and taught to hate themselves and there culture and family in does schools there was high rate of sucide physcal,mental,social,sexual,and emotional abuse and wasn\u2019t a very happy place I\u2019m thinking of one where there where wendigo reports","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:04:59-07:00","id":1194921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1194891#post1194891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I thought it would be best to leave details vague so other people can fill in the blanks and it\u2019s an American Indian residential school just be that description you should know it wasn\u2019t a good place of learning but when children where stolen from the parents and taught to hate themselves and there culture and family in does schools there was high rate of sucide physcal,mental,social,sexual,and emotional abuse and wasn\u2019t a very happy place I\u2019m thinking of one where there where wendigo reports</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, with several atrocities as such, there's a number of Maeljin that would patronize such a place becoming ripe with Wounded essence. The important thing to determine which one does, is to figure out what is the ultimate purpose for said atrocities committed.<br /> <br /> Is it due to the inherent violence of the system? Therifuge would fit. Is the abuse aimed at denying the sexual identity of students so that they conform with the practices and taboos of mainstream society? Carnala would love that show. Or is it merely using heavy handed methods of discipline because damnit, these don't know any better? Pseulak would cackle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts