stion-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1198137#post1198137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Huntsman's Compass, it points towards the nearest ephemeral entity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okey, but if a need it to find a <i>specific</i> ephemeral entity. The named spirit of blood and murder that happens to be loose in the city for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T16:50:41-07:00","id":1198166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1198151#post1198151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okey, but if a need it to find a <i>specific</i> ephemeral entity. The named spirit of blood and murder that happens to be loose in the city for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fetish to look for a specific individual spirit would suggest a very powerful spirit, or very unique fetish.<br /> <br /> Tracking a spirit of blood and murder is something you could do with just werewolf abilities, especially if it's in the physical world. Something like the Huntsman's Compass would help, but generally you would just call a sacred hunt and hunt it. If it's doing anything in the city it shouldn't be too hard to find. It's what a lot of Skills and Merits exist for.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to cut the player side out of it just have the Huntsman's Compass be 'Johann's Compass' where Johann was another werewolf who hunted the spirit and it only points in the direction of that spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-21-2018, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:21:10-07:00","id":1198171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1198166#post1198166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fetish to look for a specific individual spirit would suggest a very powerful spirit, or very unique fetish.<br /> <br /> Tracking a spirit of blood and murder is something you could do with just werewolf abilities, especially if it's in the physical world. Something like the Huntsman's Compass would help, but generally you would just call a sacred hunt and hunt it. If it's doing anything in the city it shouldn't be too hard to find. It's what a lot of Skills and Merits exist for.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to cut the player side out of it just have the Huntsman's Compass be 'Johann's Compass' where Johann was another werewolf who hunted the spirit and it only points in the direction of that spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that thing about an old werewolf compass that (s)he used to hunt the spirit seems pretty fine actually. <br /> The reason i was asking was that the PCs are mortals, not wolf-blooded either but with some supernatural merits. Sleepwalkers by mage standards. They have convinced a neighboring werewolf pack to help them find this spirit, that's outside the werewolves territory in exchange for digging into the reasons why the local mages hunted down the ancestors of the werewolves and sealed of the gauntlet around the city. I thought that the werewolves in question would be able to lend them a Talen or minor Fetish to help them find the spirit. <br /> <br /> Now that I'm thinking about it, maybe a minor fetish that lets a mortal use wolf senses or something like it. Perhaps it need some sort of connection towards a specific being to activate. <br /> Like putting in some Spoor into the fetish, and being able to use wolf senses to hunt after that particular spirit. What would you say a reasonable fetish level would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T18:00:24-07:00","id":1198188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1198171#post1198171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like putting in some Spoor into the fetish, and being able to use wolf senses to hunt after that particular spirit. What would you say a reasonable fetish level would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've no idea, really high, I guess it would depend on the limitations. It may seem like a simple item, but 'put some evidence in and it points you in that direction' is pretty powerful, especially for folks who deal with spirits. If you could use it for mortals, for instance, you could find anyone who commit any crime and left any amount of evidence. Plus there's the whole humans not being able to use fetishes thing. If you're just using it for this event you don't really need a dot rating for it, though.<br /> <br /> Have you thought about fettering them with a spirit? Werewolves could arrange for a spirit to assist the mortals in their investigation. It could use something like the Sign Numen to send directions or messages, or just Materialize and speak to them. You could have it be the same spirit from the 'Johann's Fetish,' Johann's ancestor spirit, or even a ghost, attempting to hunt down the spirit. Or a bloodhound spirit, if you wanted to be a little on the nose and have a weird blood-sniffling dog occasionally appear.<br /> <br /> If you want to be more creepy it could be fettered to one of the characters and occasionally possess them to lead the PCs on their hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","us