"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T00:33:19-07:00","id":1200363,"title":"","content":"Yes, but higher PU means it's less likely it'll affect them. Think Captain America &quot;So, I can't get drunk&quot; think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:12:26-07:00","id":1200366,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure where I had read it (or if I had read it), but I have a recollection that each level of Primal Urge would lessen Toxicity levels by 1. Beer and wine are considered level 3 and &quot;rubbing alcohol&quot; (which I assume stands for pure 100% alcohol) is level 5.<br /> <br /> So Primal Urge 5 werewolf could drink pure alcohol without ever getting drunk.<br /> <br /> If anyone remembers if there was a rule about this, please let us know.<br /> <br /> In my game, my players still wanted a way to get drunk so I had the idea that mixing worse poisons with the alcohol would prevent the werewolf body from clearing the alcohol before it deals with the worse poison. That way you could at least for a little while still get the &quot;benefits&quot; of alcohol even as a higher PU werewolf. They were sitting at a table with Blood Talons that were putting stuff like wolfsbane or snake venom into their own drinks.<br /> <br /> I think most snake venom is not actually that dangerous to drink, but I liked the visual of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 03-28-2018, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:23:11-07:00","id":1200370,"title":"","content":"Yeah, from p94. 'Subtract the Uratha\u2019s Primal Urge from the Toxicity rating of any poison or disease that would ail her.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T02:20:18-07:00","id":1200378,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13318\" data-vbnamecard=\"13318\">Cainite</a> A piece of unsolicited trivia. &quot;Rubbing alcohol&quot; can refer to either isopropyl alcohol, which is not fit for human consumption, or ethanol with toxic compounds purposefully mixed in. I assume pure ethanol would have a toxicity of 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, when it comes to disinfection, the optimum concentration of ethanol is about 70%, not more. Higher concentrations cause pathogen proteins to denature so hard they create a barrier against further penetration of the disinfectant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:58:51-07:00","id":1200828,"title":"","content":"Looking up rules for reaching and i was wondering can you take other people and objects with you or is it just the werewolf itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23853-vorkareth","name":"Vorkareth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:04:19-07:00","id":1200848,"title":"","content":"can a werewolf reach with another person i.e. wolfblooded and objects i.e. Bow, firearms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23853-vorkareth","name":"Vorkareth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:25:39-07:00","id":1200858,"title":"","content":"If they're wearing the object, yes. Dunno about the person. Some wolfbloods get tells that allow them to reach, but there aren't rules to Reach as a pack like in say, Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Da