past, living somewhere where there are no natural wolves, who might have never even heard of wolves, contextualize the First Change? Or were werewolves initially only found in places where wolves live and then they migrated with humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T06:27:04-07:00","id":1215015,"title":"","content":"The presence of werewolves in an area is in no way related to the presence of real wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:48:20-07:00","id":1215080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1215009#post1215009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this has been asked before, but do werewolves all have to be pure wolf in features? I mean, how does someone in the distant past, living somewhere where there are no natural wolves, who might have never even heard of wolves, contextualize the First Change? Or were werewolves initially only found in places where wolves live and then they migrated with humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah like Acrozatarim says, the presence of real wolves doesn't matter. If the person have no context for what a wolf is they'll probably be surprised, but odds are they're going to bump into another werewolf or spirit at some point that can inform them, or take advantage of the situation.<br /> <br /> From there they could always learn the Skin Thief Gift to permanently change their wolf form into another animal appropriate for the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:56:25-07:00","id":1215118,"title":"","content":"Besides the brief reference in <i>The Pack</i>, is the Lodge of Dream Eaters mentioned in any other book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:28:07-07:00","id":1215170,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of.<br /> <br /> However, there's a creature in Signs of the Moon called Maskiku, or the Omen Grinder that exists as an ancient, imprisoned enemy of the Uratha that has escaped. It feasts on dreams, but it particularly likes the madness-fueled dreams of the Uratha, like those Luna gifts the Cahalith. One of the ways to deal with it would be to make an agreement with it, which could lead to a lodge that devours the dreams of others to keep it from feeding on Luna-sent prophecies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T04:11:59-07:00","id":1215728,"title":"","content":"What would elphant spirts be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T04:49:51-07:00","id":1215737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1215728#post1215728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would elphant spirts be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Memorious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:07:02-07:00","id":1215751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1215737#post1215737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Memorious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other traits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T11:21:06-07:00","id":1215862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1215728#post1215728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would elphant spirts be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Communal. Headstrong. Passive, preferring to simple live and let live, but very dangerous when roused to action by anger or fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:31:06-07:00","id":1217023,"title":"","content":"All right, I tried doing the search thing through the core book and this forum, and I can't find the answer to this question:<br /> <br /> What happens to Uratha when they die? Do they shift to hishu? Hopefully this has an answer in 2E and if so I'd like a page number.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:04:31-07:00","id":1217109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1217023#post1217023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, I tried doing the search thing through the core book and this forum, and I can't find the answer to this question:<br /> <br /> What happens to Uratha when they die? Do they shift to hishu? Hopefully this has an answer in 2E and if so I'd like a page number.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>1e addressed this in the Myths and Facts section of its intro chapter \u2014 dead werewolves and bits separated from a werewolf revert to their human shapes.<br /> <br /> 2e, meanwhile, specifies that every form a werewolf has is completely &quot;natural,&quot; that Gauru form can only be maintained for so long before Death Rage becomes a concern, and that after Death Rage a werewolf collapses into Hishu. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:33:04-07:00","id":1217369,"title":"","content":"It would seem, then, that Hishu is a &quot;lowest energy state&quot; for beings that (in core 2e game line, anyway) originate solely from human stock. <br /> <br /> Question:<br /> <br /> 1. Is healing in forms other than Garou reflexive if the wound causes unconsciousness? If so, would the werewolf regain consciousness immediately and &quot;pop&quot; back into the fight? This question essentially amounts to &quot;is the health track as listed or is it actually health+healing in current form?&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Moon's Grace Merit from The Pack. If a pack without Uratha takes it, and they later add an Uratha to it, can we assume the grace is withdrawn? Obviously sanctity of Merits should apply, but what happens to any Renown, Rites or Gifts learned in the meantime by the pack's wolf-blooded and human members? Similarly, if the pack fails (which is more likely in a group without Uratha), what happens to anything learned under the auspice of Moon's Grace?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:41:05-07:00","id":1217374,"title":"","content":"On a similar tack to Khanwulf's #1, does the healing occur at the start or end of the werewolf's turn? It matters for wound penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T10:54:59-07:00","id":1217444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1217369#post1217369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is healing in forms other than Garou reflexive if the wound causes unconsciousness? If so, would the werewolf regain consciousness immediately and &quot;pop&quot; back into the fight? This question essentially amounts to &quot;is the health track as listed or is it actually health+healing in current form?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bashing is natural, happens anyways, so yes, you can potentially wake up. You need to be conscious to spend Essence, to up that to Lethal healing, though, as talked about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Moon's Grace Merit from The Pack. If a pack without Uratha takes it, and they later add an Uratha to it, can we assume the grace is withdrawn? Obviously sanctity of Merits should apply, but what happens to any Renown, Rites or Gifts learned in the meantime by the pack's wolf-blooded and human members? Similarly, if the pack fails (which is more likely in a group without Uratha), what happens to anything learned under the auspice of Moon's Grace? </div> </div> </div>I think the purpose of the Merit is to make mortal games mortal+ games, so it doesn't seem like the kind of thing that should occur. Everything can boil down to sanctity of Merits but you might let them keep some bonuses, unless you're changing the entire thrust of the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13628_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13628\" data-vbnamecard=\"13628\">Terrorforge</a> They heal at the start of the turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T11:54:44-07:00","id":1217466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1217444#post1217444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bashing is natural, happens anyways, so yes, you can potentially wake up. You need to be conscious to spend Essence, to up that to Lethal healing, though, as talked about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I think the purpose of the Merit is to make mortal games mortal+ games, so it doesn't seem like the kind of thing that should occur. Everything can boil down to sanctity of Merits but you might let them keep some bonuses, unless you're changing the entire thrust of the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13628_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13628\" data-vbnamecard=\"13628\">Terrorforge</a> They heal at the start of the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the link, Nofather. <br /> <br /> If your gaggle of wolf-blooded and humans forms an honest-to-Luna pack, and receives Moon's Grace, then you are definitely playing mortal+. Thing is, mortal or mortal+ is an awkward place to balance things if your group rubs shoulders with full-splats--you tend to slip one way or another and end up dead, or full splat. That's a delicious part of the natural tension, or horror, of the situation.<br /> <br /> So in the case of werewolf, said pack might well take in a fresh change and suddenly become mortal+Uratha. Or, most of the pack dies, because reasons. Or, some of the pack goes through the Change, because Luna. So I guess we're in ST-arbitration territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T18:23:38-07:00","id":1217549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1217444#post1217444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bashing is natural, happens anyways, so yes, you can potentially wake up. You need to be conscious to spend Essence, to up that to Lethal healing, though, as talked about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd\">here</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile I'd argue that death rage isn't a state of consciousness (hence why it's called so) and it can use several reflexive facets. Biologically speaking only, an organism doesn't need a conscious response to preserve itself, it would be a huge evolutionary disadvantage. And the interpretation relies in a reading that disagrees with the formal definition of 'reflexive action'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T06:53:43-07:00","id":1218512,"title":"","content":"In the case of Wolf-Blooded with the Moon-Marked Tell for the full or new moon, what is the character's effective Renown for the purposes of those Hunter's Aspects' Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:23:02-07:00","id":1218552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1218512#post1218512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Wolf-Blooded with the Moon-Marked Tell for the full or new moon, what is the character's effective Renown for the purposes of those Hunter's Aspects' Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd swing between 0 or 1 when mechanics calls for traits the character lacks, but this time it actually has the same effect for both Conditions. If you don't get at least 1 success when rolling for Swaggering you've failed the roll regardless of target number, and Unaware has a minimum penalty of -1 that only increases by having Cunning 3+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-14-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:36:23-07:00","id":1218557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1218512#post1218512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Wolf-Blooded with the Moon-Marked Tell for the full or new moon, what is the character's effective Renown for the purposes of those Hunter's Aspects' Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I default the penalty and number of success needed to shake Swaggering off to 2, with both of them, mind that doesn't actually gives them a renown trait (barring the specific pack merit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:13:01-07:00","id":1218620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1218557#post1218557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I default the penalty and number of success needed to shake Swaggering off to 2, with both of them, mind that doesn't actually gives them a renown trait (barring the specific pack merit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why -2 and target number 2? If a Tell uses an otherwise werewolf exclusive mechanic, wouldn't it make more sense if the Wolf-Blooded gets the minimum a werewolf could get? (Except in cases where the mechanic is dependent on a trait that both WBs and werewolves share, which still gives them equal opportunity to increase that trait.) And why would different Auspice marks gain the effects of different Renown ratings? Target number 2 on Swaggering would be the result of Purity 2 while -2 on Unaware would be the result of Cunning 3 if werewolves were to apply those hunter's aspect Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:00:21-07:00","id":1218636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1218620#post1218620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why -2 and target number 2? If a Tell uses an otherwise werewolf exclusive mechanic, wouldn't it make more sense if the Wolf-Blooded gets the minimum a werewolf could get? (Except in cases where the mechanic is dependent on a trait that both WBs and werewolves share, which still gives them equal opportunity to increase that trait.) And why would different Auspice marks gain the effects of different Renown ratings? Target number 2 on Swaggering would be the result of Purity 2 while -2 on Unaware would be the result of Cunning 3 if werewolves were to apply those hunter's aspect Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because 2 is an average number, and 1 is too little for a tell, IMO. Not my fault they decided to add weird arithmetics to Renown with condition, nevermind that's the default penalty for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T19:46:49-07:00","id":1219158,"title":"","content":"How would the moon taint condition interact with another supernatural, like a Vampire for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T20:01:35-07:00","id":1219161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1219158#post1219158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the moon taint condition interact with another supernatural, like a Vampire for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably keep it the same. It's not as if it's a mundane poison, it's flesh-warping. But if someone was really squirmy over it I don't see any problem lowering the damage to Bashing or something.<br /> <br /> Though currently the only RAW way to get it is through Maw of Madness, which specifically requires a living target. You could easily have a lune-fetish tooth or something that allows one to strike the undead with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:31:48-07:00","id":1220813,"title":"","content":"Is there Word of God on whether or not the &quot;either&quot; in the rules for Totem is exclusive or inclusive.<br /> <br /> I see a lot of people read the rule the same way I do, that you can buy a dot of the merit to represent either a level of connection to your personal totem or your pack totem. But the wording is ambiguous. Have any of the authors commented on which it is meant to say or whether the ambiguity is intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13114-cuannan","name":"CuAnnan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:13:34-07:00","id":1220880,"title":"","content":"Idigam / Influence related questions:<br /> <br /> Last play session ended mid-combat. The players and their allies are facing the Idigam Gagh-Azur for the first time. Situation is dire.<br /> Gagh-Azur has Influence 5 in Hunger. It uses that full Influence on a group of PC's in a combat situation. What happens?<br /> <br /> Initially I was thinking that I would have 5 players/characters that have their Essence down to 4 or less (which is 4/5 of them) make a resistance roll and if they have less successes than the Idigam did (pretty likely, since Resolve+PU vs 24 activation), they would be forced to take a bite out of the closest person to them and eat their flesh for Essence, causing Aggravated damage. And continue to try to eat them until they have at least half their pool of Essence (that would be 6).<br /> <br /> At this point the PC's are trying to run away and survive another day, but several of them are currently under the effects of Awe for 2 more turns (can't move or speak).The Idigam is also going to open a Shadow Gateway to send a host of spirits at the players and their allies.<br /> <br /> Is this at all reasonable? Am I being way too forgiving or is this not enough for Influence 5? The rules for Influence are so vague, I have no clue on how much they should remove player Agency. At this point the situation is pretty dire and I have a feeling that a delay of a turn or two is going to cost at least some of the player characters their lives. If they get left behind, they will be swarmed by a number of spirits and/or be devoured by the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Now, if it was the Players using Influence 5 Hunger, I would probably have the targets go berserk and eat each other, but mind controlling powers against PC's cause me to hesitate. I don't want to cause a situation where several of them die without being able to save themselves and not have &quot;the rules&quot; supporting their deaths.<br /> <br /> Any advice would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 05-21-2018, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:15:06-07:00","id":1220914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1220880#post1220880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam / Influence related questions:<br /> <br /> Last play session ended mid-combat. The players and their allies are facing the Idigam Gagh-Azur for the first time. Situation is dire.<br /> Gagh-Azur has Influence 5 in Hunger. It uses that full Influence on a group of PC's in a combat situation. What happens?<br /> <br /> Initially I was thinking that I would have 5 players/characters that have their Essence down to 4 or less (which is 4/5 of them) make a resistance roll and if they have less successes than the Idigam did (pretty likely, since Resolve+PU vs 24 activation), they would be forced to take a bite out of the closest person to them and eat their flesh for Essence, causing Aggravated damage. And continue to try to eat them until they have at least half their pool of Essence (that would be 6).<br /> <br /> At this point the PC's are trying to run away and survive another day, but several of them are currently under the effects of Awe for 2 more turns (can't move or speak).The Idigam is also going to open a Shadow Gateway to send a host of spirits at the players and their allies.<br /> <br /> Is this at all reasonable? Am I being way too forgiving or is this not enough for Influence 5? The rules for Influence are so vague, I have no clue on how much they should remove player Agency. At this point the situation is pretty dire and I have a feeling that a delay of a turn or two is going to cost at least some of the player characters their lives. If they get left behind, they will be swarmed by a number of spirits and/or be devoured by the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Now, if it was the Players using Influence 5 Hunger, I would probably have the targets go berserk and eat each other, but mind controlling powers against PC's cause me to hesitate. I don't want to cause a situation where several of them die without being able to save themselves and not have &quot;the rules&quot; supporting their deaths.<br /> <br /> Any advice would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as it is an Idigam, an easy solution would be <u>Mass Create</u> of Hunger Spirits to tie up the characters. Otherwise, I'd restrict that kind of &quot;Ravenous Curse&quot; (see Persistent Condition) to a single target (<u>Permanent Create</u> for the Influence). You could do a mass stoking of the PCs' hunger via <u>Manipulate</u> or <u>Control</u>, but if they escape (and it sounds like you want them to), long term consequences seem to have a better payoff (such as Hunger Spirits Fettering or Possessing people, or a long-term curse to saddle a character with).<br /> <br /> EDIT: For the mechanics of the Condition, maybe it gives them additional <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers#post433833\">Kuruth Triggers</a> (with the behavior during Death Rage being what you have in mind above).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-21-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:22:01-07:00","id":1220920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1220880#post1220880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this at all reasonable? Am I being way too forgiving or is this not enough for Influence 5? The rules for Influence are so vague, I have no clue on how much they should remove player Agency. At this point the situation is pretty dire and I have a feeling that a delay of a turn or two is going to cost at least some of the player characters their lives. If they get left behind, they will be swarmed by a number of spirits and/or be devoured by the Idigam.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, and fits for an empowered version of the Control Influence, or just creating a powerful hunger in the werewolves present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, if it was the Players using Influence 5 Hunger, I would probably have the targets go berserk and eat each other, but mind controlling powers against PC's cause me to hesitate. I don't want to cause a situation where several of them die without being able to save themselves and not have &quot;the rules&quot; supporting their deaths. </div> </div> </div>Depending on the target you would have more successful contests so that seems fair, I can appreciate not wanting to mind control the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-21-2018, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:40:43-07:00","id":1220953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1220880#post1220880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam / Influence related questions:<br /> <br /> Last play session ended mid-combat. The players and their allies are facing the Idigam Gagh-Azur for the first time. Situation is dire.<br /> Gagh-Azur has Influence 5 in Hunger. It uses that full Influence on a group of PC's in a combat situation. What happens?<br /> <br /> Initially I was thinking that I would have 5 players/characters that have their Essence down to 4 or less (which is 4/5 of them) make a resistance roll and if they have less successes than the Idigam did (pretty likely, since Resolve+PU vs 24 activation), they would be forced to take a bite out of the closest person to them and eat their flesh for Essence, causing Aggravated damage. And continue to try to eat them until they have at least half their pool of Essence (that would be 6).<br /> <br /> At this point the PC's are trying to run away and survive another day, but several of them are currently under the effects of Awe for 2 more turns (can't move or speak).The Idigam is also going to open a Shadow Gateway to send a host of spirits at the players and their allies.<br /> <br /> Is this at all reasonable? Am I being way too forgiving or is this not enough for Influence 5? The rules for Influence are so vague, I have no clue on how much they should remove player Agency. At this point the situation is pretty dire and I have a feeling that a delay of a turn or two is going to cost at least some of the player characters their lives. If they get left behind, they will be swarmed by a number of spirits and/or be devoured by the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Now, if it was the Players using Influence 5 Hunger, I would probably have the targets go berserk and eat each other, but mind controlling powers against PC's cause me to hesitate. I don't want to cause a situation where several of them die without being able to save themselves and not have &quot;the rules&quot; supporting their deaths.<br /> <br /> Any advice would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all plausible, and part of the horror from Werewolf comes from the lose of control even such massive amounts of influence can cause. A good compromise would be to illicit soft rage rather than straight hard one, and have them try to bail under such condition. Sounds like they're wholly unprepared to deal with the Idigam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:55:43-07:00","id":1221010,"title":"","content":"I keep seeing references to &quot;Skill Proficiencies&quot; with regard to Mr. Gone's Forsaken sheet, but I can't for the life of me find them in <b>ANY</b> of the books.<br /> <br /> What the frak are these things and where are the rules for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5766-nouveaurich","name":"NouveauRich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5766_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:45:36-07:00","id":1221080,"title":"","content":"I presume is the skill an auspice can get upgraded by +1, but that's just conjecture on my part. Can you show me exactly where they're mentioned? I haven't come across them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T02:48:19-07:00","id":1221110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221080#post1221080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume is the skill an auspice can get upgraded by +1, but that's just conjecture on my part. Can you show me exactly where they're mentioned? I haven't come across them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bottom right of page 3 of this: <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/WtF/WtF_2ndED_Unofficial_4-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/p...nteractive.pdf</a><br /> <br /> I've also wondered what they are, I just assumed they are space for you to write some specialities that you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T03:51:14-07:00","id":1221116,"title":"","content":"It's right next to the Auspice Ability so it might refer to Auspice Skills? The words &quot;proficiency&quot; and &quot;proficiencies&quot; doesn't even exist in the core rule book. The official character sheet has an extra box for recording XP in that space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:18:38-07:00","id":1221128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221116#post1221116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's right next to the Auspice Ability so it might refer to Auspice Skills? The words &quot;proficiency&quot; and &quot;proficiencies&quot; doesn't even exist in the core rule book. The official character sheet has an extra box for recording XP in that space.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do Auspice skills matter other than you get to add +1 to one of them at character creation? Am I missing something, do WW get some other affinities/bonuses when using their auspice skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:29:40-07:00","id":1221131,"title":"","content":"The Moon-Kissed Merit modifies rolls with a chosen Auspice Skill. Other Merits, Rituals, or maybe Gifts (in future supplements or home brew) could also have extra effects based on Auspice Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:42:46-07:00","id":1221143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221128#post1221128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But do Auspice skills matter other than you get to add +1 to one of them at character creation? Am I missing something, do WW get some other affinities/bonuses when using their auspice skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I use that to note specialties if I happen to put too many in a single skill. Brawl specs come easily for my Rahus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T08:27:10-07:00","id":1221159,"title":"","content":"You could just ask Mr. Gone.<br /> <br /> He has his own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets\">stickied thread here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:34:23-07:00","id":1221323,"title":"","content":"Can firstborn have children with human women?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:19:11-07:00","id":1221387,"title":"","content":"Firstborn can't manifest in the material plane without some cataclysm happening because of that. Nor can a human vessel contain their essence. Nor would they be interested in mating with simpleton, fleshy beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T05:43:42-07:00","id":1221460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221387#post1221387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstborn can't manifest in the material plane without some cataclysm happening because of that. Nor can a human vessel contain their essence. Nor would they be interested in mating with simpleton, fleshy beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Royal Avatars of them, on the other paw <i>can</i>, though this still leaves &quot;why&quot;. (Though in Red Wolf's case &quot;to see what would happen&quot; might be valid)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:45:58-07:00","id":1221488,"title":"","content":"Either way, there doesn't seem to be any hard mechanics on spirit-human reproduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T09:53:04-07:00","id":1221490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221460#post1221460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Royal Avatars of them, on the other paw <i>can</i>, though this still leaves &quot;why&quot;. (Though in Red Wolf's case &quot;to see what would happen&quot; might be valid)</div> </div> </div> </div>If some part of Red Wolf actively considered breaking Urfarah's edict, it damned well try to appease the Pure Firstborns for membership with it's tail between it's legs on my setting, if for some disturbing moment I considered the possibility of spiritual bestiality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:05:35-07:00","id":1221493,"title":"","content":"Can werewolves have a hostile Spirit Fettered to them and become/be Urged without them really knowing that it's happening? I know they see/sense Spirits in Twilight, but can the Fettered Spirit hide inside them and influence their actions in some subtle ways that they might not know they are Urged? I had an idea that the Fettering might have happened in a time when they were not fully aware/can't remember such as Kuruth.<br /> <br /> If they can be, how do they get rid of that Fettering? Utilizing its Bane is one thing, right? The rite &quot;Expel&quot; would not be useful, it only works on humans or objects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:24:35-07:00","id":1221496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221493#post1221493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can werewolves have a hostile Spirit Fettered to them and become/be Urged without them really knowing that it's happening? I know they see/sense Spirits in Twilight, but can the Fettered Spirit hide inside them and influence their actions in some subtle ways that they might not know they are Urged? I had an idea that the Fettering might have happened in a time when they were not fully aware/can't remember such as Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. As you note, it's harder, because the spirit can be seen hanging around in Twilight. It could hide, though, and while it may be difficult this is the kind of thing that happens to lone wolves, and it's why it happens, because they don't have other wolves able to help with this stuff. It can happen with a pack wolf, too, but obviously it involves more sneakery from the spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they can be, how do they get rid of that Fettering? Utilizing its Bane is one thing, right? The rite &quot;Expel&quot; would not be useful, it only works on humans or objects? </div> </div> </div>At that point you're dealing with a spirit in Twilight (we've had a couple of threads on how to deal with these). So a Bone Shadow's sacred hunt allows you to affect them, a bane or ban, Barghest if it's a death-related spirit, rituals like Twilight Purge or simply Banish. I think you could use Expel, it's just not normally used on werewolves (RAW says just humans and objects, yes). A totem spirit can help a lot, being able to exist in the same spectrum as the Fettering spirit. If the werewolf was particularly sneaky about it in turn, they could imprison it with Shadowbind or the Fetish rite. The options depend on whether you want to just get rid of the Fettering, or get rid of the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T13:08:34-07:00","id":1221530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221490#post1221490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If some part of Red Wolf actively considered breaking Urfarah's edict, it damned well try to appease the Pure Firstborns for membership with it's tail between it's legs on my setting, if for some disturbing moment I considered the possibility of spiritual bestiality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did father wolf say the firstborn can\u2019t have children with humans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T14:06:30-07:00","id":1221539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221530#post1221530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did father wolf say the firstborn can\u2019t have children with humans</div> </div> </div> </div>Urfarah's whole sort of deal was that the various denizens of Flesh, the Shadow, and the Border Marches stay in their respective lanes and that deviation from this model warranted correction.<br /> <br /> It is <i>also</i> known that the Firstborn are given free passage throughout the worlds to indulge themselves and that this is a sticking point with basically every other major supernatural mover and shaker of the era, so the above doesn't really make much difference without the supposition that the death of the Wolf is something his children have uniform feelings on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T14:18:25-07:00","id":1221543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221490#post1221490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If some part of Red Wolf actively considered breaking Urfarah's edict, it damned well try to appease the Pure Firstborns for membership with it's tail between it's legs on my setting, if for some disturbing moment I considered the possibility of spiritual bestiality.</div> </div> </div> </div>What edict would this be, and where would it be beastiality, seeing as Royal Avatars can have many forms, and can be considered to be sentient/sapient?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:13:46-07:00","id":1221567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221493#post1221493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can werewolves have a hostile Spirit Fettered to them and become/be Urged without them really knowing that it's happening? I know they see/sense Spirits in Twilight, but can the Fettered Spirit hide inside them and influence their actions in some subtle ways that they might not know they are Urged? I had an idea that the Fettering might have happened in a time when they were not fully aware/can't remember such as Kuruth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how I'd do it: Have the spirit fetter into a wearable object, probably jewelry, hide therein, then influence the one who wears it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T21:31:15-07:00","id":1221613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221567#post1221567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I'd do it: Have the spirit fetter into a wearable object, probably jewelry, hide therein, then influence the one who wears it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea. The thing a Spirit Fetters to has to be Open to it, right? Somehow Resonant with the Influence of the Spirit?<br /> <br /> In this particular case my first idea was having a Spirit of Hunger attached to them, urging them to eat more, especially when they get low on Essence. Perhaps take a bite out of a human. I'm not sure the characters are wearing anything that could be associated with Hunger. Mostly just armor and weapons.<br /> <br /> What about Fetishes? Can a Spirit Fetter or Possess a Fetish? My first thought is no, since they already have a Spirit in them and it would somehow prevent this. One of the PC's has a &quot;Devourers Fang&quot; fetish with them....<br /> <br /> Also, can an object have more than 1 Spirit Fettered in it, or be possessed by more than 1?<br /> Can Spirits Possess an object that is a Locus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 05-24-2018, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:05:47-07:00","id":1221691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221539#post1221539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urfarah's whole sort of deal was that the various denizens of Flesh, the Shadow, and the Border Marches stay in their respective lanes and that deviation from this model warranted correction.<br /> <br /> It is <i>also</i> known that the Firstborn are given free passage throughout the worlds to indulge themselves and that this is a sticking point with basically every other major supernatural mover and shaker of the era, so the above doesn't really make much difference without the supposition that the death of the Wolf is something his children have uniform feelings on.</div> </div> </div> </div> silver wolf and rabid wolf don\u2019t give a fuck about dad wolfs laws","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:25:32-07:00","id":1221715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221613#post1221613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an interesting idea. The thing a Spirit Fetters to has to be Open to it, right? Somehow Resonant with the Influence of the Spirit?<br /> <br /> In this particular case my first idea was having a Spirit of Hunger attached to them, urging them to eat more, especially when they get low on Essence. Perhaps take a bite out of a human. I'm not sure the characters are wearing anything that could be associated with Hunger. Mostly just armor and weapons.<br /> <br /> What about Fetishes? Can a Spirit Fetter or Possess a Fetish? My first thought is no, since they already have a Spirit in them and it would somehow prevent this. One of the PC's has a &quot;Devourers Fang&quot; fetish with them....<br /> <br /> Also, can an object have more than 1 Spirit Fettered in it, or be possessed by more than 1?<br /> Can Spirits Possess an object that is a Locus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have the ring be an artistic representation of hunger to make it open to that particular spirit.<br /> <br /> No, I wouldn't allow a fetish being open to anything else other than it's attuned wielder, barring specific corrupting numina if you want to make a story out of it. An Idigam corrupting fetishes doesn't sounds far fetched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:48:17-07:00","id":1221739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1221691#post1221691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> silver wolf and rabid wolf don\u2019t give a fuck about dad wolfs laws</div> </div> </div> </div>They give substantially less of a fuck to humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","ra