class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223550#post1223550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a werewolf, with Influence over water at 3 (don't remember the name of the gift at the moment), invert the flow of a river in order to try to let some fugitive to sink or be dragged back to him?<br /> How can I calculate the area affected by the influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Control Influence? Sounds doable. Dunno about the area, though - if it\u2019s not in the Ephemeral Entity rules, then I\u2019d assume it\u2019s just enough to tie up most of the fugitives but leave one or two free and able to help the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:30:43-07:00","id":1223614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223550#post1223550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a werewolf, with Influence over water at 3 (don't remember the name of the gift at the moment), invert the flow of a river in order to try to let some fugitive to sink or be dragged back to him?<br /> How can I calculate the area affected by the influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd reserve it for a dramatic use of Create, because by reversing a river's flow, you're basically creating something new, geographically speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:36:15-07:00","id":1223775,"title":"","content":"Do some werewolves have sex in non hishu forms? Is it like a kink?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:23:13-07:00","id":1223790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223775#post1223775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do some werewolves have sex in non hishu forms? Is it like a kink?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. Ask the people who wrote Changing Breeds back in nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:28:07-07:00","id":1223791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223775#post1223775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do some werewolves have sex in non hishu forms? Is it like a kink?</div> </div> </div> </div>So technically, it's not exactly against the oath, and humans will be humans. Hell, I've had a PC do that off screen just to attempt a harmony break towards spirit. I'd say it's not likely to be kosher, at the minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:43:50-07:00","id":1223794,"title":"","content":"If they have sex in wolf form will they get stuck like wolves for a hour that would be funny","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:46:48-07:00","id":1223797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223775#post1223775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do some werewolves have sex in non hishu forms? Is it like a kink?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attitudes towards sex and attraction seem like one of the biggest things that would vary depending on the individual and whatever social group influences them (along with acceptable application of violence). At the very least, having sex in dalu form isn't exactly exploring the far frontier of sexual imagination, and probably wouldn't even be considered weird, again depending on the individual (one werewolf's dalu form can, through the Favored Form Merit, be particularly charismatic and empathetic, while another through Fortified Form can be covered in thick, knotted scar tissue like Deadpool).<br /> <br /> It's possible Blood of the Wolf gets into this, one chapter seemed to be about pinning down the 'everyday life' of werewolves. But werewolves have changed a lot since first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2018, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:06:08-07:00","id":1223799,"title":"","content":"How have they changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:06:21-07:00","id":1223800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223794#post1223794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have sex in wolf form will they get stuck like wolves for a hour that would be funny</div> </div> </div> </div>No such thing, but consider that certain substancess that wouldn't matter much to a human would matter to a wolf, and while the niche of materials that do nothing to a human but get a canine high is unknown to me, it's not impossible that a shape change after the wrong meal or drug session could result in a werewolf spontaneously getting high.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not much from CHapter 1 of Blood of the Wolf would need to be changed in response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-31-2018, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:18:56-07:00","id":1223804,"title":"","content":"That could be hilarious to GM!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:33:02-07:00","id":1223811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1223799#post1223799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How have they changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Less influence from Werewolf The Apocalypse. Which includes werewolves as literal human-wolf hybrids and their wolf form as literal wolves being heavily deemphasized, in favor of presenting werewolves as shapeshifting predators to whom the human and wolf forms are only skins to wear as tools on the hunt.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is also likely why there isn\u2019t the concept of \u201cdefault\u201d or \u201cnatural\u201d forms for the Uratha of Forsaken, unlike the Garou of Apocalypse having Breeds. Sure, Uratha grew up in human form, but that\u2019s just because they didn\u2019t Change. Sure, they die in human form, but that\u2019s the human form doing its job of hiding from the masses one last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-31-2018, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:53:26-07:00","id":1223829,"title":"","content":"What are bonobo spirts like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:46:41-07:00","id":1223909,"title":"","content":"Do ivory claws still treat there elf blood like prized breeding show dogs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T21:26:47-07:00","id":1224077,"title":"","content":"As I was pressed before to use this topic - How long takes from Urged to go Claimed? I cannot find in 2E rules on Spirits in corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T23:32:44-07:00","id":1224090,"title":"","content":"They start on page 186. You don't need to be Urged to be Claimed, and Claiming causes the Urged Condition anyways. You might be thinking of the Controlled Condition, which is a prerequisite for Claiming. Aside from its further prerequisites, Controlled can be created by the use of the Control Influence, or using the Possess Manifestation on a number of times equal to the target or spirit's Willpower, whichever is higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T01:42:18-07:00","id":1224111,"title":"","content":"So nothing hard like 'Urged character after Spirit's Rank in days become Claimed', yes? I look for some guidelines here how much time may pass between Urging and Claiming on each individual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-02-2018, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:45:18-07:00","id":1224158,"title":"","content":"There's no period between Urging and Claiming because Urging doesn't actually lead to Claiming. It is a side effect of the process of Claiming, as stated in the Claimed Manifestation Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T08:16:51-07:00","id":1224169,"title":"","content":"From the read of Condition Claimed gains one Spirit's Attributes dot per day - so full Claiming is when all Spirits Attributes will be added, yes? So when is Spirit-Ridden still Urged and when Claimed? When 1/3 of Spirits Attributes were added is he Claimed? All of them? Do Storm Lords even make a difference on their Hunts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T08:20:00-07:00","id":1224170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1224169#post1224169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the read of Condition Claimed gains one Spirit's Attributes dot per day - so full Claiming is when all Spirits Attributes will be added, yes? So when is Spirit-Ridden still Urged and when Claimed? When 1/3 of Spirits Attributes were added is he Claimed? All of them? Do Storm Lords even make a difference on their Hunts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Storm Lords make a difference? All Ridden are their Sacred Prey, and their Siskur-Dah Condition works identically on all types of Ridden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:18:17-07:00","id":1224747,"title":"","content":"Hi, does anyone know where to look for an ancestor ghost summoning rite or something like that? I'm interested in summoning a ghost of the deceased werewolf and making him a mentor. I realize, that mentor itself will need to be bought as a merit, but wanted to tackle this subject from fluff/lore perspective as well. Couldn't find any ritual that could be used for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24289-wamesahau","name":"wamesahau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:54:04-07:00","id":1224761,"title":"","content":"Werewolves tend to have ancestor spirits, rather than ancestor ghosts. It's not clear if werewolves even have ghosts, and if they do they don't play by the same rules as human ones.<br /> <br /> But if you want to find an ancestor spirit, you could use the Shadowcall rite.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind this isn't exactly 'your ancestor' as much as 'a spirit created by the memory of your ancestor' which can be warped depending on how people viewed them.<br /> <br /> If you really want a ghost, the character could potentially track down a variant rite that allowed them to summon ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T22:03:10-07:00","id":1224892,"title":"","content":"I based my line of thinking on &quot;Funeral Rite&quot;, that's why I mentioned ancestor ghost (even though the description mentions &quot;spirit of the dead wolf&quot;).<br /> I assume I would need to create such a rite on my own (based on e.g. Call Gaffling or Call Jaggling)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24289-wamesahau","name":"wamesahau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T22:05:15-07:00","id":1224894,"title":"","content":"Ah first edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wamesahau</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1224892#post1224892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I based my line of thinking on &quot;Funeral Rite&quot;, that's why I mentioned ancestor ghost (even though the description mentions &quot;spirit of the dead wolf&quot;).<br /> I assume I would need to create such a rite on my own (based on e.g. Call Gaffling or Call Jaggling)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though if you go the ancestor spirit route you just need Call Gaffling or Call Jaggling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T08:48:32-07:00","id":1226471,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> 1. My player asked me if she can create a fetish to change the effect of the Catastrophe facet of the Gift of the Elements to work with Influences other than the ones included, so she could use it with her Totemic Empowerment and create rather bountiful harvest for the pack Totem. How would you rate such a fetish? If it would work on specific Influence by binding a coressponding spirit, or all of them with a spirit of Strenght or maybe even one of the Cahalunim (General &quot;I will unleash the power, to hell with consequences&quot;)? Also, would Influence (Electricity) would be considered elemental, if so, which other elements could be included - metal, wood, light/darkness etc?<br /> <br /> 2. Also, she asked me if there is another reliable way of regaining lost Willpower other than acting as her Blood/Bone archetypes, I looked over the Inspired condition for herself but it does it only by two consecutive exceptional success rolls (one to gain the condition, and one when resolving it). <br /> <br /> \u200bAny feedback is appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24303-shikaree","name":"Shikaree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:26:01-07:00","id":1226481,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have no experience with fetishes this edition. I'd say three dots, since I would say it's not really a question of 'can I do this' and more 'What will the consequences be if I do this?' As for electricity, I'd say yes, but this is really the sort of thing where the ruling is up to the story you want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:30:04-07:00","id":1226482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226471#post1226471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. My player asked me if she can create a fetish to change the effect of the Catastrophe facet of the Gift of the Elements to work with Influences other than the ones included, so she could use it with her Totemic Empowerment and create rather bountiful harvest for the pack Totem. How would you rate such a fetish? If it would work on specific Influence by binding a coressponding spirit, or all of them with a spirit of Strenght or maybe even one of the Cahalunim (General &quot;I will unleash the power, to hell with consequences&quot;)? Also, would Influence (Electricity) would be considered elemental, if so, which other elements could be included - metal, wood, light/darkness etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, it allows you to amplify Influence given by another Elemental Facet. So mechanically speaking, an easy way to do it is a fetish to alter one of the other Elemental Facets, and Catastrophe would just work with that. If you wanted to use it with Totemic Empowerment, you would need the fetish to alter Catastrophe. Either way, I think it would just need to be a 3 dot fetish, which offers, 'a modification to a specific Facet that allows it to be used in new ways.' This would require a 3 dot spirit to be bound. If you were altering Catastrophe to work based off Totemic Empowerment, you might want a totem spirit for it (preferably not your own). If you were altering one of the other Elemental Gifts you could probably manage it just by binding another elemental spirit, like an electrical spirit or lightning spirit. Some sample elemental spirits from other werewolf books are electricity, plastic, steel, granite, flame, storm. I think you could probably manage more far out, non-elemental things like Influence: Snakes if you went up and used a 5 dot fetish instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Also, she asked me if there is another reliable way of regaining lost Willpower other than acting as her Blood/Bone archetypes, I looked over the Inspired condition for herself but it does it only by two consecutive exceptional success rolls (one to gain the condition, and one when resolving it).<br /> <br /> \u200bAny feedback is appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>You're supposed to be able to get 1 Willpower back for a good night's rest. It was left out of the book by mistake. Other ways are mentioned <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/788869-ways-to-recover-willpower\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:55:19-07:00","id":1226490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226471#post1226471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. My player asked me if she can create a fetish to change the effect of the Catastrophe facet of the Gift of the Elements to work with Influences other than the ones included, so she could use it with her Totemic Empowerment and create rather bountiful harvest for the pack Totem. How would you rate such a fetish? If it would work on specific Influence by binding a coressponding spirit, or all of them with a spirit of Strenght or maybe even one of the Cahalunim (General &quot;I will unleash the power, to hell with consequences&quot;)? Also, would Influence (Electricity) would be considered elemental, if so, which other elements could be included - metal, wood, light/darkness etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have a fetish make Black Earth, Red Hunger work with Catastrophe for such. You have an example of a fetish that allows you to use electricity influence in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226471#post1226471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Also, she asked me if there is another reliable way of regaining lost Willpower other than acting as her Blood/Bone archetypes, I looked over the Inspired condition for herself but it does it only by two consecutive exceptional success rolls (one to gain the condition, and one when resolving it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rest, each night's sleep is worth 1 WP for Uratha, same as humans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T10:44:21-07:00","id":1226505,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the quick recommendations! Regarding Willpower I also would ask:<br /> <br /> Do you allow your players to spend Willpower to boost rolls which, if successful, would result in fulfilling their blood/bone Archetype conditions for regaining Willpower? It would seem that they become great at what they are - its basically a free +3 enhancement bonus to such rolls. Like, for example, Intimidation rolls with the Monster, or a Stealth roll for a Lone wolf acting independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24303-shikaree","name":"Shikaree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T15:51:06-07:00","id":1226593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226505#post1226505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the quick recommendations! Regarding Willpower I also would ask:<br /> <br /> Do you allow your players to spend Willpower to boost rolls which, if successful, would result in fulfilling their blood/bone Archetype conditions for regaining Willpower? It would seem that they become great at what they are - its basically a free +3 enhancement bonus to such rolls. Like, for example, Intimidation rolls with the Monster, or a Stealth roll for a Lone wolf acting independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, given they get no net gain in Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T16:16:43-07:00","id":1226601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226505#post1226505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow your players to spend Willpower to boost rolls which, if successful, would result in fulfilling their blood/bone Archetype conditions for regaining Willpower? It would seem that they become great at what they are - its basically a free +3 enhancement bonus to such rolls. Like, for example, Intimidation rolls with the Monster, or a Stealth roll for a Lone wolf acting independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Both for a single point and for a full refill. WP is there to be used, and especially when performing something risky (which most Blood &amp; Bone archetypes requires). Is it metagaming? Debatable, but I'd never impose a limitation on a player choosing to act according to the character sheet. Besides, only a few archetypes grants WP depending on the outcomes of your actions rather than just simply taking the action regardless of the outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T18:06:11-07:00","id":1226624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1226471#post1226471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Also, she asked me if there is another reliable way of regaining lost Willpower other than acting as her Blood/Bone archetypes, I looked over the Inspired condition for herself but it does it only by two consecutive exceptional success rolls (one to gain the condition, and one when resolving it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspired gives you a Willpower point regardless of how successful the roll is. That's the primary benefit of the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T18:18:49-07:00","id":1228722,"title":"","content":"Would a Phantom Pack set off spirit detecting powers? I don't think they're visible to others, but I'd like a second opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T20:26:16-07:00","id":1228739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1228722#post1228722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Phantom Pack set off spirit detecting powers? I don't think they're visible to others, but I'd like a second opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the line, 'A pack of phantom wolves, possibly spirits or ghosts, lurk at her periphery at all times.' I'd say it depends. It looks like you could have it be ghosts (say, if the character was born at a place a pack of wolves were killed) or spirits (for instance in a territory that was a hunting ground but is now free of wolves or werewolves). Presumably you could come up with some other things that would fit.<br /> <br /> So, yes if they're spirits. No if they're something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T22:43:03-07:00","id":1228778,"title":"","content":"What about the creation element of Influences while in the Shadow - does it create ephemera or is special case of essence locked in a flavour or form? Can a fire light other ephemera on fire? Could a spirit with the same resonanse eat it up - doew he eat the substance if it's ephemeral, ot feed through its resonance, leaving the created substance in existance like when it is in the flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24303-shikaree","name":"Shikaree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T23:05:20-07:00","id":1228779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shikaree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1228778#post1228778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the creation element of Influences while in the Shadow - does it create ephemera or is special case of essence locked in a flavour or form?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you're making, I think you could make some sort of raw Essence if you tried, but for the most part if you made a Fire, for instance, it would create fire made of ephemera. Technically, everything in the Shadow is ephemera, even werewolves or mages who transport there. It's the 'matter' of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a fire light other ephemera on fire? </div> </div> </div>If they're flammable. Or inflammable. It might work if something was conceptually inflammable, like a Rage or Pain spirit. Though it might not be hurt from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a spirit with the same resonanse eat it up - doew he eat the substance if it's ephemeral, ot feed through its resonance, leaving the created substance in existance like when it is in the flesh? </div> </div> </div>The substance created in the Shadow is ephemeral, so it wouldn't leave an existing piece behind, unless the eater wanted to or it fit whatever was happening, like if a Fire spirit ate a big fire it might leave ashes or smoke behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T09:44:18-07:00","id":1228878,"title":"","content":"Are there any official or homebrew alternate Auspice abilities, similar to the alternate Birthrights presented in the Beast Player's Guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T23:05:12-07:00","id":1229090,"title":"","content":"There is the Doom Howler merit, which is unnofficial content from one of the Werewolf writers. Not exactly what you asked for, since it's a merit, but as far as I know it's the closest we have currently.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Doom Howler (Werewolf Merit \u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Cahalith Auspice<br /> Effect: Your character replaces the Prophetic Dreams Auspice Ability with the Doom Howler ability: Once per chapter, you can force an attack or hostile effect that would be targeted at a packmate to be targeted at the Cahalith instead, if it would possibly be viable. This is your choice as the player, rather than a conscious ability on the Cahalith, and so they do not need to be aware of the attack to retarget it; however, the source of the effect must be aware of the Cahalith's presence. Ablaze with the moon's power, the Cahalith is rendered as a threatening apparition of Luna's might, and draws the greatest risks of battle onto themselves.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T23:18:24-07:00","id":1229092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1228878#post1228878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any official or homebrew alternate Auspice abilities, similar to the alternate Birthrights presented in the Beast Player's Guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the alternative Auspices in Signs of the Moon. For Solar Eclipse, Lunar Eclipse, Stellar Eclipse and Blood Moon. There's also alternative Moon Gifts, as each Auspice does cover a range of concepts, such as the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Screaming Moon of the Cahalith</a>. Aside from Auspices there are things that can happen during the First Change, with some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1174969-six-pups-a-changing?p=1175434#post1175434\">homebrew examples from a writer</a>.<br /> <br /> So far the books have been more about the core of the game, with the Pack expanding on it. Presumably there will be some interesting options in Shunned by the Moon, as some of the werewolves within may have a skewed relationship with Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2018, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T15:17:34-07:00","id":1230379,"title":"","content":"I'm a very new DM to Chronicles of Darkness, and a new DM to tabletops in general, I've been pouring over the resource material and I had a couple of questions, I'm sorry if maybe these are easy to answer but with so much information I'm feeling a bit lost (I apologize if these questions have been asked before): <br /> <br /> 1. Wounds, from what I understand they are places that permeate this horrific aura that detracts spirits of pain, and usually they're the sites of atrocities like the wound in Rwanda where the genocide happened - But my question is what is significant enough to make a wound, area there specific requirements and how best would it be to go about establishing one in a game?<br /> <br /> Additionally, there's the notation of &quot;rare wounds&quot; which seems vague, how would one be able to distinguish a rare wound if they don't know it was one?<br /> <br /> Also how does one go about closing a wound?<br /> <br /> 2. I'm running a cross over with Sin-eaters, mainly because one of my players really want to play a sin-eater and I was wondering how well they would get along with werewolves and vice versa?<br /> I know they can share some commonalities and I believe my player wants to do an advocate-based sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Is there anything I should be aware of in terms of dynamics with sin-eaters and werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24328-talona","name":"Talona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24328_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T16:15:59-07:00","id":1230389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1230379#post1230379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Wounds, from what I understand they are places that permeate this horrific aura that detracts spirits of pain, and usually they're the sites of atrocities like the wound in Rwanda where the genocide happened - But my question is what is significant enough to make a wound, area there specific requirements and how best would it be to go about establishing one in a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Blasphemies, 'Opening new Wounds requires localized bursts of negative emotion and behavior.' Bale Hounds, who enjoy having Wounds around, often would help them get established by encouraging negative emotions or behavior. Keep in mind this doesn't require any human impact. A plague pushing wildlife in an isolated area to extinction or erratic behavior can be enough. But the site of a horrific and unnatural or rare human/werewolf-led event can do it too, the place where Father Wolf was killed is supposed to be one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, there's the notation of &quot;rare wounds&quot; which seems vague, how would one be able to distinguish a rare wound if they don't know it was one? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where 'rare wounds' come up, do you have a book reference or page number or something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also how does one go about closing a wound? </div> </div> </div>Time and effort. The Resonance Shaper Merit can help, but you're basically attempting to heal the metaphysical 'memory' of a horrific act. Getting those who live in the area to move beyond it would help, but you'd still have a lot of work to do keeping Wounded spirits from making it worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I'm running a cross over with Sin-eaters, mainly because one of my players really want to play a sin-eater and I was wondering how well they would get along with werewolves and vice versa?<br /> I know they can share some commonalities and I believe my player wants to do an advocate-based sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Is there anything I should be aware of in terms of dynamics with sin-eaters and werewolves? </div> </div> </div>If you're using first edition, Sin-Eaters are mechanically overpowered, compared to werewolves. But they could be good for hunting down ghosts, and I believe hunting abmortals is a side job of Sin-Eaters that werewolves may be good at. It's possible other werewolves wouldn't like the deathly energy they were about. The Pack also gets into some details about how it can work out, or not. Werewolves don't belong in the Underworld, though, so trips there would be easy on the Sin-Eater and bad on them.<br /> <br /> There's no in-grained hatred or animosity though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2018, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T23:39:00-07:00","id":1230754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1230379#post1230379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I'm running a cross over with Sin-eaters, mainly because one of my players really want to play a sin-eater and I was wondering how well they would get along with werewolves and vice versa?<br /> I know they can share some commonalities and I believe my player wants to do an advocate-based sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Is there anything I should be aware of in terms of dynamics with sin-eaters and werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1230389#post1230389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using first edition, Sin-Eaters are mechanically overpowered, compared to werewolves. But they could be good for hunting down ghosts, and I believe hunting abmortals is a side job of Sin-Eaters that werewolves may be good at. It's possible other werewolves wouldn't like the deathly energy they were about. The Pack also gets into some details about how it can work out, or not. Werewolves don't belong in the Underworld, though, so trips there would be easy on the Sin-Eater and bad on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree Sin-Eater suffered from <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PowerCreep\" target=\"_blank\">Power Creep</a> in first edition. Here is some of what I did to bring them back inline with my interpretation of the other game lines*:<br /> <br /> *Disclaimer: Includes references to homebrew rules and are built for Frailty Chronicle themes and context click the spoiler to continue<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801821#post801821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Sin-Eater Banes</span></span></b><br /> <b>Netherworld Maelstrom</b><br /> The geist within sin-eaters are extremely unnatural beings and act as conduit of the power of the underworld. Sin-eaters are extremely susceptible to ghostly numina and ghosts gain power while within their presence. A ghost outside of the underworld gain an additional rank in Intensity while within 300ft of a sin-eater. Whether within the underworld or elsewhere the sin-eaters suffers a penalty to resist ghostly numina equal to Permanent Atrocity + 10 \u2013 Synergy, and take the same penalty while<br /> <br /> This bane may be temporarily suspended for a Sin-Eater that Opens a Deathgate. See Opens a Deathgate for more information.<br /> <br /> <b>Backseat Driver</b><br /> Every Geist has a Deadly Aspiration which reflects its nature as an avatar of a certain type of death, using involving promoting the type of death it represents. Upon character creation the Storyteller assigns this Aspiration based on collaboration of the back story of the Geist done by the player and Storyteller. This Ossurary Aspiration applies to the Geist, not necessarily the Sin-eater, (though the Sin-Eater is free to take a Personal Aspiration in line with or identical to Geist if they choose) and does not apply for earning beats for the Sin-Eater (though if the Sin-Eater opted for mirror their Geist in Personal Aspirations, those apply as normal).<br /> <br /> Why the Geist\u2019s Aspiration is important to track is because it provides tips for role playing interactions with Geist, and when the Sin-Eater has Synergy (ei number of Supports) less than Permanent Atrocity plus Temporary Atrocity, they gain the Leveraged condition from their Geist once per chapter, which is always applied towards furthering this Aspiration to get its resolution. Frequently this causes a feedback loop of gaining more Temporary Atrocity unless the Sin-Eater can raise their Synergy or dump Temporary Atrocity. Giving in to this Leveraged condition does not count as supernaturally compulsion when interacting with Hesitation, Compunction and Post Traumatic Stress Disorder.<br /> <br /> <b>(Switch-able) Echoes of Change</b><br /> Each supernatural being with this bane has a set of circumstances described in a brief phrase that relates to how they gained their major template. This phrase is approved by the storyteller and recorded on the character sheet. Injuries inflicted when the circumstances described by the brief phrase are applicable cannot be regenerated or healed via supernatural means, it counts as resistant damage of the type normally associated with the damage inflicted. Supernaturally provided armors and supernatural powers don't provide protection from damage gained during circumstances described by the brief phrase. While circumstances described by the brief phrase are applicable the supernatural being's max die pool for any action is capped by their Morality Advantage. In addition while circumstances described by the brief phrase are applicable to the supernatural takes 1 point of Aggravated damage per Permanent Atrocity they have per combat turn. Supernatural powers used by a being with this bane do not work while the bane is in contact with the being, or the circumstance is applicable to the being. Abilities of a supernatural to rise from the dead do not work if this bane was involved with their death.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>to convert to a system that doesn't use Atrocity you could instead use 10-Stability Advantage as the place holder of the value when Permanent Atrocity is mention, meaning a Maximum Stability Advantage (Syntheses in the case of Sin-Eaters) wouldn't take damage per round in the same way a vampire in my setting wouldn't take Aggravated from Sunlight unless they had acquired a Permanent Atrocity. Also I hve the follow Sin Eater and Werewolf Ban which increase as they gain power stat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=1021407#post1021407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural Bans<br /> This is a a list of Standard Bans each Major Template has per dot of Power Stat, and are Cumulative.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spend 1 Essence for each night without a Pack or outside your Pack\u2019s Territory (or if the Pack has no Territory)</li> <li>Spend 1 Essence for each month without Siskur-Dah</li> <li>Spend 1 Essence for each month without time in the Material world</li> <li>Spend 1 Essence for each month without time in the Hisil</li> <li>Spend 1 additional Essence for each phase of the moon that passes without the Siskur-Dah.</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by an Environmental Condition Resonant with Siskur-Dah of their Pack. (Pulled into nearest <i>Hisil</i> Verge when support collapses)</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by an Open Environmental Condition Resonant with Siskur-Dah of their Pack. (Pulled into nearest <i>Hisil</i> Verge when support collapses)</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by a Shadow Gateway which relies upon an Environmental Condition Resonant with Siskur-Dah of their Pack. (Pulled into nearest <i>Hisil</i> Verge when support collapses)</li> <li>Never remain in areas in the Hisil that reflects the Material World unless supported by an Environmental Condition Resonant with Siskur-Dah of their Pack. (Pulled into nearest section of the <i>Hisil</i> that doesn\u2019t reflect the Material World when support collapses)</li> <li>Never remain in areas in the Hisil that reflects the Material World unless supported by an Open Environmental Condition Resonant with Siskur-Dah of their Pack. (Pulled into nearest section of the <i>Hisil</i> that doesn\u2019t reflect the Material World when support collapses)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spend 1 Plasm for each week without gaining a Clue for a Death focused Mystery</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm for each night without spending time in a place with a Menace that matches your Threshold</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm for each week without a Krew</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm for each month without time in the Material world</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm for each month without time in the Great Below</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by an Environmental Condition Menace that matches your Threshold. (Pulled into nearest Avernian Gate when support collapses)</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm for each day without ferrying a dead soul deeper into the Great Below</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by an Open Environmental Condition Menace that matches your Threshold. (Pulled into nearest Avernian Gate when support collapses)</li> <li>Spend 1 Plasm each day that time was spent above ground in the Material World</li> <li>Never remain in the Material World unless supported by an Avernian Gateway which relies upon an Environmental Condition Menace that matches your Threshold. (Pulled into nearest Avernian Gate when support collapses)</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of my Homebrew rules I'd recommend regardless of whether you use the above to help highlight the differences of mindset the breaking points of Harmony versus Sins against Synergy is this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Compunction, Hesitation</span>, and Post Traumatic Stress Disorder</b><br /> To initiate using lethal force during a scene that would be a breaking point for your characters Stability Advantage if the subjects of your violence were to die you must succeed a reflexive Resolve + Composure check, or spend a point of Willpower. If you fail you may spend an Instant Action to reroll (with the standard -1 for the previous failure). All further re-rolls within the same scene to avoid natural compunction against this type of violence are also instant actions. This does not apply when they character is acting on compulsions caused by the supernatural powers of others, or internal supernatural urges beyond their control. Being supernaturally controlled towards this type of violence, whether internal or externally, is always a breaking point due to its traumatic nature and damage to sense of identity.<br /> <br /> Should a character need to initiate lethal force when they are out of Willpower, they may do so but must take one of the following Conditions at the end of the Scene: Guilty, Shaken, or Spooked. If they already have all these conditions they instead choose from this list: Broken, Fugue, or Madness. If they are unfortunate enough to have all those conditions they instead roll three basic stress against a Support. Once a character has only has one Support left they take a Minor Undertaking as a Slasher, and when a character has no Supports they take Major Undertaking as a Slasher and no longer count as an ensoulled being with breaking points. For more details check the Slasher Section.<br /> <br /> This mechanic reflects that character's within this iteration of World of Darkness are not video game characters that perpetrate gruesome violence easily without care, and to also increase the value of refreshing Willpower for violent characters, which fits trope of within retelling of the stories characters that regularly engage in battle which is portrayed as gritty, to include real life war-stories, and some police dramas. (think of people indulging vices to &quot;blow off steam&quot; or commit acts of charity because &quot;I had to make sense of it all&quot;) It also increases how dangerous creatures that lack breaking points that allow violence seem compared to those that have them; it literally costs them nothing to harm others. It also highlights how compulsions from supernatural forces towards violence are even more frightening for the loss of control. This also helps portray the mental stresses of combat, and battle fatigue.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-28-2018, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:08:05-07:00","id":1231428,"title":"","content":"Quick question since Geist Kickstarter is coming soon and I alway save more than needed for those: how's <b>The Pack</b>? Would you recommend it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:21:01-07:00","id":1231431,"title":"","content":"I've only read it once, and I thought it was rather short (105 pages), with only a few things I think I could use in my current chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T16:13:51-07:00","id":1231472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1231428#post1231428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question since Geist Kickstarter is coming soon and I alway save more than needed for those: how's <b>The Pack</b>? Would you recommend it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Geist stuff is very brief, but it's good for a lot of other things, the daily life (and life on the hunt) of werewolves, how to play spirits, what protectorates are like, and 5 Lodge examples and rules for them in general which are great. There's also a few hunting grounds, Bangkok, Dubai and Malta. It is short, as Lost-His-Mind says, but good for werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T13:29:19-07:00","id":1232215,"title":"","content":"Is eating stray dogs ok, or should I draw the line at cats? (high PU Iron Master)<br /> also how old would such a werewolf usually be or possibly be since high PU slows down aging?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:44:18-07:00","id":1232233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1232215#post1232215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is eating stray dogs ok, or should I draw the line at cats? (high PU Iron Master)</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Primal Urge. Just because you only get nourishment from it doesn't mean you have to automatically go for the lowest possible choice. Humans have loads of food above spam and soylent. Dogs are omnivores, so if you're getting raw meat you can get it straight from a butcher. If you really want the 'fresh from the streets' taste dogs and cats are probably fine. If you're at the Carnivore level, cats are available, but 'drawing the line' there seems pretty self destructive for an inhuman shapeshifting apex predator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also how old would such a werewolf usually be or possibly be since high PU slows down aging? </div> </div> </div>Depends entirely on the werewolf. Some will start young and rocket through Primal Urge then slow down. Some werewolves can live till 90 and never hit 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-03-2018, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T17:44:52-07:00","id":1232261,"title":"","content":"Has there been another night horrors book for this game? Primarily wondering because someone told me about the spirit of the United States of America for the first one, and I'm wondering if that spirit carried on from the first night horrors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T17:59:15-07:00","id":1232263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1232261#post1232261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been another night horrors book for this game? Primarily wondering because someone told me about the spirit of the United States of America for the first one, and I'm wondering if that spirit carried on from the first night horrors</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_Wolfsbane\" target=\"_blank\">Wolfsbane</a>. It's where that spirit is though it's not 'the' spirit of the United States and is 'a' spirit of American symbols and some other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:05:05-07:00","id":1234688,"title":"","content":"Awe Numina. &quot;The spirit causes terror in anyone who can see it... Anyone gaining fewer successes than the spirit is unable to move and speak....&quot;<br /> <br /> What does this actually mean? The spirit is unable to choose to who is affected or not? So even spirits allied to it are affected? Also, &quot;anyone who can see it&quot; I assume that could have a line of sight to it, no walls and such, not just closing your eyes or turning your head away. You would still be able to see it if you chose to, you just choose not to. What about blind/blinded things, things that don't have functional eyes?<br /> <br /> &quot;Unable to move or speak&quot; Would that mean they can do absolutely nothing that would require movement or speech? I assume Immobilized tilt would be what it causes, so no defense. Would you even allow for someone do a Killing Blow if they are unable to move for let's say 3 turns with exceptional success?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:20:07-07:00","id":1234693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1234688#post1234688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does this actually mean? The spirit is unable to choose to who is affected or not? So even spirits allied to it are affected? Also, &quot;anyone who can see it&quot; I assume that could have a line of sight to it, no walls and such, not just closing your eyes or turning your head away. You would still be able to see it if you chose to, you just choose not to. What about blind/blinded things, things that don't have functional eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's implying you have to be someone who does see it, not just someone who could potentially see it. If you're about to use it and have allies, you should probably suggest they avert their eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Unable to move or speak&quot; Would that mean they can do absolutely nothing that would require movement or speech? I assume Immobilized tilt would be what it causes, so no defense. Would you even allow for someone do a Killing Blow if they are unable to move for let's say 3 turns with exceptional success? </div> </div> </div>Sure and yes.<br /> <br /> The Numina given are meant to represent a fraction of the abilities available to ephemeral entities. If you feel that one is inappropriate and you want to change it to make it feel 'more fitting' in a game of yours, you should do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T17:01:40-07:00","id":1235367,"title":"","content":"Can the 'Organization Size' merit in Hurt Locker be taken as a Pack Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:42:43-07:00","id":1235421,"title":"","content":"Probably. It does imply that there's more knowledge going on, so it would have to be a specific kind of pack, like a criminal organization, or very large one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:53:48-07:00","id":1236567,"title":"","content":"Are the cahalith hunters in darkness like go in quiet, go out loud? Im having troubke understamding how they differentiate from the others besides more restraint","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T15:05:57-07:00","id":1236571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1236567#post1236567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the cahalith hunters in darkness like go in quiet, go out loud? Im having troubke understamding how they differentiate from the others besides more restraint</div> </div> </div> </div>'Hunters in Darkness: The Mennina are the fear of the night, and that means that their Cahalith are silent and terrifying. A gibbous-moon Hunter is invisible until she wishes to strike, and then the story of her Rage is a quiet, intimate thing, a meeting that she and her prey share. In an auspice composed of the boisterous and the glorious, the Cahalith Hunters are more introspective and focused.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T15:18:09-07:00","id":1236575,"title":"","content":"That's actually why I'm asking, funnily enough. What I don't understand is does it mean unlike most others they prefer a quiet story? Or that they are more logical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T15:28:28-07:00","id":1236580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1236575#post1236575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually why I'm asking, funnily enough. What I don't understand is does it mean unlike most others they prefer a quiet story? Or that they are more logical</div> </div> </div> </div>Cahalith are usually big and loud. Hunter in Darkness are usually more quiet and focused. When you have someone who is both, rather than lean one way over the other, they mix both. So they won't come charging at you with war cries, and instead be quiet about it. But when it comes to the actual fight, they mix the Hunters ferocity and the Cahaliths passion, and things can get loud.<br /> <br /> Regarding their stories, it seems like they would pivot more towards a story that really hits home with one listener, rather than hits on surface emotions with a crowd. Sort of like the difference between a slow dance between lovers and a mosh pit at a concert.<br /> <br /> That all said it's just tendencies and shouldn't block off a character concept you want to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:06:45-07:00","id":1236596,"title":"","content":"With the Hunters in Darkness focused on their territory and defending it, I could easily see a Cahalith who makes their territory as frightening as possibly, human bones turn up in places they weren't a moment ago, howling in the distance. They want the prey to know their being hunted, but they don't want to be seen until it's time for the kill. At least that's how I think of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:19:09-07:00","id":1236603,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok, thanks guys, also nofather I'll keep that in mind, as I just didn't understand what the &quot;average&quot; hunter cahalith was like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:24:35-07:00","id":1236604,"title":"","content":"I think Gryphon's Feather had a good point, too. They're territorial to begin with, and likely to dot their territories with warnings. they even have the Lodge of the Hook Hand, with hyper-territorial werewolves that usurp the narrative of urban legends. In one game I heard of there was a member of the Hunters in Darkness who protected a house, a sacred place in their territory, by spreading word that it was haunted, which was backed by the people who went in then disappeared, never to be seen again.<br /> <br /> A lot of first edition information still stands, as well. From Tribes of the Moon, 'Cahalith: Some Gibbous Moons talk their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s\u2019 ears off, but this isn\u2019t so often the case with the Hunters in Darkness. Hunter Cahalith try to teach their students to listen, and if everything is an anecdote, sooner or later it all sounds the same. These mentors would rather stay quiet, listen to the world and collect information \u2014 until it\u2019s time to howl. Hunter Cahalith usually know the history of their territory down to the dirtiest little secret, and because of that familiarity, they often count an inordinate number of places as \u201csacred.\u201d A student of such a Hunter can expect to spend some time helping guard such places, often without knowing why the area is so important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-18-2018, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:47:52-07:00","id":1236614,"title":"","content":"Oh ok, that actually a pretty good example of what you and gryphons feather said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T10:59:33-07:00","id":1240140,"title":"","content":"Do any of you remember the lodge of the broken pledge.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:58:21-07:00","id":1240513,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to sense if someone has the Open Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:27:10-07:00","id":1240646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1240513#post1240513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to sense if someone has the Open Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having the relevant Influence to have spirit senses attuned to it. Otherwise, use common sense and empathy but that's within the domain of educated guesses. It wouldn't be difficult to devise a rite to that effect; Or a merit with the pre-requisite of Resonance Shaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:32:34-07:00","id":1240909,"title":"","content":"Anyone who has no legs or arms before the First Change can regenerate the missing limb when he becomes a Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","user":"RaphaTheAscended","date":". 07-31-2018, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:43:29-07:00","id":1240910,"title":"","content":"Yes, the uratha change makes sure you are the ultimate predator, from gaining 20/20 vision to growing back your limbs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:57:00-07:00","id":1240916,"title":"","content":"I had been in doubt because in the book I only found talking about senses and sensory organs. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","user":"RaphaTheAscended","date":". 07-31-2018, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:03:07-07:00","id":1241113,"title":"","content":"No problem<br /> <br /> Does the first night horrors book (or really, any book in general) give more information about majlin, amalgram, and Bale hounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Ap