m/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T14:19:49-08:00","id":1277544,"title":"","content":"while I know The forsaken is a spiritual successor to apocalypse, what were the main influences in folklore for the making of Werewolf: The Forsaken<br /> <br /> EDIT: reason for question is because takes much more heavily from traditional folklore than more movie inspired vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 12-30-2018, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T16:42:46-08:00","id":1277561,"title":"","content":"Animism and the idea of a lost paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T21:54:07-08:00","id":1277600,"title":"","content":"what about the nature of werewolves specifically? all I know is that some religions, including obscure protestant religions, saw werewolves as spiritual protectors (though most saw them as demon possessed/dealing humans)<br /> <br /> EDIT: even with the sidebar, I dont understand. what's the point of using The Fathers Form? it already seems contradictory to th