,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:51:53-08:00","id":1279522,"title":"","content":"Having read conflicting answers on these forums, would like to know once and for all:<br /> Do Uratha inflict lethal damage against Kindred, when attacking with their natural weaponry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","name":"blodm\u00e5ne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24954_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:05:04-08:00","id":1279528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blodm\u00e5ne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1279522#post1279522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read conflicting answers on these forums, would like to know once and for all:<br /> Do Uratha inflict lethal damage against Kindred, when attacking with their natural weaponry?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW says yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:39:10-08:00","id":1279540,"title":"","content":"Any form? Dalu bite/claws too?<br /> That sounds a tad too powerful for 0 cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","name":"blodm\u00e5ne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24954_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:43:31-08:00","id":1279541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blodm\u00e5ne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1279540#post1279540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any form? Dalu bite/claws too?<br /> That sounds a tad too powerful for 0 cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire can make someone slavishly addicted to them with three drops of blood, by contrast.<br /> <br /> And I think that applies to any form except for Hishu and Urhan, though being away from my books, don't quote me on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:47:57-08:00","id":1279543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire can make someone slavishly addicted to them with three drops of blood, by contrast. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","name":"blodm\u00e5ne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24954_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T13:16:43-08:00","id":1279551,"title":"","content":"Teeth are supernaturally enhanced even in hishu (though you still have a 0 Weapon bonus unless you have some special teeth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T16:45:34-08:00","id":1279597,"title":"","content":"It specifically deals lethal to vampires in all five forms. I just wish the rationale given was phrased better. It sounds like it works on those who have a general weakness to mystical sources of damage, and that's just not the case for vampires (nor for spirits for that matter but it works against them as well). I do think the likely intended reading is good, though, counting as a type of Bane for all manner of beings that already have Banes or equivalent weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T08:26:47-08:00","id":1280906,"title":"","content":"Well, don't take my word as gospel in this case and I might just be messily putting an argument together just to have a reason to explain a quality of werewolves, but here me out.<br /> <br /> Werewolves come from Father Wolf, right? Father Wolf was a primordial aspect of the hunt, it was 'The Hunter' in old pangea, simply put there was nothing that FW couldn't hunt since he was one of the cornerstones aspect of the hunt it defined it him as much he defined it, to the point that his descendants carry a bit of his legacy with them, for example in Dark Eras, werewolves are the bane of all pangeans, those were like the primordial spirits, that has been diluted over time as there is a level of separation between pangeans and spirits (not sure about this, don't have the book open here with me) <br /> <br /> Basically what I'm trying to say is that their connection to Father Wolf the great hunter is what grants them that bonus to their natural weaponry, it might be diluted through grades of separation or weakend because of the death of Father Wolf but it's not gone, just locked away under certain conditions, their natural weaponry is still a bane for most things, in the case of spirits, they have to outrank it, in the case of human like creature and humanity itself, they have to want to consume it for essence. When attacking to consume werewolves do aggravated damage after all.<br /> <br /> Hope it helps, might not be word of god, but it might point in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T15:23:06-08:00","id":1280992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1280906#post1280906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, don't take my word as gospel in this case and I might just be messily putting an argument together just to have a reason to explain a quality of werewolves, but here me out.<br /> <br /> Werewolves come from Father Wolf, right? Father Wolf was a primordial aspect of the hunt, it was 'The Hunter' in old pangea, simply put there was nothing that FW couldn't hunt since he was one of the cornerstones aspect of the hunt it defined it him as much he defined it, to the point that his descendants carry a bit of his legacy with them, for example in Dark Eras, werewolves are the bane of all pangeans, those were like the primordial spirits, that has been diluted over time as there is a level of separation between pangeans and spirits (not sure about this, don't have the book open here with me)<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm trying to say is that their connection to Father Wolf the great hunter is what grants them that bonus to their natural weaponry, it might be diluted through grades of separation or weakend because of the death of Father Wolf but it's not gone, just locked away under certain conditions, their natural weaponry is still a bane for most things, in the case of spirits, they have to outrank it, in the case of human like creature and humanity itself, they have to want to consume it for essence. When attacking to consume werewolves do aggravated damage after all.<br /> <br /> Hope it helps, might not be word of god, but it might point in the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, I'm totally behind the idea. I just don't think it's explained that well. The Predator's Jaws sidebar is phrased in a way that makes it seem dependent on vampires having a generic weakness against the supernatural, which they don't.<br /> <br /> A few clarifications, though:<br /> First off, it's only their bites that have this quality. Other natural weapons such as claws does not.<br /> Secondly, Uratha bites counts as Banes for all spirits (and other ephemeral entities) regardless of Rank. Outranking spirits by two Ranks makes all unarmed attacks (clawing, punching, grappling) the equivalent to a Bane, rather than just their jaws. The whole honorary Rank thing is a generic spirit trait (possibly inherited by Luna rather than Wolf, and can only be permanently increased through interactions with Lunes) that is separate from the Predator's Jaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T18:56:29-08:00","id":1281234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1280992#post1280992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yeah, I'm totally behind the idea. I just don't think it's explained that well. The Predator's Jaws sidebar is phrased in a way that makes it seem dependent on vampires having a generic weakness against the supernatural, which they don't.<br /> <br /> A few clarifications, though:<br /> First off, it's only their bites that have this quality. Other natural weapons such as claws does not.<br /> Secondly, Uratha bites counts as Banes for all spirits (and other ephemeral entities) regardless of Rank. Outranking spirits by two Ranks makes all unarmed attacks (clawing, punching, grappling) the equivalent to a Bane, rather than just their jaws. The whole honorary Rank thing is a generic spirit trait (possibly inherited by Luna rather than Wolf, and can only be permanently increased through interactions with Lunes) that is separate from the Predator's Jaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>If bite in any form counts as a bane against all spirits, then what even is the point of trying to figure out the bane of a spirit? A ban sure, but why go through the extra effort when can just gnaw on it? For low rank spirits, I can see this going either way, but for significantly more powerful spirits where the bane may be super annoying to find, this seems like a pretty big cop out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T21:07:56-08:00","id":1281247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1281234#post1281234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If bite in any form counts as a bane against all spirits, then what even is the point of trying to figure out the bane of a spirit? A ban sure, but why go through the extra effort when can just gnaw on it? For low rank spirits, I can see this going either way, but for significantly more powerful spirits where the bane may be super annoying to find, this seems like a pretty big cop out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, the potency of a werewolf's bite is being mischaracterized; the more practical reading would be &quot;even against enemies who reduce mundane weapon damage to bashing, a werewolf's jaws deal lethal damage due to their mystical qualities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly, many spirits are not made of things you want to put in your mouth even with the Uratha's heightened resistance to toxins. Show me a werewolf who doesn't hesitate to bite into a sewage-spirit or a disease-ridden Beshilu and I'll show you a rare specimen indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T04:43:11-08:00","id":1281277,"title":"","content":"Depends on your reading, but I'll admit that just causing lethal to ephemeral entities rather than being a Bane (and have all the extra effects like solidity to beings in Twilight) would make more sense from a game design perspective and is likely the intended rule.<br /> I really just dislike how badly written that side bar is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T17:30:50-08:00","id":1285085,"title":"","content":"Got a question about the Crimson Falx it says it cuts off a limb permanently, was that meant to say that it prevents a werewolf from regenerating and regrowing the limb? or just that the tilt becomes persistent until healed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T18:14:56-08:00","id":1285091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1285085#post1285085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a question about the Crimson Falx it says it cuts off a limb permanently, was that meant to say that it prevents a werewolf from regenerating and regrowing the limb? or just that the tilt becomes persistent until healed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tilt becomes persistent until healed. More of a temporary solution against werewolves, long term against people that don't naturally regenerate. Though even werewolves aren't usually going to be able to grow back that limb in the midst of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T21:12:33-08:00","id":1285122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1285091#post1285091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tilt becomes persistent until healed. More of a temporary solution against werewolves, long term against people that don't naturally regenerate. Though even werewolves aren't usually going to be able to grow back that limb in the midst of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't they just drop into Death Rage and giggle?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, being in Death Rage has consequences, but it's totally awesome at not-dying for a while!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T23:06:56-08:00","id":1285131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1285122#post1285122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't they just drop into Death Rage and giggle?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, being in Death Rage has consequences, but it's totally awesome at not-dying for a while!</div> </div> </div> </div>When a similar incident happened to me I dropped into gauru but it didn't get into death rage. Losing an arm can really cripple ones ability to fight, even in gauru, which can diminish some of gauru's effectiveness (especially if they lean on a weapon or fighting style), and losing a leg can basically leave you a sitting duck, as it reduces your speed and Defense . But it, as always, depends on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> There's a pair of Pure sisters in my first game who would likely each have one of these weapons, effectively being able to take one character out of a battle entirely or severely disable two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2019, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:49:47-08:00","id":1285236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1285131#post1285131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a similar incident happened to me I dropped into gauru but it didn't get into death rage. Losing an arm can really cripple ones ability to fight, even in gauru, which can diminish some of gauru's effectiveness (especially if they lean on a weapon or fighting style), and losing a leg can basically leave you a sitting duck, as it reduces your speed and Defense . But it, as always, depends on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> There's a pair of Pure sisters in my first game who would likely each have one of these weapons, effectively being able to take one character out of a battle entirely or severely disable two.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious lesson here being: &quot;If someone is lopping off your body parts you have already reached time for the Killing Form.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T20:00:26-08:00","id":1285463,"title":"","content":"Ok, question: is there a Gift that adjusts physical age in much the same way that gender altered? (per the Wolf Gift) [Assumption: doing so neither reduces nor extends total lifespan.]<br /> <br /> If nothing printed exists, what would you suggest as the spirit source for teaching such a gift? Time spirit, ok--what else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T20:57:52-08:00","id":1285469,"title":"","content":"a spirit of youth, one of age, or even a spirit of BIRTHDAYS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T21:05:35-08:00","id":1285470,"title":"","content":"You could probably just have a fetish that does that. I'll put one in the fetish thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:10:17-08:00","id":1285568,"title":"","content":"Riding on the coattails of that last question-answer pairing, are there any solid guidelines on whether any given effect should be designed as a Gift, a Rite, or a Fetish?<br /> <br /> For instance, say I wanted a werewolf to summon a blizzard. That seems like a werewolfy thing to do. I could see maybe a Fetish that modifies the Cunning Facet of the Gift of Elements (or basically any Facet of Weather's), or a Wolf Rite that, after an hour of supplication to the spirits of winter, covers the Uratha's territory in the Blizzard and Extreme Cold Tilts, or even as the Glory Facet to a new Gift of Frost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:37:47-08:00","id":1285592,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>. That answers the question (no Gift) and suggests solutions. Also, finding spirits like that sounds... not easy. Which is good!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. I'll look in the fetish thread later as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:24:02-08:00","id":1286189,"title":"","content":"The Blood Talons' sacred prey is other werewolves<br /> What do they mean when they say &quot;creepy dead bastards do half our work for us&quot; about Vampires, when vampires are equally likely to be hostile to/ not care about any werewolf, proper Forsaken, Improper ones, Pure, or Bale Corgis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:00:53-08:00","id":1286213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1286189#post1286189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blood Talons' sacred prey is other werewolves<br /> What do they mean when they say &quot;creepy dead bastards do half our work for us&quot; about Vampires, when vampires are equally likely to be hostile to/ not care about any werewolf, proper Forsaken, Improper ones, Pure, or Bale Corgis</div> </div> </div> </div>It's referring to the vampires as prey, they are already dead, so they did half the work for the Blood Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:09:17-08:00","id":1286215,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it means that they take care of the pure on the social level of things. the blood talons work is not about vampire but other werewolves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:42:37-08:00","id":1286220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1286215#post1286215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it means that they take care of the pure on the social level of things. the blood talons work is not about vampire but other werewolves</div> </div> </div> </div>In some folklore, vampires are undead werewolves. But Blood Talons aren't confined to just killing werewolves anyways, and are free to use vampires as prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:44:35-08:00","id":1286221,"title":"","content":"I suppose so. but being dead in the sense they are does make me think of doing half the work for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T03:52:08-08:00","id":1289140,"title":"","content":"Can a Shadowbind ritual bind a Claimed, Possessed or Urged human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:47:54-08:00","id":1289186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1289140#post1289140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Shadowbind ritual bind a Claimed, Possessed or Urged human?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, though if you had the person there it could probably be used to bind the spirit Possessing or Urging them. Since such spirits are either sharing the same space with them, while Possessing, or fairly nearby, when Urging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T08:50:30-07:00","id":1297734,"title":"","content":"This question might have been asked before, but do you think that high defense is too broken? Taking in consinderation that in Dalu-Gauru-Urshul applies on firearms as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T09:24:35-07:00","id":1297741,"title":"","content":"It's a highly subjective question. I personally say no.<br /> Attack dice pools and Defense are both calculated through combining two traits, but the former is much easier to increase than the latter. Especially melee attack dice pools already have built in increases in various forms while Defense may only increase through shapeshifting if you have more Wits than Dex. Willpower adds more to attacks than Defense, and there are many more Facets that boosts attack dice pools than Defense (and one that decreases the opponent's Defense).<br /> It's possible to create a character with insane Defense, but that's just minmaxing.<br /> If you really want to be invincible, you can Dodge with an insane dice pool as long as you have a pretty good Defense rating, but then you're also unable to do virtually anything else that turn. It merely prolongs combat unless you have allies that can deal with the threat for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-18-2019, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:22:14-07:00","id":1299394,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this question was already addressed in this thread but I have a question regarding calculating a characters height and weight in each of his five forms, as I was reading through the section on the forms in the Werewolf 2nd Ed book, I noticed that they were really vague when it came to the Height/Weight changes in certain forms, for example it said that when in Dalu form the character grows to 150% body mass, I am unclear as to what this means for an exact increase in height and Weight? A Werewolf in Gauru form would weigh almost four times his Hishu form and stand 1.5 times taller so that a 5'8&quot; 150 lb werewolf in Hishu would grow to 8'6&quot; and 600 lbs in Gauru, would this be a correct assessment? It also says that a werewolf in Urshul form has 2 times the body mass of his Hishu form and a shoulder height equal to her Hishu form. Would that mean that one would multiply the Hishu weight of the character by two? Also, how would one calculate a persons height at the shoulder? It also gives no measurement at all for height/weight in Urhan form. Does this mean one should just use the average height/weight listed for a the common Timber Wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","user":"Darklander","date":". 03-24-2019, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:32:23-07:00","id":1299429,"title":"","content":"As you noticed they're vague, but that's more on purpose. Some people like being more hulking caveman while others might prefer more sleek but muscular like Tarzan. Mass isn't weight but it seems a pretty fair way to go about it for the humanoid forms. The Giant Merit, which gives you Size 6 (like Dalu) is described as, 'Your character is massive. She\u2019s well over six feet tall, and crowds part when she approaches.' I generally have it go between 6'6 and 7'11. You got Gauru, it's pretty easy, weighing 4x your Hishu weight, and x1.5 your Hishu height, so someone who is 5'10 and 170 in Hishu form would be 8'9&quot; and (almost) 680 lbs. You put on a lot of muscle there.<br /> <br /> When it says your shoulder height is equal to your Hishu form, that's because a wolf (or most quadrupeds in general) are measured to their shoulder (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withers\" target=\"_blank\">the withers</a>), since it's the highest point of the body (some animals stretch their head higher, but others keep them low). So your Hishu at 5'8&quot; would have an Urshul form that's 5'8&quot; at the shoulder, as described the rest of it is pretty horse-like in size. I think if you use mass as weight here you get a really lean animal, though, practically skinny, so you might want to beef that up a bit.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Withers.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>The circled part would be at 5'8&quot; for your werewolf.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And yeah using average height and weight for a wolf makes sense for Urhan. Though obviously some people might choose the Giant or Small-Framed Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-24-2019, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:07:53-07:00","id":1299446,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification nofather but I think I need to clarify one thing which I am quoting from the book:<br /> &quot;Urshul is a beast of legend. It looks the part of a wolf, but with<br /> the size of a horse. It\u2019s double the body mass of the Hishu form,<br /> and its shoulders stand at the same height her human shoulders do.&quot;<br /> <br /> As it says that an Urshul form werewolf's shoulders stand at the same height as her Hishu form shoulders, so considering that humans measure height to the top of the head, wouldn't one subtract the measurement of the head and neck to find how high the characters shoulders are off the ground in Hishu form?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:46:54-07:00","id":1299458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1299446#post1299446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it says that an Urshul form werewolf's shoulders stand at the same height as her Hishu form shoulders, so considering that humans measure height to the top of the head, wouldn't one subtract the measurement of the head and neck to find how high the characters shoulders are off the ground in Hishu form?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, I got that one wrong. Subtracting a head in height seems the best way to go about it, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:53:36-07:00","id":1301439,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, bit of a really stupid question because I need this for a totally different game, but, I value the Werewolf priorities on the portrayal of Luna and Helios more than what might fit better for, uh, archmage, but I have a situation where a player's archmage wants to bring down the gauntlet for an entire country and is going to try and talk to Luna and Helios and negotiate so they don't retaliate.<br /> <br /> How should they react? My gut is that Luna will be willing to discuss it depending on her mood, and that Helios will flat out say &quot;NO!&quot; So yeah, simple question, maybe complicated answers.<br /> <br /> Someone wants to bring down the gauntlet for a set area, how will Luna and Helios react?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:08:02-07:00","id":1301444,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind this person is basically asking to kill an entire country and expose the supernatural to the world in an incredibly gross way, so there might be more forces involved (Exarchs, for instance, don't like this stuff).<br /> <br /> But otherwise yes, Helios would not want it, Luna might be open to it. They might be able to sidestep Helios by having it happen at nighttime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:11:59-07:00","id":1301447,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, there will be Hubris...! I just needed to know how Helios and Luna will... participate. Thanks~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T11:13:03-07:00","id":1302606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1301439#post1301439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is going to try and talk to Luna and Helios and negotiate so they don't retaliate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule out the possibility of actually talking to them, as &quot;spirits of this rank are almost never seen in person, preferring to make their lairs in deep, protected Places-That-Aren't, and are too powerful for the world of Flesh to support them - they can't cross the Gauntlet. Their servant <i>umia </i>enact their will across the <i>Hisil.</i>&quot; (WtF 2e, 181)<br /> <br /> Nothing stopping you from dealing with their spirit servants though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T12:00:34-07:00","id":1302610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost-His-Mind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1302606#post1302606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rule out the possibility of actually talking to them, as &amp;quot;spirits of this rank are almost never seen in person, preferring to make their lairs in deep, protected Places-That-Aren't, and are too powerful for the world of Flesh to support them - they can't cross the Gauntlet. Their servant <i>umia </i>enact their will across the <i>Hisil.</i>&amp;quot; (WtF 2e, 181)<br /> <br /> Nothing stopping you from dealing with their spirit servants though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages can actually get an actual audience, but its not a smart idea. The jerks can get up to like honorary rank 9. Even so, my player had to negotiate with Helions as proxies and got the best he got was Helios agreeing to not kill him on principle in exchange for a massive tithe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T09:41:25-07:00","id":1305074,"title":"","content":"Maybe someone has already addressed the issue, however, anyone has hints about how put together a pack for a chronicle? Especially if you want to give total freedom to players in the characters creation step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T09:46:49-07:00","id":1305075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1305074#post1305074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone has already addressed the issue, however, anyone has hints about how put together a pack for a chronicle? Especially if you want to give total freedom to players in the characters creation step.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character creation section in the core is pretty good for that. Each player can also make 1 wolf-blooded, or 1-3 humans as supporting characters (in addition to their werewolf), and they collaborate on the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2019, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:31:03-07:00","id":1306605,"title":"","content":"So a Waystone Wolf-Blooded acts as a one dot locus.<br /> <br /> Could you actually improve that rating same as any other locus, and if so, how fucked up is that kid going to end up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T08:13:31-07:00","id":1307761,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s that Lodge that Helps people that made terrible deals with Sprits,Far,demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:32:12-07:00","id":1307778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1307761#post1307761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s that Lodge that Helps people that made terrible deals with Sprits,Far,demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of the Broken Pledge, from Signs of the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:53:35-07:00","id":1307786,"title":"","content":"Thanks A lot .<br /> <br /> They\u2019d Have a Interesting relationship With The Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:16:31-07:00","id":1307793,"title":"","content":"Guys!<br /> How you would depict the act to step inside the Shadow Realm to your players? I mean the characters just fade from the material word (maybe just like a teleport)? Or a portal opens (maybe something made of mist) and they cross it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:21:57-07:00","id":1307794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1307793#post1307793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys!<br /> How you would depict the act to step inside the Shadow Realm to your players? I mean the characters just fade from the material word (maybe just like a teleport)? Or a portal opens (maybe something made of mist) and they cross it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely more of the fade, I think they disappear the moment it happens, then linger in the Gauntlet for a bit before fading into existence in the Shadow. There's abilities that do the portal thing, like Gauntlet Breach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-25-2019, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T04:48:45-07:00","id":1308004,"title":"","content":"I depict it as the character seeming to walk round a corner that isn't there - physically moving out of sight, slipping out of vision in a way that makes a human viewer feel queasy or spooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T11:59:33-07:00","id":1310783,"title":"","content":"I got a simple question - <b>If spirit is on Flesh over Gauntlet, and is Materialized - can Uratha do it physical damage with their claws and jaws?</b> <i>Especially</i>, as Materialized Spirit is Elemental of Fire, i.e. spirit is living flame in Flesh. Can Uratha hit with their claws the living flame body of Elemental? ( Character <b>do not</b> have Bone Shadows Siskur-Dah blessing now. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-08-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T12:38:15-07:00","id":1310790,"title":"","content":"Yes, though it wouldn't be a flame like a campfire flame. It might appear that way but there would be more substance to it. It's a living entity, not an image (which would be done via the Sign or Hallucination Numina or potentially the Image Manifestation). P190, 'The spirit has shifted from ephemeral to material substance, Manifesting in physical form. All the rules for ephemeral spirit\u2019s traits still apply <i>except for the effects of being in Twilight</i>. This Condition protects the spirit from Essence bleed for its duration.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2019, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:23:40-07:00","id":1310859,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s that Werewolf or Bluebook That ends with Sections on various animals and there Mystical and Symbolic Meaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T19:41:26-07:00","id":1310889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1310859#post1310859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s that Werewolf or Bluebook That ends with Sections on various animals and there Mystical and Symbolic Meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/12402/World-of-Darkness-Skinchangers?affiliate_id=386172\" target=\"_blank\">Skinchangers.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T19:42:24-07:00","id":1310890,"title":"","content":"It was Skin!-<br /> <br /> Oh. Ninja'd by Nof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T02:41:24-07:00","id":1310949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1310783#post1310783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Can Uratha hit with their claws the living flame body of Elemental?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T12:25:33-07:00","id":1311031,"title":"","content":"If you had to rethink the principle on which Gauntlet Strength worked, what would you build upon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T15:53:12-07:00","id":1313925,"title":"","content":"We have two books about wtf2, core book and the pack.<br /> We have already several examples from those books about forsaken/pure mixed packs (australia right?) or hunting grounds with weird alliances ( ivory claws/iron masters, in Thailand, from the pack right?), or places where the two factions do not kill each other at sight.<br /> Also in Dark Eras is suggested that the pure and the forsaken can bond together in front of huge problems, enough to allow the pure to be playable.<br /> <br /> I can't remember about something like this in the first edition.<br /> How common can be this kind of scenario? <br /> The books seems to suggest it more than once. Of course I'm not talking about ''friendship'' between the two spiritual/ideological factions, but more about some kind of non aggression pact because of a particulary situation in the hunting ground, or because of a weird spiritual resonance ( in australia I read something about blood talons and predator kings running together because the land resemble Pangea)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T01:47:45-07:00","id":1314010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1313925#post1313925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember about something like this in the first edition.<br /> How common can be this kind of scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>As common as you want it to be. 2nd edition takes the view that the world is large and tribes aren\u2019t monoliths. Local culture, needs, and expectations will play a big part in forming the microcosm of any given hunting ground. Sometimes there\u2019s reason for Forsaken and Pure to put aside differences to achieve some other goal. Other times there isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> The Australian hunting ground has Forsaken and Pure in the same lodge (not packs) because their ancient expectations and wide open spaces mean more than hatred because some distant Wolf spirits say so. Rome has Ivory Claws and Iron Masters working side by side in an empire-spanning protectorate to enforce their interests across the world, and Germanic tribes starting to see that they may need to adopt the same tactics to counter the Roman legions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T06:09:38-07:00","id":1314046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1311031#post1311031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had to rethink the principle on which Gauntlet Strength worked, what would you build upon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three possible ideas spring to mind for me:<br /> <br /> 1. Spiritual activity. Places where there is already a lot of interaction between the two realms, whether in the form of entities crossing over, spirits using Reaching powers, Rites, or anyone tinkering around with their scrap of occult knowledge, results in a thinning of the Gauntlet. It's like picking at a scab and never letting it heal.<br /> <br /> 2. Shifting Resonance. The Gauntlet is much thinner in locations where Resonance is constantly changing type, rather than building up a steady flow over time, such as in densely packed urban areas or an environment with unpredictable weather patterns. It's like the Gauntlet is a living organism that constantly has to readapt itself to local conditions.<br /> <br /> 3. Barrens. Places where, for whatever reason, there is a lack of natural Essence flow causes the Gauntlet to weaken and crumble. It's like keeping someone weak by denying them sustenance.<br /> <br /> All of these, of course, have all sorts of implications for the setting, and so I guess it depends on why one would desire to change the principle on which Gauntlet Strength works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T07:10:57-07:00","id":1314061,"title":"","content":"I don't think I would change the Gauntlet; my first idea was to base it more on the Border Marches, but the Border Marches was quite closely based on the Gauntlet in terms of Depth/Strength. No, what I would do is I'd change how Essence is transferred across the Gauntlet since the current system meshes badly with the intended setting. Right now Gauntlet Strength only penalises a Power+Finesse roll to draw as much Essence across the Gauntlet as you can handle. Not only should most spirits have no trouble sustaining themselves, the most powerful spirits would gain the most Essence through Resonance alone. The Shadow as an ecology idea doesn't work when the rules as written would create such a top heavy abundance of Essence to go around.<br /> <br /> So, what I'd change is that I'd actually have Gauntlet Strength throttle/cap the amount of Essence that can pass through rather than merely penalising it.<br /> Edit: I'd also provide some rules for the natural Essence flow. Right now we're only told that Essence flows through the Gauntlet but no system for engaging with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-24-2019, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T07:35:24-07:00","id":1314068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1314061#post1314061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now Gauntlet Strength only penalises a Power+Finesse roll to draw as much Essence across the Gauntlet as you can handle. Not only should most spirits have no trouble sustaining themselves, the most powerful spirits would gain the most Essence through Resonance alone. The Shadow as an ecology idea doesn't work when the rules as written would create such a top heavy abundance of Essence to go around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea behind spirits' Essence economy is that harvesting produces more limited gains than theft and tithing. Powerful spirits having more Essence with which to influence and gradually reshape other spirits is working as intended; nobody at the top is taking collections for survival alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T10:06:06-07:00","id":1314314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1314068#post1314068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea behind spirits' Essence economy is that harvesting produces more limited gains than theft and tithing. Powerful spirits having more Essence with which to influence and gradually reshape other spirits is working as intended; nobody at the top is taking collections for survival alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that harvesting produces extreme amounts of Essence for anyone who's strong enough to demand tithes, and tithes comes from those spirits that have the least possibilities of gaining Essence. That's not an ecology as described in the book. Disrupting the Shadow ecology is supposed to destabilise the spirit ecology, but if you remove one spirit you'll at most disrupt a chain in the tithe system, which doesn't have any negative effects of note since some low-Ranking spirits won't have to pay tithe temporarily (until another link is forged) and the higher Ranking spirit have no actual need for that tithe since harvesting should be more than enough to keep it sated.<br /> Expending on the rules as written, it's not an easily disturbed ecology that Uratha needs to carefully police, unlike how it's described in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T10:30:48-07:00","id":1314322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1314314#post1314314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the higher Ranking spirit have no actual need for that tithe since harvesting should be more than enough to keep it sated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because, again, the things at the top aren't looking for satiation alone. They're managing agendas that necessitate they pay off other spirits to handle tasks for them, and they get better returns on that by cycling their lessers' Essence into their own and back and keeping the environment dog-eat-dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:10:52-07:00","id":1314504,"title":"","content":"No, I get that. My problem with it is that the book describes it both as an economy run by powerful spirits in a court system <i>and</i> an ecology that can easily be toppled by a careless pack of Uratha killing the wrong spirit. As the rules are written only the former can be true. Disrupt a link at the bottom of the food chain and the ripples should subside quickly rather than be significant and possibly dangerous all the way to the top since the predators higher up can just eat from the same overabundance of plants as everyone else (and actually gain more nutrients than lower links) rather than risk starvation for lack of prey.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the tithe/court system, but I think it should be combined with an actual scarcity of Essence trickling through the Gauntlet, or at least not make it dependent on the spirit's own stats since it allows for some spirits to gain more Essence from a Resonant Condition of their own making than it cost to apply it across the Gauntlet while still remaining in the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T22:01:15-07:00","id":1314887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1314504#post1314504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I get that. My problem with it is that the book describes it both as an economy run by powerful spirits in a court system <i>and</i> an ecology that can easily be toppled by a careless pack of Uratha killing the wrong spirit. As the rules are written only the former can be true. Disrupt a link at the bottom of the food chain and the ripples should subside quickly rather than be significant and possibly dangerous all the way to the top since the predators higher up can just eat from the same overabundance of plants as everyone else (and actually gain more nutrients than lower links) rather than risk starvation for lack of prey.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the tithe/court system, but I think it should be combined with an actual scarcity of Essence trickling through the Gauntlet, or at least not make it dependent on the spirit's own stats since it allows for some spirits to gain more Essence from a Resonant Condition of their own making than it cost to apply it across the Gauntlet while still remaining in the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, in turn, is more a matter of how the narrative ways in which the Shadow is an ecology can't really translate fully into mechanics without making the systems for Essence and Resonance way more granular than can be justified for a widget that exists to explain how a category of NPC stays fed and active: All that Essence moving around has an impact on the spirits who partake of it, and power vacuums don't last long without something new making a grab for freshly-vacant prime real estate.<br /> <br /> As others have observed before, the Shadow is an ecology of the sort where the introduction of wolves changes the way the rivers flow \u2014 it's not so much &quot;toppling&quot; as &quot;re-forming,&quot; and you can't really get into the fine-slicing detail work of defining what changes when the up-and-coming spirit of the new corner store gets fed to the burgeoning colossus made of astroturf, gentrification, and crooked zoning laws in any way that wouldn't be managed faster by knowing who's in bed with whom as far as the local descants go.<br /> <br /> Essence impacts the Shadow as an ecology because it's the primary currency the power dynamics run on and the main thing that shapes its predominant actors, but the mechanics can't really compel the interactions spirits are stated to engage in regularly without getting a lot more weird and fiddly than the framework is set up to account for, short of making &quot;ephemeral beings can give other ephemeral beings of the same type Essence without a special ability&quot; textual and introducing some kind of keyword system for Resonance beyond the bounds of Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-28-2019, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T18:57:50-07:00","id":1315063,"title":"","content":"Regarding Influences, a spirit with Influence 4 can permanently create anything in its purview, there is a limit of 1 item and a cost to the duration, but not on max size or complexity ? So the spirit of a boat harbor can create a bleeding edge warship, a road spirit can create one connecting any two points, a spirit of art can create a statue the size of a skyscraper to squish its enemies and a chess spirit create an entire tower (rook in modern chess) or elephant (bishop in medieval chess ) ? <br /> <br /> Granted that to even get to that Rank they would have developed the intelligence not to do something so overt. But if desperate, can they go crazy like that ? In other words, leveraging their ban or diplomacy are the common ways to stop their shenanigans, correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-28-2019, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T20:45:23-07:00","id":1315076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1315063#post1315063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Influences, a spirit with Influence 4 can permanently create anything in its purview,</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence 5 is required for permanent creation. The dots on the Influence Durations chart are added to the dots on the Influence Effects chart and compared to the spirit's dots in the Influence to determine its possibility. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there is a limit of 1 item and a cost to the duration, but not on max size or complexity ? </div> </div> </div>I think it's safe to say that without getting into bizarre side ventures like magath and hive-claimed, Ensahim and Dihim work their Influences with reference to the typical bounds of their concepts and the things that gave them that Influence. Some flexibility of scale might be managed to account for powerful spirits tending to be larger than weaker spirits, but the comparative rarity of single-concept spirits above the Rank of Ensihim means Influence 5 takes some building towards even at Rank 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted that to even get to that Rank they would have developed the intelligence not to do something so overt. But if desperate, can they go crazy like that ? In other words, leveraging their ban or diplomacy are the common ways to stop their shenanigans, correct ? </div> </div> </div>If desperate, they're some of the strongest beings in the Shadow even before getting Numina involved, to say nothing of the social and territorial resources they often have at their disposal. Influence is generally a geopolitical tool at that level, and it doesn't take scale-breaking manifestations of spiritual might for &quot;make lasting sources of Resonance&quot; a potent expression of their primordial selfhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T08:50:33-07:00","id":1315189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1315076#post1315076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influence 5 is required for permanent creation. The dots on the Influence Durations chart are added to the dots on the Influence Effects chart and compared to the spirit's dots in the Influence to determine its possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification: Mass Create is required for permanent creations as an option to the regular effect. The duration chart doesn't factor in unless the entity happens to have 8 dots in its Influence (4 for Create and 4 for permanent duration in the chart). Since statted entities stop at Rank 5 only Strengthen can reach permanent duration through the duration chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T08:53:03-07:00","id":1315191,"title":"","content":"Ok, that makes a lot more sense. So a permanent creation would need effect level 4 + duration level 4 = 8 influence. But at that point, you are in the level of Luna, Helios or some other world class power with Imperial Magic levels of might, so random stuff appearing is the least of your worries.<br /> <br /> But it does mean a Rank 4 could probably conjure an object up for a couple of minutes, which is still quite powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T08:58:18-07:00","id":1315194,"title":"","content":"As long as it hasn't split its Influence dots in multiple Influences with neither reaching four dots. As Rank 4 it would have 14-24 as a base dice pool, gaining one minute per success rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T09:06:39-07:00","id":1315198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1315191#post1315191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that makes a lot more sense. So a permanent creation would need effect level 4 + duration level 4 = 8 influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>If not for the specific inclusion of permanent singular instances of the Influence in Mass Create, yes; I brought up the Duration chart because I thought the fact that permanence was listed at four (additional) dots on that chart might have been confounding the reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T10:45:22-07:00","id":1315894,"title":"","content":"Got some next simple question - <b>What happens when Pure Tribes pack lose suddenly their super Totem?</b> I mean disappearance of Totem in the context of 'one nigh, our Totem vanished'. Is this stops any pack related bonuses? The Uratha of Pure start to treat each other as alien werewolves, from mechanical stand point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T11:49:16-07:00","id":1315900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1315894#post1315894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got some next simple question - <b>What happens when Pure Tribes pack lose suddenly their super Totem?</b> I mean disappearance of Totem in the context of 'one nigh, our Totem vanished'. Is this stops any pack related bonuses? The Uratha of Pure start to treat each other as alien werewolves, from mechanical stand point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether they're still getting their bonuses would be a big indicator of their totem being alive and separate, or destroyed or confined (as in a fetish). Presumably they would perform a hunt to find what happened, its really hard to make a powerful spirit disappear without anyone knowing anything about it. If the spirit is confined they'd likely try to free it, if it's dead to kill the perpetrators and find a spirit to replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T21:05:42-07:00","id":1316553,"title":"","content":"Does entering Basu-Im count as entering Gauru form for the scene? That is, if, for some reason, I end Basu-Im and still are on the same scene, can I get into Gauru form again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:58:22-07:00","id":1316581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1316553#post1316553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does entering Basu-Im count as entering Gauru form for the scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1316553#post1316553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, if, for some reason, I end Basu-Im and still are on the same scene, can I get into Gauru form again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once Basu-Im ends you collapse and you\u2019re pretty much out of the rest of that scene. You might crawl away, or your pack mates might carry you, but the scene is over for your character and you won\u2019t be retaking Gauru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T02:26:56-07:00","id":1317142,"title":"","content":"So, I was reading the rules for building The Pack as a character, in &quot;The Pack&quot; and I got a little confused about the &quot;Populating the Pack&quot; rule in page 22. There is a table where the players spend 10 points each in characters to populate the pack and one of the Character Types was &quot;Supernatural Creatures 6+&quot; and I'm trying to understand what the 6+ means, anyone has a clue?<br /> <br /> And in the same table there is &quot;Average Dice Pool&quot; for each type of character that ranges from 1 to 20 depending on the type, but below the table there is a part that says that each character has a dice of 5, 4 and 3. How should I consider then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","user":"jclepf","date":". 06-08-2019, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","name":"jclepf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T04:40:11-07:00","id":1317156,"title":"","content":"You\u2019ve referenced it in your second paragraph. The column heading is \u2018Average Dice Pool\u2019 and two paragraphs before the table says \u201cThe table gives a rough guide to power level based on dice pool to help Storytellers gauge how much individual characters should cost.\u201d<br /> <br /> IT helps in two directions. When you\u2019re adding a character to the story using those rules and you have an idea what size dice pool it has on average for actions, you can figure out how much it should cost. Or if you have a rough idea of the kind of character it is (human, spirit, supernatural) but you don\u2019t know how many dice it should be rolling in the story, the table is a guide.<br /> <br /> I have no idea where you\u2019re getting \u20181 to 20 from\u2019. The only range on that table is 3-5, and five rows have a number with a +. There\u2019s no 1 to 20.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: It appears that an older version of the book has formatting issues with this table. My version doesn't have those, apologies for therefore misunderstanding your question.</i><br /> <br /> The paragraph below the table refers to \u2018everyone else\u2019. If the characters add a character from their pool of points (or the ST does), use the table as a guide for the dice pool it\u2019s going to roll if necessary (though it should be rare). Anyone else who is just a random character who won\u2019t appear again rolls either 5, 4 or 3 dice, depending on whether this is a strength of theirs, is just something they can kinda do, or is something they\u2019re not very good at. Again, actually rolling dice during the Zakmur-Dah is meant to be rare.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 06-08-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T05:25:47-07:00","id":1317161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317156#post1317156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea where you\u2019re getting \u20181 to 20 from\u2019. The only range on that table is 3-5, and five rows have a number with a +. There\u2019s no 1 to 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is why dice pools (ranging from 1 for some to 20 for others) are immediately simplified to 5/4/3 in the text immediately following the table. I get what's intended now that you've explained, but I too was confused when I first read the text since &quot;secondary actors&quot; in the context seems to refer to everyone except Uratha; i.e. almost everyone on the table above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317142#post1317142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a table where the players spend 10 points each in characters to populate the pack and one of the Character Types was &quot;Supernatural Creatures 6+&quot; and I'm trying to understand what the 6+ means, anyone has a clue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural creatures 6+ is just a formatting error. &quot;6+&quot; is supposed to be their dice pool. Just shift all numbers one column to the right, or download an updated copy from the store.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T06:27:47-07:00","id":1317169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317161#post1317161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural creatures 6+ is just a formatting error. &quot;6+&quot; is supposed to be their dice pool. Just shift all numbers one column to the right, or download an updated copy from the store.</div> </div> </div> </div>My version doesn't have any formatting issues with that table, but I take it from your post that an older version does have some, which I presume explains the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T07:34:02-07:00","id":1317179,"title":"","content":"Well, jclepf's version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T09:54:38-07:00","id":1317368,"title":"","content":"Is there a symbol, rune or any kind of First Tongue sign/sigil for Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T17:50:26-07:00","id":1317460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317368#post1317368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a symbol, rune or any kind of First Tongue sign/sigil for Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The canon First Tongue name for Essence is &quot;ulal&quot;, if that's what you're referring to. Otherwise, I have not seen any canon representation of Essence as a sign, glyph or otherwise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:09:14-07:00","id":1317559,"title":"","content":"Is it possibile to have a version of contact/allies/retainer/mentor ecc.. with spirits?<br /> How can i price them fairly, retainer in particular?<br /> The only official rule that i can find is the +1 cost for ghouls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T08:36:04-07:00","id":1317585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317559#post1317559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only official rule that i can find is the +1 cost for ghouls</div> </div> </div> </div>The official rule is that they gain Discipline dots depending on how many dots of the Merit you've bought, not that they cost more XP.<br /> <br /> Afaik there are no rules on the subject other than the extra bit given to ghoul retainers. You'll have to house rule. For spirit retainers you could have them have Influence dots equal to the number of Discipline dots given to a ghoul of the same rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T12:50:19-07:00","id":1317657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1317585#post1317585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The official rule is that they gain Discipline dots depending on how many dots of the Merit you've bought, not that they cost more XP.<br /> <br /> Afaik there are no rules on the subject other than the extra bit given to ghoul retainers. You'll have to house rule. For spirit retainers you could have them have Influence dots equal to the number of Discipline dots given to a ghoul of the same rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t know why i remembered an extra cost, my bad.<br /> So having a minor or major splat npc as a social merit cost the same, probably because of the extra &quot;maintenance&quot; you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T19:44:29-07:00","id":1320043,"title":"","content":"What happens to equipment when a Uratha crosses over to Hisil? What about electronic equipment? I don't recall that being stated anywhere on the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T19:51:25-07:00","id":1320044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1320043#post1320043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to equipment when a Uratha crosses over to Hisil? What about electronic equipment? I don't recall that being stated anywhere on the book</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition, you needed to use a rite to allow it to cross over with you. In second edition your stuff just goes with you. I think metaphysically it becomes ephemeral but that isn't really relevant.<br /> <br /> I think it would come back okay, but obviously you would have issues using it in the other world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T20:08:40-07:00","id":1320046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1320044#post1320044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first edition, you needed to use a rite to allow it to cross over with you. In second edition your stuff just goes with you. I think metaphysically it becomes ephemeral but that isn't really relevant.<br /> <br /> I think it would come back okay, but obviously you would have issues using it in the other world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, the question was more in the vein of confirmation. I know that it used to need the &quot;dedication&quot; rite, but that isn't on 2E, so I figured it would cross over, just not functional","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T03:18:14-07:00","id":1320070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1320043#post1320043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to equipment when a Uratha crosses over to Hisil? What about electronic equipment? I don't recall that being stated anywhere on the book</div> </div> </div> </div><b>WtF </b>2E, page 96 - 'BELONGINGS<br /> At Harmony 9 or above, the character\u2019s clothes and belongings do not shift with her. Below that, assume her clothing and immediate possessions shift with her, subsuming into her body in Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan form, or stretching to fit Dalu, whatever makes the most sense for the scene.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-22-2019, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T03:24:23-07:00","id":1320071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1320070#post1320070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>WtF </b>2E, page 97 - 'BELONGINGS <br /> At Harmony 9 or above, the character\u2019s clothes and belongings do not shift with her. Below that, assume her clothing and immediate possessions shift with her, subsuming into her body in Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan form, or stretching to fit Dalu, whatever makes the most sense for the scene.'</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s on p.96 and has nothing to do with the question asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 06-22-2019, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T03:30:17-07:00","id":1320072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1320043#post1320043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to equipment when a Uratha crosses over to Hisil? What about electronic equipment? I don't recall that being stated anywhere on the book</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything comes with the Uratha - within reason and up to the Storyteller if the player is trying to push it too far.<br /> <br /> But just because the equipment comes with the character doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019ll work as expected. Electronic equipment might run self contained, eg. you could use your phone to record notes but not to make phone calls. It\u2019s also possible that spirits of a thing, or spirits compatible with its resonance, may be able to scent it and flock to the location to consume the item and take in its pure essence. (Which could be small \u2018e\u2019 or capital \u2018E\u2019 depending on how the ST wants to run it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T11:08:24-07:00","id":1321617,"title":"","content":"the Wolf-Blooded Tell - &quot;Anger Issues&quot; says that the WB is &quot;affected by a specific Kuruth trigger.&quot; I need some help understanding the scope of this statement. Does this mean that the WB is affected by the &quot;Specific&quot; level of a single type of trigger (ie specifically swallowing human blood) or does this mean that the WB is affected by all aspects of a single trigger (ie Smelling, tasting OR swallowing human blood)<br /> <br /> Main reason for the confusion being that since WBs don't have Harmony, there's no good explanation for how to use the different levels of Kuruth trigger, but also many of the &quot;specific&quot; level triggers don't really apply to WBs (Moon doesn't really apply at all, but having to specifically swallow human blood seems like almost a non-issue for a Wolf-Blood since it's only really going to happen with intent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T18:58:13-07:00","id":1321683,"title":"","content":"The way I read it is that it's a specific level of a Kuruth trigger.<br /> <br /> If this is an issue, homebrewing a trigger would certainly work in this instance, and there's a forum page with a bunch of other homebrew triggers that you could take a look at (I think the page title is &quot;Some New Kuruth Triggers&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T00:47:28-07:00","id":1321698,"title":"","content":"The WB gains a specific level trigger. If a given trigger doesn\u2019t make sense for a WB, don\u2019t allow it or modify it to make sense. You could alter Moon to either be when you hear a werewolf howl regardless of moon phase - which is harsh but could work in a game - or you could assign the WB an auspice she resonates with and that\u2019s the one that\u2019s associated with the trigger.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: Swallowing human blood doesn\u2019t say it has to be someone else\u2019s. I\u2019d be very comfortable with ruling that a WB with that tell who gets smacked in the mouth hard enough to draw blood is going to lose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T12:26:05-07:00","id":1321759,"title":"","content":"thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> - that was the clarification I needed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:49:10-07:00","id":1324019,"title":"","content":"Are snake Hosts detailed anywhere? In 1e or 2e. Shunned by the Moon adds a lot of really cool new hosts, and then mentions &quot;the rare snake Hosts,&quot; which of course piqued my curiosity.<br /> <br /> Definitely possible they're being saved for potential future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T12:43:57-07:00","id":1324034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1324019#post1324019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are snake Hosts detailed anywhere? In 1e or 2e. Shunned by the Moon adds a lot of really cool new hosts, and then mentions &amp;quot;the rare snake Hosts,&amp;quot; which of course piqued my curiosity.<br /> <br /> Definitely possible they're being saved for potential future books.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, in 1e. If I remember correctly, they were in Predators, but I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T14:13:34-07:00","id":1324044,"title":"","content":"They are in Predators, as one of the 'hidden hosts' that aren't as well known. The mystery extends to the write-up, however, and I don't know if I'd say they were really 'detailed.' While there is an example one, it hides their motives and asks you to come up with one on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T04:36:54-07:00","id":1324413,"title":"","content":"Reading the WtF core, there is no hard cap of 10 on Willpower for Werewolves, but the Zeal facet of the Gift of Fervor states that &quot;<i>Zeal allows a werewolf\u2019s Willpower to go above 10.</i>&quot; Isn't that redundant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Clarifiying the question. 07-14-2019, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T05:19:42-07:00","id":1324420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1324413#post1324413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the core there seem to be hard cap of 10 on Willpower, but the Zeal facet of the Gift of Fervor states that &amp;quot;Zeal allows a werewolf\u2019s Willpower to go above 10.&amp;quot; Isn't that redundant?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? How is it redundant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T06:22:22-07:00","id":1324436,"title":"","content":"It's not redundant the way Ibeaumanior phrased it (perhaps there should've been a &quot;doesn't&quot; in there in case they're referring to WtF core and not CofD).<br /> It is, however, a stealth errata because because as far as I can tell the only mention of the ten dot limit (for beings other than ephemeral entities) in all of second edition is hidden away in the lexicon of the CofD book, the book that deals with mortals. By RAW, werewolves and other splats did not have a ten dot limit, and RAI has been heavily disputed up until now that we have an explicit exception that confirms that the rule does in fact exist, at least for Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-14-2019, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T06:31:30-07:00","id":1324440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1324420#post1324420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No? How is it redundant?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1324436#post1324436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not redundant the way Ibeaumanior phrased it (perhaps there should've been a &quot;doesn't&quot; in there in case they're referring to WtF core and not CofD).<br /> It is, however, a stealth errata because because as far as I can tell the only mention of the ten dot limit (for beings other than ephemeral entities) in all of second edition is hidden away in the lexicon of the CofD book, the book that deals with mortals. By RAW, werewolves and other splats did not have a ten dot limit, and RAI has been heavily disputed up until now that we have an explicit exception that confirms that the rule does in fact exist, at least for Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> thanks for pointing that error. I will edit my post to make it more clear.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Yes, ephemeral entities are supposed to have a limit of 10 on willpower, Werewolves and other supers are not limited (RAW). I want to know if it was either a mistake in the Night horrors or an omission in the Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-14-2019, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:02:43-07:00","id":1324447,"title":"","content":"When I read that part in SbtM I assumed it meant the ten dot rule was only an omission in the core book but now that you bring it up I wouldn't be that surprised if the writer worked under the assumption that the 10 dot rule applied when it doesn't and it's mention in CofD also was a mistake.<br /> Writers will always make mistakes so I don't blame them, but it's so typical for OPP to miss these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:11:52-07:00","id":1325251,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or does the Ivory Claws Refinement of Flesh merit from SbtM seem a little insane for its prereqs? Primal Urge 2 and a two dot merit to be able to regenerate Lethal with no Essence expenditure sounds a little insane, given you can easily achieve that at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:24:54-07:00","id":1325353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1325251#post1325251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does the Ivory Claws Refinement of Flesh merit from SbtM seem a little insane for its prereqs? Primal Urge 2 and a two dot merit to be able to regenerate Lethal with no Essence expenditure sounds a little insane, given you can easily achieve that at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it can seem big at first glance, it's not that big once you explore the idea a bit, and rather than offering something insane, adds a quirk to the antagonists that won't break the game but does add to difficulty, and can make fighting Ivory Claws with very high Primal Urge and this merit particularly tough. The amount you heal at even middle Primal Urge isn't that overwhelming, and can be improved multiplicatively by going into Gauru form. Compound that with the fact that you have to be a member of a specific Tribe that flays your Auspice and removes your potential to get Moon Gifts.<br /> <br /> At Primal Urge 2 and 3, you're still only regenerating 1 Lethal per turn. Remember they can't just spend more Essence to heal every turn, there's a flat regeneration that can be improved (from healing Bashing to Lethal) by spending Essence. But it's still something that only occurs once a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Expanded a bit, tried to seem less confrontational 07-18-2019, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:03:30-07:00","id":1325938,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, just thought the merit seemed off at first glance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T12:25:24-07:00","id":1326068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1325251#post1325251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or does the Ivory Claws Refinement of Flesh merit from SbtM seem a little insane for its prereqs? Primal Urge 2 and a two dot merit to be able to regenerate Lethal with no Essence expenditure sounds a little insane, given you can easily achieve that at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the same cost of unlocking the Black Earth, Red Hunger facet, which also provides environmental hazards and disposes corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T04:30:30-07:00","id":1326928,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has come up and I missed it.<br /> If you have a Moon's Grace Pack, or if the ST allows it to be purchased by an individual wolf-blooded regardless of pack status, does that wolf-blooded become able to obtain renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T04:35:51-07:00","id":1326929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1326928#post1326928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has come up and I missed it.<br /> If you have a Moon's Grace Pack, or if the ST allows it to be purchased by an individual wolf-blooded regardless of pack status, does that wolf-blooded become able to obtain renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who else could the text refer to? In fact, it's written to apply to <i>all</i> pack members, including humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T05:25:07-07:00","id":1326937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1326929#post1326929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who else could the text refer to? In fact, it's written to apply to <i>all</i> pack members, including humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>....in my defense I woke up an hour early and forgot that there was a four dot effect AND more to the five. Somehow my mind ignored it and went straight from &quot;pack tactics&quot; to &quot;gifts&quot; and missed the middle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T01:56:22-07:00","id":1327372,"title":"","content":"There's a paragraph on p59 of The Pack saying human and Wolf-Blooded pack members can use Pack Tactics. On the very same page there's a sidebar saying they can't (except for Wolf-Blooded with the Tell presented in the sidebar). So which is true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T02:11:22-07:00","id":1327373,"title":"","content":"The sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T08:37:07-07:00","id":1327585,"title":"","content":"Maybe I missed an explanation elsewhere in the chapter but what exactly does the \u201cWolf-Blooded and Human Pack\u201d tag on Moon\u2019s Grace mean? It sounds kind of like the pack can\u2019t have any werewolves in it but the merit description not only makes no mention of such a thing but repeatedly refers to \u201cWolf-Blooded and human members of the pack\u201d in such a way as to imply that they aren\u2019t the only members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T09:15:23-07:00","id":1327591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1327585#post1327585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed an explanation elsewhere in the chapter but what exactly does the \u201cWolf-Blooded and Human Pack\u201d tag on Moon\u2019s Grace mean? It sounds kind of like the pack can\u2019t have any werewolves in it but the merit description not only makes no mention of such a thing but repeatedly refers to \u201cWolf-Blooded and human members of the pack\u201d in such a way as to imply that they aren\u2019t the only members.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;MOON\u2019S GRACE (\u2022\u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 OR \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, WOLF-BLOODED AND HUMAN PACKS ONLY)&quot;<br /> <br /> It's for packs without werewolves. Just wolf-blooded and humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T00:20:50-07:00","id":1327696,"title":"","content":"What do Lunes look like? I've spent an hour trying to research this on the website... no luck, so sorry if it was asked before.<br /> <br /> The description of Lunes as angels took me off-guard for Shunned by the Moon's opening fiction. I don't dislike it, but it was not what I had in mind, especially one of them being the ring-angels called Thrones/Ophanim.<br /> <br /> I suppose there'd be nothing preventing that, but, is that typical, or, is that not something I should feel pressured by? Is that normal for Lunes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T01:11:09-07:00","id":1327701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1327696#post1327696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do Lunes look like? I've spent an hour trying to research this on the website... no luck, so sorry if it was asked before.</div> </div> </div> </div>An image of various Lunes from <b>Predators</b> 1E book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-6g4OPDcapSA/WVk5IhFNj3I/AAAAAAAAwcQ/Aoa5b4wtFsEWWWh5MFeVRsPTsJZaq4KQQCLcBGAs/s1600/five_lunes.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I once run mine Gibbious Moon Lune as 'Silver Man in Silver Armour' - but somehow without proper man features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T06:29:07-07:00","id":1327732,"title":"","content":"Lunes being metamorphic spirits can very much take in on the inhuman, old testament shape of angels that usually began their revelations with &quot;do not be afraid&quot; because they looked like fucking monsters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T11:18:52-07:00","id":1327766,"title":"","content":"Yes. In addition to the picture, Predators explains, 'All Lunes have the ability to change their shape to some extent. Depending on their choir and the current phase of the moon, they may appear as abstracted beasts or humans, chimerical fusions of both, even as inanimate objects or imitations of werewolves.'<br /> <br /> And each of the 'prime' lunes (one representing each auspice, and glimmerlings for stray moonlight) has a physical description that offers a variety of takes. As an example, 'The Elunim are entities of both light and dark, a duality re\ufb02ected in their forms. An Elunim often appears luminescent on one half of their form, and shadowy on the other. The \u201clight\u201d and \u201cdark\u201d aspects may even possess dramatically different features: a Cloven Lune that wears a wolf form may have sleek, silver fur and a slender build on one side and a shaggy, dark coat and bulge with brawny strength on the other. A few even lack substance on their \u201cshadowed\u201d side, and appear like lambent \ufb01gures that have been sliced in half.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T12:16:48-07:00","id":1327777,"title":"","content":"Predators book eh? Thanks you all!<br /> <br /> Oh this is very exciting! Thanks! I was worried I was *supposed* to portray them as judeo-christian angels with lunar symbols...!<br /> <br /> Malus's clear up also helps on how they're not necessary but fitting for contexts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T03:45:19-07:00","id":1327880,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know where to buy Predators in pdf? It's only available in print from DrivethruRPG for some reason, despite every other title having a pdf option, and I'm not keen on getting a physical book from last edition when I really just need a pdf for reference/inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T04:32:41-07:00","id":1327883,"title":"","content":"That is strange. I'd suggest contacting Drivethru and asking what's up. I have the pdf from there so it was available at some point. I suspect it's a system error that they could address quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T11:56:48-07:00","id":1328138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After that point, she must choose: Shift<br /> down into Dalu or Urshul, or fall into Kuruth. If she does not shift,<br /> roll Resolve + Composure as a reflexive action. If she succeeds, she<br /> has one more turn in Gauru, then must shift to Dalu or Urshul,<br /> and enters Wasu-Im. If she fails, she enters Basu-Im immediately </div> </div> </div>If he success the roll he can stay a turn more then he's forced to transofrm back in Dalu or Urshul (in Wasu-Im), no matter if he wants to keep the Gauru form falling in Basu-Im. Or he can decide to fall in Basu-Im to stay Gauru as per his primal urge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-29-2019, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T16:35:52-07:00","id":1328186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1328138#post1328138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he success the roll he can stay a turn more then he's forced to transofrm back in Dalu or Urshul (in Wasu-Im), no matter if he wants to keep the Gauru form falling in Basu-Im. Or he can decide to fall in Basu-Im to stay Gauru as per his primal urge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The later. You can give into the Death Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T21:07:28-07:00","id":1329221,"title":"","content":"Barring the relevant Gift, what are some possible means to ascertain a spirit's Ban or Bane? One of my players can see spirits and is well versed in spirit lore but isn't a werewolf; and I'm trying to give her options to suss these out that don't take lots of game time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T23:30:30-07:00","id":1329232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1329221#post1329221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring the relevant Gift, what are some possible means to ascertain a spirit's Ban or Bane? One of my players can see spirits and is well versed in spirit lore but isn't a werewolf; and I'm trying to give her options to suss these out that don't take lots of game time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Research rolls are the go-to; if you've got the Chronicles of Darkness Core Rulebook, the systems for mortal interaction with ephemeral beings includes a basic system of extended actions to find either or both of an entity's main weaknesses on page 139, reproduced from the page labeled as 230 in the free <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">God-Machine Rules Update</a>, though if you're looking for means that don't need some time investment and the spirit's not low-Ranking then making a lucky/educated guess is about as good as can reliably be used without simply providing a homebrewed option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-04-2019, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:40:19-07:00","id":1330099,"title":"","content":"Is rape an actual &quot;frecuent&quot; thing in fosaken society? or just a crime that happens becuase &quot;some&quot; uratha are true monsters? what\u00b4s the frecuency?<br /> <br /> I ask this becuase in the pure supplement one of the posible reasons for forsaken going pure is the alpha of a pack selecting the sister of a beta as a &quot;breeding mare&quot; and other books talk about the wolf blooded being used as a bredding stock not to mention that in TV Tropes talks about the Call Human rite being used to summon woman and spreed the seed...<br /> <br /> Mind that i have no problem with CoD not holding his punches in fact I like it becuase that way avoids sounding edgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 08-09-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:05:21-07:00","id":1330103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1330099#post1330099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is rape an actual &quot;frecuent&quot; thing in fosaken society? or just a crime that happens becuase &quot;some&quot; uratha are true monsters? what\u00b4s the frecuency?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, its something that happens because some are just monsters, there's no given frequency.<br /> <br /> Second edition removed a lot of these things, 'breeding mares' aren't a thing since now werewolves can safely reproduce on their own (and wolf blooded are not to be abused), and there is no call human rite in second edition, though if you added one there would be plenty of things to do with it than use it to rape.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:35:45-07:00","id":1332694,"title":"","content":"Quick Question. Do werewolf claws (in all 4 forms except Hishu) deal lethal or bashing damage to vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:47:19-07:00","id":1332699,"title":"","content":"Generally they would just do Bashing to vampires, because vampires have a sort of Lethal damage-reducer. But you could get enhancements that claw through it.<br /> <br /> It's the jaws, the bite attack, that always do Lethal (except when they do Aggravated, during eating attacks), even in Hishu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:00:48-07:00","id":1332705,"title":"","content":"Thanks mate. Can I ask though where you found this information about the bite, because in the forms, it is part of the same text with the claws, and I'm not sure werewolves can feed on vampires to gain essence and deal aggravated damage and in the unarmed Combat bit, it doesn't say anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T14:07:29-07:00","id":1332729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332705#post1332705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks mate. Can I ask though where you found this information about the bite, because in the forms, it is part of the same text with the claws, and I'm not sure werewolves can feed on vampires to gain essence and deal aggravated damage and in the unarmed Combat bit, it doesn't say anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Top of page 99, in the 'The Predator's Jaws' sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T14:13:48-07:00","id":1332730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332729#post1332729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Top of page 99, in the 'The Predator's Jaws' sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That settles it. Thank you. You were really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T17:39:42-07:00","id":1332751,"title":"","content":"Hello, I have some questions on Hosts and their whereabouts, which are not much clear to me (and i think i have made a lot of mistakes on an old Chronicle).<br /> <br /> In a precedent chronicle there were this big Azlu that was going to eat some werevoles that were caught in her webs in the Shadow. The PCs, which were mages, confronted the thing in the Shadow (since it was a trap the Gauntlet wasn't too much thick. Yet) and one of them finally drove a Prime infused bastard sword in the head of the Azlu as killing blow (one of the luckiest roll I've ever seen, btw)<br /> <br /> The questions are:<br /> - &quot;big&quot; meaning she was like size 7-8 and rank 3 or 4 (not sure, was a couple of year ago) and of 3/4 spider 1/4 woman aspect. Humanlike intelligence.<br /> - She was dwelling in the shadow and not in a body of some unlucky dude. I read that the shards are physical, so dwelling in the Shadow doesn't work? Are the Hosts always in the physical world but have the ability to cross the gauntlet to do their things or influence the Gauntlet from the Physical world side?<br /> - The Azlu was discorporated after the killing blow, not killed outright (because she still had essence, at least this was the idea at the time), so the shard should have reformed somewhere else in the Shadow and started all over again? If so, like a new being or the same one reforming slowly?<br /> - Since that chronicle is going to continue with a new story arc, I wanted to bring back that &quot;old friend&quot;, if it makes sense, and this time have her infiltrate a body and move differently. I did not understand how getting a corpse works for a Host: would a swarm of spiders physically attack un unfortunate dude or the hosts use other means?<br /> <br /> <br /> Did I get anything right about how the hosts works? ^_^'<br /> <br /> (Thanks in advance for reading the gibberish ^_^')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T18:01:34-07:00","id":1332757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332751#post1332751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I get anything right about how the hosts works? ^_^'</div> </div> </div> </div>Hosts don't have Ranks, nor do they engage with the state of Twilight; depending on the type, they may or may not engage with the Shadow itself as part of any meddling with the Gauntlet they do, but their Shards are material creatures and the Joining with a human body doesn't change that; they don't depend on Essence to survive the way spirits do, so discorporation relies purely on the fact that they survive as long as even one of the multiple targets it becomes escapes; a single Shard merges with a human by getting into the body in some way that varies by the type of Host but usually entails consuming part of the body in the process (Azlu and Beshilu traditionally eat the brain and the heart, respectively).<br /> <br /> Separately from that, it's important to note that Twilight and the Shadow are different things; Twilight is the state spirits inhabit when they're in the material world, whereas the Shadow is the world they come from on the other side of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T18:42:27-07:00","id":1332761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332757#post1332757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hosts don't have Ranks, nor do they engage with the state of Twilight; depending on the type, they may or may not engage with the Shadow itself as part of any meddling with the Gauntlet they do, but their Shards are material creatures and the Joining with a human body doesn't change that; they don't depend on Essence to survive the way spirits do, so discorporation relies purely on the fact that they survive as long as even one of the multiple targets it becomes escapes; a single Shard merges with a human by getting into the body in some way that varies by the type of Host but usually entails consuming part of the body in the process (Azlu and Beshilu traditionally eat the brain and the heart, respectively).<br /> <br /> Separately from that, it's important to note that Twilight and the Shadow are different things; Twilight is the state spirits inhabit when they're in the material world, whereas the Shadow is the world they come from on the other side of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Soooooo, I got that wronger than I thought ^_^'<br /> I'll have to do a little retcon with the players, luckily for me at the time it was a short one-time side story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Many thanks for the enlightening answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I got some more questions, if I may:<br /> - Is there something in particular that steers a host toward one body or another to inhabit?<br /> - So, whatever they do to the Gauntlet they do it from this side. Can the Azlu interact with the Gauntlet in other ways that is not only strengthening it?<br /> - Essence for them is only fuel for Dread Powers and maybe their evolution to a bigger, more powerful form? I guess that after having accumulated enough essence (and shards) a Host becomes bigger, stronger and more intelligent, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T18:52:06-07:00","id":1332762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332751#post1332751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I get anything right about how the hosts works? ^_^'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, issues you seemed to have had were more about conflating spirits and hosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - &quot;big&quot; meaning she was like size 7-8 and rank 3 or 4 (not sure, was a couple of year ago) and of 3/4 spider 1/4 woman aspect. Humanlike intelligence. </div> </div> </div>Size is fine, Azlu don't go by spirit ranks but you might use the Horror system (which has Ranks) for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - She was dwelling in the shadow and not in a body of some unlucky dude. I read that the shards are physical, so dwelling in the Shadow doesn't work? Are the Hosts always in the physical world but have the ability to cross the gauntlet to do their things or influence the Gauntlet from the Physical world side? </div> </div> </div>They are physical, but they can go into the Shadow and sometimes make a name for themselves there instead of flesh-side. For the Azlu they're more likely to dwell inside the Gauntlet itself, where they can make webbed tunnels to hide in like trapdoor spiders. I don't believe it's explicitly written in the core but in first edition they had an ability called Breach the Barrier, which allowed them to cross the Gauntlet at a locus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Azlu was discorporated after the killing blow, not killed outright (because she still had essence, at least this was the idea at the time), so the shard should have reformed somewhere else in the Shadow and started all over again? If so, like a new being or the same one reforming slowly? </div> </div> </div>This is one of the fun things with hosts. When you kill them they Discorporate into a bunch of individual soul shards, in the case of Azlu, you would have a swarm of spiders. Providing one gets free, they could potentially rebuild their power by eating up other shards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Since that chronicle is going to continue with a new story arc, I wanted to bring back that &quot;old friend&quot;, if it makes sense, and this time have her infiltrate a body and move differently. I did not understand how getting a corpse works for a Host: would a swarm of spiders physically attack un unfortunate dude or the hosts use other means? </div> </div> </div>One soul shard would need to make contact. In first edition they crawled into a hole in your head (made by smashing, or in your ear, or up your nose) but in second edition it seems like more of a merging into flesh (though this might just be how they represent it mechanically). It's called the Joining, and gets some detail in this blog post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-joining-shunned-by-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-joining-shunned-by-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Joining [Shunned by the Moon] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-joining-shunned-by-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-joining-shunned-by-the-moon/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While most of the post is about the Ukusgualu, the lamprey hosts, the first part 'The Joining' talks about hosts in general in a brief but informative fashion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T21:45:24-07:00","id":1332776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1332762#post1332762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe it's explicitly written in the core but in first edition they had an ability called Breach the Barrier, which allowed them to cross the Gauntlet at a locus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following up on this: It's a one-dot Aspect for the Azlu in <i>Predators</i> (the same book gives it to the Beshilu as an innate Aspect), which in Second Edition would translate straightforwardly enough into a Dread Power that might take cues from how spirit-Claimed accomplish Reaching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:06:55-07:00","id":1333242,"title":"","content":"The moon is crescent or gibbous for much more of the time than it\u2019s new, full, or half. Do auspice numbers reflect that or are Cahalith and Ithaeur Changes less likely per time to compensate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:46:11-07:00","id":1333254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1333242#post1333242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moon is crescent or gibbous for much more of the time than it\u2019s new, full, or half. Do auspice numbers reflect that or are Cahalith and Ithaeur Changes less likely per time to compensate?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lunar month is about 28 days, give or take one or two depending on the specific definition you use, and a sidereal lunar month is about 29.5. Even assuming that doesn't round off to 30, it's simple enough to conclude the intermediate phases being two clusters of three-ish days each instead of the five-ish days each that the new and full moons doesn't produce a significantly higher number of other auspices than the Rahu and Irraka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T10:16:18-07:00","id":1333274,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a schedule like one First Change doled out a week, there seems to be some agency behind it (Signs of the Moon might get into it). But nothing keeps you from having one auspice represented more. The anomalous auspices are called out as rare, having some non-anomalous auspices be more common fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T15:11:37-07:00","id":1336950,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this has been asked before but I cannot for the love of me figure out where I last saw this, so I have to ask cuz I can't find it.<br /> <br /> How possible is it (if at all) for a Pure to return to being Forsaken? I'm guessing it is impossible, but I wanna be certain. How impossible is it? Like, say the Pure is earnest and there's a Forsaken pack willing to play ball, what sort of obstacles would make it impossible, or make it simply unlikely?<br /> <br /> I have another question--I know people talk a lot about how bipolar or much of a bitch Luna is, but, I've not seen anything outside of epithets and some vague lore stuff like how werewolves suffer under the rage and all that, to get a good feel on how much of a bitch Luna is. I know the Warden Moon communicates through Lunes, but, exactly what sort of characterization should I be considering for Luna? Or does it matter? Like how mercurial or callous should the god(dess) be to Her/His own children? Or is it only the Pure that really characterize her as a mad, piece of shit god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T15:48:15-07:00","id":1336956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1336950#post1336950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How possible is it (if at all) for a Pure to return to being Forsaken? I'm guessing it is impossible, but I wanna be certain. How impossible is it? Like, say the Pure is earnest and there's a Forsaken pack willing to play ball, what sort of obstacles would make it impossible, or make it simply unlikely?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rare enough that the only times it's mentioned in the setting is when there's specifically an option for redeeming them. Usually you want a high bar for it, so you don't just have a tug of war with Forsaken grabbing Pure and giving them Auspices, then Pure grabbing them back and ripping them off. You can see some options for it scattered across the books, one of the more notable ones is the Lodge of Salvation, a lodge about, well, saving Pure and re-Baptizing them with a new (only Rahu) auspice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have another question--I know people talk a lot about how bipolar or much of a bitch Luna is, but, I've not seen anything outside of epithets and some vague lore stuff like how werewolves suffer under the rage and all that, to get a good feel on how much of a bitch Luna is. I know the Warden Moon communicates through Lunes, but, exactly what sort of characterization should I be considering for Luna? Or does it matter? Like how mercurial or callous should the god(dess) be to Her/His own children? Or is it only the Pure that really characterize her as a mad, piece of shit god? </div> </div> </div>Mostly a vestige of first edition, where the Pure put forth the theory that the bane of silver was a curse from Luna for killing Urfarah (though later she embraced the Forsaken), this sort of led to her being considered cruel and mercurial, especially since Luna seemed to want werewolves to act one way, but still made them all suffer from the bane of silver. In second edition, we see in Dark Eras before Urfarah is dead that werewolves already had the bane of silver (though it's not as much of an obstacle in an era without much in the way of metallurgy), and perhaps the Pure were wrong. It's still possible Luna gave them the bane from the start, but when we've seen focuses on her it's less as a 'sad Queen crying over her King's death thousands of years ago' and more 'distant barrier god.'<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that werewolves don't really usually get direct words from Luna, what they usually hear from is instead lunes. And while lunes are ostensibly servants of Luna it's impossible to say how loyal, truthful, and right they are, especially since lunes can seem pretty arbitrary and you can probably find more lunes with conflicting agendas than lunes that agree with one another. Exceptions mostly revolve around things like the void spirits and Pure. So if you take for granted that lunes carry the word of Luna, seeing lunes with such differing outlooks and demands can lead to the idea that maybe Luna is as fractured as they are. And as a spirit god of change and basically everything under the moon there's a ton of portfolios under her belt and she may well be (as fractured as all the lunes seem).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T16:12:53-07:00","id":1336957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1336956#post1336956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (plentiful useful information) .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow thanks for the fast response ;o, yeah, I'd mentioned the Lune thing cuz I figured that would make it near impossible to know what Luna is like &quot;personally&quot; if such a thing can even work. Sundered World was soooo goood.<br /> I'm glad you said all this, it was what I was hoping would be the case, infact! Its funny you mention Rahu cuz my Ivory Claw from a failed game, was JUUUST who I had in mind!! So this Lodge is perfect. Does she have to join it or just meet someone from it though?<br /> <br /> I'm leaning toward a Lune putting her up to it to restore her Auspice and become a Blood Talon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T17:27:38-07:00","id":1336965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1336957#post1336957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow thanks for the fast response ;o, yeah, I'd mentioned the Lune thing cuz I figured that would make it near impossible to know what Luna is like &quot;personally&quot; if such a thing can even work. Sundered World was soooo goood.<br /> I'm glad you said all this, it was what I was hoping would be the case, infact! Its funny you mention Rahu cuz my Ivory Claw from a failed game, was JUUUST who I had in mind!! So this Lodge is perfect. Does she have to join it or just meet someone from it though?</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, though I might have gotten some details wrong, the rite says it can let you join the Tribes of the Moon, and it gets rid of your Pure renown, but it doesn't give you a new auspice, it just sort of makes you a Forsaken. There were some plot hooks for getting your full auspice blessing back, however. The lodge is more about finding and helping Pure convert back, so the ex-Pure don't have to join, but it's easy to imagine them joining up to help others later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm leaning toward a Lune putting her up to it to restore her Auspice and become a Blood Talon. </div> </div> </div>I say go for it, I always liked the idea of quests to earn the auspice back, something to make yourself open and available to lunes and Luna's blessing. I think someone on the forum once posted about having to find your original, scoured Auspice, the idea being that they weren't just ripped off and destroyed but instead stashed away somewhere. Which seemed like a neat hook too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T14:39:58-07:00","id":1338507,"title":"","content":"Another (possibly dumb) question: Is Locus required in order for Uratha to cross the gauntlet? Is it possible to Reach at any other place than Locus? My understanding is that Locus provides strong mechanical bonus which, for most Uratha, is neccessary to Reach, but there are some descriptions throughout the book, that are being intepreted as indications that Reaching is possible only at Locus, and cannot be done anywhere else. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24289-wamesahau","name":"wamesahau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T14:42:54-07:00","id":1338508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wamesahau</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1338507#post1338507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another (possibly dumb) question: Is Locus required in order for Uratha to cross the gauntlet? Is it possible to Reach at any other place than Locus? My understanding is that Locus provides strong mechanical bonus which, for most Uratha, is neccessary to Reach, but there are some descriptions throughout the book, that are being intepreted as indications that Reaching is possible only at Locus, and cannot be done anywhere else. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Normally, werewolves need to Reach at a locus.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolves with Harmony 3 or lower do not require a locus to enter the Shadow. Werewolves with Harmony 8 or higher do not require a locus to enter the physical world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T14:47:45-07:00","id":1338510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wamesahau</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1338507#post1338507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another (possibly dumb) question: Is Locus required in order for Uratha to cross the gauntlet? Is it possible to Reach at any other place than Locus? My understanding is that Locus provides strong mechanical bonus which, for most Uratha, is neccessary to Reach, but there are some descriptions throughout the book, that are being intepreted as indications that Reaching is possible only at Locus, and cannot be done anywhere else. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general terms, Uratha can only Reach at a locus, unless they have a Gift or some other power that specifically allows it, or Harmony imbalance.<br /> <br /> For individual games, settings, and scenarios, the Storyteller may introduce other phenomena/situations that work for Reaching. Additionally, some other creatures have their own powers that they could use on a Uratha, or that a Uratha could take advantage of, but they\u2019re not the werewolf\u2019s inherent Reaching ability.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja\u2019d by Tessie \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T00:45:09-07:00","id":1339137,"title":"","content":"Does the Pack Totem is still around its pack or it's roaming free and come to the pack if asked? How independent being is the Pack Totem?<br /> <br /> If the pack doesn't have locus where the Pack Totem would reside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T01:14:25-07:00","id":1339141,"title":"","content":"It varies from pack to pack. Some pack totems are free to do whatever they want, some totems are forced to behave according to certain rules by their pack, and some totems boss around with their pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:30:05-07:00","id":1339214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1339137#post1339137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Pack Totem is still around its pack or it's roaming free and come to the pack if asked? How independent being is the Pack Totem?<br /> <br /> If the pack doesn't have locus where the Pack Totem would reside?</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets more detailed in the Pack book.<br /> <br /> But if the pack is at rest and nothing's going on, the totem is usually at rest as well. When the Pack is active, say, responding to a threat or investigating something new, it gets more active as well. And most totems participate on the hunt, so if there's a hunt it's usually going with. An obvious exception is totems based on a location, say a lake or marketplace, who might not be able to leave it (and may even have a ban keeping them from leaving it).<br /> <br /> What kind of totem it is can make a big difference. One more about watchful vigilance would probably always be watching over the territory and pack, while one of Death and Silence might hang out at a graveyard whenever it's not being called upon for something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T03:16:03-07:00","id":1339325,"title":"","content":"How Uratha sense Spirit-Ridden, especially Urged? It's only by Scent the Unnatural gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T04:49:33-07:00","id":1339334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1339325#post1339325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Uratha sense Spirit-Ridden, especially Urged? It's only by Scent the Unnatural gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>With their Spirit senses uratha can see spirits in twilight and across the gauntlet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:26:34-07:00","id":1339650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wamesahau</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1338507#post1338507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another (possibly dumb) question: Is Locus required in order for Uratha to cross the gauntlet? Is it possible to Reach at any other place than Locus? My understanding is that Locus provides strong mechanical bonus which, for most Uratha, is neccessary to Reach, but there are some descriptions throughout the book, that are being intepreted as indications that Reaching is possible only at Locus, and cannot be done anywhere else. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the Waystone Tell, for another example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:30:51-07:00","id":1339652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1339325#post1339325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Uratha sense Spirit-Ridden, especially Urged? It's only by Scent the Unnatural gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits urging a mount suffuse it entirely, so they aren't visible - but there's signs to the educated, and they can probably sniff out influences with a successful Wits+Primal Urge roll penalized by the spirit's Resistance. <br /> <br /> Claimed are usually readily apparent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T10:12:02-07:00","id":1339870,"title":"","content":"The Storm Lord Sacred Hunt also offers the ability to perceive the Riding spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T18:46:47-07:00","id":1340704,"title":"","content":"dumb question, but it's been gnawing on me for a while. the corebook mentions Creator wolf, who was the yin to Destroyer wolf's yang. it also says creator wolf became rabid gibbering wreck who spread his madness like a plague. is rabid wolf what creator wolf became?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:20:52-07:00","id":1340721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1340704#post1340704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dumb question, but it's been gnawing on me for a while. the corebook mentions Creator wolf, who was the yin to Destroyer wolf's yang. it also says creator wolf became rabid gibbering wreck who spread his madness like a plague. is rabid wolf what creator wolf became?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. The Blood Talons legend clashes with what\u2019s possibly going on in Basra , for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:10:28-07:00","id":1340840,"title":"","content":"Can spirits use gifts since they are the ones who give them to werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:22:24-07:00","id":1340842,"title":"","content":"No. A Gift isn't something a spirit has that it shares with you or a trick it knows that it teaches to you. It's a ritual scar a spirit can tear into a werewolf's body and spirit (or which a werewolf can tear into herself <i>from</i> a successfully hunted spirit), like the spirit's Essence lodging itself in as a part of the half-flesh, half-spiritual werewolf. A Gift is more like the product of intermingling of Uratha and spirit Essence. Spirits are missing half the equation.<br /> <br /> Nothing's stopping a Storyteller from giving a spirit a Numen based on a Gift effect (or any other supernatural power writeup from another gameline, for that matter), but that should probably be saved for when the available Numina and Influences don't adequately represent some signature thing a spirit would do. Gifts are written for werewolves, so they're huntier (and PC-ier) than the average spirit Numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T15:58:52-07:00","id":1340855,"title":"","content":"Imagine it like this: The power behind all Gifts is that of the werewolf. The Gifts provide Facets, aka lenses, through which the werewolf can express their powers in different ways. That's why so many Facets affect werewolf subjects, like packs, or Death Rage, when those would be unusable for the spirit who imparted the Gift in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T17:10:27-07:00","id":1345351,"title":"","content":"In Book of Spirits it mentions that Naturae can take the Greater Influence Numina. Is that still valid in 2ed ? So lets say we have a Rank 3 sea spirit with Influence: Storms 3.<br /> <br /> Does it mean it can be taken once to gain Influence 4 ? If so, it can only be taken once, correct ? Or does the Rank limit still apply ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T17:46:59-07:00","id":1345359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1345351#post1345351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Book of Spirits it mentions that Naturae can take the Greater Influence Numina. Is that still valid in 2ed ? So lets say we have a Rank 3 sea spirit with Influence: Storms 3.<br /> <br /> Does it mean it can be taken once to gain Influence 4 ? If so, it can only be taken once, correct ? Or does the Rank limit still apply ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank always applied with Greater Influence. In the Book of Spirits Greater Influence just allowed you to have more Influences but as it states on p142, 'No spirit may have a single Influence greater than its Rank, or more different kinds of Influences than its Rank.'<br /> <br /> In second edition this is simplified by not having a separate Numina for Greater Influence, and just offering a flat 'Spirits may reduce their number of Numina granted by Rank to increase Influence dots at a cost of one Numen per dot.' From p186 of the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T21:01:29-07:00","id":1345380,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T09:05:34-08:00","id":1351667,"title":"","content":"Hunter\u2019s Aspect question - <b>Can Aspect be put on <i>multiple</i> targets? </b>Like my PCs pack was fighting with enemy pack of Uratha and Wolf-Blooded, circa 30 members. Can one flared Aspect works on all 30 enemies?<br /> <br /> Even if they are singular, I can see execution of this rule on working on <i><b>whole</b></i> humans Sacred Prey organization that Iron Masters mark with <i>Siskur-Dah</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:35:44-08:00","id":1351683,"title":"","content":"If you do something to affect them all, I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T19:17:33-08:00","id":1353677,"title":"","content":"This is a very simple question probably but I want to be super sure about it before I get going running my first game that might feature WtF in it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken 2e, page 96: \u201cWhen the character is stressed \u2014 during combat, a chase, or when she feels threatened \u2014 she shifts one form towards an appropriate form each turn. The stress means she cannot resist\u201d<br /> <br /> Assuming that you have a character just fresh out of char gen, this is an instant action. Which means it takes your whole turn.<br /> <br /> This isn't getting into the idea of 'well what if I want to have a werewolf who fights with a gun when appropriate' or the idea of a non-lethal hand to hand fight in a public arena, be it trying to beat someone down in a brawl to secure a rep or simply take someone alive for questioning.<br /> <br /> Say you were in basic human form at the start of an unarmed fight. You're Werewolf Bob fighting Wolf Blooded Charles, who is part of a different pack and is blocking your way chasing after a figure. Presumably for political reasons. Round one, you throw a punch, he throws a punch.<br /> <br /> Round two, you spend an Instant Action and thus your whole turn (unless you spend Essence) transforming to Dalu. He throws another punch.<br /> <br /> Round three, you throw a punch, he throws a punch.<br /> <br /> Round four, you automatically make the once a scene transition to Garaou and are going to destroy him now because that's how this goes.<br /> <br /> Is there no viable way to go 'no this is meant to be a fistfight?' or even just planning to be able to shoot dudes for a bit? I can really easily imagine a lot of reasons you might get into a fight in public but need to maintain cover and the ignorance of the herd. Or not lose an entire action to a dramatic bone snapping Hollywood horror transformation sequence, until that becomes dramatically appropriate.<br /> <br /> I mostly am weirdly bothered by the huge intrusion into the action economy and the edging out of ranged options. I know it is a quick stroke of the pen to fix it as houserules if so inclined but I want to make sure I'm understanding what it is right now. The action economy thing especially bothers me a lot, too many years of Exalted and Dungeons and Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 12-08-2019, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T21:55:42-08:00","id":1353695,"title":"","content":"If you check out the previous paragraph, you'll see that the change while stressed refers to Low Harmony werewolves (3 or below), so this isn't likely to occur fresh out of chargen. The the paragraph break has caused this question to pop up before. Also shifting in this manner (and at this Harmony) is not an instant action, it's reflexive. Action economy isn't really an issue.<br /> <br /> Also Dalu is made for urban hunts so you don't really have to rush into Gauru, though it's a good way to say 'fuck this I'm going to kill them.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T21:59:30-08:00","id":1353696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353677#post1353677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very simple question probably but I want to be super sure about it before I get going running my first game that might feature WtF in it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken 2e, page 96: \u201cWhen the character is stressed \u2014 during combat, a chase, or when she feels threatened \u2014 she shifts one form towards an appropriate form each turn. The stress means she cannot resist\u201d<br /> <br /> Assuming that you have a character just fresh out of char gen, this is an instant action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you have a character just fresh out of chargen, this is a non-issue. Read the paragraph directly preceding the quoted sentence, whose terms the quoted sentence is offering immediate clarification on:<br /> <br /> &quot;She can spend Essence to avoid this shift, as long as she isn't stressed.&quot; &gt; &quot;When the character is stressed [\u2026] she cannot resist.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T22:09:19-08:00","id":1353699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353696#post1353696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you have a character just fresh out of chargen, this is a non-issue. Read the paragraph directly preceding the quoted sentence, whose terms the quoted sentence is offering immediate clarification on:<br /> <br /> &quot;She can spend Essence to avoid this shift, as long as she isn't stressed.&quot; &gt; &quot;When the character is stressed [\u2026] she cannot resist.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the ability to spend essence is an option, but I feel like we have a conundrum. It just defined the framework of the change only being mandatory when stressed which includes such times as combat or a chase. There is no time that this mandatory shift would happen that isn't set up definitionally as unavailable for the essence spend rule.<br /> <br /> I mean my gut would say they can spend essence to not change whenever, but feel like either I'm not grokking some rule element here or there was a writing error.<br /> <br /> &quot;You always shift one form towards a more ideal one for the situation when stressed, but can spend an essence to avoid that mandatory shift but only when you aren't stressed.&quot; seems wrong.<br /> <br /> Or is that final paragraph meaning only for low Harmony figures? If so that fixes everything but is not at all how that text block reads to me, which means I'm an idiot or it needs better structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 12-09-2019, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T22:14:26-08:00","id":1353701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353699#post1353699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You always shift one form towards a more ideal one for the situation when stressed, but can spend an essence to avoid that mandatory shift but only when you aren't stressed.&quot; seems wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shift irresistibly under stress and must either change shape every scene or spend Essence every scene to avoid changing shape in the absence of stressful conditions.<br /> <br /> Again: This is literally not a concern for characters with a Harmony higher than 3, which includes every starting character under the game as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T22:17:15-08:00","id":1353703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353701#post1353701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: This is literally not a concern for characters with a Harmony higher than 3, which includes every starting character under the game as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>See okay, that works but is not how I read that block at all. The rules for all the various Harmony levels had been in a single paragraph each so I felt that the last paragraph being absent any specific note of Harmony applied to everyone! I have been misreading that for years apparently!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T00:12:09-08:00","id":1353724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353703#post1353703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See okay, that works but is not how I read that block at all. The rules for all the various Harmony levels had been in a single paragraph each so I felt that the last paragraph being absent any specific note of Harmony applied to everyone! I have been misreading that for years apparently!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The paragraph concerning low Harmony literally ends with \u2018 She can spend Essence to avoid this shift, as long as she isn't stressed.\u2019. The next paragraph literally then begins with \u2018When the character is stressed\u2019, which links the two.<br /> <br /> But as others have said, this is a non-issue for new characters and only applies to low Harmony Uratha, as they struggle to avoid shifting constantly. If your characters avoid such a low Harmony extreme they should be okay.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad people could clear that up before your first game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:11:17-08:00","id":1353924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1353724#post1353724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. The paragraph concerning low Harmony literally ends with \u2018 She can spend Essence to avoid this shift, as long as she isn't stressed.\u2019. The next paragraph literally then begins with \u2018When the character is stressed\u2019, which links the two.<br /> <br /> But as others have said, this is a non-issue for new characters and only applies to low Harmony Uratha, as they struggle to avoid shifting constantly. If your characters avoid such a low Harmony extreme they should be okay.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad people could clear that up before your first game!</div> </div> </div> </div>I misread it years ago and that basically colored every time I saw that passage again. I'm putting together a mixed game with WtF and Mage, and while I know mage fairly well now after playing one for a year and a bit, werewolf I am refreshing memory on and that jumped out. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T05:31:13-08:00","id":1354338,"title":"","content":"The &quot;move one step towards the appropriate form&quot; bit doesn't really work either, cos say you're in human form and you're trying to run somewhere. You slowly shift towards urhan and- wait, no, you're in gauru now so you death rage never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:05:12-08:00","id":1354379,"title":"","content":"That if you view the five forms as a cycle. You could just go human, near human, near wolf, wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T11:03:06-08:00","id":1354416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1354338#post1354338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;move one step towards the appropriate form&quot; bit doesn't really work either, cos say you're in human form and you're trying to run somewhere. You slowly shift towards urhan and- wait, no, you're in gauru now so you death rage never mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking it's only when stressed (which usually means threatened) you're forced to change shape form-by-form. I do think it makes a little sense that you can end up in Death Rage due to being too far from the goal form when exposed to certain stimuli. Also, you'll always be able to shift through Gauru this way once per scene without falling to Kuruth.<br /> If your example human-formed uratha isn't stressed, then they're only forced to shift once per scene, and can shift directly into Urhan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T09:34:38-08:00","id":1356113,"title":"","content":"Is there a specific reason why Dalu form provides a bonus to enacting Rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T10:02:30-08:00","id":1356118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1356113#post1356113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a specific reason why Dalu form provides a bonus to enacting Rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it's the most spiritual form that either doesn't lack opposable thumbs or makes you a bit angery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T18:45:44-08:00","id":1356212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1356118#post1356118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because it's the most spiritual form that either doesn't lack opposable thumbs or makes you a bit angery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can buy that. Simple enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T08:51:21-08:00","id":1356650,"title":"","content":"<b>Heavens Unleashed Weather Facet</b><br /> <br /> Relatively new to storytelling Werewolf here \u2014 as such, I've run into an oddity with the aforementioned Glory Facet of the Gift of Weather <b>(WtF2e pp.135\u2013136)</b>. Heavens Unleashed requires 10 successes to activate, with extended rolls taking a minute apiece. The duration is 1hr/success. My presumption is that this means it will last an hour if all ten successes are achieved, plus an extra hour for any above that number. Am I reading too much into that?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if I <i>am</i> actually interpreting that correctly, can the Uratha keep rolling 1/min even after the requisite 10 successes are rolled, in order to extend the duration of the storm? The text under the exceptional success paragraph leads me to believe the intention is to spend more Essence and activate the power again if you want the storm to rage on.<br /> <br /> First time actually posting here, so I apologize in advance if I've overlooked any forum rules!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25547-hamildong","name":"hamildong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T10:18:28-08:00","id":1356661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hamildong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1356650#post1356650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Heavens Unleashed Weather Facet</b><br /> <br /> Relatively new to storytelling Werewolf here \u2014 as such, I've run into an oddity with the aforementioned Glory Facet of the Gift of Weather <b>(WtF2e pp.135\u2013136)</b>. Heavens Unleashed requires 10 successes to activate, with extended rolls taking a minute apiece. The duration is 1hr/success. My presumption is that this means it will last an hour if all ten successes are achieved, plus an extra hour for any above that number. Am I reading too much into that?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if I <i>am</i> actually interpreting that correctly, can the Uratha keep rolling 1/min even after the requisite 10 successes are rolled, in order to extend the duration of the storm? The text under the exceptional success paragraph leads me to believe the intention is to spend more Essence and activate the power again if you want the storm to rage on.<br /> <br /> First time actually posting here, so I apologize in advance if I've overlooked any forum rules!</div> </div> </div> </div>Powers that are activated as extended actions with outcomes scaled by successes are tricky in general, but given that Heavens Unleashed costs five Essence and is, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">as Chris Allen puts it</a>, a &quot;killing your city&quot; Facet (and it needs a separate Facet to not have it impede you or your packmates), I'd say it lasts at least ten hours.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking an extended action completes once its target success count is reached, and the target success count is set from the start; complications might undo your work or force you to start over, but it's not like Social Maneuvering where you're aiming for a certain number of successful rolls to influence a complicated circumstance over a set of intervals substantially longer than once per minute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T11:23:50-08:00","id":1356669,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick response there!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1356661#post1356661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powers that are activated as extended actions with outcomes scaled by successes are tricky in general, but given that Heavens Unleashed costs five Essence and is, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">as Chris Allen puts it</a>, a &quot;killing your city&quot; Facet (and it needs a separate Facet to not have it impede you or your packmates), I'd say it lasts at least ten hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that city-killing metric, is the Facet actually that strong? The success result specifically states it's &quot;unlikely to be as destructive as the Catastrophe Facet&quot; but that invoking it repetitively &quot;can have very serious results&quot; (<b>WtF2e p.136)</b>. If the one activation of this Facet is that potent, I'm struggling to find a reason the book would even <i>mention</i> repeated uses, and at that point it feels like it's treading on the territory of the combined Catastrophe + Heart of Water Elemental Facets just in and of itself. Totally not meaning to be contrary \u2014 just trying to work my head around this minutia!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25547,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25547-hamildong","user":"hamildong","date":".  edited for formatting error 12-23-2019, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25547-hamildong","name":"hamildong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T12:03:14-08:00","id":1356674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hamildong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1356669#post1356669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that city-killing metric, is the Facet actually that strong?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an indiscriminate supernatural power that allows you to summon a torrential thunderstorm that lasts for hours regardless of the normal weather. I bring up the &quot;killing your city&quot; note to point out that it's not a precision-targeted effect even without the need for an insulator Facet, which means having it last for ten hours minimum is not universally a benefit \u2014 at the same cost as Catastrophe (Strengthen with no added duration), Read the World's Loom, and most of the Warding Facets, the ability to introduce an environmental complication for most of a day or night with conditional immunities for you and your allies makes more sense as a tool of the hunt than spending several minutes building up the power to apply the same conditions for an hour or two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The success result specifically states it's &quot;unlikely to be as destructive as the Catastrophe Facet&quot; but that invoking it repetitively &quot;can have very serious results&quot; (<b>WtF2e p.136)</b>. </div> </div> </div>Catastrophe costs substantially more to use as a modifier on a second Facet and half of its options on that front start from &quot;strengthen a potentially destructive natural element in a radius measured in miles.&quot; Most environments can weather an isolated incident of sudden rainfall, but Catastrophe is set up for large bursts of elemental power in line with natural disasters worthy of the Facet's name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T17:15:47-08:00","id":1360611,"title":"","content":"I couldn't find the answer to this in either the corebook or <i>Shunned</i>: How do the Pure increase Renown? Do they receive their crimson brands from powerful Totems instead of Lunes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T18:02:47-08:00","id":1360615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1360611#post1360611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't find the answer to this in either the corebook or <i>Shunned</i>: How do the Pure increase Renown? Do they receive their crimson brands from powerful Totems instead of Lunes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T07:30:46-08:00","id":1370755,"title":"","content":"Is it metaphysically possible for Forsaken to switch Tribes, and more importantly, Tribal Oaths? Are the Pure beholden to the same rules or are Pure Firstborn more jealous than that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:27:19-08:00","id":1370780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1370755#post1370755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it metaphysically possible for Forsaken to switch Tribes, and more importantly, Tribal Oaths? Are the Pure beholden to the same rules or are Pure Firstborn more jealous than that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it's possible to switch tribes (it's a key element of becoming Pure, after all). It is a metaphysically weighted system, though (and as you note moreso for the Pure). While the Firstborn have their own desires that can be sometimes borne out through tribe members, the bigger issue is the social one. Being part of a tribe can mean (providing you were an involved member) you know tribal secrets, and some of your friends and allies were part of that tribe. Switching over can be seen as an act of betrayal, or at least one that forever marks the person as someone you can't trust or someone who's indecisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:29:16-07:00","id":1374068,"title":"","content":"Question on odd Rite case question...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1197077-2e-uratha-and-languages?p=1197293#post1197293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pack Rite - Shared Tongue (\u2022)</b><br /> This rite invokes ancient laws of Shadow Realm that Pack speak in one voice. Ritemaster\u2019s languages become known to all Pack members \u2013 even First Tongue.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Tongue, sharing, pack, First Tongue<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> Ritemaster makes invocations to Gods of Shadow Realm in First Tounge. Pack is joining in chorus of invocations. Then Ritemaster is splitting sacrificed tounge of the being and gives to all pack members on ceremony. Everyone swallow their parts and continue invocations. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (5 successes; each roll represents 1 minute);<br /> <b>Success:</b> This rite shares all known languages by ritemaster to all pack members. For one full lunar month all participants know those languages. If ritemaster know First Tongue, they also know it \u2013 but without non-human forms physicality they may not be able to articulate words in it. However they understand what ritemaster understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>If <i>Shared Tounge</i> is Pack Rite, and one of Uratha was <i><b>not</b></i> partaking in it, should he have benefits of it also? Corebook here says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p.138</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pack Rites</b> are reliant upon the spiritual bond that ties a pack together, amplifying or using it as a channel. Such shamanic rites empower all within a pack, whether they are Uratha, human, or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:36:46-07:00","id":1374069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374068#post1374068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">T<i>his rite shares all known languages by ritemaster to all pack members.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to suggest that yes it would affect the packmember even if they weren't personally involved in the rite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:39:43-07:00","id":1374070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374068#post1374068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>Shared Tounge</i> is Pack Rite, and one of Uratha was <i><b>not</b></i> partaking in it, should he have benefits of it also? Corebook here says:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. The passage in the book you quote is not saying that a Pack Rite's benefits spread across all pack members no matter where they are in the world. It's saying that non-Uratha packmates (humans, Wolf-Blooded, any local weirdos) also benefit when they participate in a Pack Rite, unlike Wolf Rites, whose benefits are only conferred to Uratha participants.<br /> <br /> You could write a homebrew rite whose effects are conferred even to non-participants, as a weird exception case. But it'd be weird and you usually shouldn't, because Rites are established as being communal in nature. You don't sit out a Rite. Rites are inclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-11-2020, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T19:19:15-07:00","id":1374474,"title":"","content":"...................","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25584,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","user":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","date":". 03-13-2020, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:04:14-07:00","id":1374478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374474#post1374474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly are the Mimics supposed to have come from? I never got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly an open question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:24:28-07:00","id":1374481,"title":"","content":"...........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25584,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","user":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","date":". 03-13-2020, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:37:40-07:00","id":1374484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374481#post1374481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right. I don't see how that's an open question. I'm just asking for an answer on the origin of the Mimics. Either a quick run-down or simply pointing me to the book/piece of fluff that contains it would be more than enough. Seems simple to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Satchel</b> meant that, by canon as it now, Mimcs do not have origin. They are only mentioned in <b>Night Horrors Shunned by the Moon</b> book - that's all. You need to ask author of them, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>, on their possible origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:48:08-07:00","id":1374485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374481#post1374481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. I don't see how that's an open question. I'm just asking for an answer on the origin of the Mimics. Either a quick run-down or simply pointing me to the book/piece of fluff that contains it would be more than enough. Seems simple to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire paragraph on the first page of their writeup dedicated to explaining that someone made the Mimics and that there's a conspiracy theory attributing their creation to Red Wolf. The second of the writeup's three addressed rumors explicitly says that nobody's entirely sure <i>who</i> made the Mimics. The first of the writeup's three addressed rumors says that prior to the modern incidence something very like Mimics occasionally came into being as freak occurrences.<br /> <br /> This indicates that there is no definite established answer to the question, i.e. it is an open question.<br /> <br /> The Mimics writeup is about two pages in all after accounting for sidebars and insert art. This is not hidden information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T23:17:59-07:00","id":1374511,"title":"","content":"Yes, basically everything in the Mimics section is everything concrete about them. The best lead is a rumor, and you can choose that to be fact in your game, or not.<br /> <br /> There's been a number of little things like this throughout the books that make me hopeful we're expecting a shard of some sort where something Big has happened to the Forsaken (an update to Mirrors was long ago suggested as coming out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2020, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T01:40:51-07:00","id":1374519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1374481#post1374481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. I don't see how that's an open question. I'm just asking for an answer on the origin of the Mimics. Either a quick run-down or simply pointing me to the book/piece of fluff that contains it would be more than enough. Seems simple to me.<br /> <br /> What are you even on about, troll? Ever since that Beast re-write thread I keep seeing you reply to my posts all over this site with the same confrontational tone and passive-agressive attitude. Go away. I have no wish to engage with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel was directly answering your question with the correct answer. The origins of Mimics hasn\u2019t been defined and you can\u2019t be pointed to any book that says otherwise.<br /> <br /> The only person being impolite here is you. Please tone it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T05:40:19-07:00","id":1375939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253147-who-can-see-through-the-mask-without-actively-using-a-power?p=1375893#post1375893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have coming changeling NPC to our Werewolf game - question is simple - <b>Do Uratha 'automatically' smell out the other monsters?</b> Or do they need to declare it and roll some dicepool against their target?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for a werewolf's sense of smell are on page 94. But no, they can't determine <i>what</i> other people are monsters unless they're Uratha or Wolf-Blooded. In the case of a changeling I would just mention whether the Mien has a distinct scent that isn't human (such as smoke from a fire elemental).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-21-2020, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T06:50:35-07:00","id":1375951,"title":"","content":"With changeling of this description, Uratha what would smell? Vines and fresh bushes? 'What appear to be tattoos are actually tiny vines wrapping around his arms, spelling out complex legal terms and burrowing into the skin. He is the person court \u2013 and Courts - come to for settling petty disputes.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T11:54:15-07:00","id":1375991,"title":"","content":"I think the thing is that the Mask is specifically called out as being penetrated by supernaturals. 'Fae beings and other supernatural creatures with mystical senses can see through the Mask.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:59:12-07:00","id":1376007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1375991#post1375991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing is that the Mask is specifically called out as being penetrated by supernaturals. 'Fae beings and other supernatural creatures with mystical senses can see through the Mask.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I migrate this question from the Changeling subforum only to discuss changelings anyway?<br /> As mentioned <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1253147-who-can-see-through-the-mask-without-actively-using-a-power\">here</a> a changeling's Mask is penetrated by supernatural senses, yes, but the supernatural sense will be the only thing that detects the Mien instead of the Mask. In Wyrd's example, the Uratha will smell plant matter because their sense of smell is supernatural, <i>provided that scent is strong enough</i>. Werewolf senses paints a holistic picture, with no focus on details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T21:39:48-07:00","id":1376209,"title":"","content":"Werewolves have all their senses ramped up, not just smell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T03:05:31-07:00","id":1376231,"title":"","content":"That is true, but the question is how many of the senses are supernatural in nature rather than only supernatural in origin. Anything that uses Primal Urge for scaling or in a dice pool is obviously supernatural, which would include both smell and hearing but not sight. Knowing the prey's location only by the taste of its blood is also obviously supernatural.<br /> The simplest would be to say that sight also is supernatural, but that's up for discussion.<br /> Either way, these are the wolf senses, which are by default not active in Hishu/Dalu. If you wish to see through the Mask of a changeling, you'll either have to specify that you use the wolf senses or be in Urhan/Urshul. (Gauru does not specify which senses are default.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T05:17:52-07:00","id":1376244,"title":"","content":"My quick opinion is that Uratha can\u2019t automatically sense through the Mask with their usual suite of senses. That\u2019s what Scent the Unnatural from the Gift of Insight is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:20:56-07:00","id":1378829,"title":"","content":"Is there more information on the &quot;Totem-Lords&quot; of the Pure? They get a lot of mention, especially in the newest Night Horrors, but it seems incredibly nebulous, probably on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:33:27-07:00","id":1381133,"title":"","content":"About the First Change, I've always read it as excluding clothes &amp; possessions that a person has on them at the time.<br /> Now some this wouldn't be the only way the First Change is different to later shapeshifting.<br /> That said I don't actually know for certain, &amp; the not knowing has started bugging me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T01:53:20-07:00","id":1381245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1381133#post1381133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the First Change, I've always read it as excluding clothes &amp; possessions that a person has on them at the time.<br /> Now some this wouldn't be the only way the First Change is different to later shapeshifting.<br /> That said I don't actually know for certain, &amp; the not knowing has started bugging me.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the time of the First Change, the character is a creature entirely of flesh. Her Harmony is supremely unbalanced towards Flesh, in the 9-10 range (probably 10). The events of the First Change are painful and scary and involve a lot of trauma. The character\u2019s clothes and belongings are destroyed as her Harmony is too high to shapeshift them with her. <br /> <br /> Through the course of the First Change most Uratha\u2019s Harmony drops a bit - probably to 8-9. It\u2019s still scary and a bit painful and her clothes still rip and tear until her Harmony drops to a comfortable 8 or less. <br /> <br /> By the time she\u2019s figured a few things out, learned some Gifts and had a few Breaking Points (is, becomes a starting player character) her Harmony is 7 and she\u2019s now much more comfortable with shapeshifting, and her clothes aren\u2019t being trashed all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T20:27:23-07:00","id":1381516,"title":"","content":"Edit: Answered elsewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-14-2020, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T16:51:55-07:00","id":1382012,"title":"","content":"Bowry Dogs say that werewolves don't really have to worry about addiction to substance-abuse. Is there any rules for how they shed Addicted over time or is it just generally assumed they never develop an actual chemical dependency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:57:06-07:00","id":1383183,"title":"","content":"What would be a fun ban and bane combo for a newly formed Lune?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:02:17-07:00","id":1383197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1383183#post1383183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a fun ban and bane combo for a newly formed Lune?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's Rank 1, I would keep it relatively simple. <br /> <br /> Ban: Can't manifest in any area not bathed by natural moonlight. <br /> Bane: Something related to the Sun, so gold, natural sunlight, or even something as simple as sunflowers or daylilies. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:57:43-07:00","id":1383399,"title":"","content":"Also because there are so many mechanics for Spirits that I constantly forget and overlook things, can any Spirit go into Twilight whenever? Do they need a locus to cross or can they just slip through the gauntlet whenever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:12:58-07:00","id":1383418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1383399#post1383399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also because there are so many mechanics for Spirits that I constantly forget and overlook things, can any Spirit go into Twilight whenever? Do they need a locus to cross or can they just slip through the gauntlet whenever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight only exist on the material side of the Gauntlet. Spirits need to use a Manifestation to get across the Gauntlet (and once they do they automatically enter Twilight unless there are other Manifestations at play). Funnily enough Loci are 100% optional for spirits.* They only make the roll easier.<br /> <br /> *With the exception of Claimed. All Claimed can pass through the Gauntlet even if they don't have any Manifestation to do so, but unlike other spirits it has to be at a Locus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-23-2020, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:13:23-07:00","id":1383419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1383399#post1383399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also because there are so many mechanics for Spirits that I constantly forget and overlook things, can any Spirit go into Twilight whenever? Do they need a locus to cross or can they just slip through the gauntlet whenever?</div> </div> </div> </div>They need an appropriate Manifestation or help, generally speaking. Loci are useful in that they provide a bonus, but Gauntlet Breach and Shadow Gateway work anywhere the appropriate Conditions exist between worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:43:51-07:00","id":1383533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1383418#post1383418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough Loci are 100% optional for spirits.* They only make the roll easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, WHAT? I always played spirits can only cross in Loci, that was my rules reading. Where is that they cross Gauntlet anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:18:33-07:00","id":1383538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1383533#post1383533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, WHAT? I always played spirits can only cross in Loci, that was my rules reading. Where is that they cross Gauntlet anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Core book pag 187, but Gauntlet breach and Shadow gateway requires respectively the Resonant and Open condition, so they cannot properly cross anywhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:48:12-07:00","id":1383607,"title":"","content":"Another Spirit question, this time about a Numen.<br /> <br /> Does Pathfinder automatically <b>deduce</b> a location? Or does it need a general area to sort of &quot;scan&quot; first?<br /> <br /> Also, because it just came up in my game a bit ago, if a spirit has Materialize but not Gauntlet Breach, can it still actually Materialize in the Flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","user":"Voytek","date":". 04-24-2020, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T07:03:24-07:00","id":1385073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1385071-2e-renown-questions#post1385071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Renown for other things than getting and activating Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honorary Rank and Hunter's Aspect comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:08:26-07:00","id":1386437,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain the Resonance -&gt; Essence -&gt; Spirit cycle to me? I've been reading the material and I'd like a concise explanation from someone else to hang mine off, to see if I've got it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:01:55-07:00","id":1386448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386437#post1386437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain the Resonance -&gt; Essence -&gt; Spirit cycle to me? I've been reading the material and I'd like a concise explanation from someone else to hang mine off, to see if I've got it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i understand, every strong specimen of every thing (items, animals, concepts) generates essence, if a spirit can feed on a particular flavour of essence it is said that the fount is Resonant for that spirit.<br /> Spirits need to feed from resonant essence regulary, to remain active and to grow.<br /> High rank spirits can use their powers to protect a source of essence, or requires a essence &quot;tax&quot; from lesser spirits under their domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:08:52-07:00","id":1386467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386437#post1386437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain the Resonance -&gt; Essence -&gt; Spirit cycle to me? I've been reading the material and I'd like a concise explanation from someone else to hang mine off, to see if I've got it right.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Resonance is spiritual flavour. Everything in the Flesh (material world; not the Shadow) is spiritually Resonant (which means everything has the appropriate Resonant Conditions).<ul><li>A fire has a fire Resonance (and the Resonant Condition for fire).</li> </ul></li> <li>Objects and locations generates Essence that share the same resonance as its source.<ul><li>A fire generates Essence that has a fire resonance (aka, fire Essence).</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirits also match resonances (though we generally refer it to their nature or their Influences, just to make it a little less confusing), and they feed on Essence that has compatible resonance.<ul><li>A spirit of a fire nature (aka, a fire spirit) feeds on fire Essence.</li> </ul></li> <li>Essence that is not eaten or otherwise removed may coalesce into motes (Rank 0 spirits) that naturally grows if they are near appropriate Resonances.<ul><li>A fire generates fire Essence that coalesce into a mote. If the fire continues to burn for a long time or is repeatedly reignited, the mote may become a sentient spirit with time.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Technically this is not a cycle. Essence generates naturally and spirits doesn't have to do anything, but spirits are hungry and competitive so if they can they will try to maximise the amount of Essence of the appropriate type that generates. The fire spirit would use its Influence: Fire to start new fires so that more fire Essence is generated.<br /> <br /> (Stronger Resonances are supposed to grant more Essence, but this is not reflected in the game rules except when it comes to Loci. This means a fire spirit should want to increase the size and intensity of a preexisting fire because that would cause the fire to generate more Essence. The problem is that the roll for gaining Essence is based on the spirit's own traits so in practice it's larger spirits that <i>pull</i> more Essence from Resonances rather than the intensity of the Resonances <i>generating</i> varying amounts of Essence. I recommend just skipping that rule and just grant an amount of Essence appropriate for the situation if you want to track the Essence pool of a spirit.)<br /> <br /> Also note that Resonances can be a lot more abstract than &quot;object A has Resonance A&quot;. A fire will Resonate fire but also Resonate light and heat, as well as more abstract concepts like destruction (if it's a destructive fire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:00:32-07:00","id":1386481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386467#post1386467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Resonance is spiritual flavour. Everything in the Flesh (material world; not the Shadow) is spiritually Resonant (which means everything has the appropriate Resonant Conditions).<ul><li>A fire has a fire Resonance (and the Resonant Condition for fire).</li> </ul></li> <li>Objects and locations generates Essence that share the same resonance as its source.<ul><li>A fire generates Essence that has a fire resonance (aka, fire Essence).</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirits also match resonances (though we generally refer it to their nature or their Influences, just to make it a little less confusing), and they feed on Essence that has compatible resonance.<ul><li>A spirit of a fire nature (aka, a fire spirit) feeds on fire Essence.</li> </ul></li> <li>Essence that is not eaten or otherwise removed may coalesce into motes (Rank 0 spirits) that naturally grows if they are near appropriate Resonances.<ul><li>A fire generates fire Essence that coalesce into a mote. If the fire continues to burn for a long time or is repeatedly reignited, the mote may become a sentient spirit with time.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Technically this is not a cycle. Essence generates naturally and spirits doesn't have to do anything, but spirits are hungry and competitive so if they can they will try to maximise the amount of Essence of the appropriate type that generates. The fire spirit would use its Influence: Fire to start new fires so that more fire Essence is generated.<br /> <br /> (Stronger Resonances are supposed to grant more Essence, but this is not reflected in the game rules except when it comes to Loci. This means a fire spirit should want to increase the size and intensity of a preexisting fire because that would cause the fire to generate more Essence. The problem is that the roll for gaining Essence is based on the spirit's own traits so in practice it's larger spirits that <i>pull</i> more Essence from Resonances rather than the intensity of the Resonances <i>generating</i> varying amounts of Essence. I recommend just skipping that rule and just grant an amount of Essence appropriate for the situation if you want to track the Essence pool of a spirit.)<br /> <br /> Also note that Resonances can be a lot more abstract than &quot;object A has Resonance A&quot;. A fire will Resonate fire but also Resonate light and heat, as well as more abstract concepts like destruction (if it's a destructive fire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. I'm only vaguely aware of motes from this forum. What book are they present in? As for essence generation, would the flesh not be awash with essence that hasn't yet leaked through the gauntlet. How come wolves can only tap loci for essence if this is the case?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:34:15-07:00","id":1386496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386481#post1386481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect. I'm only vaguely aware of motes from this forum. What book are they present in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386481#post1386481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for essence generation, would the flesh not be awash with essence that hasn't yet leaked through the gauntlet. How come wolves can only tap loci for essence if this is the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a wait between the generation of Essence and the Essence pushing through the Gauntlet. The natural place for Essence is the Shadow, and I think any generated Essence ends up there. It might be more useful to think of the Gauntlet as dampening the generation of Essence rather than stopping generated Essence from seeping through.<br /> <br /> Either that or werewolves just have no natural ability to take in free floating Essence. Almost all the ways for werewolves to gain Essence requires physically manipulating (sometimes by devouring) something that stores Essence. For loci this means touching the focus object or eating the manifested Essence in the Shadow. The only exception I can think of is the auspice moon, which is basically Resonant for werewolves.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now that I think about it, any Essence in the material world would naturally be in Twilight, and werewolves have no innate means of physically affecting anything in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:21:27-07:00","id":1386511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386496#post1386496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386496#post1386496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The natural place for Essence is the Shadow</div> </div> </div> </div>The book contradicts this on page 182 when talking about Spirits fettering themselves to resonant people. The spirit is 'safe from starvation as long as the host generates enough Essence to feed it.' Nothing is said about the gauntlet nor the spirit reaching back to the Hisil to feed. Essence seems to exist in the Flesh, though I agree it is likely a twilight phenomena. Further, your answer that Werewolves lack the means to engage with it beyond what is spelt out for them in the core book would explain why they don't have an infinite supply of Essence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:04:08-07:00","id":1386524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386511#post1386511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page?</div> </div> </div> </div>180<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386511#post1386511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book contradicts this on page 182 when talking about Spirits fettering themselves to resonant people. The spirit is 'safe from starvation as long as the host generates enough Essence to feed it.' Nothing is said about the gauntlet nor the spirit reaching back to the Hisil to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't mention the Gauntlet or the Shadow because the spirit is already in the Flesh, intercepting the natural process. Naturally, Essence generated in the Flesh does move through the Gauntlet and into the Shadow, but it may do so too rapidly to accumulate in the Flesh (unless someone hooks themselves up directly to the output, i.e. Spirit-Ridden) in most cases. When the Essence do accumulate, it forms a locus unless someone siphons it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:34:56-07:00","id":1386542,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. So, one might find an area awash in essence when the gauntlet is thickened but otherwise, that would be the exception and the rate of generation wouldn't lag behind the transfer rate by much. For example: Spirits that get word of a major sporting event, for example, might invade the Flesh for a feast, explaining the buzz of a crowd as the nearby spirits reinforce the competitive resonance. They do this because the sudden influx and concentration of humans would thicken the gauntlet for a period, and it is first come, first serve for spirits. If the wolves beat back the invasion, then the extra essence would eventually flow through but by that point, the concentration might be enough to generate new spirits and loci altogether.<br /> <br /> It is coming together as a system in my head. So long as I can consistently rule in-game, I'll be more or less content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:46:57-07:00","id":1386550,"title":"","content":"Spirits generally don't invade the Flesh unless they're forced to or is looking to Urge or Claim a fitting target. Essence bleed becomes worse than in the Shadow, and bypassing the Gauntlet to feed on Essence directly from the source would rarely be worth the effort and cost involved. (At least, according to the rules for gorging on Resonant Conditions, where the Gauntlet is just a penalty.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:47:28-07:00","id":1386551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386481#post1386481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How come wolves can only tap loci for essence if this is the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>While werewolves are part spirit and part flesh, they are wholly neither. They don't need Essence to survive except at high ranks of Primal Urge, and they get it differently. So they do not have an innate mechanism for devouring Essence the way spirits do (outside of eating people and other werewolves, which is verboten). In their own world, Pangaea (detailed in Dark Eras, but now gone) every act of the hunt was effectively a sacred hunt, allowing them to sate themselves of the needs of their primal urge. As the world is gone, they are forced to use the Sacred Hunt rite as a medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:26:21-07:00","id":1386565,"title":"","content":"Elements of the physical world generally create resonance(s) around them. A river might have resonances of life, travel, and water, among others. These resonances leak through the Gauntlet, making zones that spirits can harvest for Essence. Humans are particularly good at generating all kinds of complicated resonances, especially emotionally-charged ones.<br /> <br /> When a spirit is on the flesh side of the Gauntlet, they\u2019re tapping into the Resonance directly. It\u2019s not being filtered through the Gauntlet to pool for others to take, the spirit can take it from the source. As an imperfect metaphor, it can be like the difference between drinking a beer poured straight from the tap versus one that you\u2019ve purchased in a can. Normal spirit feeding isn\u2019t going to exhaust a resonance, but spirits are greedy and their Influences often align with the resonances they feed from so they use them to inflame the resonance and give themselves more to gorge on. Unchecked, this often leads to burning out the source of the resonance.<br /> <br /> When resonance pools on an object or creature and no spirits come to sup at it the accumulation can turn that object/creature into a locus.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can\u2019t access Essence as easily as spirits because they\u2019re creatures of half flesh and spirit. They have a bunch of advantages from that but also a few disadvantages such as less ready access to Essence and needing to Reach at a locus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:46:04-07:00","id":1386568,"title":"","content":"I might have to make this a trend. Not that I don't get it; just full of questions. Does Werewolf have an Errata?<br /> <br /> After going back through the book, I did find some seeming contradictions. Pg 71 notes that 'Resonance creates the conditions in the material world to generate essence in the shadow.' However, this disagrees with a few other passages, and is somewhat awkwardly put anyway. I would call Resonance the condition, not the condition's cause. Otherwise, what is the condition? Elsewhere, it is confirmed, as others and yourself have said, that Essence is found in the physical world and passes into the spiritual world.<br /> <br /> I also found some really interesting elements that only stuck out because I was doing such a close reading. For example, on page 184, it says that spirits need to spend an essence per day to remain active. This is true even in the Shadow. However, if they fail to do so, they go dormant. Dormancy is said to be dangerous because a spirit remains in twilight and can be destroyed. The weirdness is the implication that exhaustion in the Hisil puts you in a state of twilight. To be fair, the passage explaining twilight says it is more a state of being than place in the physical but does that mean that a Shadow twilight exists?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:19:41-07:00","id":1386576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386568#post1386568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weirdness is the implication that exhaustion in the Hisil puts you in a state of twilight. To be fair, the passage explaining twilight says it is more a state of being than place in the physical but does that mean that a Shadow twilight exists?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a case of the generalized Ephemeral Beings mechanics being pared down in Werewolf; ghosts with Anchors and angels remain in the material world in a state of Twilight, but spirits are pulled back into the Shadow when they enter dormancy \u2014 see the rest of the note on page 184.<br /> <br /> Twilight is the natural state of being for ephemera, and everything in the Shadow is made of ephemera. The only situation so far where an entity can be in a Twilight-like state in the Shadow exists in Mage, where this is a specifically weird extra effect on a normal &quot;enter spiritual Twilight&quot; spell and it's keeping company with other quirks like &quot;you can make the local Gauntlet lower in only one direction&quot; or &quot;you can create a locus, but making it generate Essence is an added quirk.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:30:03-07:00","id":1386582,"title":"","content":"That also makes sense. So Twilight might technically exist, but in the Shadow, it is a meaningless state. Cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T04:38:18-07:00","id":1386658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1386568#post1386568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Werewolf have an Errata?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish. OPP does not release errata for their CofD books at all. If people talk about errata, they're referring to the final public editing pass before the book goes to print.<br /> The only reason I've been given for the lack of errata is that OPP doesn't want to make any physical books bought by consumers outdated, but this does in no way prevent them from having it just be a complementary document. You know, <i>which was done for the first edition core book</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:36:25-07:00","id":1386903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1386899-2e-harmony-questions#post1386899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Tribal Oath permanent Ban Condition on particular Uratha? [/B]I ask as one PC in our game have lowered Harmony to Ban territory ( Harmony 4 ). His Tribal Oath would make great Ban Condition to him. However, I'm not sureif Tribal Oath, de facto, <i>already</i> the Ban of all Tribes characters - only it's not written for all of them on sheets. <b>Rephrasing the question then - Is Tribal Oath hard ( rules-wise ) Ban Condition on everyone - or just guidance for tribes characters?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A tribal character's given extra facet of the Oath is mechanically a thing that will cause their Harmony to veer away from Spirit. It is <i>absolutely not</i> a Ban in the mechanical sense of the Condition, which is <i>a spiritual compulsion that is difficult to break</i>, which even a pack's ban doesn't start out as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:15:09-07:00","id":1387126,"title":"","content":"So I came across a line in Lore of the Forsaken that implies that Uratha can get possessed. Wondering am I interpreting that correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:22:35-07:00","id":1387127,"title":"","content":"Uratha can get possessed and Claimed just like anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:30:24-07:00","id":1387141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1387126#post1387126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I came across a line in Lore of the Forsaken that implies that Uratha can get possessed. Wondering am I interpreting that correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Voytek says it can happen to werewolves. In second edition the Bound from Geist: Sin-Eaters are the only gameline inherently immune to possession or claiming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:49:24-07:00","id":1387149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1387141#post1387141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Voytek says it can happen to werewolves. In second edition the Bound from Geist: Sin-Eaters are the only gameline inherently immune to possession or claiming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't Mummies also immune to possession?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:18:45-07:00","id":1387154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1387149#post1387149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Mummies also immune to possession?</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked through it the first time but just checked for Claiming so I missed it, double-checking found their Ephemeral Ward ability, so yes you're right, Mummies and Sin-Eaters, though it may have some workarounds with powers that aren't Possess.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ephemeral Ward: Ephemeral entities (p. XX) are incapable of possessing mummies. Any attempt to use the Possess Manifestation (p. XX) on a mummy automatically fails.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-09-2020, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:08:48-07:00","id":1387324,"title":"","content":"If Claimed is killed not with spirit's Bane but with claws/teeth of a werewolf, will the spirit survive or not? Will it be posessing the corpse? Will it die forever? Will it die and re-appear (if it had Essence)? Or will it just leave the Claimed body and have all it's Corpus untouched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:22:24-07:00","id":1387328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1387324#post1387324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Claimed is killed not with spirit's Bane but with claws/teeth of a werewolf, will the spirit survive or not? Will it be posessing the corpse? Will it die forever? Will it die and re-appear (if it had Essence)? Or will it just leave the Claimed body and have all it's Corpus untouched?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe so, unless the Claimed is hurt by it's Bane I don't think the Spirit itself takes any damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T16:50:59-07:00","id":1388790,"title":"","content":"Would supernaturals powers from other splats (like mage's spells of Vampire's disciplines) do aggravated damage to Werewolves? Or they suffer agg only from silver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T17:06:49-07:00","id":1388792,"title":"","content":"That is expressly, and almost verbatim brought up as things that cause aggravated damage to Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T10:04:53-07:00","id":1388979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1388790#post1388790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would supernaturals powers from other splats (like mage's spells of Vampire's disciplines) do aggravated damage to Werewolves? Or they suffer agg only from silver?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each source of damage dictates what type of damage it deals. Punches and electricity deal bashing damage, weapons and fire deal lethal damage, and a few sources cause aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Unless it is stated specifically that a particular creature takes a particular damage type from a particular source (like werewolves taking aggravated damage from silver, and vampires taking bashing damage from weapons), the damage type is the default one for that source.<br /> <br /> Which means that things like 4th-dot mage attack spells with an extra reach to change the damage type to aggravated, or a vampire's claws with Protean 4 and the Claws of the Unholy Merit while in frenzy deal aggravated damage to werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:48:26-07:00","id":1389586,"title":"","content":"The Duration of the Feet of Mist Gift is 1 hour. When this duration ends do the traces it hid previously re-appear or they just don't exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T10:17:28-07:00","id":1389688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1389586#post1389586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duration of the Feet of Mist Gift is 1 hour. When this duration ends do the traces it hid previously re-appear or they just don't exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would seem more like you just start leaving traces again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:18:57-07:00","id":1391283,"title":"","content":"A Uratha gets one essence when they see their auspice moon in the sky for the first time. I presume that doesn't mean 'for the first time, ever, forever, and never again' but just for the first time that night. As such, do they get their auspice essence across a span of time? If so, does this mean that Raha and such get less 'natural' essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:37:58-07:00","id":1391301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391283#post1391283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Uratha gets one essence when they see their auspice moon in the sky for the first time. I presume that doesn't mean 'for the first time, ever, forever, and never again' but just for the first time that night. As such, do they get their auspice essence across a span of time? If so, does this mean that Raha and such get less 'natural' essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between five and six Essence per month, and the two fives get theirs all in a row. It's not a huge distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:54:49-07:00","id":1391381,"title":"","content":"Really? When I looked at a moon chart, it looked like the New Moon, Half Moon, and Full Moon got much less than Gibbous and Crescent. I had one player assert that Full Moon only occurred once. (I'm aware how petty this sounds but) Is there an official chart/table that I can use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:31:22-07:00","id":1391397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391381#post1391381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? When I looked at a moon chart, it looked like the New Moon, Half Moon, and Full Moon got much less than Gibbous and Crescent. I had one player assert that Full Moon only occurred once. (I'm aware how petty this sounds but) Is there an official chart/table that I can use?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's math.<br /> <br /> Approximately twenty-eight days to a lunar month, divided five ways, results (approximately) in five days of a New Moon, three days of Crescent Moon, three days of Half Moon, three days of Gibbous Moon, five days of Full Moon, three days of Gibbous Moon, three days of Half Moon, three days of Crescent Moon, and back to the start. Unless you're <i>really</i> finely slicing when moon phases change or running a very weird chronicle, the phases of the moon shift at a fairly regular interval in the Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T20:58:59-07:00","id":1391411,"title":"","content":"The math doesn't capture the 'dynamics' of the lunar calendar though. Consider this moon chart: <a href=\"https://www.moongiant.com/calendar/May/2020\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.moongiant.com/calendar/May/2020</a><br /> <br /> The chart goes with the extreme view that there is a single Full Moon, a single New Moon, and two half moons, the first and last quarter respectively. The rest is gibbous and crescent. This view is one that one of my players was backing, based on how the moon appeared in the images. They talked about the border of a gibbous being present, and such.<br /> <br /> If I use illumination to bracket the moons for a more 'objective' approach, I get interesting results based on the numbers used to define the range of the bracket. An even split for the period I measured, where the first bracket is 0-20%, the next 20%-40%, and so forth, makes the New Moon and Full Moon incredibly long. Meanwhile, an 'eyeballed' bracket gives Gibbous and Crescent more wiggle room leaves Half Moon and Full Moon with four and five days respectively. Sadly, Half Moon is always the least present (of my TWO sets.) Using the illumination method, and 0% as the ends of the lunar cycle, gave me a 31 day cycle as well. This is wrong, as you point out, but softening the edges would just mean even less time for New Moon. That and I got 31 days by counting, so even though it is definitely wrong, I'm not sure how I mucked that up.<br /> <br /> I guess this really just comes down to a judgement call and resumption of play. But I felt like spelling out my situation, because I opened a can of worms and was wondering anyone had a lid handy. XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  inconsistent lunar nights 05-25-2020, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:12:34-07:00","id":1391416,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty interesting worm can, though. If some are getting less Essence, (especially with an entire pack of similar auspice) it would suggest they might need to rely more on loci.<br /> <br /> There should probably be a condition attached to it. I appreciate the writers might not want to force players to rely on moon calendars (or, more harshly, actual times and dates) in their games, but it might be incentive if there was an auspice-related Gift you could get with that first Essence. Or if instead of getting that 1 Essence, you had a condition that let you get Essence by behaving certain ways.<br /> <br /> Though Essence shortage isn't really an issue in any game I've played, it could just be a cool way to get them doing stuff with the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-25-2020, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T23:28:43-07:00","id":1391430,"title":"","content":"I run with Moon Calendars and players don't complain. Gibbous and Crescent Moons, by Ithaeur and Cahalith Auspices, are already more 'mystical' and naturally flow to seek other sources of Essence - not only Loci, but also sacrifices and Gathra.<br /> <br /> Here is Moon Calendar for my 800 AD Vikings game in month of June - most of Auspices are not loosing on this one:<ul><li>Full Moon \u2013 30.05-1.06</li> <li>Gibbous Moon \u2013 2-6.06</li> <li>Half Moon \u2013 7-9.06</li> <li>Crescent Moon \u2013 10-13.06</li> <li>New Moon \u201314-16.06</li> <li>Crescent Moon\u2013 17-21.06</li> <li>Half Moon \u2013 22-24.06</li> <li>Gibbous Moon \u2013 25-28.06</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:15:54-07:00","id":1391445,"title":"","content":"Do spirits add their Defence against firearms? And if no do the stalwart ones do? And do firearms work in Hisil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T05:24:55-07:00","id":1391464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391445#post1391445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do spirits add their Defence against firearms? And if no do the stalwart ones do?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;COMBAT<br /> As noted earlier, spirits use the lower of Power or Finesse for Defense unless they are Rank 1, in which case they use the higher. They apply Defense against all attacks, even firearms.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391445#post1391445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And do firearms work in Hisil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason for why they wouldn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T06:41:59-07:00","id":1391470,"title":"","content":"Hey question, when it says you get a beat from &quot;taking lethal damage in one of your rightmost health boxes&quot; does it mean the right half of your health track? And does that mean you get a beat for EACH damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T06:48:30-07:00","id":1391472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391470#post1391470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey question, when it says you get a beat from &amp;quot;taking lethal damage in one of your rightmost health boxes&amp;quot; does it mean the right half of your health track? And does that mean you get a beat for EACH damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means one of the rightmost three boxes, and given you can only take one beat per type per scene, you do not receive a beat for each box","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T06:50:24-07:00","id":1391473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1391472#post1391472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It means one of the rightmost three boxes, and given you can only take one beat per type per scene, you do not receive a beat for each box</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, that's what I thought it was but I never noticed the wording before and it confused the hell out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T15:35:47-07:00","id":1394441,"title":"","content":"Hey, so I was reading the Leg Wrack Tilt and it says, under ending the Tilt, that 'If the damage that inflicts this Tilt is aggravated, the character loses use of his leg permanently.' Now, that is awesome. It is horrific and gives combat some serious teeth. My question is whether this applies to Werewolves. Nothing in the condition text would preclude them, but seriously, Werewolves regenerate and shapeshift. Even a serious leg injury is only a time penalty for them. So, is this something I need to homerule or is there something I am missing?<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it. Page 178: 'Tilts dealt with aggravated damage cause permanent disability \u2014 to humans, at least. A werewolf \u2019s regenerative powers can re-grow even missing limbs.'<br /> <br /> This is also wrote on page 178. 'Tilts provide a way of handling drugs, poisons, sickness, and environmental and weather effects, but only as they apply to combat. Out of combat, use the normal rules for these effects.' I don't really know what this means, especially with regard to permanent effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Used the index like a big boy. 06-05-2020, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:02:03-07:00","id":1394445,"title":"","content":"Medical conditions are usually handled by Conditions when out of combat, and as Tilts when in combat. I.e. losing an arm leads to the Arm Wrack Tilt, but when combat ends you instead take a Condition to represent the lost arm.<br /> <br /> Extreme environments also have their own separate rules, but I've previously found it pretty unclear when to apply extreme environment rules and when to apply them as environmental Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:25:17-07:00","id":1394447,"title":"","content":"If you want a big write up on conditions for stuff like missing limbs and stuff, I'd recommend picking up Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T20:54:16-07:00","id":1394494,"title":"","content":"My search function is being silly, so I do apologize if this has been asked:<br /> <br /> In 2E, with werewolf regenerative abilities being able to regrow limbs and whatnot - how do scars work? <br /> <br /> I would expect wounds that heal slowly - like from silver or another supernatural effect to scar up, but what about regular ol' injuries?<br /> <br /> Player Choice? ST decision? Or am I missing a rule in the books somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T20:57:49-07:00","id":1394495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1394494#post1394494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My search function is being silly, so I do apologize if this has been asked:<br /> <br /> In 2E, with werewolf regenerative abilities being able to regrow limbs and whatnot - how do scars work? <br /> <br /> I would expect wounds that heal slowly - like from silver or another supernatural effect to scar up, but what about regular ol' injuries?<br /> <br /> Player Choice? ST decision? Or am I missing a rule in the books somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly player choice. If they want cool scars they can have them.<br /> <br /> If the ST wants a big bad to be particularly noteworthy they can feel free to have their attacks leave scars, which should reinforce in player\u2019s minds that this thing is a concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T23:14:10-07:00","id":1397457,"title":"","content":"Is there an explanation for where the name &quot;Geryo&quot; comes? In-universe I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T23:40:01-07:00","id":1397459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1397457#post1397457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an explanation for where the name &quot;Geryo&quot; comes? In-universe I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Shunned by the Moon, p153, 'The First adopt the classical names given them by myth and fable, shucking the hated First Tongue name that once collared them.' This gives us two big options. One, from Greek and the mythological giant <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geryon\" target=\"_blank\">Geryon</a>. Two, as they have a history in Japan, and it may be the place where they were released way back aroudn 794 CE \u2013 1185 CE, it's possible Geryo means something in Japanese, but I have no idea. Some google searches suggest ge could mean low, and ryo hunting, so that could fit, but I know nothing about the language least of all how accurate that is and would probably stick with the Geryon giant, as they seem to enjoy similar names, such as Orthus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-19-2020, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:41:01-07:00","id":1398028,"title":"","content":"What's happen when a werewolf in Garou suffers more aggravated damages than his human health points form? Does he suddenly die when getting back to his human form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:43:43-07:00","id":1398042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1398028#post1398028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's happen when a werewolf in Garou suffers more aggravated damages than his human health points form? Does he suddenly die when getting back to his human form?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a sidebar about this in the Healing and Wounds section on p172. But short answer yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T23:26:16-07:00","id":1401066,"title":"","content":"Would making a custom set of personal kuruth triggers be homebrew or is that intended to be normal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T23:52:24-07:00","id":1401069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1401066#post1401066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would making a custom set of personal kuruth triggers be homebrew or is that intended to be normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. You're encouraged to make your own, they would be homebrew, and that's just an accepted part of the game. We even have a couple threads with them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers\">here </a>and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers\">here</a>, with writers and devs popping in some of their own ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T00:02:14-07:00","id":1401071,"title":"","content":"Beaten Down and Surrender and gauru.<br /> Let's say I want to just dominate my opponent without killing him, even if he is a pure or a forsaken dangerous enemy or another random werewolf.<br /> Beaten Down can be used in gauru as rule? Or do we have to bite and slash the fuck out from us until gauru's turns end?<br /> With gifts like Berserker's Might, fortified forms and others things like that I never seen an health bar becoming aggravated from lethal in a gauru vs gauru fight.<br /> Plus, gauru has Rage. That's make beaten down a little bit.... not realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T21:36:03-07:00","id":1401268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1401071#post1401071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beaten Down and Surrender and gauru.<br /> Let's say I want to just dominate my opponent without killing him, even if he is a pure or a forsaken dangerous enemy or another random werewolf.<br /> Beaten Down can be used in gauru as rule? Or do we have to bite and slash the fuck out from us until gauru's turns end?<br /> With gifts like Berserker's Might, fortified forms and others things like that I never seen an health bar becoming aggravated from lethal in a gauru vs gauru fight.<br /> Plus, gauru has Rage. That's make beaten down a little bit.... not realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Beaten Down's just there so when, for example, John the Killer needs the Key from Jeff the Guard, but it doesn't make sense for Jeff to fight to the death. It's a quick way to end combat using the Intent rules (where you decide what your character wants out of combat) and have it given over. You do that amount of damage, Jeff is Beaten Down, and he gives John the Key.<br /> <br /> Generally with Gauru what you use is Down and Dirty, which just means, one roll, and your goal is done. Your gauru wants to dominate? Down and Dirty. Success? Those people are hurt and dominated, but alive. Failure? they probably ran away.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Beaten Down doesn't work well against werewolves, I think it says it in the section. Core, p165, 'These rules only apply to people who would incur a breaking point for committing (or attempting) \u201cmurder.\u201d <b>Most Uratha \u2014 along with other creatures that don\u2019t have a problem killing people \u2014 can ignore surrender without penalty and don\u2019t get Beaten Down</b>.'<br /> <br /> A way to do something similar with werewolves is through the Lay Low the Challenger Facet, fantastic one in the Dominate Gift. Hit someone, activate, target resists or is now Cowed. 'She suffers a \u20132 penalty on any Physical and Social rolls to oppose the character who inflicted this Condition if she does not spend Willpower.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:10:02-07:00","id":1404275,"title":"","content":"So I'm making a character for a future game of Werewolf, and I am being fairly ambitious on this one and I need a little help<br /> <br /> I plan on making a cahalith with a Lune following him around. Before his first change, he was a Wolf-Blooded who always wanted to truly he part of the Pack. Unknown to him, a Lune had taken interest in him and kinda, well forced the first change to happen. <br /> <br /> Now, he suffers from dreams bizarre even by Cahalith standards due to the Lune. This is the part that I struggle with. I plan on modifying Prophetic dreams. The general idea is that it has even more wisdom in it that can be gleaned from it, but can also give mental conditions. I just dont know how I could balance well. I would like to present it to my storyteller in a state that would not need much tweaking if he had issue with it. Can I please get a little help here? I also wonder how I should present the Lune. As of now I'm thinking it should be a sorta frenemy/Poisonous friend, but other ideas are welcome.<br /> <br /> Also, uh, is Secrets of the Tribes still on the table as a possible book? It would really be great as a I have always a had slight difficulty fully establishing my characters' relationships with their Tribes and how I can apply them to my individual story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:26:13-07:00","id":1404277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1404275#post1404275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, he suffers from dreams bizarre even by Cahalith standards due to the Lune. This is the part that I struggle with. I plan on modifying Prophetic dreams. The general idea is that it has even more wisdom in it that can be gleaned from it, but can also give mental conditions. I just dont know how I could balance well. I would like to present it to my storyteller in a state that would not need much tweaking if he had issue with it. Can I please get a little help here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make him subject to the effects of the Lunatic Inspiration Facet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:35:54-07:00","id":1404280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1404277#post1404277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make him subject to the effects of the Lunatic Inspiration Facet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now I feel dumb for not seeing such an obvious answer lol. Ok that should work, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T20:57:42-07:00","id":1414504,"title":"","content":"Is the relationship between Beshilu and Fire Touched a unique one? From what I've always understood, the fire touched worship the spirits, or really more the Hisil itself, but do yall see them as also sorta stewards to it? Like surely they wouldnt approve of Hosts breaking the barriers between worlds, but they also want paradise back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T21:36:30-07:00","id":1414507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1414504#post1414504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the relationship between Beshilu and Fire Touched a unique one? From what I've always understood, the fire touched worship the spirits, or really more the Hisil itself, but do yall see them as also sorta stewards to it? Like surely they wouldnt approve of Hosts breaking the barriers between worlds, but they also want paradise back</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're likely to find a lot of fire-touched who don't appreciate the beshilu damaging the gauntlet, even if you do find others who would like them wanting to rip the gauntlet open.<br /> <br /> That said, azlu are called out a few times in first edition as a source of a fix if Forsaken needed the Gauntlet repaired and didn't have other powers that can allow it. You could probably do the same now, I wouldn't encourage a long term relationship without a lot of bumps, though. The toad hosts, in Shunned by the Moon, are also able to develop relationships with werewolves due to their more neutral (but manipulative) outlook on everything. When it comes to others I'd probably go the same route with azlu, close relationships would be rare and more a result of unique circumstance for individuals and smaller groups instead of 'this tribe does x, this host do y, they're friends,' as well as one fraught with danger, since hosts are battered by supernatural urges just like werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T17:30:11-07:00","id":1415137,"title":"","content":"Something I've always been confused about. Are Coalesced Idigram taking of concepts that cant be, or are they simply taking the form of something so specific that it should not have spiritual reflections? I've always been confused by that, and to my understanding, there was an ancient Idigram who's coalesced form represented Deja Vu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T18:58:21-07:00","id":1415146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415137#post1415137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've always been confused about. Are Coalesced Idigram taking of concepts that cant be, or are they simply taking the form of something so specific that it should not have spiritual reflections? I've always been confused by that, and to my understanding, there was an ancient Idigram who's coalesced form represented Deja Vu</div> </div> </div> </div>Coalesced Idigam take on concepts that are at work in the environment when they Coalesce, but their relationship to that concept is askew from what spirits of those concepts would be.<br /> <br /> Typical spirits basically are what they eat, and as a rule generally seek a propogation of their essence in the environment so as to eat more and more and possibly move up the food chain as they develop courts to sustain them while playing to higher predators above them.<br /> <br /> An Idigam eats what it is, of course, but at the end of the day, it's not <i>really</i> those things, and as such it's more experimental in what it can do/be and how it can fill it's other inscrutable ends. Of course, since this is a very weird thing, they can be obsessive in finding out their results and answers.<br /> <br /> But yeah, a Coalsced Idigam metaphorically pokes it's belly button where a typical spirit doesn't even acknowledge it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:37:27-07:00","id":1415153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415137#post1415137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've always been confused about. Are Coalesced Idigram taking of concepts that cant be, or are they simply taking the form of something so specific that it should not have spiritual reflections? I've always been confused by that, and to my understanding, there was an ancient Idigram who's coalesced form represented Deja Vu</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a story hook about an ancient idigam that became <i>the concept of translation</i> for a prehistoric tribe \u2014 the structure it gestated in after that duty was long past is the basis for a Tower of Babel send-up, and the hook suggests that letting it finish remaking itself produces a spirit-god of the particular concept of <i>words that trigger memories</i>, as anyone who visited its tower chrysalis was imprinted with the language and memories of its long-dead (maybe never-extant?) patrons.<br /> <br /> A Coalesced idigam can fill a similar role to how Demon treats exiles looking to reintegrate with the God-Machine: they're powerful things attempting to carve out a place for themselves in the framework of a metaphysic that rejects or ignores them, and the fallout of their efforts is often going to be weird and terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:43:20-07:00","id":1415154,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. So let me make sure I got this right<br /> <br /> The Idigram Coalesced does not truly reflect what it has formed, but is more of a chrysalis so that a hopeful concept can come from it. Is that right? Also satchel, so that idigram Coalesced into the concept of translation successfully made that concept concrete, and THEN went on to be reborn as a true spirit that reflected words that triggered memories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:43:59-07:00","id":1415155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415137#post1415137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've always been confused about. Are Coalesced Idigram taking of concepts that cant be, or are they simply taking the form of something so specific that it should not have spiritual reflections? I've always been confused by that, and to my understanding, there was an ancient Idigram who's coalesced form represented Deja Vu</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem to be things that aren't, rather than 'can't be.'<br /> <br /> A star, translation, Father Wolf, a god. These things can all exist in the Chronicles of Darkness, though you don't want a star in the Pacific Ocean and we probably have more than enough gods. Their becoming these things can be good, but the act of it is going to lead to a lot of upheaval and change, which isn't always a good thing and even when it is isn't something people or People react well to.<br /> <br /> Things that 'can't be' are more the domain of the Abyss. A parasite that reproduces by its host being mind controlled, yoga that turns one of your organs into a portal, a personal assistant that lets you make the impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:47:29-07:00","id":1415156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415155#post1415155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They seem to be things that aren't, rather than 'can't be.'<br /> <br /> A star, translation, Father Wolf, a god. These things can all exist in the Chronicles of Darkness, though you don't want a star in the Pacific Ocean and we probably have more than enough gods. Their becoming these things can be good, but the act of it is going to lead to a lot of upheaval and change, which isn't always a good thing and even when it is isn't something people or People react well to.<br /> <br /> Things that 'can't be' are more the domain of the Abyss. A parasite that reproduces by its host being mind controlled, yoga that turns one of your organs into a portal, a personal assistant that lets you make the impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wouldn't it be safe to say that at one point, Idigram DID have a reason for their existence, but that Urfarah and Luna considered them to dangerous to run free anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:54:21-07:00","id":1415157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415156#post1415156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wouldn't it be safe to say that at one point, Idigram DID have a reason for their existence, but that Urfarah and Luna considered them to dangerous to run free anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idigam, and yeah. That actually comes up a lot in the books, theories for their existence beyond walking disasters. They may have been prototypes for spirits as a whole, or Pangaeans, or werewolves, or humans, or souls, or just everything that can exist but doesn't yet. But Father Wolf and the Uratha seemed to have really hit them hard, as most of the idigam on Earth hate or fear werewolves, or both.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The few other supernatural entities that seem to have knowledge of them are equally unsure. They're mentioned in the Demon Storyteller Guide where, from the point of view of Demons, they're terrified by them. They have seen parallels between the God-Machine and Luna, in that they both have inscrutable desires they make work through the world via weird proxies in the form of angels and werewolves, respectively. They even have rebels, in the form of Unchained and Pure. So the general suspicion from the few Demons that know about them is that idigam are would-be God-Machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2020, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T20:03:11-07:00","id":1415161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415154#post1415154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Idigram Coalesced does not truly reflect what it has formed, but is more of a chrysalis so that a hopeful concept can come from it. Is that right? Also satchel, so that idigram Coalesced into the concept of translation successfully made that concept concrete, and THEN went on to be reborn as a true spirit that reflected words that triggered memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Builder of Tongues (presumably) Coalesced around concepts that would allow it to facilitate linguistic understanding between different tribes, and, in the version of history where it pupates in the Neolithic and emerges undisturbed, has a new form that descriptively lacks the signifiers that would indicate it as <i>magath</i> to the surrounding choirs. It may well have ceased to be an <i>idigam</i> \u2014 at the very least, when it was doing its proto-Earthbound job it almost certainly retained the ability to return to Formlessness \u2014 but the significance of the outcome is more in that outcome being &quot;there is now a powerful spirit of a specific concept.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember, spirits mostly get <i>less pure</i> as they rise in Rank, such that one of the sources of <i>magath</i> is a spirit making a power-play it doesn't have the bandwidth to back up and becoming powerful but ostracized from the natural order; when we say &quot;there's a spirit for everything,&quot; we mostly don't mean that literally, as the fine-slicing of similar concepts tends to sand itself down to more generalized classifications that a spirit then builds outward from toward influence over spirits of related things. The exceptions tend to be correspondingly large; the spirit of a city is powerful because it is attached to a defined phenomenon that is versatile within its territory, old elementals are powerful because they represent ubiquitous and ancient phenomena, and the dragon of thought and contemplation that the Builder of Tongues reforges itself into is the ambitious work of a powerful force of primordial Essence-shaping.<br /> <br /> It's rare for a powerful spirit to get to do what Dreamborn do and derive Resonance from a singular defining concept, but certain idigam functionally aim to do exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:16:20-07:00","id":1415314,"title":"","content":"Couldn't find an answer elsewhere, or my Googling isn't deep enough.<br /> <br /> The 2e Werewolf core mentions Bone Shadows as (among other things) &quot;explorers\u2026 of the Shadow <i>and otherworlds</i>&quot;, talking about how the tribe tends to know more about things other than just spirits, etc.<br /> One of the character concepts listed for Bone Shadows is &quot;Underworld explorer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Question: How can werewolves explore the Underworld?<br /> The word &quot;Underworld&quot; is mentioned in the book in the context of <i>the </i>Underworld exactly once \u2013 it's just that concept name listed above.<br /> <br /> There is no mention in the book of werewolves being able to travel to any &quot;otherworld&quot; other than the Shadow.<br /> The Reaching mechanic only seems to apply to the Shadow, not to anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Is this a figurative &quot;Underworld&quot; within the Shadow, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:37:52-07:00","id":1415320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415314#post1415314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a figurative &quot;Underworld&quot; within the Shadow, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld is accessed through Avernian Gates, which are present in many places with a Resonance of Death and may be Opened through a variety of Keys and rituals. Much as there's a rite for cracking a locus to enter the Gauntlet, there is ludonarrative space for a 2e version of 1e's rite to enter the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T18:57:30-07:00","id":1415495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415314#post1415314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't find an answer elsewhere, or my Googling isn't deep enough.<br /> <br /> The 2e Werewolf core mentions Bone Shadows as (among other things) &amp;quot;explorers\u2026 of the Shadow <i>and otherworlds</i>&amp;quot;, talking about how the tribe tends to know more about things other than just spirits, etc.<br /> One of the character concepts listed for Bone Shadows is &amp;quot;Underworld explorer&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Question: How can werewolves explore the Underworld?<br /> The word &amp;quot;Underworld&amp;quot; is mentioned in the book in the context of <i>the </i>Underworld exactly once \u2013 it's just that concept name listed above.<br /> <br /> There is no mention in the book of werewolves being able to travel to any &amp;quot;otherworld&amp;quot; other than the Shadow.<br /> The Reaching mechanic only seems to apply to the Shadow, not to anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Is this a figurative &amp;quot;Underworld&amp;quot; within the Shadow, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other worlds simply mean &quot;other than the shadow&quot;. Boneshadows, like their patron, wish to explore the unknown, and for them the Shadow just happens to be the most well known UNKNOWN. There are still the worlds of ghosts, fae, angels and many others to explore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T21:46:08-07:00","id":1415502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1415314#post1415314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't find an answer elsewhere, or my Googling isn't deep enough.<br /> <br /> The 2e Werewolf core mentions Bone Shadows as (among other things) &quot;explorers\u2026 of the Shadow <i>and otherworlds</i>&quot;, talking about how the tribe tends to know more about things other than just spirits, etc.<br /> One of the character concepts listed for Bone Shadows is &quot;Underworld explorer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Question: How can werewolves explore the Underworld?<br /> The word &quot;Underworld&quot; is mentioned in the book in the context of <i>the </i>Underworld exactly once \u2013 it's just that concept name listed above.<br /> <br /> There is no mention in the book of werewolves being able to travel to any &quot;otherworld&quot; other than the Shadow.<br /> The Reaching mechanic only seems to apply to the Shadow, not to anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Is this a figurative &quot;Underworld&quot; within the Shadow, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Underworld_(CofD)\" target=\"_blank\">Underworld</a> detailed in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Book_of_the_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">the Book of the Dead</a>. The first edition rite to enter is in the book if you want to use that. The second edition Geist core details the Underworld for second edition, and has ceremonies (open to all) that could do similarly. One can always just use the Barghest Gift and speak to ghosts of graveyards to find the ways to open the Avernian Gate there, or learn the Persephone's Return ceremony so they can do it themselves (this happens in Dark Eras 2's World War 1 setting, which mixes Sin-Eaters, Prometheans, and Werewolves).<br /> <br /> Remember that some of the first second edition books were written as part of the 'God Machine Chronicle' and not quite second edition. They fixed it but I believe it was still expected you'd use the Book of the Dead until the next book arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T19:16:26-08:00","id":1422859,"title":"","content":"Pretty basic questions, I think, but after reading the rulebook, I'm still not quite sure I understand Hisil and spirits. I always stumble at thing like these and need explanations, huh. So, pretty much everything in the material world has a reflection in Hisil, except humans? Rage, hospital, vodka, dog, river, chair are spirits and there are many more? What about concepts like life, death, time or something similar, do they have representation? But not all spirits are active and they also have hierarchy. All spirits need essence from material world to function. They can also eat the spirits that are completely different from what they are and become hybrids, which is usually bad. There are also things that aren't exactly spirits, but...worse. If a wound opens up, corrupting essense seeps in and transforms spirits. And there are also Idigam, which are big bad scary spirit-things that are even more otherworldly?<br /> <br /> Now, many spirits are not active. If they're not active, are the things just...there? I'm not sure I completely get this. Like a chair will be just a chair, in the same or similar place it is in material world unless for some reason this spirit is active. If a create a big campfire in material world, will it create one fire spirit in Hisil? Multiple? Multiple that will assimilate each other until only one big fire spirit remains? And before that they'll eat wood spirits from firewood? And when the fire dies out, the spirit will probably die too, but if it somehow becomes too powerful, it can influence material world and start a forest fire, for example?<br /> <br /> Let me try to imagine visiting a hospital in Hisil. I'm not sure what exactly would create a locus without werewolves chasing spirits away? But they would use it to cross over into spirit world. It's mirroring the real one and not at the same time, influenced by real world just like everything else. During day pretty much everything is sleeping and sunlight is making it hard for spirits and travelers to move, if it penetrates the clouds. At night Hisil is more alive, but the sky is always covered in clouds, day or night. The envinronment is not supposed to be washed out, always dark or something like that. Now, the hospital. It's probably a spirit, but not really active, right? It might look different, for example, if it doesn't have enough funding and is barely hanging on despite the appearances, in Hisil it may look the part. Faded paint, broken windows and something like this. Anyway, inside it might look too sterile or clean or little bit bloody, scary and creepy, depending on the hospital and what happens inside of it. It's populated by spirits of sickness, loneliness...medicine? Are there spirits of blood? And obviously, many other, just can't name them at the top of my head, but hospitals can have a lot of stuff. Anyway, related spirits coexist with each other and feed on the resonance from the real world. If a sickness spirit somehow gets too much power and decides to be greedy, it might influence the real world and for example, make patients to stay sick longer, make the disease easier to spread inside the hospital. Now, various scalpels or beds don't have active spirits because there's no need for them to exist, so they're just there. Spirit of sickness might look like something vaguely humanoid diseased shape or something more weird. It might not really talk or act in a understandable manner, because it's not a human and doesn't have to act like it. Morgue might look bigger and have way more freezers. Do I get the idea right? And for example, if there's a secret lab in the basement where people are being tortured and murdered, it might open a wound in that same basement which might look like an actual bleeding wound or just...wrong in any other way. Something bad might come out of it(there are things that come out of it, right?) or the essence from it might corrupt the spirits around and they will take control of the hospital, will become the most powerful spirits there and will start to influence the real world somehow, making everything worse.<br /> <br /> I guess it's a lot of questions and a huge wall of text, but in the end these are just pretty noob questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","user":"Dante[RU]","date":". 11-09-2020, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T20:21:23-08:00","id":1422866,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23530\" data-vbnamecard=\"23530\">Dante[RU]</a> Attempting to parse through the wall of text to answer holistically rather than pick through to quote and respond to specific queries:<br /> <br /> The vast majority of things that exist and are not sapient beings like humans have a spiritual reflection in the Hisil, though abstract spirits are more reliant on resonant conditions beyond the prosaic for sustenance (i.e. a spirit of murder or jealousy does not have the same easy fallback for continued activity that a spirit of water or dogs does).<br /> <br /> Rank 0 spirits (motes/<i>muthrum</i>) are the spiritual equivalent of algae, with no Attributes or Numina; they're the most straightforward example of how the ecology of the Shadow works, because they only passively accumulate resonant Essence from nearby and other spirits get better returns from eating them than directly harvesting their purviews (in the sense that there's no daily limit on how many motes a spirit can steal from). Some things might not have picked up enough significance to have their own spirits right out the gate, but as set dressing it doesn't take much recognition for a mote to form in the Shadow's record of events; by the same token, there's little stopping a less forward-thinking spirit from consuming a mote whole instead of skimming its Essence stores and letting them grow back.<br /> <br /> A spirit that has a proper Rank and is aware is still the sum of its parts and inclined to act in ways appropriate to its nature; most Gafflings are still tied to a single specimen of their purviews and therefore not likely to become <i>magath</i> on their own initiative, such that desperation brought about by sudden environmental changes or mystical tampering is the more likely cause for hybridizing a minor spirit out of the natural order. This and the relatively simple bans they operate under can be pointed to as one reason why they're the favored level of power for Forsaken pack totems (particularly given the excesses the Pure's patrons often drive them to).<br /> <br /> Stronger spirits tend to be less pure-concept and more of their own personalities, having incorporated enough power to outgrow a singular focus (with the most prominent exceptions being very large things like cities or the elements). Sometimes a spirit is formed at a higher Rank (most animal spirits are at least strong enough to be awake, for example, and an especially major event may birth a Jaggling wholesale), but for the most part spiritual power is aggregated over time through found significance and the weight of history \u2014 the spirit of a bonfire may be shocked into wakefulness by the events surrounding it and frantically gather power from the spirits of things burned and burning, but it's probably going to start that feeding frenzy at Rank 1 and maybe work its way up to Rank 2 if it's very well-placed. Maybe a viral rumor instantiates a Place-That-Isn't and an Ensih to safeguard it, but that sort of thing is uncommon<br /> <br /> Despite the Uratha's mandate, spirits tend to work out an equilibrium in most circumstances, such that if there's room in the hospital for two different death spirits to operate they probably won't consume each other out of hand until and unless they grow particularly close to each other and judge that they could command more influence as a single powerful death-Jaggling taking tithe from their lessers than splitting the cut with the guy in the morgue.<br /> <br /> Finer details than Influence and broad concept filter into a spirit through the resonance of what it eats and where it lives, such that urban spirits of the same animals will usually look different than their rural counterparts even before the distortions of memory and perception brought about by the Gauntlet and the type of observers contributing to the spiritual makeup of an area; in the countryside, many animal-spirits and natural features are larger and more extreme because their presence is described by the viewpoints of smaller animals, while the Shadow of a city tends to be a more human-scale stylized impression that turns buildings into sleeping giants and vehicles into fast-moving monsters. Regardless of where they develop, though, spirits tend to have appearances and powers appropriate to their natures, just as the resonance of an area tends to paint it with the brush of its resident concepts \u2014 which is why Wounds tend to look really messed up, since they're sites of self-perpetuating negative resonance.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is, it should be noted, a concrete place \u2014 even spirits of abstract concepts have ephemeral flesh that is every bit as tangible in their home realm as wood or stone is in the Flesh. Things come into existence and change there through spooky abstract processes that are more art than science, but the natural order of the Shadow is built on a huge esoteric set of agreements between groups of spirits that rites tap into in a way that roughly mirrors the material world's sensibilities \u2014 plants grow for reasons that have little to do with the Sun, so the lingering memories of millions of clouds crowd the sky if the Lord of the Day doesn't see fit to throw his weight around, but it's cold in the winter and hot in the summer, the spiders eat flies, the rats hide from cats, and when the Moon is out you can hear the wolves howl.<br /> <br /> If it weren't an ancient playground for dreaming gods sheltering weird remnant populations and dormant fossil specimens, the biggest problems the Uratha would have to deal with would be knock-on complications from catastrophe and human action and the occasional demonic incursion from same, but unfortunately, the Hosts and the idigam hook into the Shadow from older points in its cosmogony and Wolf's whole job seems to have been keeping out the weird shit and culling pieces of runaway history before they got big enough to become dangerous, and <i>most</i> of that isn't the level of Shadow-stuff the average werewolf needs to worry themselves with compared to taking a bite out of occult crime and trimming the cannibal rosebushes.<br /> <br /> tl;dr You've just about got the size of it, bearing in mind that spirits themselves are, while collectively versatile, among the least bizarre things a werewolf can run into when things are operating normally. Mage's perspective on the cosmology puts a nebulous link between the Shadow and the dreams/mind/soul of the world beyond humanity, which contains many psychic presences of a dubious and/or occult nature, but otherwise tends to be the most grounded of the Astral realms in its representation of geography. Some variant on &quot;spooky funhouse-mirror version of material reality&quot; will serve you well enough as long as you keep an individual locale's history, significance, and mood in mind when describing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T05:54:11-08:00","id":1422899,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Yeah, sorry for the wall of text. I guess I'm in the right direction then, was just slightly confused about the whole thing and how it might look. Thank you for the explanation. So death spirits are a thing then and not some kind of other big overarching entity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T09:25:23-08:00","id":1422913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1422899#post1422899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Yeah, sorry for the wall of text. I guess I'm in the right direction then, was just slightly confused about the whole thing and how it might look. Thank you for the explanation. So death spirits are a thing then and not some kind of other big overarching entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death spirits are a thing. Depending on the specimen they might be able to interact with the same band of Twilight that ghosts inhabit, but generally they're the same as any other spirit \u2014 they'll inhabit or be drawn to places and things that resonate with the concept of death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T05:13:44-08:00","id":1423040,"title":"","content":"Another silly question: Are there any good sources of inspiration for what a spirit might want? For example, when bargaining with a werewolf. My brain only produces boring human-like politics, like &quot;Spirit wants to eat me, help me&quot;, but I'd like something more otherworldly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T06:11:08-08:00","id":1423045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1423040#post1423040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another silly question: Are there any good sources of inspiration for what a spirit might want? For example, when bargaining with a werewolf. My brain only produces boring human-like politics, like &amp;quot;Spirit wants to eat me, help me&amp;quot;, but I'd like something more otherworldly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don t want to consider the give me essence/protection options, then you can opt to a more long term plan.<br /> Most spirit would like a werewolf to create a permanent suitable Resonant source, protect one of such source or remove/convert a rival spirit ones.<br /> For example a spirit of sickness could ask to kill a physician, a darkness spirit could ask to destroy all the street lamps of an alley, a spirit of sadness could ask you to change the script of a popular tv show, ecc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T06:16:52-08:00","id":1423047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1423040#post1423040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another silly question: Are there any good sources of inspiration for what a spirit might want? For example, when bargaining with a werewolf. My brain only produces boring human-like politics, like &quot;Spirit wants to eat me, help me&quot;, but I'd like something more otherworldly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Politics is unfortunately going to be the main source of answers that aren't obvious or particularly esoteric; if a task doesn't directly benefit a spirit's feeding stock or relative importance, it'll probably have to do with someone it wants to curry favor with, someone it wants taken down a peg, someone it owes a favor, someone who owes it a favor, or something that connects to the spirit's nature (or that of someone in the other categories) through a train of thought that is either circuitous or obscure enough to require research.<br /> <br /> The spirit that guards the baptismal font in a local church might want a specific person's silver crucifix because it resonates with purity, because it needs that person to be slightly more vulnerable to werewolves (personally or on behalf of someone else), because it's the keystone of another powerful spirit's ban, or to invoke some roundabout clause in the laws of the Shadow that concerns purity, water, silver, churches, that person's family, crucifixes, or any number of other things.<br /> <br /> As with spirits and the Shadow in general, this benefits from building out the background of the things you're dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T11:41:27-08:00","id":1423087,"title":"","content":"Just to throw this out there, the best books to use as resources for a wide variety of spirits are probably first edition's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a> and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/27863/World-of-Darkness-Book-of-Spirits?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Spirits</a>. Predators has something like 80 different spirits that fit a wide variety of common types, along with what they might look like, what they might want, how they might act, and possible bans. The Book of Spirits I think has less, but also goes into what the Shadow itself is like. While a good source of information, the Book of Spirits is written from a mortal standpoint, and so it sets the Shadow as a more dangerous and alien place where humans are prey and playthings. Werewolves are likely to have a better understanding of things (even if they find it alien at first) and not be considered as easy prey. Fortunately, mechanically, spirits don't need much work to convert across editions, most of the work being adding a bane (or turning a ban into a bane and adding a ban) and Manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-11-2020, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T12:57:12-08:00","id":1423098,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers. I'll try to keep everything in mind and check the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T17:40:58-08:00","id":1426057,"title":"","content":"A silly question again, but how does Werewolf regeneration interact with pre- and post change body modifications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T23:30:34-08:00","id":1426082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1426057#post1426057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A silly question again, but how does Werewolf regeneration interact with pre- and post change body modifications?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 102 of core book states that only silver and aggravated (to werewolf) damage can do lasting scars on werewolf.<br /> As for pre change, i suppose that father wolf would like his childrens to be at theirs physical peak after the first change, so i think that all previous scars and modifications could be healed as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T23:35:57-08:00","id":1426083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1426057#post1426057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A silly question again, but how does Werewolf regeneration interact with pre- and post change body modifications?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the player. Generally, if they want the character to retain the modifications, they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T03:26:36-08:00","id":1426099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1426082#post1426082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pag 102 of core book states that only silver and aggravated (to werewolf) damage can do lasting scars on werewolf.<br /> As for pre change, i suppose that father wolf would like his childrens to be at theirs physical peak after the first change, so i think that all previous scars and modifications could be healed as well</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's pretty much why I asked. I'm not sure where I read that or maybe I'm misremembering something, but for some reason I thought that during your First Change your body fixes itself into the peak condition, so if you were sick/had lasting chronic injuries/etc, it's gone now(unlike what happens if you're Embraced). And I got the body-horror feel from Werewolf regeneration afterwards. It's really potent, it doesn't really care what you want and it hurts(unless you spend Essence). So what happens if you have any piercings, earrings, tooth fillings, artificial hips before the change? What happens if you want a tat or a nose ring after the change? Was just curious if there are canonical answers to that.<br /> <br /> P.S. Now I'm suddenly reminded of Underworld 4 finale.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> That's probably the best way to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T04:11:05-08:00","id":1426108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1426099#post1426099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's pretty much why I asked. I'm not sure where I read that or maybe I'm misremembering something, but for some reason I thought that during your First Change your body fixes itself into the peak condition, so if you were sick/had lasting chronic injuries/etc, it's gone now(unlike what happens if you're Embraced). And I got the body-horror feel from Werewolf regeneration afterwards. It's really potent, it doesn't really care what you want and it hurts(unless you spend Essence). So what happens if you have any piercings, earrings, tooth fillings, artificial hips before the change? What happens if you want a tat or a nose ring after the change? Was just curious if there are canonical answers to that.<br /> <br /> P.S. Now I'm suddenly reminded of Underworld 4 finale.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> That's probably the best way to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to apply modifications after the first change would be to pierce the flesh with silver needles, as it would leave a lasting hole for a piercing or ink drop.<br /> Probably in some packs they use those methods to mark membership","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 11-25-2020, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T06:30:09-08:00","id":1429015,"title":"","content":"Can the Totem's Wrath Facet only be used on a werewolf's own totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T12:17:37-08:00","id":1429046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1429015#post1429015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Totem's Wrath Facet only be used on a werewolf's own totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T13:52:39-08:00","id":1430370,"title":"","content":"I was wondering...do werewolves have easy ways to increase combat dicepools? Vampires have physical intensity, potence and celerity, Mages can buff skills ad attributes and so on. It would seem strange that the most combat oriented of the splat Is the one with the smallest combat dicepools...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T14:21:21-08:00","id":1430372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1430370#post1430370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering...do werewolves have easy ways to increase combat dicepools? Vampires have physical intensity, potence and celerity, Mages can buff skills ad attributes and so on. It would seem strange that the most combat oriented of the splat Is the one with the smallest combat dicepools...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few Gifts that can grant extra dice or dots to relevant stats or increased damage modifier, but it's kinda limited to that and shapeshifting, I'm afraid. Check out Full Moon, Rage and Strength. So yeah, it's linear werewolves, quadratic vampires in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T14:52:40-08:00","id":1430376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1430370#post1430370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering...do werewolves have easy ways to increase combat dicepools? Vampires have physical intensity, potence and celerity, Mages can buff skills ad attributes and so on. It would seem strange that the most combat oriented of the splat Is the one with the smallest combat dicepools...</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning into a wolf/wolfman/direwolf/berserker demigod along with the Merits that enhance that ability, potentially the benefits of pack membership, and also most of the Gift of Strength, for starters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T15:58:11-08:00","id":1430388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1430370#post1430370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering...do werewolves have easy ways to increase combat dicepools? Vampires have physical intensity, potence and celerity, Mages can buff skills ad attributes and so on. It would seem strange that the most combat oriented of the splat Is the one with the smallest combat dicepools...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have a few options for increasing stats, yes, but white room scenarios such as these are largely worthless for understanding how a splat works. Uratha aren\u2019t just going to come at their opponents with dice pools and stand face to face trading blows. They\u2019re going to buff themselves and their pack, debuff their opponents until they\u2019re cowering wrecks, and then strike hard and fast to take them down.<br /> <br /> But when caught out in an unexpected situation, being able to reflexively add 6 dots across your physical stats and regenerate all lethal and bashing every single turn is a nice fallback that every werewolf has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T17:17:49-08:00","id":1430391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1430388#post1430388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when caught out in an unexpected situation, being able to reflexively add 6 dots across your physical stats and regenerate all lethal and bashing every single turn is a nice fallback that every werewolf has.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>is</i> really nice, but it has always felt weird to me who has primarily played VtR that the shapeshifting and Death Rage bonuses are so static. <i>Every</i> werewolf gets those advantages, with comparatively little room to improve those aspects further. I really don't want it to be as rieiculous as in VtR where elder vampires become combat monsters no matter how they're statted by sheer virtue of high BP (up to potentially 30 dice from Phyiscal Intensity and an additional 10 dice from Frenzy, to compare to equivalent innate abilities/traits), but it feels like untapped potential that the Main Thing about werewolves grants a flat bonus to everyone and it's really everything else that matters when it comes to werewolf vs werewolf combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T17:29:35-08:00","id":1430396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1430391#post1430391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That <i>is</i> really nice, but it has always felt weird to me who has primarily played VtR that the shapeshifting and Death Rage bonuses are so static. <i>Every</i> werewolf gets those advantages, with comparatively little room to improve those aspects further. I really don't want it to be as rieiculous as in VtR where elder vampires become combat monsters no matter how they're statted by sheer virtue of high BP (up to potentially 30 dice from Phyiscal Intensity and an additional 10 dice from Frenzy, to compare to equivalent innate abilities/traits), but it feels like untapped potential that the Main Thing about werewolves grants a flat bonus to everyone and it's really everything else that matters when it comes to werewolf vs werewolf combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember that certain Facets activate automatically when you enter Death Rage, like the Strength and Rage Facets. So I wouldn't say that they're static, it just requires some investment.<br /> <br /> And lets not forget the form boosting Merits like Living Weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 12-29-2020, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T10:42:36-08:00","id":1431298,"title":"","content":"Eating flesh of man of wolf to deal aggravated damages.<br /> Are mage or other supernatural creatures considered still human? If yes, which one?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would consider mages as humans. Dunno about vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T11:26:57-08:00","id":1431301,"title":"","content":"We haven't incorporated every gameline in, but ghouls, mages, changelings, sin-eaters and demons in human guises. A big thing with mage is that they're still humans with human weaknesses, just some added potential. We wouldn't count vampires or prometheans. Never thought about mummies, Deviants seem like they could go either way depending on how they were built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T10:19:57-08:00","id":1431847,"title":"","content":"Fetishes and some facets (esp of Elemental gift) could be very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T07:07:03-08:00","id":1434118,"title":"","content":"Hosts have (at least going by the examples on p. 204) no Supernatural Tolerance or Rank. How are you supposed to determine the amount of Essence they have access to (max/per Turn)? Is it intentional that they are quite bad at Contesting supernatural powers because of their lack of Supernatural Tolerance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T08:00:23-08:00","id":1434127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434118#post1434118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hosts have (at least going by the examples on p. 204) no Supernatural Tolerance or Rank. How are you supposed to determine the amount of Essence they have access to (max/per Turn)? Is it intentional that they are quite bad at Contesting supernatural powers because of their lack of Supernatural Tolerance?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have any powerstat, no. If you don't have Shunned by the Moon, their Essence pool size is essentially ST fiat. If you do have Shunned by the Moon, page 107 has the rules for how much Essence they can hold at various states (1-2 for base Shards, 3-5 when possessing a human, 6-50 when having formed a full hybrid).<br /> Like spirits they don't have any per turn limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T08:54:00-08:00","id":1434137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434118#post1434118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it intentional that they are quite bad at Contesting supernatural powers because of their lack of Supernatural Tolerance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the lack of a Supernatural Tolerance Trait as a metric for calling something &quot;quite bad&quot; at contesting supernatural powers doesn't really track when the thing's main method of increasing its supernatural potency improves its Attributes; Claimed <i>also</i> don't retain their core spirit's Rank, remember, and one of the published Dread Powers adds three dice to contest supernatural powers in particular territory.<br /> <br /> They're distributed processes for fucking up the Gauntlet and eating people. Their main opposition is werewolves, who are hunters with a list of contested powers that mostly just create opportunities. Expecting them to be broadly good at resisting the supernatural powers of other monsters is kind of like expecting a Huntsman to be particularly good at a task that isn't ruining a changeling's life \u2014 it's not what they're for, and if it comes up anyway then it's a storyhook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T09:10:33-08:00","id":1434144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434137#post1434137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expecting them to be broadly good at resisting the supernatural powers of other monsters is kind of like expecting a Huntsman to be particularly good at a task that isn't ruining a changeling's life \u2014 <b>it's not what they're for, and if it comes up anyway then it's a storyhook</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That for example is a perfectly legitimate reason for that to be the case, which is what I was asking about. However..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434137#post1434137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the lack of a Supernatural Tolerance Trait as a metric for calling something &quot;quite bad&quot; at contesting supernatural powers doesn't really track when the thing's main method of increasing its supernatural potency improves its Attributes...</div> </div> </div> </div>...at least none of the examples I have seen have been Hosts with superhuman Resolve or Composure, which - for the purposes of Contesting supernatural powers - is much more relevant than having Strength 8 for example. The latter isn't going to help in this case. Most Hosts can Contest mind or emotion control powers about as well as an intrepid mortal. Which is fine if that is intentional. I just was not sure it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T09:51:03-08:00","id":1434150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434144#post1434144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Hosts can Contest mind or emotion control powers about as well as an intrepid mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most supernatural beings whose templates aren't built toward accelerated Supernatural Tolerance fare little better; a demon with Cover lower than their Primum has to risk compromise to use their better dicepool, and a Beast at high Satiety <i>literally</i> contests supernatural powers of the sort that Resolve and Composure manage in the same way as an identically-statted mortal does; vampires who haven't been around for more than fifty years or dedicated effort to thickening their blood roll a whopping one extra die, Prometheans running silent to avoid Disquiet likewise don't get much better resistance than mortals do, and Deviants have their zero to five extra dice starkly limited in when they can increase it while on the run and dealing with the drawbacks of their own powers. On the other end of things, Awakened magic only interacts with Resistance as a source of penalties to overcome, which mostly doesn't need superhuman ratings to be a resource-tapping obstacle.<br /> <br /> Hosts start as infiltrators and progress to overt monsters who hide. Their principal concerns are the ninety-some percent of the Flesh's sapient population that has no supernatural powers to contest, plus the ancient legacy of shapeshifting hunters that needs to find them to affect them with tricks that put them in a slasher film. Rantings of the Beshilu notwithstanding, they're playing a quiet game against the werewolves, and that mostly doesn't call for a generalized bonus to their drive and stability.<br /> <br /> Finally, contested rolls are <i>rolls</i> \u2014 even though the system favors the aggressor, it's entirely possible for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1424436-hedge-navigation-examples?p=1432751#post1432751\">a mortal character with completely average Resistance Attributes to hold out multiple times against the intimidation efforts of a specialized monster with more than twice their dicepool</a>, never mind a hybrid monstrosity with &quot;only&quot; above-above-average to peak-human Resolve. Having worse odds of resisting an effect than a powerful werewolf with the same stats doesn't make something <i>bad at</i> resisting that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T14:40:44-08:00","id":1434420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434150#post1434150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants have their zero to five extra dice starkly limited in when they can increase it while on the run and dealing with the drawbacks of their own powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Deviant Supernatural Tolerance is actually Acclimation plus their highest-Magnitude Variation (<b>Deviant: the Renegades</b>, p. 94), meaning that all but the weakest Remade <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2013</span></span> Hyperplasia chargen and up <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2013</span></span> can theoretically start with +6 dice to any contested roll involving Supernatural Tolerance. Most, however, are likely going to start out in the +3 to +5 range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T15:19:53-08:00","id":1434423,"title":"","content":"Has the question &quot;What the hell are the Idigam and what do they do?&quot; already been answered?<br /> Cuz I really can't wrap my head around it (I guess that's the purpose). I mean, their origin is unknowable mumbo-jumbo that nobody is certain in-universe or out. But I still don't get where they come from (like, they fall from space? appear in the dusty cellar of an old house? a super-computer? in the mind of a lunatic in an asylum?). And their purpose or activities aren't explained either, do they warp everything like Paradox bugs, do they try to fit in a world too alien for them, or try to make the alien world more natural according to their view? I wanted to understand how to use them in game by understanding what they are and do. (although not it might not be a simple question anymore)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T15:45:46-08:00","id":1434426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434423#post1434423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has the question &quot;What the hell are the Idigam and what do they do?&quot; already been answered?<br /> Cuz I really can't wrap my head around it (I guess that's the purpose). I mean, their origin is unknowable mumbo-jumbo that nobody is certain in-universe or out. But I still don't get where they come from (like, they fall from space? appear in the dusty cellar of an old house? a super-computer? in the mind of a lunatic in an asylum?). And their purpose or activities aren't explained either, do they warp everything like Paradox bugs, do they try to fit in a world too alien for them, or try to make the alien world more natural according to their view? I wanted to understand how to use them in game by understanding what they are and do. (although not it might not be a simple question anymore)</div> </div> </div> </div>The core reason for their being is up to you, but some of this at least has been answered.<br /> <br /> Where they come from: Here, our world. Father Wolf caught as many as he could and threw them up to the moon to act as a prison. These are called the Moon-Banished. During strange astronomical events and things like the moon landing many have hitched their ways back. Others fled from Father Wolf, to the depths of the sea or Earth, and bided their time until they sensed no danger from him and resurfaced. These are called the Earthbound. There's no mechanical difference between them but the the ones who've stayed on Earth are probably more tapped into how the world works than those trapped on the moon.<br /> <br /> Their purpose seem to be to create new things. I've mentioned elsewhere I think they acted as a bridge between the Abyss and the real world, but discounting mage they can just be a foundation for things that don't exist, but should, or could eventually. Some of these things probably shouldn't exist, like a star in the middle of the Pacific Ocean that would wipe out all of Earth. Some of them are probably less inherently catastrophic, like a variant of the Underworld or the concept of Recollection. Whatever the end results, however, in gathering the Essence and setting up the Resonance to empower this creation and their own chrysalis, they can do a lot of the type of damage that attracts the attention of werewolves. And since they're not fans of Father Wolf or his children they're likely to not react well to that.<br /> <br /> They're couched as an out of context problem for werewolves because they don't offer a simple solution. They're spirits, but do a lot of things spirits can't. They don't claim people, but they can make all sorts of Claimed and Ridden. They're not hosts, but they can make hosts. They're not werewolves or humans, but they can co-opt werewolves or humans. They offer a Storyteller an opportunity for big story antagonists. Things in the vein of Sauron or Randal Flagg or Father from Fullmetal Alchemist or the Anti-God from Prince of Darkness. They're highly variable and hard to understand, but from an ST standpoint they're pretty easy, in that they're powerful NPCs that are interested in a concept enough to want to make it real, through themselves. How they do that can be complicated (setting up conspiracies and cults) or simple (brute-forcing their way through the understanding).<br /> <br /> The section on them in the second edition core offers a lot of options that could help guide a storyteller, but the obvious section to look at is the example idigam starting on page 222, which vary a lot, or the ones in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon. And while they've mechanically changed a lot across editions, the ones written up in first edition's Night Horrors: Wolfsbane would still fit thematically.<br /> <br /> Idigam can be a pretty big story aspect, and that alone can be the most daunting thing about them, especially given they're not likely to have a personal vendetta against an individual werewolf or pack. For that one might use the Geryo, introduced in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon and the Contagion Chronicle. They're old and powerful, also hate werewolves, but I think work better on a more personal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T16:14:48-08:00","id":1434431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434423#post1434423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still don't get where they come from (like, they fall from space? appear in the dusty cellar of an old house? a super-computer? in the mind of a lunatic in an asylum?).</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above. Idigam are natives to our world so they can show up basically anywhere. A subset of them were imprisoned on the moon but hitched a ride back after the moon landings. The rest have just gone about by being dormant, hidden, inaccessible and/or disguised. If a pack encounters an idigam, it's generally either because the pack just moved into the location, the idigam moved into the location, or the idigam has just gone under their radar until now.<br /> <br /> As for what idigam are, I think the most concise (but probably too simplistic to be fully accurate) explanation would be that they're spirits that somehow are free from having to conform to a specific nature. They can assume and abandon concepts that would be so innate for normal spirits that they could not exist without them. A spirit of fire could literally not stop being a spirit of fire because that's its core defining trait, but an idigam coalesced around the concept of fire can actually stop being a fire spirit and just become a spirit with the potential for a nature but no nature attached, if that makes sense.<br /> Essence Shaping could very well be a result of a spirit having such control over their own nature and Essence that they can apply similar principles on others.<br /> <br /> Other than that I think nofather has got you covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T17:39:57-08:00","id":1434438,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> ! That helped a lot, more than I hoped for.<br /> As usual with the CoD they are very cool antagonists, especially for Mages and Werewolves. <br /> <br /> <i>One other thing entirely different</i>:<br /> Is every Uratha born (First Changed) already sworn to the Oath of the Moon, and has the 'suffer less from silver' thing and Auspice?<br /> It's not explained in the tabs about it, and on the First Change or Tribes, as far as i've read in both 1st and 2nd editions. It is said that Ghost Wolves still adhere to it. And that the Pure reject the mark of Luna and the Oath (having their own). So it made me wonder if when you First Change it kind of comes with the package (which for me revolves around getting the Auspice and less silver damage) naturally and you either accept it or not, or its benefits just happen when you make the Oath actively, otherwise I imagine doing the oath verbally would be &quot;just&quot; a formality.<br /> I mean, most of the material kind of implies that you become a werewolf <b>with</b> the Luna gifts, foremost the Auspice, and you can reject it and become a Pure (or maybe Bale Hound) by choice. At the same time it's an Oath, not the kind of things that works automatically, but it might just be a fancy word too for the ancestral burden of their job as Father-Wolf substitutes. Is this clarified somewhere? Or from the clarity of reading more of the material maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T19:47:29-08:00","id":1434448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434438#post1434438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is every Uratha born (First Changed) already sworn to the Oath of the Moon, and has the 'suffer less from silver' thing and Auspice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspice yes, Oath no. Barring Pure tampering or other aberrant circumstances, a First Change includes (culminates in, often) the acquisition of your Auspice and your first bit of Renown.<br /> <br /> Ghost wolves often adhere to the tenets of the Oath in practice because many of the things on it are breaking points anyway, but \u2014 most straightforwardly \u2014 no Ghost Wolf has a tribal ban to worry about breaking because those bans are part of a tribe's variant on the Oath, which is sworn at initiation and tends to accompany your first bit of tribal Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T00:18:37-08:00","id":1434461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434438#post1434438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, thanks <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> ! That helped a lot, more than I hoped for.<br /> As usual with the CoD they are very cool antagonists, especially for Mages and Werewolves. <br /> <br /> <i>One other thing entirely different</i>:<br /> Is every Uratha born (First Changed) already sworn to the Oath of the Moon, and has the 'suffer less from silver' thing and Auspice?<br /> It's not explained in the tabs about it, and on the First Change or Tribes, as far as i've read in both 1st and 2nd editions. It is said that Ghost Wolves still adhere to it. And that the Pure reject the mark of Luna and the Oath (having their own). So it made me wonder if when you First Change it kind of comes with the package (which for me revolves around getting the Auspice and less silver damage) naturally and you either accept it or not, or its benefits just happen when you make the Oath actively, otherwise I imagine doing the oath verbally would be &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; a formality.<br /> I mean, most of the material kind of implies that you become a werewolf <b>with</b> the Luna gifts, foremost the Auspice, and you can reject it and become a Pure (or maybe Bale Hound) by choice. At the same time it's an Oath, not the kind of things that works automatically, but it might just be a fancy word too for the ancestral burden of their job as Father-Wolf substitutes. Is this clarified somewhere? Or from the clarity of reading more of the material maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated several times in the core book that you get the Auspice upon the First Change. An important part of joining the Pure is to burn away your Auspice using Rites known by the Pure.<br /> Side notes:<br /> There are a select few that go through the First Change without gaining an Auspice, but they are incredibly rare and the exception that proves the rule. Afaik the concept was introduced in Shunned by the Moon, meaning it took years into the game's second edition before they showed up.<br /> Both Forsaken and Pure (and Ghost Wolves) can become Bale Hounds, and there's no reason to get rid of your Auspice (if you still have an Auspice) to become one.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon is a choice, but anyone joining a Tribe will swear it (if Forsaken) or a variation of it (if Pure). Only Ghost Wolves can get away without swearing it (or one of its variations) but theoretically speaking even they can swear it if they associate with the Forsaken at large.<br /> But I don't think it's possible to swear one of the versions used by the Pure, though, without fully joining one of their Tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T05:21:00-08:00","id":1434475,"title":"","content":"Gotcha! Thanks, these answers helped a bunch. <br /> Because I like to tinker with my version of WoD but like to keep as close to the canon as written as possible, and this was an important part of the setting that by oversight or ignorance I couldn't find the answer by myself. Thanks a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T14:30:06-08:00","id":1434643,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m having some trouble grasping how Rites that target unwilling or hostile entities can be used practically. Namely, most rites require at least one minute to complete (usually more), and I haven\u2019t found any explanation of how is pack is supposed to perform an intricate mystical ritual while a target is actively resisting. <br /> <br /> As a specific example, Shadowbind seems to be the worst in this regard, since its whole purpose is to hold a spirit in place. Mechanically, the spirit contests with Resistance, but unless you interpret that to mean that the spirit can do nothing but sit there and...Resist, there\u2019s nothing indicating it can\u2019t instead run away, attack, or otherwise attempt to disrupt the ritual. And I don\u2019t think the intention is for the rite master to frantically chant for 5 minutes while the rest of the pack is in combat with the spirit. Also, spirits in particular tend to be fast and non-corporeal. I suppose some spirits will have bans and/or banes you could effectively use to pin them down, but then the Rite becomes a tad redundant. <br /> <br /> It feels like I\u2019m missing an important puzzle piece here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T15:17:01-08:00","id":1434644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434643#post1434643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m having some trouble grasping how Rites that target unwilling or hostile entities can be used practically. Namely, most rites require at least one minute to complete (usually more), and I haven\u2019t found any explanation of how is pack is supposed to perform an intricate mystical ritual while a target is actively resisting.<br /> <br /> As a specific example, Shadowbind seems to be the worst in this regard, since its whole purpose is to hold a spirit in place. Mechanically, the spirit contests with Resistance, but unless you interpret that to mean that the spirit can do nothing but sit there and...Resist, there\u2019s nothing indicating it can\u2019t instead run away, attack, or otherwise attempt to disrupt the ritual. And I don\u2019t think the intention is for the rite master to frantically chant for 5 minutes while the rest of the pack is in combat with the spirit. Also, spirits in particular tend to be fast and non-corporeal. I suppose some spirits will have bans and/or banes you could effectively use to pin them down, but then the Rite becomes a tad redundant.<br /> <br /> It feels like I\u2019m missing an important puzzle piece here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, rites are not normally things you use in battle, or in the battles of others. Theoretically you could manage it so that the pack is holding something long enough to enact Shadowbind or Fetish, especially with bans or banes like you mentioned, but that's not their primary use.<br /> <br /> Normally, when you 'kill' a spirit, you haven't drained all its Essence, and now it will discorporate and be inactive for a long period of time until it gets enough Essence back. This is when you use Shadowbind or Fetish. After you've beaten a spirit. You can manage some other ways, like threatening it enough that this is its only option. 'Why don't you just kill it?' It may be something too important to kill, having vital knowledge or earning a reprieve from destruction in other ways, it might have a method of being too powerful to kill, the werewolves never being able to drain its Essence fully. Otherwise, fetishes can act as a 'prison' alternative to the death penalty of final discorporation, with the added benefit that werewolves can get some power out of it. Going around just slaughtering every spirit you don't like isn't really the Forsaken way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T15:50:53-08:00","id":1434645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434644#post1434644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally, when you 'kill' a spirit, you haven't drained all its Essence, and now it will discorporate and be inactive for a long period of time until it gets enough Essence back. This is when you use Shadowbind or Fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, I think that makes sense. Though it reminds me of another question. <br /> <br /> On a scale of \u201crun off to the nearest Resonant location\u201d to \u201cgo on a quest to track down a hidden location specific to that spirit\u201d, how involved/difficult should it typically be for players to find a newly hibernating spirit\u2019s resting place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 02-05-2021, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T15:59:35-08:00","id":1434646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1434645#post1434645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah okay, I think that makes sense. Though it reminds me of another question.<br /> <br /> On a scale of \u201crun off to the nearest Resonant location\u201d to \u201cgo on a quest to track down a hidden location specific to that spirit\u201d, how involved/difficult should it typically be for players to find a newly hibernating spirit\u2019s resting place?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are expert trackers, so I wouldn't say it would be too hard to find it unless it was a really trickily unique spirit, or magath, which could be anywhere. Even then it might just be some tracking, Gifts can go a long way to help. For more powerful spirits the harder issue might be dealing with their minions. You can easily justify making it more difficult, of course, like having it be the minion of a more powerful spirit (or other thing, like a claimed or idigam) who its discorporated self returns to. Nice way to bring cults into the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-05-2021, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T18:35:41-08:00","id":1434721,"title":"","content":"Hi here!<br /> Long time DT at WtA and WtF. Starting my first chronicle at WtF2 and trying to figure the differences.<br /> I am not sure if I dreamt it, are there rules for a &quot;flight response&quot; aka Fox frenzy? Can't remember or find them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26374-shadowchaser","name":"Shadowchaser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T18:53:26-08:00","id":1434722,"title":"","content":"The frenzy equivalent in Forsaken is Death Rage. In 1e, one of the possible triggers for Death Rage was taking damage in your last Health boxes, and if you took damage in those boxes the goal of Death Rage changed from &quot;slaughter everyone&quot; to &quot;get away, slaughtering anyone blocking you from doing so.&quot; 2e doesn't have that \u2013 and the amazing regenerative powers of 2e's Gauru form give a werewolf in Death Rage little to fear for his own life anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T18:26:37-08:00","id":1435605,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, excuse me, I want to bring something that is happening on game I'm playing and ask for your opinion.<br /> It's about regenation on Gauru form.<br /> The GM keep saying that regeneration is just by the chart on page 93 and the regeneration on Gauru form is limited by that.<br /> I'm not going to make a noise at the table to ruin the game, but I want your opinion on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T18:35:41-08:00","id":1435606,"title":"","content":"As written, the table values are for healing outside of Gauru. As the section on Regeneration near the table notes, Uratha in Gauru are an exception and heal <i>all</i> bashing and lethal damage every turn.<br /> <br /> It sounds possible to me that your Storyteller knows this and is deliberately house-ruling this away, in which case it doesn't matter what the book says. They should know, at the least, that this heavily changes the balance on Gauru, and may turn deliberately shifting to Gauru from a dangerous but potent gamble to a near-pointless risk.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T01:23:34-08:00","id":1435626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrunoMoonChangeling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1435605#post1435605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, excuse me, I want to bring something that is happening on game I'm playing and ask for your opinion.<br /> It's about regenation on Gauru form.<br /> The GM keep saying that regeneration is just by the chart on page 93 and the regeneration on Gauru form is limited by that.<br /> I'm not going to make a noise at the table to ruin the game, but I want your opinion on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the rules text for Regeneration on page 94:<br /> &quot;<b>Gauru:</b> When in Gauru form, Uratha heal all bashing and lethal damage at the start of each turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rules for regeneration also includes things like how fast they heal lethal damage, spending Essence to heal lethal damage according to the table instead of bashing damage, downgrading many sources of aggravated damage, how fast they heal aggravated damage from the few sources that do deal that kind of damage, how they heal Tilts, and how they deal with Toxins. A lot more than could fit in the table that just shows the effects that your Primal Urge rating has on regeneration.<br /> <br /> Additionally, each form has specific rules described later in the book, so this is repeated under the Gauru form on page 97:<br /> &quot;<b>Regeneration:</b> Uratha in Gauru form regenerate <i>all</i> bashing and lethal damage each turn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T03:02:50-08:00","id":1435835,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can see ghosts, geists and reapers as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T04:10:42-08:00","id":1435838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1435835#post1435835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can see ghosts, geists and reapers as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without a Gift (or possibly a Rite) giving them that ability. Ghosts are also in Twilight but in a &quot;different&quot; Twilight and does not interact at all with spirits in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T05:56:50-08:00","id":1436000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1435838#post1435838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not without a Gift (or possibly a Rite) giving them that ability. Ghosts are also in Twilight but in a &quot;different&quot; Twilight and does not interact at all with spirits in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically the Gift of Death and the Glory facet Barghest is all they would need to interact with Death aligned entities, some of its effects would work even on Vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T14:40:17-08:00","id":1436452,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> Is there a difference between man and woman in Gauru form?<br /> On my TTRPG I leave it to player imagination, I don't establish that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T16:27:31-08:00","id":1436470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrunoMoonChangeling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1436452#post1436452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> Is there a difference between man and woman in Gauru form?<br /> On my TTRPG I leave it to player imagination, I don't establish that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the art shows female Werewolves in Gauru form with breasts (e.g. page 47). My own headcanon is that male and female Werewolves in Gauru form are indistinguishable (and in fact that the male sex organs are not present in Gauru form either), but if I had a player playing a female Werewolf I would leave it up to them to define this (or just leave it undefined)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T11:34:30-08:00","id":1436852,"title":"","content":"Hi guys!<br /> Having a Lune as totem is really so bad? And It affects the game mechanics, or the potential madness is just narrative stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T11:40:42-08:00","id":1437019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1436852#post1436852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys!<br /> Having a Lune as totem is really so bad? And It affects the game mechanics, or the potential madness is just narrative stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>The pack's totem has a deep spiritual connection with a pack - to the point that pack members gain its ban. Totems will also influence the pack as much as any other member - either directly by stating their demands, or indirectly using their influences. For this reason packs need to be careful in their choice of totem, and taking a spirit of madness as a totem is just a bad idea.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't give any mechanics for how exactly a Lune totem drives packs mad but it isn't hard to imagine. The totem's ban and aspiration would change with the phases of the Moon, spiritually pulling the pack this way and that. Uratha vulnerable to frenzying at the sight of their Auspice Moon might find themselves frenzying all the time, even if they keep their harmony in check. And the Lune is certainly going to extend its maddening influence over the mortals and wolf-blooded in the pack, perhaps poking and prodding them to see if it can cause them to change into full children of Luna.<br /> <br /> If you were going to run a game where the Pack's totem is a Lune it might be possible, but to do it justice I think you'd need to be very liberal with the madness condition. All the players should find their characters repeatedly afflicted by madness due to the Lune's changing whims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T09:39:15-08:00","id":1437969,"title":"","content":"Do Spirits &quot;bleed&quot; for the purposes of that Uratha tracking power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T14:29:55-08:00","id":1438173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1437969#post1437969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Spirits &quot;bleed&quot; for the purposes of that Uratha tracking power?</div> </div> </div> </div>The tracking power only works if the Uratha has tasted their blood. Spirits don't have blood, they have essence, so my guess would be that the ability doesn't work on Spirits. Other more physical entities like claimed and hosts probably do have blood, or something near enough that Uratha can track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T10:07:19-08:00","id":1438472,"title":"","content":"Can Werewolves &quot;eat&quot; essence from other human adjacent creatures like Vampires, Changelings, and so on, or is just only pure humans, wolves and other Werewolves? If they can or could &quot;eat&quot; essence from other almost-humans, would this be a violation of their Oath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26458-gungnir","name":"Gungnir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T14:08:09-08:00","id":1438496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gungnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1438472#post1438472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Werewolves &quot;eat&quot; essence from other human adjacent creatures like Vampires, Changelings, and so on, or is just only pure humans, wolves and other Werewolves? If they can or could &quot;eat&quot; essence from other almost-humans, would this be a violation of their Oath?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there's official word on it but we usually rule that it depends on the creature and how human it is. So Changelings and Mages, yes, Prometheans and Vampires no (barring a way to get it from corpses). We do have it be a violation of the Oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T14:55:19-08:00","id":1438503,"title":"","content":"Also, do you need the Fetish Rite to make a Talen? Or is there a Talen-specific rite? The book doesn't specify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T15:50:28-08:00","id":1438508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1438503#post1438503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you need the Fetish Rite to make a Talen? Or is there a Talen-specific rite? The book doesn't specify.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says you can make them with a rite, though the write-up explains that it would just be targeting very weak spirits, like Rank 1. Considering how rites work it would probably just make sense to use the Fetish rite rather than creating an entirely new one. The more usual way of getting talens is through a spirit taking off piece of itself to do so. This can be useful when werewolves ruling a territory demand a tithe from certain spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T11:00:33-08:00","id":1438974,"title":"","content":"Is the number of turns an Uratha can hold Gauru form strictly limited to their base Stamina + Primal Urge, or can it be increased by buffing their Stamina? For example, my characters has Stamina + Primal Urge of 3, if I use the Totemic Empowerment rite my Stamina is boosted by 1. Does this mean I can hold Gauru form for one turn longer before falling into Basu-Im?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:06:19-08:00","id":1439008,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s no reason given why not as long as the buff applies in hishu form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:50:17-08:00","id":1439020,"title":"","content":"Do you have to roll for Harmony three times when you hunt and eat a human or a wolf? Once for the hunt, once for the kill, and once for consuming the flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:10:06-08:00","id":1439028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439020#post1439020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have to roll for Harmony three times when you hunt and eat a human or a wolf? Once for the hunt, once for the kill, and once for consuming the flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally just two of them, killing and consuming flesh.<br /> <br /> The hunt one is only if you're hunting them for food. And you'll generally have other avenues for food unless you're really stuck..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T23:17:06-08:00","id":1439600,"title":"","content":"Okay, that sort of answered my question, but the more I read this chart the more confused I get.<br /> <br /> If I'm a Forsaken and I deliberately hunt a human, kill them, and eat them, how many <i>total</i> Harmony breaking points do I actually roll? It seems absurd, but by a very strict interpretation, it seems like it would be four, with two of them directly contradicting:<br /> <br /> * Killing a human or wolf -&gt; Spirit<br /> * Hunting humans or wolves for food -&gt; Spirit<br /> * Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence -&gt; Spirit<br /> * Violating the Oath of the Moon (&quot;Do Not Eat the Flesh of Wolf or Man&quot;) -&gt; Flesh<br /> <br /> I figured this can't possibly be correct, so I've been ruling that you roll twice: Once for intent, and once for action. If you engage in a premeditated hunt with the intent to devour human flesh, whether you succeed or not, you roll one breaking point. If you actually do it, whether premeditated or not, you roll one breaking point. If you succeed in a premeditated hunt and devour human flesh, you roll twice. These are both toward Spirit, even though a violation of the Oath should pull you toward Flesh, because otherwise it's a sin in both directions which seems bizarre.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you wanted to get <i>really</i> technical, you could say that you have to roll again if they die. &quot;Eating humans or wolves for food&quot; could mean that you just bit off an arm or leg and left them alive. Again, this seems ridiculously legalistic and complicated though.<br /> <br /> Does my solution seem reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","user":"AsaTJ","date":". 03-13-2021, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T00:38:35-08:00","id":1439608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439600#post1439600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because otherwise it's a sin in both directions which seems bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you are offering a bizarre situation, one that is only really necessary for the very powerful werewolves with high Primal Urge and who would likely have other means at their disposal to get Essence.<br /> <br /> If you are hunting to eat a man for food, and eat them for Essence, then it stands that your food is Essence, which is your diet at Primal Urge 8-10. If you are hunting a man for food, and you kill them, and they're now dead, then you start eating them, you don't get any Essence. It requires live prey.<br /> <br /> So if you -are- the high Primal Urge Werewolf and you've performed a hunt solely for food and you've eaten that person alive, then killed them, that is four rolls (for simplicity's sake, you can make it two, adding up the penalties to Spirit for one Spirit roll, but it's such a bizarre and noteworthy act that you should probably roll it separately, I mean you just hunted a person down to eat what may be their soul, this is wildly spirit-like).<br /> <br /> But as a new PC out of chargen at Primal Urge 1, you would just kill them and cook them up, since at that point you can't eat raw meat, but you wouldn't have had to do the 'eating flesh for Essence' sin if you didn't want to. Then you just have the 3 Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> To sum up, it's natural. Expect Harmony to yo-yo. Werewolves are shapeshifters, and pulled apart by the rules of two worlds they don't wholly belong to. The disruption is intended, especially when put into extreme circumstances like starving and having nothing to eat but another person who's hiding from you. It's not meant to be that easy to stay at Harmony 5, and it is meant to be easy to slip away. You don't lose your character sheet for bottoming out anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2021, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:03:01-08:00","id":1439610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439608#post1439608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are hunting to eat a man for food, and eat them for Essence, then it stands that your food is Essence</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, necessarily. You get Essence from eating human or wolf flesh regardless of your primal urge. So you might not need it to survive but it's a very quick way to get 7 or 8 Essence without having to go into the Shadow or piss off the spirit courts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439608#post1439608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's such a bizarre and noteworthy act</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently my group is bizarre.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439608#post1439608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at Primal Urge 1, you would just kill them and cook them up, since at that point you can't eat raw meat</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't read it that way at all. I think at Primal Urge 4+ you can <i>no longer </i>benefit from cooked meat, but nowhere does it suggest that you <i>can't </i>get nourishment from raw meat at lower levels. I interpret those diet restrictions as not being that you have to stay exactly at that tier. You just have to eat the food for your Primal Urge or higher. ie: A Primal Urge 3 werewolf could still get nourishment from tiger meat, even though they're not at the level that they <i>have to</i> prey on carnivores.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439608#post1439608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expect Harmony to yo-yo. Werewolves are shapeshifters, and pulled apart by the rules of two worlds they don't wholly belong to. The disruption is intended, especially when put into extreme circumstances like starving and having nothing to eat but another person who's hiding from you. It's not meant to be that easy to stay at Harmony 5, and it is meant to be easy to slip away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but it seems like if one act is a breaking point in both directions (like eating human flesh), then it shouldn't even be a breaking point at all. Because at that point it doesn't really pull you one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:15:57-08:00","id":1439612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439610#post1439610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so, necessarily. You get Essence from eating human or wolf flesh regardless of your primal urge. So you might not need it to survive but it's a very quick way to get 7 or 8 Essence without having to go into the Shadow or piss off the spirit courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but you're not hunting for food there, you're just hunting for Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apparently my group is bizarre. </div> </div> </div>Human eating comes up (my first 2e character routinely ate humans for Essence), it's just the situation of having no food around except one person you have to hunt down is a unique one, to me. Like maybe a human Uber driver was driving a pack of werewolves through a desert or other place far from civilization, and the car breaks down but no one has a way to fix it, and for some reason there's also no animals around for them to hunt and eat, and some of the werewolves were already starving, and the Uber driver somehow got away so they had to be hunted down, rather than just killed on the spot? I'm not sure. I think except for extreme environments like Antarctica a werewolf who was concerned would be able to shift to wolf form and hunt down some small animal. I'm honestly curious at this point how is it working out? I want to ask if it's a Dark Era but those would probably have more animals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't read it that way at all. I think at Primal Urge 4+ you can <i>no longer </i>benefit from cooked meat, but nowhere does it suggest that you <i>can't </i>get nourishment from raw meat at lower levels. I interpret those diet restrictions as not being that you have to stay exactly at that tier. You just have to eat the food for your Primal Urge or higher. ie: A Primal Urge 3 werewolf could still get nourishment from tiger meat, even though they're not at the level that they <i>have to</i> prey on carnivores. </div> </div> </div>You're right, it's just that eating uncooked human flesh at Primal Urge 1 is more likely to make you vomit at some point than fill you with nourishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that, but it seems like if one act is a breaking point in both directions (like eating human flesh), then it shouldn't even be a breaking point at all. Because at that point it doesn't really pull you one way or another. </div> </div> </div>That's providing you fail both or succeed at both. It's possible to succeed all three checks to pull you to spirit and fail the one to pull you to flesh. Benefit of the dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2021, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T04:05:34-08:00","id":1439627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439600#post1439600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm a Forsaken and I deliberately hunt a human, kill them, and eat them, how many <i>total</i> Harmony breaking points do I actually roll? It seems absurd, but by a very strict interpretation, it seems like it would be four, with two of them directly contradicting</div> </div> </div> </div>The way my group has been running it is that Harmony rolls occur at the end of the scene. If you have multiple breaking points towards spirit, apply those as modifiers to the roll. However you can end up needing to roll once towards Flesh and once towards Spirit at the end of a scene and that's totally fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439608#post1439608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as a new PC out of chargen at Primal Urge 1, you would just kill them and cook them up, since at that point you can't eat raw meat, but you wouldn't have had to do the 'eating flesh for Essence' sin if you didn't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure where you're getting this idea from. Urshul and Urhan forms would be more than capable of eating raw meat (wolves do it all the time after all) and arguably Dalu form would too. The book even has a sidebar on this very point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can eat the flesh of wolves and humans. For every point of damage caused by an Uratha\u2019s bite, they can choose to ingest the flesh and gain a point of Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to remember that Hishu form isn't the &quot;natural&quot; or &quot;native&quot; form of Werewolves. All 5 forms are equally natural to them, including forms that have a much easier time eating raw meat than most humans would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1439612#post1439612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, it's just that eating uncooked human flesh at Primal Urge 1 is more likely to make you vomit at some point than fill you with nourishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt this. Even at Primal Urge 1 any poison or toxin is reduced in severity by 1, and I very much doubt that raw meat would count as anything more than a severity 1 toxin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T15:30:04-07:00","id":1440758,"title":"","content":"I was just looking through werewolf and I was wondering does fearless hunter let you enter a contest of wills when against mind influencing powers because if not that's rather odd. Mind-influencing powers, last time I checked, don't by default into a clash of wills unless you have a power that protects you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T15:49:51-07:00","id":1440761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440758#post1440758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just looking through werewolf and I was wondering does fearless hunter let you enter a contest of wills when against mind influencing powers because if not that's rather odd. Mind-influencing powers, last time I checked, don't by default into a clash of wills unless you have a power that protects you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills comes up in two situations (and the second situation is just a clarification that the first situation has occurred): When there's no other way to resolve the conflict between two powers, and when a power explicitly calls for it. Fearless Hunter clearly states how it affects mind affecting powers so there's no reason to use Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:01:21-07:00","id":1440764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440761#post1440761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clash of Wills comes up in two situations (and the second situation is just a clarification that the first situation has occurred): When there's no other way to resolve the conflict between two powers, and when a power explicitly calls for it. Fearless Hunter clearly states how it affects mind affecting powers so there's no reason to use Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fearless hunter stats that it adds glory to rolls contesting mind-influencing powers. I guess this is the problem with being one of the first 2e books, but most powers don't actually contest outside of clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:03:21-07:00","id":1440765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440758#post1440758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just looking through werewolf and I was wondering does fearless hunter let you enter a contest of wills when against mind influencing powers because if not that's rather odd. Mind-influencing powers, last time I checked, don't by default into a clash of wills unless you have a power that protects you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most mind-influencing powers will either let you contest the roll - for example Primal Allure from the Gift of Dominance - or resist the power. There are only a few examples of Werewolf powers that are resisted rather than contested - an example is Garble from the Gift of Technology - so you'll typically be rolling against them, and having + Glory Renown is extremely helpful in such scenarios.<br /> <br /> Fearless Hunter doesn't seem to let you enter into a Clash of Wills in situations where there is no roll, but I can't think of any such examples off the top of my head. Is there a specific situation that doesn't call for a roll that you were thinking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:06:38-07:00","id":1440767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440765#post1440765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most mind-influencing powers will either let you contest the roll - for example Primal Allure from the Gift of Dominance - or resist the power. There are only a few examples of Werewolf powers that are resisted rather than contested - an example is Garble from the Gift of Technology - so you'll typically be rolling against them, and having + Glory Renown is extremely helpful in such scenarios.<br /> <br /> Fearless Hunter doesn't seem to let you enter into a Clash of Wills in situations where there is no roll, but I can't think of any such examples off the top of my head. Is there a specific situation that doesn't call for a roll that you were thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just research for a crossover game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:30:17-07:00","id":1440771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440764#post1440764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fearless hunter stats that it adds glory to rolls contesting mind-influencing powers. I guess this is the problem with being one of the first 2e books, but most powers don't actually contest outside of clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most powers that would affect agency of a character are rolled, and that activation roll is either contested or resisted. It's that dice pool or resistance that Fearless Hunter adds Glory to. Clash of Wills rolls are contested, but it's not that kind of roll that Fearless Hunter refers to.<br /> <br /> The only two situations Fearless Hunter wouldn't work is when it's a Mage spell/Attainment since those are Withstood (though it's ridiculously easy to house rule that Fearless Hunter increases Resolve/Composure when Withstanding spells/Attainments that inflict mind control or fear) and when the power isn't rolled at all (for example Dread Presence, the first dot of Nightmare in VtR). In general I think such effects are pretty tame so it's not much of a bother, but I might be mistaken. It's not like I can remember every single power over twelve different games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:35:58-07:00","id":1440773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440767#post1440767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just research for a crossover game.</div> </div> </div> </div>In crossover I would probably be a bit more generous with how the power works. For example there are a few Vampire powers (Majesty 1 and Nightmare 1) that can only be contested by Lashing Out with Predatory Aura. Since other splats don't have a Predatory Aura, I would tend to let them Clash of Wills these powers (although we have a house rule for Werewolf that the Hunter's Aspect can challenge a Vampire's Predatory Aura).<br /> <br /> Beyond that, most other mind-influencing powers across all splats I can think of are either contested or resisted. In cases where they aren't I would take a look to see if the splat in question has some way to avoid them (like with Predatory Aura). If they do I would lean towards Clash of Wills, if they don't then the power is probably not intended to be resisted and I would tend not to allow Fearless Hunter to work in those cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:48:31-07:00","id":1440776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440773#post1440773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although we have a house rule for Werewolf that the Hunter's Aspect can challenge a Vampire's Predatory Aura)</div> </div> </div> </div>While not explicit (and thus definitely a house rule), I'm like 75% sure that's intended since some other splats can explicitly counter other splats' auras with their own auras and Awe/Dread Presence are intended to be an extension of a vampire's Predatory Aura, hence why it's countered using the Predatory Aura. Unfortunately Werewolf is one of the games where it's not stated they can use their Hunter's Aspect to protect against other splats' auras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T15:20:48-07:00","id":1440864,"title":"","content":"Does the Knotted Paths Facet of Nature's Gift prevent escape via supernatural powers such as teleportation? I'm sure that it would at least afford a Clash of Wills, but such powers don't just overcome it entirely, do they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T16:53:01-07:00","id":1440874,"title":"","content":"Clash of Wills sounds like the appropriate response there. It normally manifests as a &quot;no matter where you turn&quot; experience, but the actual effect of the facet is &quot;you can't escape the area.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T18:16:40-07:00","id":1440883,"title":"","content":"Does the Werewolf Second Edition core have anything that is direct about the question of where Uratha come from? Do they all start out as Wolf-Blooded? Does that mean that people who become Wolf-Blooded through a supernatural encounter can later experience the First Change? Is it still a particular part of the lore that being a werewolf is hereditary? Is everybody who is the child of a werewolf a Wolf-Blooded, and if they aren't can the seemingly normal ones still inherit the capacity to Change?<br /> <br /> I've looked around the book, particularly at the Wolf-Blooded appendix, but I don't quite feel like I've found a straight answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T18:17:51-07:00","id":1440884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440773#post1440773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although we have a house rule for Werewolf that the Hunter's Aspect can challenge a Vampire's Predatory Aura)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the \u201cOther Auras\u201d sidebar in Requiem not say that it can? I thought it did but can\u2019t check right now. EDIT: It does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 03-21-2021, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T19:37:01-07:00","id":1440893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440883#post1440883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Werewolf Second Edition core have anything that is direct about the question of where Uratha come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the same as 1e \u2014 lycanthropy isn't consistently hereditary, but the spiritual significance of a family legacy means it tends to garner notice and Wolf-Blooded who're related to werewolves aren't hard to find, nor is a Wolf-Blooded guaranteed to result from werewolf stock or to experience or be prevented from experiencing the First Change. The only change of note is that Ghost Children aren't a thing anymore and thus werewolves can have children with other werewolves just fine.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can come from anywhere, but they tend to be modeled as Wolf-Blooded in the leadup to the First Change if not sooner, and Wolf-Blooded tend to be proximate to werewolves from causes both familial and revelatory. Werewolves come from First Changes, which happen on arbitrary criteria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T19:38:12-07:00","id":1440894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440884#post1440884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the \u201cOther Auras\u201d sidebar in Requiem not say that it can? I thought it did but can\u2019t check right now. EDIT: It does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's a bit vague. VtR just says Werewolves have their own aura too, but doesn't clarify what that is mechanically. It seems pretty obvious that the intent was that Predatory Aura and Hunter's Aspect should interact, but as it's not stated in the rules anywhere we just make is explicit via houserule. It's not perfect either since Hunter's Aura is almost always stronger (attribute + skill + renown versus attribute + blood potency).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440883#post1440883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Werewolf Second Edition core have anything that is direct about the question of where Uratha come from? Do they all start out as Wolf-Blooded? Does that mean that people who become Wolf-Blooded through a supernatural encounter can later experience the First Change? Is it still a particular part of the lore that being a werewolf is hereditary? Is everybody who is the child of a werewolf a Wolf-Blooded, and if they aren't can the seemingly normal ones still inherit the capacity to Change?<br /> <br /> I've looked around the book, particularly at the Wolf-Blooded appendix, but I don't quite feel like I've found a straight answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge it's not made explicit anywhere in the book, but it is implied in the section on the First Change on page 57 and in the Wolf-Blooded appendix. The assumption is that most Werewolf characters do not have Werewolf or Wolf-Blooded parents - they appeared to be totally normal people until Luna chose to grant her gift for her own inscrutable reasons. On the flip side though, the implication is that the offspring of Wolf-Blooded and of Werewolves are more likely (though by no means guaranteed) to be Wolf-Blooded or Werewolves themselves (though the chance of being a full Werewolf is still vanishingly slim). Most Werewolves probably have Wolf-Blooded ancestry if you go back far enough as do most Wolf-Blooded. Being born and raised within a pack is a merit Wolf-Blooded can take though, so it's safe to assume that this is the exception rather than the rule. Wolf-Blooded <i>can</i> experience the First change and become full Werewolves, but most don't. However there is nothing to stop a character from starting as mortal, becoming Wolf Blooded via dramatic failure on a lunacy check, and then later becoming a full Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T19:51:55-07:00","id":1440895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440894#post1440894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not perfect either since Hunter's Aura is almost always stronger (attribute + skill + renown versus attribute + blood potency).</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably, the Predatory Aura fills this discrepancy with bonuses from hunger and territory, and has three different inexpensive Merits to specialize its use \u2014 a vampire on their turf rolls Attribute + Blood Potency + Feeding Grounds; even off their turf, their dicepool is largely consistent and they very probably have 8-Again on the method they favor. Being able to roll Attribute + Skill + Renown is skewed by the need to roll <i>contextually appropriate</i> Attribute + Skill, whereas a Ventrue looking to drag you into a Competitive mood gets an approach-agnostic Intelligence + Blood Potency every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T01:49:42-07:00","id":1440913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1440894#post1440894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's a bit vague. VtR just says Werewolves have their own aura too, but doesn't clarify what that is mechanically. It seems pretty obvious that the intent was that Predatory Aura and Hunter's Aspect should interact, but as it's not stated in the rules anywhere we just make is explicit via houserule. It's not perfect either since Hunter's Aura is almost always stronger (attribute + skill + renown versus attribute + blood potency).</div> </div> </div> </div>The sidebar says nothing about interactions because it's not actually about what kind of aura werewolves have as much as it's about vampires instinctively recognising other predators on sight. It's an extension of vampires being able to recognise each other on sight.<br /> Also, Hunter's Aspect was almost definitely not written or even fully decided upon when Blood &amp; Smoke was released, so not really possible to reference other rules. This is in contrast to the Nimbus in Mage that has explicit rules for how to defend against other splats' auras, even though they're kinda sucky. My guess is that by that point the aura thing was settled to a certain extent, allowing for generic rules for crossover interactions, but later games and 2e updates dropped it either because the writers didn't think/care about such things and/or because the aura powers started taking weird forms that weren't really compatible with Mage's generic aura defense rules.<br /> <br /> Vampires can easily have 8 Again on their preferred aspect since it's a whole whopping one dot Merit (more specifically, three mutually exclusive one dot Merits), but in practice I wouldn't say it's common since players, STs, and writers for published NPCs can and does just as easily forget that those Merits exists.<br /> On the other hand, Renown is capped at five dots so for advanced characters the difference in dice pools becomes less pronounced. That coincides nicely with vampires generally scaling much better with higher power stats than werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T12:18:05-07:00","id":1441283,"title":"","content":"Is there anything that mentions details of how long Uratha live? To my recollection, First Edition had ideas seeded about that it had been observed that some werewolves had lived longer than the natural human lifespan, and nobody could really say if any of them had ever died of old age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T14:32:38-07:00","id":1441302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441283#post1441283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that mentions details of how long Uratha live? To my recollection, First Edition had ideas seeded about that it had been observed that some werewolves had lived longer than the natural human lifespan, and nobody could really say if any of them had ever died of old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the corebook just says that Uratha lead dangerous lives and so they are always killed before they can die of old age.<br /> <br /> Thinking about how Uratha regeneration works it seems unlikely that they would suffer any of the usual drawbacks due to aging. If they can regrow whole limbs and organs then repairing damage to their bodies due to age should be something their regeneration can do as well. The book also says they subtract their Primal Urge from the Toxicity rating of poisons and diseases, so provided an older Uratha is Primal Urge 5 or higher they should be immune to all mundane poisons and diseases.<br /> <br /> Personally my thinking is that Uratha are functionally immortal, and so centuries old Uratha do exist. However they are very rare and tend towards Primal Urge 10. Their packs have probably died off long ago, and so they struggle to maintain their harmony and often lean towards the Spirit, some even ending up trapped in the Shadow with no one to help pull them back. Their high Primal Urge means that they are almost entirely consumed by the Hunt, and they have a difficult time interacting with normal Humans due to the effects of lunacy and their feeding restrictions. The effects of Sheep's Clothing becomes so powerful for them that even other Werewolves don't notice if they happen to pass them on the street. These ancient wolves might end up working with their Tribal Totems or other extremely powerful spirits, taking entire countries as their territory and hunting the most powerful threats from the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T15:34:51-07:00","id":1441313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441283#post1441283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that mentions details of how long Uratha live? To my recollection, First Edition had ideas seeded about that it had been observed that some werewolves had lived longer than the natural human lifespan, and nobody could really say if any of them had ever died of old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I believe they've doubled down on that just because it's more interesting than saying 'At Primal Urge X, you live to Y years old.' Like our example werewolves, particulary Cyrus and Zud'nalu are very old and in good shape for it, at least physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T18:31:52-07:00","id":1441333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441302#post1441302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the corebook just says that Uratha lead dangerous lives and so they are always killed before they can die of old age.<br /> <br /> Thinking about how Uratha regeneration works it seems unlikely that they would suffer any of the usual drawbacks due to aging. If they can regrow whole limbs and organs then repairing damage to their bodies due to age should be something their regeneration can do as well. The book also says they subtract their Primal Urge from the Toxicity rating of poisons and diseases, so provided an older Uratha is Primal Urge 5 or higher they should be immune to all mundane poisons and diseases.<br /> <br /> Personally my thinking is that Uratha are functionally immortal, and so centuries old Uratha do exist. However they are very rare and tend towards Primal Urge 10. Their packs have probably died off long ago, and so they struggle to maintain their harmony and often lean towards the Spirit, some even ending up trapped in the Shadow with no one to help pull them back. Their high Primal Urge means that they are almost entirely consumed by the Hunt, and they have a difficult time interacting with normal Humans due to the effects of lunacy and their feeding restrictions. The effects of Sheep's Clothing becomes so powerful for them that even other Werewolves don't notice if they happen to pass them on the street. These ancient wolves might end up working with their Tribal Totems or other extremely powerful spirits, taking entire countries as their territory and hunting the most powerful threats from the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there also may have been lines in the past suggesting that very old werewolves were speculated to kind of become spirits, and I was thinking myself that getting more powerful doesn't make them safer if it ups the ante for what qualifies as valid prey, so I'd find your ideas here in line with that. I think it's particularly interesting to extrapolate from strong breaking points towards the Spirit that push them deep into the Shadow and make it hard to come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T17:37:21-07:00","id":1441439,"title":"","content":"Would packs of the Pure ever include humans the way that Forsaken ones do? Or at least Wolf-Blooded? I do expect such a thing is incompatible with the driving ethos of the Ivory Claws and especially the Predator Kings, but maybe there could be some Fire-Touched out there who accumulate a little cult of people fanatically drawn into a system of abuse and self-flagellation?<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering because I had this notion of a mage trying to investigate a Pure pack through pursuing the realm in the Astral Temenos formed around the human side of it, and I wanted ideas on if that was really a thing.<br /> <br /> (Of course, it's possible for Forsaken to be antagonists to mages themselves, so one could definitely approach the realms for the human element of their packs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T18:36:24-07:00","id":1441446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441439#post1441439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would packs of the Pure ever include humans the way that Forsaken ones do? Or at least Wolf-Blooded? I do expect such a thing is incompatible with the driving ethos of the Ivory Claws and especially the Predator Kings, but maybe there could be some Fire-Touched out there who accumulate a little cult of people fanatically drawn into a system of abuse and self-flagellation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they would. It would be hard for the Ivory Claws to maintain an importance of bloodlines and familial honor if they just tossed humans out with the rubbish. Even the Predator Kings would do it, they would just be sure to instill in them a sense of honor and reliance for the hunt. Plus it's good to have extra manpower that isn't as valuable as those who have gone through the First Change. All the tribes seem to appreciate the value of wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> From the core, 'Family is family, and the Wolf-Blooded of the Pure are fierce and dangerous and useful so long as they aren\u2019t broken and spineless. No Wolf-Blooded is good for a pack if he is feckless.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T20:03:13-07:00","id":1441456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441446#post1441446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, they would. It would be hard for the Ivory Claws to maintain an importance of bloodlines and familial honor if they just tossed humans out with the rubbish. Even the Predator Kings would do it, they would just be sure to instill in them a sense of honor and reliance for the hunt. Plus it's good to have extra manpower that isn't as valuable as those who have gone through the First Change. All the tribes seem to appreciate the value of wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> From the core, 'Family is family, and the Wolf-Blooded of the Pure are fierce and dangerous and useful so long as they aren\u2019t broken and spineless. No Wolf-Blooded is good for a pack if he is feckless.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, good. An interesting and oblique angle for mages to investigate such groupings, a slight liability that can be introduced by the human association.<br /> <br /> Mind, I expect the realm of a werewolf pack could have some very scary Goetic archetypes representing how those humans perceive the werewolves. I would also find it fitting for a mage to think they're being very clever to launch an inquiry or attack through the Temenos, and then find they've bitten off more than they can chew in the human dreams about the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Although now I'm also picturing a mage who summons that archetype into reality, binds it to their will and sets it against the pack that spawned it. Interesting fight, presuming the Ban does not prevent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T20:49:14-07:00","id":1441458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1441456#post1441456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, good. An interesting and oblique angle for mages to investigate such groupings, a slight liability that can be introduced by the human association.<br /> <br /> Mind, I expect the realm of a werewolf pack could have some very scary Goetic archetypes representing how those humans perceive the werewolves. I would also find it fitting for a mage to think they're being very clever to launch an inquiry or attack through the Temenos, and then find they've bitten off more than they can chew in the human dreams about the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Although now I'm also picturing a mage who summons that archetype into reality, binds it to their will and sets it against the pack that spawned it. Interesting fight, presuming the Ban does not prevent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots you can do with that, not all of the tribes would be aggressive to a mage outsider. There was a cabal of wolf-blooded in our last mage game, descended from Pure ancestry and raised by Pure tribes before they awakened. The one who was raised by the Predator Kings was sort of nabbed and hoodwinked, though. The mage who had been studying their pack was a member of the Devourers of Flesh legacy, who basically tap into the last vestiges of Pangaea (at least it seemed this way reading about them after second edition came out) and empower themselves by hunting and eating their prey. He managed to hide his legacy from the Order (they're a left hand path) but hid it's forbidden nature to his student, so the Predator King Mage who had a chance to basically become anything after Awakening was then lured into forging his soul into a thing of cannibalistic predation. Great guy, sad sacrifice at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T19:28:01-07:00","id":1442350,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a supernatural creature to be claimed by a spirit and become a host?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T19:48:16-07:00","id":1442352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442350#post1442350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a supernatural creature to be claimed by a spirit and become a host?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mummies and Sin-Eaters are the only ones immune to claiming in second edition, so yes. At the very least the big three (vampires, werewolves, and mages) could be possessed or claimed. Individual cores will have individual rules for more.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing you didn't mean hosts as in shartha but the ruling on them with other supernaturals is unclear. Werewolves are immune to Joining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T11:43:46-07:00","id":1442417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442352#post1442352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Individual cores will have individual rules for more.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing you didn't mean hosts as in shartha but the ruling on them with other supernaturals is unclear. Werewolves are immune to Joining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm asking if they would become strange hybrid monsters between spirit and flesh.<br /> Like, what would a changeling become if a spirit merge with them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T11:53:08-07:00","id":1442418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442417#post1442417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm asking if they would become strange hybrid monsters between spirit and flesh.<br /> Like, what would a changeling become if a spirit merge with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they would. All the stuff described in the Claimed Condition.<br /> <br /> Based on the example in werewolf, they'd have access to all the changelings powers but the new entity would be unable to get new contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T13:03:29-07:00","id":1442429,"title":"","content":"On that note, I wonder what would happen if a human underwent the First Change while Claimed? Immediate exorcism? A nightmarish <i>Kuruth</i> for the ages? Something even stranger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T14:30:20-07:00","id":1442437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442429#post1442429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, I wonder what would happen if a human underwent the First Change while Claimed? Immediate exorcism? A nightmarish <i>Kuruth</i> for the ages? Something even stranger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it could happen since, at the point you're claimed, you're no longer human. And if Luna or whoever wanted to force the matter they maintain the power to kick out a spirit even if it's embedded in someone's mind, body, and soul.<br /> <br /> But if you want a, Mimic could be a good example, it might even be the source of them. The problem is you wouldn't be able to get new Gifts and such so while you would have the nice Attribute increases and shapeshifting you would lack supernatural powers beyond the Dread Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-02-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T14:54:14-07:00","id":1442770,"title":"","content":"Is there any rumours about a next book for Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T17:02:41-07:00","id":1442785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442770#post1442770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any rumours about a next book for Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing past dev prep, but they're not allowed to talk about anything before that. A few years ago Secrets of the Tribes was announced in a brochure and there has been no word of it being cancelled. Basically, rumors aren't really that common. Hopes are, but if people are talking about a book it's because it was announced at some point. Books like Tome of the Pentacle and such were all announced years before they made it to the Monday meeting list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Named wrong book 04-05-2021, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T22:48:42-07:00","id":1442804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442785#post1442785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing past dev prep, but they're not allowed to talk about anything before that. A few years ago Secrets of the Tribes was announced in a brochure and there has been no word of it being cancelled. Basically, rumors aren't really that common. Hopes are, but if people are talking about a book it's because it was announced at some point. Books like Tome of the Pentacle and such were all announced years before they made it to the Monday meeting list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully the brochure that's supposed to be coming out in the next few months will reveal an upcoming product (Secrets of the Tribes would be awesome) though with Dixie's comments on the podcast I'm less hopeful (Forsaken doesn't have a line developer anymore and Acrozatarim likely has his plate full with Aberrant).<br /> <br /> Several of the CofD lines don't seem to have anything coming up in the Monday Meeting Notes other than fulfilling kickstarters, so the brochure should let us know what's coming down the pipe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T23:37:31-07:00","id":1442805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1442804#post1442804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully the brochure that's supposed to be coming out in the next few months will reveal an upcoming product (Secrets of the Tribes would be awesome) though with Dixie's comments on the podcast I'm less hopeful (Forsaken doesn't have a line developer anymore and Acrozatarim likely has his plate full with Aberrant).<br /> <br /> Several of the CofD lines don't seem to have anything coming up in the Monday Meeting Notes other than fulfilling kickstarters, so the brochure should let us know what's coming down the pipe.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of their 'Ask Onyx Path' videos they did say that they were trying to focus on getting the Kickstarter stuff out, and it seemed like a big priority. Which makes sense, people have been complaining about the Kickstarters not coming out fast enough and refusing to back others due to the potential length of time until the books come out.<br /> <br /> Most of the Chronicles stuff doesn't have line developers. Dixie explained (it might have been in the next one) that they usually only have a line developer when a lot of books are going to come out at once, like at the beginning of a line (like Scion). I think of all the Chronicles books to come out in the past few years only one mentions having a line developer.<br /> <br /> Anyways I certainly hope we'll get more books for Werewolf the Forsaken. I've never been more interested or invested in the game, and we have great writers that have been putting out absolute home runs for books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-06-2021, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:44:27-07:00","id":1443839,"title":"","content":"City-spirits. Not just urban spirits, but spirits of the actual city, or town and such. Are there any examples, canon or not, 1E or 2E?<br /> <br /> Scouring the forums gives me the Urban Avatar from Territories (which... I don't have), something in Wolfsbane (yay I have this one), something in Shadows Over the UK (also lacking), and a mention of chenghuanshen from the Actual Play: Eater of Names thread (which I haven't read yet). Any more out there that I missed, even it's not from Werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T06:45:15-07:00","id":1443871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1443839#post1443839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">City-spirits. Not just urban spirits, but spirits of the actual city, or town and such. Are there any examples, canon or not, 1E or 2E?<br /> <br /> Scouring the forums gives me the Urban Avatar from Territories (which... I don't have), something in Wolfsbane (yay I have this one), something in Shadows Over the UK (also lacking), and a mention of chenghuanshen from the Actual Play: Eater of Names thread (which I haven't read yet). Any more out there that I missed, even it's not from Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>They tend to be rather big so they don't usually get statted up for play. But Night Horrors: Wolfsbane has Lonesome Forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T16:33:52-07:00","id":1443948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1443871#post1443871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They tend to be rather big so they don't usually get statted up for play. But Night Horrors: Wolfsbane has Lonesome Forest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that might actually be close to what I'm looking for. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:59:47-07:00","id":1445549,"title":"","content":"The Madness Condition uses Integrity, but what happens if it's used on something that doesn't have Integrity, like a werewolf? Does it just not work? Do you use Harmony instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:24:17-07:00","id":1445553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1445549#post1445549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Madness Condition uses Integrity, but what happens if it's used on something that doesn't have Integrity, like a werewolf? Does it just not work?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to work at least sometimes, because the Dement Numina says that it can be resisted with Composure + Primal Urge and it can be inflicted by an <i>idigam</i> on werewolves using Forge Empty Wolf. So it seems like only relatively powerful magic can do that to something other than normal human in the first place (and Dement only works for a scene).<br /> <br /> Still, I think it's reasonable enough for it to substitute Harmony for werewolves, both in the interests of letting the mechanics function and following a logic in which being a lot closer to the Spirit side creates quirks in behaviour that at least resemble the mental disruption that humans experience, which powers that impose the Condition can capitalise upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T02:31:03-07:00","id":1445632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1445549#post1445549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Madness Condition uses Integrity, but what happens if it's used on something that doesn't have Integrity, like a werewolf? Does it just not work? Do you use Harmony instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird. There's five sources of the Madness Condition in WtF 2e core. Three are only applicable to humans and one is applicable on everyone* but the last one, Forge Empty Wolf, is <i>specifically only applicable on werewolves</i>. It's quite the oversight that the Madness Condition doesn't actually reflect this.<br /> <br /> In Mage, however, it's specified that mages just substitute Wisdom for Integrity. Changeling also handles it the same way by using current Clarity while Deviant uses (Resolve + Acclimation) since Acclimation starts at 0 and that'd be really bad for deviants.<br /> I'd recommend just using Harmony in Werewolf. Isator Levi makes a good point about spirit-like behaviour.<br /> <br /> *Fun fact: The Dement Numen, which can apply the Madness Condition on everyone, can also be found in GMC/DtD, CofD, MtA 2e, BtP, CtL 2e and PtC 2e. But in all those books it instead applies the Insane Tilt which doesn't use Integrity or equivalent traits. But for some reason Werewolf does not include the Insane Tilt so I guess they had to change Dement to reflect this but forgetting to change Madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:51:24-07:00","id":1445679,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I've always wondered about some applications of the Create and Mass Create functions of Influence. Suppose it's a spirit with Influence Mountain or Building, would you be creating a structure in the Shadow akin to unawakened reflections? If used in the material world, would you think it can only ever cause these things to spring up in complete form out of nowhere, or could it be valid to define an end result that circumstances then work to bring about naturally?<br /> <br /> On the other side, if a high Rank wolf spirit Creates wolves in the Shadow, are they going to be running around same as if an animal stumbled through a Verge until the power ends or... they starve?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T00:04:33-07:00","id":1445939,"title":"","content":"Is there a way for wolf-blooded to identify uratha without straight up seeing something werewolf-y happen and recognizing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26808-katieplays","name":"KatiePlays","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26808_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T10:43:41-07:00","id":1445984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KatiePlays</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1445939#post1445939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for wolf-blooded to identify uratha without straight up seeing something werewolf-y happen and recognizing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing by default, nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T16:15:47-07:00","id":1446002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1445984#post1445984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing by default, nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thanks for confirming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26808-katieplays","name":"KatiePlays","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26808_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T19:20:10-07:00","id":1446018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1445679#post1445679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit, I've always wondered about some applications of the Create and Mass Create functions of Influence. Suppose it's a spirit with Influence Mountain or Building, would you be creating a structure in the Shadow akin to unawakened reflections? If used in the material world, would you think it can only ever cause these things to spring up in complete form out of nowhere, or could it be valid to define an end result that circumstances then work to bring about naturally?<br /> <br /> On the other side, if a high Rank wolf spirit Creates wolves in the Shadow, are they going to be running around same as if an animal stumbled through a Verge until the power ends or... they starve?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea on how it\u2019s supposed to work by RAW, but I\u2019d rule it so that using Create Influence to naturally make things over a long period, part-by-part, is just... done, without even spending Essence. The spirit wills, and the world resonates. This would mean that spending Essence to Create (as the normal mechanics) results in \u2018whole\u2019 but only temporary creations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T09:31:24-07:00","id":1446994,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how fo you handle Rituals during combat? I know the book gives a -2 because of the distraction, but is the time handled different in those ocassions, I mean each turn is like a couple of seconds (in 1ed it was 3 seconds each turn iirc) and some of the rites could last hours...so I'm kind of wondering what happened there and how do you handle it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:54:11-07:00","id":1447064,"title":"","content":"Does a spirit inside a Claimed host dies when the host dies? Or he merely hibernate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:06:13-07:00","id":1447065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1447064#post1447064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a spirit inside a Claimed host dies when the host dies? Or he merely hibernate?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're expelled but still active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:23:23-07:00","id":1447069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1446994#post1446994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering how fo you handle Rituals during combat? I know the book gives a -2 because of the distraction, but is the time handled different in those ocassions, I mean each turn is like a couple of seconds (in 1ed it was 3 seconds each turn iirc) and some of the rites could last hours...so I'm kind of wondering what happened there and how do you handle it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intention is that Rituals can't be cast during combat - they simply take too long to cast and most combats are over within 1 minute of real time (a turn is still supposed to be about 3 seconds per page 162).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1447064#post1447064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a spirit inside a Claimed host dies when the host dies? Or he merely hibernate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this <i>should</i> permanently kill the Spirit, but since that doesn't seem to be stated anywhere I'm guessing the intent is that they become dormant as long as they have any essence left. If this is the intent, then I would probably allow Werewolves to kill the Spirit permanently if it is the target of the Siskur-Dah using the normal rules for splitting its essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:04:38-07:00","id":1447079,"title":"","content":"If you kill a Claimed, the spirit is ejected and 'disoriented' in Twilight, but likely safe unless you did enough damage to bring it to Discorporation, in which case it reforms in another place. In Shunned by the Moon, Jeremiah's spirit is given stats and if the PCs kill him it will stick around and fight. Though it's likely lost most of the Manifestations letting it stay here (if it died in the flesh world).<br /> <br /> And rites aren't made to be used in combat, aside from the relatively long lengths they can take, as it says on p140, 'If the performance of a rite breaks at any point \u2014 such as a participant being attacked and injured \u2014 a dramatic failure ensues.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2021, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T11:34:15-07:00","id":1447957,"title":"","content":"What are the key means for identifying someone as urged? Claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:18:40-07:00","id":1447972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1447957#post1447957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the key means for identifying someone as urged? Claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scent the Unnatural (Gift of Insight, Purity Facet) can identify Ridden within 10 yards per dot of Purity, and characters benefiting from the Siskur-Dah Condition granted by a Storm Lord ritemaster can clearly perceive if their prey is possessed, Urged, or Claimed.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, inference from behavior, physical changes (if any), and normal detective work (i.e. &quot;A spirit went missing recently and that guy seems to be acting funny.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T10:14:35-07:00","id":1448052,"title":"","content":"A big one for Urged is just looking. Spirits inflict the Urged Condition by using Fetter which sort of anchors them in Twilight to the target. Werewolves see spirits in Twilight as if they are Manifested, so they could see a spirit looming over someone clear as day. The spirit could try to hide, apparently inside the Fettered is a good spot, but werewolves do have senses that could find them if they search, in addition to what Satchel pointed out.<br /> <br /> Claimed often become monstrous in appearance, which can be an indicator, but that's not exactly uncommon in the world of Chronicles. I think changes are less apparent if the spirit is more human related, as well, like an obsession spirit born of a humans passions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T12:15:04-07:00","id":1448060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1448052#post1448052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claimed often become monstrous in appearance, which can be an indicator, but that's not exactly uncommon in the world of Chronicles. I think changes are less apparent if the spirit is more human related, as well, like an obsession spirit born of a humans passions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's little in the way of guidelines in Werewolf, but Hunter's 1e supplement Spirit Slayers puts the point of obvious inhumanity at the point where the host's increased Attributes break the mortal Trait cap for its take on the Ridden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T08:38:17-07:00","id":1448425,"title":"","content":"Which 1e Werewolf books are most interesting and/or important to read for someone who touched only 2e? Like, on what I should not miss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T14:44:20-07:00","id":1448467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1448425#post1448425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which 1e Werewolf books are most interesting and/or important to read for someone who touched only 2e? Like, on what I should not miss?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Predators and Territories, others depend on what you really need to know. But aside from the Pack and Shunned by the Moon, a lot of the werewolf Dark Eras are invaluable and might not be considered 'werewolf' books.<br /> <br /> Predators is, I think, the most important first edition book. It's got write-ups for something like more than 80 spirits of different types. The spirit system has changed across editions but not that much (you would have to add Manifestations and a ban or bane, though many of the write-ups offer options that could fit both), fluffwise they've just toned down the animosity towards werewolves and I think the book is good at displaying that. It gets into how spirits grow, what lunes and helions are like (might want to up the animosity with helions), explains the why and how of magath, and that's all just in one chapter. The rest has systems for urged and claimed and hosts. The mechanics for them are more different but the fluff behind it is still valid and the powers can mostly be easily transferred or just guide you idea-wise. The last chapter has the Ancients, which are easily slotted in as Pangaeans that turned to the flesh or idigam that have managed to become what they wanted to become.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, I think it depends on your interests. A lot of people have mentioned not understanding tribes, or auspices, or how they work. For them Signs of the Moon or Tribes of the Moon are pretty good for offering ideas for lore and how these things work in-setting, but the mechanics are mostly useless except as inspiration. They each have a chapter on one of the auspices or tribes and get into how they work, even offering glimpses of them across the globe. If you're interested in Ghost Wolves or Protectorates and the Pack doesn't help, The Rage might. It offers some options for them and gets into how some of the mechanical systems may be represented in-setting, but it's anchored in 1e and a lot of the mechanics are backwards.<br /> <br /> I'd like to suggest the Pure but it is very dated. It can still be used to guide the personalities and attitudes of the Pure, but a lot of it might not jibe with how they exist in second edition, focusing on the hunt and so forth. The Pure had some more objectionably bad or stupid mindsets too. War Against the Pure seems focused just on wars with the Pure, but it really opens up a concept of 'silver crusades' which are basically when the Forsaken go to war with anyone. If you want a big chronicle it can offer a lot of advice for that.<br /> <br /> Then Lore of the Forsaken. I think it was one of the first 1e supplements published, so it is -way- dated, but it can offer an outlook on the Firstborn (including the Pure ones) if you're not up to looking through the Dark Eras or forum. The big thing is that it has some systems and descriptions for how Essence appears to werewolves. It also has the Maeljin, which can be slotted in as extras beyond the prime five introduced in Shunned, or just turned into powerful spirits, each is given a lieutenant (I think they're all Rank 4?) Maeltinet spirit that, like the other spirits in Predators, can be easily converted.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Territories is a book I didn't like in first edition but looking back is still really useful (not as good as Predators but it's probably second in regards to setting-building). My problem with it as a player was that it offers a bunch of options for a territory (like park, or stadium, or university) and it was portrayed as 'if you want this, you have to pay experience to get it into your territory,' which was ridiculous given the exp costs in first edition and me believing 'getting' these things should be entirely in-story achievements. But as I've ST'd more there's a lot of good advice there for these things, it even gets into descriptions of Wounds, Glades, Barrens and Shoals. The mechanical affects for these things can be easily converted, but there are rites in it that I think should stay back in first edition. The best part, however, is that it has a few settings, specifically 'a small town, a stretch of wilderness, a section of city, a swath of suburbia and a incipient war zone.' The 'war' mentioned is in the hisil, a shadow war between spirit courts. These can do a lot to help someone who's trying to figure out how to build a setting or convert a real life setting into a more gamable playground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T07:09:58-07:00","id":1449114,"title":"","content":"When a werewolf is at Harmony 5, are the only things that can trigger <i>Kuruth</i> the general baseline ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T07:42:17-07:00","id":1449115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1449114#post1449114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a werewolf is at Harmony 5, are the only things that can trigger <i>Kuruth</i> the general baseline ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, their personal triggers are the only ones affected by Harmony","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T03:27:59-07:00","id":1449778,"title":"","content":"Has anyone written up any star-spirits, or are there any in any of the books? Ideally 2e, but 1e is good for inspiration as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T04:23:58-07:00","id":1449781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1449778#post1449778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone written up any star-spirits, or are there any in any of the books? Ideally 2e, but 1e is good for inspiration as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other than idigam Cthugha in the 2E core and the angel of Mars in Shunned by the Moon, I think there aren't any in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T05:22:40-07:00","id":1449966,"title":"","content":"Can a werewolf carry someone else with them when Reaching at a Locus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:26:58-07:00","id":1450103,"title":"","content":"In first edition, explicitly yes, although at a penalty for non-werewolves and only if the person consents. At a glance I don't see a direct method to do this in second edition, although if nothing else, it seems clearly within the design space of what rites should be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T05:39:33-07:00","id":1450162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1450103#post1450103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, explicitly yes, although at a penalty for non-werewolves and only if the person consents. At a glance I don't see a direct method to do this in second edition, although if nothing else, it seems clearly within the design space of what rites should be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm mildly hacking the thing anyway, so adding an ability to carry others across makes sense to me. Just wanted to make sure I wasn't reinventing the wheel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:31:41-07:00","id":1452521,"title":"","content":"What do spirits roll in grapple? Pure Power, or Power + Finesse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:38:58-07:00","id":1452539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1452521#post1452521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do spirits roll in grapple? Pure Power, or Power + Finesse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's Power + Finesse like with their other attacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T10:41:52-07:00","id":1453181,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at the Gluttony (Honor) Facet for the Gift of Hunger in Shunned by the Moon. Does this Facet affect supernatural &quot;appetites&quot; such as a Werewolf's Essence or a Vampire's Vitae or only mundane sources? The Gift doesn't seem to state one way or another. Being able to force say a Vampire to only get 1 Vitae for every 2-6 they consumed seems powerful, so I'm not sure if the Gift is intended to work this way or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:12:44-07:00","id":1453201,"title":"","content":"Is there any metaphorical (d)evolution for the Werewolves?<br /> Like, Vampires are kinda descendants from the Strix. Mages can become Archmages. Changelings can become a True Fae using some Eldritch Titles(maybe).<br /> <br /> Is there any non-playable being apart from Spirits that represents werewolves but is superior in power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:46:55-07:00","id":1453205,"title":"","content":"Devourers show snippets of what it's like to be a bodhisattva werewolf, with great benefits, but Devourers hijack that power through a rite and profane deeds. The bodhisattva predator is generally seen as the 'archmage' of werewolf. There's also Tyrants, and even idigam or Geryo depending on how you want to run with things.<br /> <br /> In terms of 'devolution' you have Zi'ir and Mimics and possibly void reivers. Geryo are often thought to be an alpha version of what would eventually become werewolves, but are far separate from them. And if you're feeling derogatory werewolves (and every other line) can be a shartha of some sort.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2384_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2384\" data-vbnamecard=\"2384\">Aurumae</a> Re: Gluttony, I'd allow it. Add Supernatural Tolerance to resist, it only works a day and if something is really being hunted it's not going to have to worry about it longer than that anyhow. Plus it works on guns and cars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T13:56:23-07:00","id":1454300,"title":"","content":"So, do Second Edition Uratha have any option for vertical advancement other than their Auspice Gifts and general Primal Urge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T14:05:33-07:00","id":1454301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454300#post1454300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do Second Edition Uratha have any option for vertical advancement other than their Auspice Gifts and general Primal Urge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Renown kind of works like this, since every dot grants you a new Gift Facet as well as increasing various dice pools and supernatural power factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:08:16-07:00","id":1454315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454301#post1454301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Renown kind of works like this, since every dot grants you a new Gift Facet as well as increasing various dice pools and supernatural power factors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's really only giving some extra heft to powers that the character already has. I'm thinking more about something that indicates options that would not have been available at a less mature stage of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:42:22-07:00","id":1454319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454315#post1454315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's really only giving some extra heft to powers that the character already has. I'm thinking more about something that indicates options that would not have been available at a less mature stage of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf abilities are pretty heavily front-loaded. You can get almost everything right out the gate assuming you have the right Renowns. Even 5 dot Rites just require you to spend large amounts of exp to acquire them.<br /> <br /> The only things I can think of that are restricted at character creation would be the Favored Form merit and the Moon Gifts. The only published Moon Gifts are the 5 in the core, but the book makes it clear that there could be more and that a Werewolf could have more than one. An alternate Cahalith Moon Gift was published on the blog during open development, which I have linked below. Acrozatarim has published others on his Patreon.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">The Giver of Gifts: 1 [Werewolf: The Forsaken] \u2013 Onyx Path Publishing (theonyxpath.com)</a><br /> <br /> There is also the Gift of the Elementals. Each Facet of that Gift (except Glory) gets much more powerful as your Renown increases since it increases your dots of influence over the relevant element.<br /> <br /> While it's not exactly what you were asking for, I could see a 4 or 5 dot Fetish as something an experienced, powerful Werewolf could seek out that would not be available to a weaker wolf. Binding a 5-dot Spirit is no mean feat, and while I think the examples in the Core book are generally very lacklustre, the examples listed for what a 4 or 5 dot fetish could do are extremely powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T17:59:54-07:00","id":1454488,"title":"","content":"It makes sense enough as their intended design model, just does end up feeling a bit of a pity that there isn't quite something to signify the more experienced werewolf the way one might get with vampires developing an arsenal of custom Devotions or Mastery for mages.<br /> <br /> Although I wonder about Gifts... I have a sense from some places that there's an idea of Gift varieties that have significant power and are obscure to Uratha at large, which might come with a qualifier that you'd need to be a big deal in the first place to get the spirits able to imprint them to recognise you. Is there anything to that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T18:57:52-07:00","id":1454492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454488#post1454488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I wonder about Gifts... I have a sense from some places that there's an idea of Gift varieties that have significant power and are obscure to Uratha at large, which might come with a qualifier that you'd need to be a big deal in the first place to get the spirits able to imprint them to recognise you. Is there anything to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be the case, but in general Facets in 2e are designed to be about the power level of a 3 dot gift from Werewolf 1e - Chris Allen states this explicitly in the open development blog post I linked above. Rare and powerful abilities that most Werewolves don't know are more likely to be powerful Rites than Gifts. I do wish the core book had had a bit more space to devote to the &quot;other&quot; parts of Werewolf Spirit magic. We have a very good number of Shadow Gifts (and more from Shunned by the Moon), but I feel like Rites, Fetishes, and Wolf Gifts were only given a cursory treatment, and alternate Moon Gifts were not covered at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454488#post1454488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense enough as their intended design model, just does end up feeling a bit of a pity that there isn't quite something to signify the more experienced werewolf the way one might get with vampires developing an arsenal of custom Devotions or Mastery for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite agree with this assessment. Due to the way Werewolves pick up additional Facets as they gain Renown, Werewolves with lots of Renown have access to <i>lots</i> of different Facets. The character I'm playing currently has 11 Shadow Gift Facets, 2 Wolf Gift Facets, and 3 dots in his Moon Gift. That's a lot more discrete abilities than a Vampire with similar amounts of exp would be likely to have. No individual Facet is as strong as an entire Discipline like Resilience (for example), but Berserker's Might (the Glory Facet from the Gift of Rage) is similar to Resilience's active effect. As the Vampire invests more dots in it Resilience that Discipline gets stronger. As the Werewolf invests more dots in Glory Berserker's Might gets stronger <i>and</i> so do all his other Glory Facets <i>and</i> he continues picking up new Facets. The end result is that you have a Vampire who is very, very good at one particular thing, and a Werewolf who has many more tools in his toolbox. He's not likely to be able to match the Vampire on pure damage mitigation, but is very likely to have other ways to even the scales.<br /> <br /> It's also the case that Werewolves have a tendency to get stronger <i>as a pack</i> as much as they do as individuals, whereas a Vampire's power is all individual. Several Gift Facets synergise extremely well together - for example there are several Gifts that penalise the opponent's initiative. If one of the Pack members has Pack Triumphs Together (the Honor Facet from the Gift of Inspiration) they can double down on this advantage and make it so that the <i>entire pack</i> gets the drop on their prey. If another pack member has Gift of the Screaming Moon from the blog post, or if there is an Irrakka present, these advantages are compounded even further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T20:15:35-07:00","id":1454498,"title":"","content":"Werewolf hasn't really gotten an 'end game' book. There's hints throughout second edition about the 'Bodhisattva predator' werewolf, who seems to be the equivalent of the...well, they don't really have big differences anymore, but about as big a difference from werewolves as werewolves are to hunters (from the Vigil). There are hints of their capabilities in the Devourer template, and some ideas that may indicate some direction they would go in in threads like the following:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed/page6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nleashed/page6</a><br /> Where Lycaon-Ur, a werewolf lodge totem from the core book manages to always maintain 5 Harmony.<br /> <br /> But as said, they haven't gotten an 'end game' book like Thousand Years of Night or Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> That said, while a werewolf at Primal Urge 1 and one at Primal Urge 10 may have access to some of the same powers (like those in the core) the gap in power tends to be pretty large. You are capable of tracking much easier, regenerating quickly and casually (to the point one doesn't really need to go into gauru to get a 'full heal'). And a lot of that journey to become like Father Wolf is going to get you picking up fetishes and obscure rites or gifts or just weird abilities, like Lycaon-Ur's ability to not be erased from existence and, if he dies, come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-07-2021, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T10:34:43-07:00","id":1454530,"title":"","content":"If you ask me \u201cBodhisattva predators\u201d are pretty clearly implied to be the werewolf equivalent of <i>archmages</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T12:59:28-07:00","id":1454543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454530#post1454530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ask me \u201cBodhisattva predators\u201d are pretty clearly implied to be the werewolf equivalent of <i>archmages</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While mechanically it does seem like it would be in a similar position, that of a sub-template, since archmages aren't really mages anymore, the comparison would be ironic because a Bodhisattva is literally someone who stays behind on the Earth to save others even though they can 'ascend' while archmages have basically said byebye to the Fallen World and run off to become symbols.<br /> <br /> We've heard some basic ideas about what some writers would like out of it but at the very least I think if we ever did end up getting them described they would be suitably different from archmages. Maybe more of a force within the world, but scaled up to deal with larger concepts. Impossible to really say until it's there though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T13:21:40-07:00","id":1454545,"title":"","content":"I think there's an obvious unfulfilled design space between basic playable splats and evolved non-playable splats, where you advance the template but not to the point where you're no longer playing the same game. Bodhisattva predators are, at least to me, by far the most suitable candidates for that due to a couple of reasons (besides the fact that maybe only one or two of the other games would be suitable for a similar concept): They are already established as an &quot;evolved splat&quot; within the setting, they still play on the same field as their former peers (as opposed to the Ascension War of archmages), and as established in this thread regular werewolves has a lack of vertical advancement, meaning vertically grown Bodhisattva predators would stand out (as they're supposed to do) with relatively small changes which would be much easier to balance within the context of the base game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T11:18:19-07:00","id":1454697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1454543#post1454543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While mechanically it does seem like it would be in a similar position, that of a sub-template, since archmages aren't really mages anymore, the comparison would be ironic because a Bodhisattva is literally someone who stays behind on the Earth to save others even though they can 'ascend' while archmages have basically said byebye to the Fallen World and run off to become symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire group of archmages called Bodhisattvas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T07:26:35-07:00","id":1466007,"title":"","content":"Did we have a Gift, Rite, Fetish, or some other power to \u2018form-lock\u2019 a werewolf into Hishu, Urhan, or any other form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T08:59:12-07:00","id":1466018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466007#post1466007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we have a Gift, Rite, Fetish, or some other power to \u2018form-lock\u2019 a werewolf into Hishu, Urhan, or any other form?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and it's unlikely that we'd see something like that published. Forcibly taking away one of a splat's core abilities is something not even high Arcana Mages can do.<br /> <br /> It might be interesting to play with something like that as a side-effect of an otherwise useful rite though. I'm always looking for balanced ways to give Werewolves access to agg healing, and being form-locked into Urhan for one night per point of agg healed could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also worth considering that the ease of changing forms or remaining in your current form is one of the ways Werewolf penalises your Harmony being out of balance. If you create a power that locks a Werewolf in one form it interferes with that, and low Harmony Werewolves might even see being locked in one form for a period as a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 10-31-2021, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T09:18:56-07:00","id":1466020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466007#post1466007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we have a Gift, Rite, Fetish, or some other power to \u2018form-lock\u2019 a werewolf into Hishu, Urhan, or any other form?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon Embed, Wave function collapse, can do something akin to this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T15:00:55-07:00","id":1466054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466018#post1466018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, and it's unlikely that we'd see something like that published. Forcibly taking away one of a splat's core abilities is something not even high Arcana Mages can do.<br /> <br /> It might be interesting to play with something like that as a side-effect of an otherwise useful rite though. I'm always looking for balanced ways to give Werewolves access to agg healing, and being form-locked into Urhan for one night per point of agg healed could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also worth considering that the ease of changing forms or remaining in your current form is one of the ways Werewolf penalises your Harmony being out of balance. If you create a power that locks a Werewolf in one form it interferes with that, and low Harmony Werewolves might even see being locked in one form for a period as a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, nothing such permanent \u2014 I was thinking of something for homebrewing the Gift of Man. Regardless, the Harmony aspect is a good idea\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466020#post1466020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Demon Embed, Wave function collapse, can do something akin to this</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, yeah, gonna go look over that one too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T00:02:45-07:00","id":1466097,"title":"","content":"There's a brief mention in The Pack about spirits of cold that can freeze werewolf shapeshifting/regeneration I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T00:27:11-07:00","id":1466098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466097#post1466097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a brief mention in The Pack about spirits of cold that can freeze werewolf shapeshifting/regeneration I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Gonna have to look that up too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T05:41:02-07:00","id":1466446,"title":"","content":"Do Werewolves regain Willpower from a full night's rest? The new contagion players guide specifies that generally if the book doesnt mention it after errata passes then that supernatural doesnt regen Willpower from sleeping. Mages do, vampires don't, demons depend, and the rest after those 3 are clearly specified in the core book. Werewolf is kind of the only odd man out. But the quote it says in Contagion chronicle seems to fit. &quot;\u201cIs sleeping truly restful for this creature? Does it help connect them to themself and affirm their identity, or does it erode it?\u201d&quot; Seems as though that would apply to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, looking through the book, it does seem that this book has significantly less Willpower use than other books. Also, I figured at the very minimum that Cahalith dreaming as they do would give Willpower and then I saw Dream Hunter. Exceptional Success says they gain Willpower when they wake, not that they gain an additional one when they wake. Hmmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 11-03-2021, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T06:05:11-07:00","id":1466451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466446#post1466446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Werewolves regain Willpower from a full night's rest? The new contagion players guide specifies that generally if the book doesnt mention it after errata passes then that supernatural doesnt regen Willpower from sleeping. Mages do, vampires don't, demons depend, and the rest after those 3 are clearly specified in the core book. Werewolf is kind of the only odd man out. But the quote it says in Contagion chronicle seems to fit. &quot;\u201cIs sleeping truly restful for this creature? Does it help connect them to themself and affirm their identity, or does it erode it?\u201d&quot; Seems as though that would apply to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, looking through the book, it does seem that this book has significantly less Willpower use than other books. Also, I figured at the very minimum that Cahalith dreaming as they do would give Willpower and then I saw Dream Hunter. Exceptional Success says they gain Willpower when they wake, not that they gain an additional one when they wake. Hmmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, werewolves regain Willpower from a full night's rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T04:17:59-07:00","id":1466633,"title":"","content":"What happens if a &quot;portable locus&quot; is transported into the Hisil.? Will it work as a &quot;gateway&quot; to return from the Hisil to the material world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs","name":"LukeZS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T09:31:09-07:00","id":1466662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LukeZS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466633#post1466633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a &quot;portable locus&quot; is transported into the Hisil.? Will it work as a &quot;gateway&quot; to return from the Hisil to the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't normally have portable loci, since they require a focal point that's likely to be drastically altered if it's moved around. So ruling on it may depend on whatever you have justifying the locus at your table, but you could use something like the Waystone Tell from the core for guidance. A Wolf-Blooded with Waystone isn't a locus (they are not a font of Essence) but they act like one &quot;for the purposes of spirits and others Reaching across to the opposite side.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:36:56-07:00","id":1466676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LukeZS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466633#post1466633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a &quot;portable locus&quot; is transported into the Hisil.? Will it work as a &quot;gateway&quot; to return from the Hisil to the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to understand the relationship between a locus and location is that the locus isn't just an object, but the relationship between this object and the place it's in.<br /> <br /> A silly ST I've played with once made an actual d20 into a Locus. The idea was that the d20 gathered the relevant essence through years of playing. The catch was that this dice was always used and kept in the room where the games happened. The locus is the dice, but the room gives it this context.<br /> <br /> If this dice was ever taken from there, it would be equivalent to breaking the Locus. It may still have a lot of coalesced essence for a time, but is no locus anymore, <i>maybe</i> if returned to that room within a reasonable time frame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T14:34:37-07:00","id":1466704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466662#post1466662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't normally have portable loci, since they require a focal point that's likely to be drastically altered if it's moved around. So ruling on it may depend on whatever you have justifying the locus at your table, but you could use something like the Waystone Tell from the core for guidance. A Wolf-Blooded with Waystone isn't a locus (they are not a font of Essence) but they act like one &quot;for the purposes of spirits and others Reaching across to the opposite side.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>People and things can also be Loci, both have showed up in different books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:49:43-07:00","id":1466712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466704#post1466704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People and things can also be Loci, both have showed up in different books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, specifically Lore of the Forsaken, and the Book of Spirits. In both cases it's explicitly not something that 'normally' happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lore of the Forsaken</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the physical representation of a locus is technically mobile, it can\u2019t be moved very far without damaging the locus\u2019 power. As a general rule, if the physical object at the heart of a locus is moved, the center of the pale doesn\u2019t move with it. If the object is moved, for instance, three feet to the left, the pale would shift its position slowly over the next few days. If the object is taken out of the pale entirely, the locus loses its power; any unharvested Essence remains until taken, but no more will be generated. The connection has been severed. <br /> This is the normal state of affairs. What if you decide to change that?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Book of Spirits</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In even more extraordinary situations, people can become loci. Those rare few who do end up as spiritual lynchpins connecting the realms are never the ones who enacted the emotion: it\u2019s never the murderer, in other words. No, that person is often the focal point of the emotion \u2014 the unrequited love, the intended target for assassination, the political figure earning a new investment of hate every second he remains alive. It\u2019s truly uncommon, and those who do become loci don\u2019t often remain that way for long. They become the targets for possession, or are killed for their presumed power or curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T01:28:20-07:00","id":1466754,"title":"","content":"Wolf-Blooded can be living, portable loci, it\u2019s not that uncommon. For <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1005_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1005\" data-vbnamecard=\"1005\">LukeZS</a>, the answer of what happens depends on the ST and the table. Options I can see:<br /> - The portable locus continues to work as a locus, just from the other side.<br /> - The locus never really \u2018crosses over\u2019 as it exists on both sides all the time. You\u2019re just moving its location.<br /> - It stops working as it\u2019s a one way gate and now it\u2019s trying to go the wrong way.<br /> - Something else that the ST comes up with.<br /> <br /> My preference is probably #2. The nature of a locus always places it on both sides, making it useful but also vulnerable regardless of which side fo the Gauntlet you\u2019re standing on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T03:03:35-07:00","id":1466756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1466712#post1466712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, specifically Lore of the Forsaken, and the Book of Spirits. In both cases it's explicitly not something that 'normally' happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another guy in the Dark Eras book for the Bowry Dogs in New York who counts as a loci.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The thing Bobby doesn\u2019t know is, he\u2019s a channel, a living<br /> locus. When Trevor died, it wasn\u2019t Bobby\u2019s fault, but Bobby<br /> was the gateway for the spirit that infected the dealer and<br /> killed Trevor. Bobby remains unaware of his strange place<br /> in the world\u2019s cosmology, but he continues to be a risk to<br /> those around him&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T16:17:45-08:00","id":1467298,"title":"","content":"If you're in Gauru when you cast(and fail) a Cmp+Res roll for Kuruth, do you skip Wasu-Im and go straight to Basu-Im or do you revert to Dalu or Urshul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27109-lawrence-kessler","name":"Lawrence Kessler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T17:47:44-08:00","id":1467308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lawrence Kessler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1467298#post1467298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're in Gauru when you cast(and fail) a Cmp+Res roll for Kuruth, do you skip Wasu-Im and go straight to Basu-Im or do you revert to Dalu or Urshul?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Normally, a werewolf who encounters a Kuruth trigger enters Wasu-Im. If he takes Gauru at any point, or falls into Kuruth while already in Gauru form (such as by taking Gauru outside of combat), he immediately enters Basu-Im.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:29:57-08:00","id":1468143,"title":"","content":"Is it stated in any 2e book that staying in the Underworld affects a werewolf like it did in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:39:46-08:00","id":1468162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1468143#post1468143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it stated in any 2e book that staying in the Underworld affects a werewolf like it did in 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>In The Pack it mentions that being in the Underworld fucks with a Werewolf's Harmony and makes them easily go into Kuruth, usually breaking a bunch of Laws in the process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T02:21:59-08:00","id":1468669,"title":"","content":"Am I missing something about the Lodge of Apollo and the Culte de la Raison? Like, the Lodge on it's own makes sense, but they have this mortal cult which is descended from the French Revolutionary Culte de la Raison... It seems kinda random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T06:43:18-08:00","id":1468681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1468669#post1468669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something about the Lodge of Apollo and the Culte de la Raison? Like, the Lodge on it's own makes sense, but they have this mortal cult which is descended from the French Revolutionary Culte de la Raison... It seems kinda random.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Nothing says they're descended from the French Revolutionary Culte de la Raison. It's a name they use for their human face. If you want they can be the source of the rumors about the centuries-gone organization in the first place, or they can never managed to have opened up in France and just pick the name because it sounds elite and respectable and not &quot;debauched and orgiastic.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T07:31:43-08:00","id":1468683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1468681#post1468681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Nothing says they're descended from the French Revolutionary Culte de la Raison.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mentioned very briefly in Dark Eras 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T07:40:08-08:00","id":1468684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1468683#post1468683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mentioned very briefly in Dark Eras 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mentioned that they corrupt one faction of it.<br /> <br /> P351, &quot;Meanwhile, the French Temple of Apollo abandons its traditional place as puppetmasters of the high aristocracy to carefully sink its claws into the Cult of Reason, hoping to appropriate one of its factions for its own purposes.&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to be just how they operate, co-opting existing human societies. Even in 1800 BC Egypt, p27, &quot;A strange cult to Apollo Lykeios emerges beside that of Arsino\u00eb in the city, its wolf-priests hungry to delve into Shedet\u2019s old secrets.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's where you're likely to find the rich or influential humans they want for their temples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-23-2021, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T08:45:04-08:00","id":1468689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1468684#post1468684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be just how they operate, co-opting existing human societies...It's where you're likely to find the rich or influential humans they want for their temples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would have been 200 years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in 1800 BC Egypt, p27, &quot;A strange cult to Apollo Lykeios emerges beside that of Arsino\u00eb in the city, its wolf-priests hungry to delve into Shedet\u2019s old secrets.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That makes more sense though. The write up of them in <i>The Pack</i> mentions an Omphalos Stone. So it makes sense to explain where they got that from. There's a <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">significance</span></span> to it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you read the same entry and note that their mortal cult has an odd name, a name it shares with a French Revolutionary state religion... Then read the Revolutionary Dark Era and find out that indeed the group originates there and... nothing really. There's no greater significance to it. You could leave the cult nameless and it wouldn't really alter the Lodge.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not unreasonable, it just seems odd from a writing perspective. Like the writers intended for this to go somewhere, but it just doesn't really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T05:35:10-08:00","id":1469307,"title":"","content":"When shapeshifting, do werewolves have to move through forms in succession (i.e. if I'm in Hishu and I want to be in Urshul, I need to go Dalu -&gt; Gauru -&gt; Urshul) or can they just go straight to the form they want?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T06:42:15-08:00","id":1469312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469307#post1469307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When shapeshifting, do werewolves have to move through forms in succession (i.e. if I'm in Hishu and I want to be in Urshul, I need to go Dalu -&gt; Gauru -&gt; Urshul) or can they just go straight to the form they want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Straight from one form to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T11:20:31-08:00","id":1469408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469312#post1469312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Straight from one form to the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> For a separate question, are there any rules for the point at which spirits can break out of a Fetish if 'fed' with Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T15:00:28-08:00","id":1469419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469408#post1469408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> For a separate question, are there any rules for the point at which spirits can break out of a Fetish if 'fed' with Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I read on it, fattening the psirit with essence won't break it out. Countering the Ritual or breaking the Fetish would do it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T15:46:19-08:00","id":1469428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469408#post1469408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> For a separate question, are there any rules for the point at which spirits can break out of a Fetish if 'fed' with Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Mage, of all places, had rules for that. Spirit 4 \u201cCraft Fetish\u201d \u2014 I don\u2019t have the pdf on hand right now, but I think it was something like feeding Essence to Rank or something. Rank\u2019s too low as a number though, so probably some other number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:40:55-08:00","id":1469445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469428#post1469428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Mage, of all places, had rules for that. Spirit 4 \u201cCraft Fetish\u201d \u2014 I don\u2019t have the pdf on hand right now, but I think it was something like feeding Essence to Rank or something. Rank\u2019s too low as a number though, so probably some other number.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Corpus, same as for waking a spirit from slumber, probably on account of how Craft Fetish binds a hibernating spirit and spends from its Essence pool to use some of its abilities (in contrast to rite-forged fetishes, which can get weirder).<br /> <br /> I vaguely remember there being rules for this in Lore of the Forsaken, but my library remains a mess and I have life stuff that needs handling at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T23:34:10-08:00","id":1469467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469408#post1469408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> For a separate question, are there any rules for the point at which spirits can break out of a Fetish if 'fed' with Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A fetish made in this way is a risk \u2014 feeding it Essence to fuel its powers will one day lead to the spirit breaking its ritual chains and escaping.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This way&quot; refers to spirits forced into fetishes rather than bargained with. Unfortunately there are no 2e rules for that. If Lore of the Forsaken has compatible rules, I'd just port them.<br /> I don't have access to that book right now to check, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, Mage 2e has rules for its kind of fetishes, but they work differently so they'll need some reworking.<br /> Notably, a Mage!Fetish uses Essence by default, and uses Essence stored in the fetish itself. The opposite of Werewolf!Fetishes where you spend your own Essence to power the fetish (unless you just make the roll instead). A Mage!Fetish gains Essence through Resonance Conditions like a slumbering spirit, or by being given Essence by a mage or another spirit. And, as mentioned, it breaks upon reaching Essence equal to or exceeding its Corpus.<br /> <br /> Since Werewolf!Fetishes don't have any means of getting rid of its Essence, I'd skip any natural Essence generation. Instead, the text directly refers to the Essence spent to forcing the spirit in the fetish to work, so I'd keep track of that and then have the spirit break out once it gains Essence equal to Corpus (alternatively, once its Essence pool is full).<br /> Of course, only spirits that are involuntarily trapped in fetishes would break out at that point. Those who were forced in the first place, those who've already fulfilled their agreements, and those who's seen the werewolf break their end of the agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T08:08:14-08:00","id":1469495,"title":"","content":"One of the intentions with making fetishes, and all their supplementary rules, in first edition was explicitly spelled out as not meaning to turn the game into a micromanager.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not meant to be a bookkeeping nightmare for players or the Storyteller; if it seems like one system too many, ignore it. The rules for honoring a fetish are just another way of reminding the players that the fetishes are in a manner of speaking alive, and that roleplaying and interacting with them does not end with the fetish creation rituals. </div> </div> </div>It's the kind of thing you should have as a looming threat, especially with as Tessie notes, unwilling spirit captives, and one that becomes a danger in a dramatically appropriate scene. But you and the players don't need to have spreadsheets tracking every use of Essence on every fetish just in case one hits an arbitrary bar and bursts out at a dramatically inappropriate moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2021, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T04:00:11-08:00","id":1469569,"title":"","content":"In the spirit (heh) of keeping it dramatically appropriate and avoiding bookkeeping, I'd design a system wherein the spirit may roll for breaking out. Keeping it exciting for the whole group by leaving it partly in the hands of fate.<br /> I'm inclined to say the dice pool should be based on the spirit, and be penalised or restricted by the user's honorary Rank compared to the spirit's own. Also, the user not being in combat or otherwise stressed should be to the spirit's disadvantage, as to not have it pop out during mundane circumstances.<br /> Alternatively, a fetish containing a non-willing spirit might have Conditions similar to those for equipment, representing failing bindings and/or resistance from the spirit.<br /> <br /> Completely theoretical systems atm, but I think those could be fun to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T12:30:15-08:00","id":1469585,"title":"","content":"Re-reading &quot;The Pure&quot; supplement from first edition, I have a question regarding the sidebar &quot;Perpetual irony&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a little outdated, as I think Pure are no longer a majority of werewolves, but my question has to do with them committing actions that leave their Harmony in tatters. Is this true, or a holdover from a system much different to 2nd edition Harmony? Would it be more likely the Pure struggle just as much as forsaken do, or that their actions still lead them to genuinely struggle more?<br /> <br /> Also concerning the Oath of the Moon/Urfarah, how do they uphold Purity considering the oath still truly functions as that of the moon? I do realize Purity is also gained through simply acting in a way a werewolf is expected to act, or more spiritual (having a mate, respecting prey), but I don't know if Purity is harder to gain votes for the Ivory claws considering they break the oath of not killing werewolves a fair bit much just like the blood talons<br /> <br /> Though, I admittedly struggle with Purity as it sometimes seems like Honor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T12:54:16-08:00","id":1469588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469585#post1469585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little outdated, as I think Pure are no longer a majority of werewolves,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brethren War meant that the Pure constituted a majority of American werewolves in the late 20th century due to lowered recruiting standards; the dynamics have always varied by time and place, and being a werewolf has never been a guarantee of longevity, especially when talking about specimens inducted into the tribes to pad the numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but my question has to do with them committing actions that leave their Harmony in tatters. Is this true, or a holdover from a system much different to 2nd edition Harmony? Would it be more likely the Pure struggle just as much as forsaken do, or that their actions still lead them to genuinely struggle more? </div> </div> </div>The more subjective nature of their tribal bans and the fact that their Sacred Hunts can be turned on their own, coupled with the higher average power of their pack totems and the power dynamic that entails, means that they're more likely to be forced into situations where their Harmony needs rebalancing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also concerning the Oath of the Moon/Urfarah, how do they uphold Purity considering the oath still truly functions as that of the moon? I do realize Purity is also gained through simply acting in a way a werewolf is expected to act, or more spiritual (having a mate, respecting prey), but I don't know if Purity is harder to gain votes for the Ivory claws considering they break the oath of not killing werewolves a fair bit much just like the blood talons<br /> <br /> Though, I admittedly struggle with Purity as it sometimes seems like Honor </div> </div> </div>Demonstrating Purity is done by living up to the legacy of the Great Hunter, the Warden Moon, and the Firstborn. Reconciling the apparent hypocrisy of killing werewolves who've killed other werewolves as devotion to the Oath is a matter of how things are weighted \u2014 it still risks unbalancing you, which is why most werewolves won't make it their first resort, but restitution for a breach of your vows is part of the societal framework werewolves inhabit, and the Pure are well-accustomed to paying penance for their indiscretions, even if those indiscretions weren't strictly their idea or were a Morton's Fork of one violation or a different one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T13:54:04-08:00","id":1469590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469588#post1469588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brethren War meant that the Pure constituted a majority of American werewolves in the late 20th century due to lowered recruiting standards; the dynamics have always varied by time and place, and being a werewolf has never been a guarantee of longevity, especially when talking about specimens inducted into the tribes to pad the numbers.<br /> <br /> The more subjective nature of their tribal bans and the fact that their Sacred Hunts can be turned on their own, coupled with the higher average power of their pack totems and the power dynamic that entails, means that they're more likely to be forced into situations where their Harmony needs rebalancing.<br /> <br /> Demonstrating Purity is done by living up to the legacy of the Great Hunter, the Warden Moon, and the Firstborn. Reconciling the apparent hypocrisy of killing werewolves who've killed other werewolves as devotion to the Oath is a matter of how things are weighted \u2014 it still risks unbalancing you, which is why most werewolves won't make it their first resort, but restitution for a breach of your vows is part of the societal framework werewolves inhabit, and the Pure are well-accustomed to paying penance for their indiscretions, even if those indiscretions weren't strictly their idea or were a Morton's Fork of one violation or a different one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok, thank you, that should be all for now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T06:02:21-08:00","id":1469723,"title":"","content":"In the Sacred Hunt right, it mentions 'bringing down' spirit prey allowing werewolves to extract Essence or Gifts from it. What exactly does 'bring down' mean in this context? Capture? Incapacitate? There seems to be an implication that it's not synonymous with discorporating a spirit, given <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T02:13:32-08:00","id":1469812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469723#post1469723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Sacred Hunt right, it mentions 'bringing down' spirit prey allowing werewolves to extract Essence or Gifts from it. What exactly does 'bring down' mean in this context? Capture? Incapacitate? There seems to be an implication that it's not synonymous with discorporating a spirit, given </div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally rule &quot;bringing it down&quot; as completion of the hunt. Maybe it has been grappled, pinned and had an attack that shows the danger or maybe it's just cornered and with no wat out.<br /> <br /> In these situations I've always seen it as the spirit bartering for their life. Either the spirit may offer or the werewolf may request something and instead of being destroyed a spirit may concede and chose to do what it must to survive.<br /> <br /> So yes, different from forcing a spirit to discorporate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T19:18:58-08:00","id":1469893,"title":"","content":"Are spirits that Claimed a person and managed to survive with separation more likely to become magath? I was reading book of spirits, and while it may give them an odd sort of humanness, it also may lead to odd interests, such as a death spirit being curious about trains after claiming a man who was a locomotive enthusiast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T20:01:13-08:00","id":1469895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469893#post1469893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spirits that Claimed a person and managed to survive with separation more likely to become magath? I was reading book of spirits, and while it may give them an odd sort of humanness, it also may lead to odd interests, such as a death spirit being curious about trains after claiming a man who was a locomotive enthusiast</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spirit, as with almost everything else. Eating yourself out of the natural order of the <i>umia</i> is largely a matter of how much latitude you've got for metaphorical interpretation \u2014 nature spirits can dip into tangential influences without shifting their core concept too far, and a death spirit that finds itself fixated on the railway system can probably link itself to train-based death easily enough, but the fallen member of the bicycle <i>ilthum</i> that Claims a champion swimmer during a triathlon is going to have a rough time reconciling a newfound desire to spend more time in the water.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that Book of Spirits is pretty much the only place this phenomenon is described, so its applicability is going to vary by game. Most <i>magath</i> are the result of bad bets or unfortunate eco-logistics moreso than the ephemera having a bit of leftover meat-suit stuck to it, because most spirits strong enough to Claim somebody are strong enough to drown out everything else about the person that doesn't suit their purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T20:41:37-08:00","id":1469896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469895#post1469895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the spirit, as with almost everything else. Eating yourself out of the natural order of the <i>umia</i> is largely a matter of how much latitude you've got for metaphorical interpretation \u2014 nature spirits can dip into tangential influences without shifting their core concept too far, and a death spirit that finds itself fixated on the railway system can probably link itself to train-based death easily enough, but the fallen member of the bicycle <i>ilthum</i> that Claims a champion swimmer during a triathlon is going to have a rough time reconciling a newfound desire to spend more time in the water.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that Book of Spirits is pretty much the only place this phenomenon is described, so its applicability is going to vary by game. Most <i>magath</i> are the result of bad bets or unfortunate eco-logistics moreso than the ephemera having a bit of leftover meat-suit stuck to it, because most spirits strong enough to Claim somebody are strong enough to drown out everything else about the person that doesn't suit their purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok, gotcha. Yeah I was reading it for to better flavor a hunter game for one of my players in an upcoming game (les mysteres), and I didn't even remember that aspect of claiming to be honest <br /> <br /> On the subject of magath, I'm also a bit confused. Is magath a whole new state of being for a spirit, or is it simply an umbrella term for those spirits that have consumed too many contradicting concepts to operate &quot;correctly&quot;? Like what makes a spirit so contradictory to the point other spirits want nothing to do with them, and what leads them to be powerful like Granny Stiches despite that setback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T01:39:30-08:00","id":1469898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469896#post1469896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of magath, I'm also a bit confused. Is magath a whole new state of being for a spirit, or is it simply an umbrella term for those spirits that have consumed too many contradicting concepts to operate &quot;correctly&quot;? Like what makes a spirit so contradictory to the point other spirits want nothing to do with them, and what leads them to be powerful like Granny Stiches despite that setback?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Magath</i> isn't a wholly different state of being. It's very common for spirits to predate upon unlike spirits and become somewhat hybridized. Werewolf 2e gives the example on pp. 179-180 of owl spirits consuming essence of night and the hunt, its resonance evolving and refining. Healthy spirits branch out into purviews that complement one another. Spirits become <i>magath</i> when they feed too much on prey of concepts that are so unrelated or contradictory that it distorts their perspective and leads to unhealthy behavior. <i>Magath</i> aren't just hybrids, but specifically <i>unhealthy</i> or <i>unviable</i> hybrids, likely to act in chaotic or self-destructive manners that will wreak collateral damage. Where that line lies, and when a spirit crosses it, is a judgment call that ultimately only matters when it concerns one of the Uratha enough to go hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T05:28:19-08:00","id":1469908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469895#post1469895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most spirits strong enough to Claim somebody are strong enough to drown out everything else about the person that doesn't suit their purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't read it as being so simple for the Spirit. To keep it fairly distinct from Possession I prefer the Claimed to really be an amalgamation with a lot of both. The spirit shouldn't start it without good reason.<br /> <br /> But that said, I entirely agree that even personality traits strange for the spirit after Claiming are unlikely to cause it to become a Magath. Even a Bicycle spirit that becomes enamored with water or airplanes do not have to <i>eat the Essence</i> of those things just because of it. Spending time around and otherwise engaging itself on those new hobbies from time to time is enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T14:32:10-08:00","id":1469957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469908#post1469908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't read it as being so simple for the Spirit. To keep it fairly distinct from Possession I prefer the Claimed to really be an amalgamation with a lot of both. The spirit shouldn't start it without good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, I get it, but on the other hand, Claimed are often characterized as the next step up from Ridden for a reason \u2014 putting a monomaniacal packet of ephemera in the passenger's seat with one hand on the steering wheel for long enough results primarily in a host who will do what the spirit wants, because following the urges from being Urged (which the Claimed starts out replicating the effects of) gives Beats (which translates to Willpower for NPCs).<br /> <br /> Most spirits have a Power + Finesse pool that will far outstrip a mortal's Resolve + Composure, and that's the contest to make you want to do what it wants while it merges into your soul. They're not unconscious while their body is being used, but the practical result is mostly the same, especially when repeat Possession is the long-term method of laying the groundwork for Claiming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T16:36:02-08:00","id":1469971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469957#post1469957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, I get it, but on the other hand, Claimed are often characterized as the next step up from Ridden for a reason \u2014 putting a monomaniacal packet of ephemera in the passenger's seat with one hand on the steering wheel for long enough results primarily in a host who will do what the spirit wants,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not questioning how much the spirit can force their actions, but how much their personality is subsumed. None of those actions by the spirit change that the Claimed will follow through them on its own way.<br /> <br /> More importantly, none of them changes that the Claimed is a personality far more complex than that of a spirit, and as any human being can have several thoughts and emotions going through their mind, an experience as alien and intense for the spirit as its monomania is for the host.<br /> <br /> During its existence as a Claimed, the combined entity will have plenty of time to experience things from the host's perspective and do stuff not directly related to absorbing Essence, like eating, sleeping, and doing the things that will eventually generate more Essence.<br /> <br /> After all, the whole purpose of the Claiming is for the spirit to achieve results it can't on its own, because they demand human action.<br /> <br /> That's my point. Claiming a human(ish) host is very intensive for the spirit as an experience. Total control over the result does not change that, because the result still isn't a spirit.<br /> <br /> On the instance of the spirit indeed drowning the human almost completely, the result will be too short-lived to matter, because the whole purpose of the ordeal is to access abilities the spirit don't have by itself, and shutting down the human will keep those abilities out of its reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T21:52:38-08:00","id":1470006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469971#post1469971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not questioning how much the spirit can force their actions, but how much their personality is subsumed. None of those actions by the spirit change that the Claimed will follow through them on its own way.<br /> <br /> More importantly, none of them changes that the Claimed is a personality far more complex than that of a spirit, and as any human being can have several thoughts and emotions going through their mind, an experience as alien and intense for the spirit as its monomania is for the host.<br /> <br /> During its existence as a Claimed, the combined entity will have plenty of time to experience things from the host's perspective and do stuff not directly related to absorbing Essence, like eating, sleeping, and doing the things that will eventually generate more Essence.<br /> <br /> After all, the whole purpose of the Claiming is for the spirit to achieve results it can't on its own, because they demand human action.<br /> <br /> That's my point. Claiming a human(ish) host is very intensive for the spirit as an experience. Total control over the result does not change that, because the result still isn't a spirit.<br /> <br /> On the instance of the spirit indeed drowning the human almost completely, the result will be too short-lived to matter, because the whole purpose of the ordeal is to access abilities the spirit don't have by itself, and shutting down the human will keep those abilities out of its reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, more recent material like Shunned by the Moon do not really show that (though if I were to storytell a game, which is soon for Hunter with Les Mysteres, i would) the Claiming is a synthesis of two beings rather than a warping possession. Saul McKay we don't even see what the host was like, and neither the spirit nor the human get much characterization as separate individuals in Jeremiah Fury. In fact the only one that really gives me an idea of this synthesis would be Surabel and Walter, and that's just a regular ridden.<br /> <br /> Not the fault of shunned, but what we do get tends to make it seem like a generic full on possession rather than a more complex spiritual process<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I'd like to say I think I am wrong concerning claiming being a sorta of synthesis. From my reading of the Predators supplement and werewolf 2nd edition, while it's still 2 beings becoming one, ultimately that one is, as Satchel pointed out, far more predisposed to the spirit's goals and needs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 12-10-2021, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T07:37:03-08:00","id":1471333,"title":"","content":"I have a vague memory from somewhere that's with a properly Resonant Rite that even humans can perform, any spirit can gain a bunch of Essence from a human sacrifice. Is this true or am I getting the Angel and Spirit rules mixed up? And if it's true, could someone help me find a page reference for it please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T15:06:48-08:00","id":1471457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1471333#post1471333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a vague memory from somewhere that's with a properly Resonant Rite that even humans can perform, any spirit can gain a bunch of Essence from a human sacrifice. Is this true or am I getting the Angel and Spirit rules mixed up? And if it's true, could someone help me find a page reference for it please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you thinking of Shadow Occultists from Shunned who gain Influences from cannibalism (among other means)? That's the only comparable effect that comes to my mind (unless you're thinking of something from 1e Forsaken, in which I am much less versed).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T11:02:30-08:00","id":1471547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469408#post1469408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a separate question, are there any rules for the point at which spirits can break out of a Fetish if 'fed' with Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I gradually get my library back in order, I can now confirm that while there aren't rules specifically for this in Lore of the Forsaken, there are some rules for similar malfunctions on page 139, under &quot;Autonomy&quot;; the pages after that include advice and optional systems for fetish maintenance and rebellious tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T22:45:06-08:00","id":1472407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1469896#post1469896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of magath, I'm also a bit confused. Is magath a whole new state of being for a spirit, or is it simply an umbrella term for those spirits that have consumed too many contradicting concepts to operate &quot;correctly&quot;? Like what makes a spirit so contradictory to the point other spirits want nothing to do with them, and what leads them to be powerful like Granny Stiches despite that setback?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just noticed I'd missed this question, so to summarize my reading of the material:<br /> <br /> A <i>magath</i> is a spirit that no longer has a place among the choirs of the spirit world. That can be nonsense hybrids of disparate elements, yes, but it's also spirits that you can easily describe a representative phenomenon for that nevertheless is not (or has ceased to be) part of the natural order, like Granny Stitches' exploratory fear or Irinam the Colossus's embodiment of Manifest Destiny or the Relict Men's representation of an extinct species.<br /> <br /> The operative distinction is that <i>magath</i> are bound to concepts that do not provide them with peers to serve as a social safety net (such as it is); The spirit of a species that has faded from all relevance needs to hitch its wagon to a close-enough relative or else forfeit its place in the choirs of nature spirits and take its chances with a diversified diet. Magath are often accordingly desperate to feed their hunger, hence the archetypal specimen that devours its way into a sort of omnivorous nightmare mishmash, but the Greater Jaggling of rivers/trains/work who manages to keep their disparate plates spinning and strongarm or manipulate their way into influence in spite of their pariah status is as much a <i>magath</i> as the swarm of snowflakes and bees that's confined to the eaves of a particular house up north for six months of the year.<br /> <br /> By analogy to a game that came out later in Chronicles history, magath are to spirits as exiles are to angels \u2014 if you're a spirit with roots in more than one thing and other spirits will have nothing to do with you if they can help it, you're a <i>magath,</i> regardless of how you got there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T07:37:11-08:00","id":1472435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1472407#post1472407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noticed I'd missed this question, so to summarize my reading of the material:<br /> <br /> A <i>magath</i> is a spirit that no longer has a place among the choirs of the spirit world. That can be nonsense hybrids of disparate elements, yes, but it's also spirits that you can easily describe a representative phenomenon for that nevertheless is not (or has ceased to be) part of the natural order, like Granny Stitches' exploratory fear or Irinam the Colossus's embodiment of Manifest Destiny or the Relict Men's representation of an extinct species.<br /> <br /> The operative distinction is that <i>magath</i> are bound to concepts that do not provide them with peers to serve as a social safety net (such as it is); The spirit of a species that has faded from all relevance needs to hitch its wagon to a close-enough relative or else forfeit its place in the choirs of nature spirits and take its chances with a diversified diet. Magath are often accordingly desperate to feed their hunger, hence the archetypal specimen that devours its way into a sort of omnivorous nightmare mishmash, but the Greater Jaggling of rivers/trains/work who manages to keep their disparate plates spinning and strongarm or manipulate their way into influence in spite of their pariah status is as much a <i>magath</i> as the swarm of snowflakes and bees that's confined to the eaves of a particular house up north for six months of the year.<br /> <br /> By analogy to a game that came out later in Chronicles history, magath are to spirits as exiles are to angels \u2014 if you're a spirit with roots in more than one thing and other spirits will have nothing to do with you if they can help it, you're a <i>magath,</i> regardless of how you got there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the explanation. I am still a little confused regarding what makes a spirit magath when at one point they weren't despite having the same concepts.<br /> <br /> As an example, I mean Granny Stiches. Unless I'm misunderstanding, hasn't she always kept those same concepts, until one day she just couldn't reconcile them and suddenly became a contradiction? Or am I reading it wrong and where at one point she was the concept of Exploration Into the Unknown, the fear she gained from the people ended up getting into her resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T17:16:21-08:00","id":1472480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1472435#post1472435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the explanation. I am still a little confused regarding what makes a spirit magath when at one point they weren't despite having the same concepts.<br /> <br /> As an example, I mean Granny Stiches. Unless I'm misunderstanding, hasn't she always kept those same concepts, until one day she just couldn't reconcile them and suddenly became a contradiction? Or am I reading it wrong and where at one point she was the concept of Exploration Into the Unknown, the fear she gained from the people ended up getting into her resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>She's sufficiently old that all we have to go off of are stories, but yes, the latter appears to be the more likely reading.<br /> <br /> Becoming <i>magath</i> isn't necessarily a thing that happens in a singular event \u2014 hence, again, Relict Men and other spirits who become hybrids through their failure to cleanly adapt to their environment \u2014 but spirits are the sum of their parts, and there's a tipping point where they go from being a member of the <i>umia</i> with some questionable feeding habits to being a thing to be shunned.<br /> <br /> Umbrella term aside, <i>magath</i> are singular creatures, and most of them aren't powerful enough to have that distinction through rising to the peak of a spirit court and organizing the world around their conceptual makeup. Most of them have warped themselves beyond recognition in the grand dance of wind and rain and cats and dogs and downtown traffic and road rage and vehicular homicide. They exist as a consequence of the spirit world being made of discrete spirits who stick around until they're destroyed instead of Venn diagrams of Essence and resonance that exist as abstract hypotheticals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T16:27:40-08:00","id":1472528,"title":"","content":"Question: Can Werewolves touch spirits in twilight without using any special gifts? Like I presume they can see spirits in twilight because they are half-spirit, but I wasn't sure about touching them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T17:02:52-08:00","id":1472534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1472528#post1472528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Can Werewolves touch spirits in twilight without using any special gifts? Like I presume they can see spirits in twilight because they are half-spirit, but I wasn't sure about touching them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ostensibly the sense of touch is included in spirit senses' ability to perceive spirits in the state of Twilight, and spirits count the unarmed attacks of werewolves of sufficiently high honorary Rank as a bane, but otherwise you need rites, fetishes, or other means of forcing a spirit out of the state of Twilight or interacting with spiritual Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T05:22:56-08:00","id":1472564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1472528#post1472528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Can Werewolves touch spirits in twilight without using any special gifts? Like I presume they can see spirits in twilight because they are half-spirit, but I wasn't sure about touching them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not usually. The ability to touch and strike ephemeral entities is the advantage imparted by the Bone Shadow version of the <i>Siskur-Dah.</i> Other than that there are Rites which can enable Werewolves to interact with Spirits in Twilight, or force Spirits to manifest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T00:36:19-08:00","id":1473239,"title":"","content":"What would even be happening in an Ocean Hisil? Does it just police itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T03:54:19-08:00","id":1473244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473239#post1473239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would even be happening in an Ocean Hisil? Does it just police itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that there are very few humans in the ocean it's just not much of an issue. There aren't many opportunities for spirits to cross the gauntlet in the ocean, and even if they could, they can't do very much once they're here.<br /> <br /> Having said that, you can use the ocean as a great source of horror of the unknown in a Werewolf game. Uratha might be the ultimate predators on land, but they are truly out of their element in the water. The ocean can easily spew forth never before seen <i>shartha</i> or even weirder creatures, which Uratha have no context for, and even worse, imagine what would happen if an Idigam ended up in coastal waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T04:46:41-08:00","id":1473245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473239#post1473239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would even be happening in an Ocean Hisil? Does it just police itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Subnautica?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T09:14:28-08:00","id":1473268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473244#post1473244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that there are very few humans in the ocean it's just not much of an issue. There aren't many opportunities for spirits to cross the gauntlet in the ocean, and even if they could, they can't do very much once they're here.<br /> <br /> Having said that, you can use the ocean as a great source of horror of the unknown in a Werewolf game. Uratha might be the ultimate predators on land, but they are truly out of their element in the water. The ocean can easily spew forth never before seen <i>shartha</i> or even weirder creatures, which Uratha have no context for, and even worse, imagine what would happen if an Idigam ended up in coastal waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I don't mean that in the context of spirits affecting humans. I mean the spirits themselves, whatever can live down there, no one really can control what they're doing? I guess a big scary pit of just &quot;unknown&quot; stuff breeding and going nuts somewhere in the depths, unknown to various normal spirits swimming closer to the surface is a good enough estimate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T09:34:44-08:00","id":1473271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473268#post1473268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but I don't mean that in the context of spirits affecting humans. I mean the spirits themselves, whatever can live down there, no one really can control what they're doing? I guess a big scary pit of just &quot;unknown&quot; stuff breeding and going nuts somewhere in the depths, unknown to various normal spirits swimming closer to the surface is a good enough estimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in 2020, Chris Allen wrote up a bit about the ocean in Forsaken, including a delectable Gift of the Sea. Some of the more interesting bits include that sometimes spirit magic will suddenly fail while out on the water, and that drowning is a conscious act that sea-spirits perform, so if you're sneaky and/or a good bargainer, you can get pretty far down in the Shadow-ocean without any specialized equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T21:07:16-08:00","id":1473312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473239#post1473239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would even be happening in an Ocean Hisil? Does it just police itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, yes.<br /> <br /> And if you stop to think about it, land spirits mostly do the same, There simply aren't enough Uratha to police spirits in every place spirits are very active. And the Shadow has its own ecology, which means that despite the complex and unbalanced dynamics of its day to day life, it tends to be more or less self-correcting in the long run (although not necessarily in the longest run).<br /> <br /> There's also the question of why would only Father Wolf's get be capable of acting as spirit police. There are many ways in which a spirit may come to act in such a capacity, as Father Wolf once did, be it to keep a desired <i>status quo </i>or just follow their own nature. You may have shark, dolphin and squid spirits acting in a similar fashion, for example, indeed you could have different dept in the sea having their own &quot;policing forces&quot;.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing to account for is that <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/icb/article/50/4/675/650584\" target=\"_blank\">the oceans have a far lower diversity in species than land, with far greater populations for those species</a>, i.e. it has more biomass as a whole, but with far more uniformity <i>in comparison</i>. The effects of this on the <i>Hisil</i> may result in less need for policing to begin with, and/or different strategies for doing so.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's the question of just how much all this &quot;policing&quot; stuff is actually relevant away from human populations. Humans increase the diversity of the <i>Hisil</i> with all the things we produce, not because we generate more emotional spirits (animals do that well enough), but because we build things that may have their own spirits. Also, accept it or not, werewolves come from a human understanding about things and have human worries about the state of the world around them, even when those worries are not direct toward humans. Do the animals, plants and stones of the physical world really care about all that &quot;policing&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you decide your setting has intelligent life unknown to mankind secretly living in the oceans, they may create the context for a similar phenomenon to the <i>Uratha</i> happening there. If not, then it needs less of this sort of interference in a general sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T07:43:08-08:00","id":1473330,"title":"","content":"The ecology of the ocean hisil is likely getting up-ended by the constant stream of pollution and trash poured into it, being used disrespectfully as entertainment and shipping routes, not to mention global warming melting glaciers and causing the oceans to rise.<br /> <br /> It's just not something that has as much of an obvious way to be dealt with by werewolves. But given the sea level is literally rising you can see the result of this conflict in the gurihal.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, Chronicles has avoided doing much with the sea. I understand there was at least <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Blood-Dimmed_Tides\" target=\"_blank\">one focused book about the supernatural aspects of the oceans in old World of Darkness</a>, but most of the new stuff is pretty landlocked. So you are free to represent these conflicts however you wish (or don't). But you do have hints of things like through the lamprey host, the brineborn, the Kraken, and the Deep. None of these things are striving for a 'balance' however and all seem pretty gung-ho about drowning the world or at least making it more hospitable for them to the detriment of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2022, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T17:55:59-08:00","id":1473368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473239#post1473239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would even be happening in an Ocean Hisil? Does it just police itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest explanation is a combination of the following:<br /> <br /> 1. There's basically nothing on the books to suggest that there <i>isn't </i>some bonkers nonsense happening in the Shadow far out to sea.<br /> <br /> 2. There is an ample supply of water and fish to feed the relevant spirits, and elementals have been repeatedly characterized as old, inertial, and dismissive of biological life, with spirits tied to bodies of water having especially powerful varieties of hunger; the ocean's Shadow could well be just as prone to frantic fugitives as the land's, but since most of the spirits there are drawing from the symbolic portfolios of things that can't leave the water, the ecosystems mostly keep to themselves whether they want to or not, barring the intrusion of humanity or freak disaster or both.<br /> <br /> 3. The way the urban Shadow works translates well to the aquatic Shadow: it's not the centers of regions that you need to worry about, it's the borders, which feeds into so much of aquatic Shadow-adjacent creatures being coastal phenomena. Werewolves happen to have a much easier time coming across such phenomena, and the big fish deeper down are sufficiently entrenched that they can enforce their agendas on anyone who can't hop the fence for the beaches.<br /> <br /> The long and short of it is that, ironically, Jules Verne got it wrong \u2014 to live within the heart of the ocean is not to be independent; the sea <i>does</i> belong to tyrants, to such a degree that the abyssal and pelagic spirit courts can be reasonably compared to the Naturae of the Anima Mundi, who basically <i>are</i> the component members of their ecosystems. This is what happens when you live in a place with Big Old Deep Fish and Ancient Things With Influence: Their Whole Environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T06:26:51-08:00","id":1473399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473330#post1473330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ecology of the ocean hisil is likely getting up-ended by the constant stream of pollution and trash poured into it, being used disrespectfully as entertainment and shipping routes, not to mention global warming melting glaciers and causing the oceans to rise.<br /> <br /> It's just not something that has as much of an obvious way to be dealt with by werewolves. But given the sea level is literally rising you can see the result of this conflict in the gurihal.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, Chronicles has avoided doing much with the sea. I understand there was at least <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Blood-Dimmed_Tides\" target=\"_blank\">one focused book about the supernatural aspects of the oceans in old World of Darkness</a>, but most of the new stuff is pretty landlocked. So you are free to represent these conflicts however you wish (or don't). But you do have hints of things like through the lamprey host, the brineborn, the Kraken, and the Deep. None of these things are striving for a 'balance' however and all seem pretty gung-ho about drowning the world or at least making it more hospitable for them to the detriment of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is sheer scope.<br /> <br /> I find it especially ridiculous to think that ocean entities are focused on taking over the land by drowning it. The ocean is already more than 70% of Earth's surface, and most of it isn't that crowded to need even more, this is a land problem, not a water one. Water entities, both real and fictional, also have far more vertical mobility even without leaving their actual favored dept, so the oceans are actually very low in population density compared to land.<br /> <br /> Pollution and trash are certainly a big thing happening there. If there's a big conflict among modern oceanic spirit courts and whatever pass as Uratha down there, it certainly has recent trash formations and temperature changes among their main reasons. But big large scale changes in the ocean aren't really such a new thing, so from a long scale perspective it isn't a reason to think the ocean needs the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Also because, again, most of those phenomena are far more drastic above the ocean than on them. Water warming is a big problem, but weather isn't so much. While we face violent storms, droughts, typhoons and the like due to climate change, those phenomena have very little direct impact in oceanic life, and less of an impact the deeper you get. It is quite the opposite: a 1\u00baC change in oceanic temperature that has medium to low impact on oceanic life (it does have some, and may deeply affect some species depending on where it happens) is more than enough to generate a surge in catastrophic weather above water.<br /> <br /> Ships and entertainment are meaningless in this regard. Our impact through direct presence is, fortunately, extremely more limited in the ocean than it is in landlocked wild environments. We can cause havoc on coastal areas, but from a oceanic perspective they're less of a thing than they are from a continental perspective. Our biggest ship can barely be noticed passing just a dozen meters below surface, even a submarine is a lonely spec in the middle of a realm where IRL whales and giant squids are already a thing. Are they something the individuals present will noticed? Yes. But hardly will they cause lasting, meaningful changes to the system itself.<br /> <br /> On the big scheme of things, the oceans simply exist in a scale too larger than ourselves, and too separated from what happens above waters. Even the problems we did caused only took the scale they did because the ocean itself wrestled the mess completely out of our control, like how ocean currents form islands of plastic with an efficiency we can only dream about and can do nothing to stop. That's the great challenge in portraying it in fiction, how utterly indifferent it is to whatever happens outside it and hard for <i><b>meaningful</b></i> exploration it is for us. An alien realm where most facts of life as we know don't apply and vastness define almost everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T12:52:41-08:00","id":1473420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473399#post1473399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it especially ridiculous to think that ocean entities are focused on taking over the land by drowning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine. But it's what at least some of the aforementioned entities are interested in. You don't have to use them but it's what they're about and while you may stand firmly against it if someone's asking about ocean-oriented monsters in the game then I see no reason why we should hide or deny their existence.<br /> <br /> War Against the Pure, p205, &quot;Unfortunately, the apocalypse cult has taken to trying to usher in the consuming wave by appeasing Mother Ocean with violent sacrifices. Animals, humans, maybe even a Forsaken. It\u2019s not without effect. The water elementals that lurk along the shore are growing potent with the sacrifices that are ostensibly in their honor. The sea grows wine-dark with bloody resonance, and threatens to truly rise up and come crashing down upon the shore.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pollution and trash are certainly a big thing happening there. If there's a big conflict among modern oceanic spirit courts and whatever pass as Uratha down there, it certainly has recent trash formations and temperature changes among their main reasons. But big large scale changes in the ocean aren't really such a new thing, so from a long scale perspective it isn't a reason to think the ocean needs the Uratha. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves, as a whole and at the table, aren't an omnipresent force. What is happening in the Pacific Ocean may not have a direct impact to a pack on Miami Beach. But if things are happening in all the oceans, a game about the pack on Miami Beach can deal with how it impacts them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also because, again, most of those phenomena are far more drastic above the ocean than on them. Water warming is a big problem, but weather isn't so much. While we face violent storms, droughts, typhoons and the like due to climate change, those phenomena have very little direct impact in oceanic life, and less of an impact the deeper you get. It is quite the opposite: a 1\u00baC change in oceanic temperature that has medium to low impact on oceanic life (it does have some, and may deeply affect some species depending on where it happens) is more than enough to generate a surge in catastrophic weather above water. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has referenced climate change as a source of problems (and ways spirits war among each other) since its inclusion in one of the first books, Chicago.<br /> <br /> Chicago, p273, referring to a particularly harsh winter exacerbated by climate change. &quot;Elementals of cold and water gain sudden power during this time, more so than in a normal winter storm. Manyof them begin to assume dominance over lesser spirits, consuming them or forcing them to perform tasks for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's Winter. The book points out that to most Urtha the cold is &quot;more a nuisance than anything.&quot; But in the Hisil it's a mess, with most sources of Essence (loci and eating other spirits) tainted with cold to the point that spirits of all sorts are coated with ice. And that, in turn, spurs a brood of fire-spirits to decide to sacrifice the entire city of Chicago in an inferno to fight back against the spirits of Winter.<br /> <br /> And the trend continues throughout the books to the most recent one, Shunned by the Moon, where Jeremiah Fury the storm-claimed fueled by climate change represents a different aspect of the same conflict. The whole game is about how issues, even seemingly innocuous ones, can cause massive repercussions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ships and entertainment are meaningless in this regard. Our impact through direct presence is, fortunately, extremely more limited in the ocean than it is in landlocked wild environments. We can cause havoc on coastal areas, but from a oceanic perspective they're less of a thing than they are from a continental perspective. Our biggest ship can barely be noticed passing just a dozen meters below surface, even a submarine is a lonely spec in the middle of a realm where IRL whales and giant squids are already a thing. Are they something the individuals present will noticed? Yes. But hardly will they cause lasting, meaningful changes to the system itself. </div> </div> </div>All it takes is one magath to throw an entire swath of the spiritual ecosystem out of balance. Not only have we been using ships to cruise across the ocean and dump trash and chemicals in for over a century now, but we've actively had wars there. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sunken_nuclear_submarines\" target=\"_blank\">We've developed and lost nuclear submarines.</a> Even before modern times, ships were used to raid and plunder and bring war, riches, plague, religion, slavery, and entire civilizations to other lands and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zong_massacre\" target=\"_blank\">occasionally just throwing them overboard.</a> <br /> <br /> And that's just one part of it, just 'the water.'<br /> <br /> The other part is the sea life. Ignoring the pollution and 'islands' of garbage, we've still managed to destroy huge populations of fish and sea mammals. <a href=\"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/ocean-fish-numbers-cut-in-half-since-1970/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Ocean fish numbers cut in half since 1970.&quot;</a> <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2003/05/15/world/commercial-fleets-reduced-big-fish-by-90-study-says.html#:~:text=In%20just%2050%20years%2C%20the,a%20new%20study%20has%20found.\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Commercial Fleets Reduced Big Fish by 90%, Study Says.&quot;</a> This has huge impacts that affect countries in real life, even leading to combat between nations. I'm not sure why it wouldn't have any impact in a world where there's an added, spiritual component.<br /> <br /> I mean a lot of these things if you don't merely have justification for disruptive spirits or other monsters, you have good reasons for heavily infectious Wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2022, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T18:07:53-08:00","id":1473435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All it takes is one magath to throw an entire swath of the spiritual ecosystem out of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>To pull some threads together:<br /> <br /> <i>Magath</i> are roundly shunned by the rest of the spirit world and there is a whole lot of ocean to ostracize them into, especially towards the top, bottom, and/or edges.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, that means most problem actors that aren't promptly shoved to the seafloor and buried or pulled to the surface and picked apart by omnivores get to be somebody else's problem when they wash ashore, but an environment dominated by ancient calms and currents and case studies in why-the-Shadow's-skies-are-so-overcast-but-like-a-fish-version is generally more robust than an environment where basic buoyancy doesn't give you a third movement axis.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marches#Noun\" target=\"_blank\">As it has ever been</a>, the areas that tend to need the most attention from non-spirit intercessors like werewolves are the liminal spaces.<br /> <br /> (Sea demons are a different matter, but suffice it to be said that the likes of the Maeltinet and the Immundi are going to have better luck with their missions working on things that aren't the sum of their parts without a regular influx of new material \u2014 and that mostly means humans and/or more foreign substances intruding into the oceans, which they'll mostly need to head to port to secure without going a long way out of their way to find or manufacture atrocity in the middle of the vasty deep.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T10:30:47-08:00","id":1473477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine. But it's what at least some of the aforementioned entities are interested in. You don't have to use them but it's what they're about and while you may stand firmly against it if someone's asking about ocean-oriented monsters in the game then I see no reason why we should hide or deny their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not denying their existence, I'm stating my opinion on them as an idea for the setting.<br /> <br /> There are circumstances that may justify such an attitude, though, but those do so by adding a new layer to the matter, and this layer is what really would drive some ocean spirit to try and take the land.<br /> <br /> And one thing that must be clear is that <b><i>Ocean</i></b> isn't <b><i>Sea</i></b>. When talking about Ocean Hisil I'm focusing on the big seas and their deep waters, and on the coastal seas only in a limited capacity as they are liminal areas. That is key here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Against the Pure, p205, &quot;Unfortunately, the apocalypse cult has taken to trying to usher in the consuming wave by appeasing Mother Ocean with violent sacrifices. Animals, humans, maybe even a Forsaken. It\u2019s not without effect. The water elementals that lurk along the shore are growing potent with the sacrifices that are ostensibly in their honor. The sea grows wine-dark with bloody resonance, and threatens to truly rise up and come crashing down upon the shore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That exemplifies the adding layer thing. Those spirits aren't interested in drowning the land because of itself, they're answering to the actions of a cult that sources essence to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves, as a whole and at the table, aren't an omnipresent force. What is happening in the Pacific Ocean may not have a direct impact to a pack on Miami Beach. But if things are happening in all the oceans, a game about the pack on Miami Beach can deal with how it impacts them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but that was not the question presented. The question was if the ocean Hisil took care of itself or what, and I said it certainly has no need for the Uratha or land-based &quot;spirit police&quot;.<br /> <br /> That the ocean will affect the land is a given, actually. Indeed, one of the interesting aspects of the ocean to explore in a game is just how much it can affect the land while being itself unaffected in return. Althou you do have a point about some shallow waters ecosystems that I'll have to address.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf has referenced climate change as a source of problems (and ways spirits war among each other) since its inclusion in one of the first books, Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Climate change is an interesting and powerful example of the above, thanks to the laws of thermodynamics.<br /> <br /> Most of it will never affect the oceans in the same way it affects the land. Indeed, the average rising in temperature is practically the only aspect of climate change that affects it, hence the old term Global Warming. Otherwise, the oceanic waters have weak response to localized and temporary changes in temperature, and practically no response to winds, precipitation or electrical currents, even shallow water life can dive deep enough to ignore those when they occur. So no big impact in the oceanic Hisil except exclusively by the general raise in temperature.<br /> <br /> But on the other direction? The ocean is the <b>single main climate engine of the planet</b>. While mountains, rivers and forests play an important role, it is just without comparison. Due to the sheer mass of the ocean, any slight variation in its temperature packs a huge, almost apocalyptic amount of energy, and air reacts to that energy far more promptly. Less than 1\u00baC is enough to make a hurricane with more energy than the entire electrical output of the state of New York in a year.<br /> <br /> For the ocean that's basically a hiccup.<br /> <br /> This is the theme I was pointing to, as it relates to the question as stated. The Uratha probably <i><b>should</b></i> worry about the ocean if they have any knowledge of how climate works, but from the ocean's perspective things are far different and the Uratha aren't needed. The waters do have their problems and events, but nothing they can't handle on their own, and if they ever need someone else to handle it, it will have to be someone specialized, not some insignificant land meddler.<br /> <br /> And while there are things happening in the land that may affect it, those things generally only do so at the end of global-spanning chains of events that make local-based packs effectively incapable of doing shit about it. The focal intervention the Uratha are used to has little impact on the ocean unless under extremely specific circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All it takes is one magath to throw an entire swath of the spiritual ecosystem out of balance. Not only have we been using ships to cruise across the ocean and dump trash and chemicals in for over a century now, but we've actively had wars there. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sunken_nuclear_submarines\" target=\"_blank\">We've developed and lost nuclear submarines.</a> Even before modern times, ships were used to raid and plunder and bring war, riches, plague, religion, slavery, and entire civilizations to other lands and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zong_massacre\" target=\"_blank\">occasionally just throwing them overboard.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, space and movement in the ocean is very different from what it is in land.<br /> <br /> Lets say we have a factory spilling pollution and that generates a Magath. If this happens at a small forest, the spiritual ecosystem affected is fairly limited and the Magath will probably at first want to stay at the forest. A small forest likely don't have a lot of powerful spirits to deal with it, or if it has they send it whining to the outskirts of the forest in a short time. One way or another, the Magath end up in a region of limited space (if big to our standards), and with few enemies with the power to actually destroy it in short order, so it can feast and grow.<br /> <br /> On the oceans there's always more ocean. While the waters aren't actually uniform, its ecosystems spam far larger areas and have a far more robust use of three dimensional space. Here, every place the Magath is expelled from, it can just wander to another not-so-terribly-worse one without any contact with the previous. And it gets moving on and on until it finally pisses of enough one of the continent-spanning elementals to whom Rank 5 spirits are an afterthought.<br /> <br /> Either they die because the ocean at large isn't forgiving, or they end up in some spot where, for all practical purposes, they're a land problem.<br /> <br /> Not to say that after some time the ecosystem can actually absorb some of those new elements into it. We have to ditch the WtA idea of pollution = Wyrm Taint. A lost nuclear submarine will produce Magath? On a sense, yes at first, as the local Court probably won't be accepting of the newcomer spirits, but those spirits will be able to form a society of their own as the submarine remains there, and with time the local court will probably reach some understanding with them, at least as far as spirits do.<br /> <br /> Dumping thrash and chemicals affects far more the coastal areas than the oceans at large, oil spills are the worst but they also affect coastal life disproportionately. The oceans aren't completely immune to those things, but they still work it on the scale factor, either it is out of proportion or the ocean shrugs it with an ease the coast and land can't. Our wars do very little to the ocean, and the spirits they spawned there will be locked and isolated to either perish or reach an accord with the local courts, and that applies to everything else we did overseas.<br /> <br /> Picture it: our entire existence over the seas barely covered a fraction of the surface of a realm that is insurmountably bigger than said surface. Yes, you can have the very point where a ship sunk or a battle occurred be a thing in the Hisil, but is that thing seen as anything resembling a significant problem for the Ocean Hisil it can't solve by itself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473420#post1473420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other part is the sea life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a sticking point of my argument, though, and you're right: while our direct impact is generally limited, our predations over some lifeforms are another matter, at least to some extent.<br /> <br /> It is important to contextualize this first, though, but I admit I won't close the question of our impacts on those species.<br /> <br /> Our impact on oceanic life is mostly related to big fish and mammals. Those creatures live mostly in the uppermost level of the oceanic surface, rarely reaching the 100 m mark that goes actually deeper than most continental platforms and is only halfway through to the first change in photic zone. The average depth of the ocean is 3.7 Km, so we're talking about a 1/37th fraction of oceanic volume in those areas.<br /> <br /> Even at those depths, those species act far more as consumers for the oceanic biomass transferring it to their predators in land, coast and air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:50:16-08:00","id":1473493,"title":"","content":"Even if you ignore the impact of humanity on the ocean, humanity itself doesn't decide what happens in the Hisil, even if the area is big. You've made your stance clear, I think I made mine.<br /> <br /> Anyways, if anyone wants an example of werewolves policing the seas, you can base it off the Lodge of the Maelstrom from Lodges: the Faithful, as it's their thing.<br /> <br /> Lodges: the Faithful, p66 &quot;Even if the Uratha had double their numbers, they couldn\u2019t be everywhere they might be needed. The entire world casts a Shadow, even the parts of the world that are inhospitable to werewolves. And strange things can be born away from humans and wolves alike, things that might follow a faint scent or sound to civilization. The Lodge of the Maelstrom knows this all too well, for lodge members have taken it upon themselves to watch the coastlines for signs of horrors that are born at sea. In an ideal world, those things that spawned down in the depths would remain in their lightless environment and never venture forth to warm air and dry land. But the world is not ideal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Their section has a sidebar explaining the kinds of sea-borne horrors they may face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-28-2022, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T18:57:17-08:00","id":1473513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1473477#post1473477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either they die because the ocean at large isn't forgiving, or they end up in some spot where, for all practical purposes, they're a land problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat that they can also get subjected to the perennial favorite Shadow story-hook of &quot;bind it in slumber and leave it somewhere it won't soon wake up,&quot; which effectively puts off the problem for another day; getting rid of it permanently from a spiritual perspective would otherwise entail eating it and hoping you can spread it thin enough that it doesn't just come back with a new name or three by getting to somebody's heart through their stomach.<br /> <br /> The Lodge of the Maelstrom mostly addresses the sea from a coastal perspective, but the element of its origin story that goes &quot;a golden belt with weird runes on it turned out to be a link in the chains holding something beneath the ocean&quot; does present the reminder that magical ocean-realms in this setting have a well-established history of serving as prisons for stuff too nasty to kill, whether that's Mother Ocean or the Ocean of Fragments or the Abyss as reflected in the Ocean Oroboros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:07:43-08:00","id":1474197,"title":"","content":"Is there an official ruling on what to use in place of Rank when determining the effects of a non-spirit using an Influence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:22:04-08:00","id":1474198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1474197#post1474197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an official ruling on what to use in place of Rank when determining the effects of a non-spirit using an Influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's own CoW rules. If it doesn't have CoW rules or have rules that doesn't cover this situation, default to the Supernatural Potency trait + Influence. If they don't have a Supernatural Potency trait, they're shit out of luck and roll pure Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T11:37:51-08:00","id":1474213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1474198#post1474198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's own CoW rules. If it doesn't have CoW rules or have rules that doesn't cover this situation, default to the Supernatural Potency trait + Influence. If they don't have a Supernatural Potency trait, they're shit out of luck and roll pure Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant for determining the direct mechanical results of an Influence effect, e.g. Strengthen to add Health or Structure equal to Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T13:44:57-08:00","id":1474226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1474213#post1474213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant for determining the direct mechanical results of an Influence effect, e.g. Strengthen to add Health or Structure equal to Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>No official ruling iirc.<br /> <br /> A quick patch would be; their Renown-derived honorary Rank for werewolves, their spirit half\u2019s former Rank for Claimed, and half of Supernatural Potency trait (rounded up) for other non-ephemeral supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:43:14-08:00","id":1474993,"title":"","content":"Can Hosts be subject to Manifestations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T11:59:08-08:00","id":1474999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1474993#post1474993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Hosts be subject to Manifestations?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, can they be Urged, Possessed, Claimed, etc? There's no blanket immunity, but getting the necessary Conditions to support the Manifestation might be tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T13:11:39-07:00","id":1477113,"title":"","content":"Is there any way Uratha can find the location of a locus beyond stepping in it? <br /> I briefly played 1st Ed WtF long ago, and have agreed to run 2nd Ed; one of my players only played WtA,so there is unlearning and relearning going on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T14:12:58-07:00","id":1477119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1477113#post1477113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way Uratha can find the location of a locus beyond stepping in it?<br /> I briefly played 1st Ed WtF long ago, and have agreed to run 2nd Ed; one of my players only played WtA,so there is unlearning and relearning going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can infer it by the sudden clarity of the Shadow when attempting to use their spirit senses across the Gauntlet, or by following the trails of spirits to the proverbial watering hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T00:27:07-07:00","id":1479114,"title":"","content":"The character sheet lists Armor of 1/1 while in Gauru form but I couldn't find any mention of this in the rules. Do you gain an armor rating in Gauru natively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T02:05:19-07:00","id":1479121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479114#post1479114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character sheet lists Armor of 1/1 while in Gauru form but I couldn't find any mention of this in the rules. Do you gain an armor rating in Gauru natively?</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition Gauru form gave 1/1 Armor, but this was removed in Second Edition (Gauru really don't need it anymore) and it isn't listed on the character sheet in the Second Edition core book. You can still have this armor in Second Edition if you want by buying the Fortified Form merit, and this can also be purchased for forms other than Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T21:55:48-07:00","id":1479276,"title":"","content":"Is there a max limit on the size of a pack? It seems like with humans being able to be pack it might be able to get quite large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T04:48:29-07:00","id":1479289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479276#post1479276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a max limit on the size of a pack? It seems like with humans being able to be pack it might be able to get quite large.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not, though gang politics, occult intrigue, differing priorities, and werewolf tempers being what they are means that as your pack gets larger the probably of betrayal, sabotage, infighting, splinter groups, and other forms of internally- or externally-sourced division approaches 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T13:29:04-07:00","id":1479366,"title":"","content":"Question raised after an irraka ambush: <br /> <br /> If a character is successfully surprised by an opponent , he can't take even reflexive actions right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T13:46:34-07:00","id":1479368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479366#post1479366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character is successfully surprised by an opponent , he can't take even reflexive actions right ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't track at all, because most forms of contested resistance are reflexive and being denied your Defense is the main way ambush gives attacks against you the advantage. What reflexive actions prompted this question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T14:01:39-07:00","id":1479370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479368#post1479368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That wouldn't track at all, because most forms of contested resistance are reflexive and being denied your Defense is the main way ambush gives attacks against you the advantage. What reflexive actions prompted this question?</div> </div> </div> </div>The facet Berserker's Might, in order to avoid some damages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T14:41:03-07:00","id":1479373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479370#post1479370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The facet Berserker's Might, in order to avoid some damages.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be used. Reflexive Actions can be used, a lot of example Reflexive actions make perfectly sense to be used while surprised, some are specifically meant for such kind of situation, and as a defensive reflex there's no reason for Berserker's Might to be an exception.<br /> <br /> Reflexive Actions are that, reflexes. While they involve the <i>player</i>'s conscious decision to use, for the character they're that, a reflex, something that just happens unless they consciously suppress it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T16:06:42-07:00","id":1479378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479366#post1479366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question raised after an irraka ambush: <br /> If a character is successfully surprised by an opponent , he can't take even reflexive actions right ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Reflexive actions are still actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T20:48:35-07:00","id":1479390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479378#post1479378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. Reflexive actions are still actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions can specifically be taken at any time and don't take your turn in combat, and Berserker's Might in particular is one of the types of Facets werewolves specifically use instinctively in Basu-Im; its use is already throttled by being limited to once per turn (and, to a lesser extent, costing Essence and having a form requirement).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T22:09:44-07:00","id":1479395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479390#post1479390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reflexive actions can specifically be taken at any time and don't take your turn in combat, and Berserker's Might in particular is one of the types of Facets werewolves specifically use instinctively in Basu-Im; its use is already throttled by being limited to once per turn (and, to a lesser extent, costing Essence and having a form requirement).</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions are still actions. They\u2019re defined as actions in the \u2018Actions\u2019 section, and Surprise specifically says \u201cAny character who fails the roll cannot take an action in the first turn of combat\u201d. Not \u201cinstant action\u201d, not \u201cextended action\u201d, not even \u201can action except reflexive actions\u201d, literally \u2018cannot take an action\u2019.<br /> <br /> Surprise isn\u2019t \u2018some guy jumped me and I had a moment to react\u2019, it\u2019s \u2018the first I knew I was under attack was when their claws were already buried deep in my back\u2019. Your chance to notice and do something was the Wits + Composure roll, if you fail that, you don\u2019t know anything\u2019s happening until you\u2019re either injured or the attacker misses and in doing so alerts you to their presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-24-2022, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T22:15:10-07:00","id":1479396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479378#post1479378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. Reflexive actions are still actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. We solved it without giving a chance to take any action to the ambushed, even reflexive. Because the book says &quot;the character loses his action&quot; . But we still had some doubts since the description of a reflexive action is something like &quot; natural as breathing&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was a carnage btw. Irraka with eviscerate and slaughterer went for the kill, swallowing flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T23:01:14-07:00","id":1479401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479395#post1479395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reflexive actions are still actions. They\u2019re defined as actions in the \u2018Actions\u2019 section, and Surprise specifically says \u201cAny character who fails the roll cannot take an action in the first turn of combat\u201d. Not \u201cinstant action\u201d, not \u201cextended action\u201d, not even \u201can action except reflexive actions\u201d, literally \u2018cannot take an action\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will repeat: This reading results in nonsensical outcomes like &quot;if you ambush someone you can automatically succeed at any supernatural power targeting them that is resolved as a contested action, because reflexive actions are actions and therefore they can't take the reflexive action of contesting the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the same page where reflexive actions are defined, the definition of contested actions says that a contested action takes up the action of the person initiating the action, then contrasts this with the person resisting the action by specifying that the resistance is a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> For all practical purposes in this system, unless stated otherwise, a reflexive action is not an action for the purposes of mechanics that reference &quot;actions;&quot; Deviant models Involuntary Variations activating themselves as reflexive actions and can involve triggers that don't require the character to be conscious. Mage models activating Mage Armor as a reflexive action and specifies that the forms of that Attainment that increase Defense apply against surprise attacks. Changeling has a Contract that activates reflexively if the character who knows it dies and has the Glamour to pay its cost. The Poisoned Tilt models counteracting its damage from turn to turn as a reflexive action and then defines intending to &quot;act&quot; as &quot;[taking] a non-reflexive action.&quot; The Stamina roll to stay conscious with a full track of damage is a reflexive action. Rolling Dexterity + Athletics to reduce fall damage is a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> I'm not super eager to rehash an argument from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/761792-how-does-regeneration-work-in-2nd?p=810154#post810154\">six years ago</a> with a slightly different coat of paint over whether or not a werewolf ambushed in Dalu, Urshul, or Gauru with a point of Essence in their system ought not be able to reduce the damage from a single attack by their Glory or undo a single Tilt, particularly since on this subject there is no ambiguity save the semantic. &quot;Reflexive actions are actions&quot; is not a sound argument in the face of substantial evidence that, in the sense under discussion, <i>they aren't</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T23:27:32-07:00","id":1479402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479373#post1479373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be used. Reflexive Actions can be used, a lot of example Reflexive actions make perfectly sense to be used while surprised, some are specifically meant for such kind of situation, and as a defensive reflex there's no reason for Berserker's Might to be an exception.<br /> <br /> Reflexive Actions are that, reflexes. While they involve the <i>player</i>'s conscious decision to use, for the character they're that, a reflex, something that just happens unless they consciously suppress it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the book specifiy that reflexive actions are actions. And a successful ambush doesn't allow you to take action. But at the same time, reflexive are described as breathing and similar. I am very confused about it. This leads me to other doubts. Like, if I'm ambushed while in urhan I can spend essence to interrupt his action. This would be uhm...weird. Basically irraka would be almost useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 04-24-2022, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T02:17:19-07:00","id":1479409,"title":"","content":"1.) As thoroughly explained, treating reflexive actions in this case as actions is wholly nonsensical.<br /> <br /> 2.) Whenever the books refer to just an &quot;action&quot;, 99% of the time they mean instant actions.<br /> <br /> 3.) The surprise rules makes a character both lose their action <i>and</i> Defense. Applying Defense is a reflexive action, so that part would be redundant. If it's meant to be a reminder it would be worded as &quot;meaning the character doesn't get to apply her Defense&quot;.<br /> <br /> By a very literal reading, you wouldn't get to do any reflexive actions, but that's ignoring hos the language is generally used in the books and what's reasonable for the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479402#post1479402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, if I'm ambushed while in urhan I can spend essence to interrupt his action. This would be uhm...weird. Basically irraka would be almost useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. Chase Down is an ability that takes an instant action to activate but can be used outside your turn in the initiative. If you can't take instant actions, you can't interrupt others.<br /> <br /> Also, Rote Action on attack rolls that you can't apply Defense for is fucking insane, even if you still have access to reflexive damage mitigation. In the first turn of combat, the Irraka is by far a more efficient killer than any Rahu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2022, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T02:23:05-07:00","id":1479410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479409#post1479409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) As thoroughly explained, treating reflexive actions in this case as actions is wholly nonsensical.<br /> <br /> 2.) Whenever the books refer to just an &amp;quot;action&amp;quot;, 99% of the time they mean instant actions.<br /> <br /> 3.) The surprise rules makes a character both lose their action <i>and</i> Defense. Applying Defense is a reflexive action, so that part would be redundant. If it's meant to be a reminder it would be worded as &amp;quot;meaning the character doesn't get to apply her Defense&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> By a very literal reading, you wouldn't get to do any reflexive actions, but that's ignoring hos the language is generally used in the books and what's reasonable for the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, you can't. Chase Down is an ability that takes an instant action to activate but can be used outside your turn in the initiative. If you can't take instant actions, you can't interrupt others.<br /> <br /> Also, Rote Action on attack rolls that you can't apply Defense for is fucking insane, even if you still have access to reflexive damage mitigation. In the first turn of combat, the Irraka is by far a more efficient killer than any Rahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes my bad , I confused with the reflexive expenditure of essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T10:28:18-07:00","id":1479430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479402#post1479402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the book specifiy that reflexive actions are actions. And a successful ambush doesn't allow you to take action. But at the same time, reflexive are described as breathing and similar. I am very confused about it. This leads me to other doubts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as many rule books, CoD has a problem with language here and there.<br /> <br /> If you take it literally by RAW, as you theoretically should be able to, you'll have a paradox as many other rules and systems work based on the assumption that Reflexive Actions are an exception. This is not just a matter of RAI vs RAW, it is RAW conflicting with itself here and there. Basically a character wouldn't roll anything when denied actions, neither would do anything that can be defined as an action, even if it is something as breathing or just be on a continuity of their movement.<br /> <br /> So this is a case where we fix RAW by using context to figure the probable meaning of the words. Because while rules should be precise and strict, they're conveyed through a language that isn't neither. It is not so much a problem with the rules and more a problem with the choice of words where it is really tricky. RAI is applied as a secondary tool, from the analysis of the competing rules, and this makes it clear that most of the time Reflexive Actions were thought as not being impeded by surprise, and surprise is probably trying to prohibit <i>conscious</i> actions while avoiding to state an action type because the author of the line couldn't yet know if Instant would be the only source of relevant conscious actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T11:06:20-07:00","id":1479432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479430#post1479430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, as many rule books, CoD has a problem with language here and there.<br /> <br /> If you take it literally by RAW, as you theoretically should be able to, you'll have a paradox as many other rules and systems work based on the assumption that Reflexive Actions are an exception. This is not just a matter of RAI vs RAW, it is RAW conflicting with itself here and there. Basically a character wouldn't roll anything when denied actions, neither would do anything that can be defined as an action, even if it is something as breathing or just be on a continuity of their movement.<br /> <br /> So this is a case where we fix RAW by using context to figure the probable meaning of the words. Because while rules should be precise and strict, they're conveyed through a language that isn't neither. It is not so much a problem with the rules and more a problem with the choice of words where it is really tricky. RAI is applied as a secondary tool, from the analysis of the competing rules, and this makes it clear that most of the time Reflexive Actions were thought as not being impeded by surprise, and surprise is probably trying to prohibit <i>conscious</i> actions while avoiding to state an action type because the author of the line couldn't yet know if Instant would be the only source of relevant conscious actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Hit and Run ? It's reflexive but I clearly read you must be &quot;engaged in combat&quot;. Also, allowing it during an ambush would mean being immune to any kind of stealth attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T12:34:36-07:00","id":1479435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479432#post1479432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Hit and Run ? It's reflexive but I clearly read you must be &quot;engaged in combat&quot;. Also, allowing it during an ambush would mean being immune to any kind of stealth attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hit and Run interrupts an action before it's taken in a way that <i>does</i> require awareness \u2014 it's an interruption-based power, not one of the Facets that automatically activates for free in the right circumstances, and of the analogous powers in other gamelines, Celerity (Vampire) explicitly can't be used to interrupt actions you're not aware of, Acceleration (Mage) and Alacrity (Deviant) model interruption as choosing when to take your within the Initiative order (when being ambushed deprives you of your ability to take an action), Unravel the Tapestry (Changeling) works post-hoc as short-term time-travel, and Shadow of Time Tier 3's Ba 5 bonus (Mummy) is an added effect on a power that already makes you immune to surprise and ambush anyway by letting you see the immediate future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T12:43:15-07:00","id":1479437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479435#post1479435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit and Run interrupts an action before it's taken in a way that <i>does</i> require awareness \u2014 it's an interruption-based power, not one of the Facets that automatically activates for free in the right circumstances, and of the analogous powers in other gamelines, Celerity (Vampire) explicitly can't be used to interrupt actions you're not aware of, Acceleration (Mage) and Alacrity (Deviant) model interruption as choosing when to take your within the Initiative order (when being ambushed deprives you of your ability to take an action), Unravel the Tapestry (Changeling) works post-hoc as short-term time-travel, and Shadow of Time Tier 3's Ba 5 bonus (Mummy) is an added effect on a power that already makes you immune to surprise and ambush anyway by letting you see the immediate future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks that makes sense. It seems stupid but the lenguage barrier for me is not easy to overcome when it's a matter of rules. Words can be confusing and sometimes I must ask or interpretate some rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T12:48:50-07:00","id":1479438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1479432#post1479432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Hit and Run ? It's reflexive but I clearly read you must be &quot;engaged in combat&quot;. Also, allowing it during an ambush would mean being immune to any kind of stealth attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Engaged in combat&quot; is their (poorly written) way of saying that you can't use it in response to an ambush, as an exception to what would be expected. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> exemplified very well, we can verify effects similar in both purpose and mechanics (if not entirely equal) to confirm that they presume such action being possible as baseline rule, then make the power specifically an exception. So we do have enough data to confidently interpret an unclear phrase as meaning this is also such a case, the rule would have it that you can, but the specific power is an exception, so you can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T19:48:30-07:00","id":1481971,"title":"","content":"Fetish Weapon Creation:<br /> <br /> By using the rules in the book we can create fetish weapon from rank 1 to 5. However, I have a hard time picturing the general power I should allow them to be. <br /> <br /> At 4, it is said that the weapon may get increased damage. Alright, but by how much ? +1 is not the same as +3. +1 with Rote, or 9 again or 8 again is not the same also...<br /> At 5, it is even more powerfull than that. It does make sens, but to me, the rules are loose and seems a little imprecise. I know its by design, but I need help figuring out, lets say a sword, with ehanced damage. How much more damage would it deliver than usual ? Would it be all the time, for the scene, during a single turn of activation ? Need help here. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:33:07-07:00","id":1481976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1481971#post1481971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetish Weapon Creation:<br /> <br /> By using the rules in the book we can create fetish weapon from rank 1 to 5. However, I have a hard time picturing the general power I should allow them to be.<br /> <br /> At 4, it is said that the weapon may get increased damage. Alright, but by how much ? +1 is not the same as +3. +1 with Rote, or 9 again or 8 again is not the same also...</div> </div> </div> </div>The sample four-dot fetish weapon has as its effect the permanent infliction of a Personal Tilt on the first enemy struck by it in the scene in which it is activated. The sample three-dot fetish weapon allows its wielder to strike beings in Twilight and identify their nature. The example powers for a two-dot fetish include increasing the equipment bonus of functionally-a-modern-technological-item by the fetish's rating<br /> <br /> Every level of weapon damage is functionally equivalent to a bonus success on the attack roll, most weapons below Size 3 don't have a Damage rating higher than 2. Permanently increasing the Damage of one of the natural weapons of one of your forms by +1 is a four-dot Merit, and most forms' default Damage rating for those weapons is +1 or +0, the Killing Form being a particularly notable exception (+2 lethal, can establish grapples in addition to causing damage, and gets an Initiative <i>bonus</i> where most weapons apply an Initiative penalty commensurate with their Damage rating).<br /> <br /> An extra +2 Damage for the scene upon activation is plenty, is what what I'm getting at with all this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At 5, it is even more powerfull than that. It does make sens, but to me, the rules are loose and seems a little imprecise. I know its by design, but I need help figuring out, lets say a sword, with ehanced damage. How much more damage would it deliver than usual ? Would it be all the time, for the scene, during a single turn of activation ? Need help here. Thanks. </div> </div> </div>A fetish weapon rated at five dots is going to have something more substantial going for it than a heightened Damage rating \u2014 again, &quot;remove a limb on a successful hit&quot; is the effect of the sample four-dot fetish weapon and &quot;weapon that can strike ephemera&quot; is a three-dot fetish. Weapons that also destroy Willpower or Essence are given as an example. If one were to go as plain as possible, a five-dot fetish weapon with a respectable Damage rating in aggravated harm would work just fine, as might an completely ignoring Armor and/or Defense, or a successful hit immediately causing the target to start bleeding out.<br /> <br /> Given that an average mortal has 7 Health and the most lopsided conceptual <i>Dihir</i> can still have 20 Corpus and 6 Defense, going much further than Damage 5 \u2014 the damage rating of a chainsaw, so unwieldy that it inflicts a -6 Initiative penalty to use in combat, needs both hands to use effectively, and requires above-average Strength to use without penalty \u2014 is probably excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T21:26:32-07:00","id":1481981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1481976#post1481976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An extra +2 Damage for the scene upon activation is plenty, is what what I'm getting at with all this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add to that that a passive, fixed, permanent bonus is the simplest benefit, but also the easiest way to end up with something that breaks the game because you put too much into that decision of deciding the number of the bonus.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb the method the game chose works better: define a condition where the weapon does something, and then what it does, so it isn't working all the time and it does something relevant but different from just more damage. Partly because it makes for more interesting fetishes, partly because it gives you a lot more control over how useful or useless the weapon will be in the game, easier both to figure out it before hand and to adjust things later if you miss the spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T15:23:14-07:00","id":1482293,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> One player exposed me to something new.<br /> <br /> As a werewolf, he took a speciality in brawling, with his claws, and he also took a specific merit wich is called Favored form.at 1 dot. Doing, so, he must choose a favored form, wich is gauru, and a specific skill, wich is brawl. When using that specific skill, in that specific form, 3 successes, becomes a exceptional succes. It is great, but how is that applicable in actual combat ?<br /> <br /> I mean, he cannot get 5 successes on a hit, everytime he deliver 3 or more successes right ? How would you choose to make that work out in your game ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T16:37:30-07:00","id":1482306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1482293#post1482293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> <br /> One player exposed me to something new.<br /> <br /> As a werewolf, he took a speciality in brawling, with his claws, and he also took a specific merit wich is called Favored form.at 1 dot. Doing, so, he must choose a favored form, wich is gauru, and a specific skill, wich is brawl. When using that specific skill, in that specific form, 3 successes, becomes a exceptional succes. It is great, but how is that applicable in actual combat ?<br /> <br /> I mean, he cannot get 5 successes on a hit, everytime he deliver 3 or more successes right ? How would you choose to make that work out in your game ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl in combat isn't like a normal roll, so you don't normally get anything on an exceptional success except more damage. There are excerptions to this though, for example in a grapple you can choose two manoeuvres on an exceptional success, which for this character would occur on 3 rather than 5 successes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T17:33:55-07:00","id":1482309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1482293#post1482293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, he cannot get 5 successes on a hit, everytime he deliver 3 or more successes right ? How would you choose to make that work out in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of specific exceptional success mechanics for a roll, the normal outcome is that you take a beneficial Condition (or pass it onto a packmate or another character, when appropriate). Attack rolls are explicitly resolved like any other action.<br /> <br /> Often that Condition will be Inspired, which in this context means that the character can use a Brawl roll with 3 or more successes in Gauru form to take a Condition that lets him recover a point of Willpower and make another roll count as an exceptional success on three successes \u2014 maybe he saves it for a later Intimidation roll to get intruders to stay off the pack's turf, maybe he spends it on an Occult roll to piece something together about the spirit he just discorporated, maybe he uses it to boost a tracking roll to hunt down the Beshilu that just burst into a swarm of rats got away, maybe he just uses it on another Brawl roll to effectively spend a point of Willpower and immediately get it back.<br /> <br /> The character has an additional incentive to use his Brawl Skill in Gauru form, with the cost of this being that one or more of his forms that aren't the Killing Form are less physically and/or mentally potent and he can't apply the Merit's bonuses to any form that isn't Gauru. This particular arrangement will probably mean either going for the kill a lot more than a character with a different Favored Form setup or else not getting the benefit as often as a less strictly metered form would allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T18:36:31-07:00","id":1483197,"title":"","content":"Are Tribe-specific Rites restricted socially or spiritually? For instance, is Veil restricted to Iron Masters because the Tribe refuses to teach the Rite to outsiders, or because it's powered by members' spiritual bond to Red Wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T19:07:45-07:00","id":1483944,"title":"","content":"The Merit Favored form... Is each dot cumulative ?<br /> Do we have to take first dot, before taking the second one, and so on, like let's say, Merit martial arts ?<br /> Can we take the merit multiple time ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","user":"Warriorshaman","date":". 06-18-2022, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T18:05:38-07:00","id":1485432,"title":"","content":"I was looking at how spirits are explained in the <i>Mage </i>core book, but a few things are unclear, so I wanted to ask for a bit more information from <i>Werewolf</i>, which goes into more detail<br /> <br /> Can Strengthen Influences be used to heal, such as a horse spirit healing one ? What kind of damage can they heal and does it go back to normal once the duration end ? Can it end non-permanent conditions ?<br /> <br /> Do spirits heal Corpus at the same speed as humans ?<br /> <br /> Can Numina like Blast and Telekinesis be used in Twilight ?<br /> <br /> How do spirits of vehicles determine their speed ?<br /> <br /> In addition, I wanted to clarify rules for skill checks. My understanding is that:<br /> <br /> * Spirits only avoid unskilled penalties within their theme<br /> * They roll Rank + Attribute for checks within their domain, Attribute + Attribute for everything else<br /> <br /> So if that is the case, wouldn't it mean that their dice pool is smaller for their concept related actions ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for the help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-30-2022, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T18:20:41-07:00","id":1485433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1485432#post1485432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, I wanted to clarify rules for skill checks. My understanding is that:<br /> <br /> * Spirits only avoid unskilled penalties within their theme<br /> * They roll Rank + Attribute for checks within their domain, Attribute + Attribute for everything else<br /> <br /> So if that is the case, wouldn't it mean that their dice pool is smaller for their concept related actions ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They roll Attribute + Attribute for rolls that would be Attribute tasks (p159) for non-ephemeral beings, for rolls to use their supernatural powers, to fight, and for anything else that specifies such a dicepool.<br /> <br /> Rolls that would be Attribute + Skill roll Attribute alone, or Attribute + Rank if appropriate to the spirit's theme. A spirit with no connection to the act of research (normally Intelligence + Academics) rolls Power alone, and probably with a -3 unSkilled penalty to boot, while it would roll Power or Finesse + Rank to do something appropriate to its type, like scrounge for food as a scavenger (Wits + Survival normally, Finesse + Rank for a spirit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T18:45:52-07:00","id":1485434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1485433#post1485433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. They roll Attribute + Attribute for rolls that would be Attribute tasks (p159) for non-ephemeral beings, for rolls to use their supernatural powers, to fight, and for anything else that specifies such a dicepool.<br /> <br /> Rolls that would be Attribute + Skill roll Attribute alone, or Attribute + Rank if appropriate to the spirit's theme. A spirit with no connection to the act of research (normally Intelligence + Academics) rolls Power alone, and probably with a -3 unSkilled penalty to boot, while it would roll Power or Finesse + Rank to do something appropriate to its type, like scrounge for food as a scavenger (Wits + Survival normally, Finesse + Rank for a spirit).</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot more sense, thank you. Can spirits see across the Gauntlet without aid ? How do they normally know what is on the other side ? Since space does not have a direct correspondence on the other side of the Gauntlet, I imagine being precise would otherwise be though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T19:05:30-07:00","id":1485435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1485434#post1485434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes a lot more sense, thank you. Can spirits see across the Gauntlet without aid ? How do they normally know what is on the other side ? Since space does not have a direct correspondence on the other side of the Gauntlet, I imagine being precise would otherwise be though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space mostly <i>does</i> have a direct correspondence across the Gauntlet \u2014 the Shadow is fairly unique among the Invisible Realms in how closely it conforms to Earthly geography, aberrant landmarks and pocket realms notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> Spirits can't usually see across the Gauntlet without specific abilities to do so, but they can detect instances of Resonant phenomena and those are by definition things they can use their Influences on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T05:45:04-07:00","id":1485491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1483944#post1483944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit Favored form... Is each dot cumulative ?<br /> Do we have to take first dot, before taking the second one, and so on, like let's say, Merit martial arts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can we take the merit multiple time ? </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T14:14:59-07:00","id":1486068,"title":"","content":"Is there a way for werewolves to bring other non-werewolves across the Gauntlet with them? Running a crossover chronicle and I it's coming up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T15:49:48-07:00","id":1486074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1486068#post1486068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for werewolves to bring other non-werewolves across the Gauntlet with them? Running a crossover chronicle and I it's coming up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there's any specific rule to cover this, but I've always thought that Werewolves should be able to bring people across the gauntlet if they want to by making physical contact while crossing over.<br /> <br /> However doing so is probably a sin towards spirit (just as helping a spirit cross is a sin towards flesh)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T18:34:11-07:00","id":1486080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1486068#post1486068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for werewolves to bring other non-werewolves across the Gauntlet with them? Running a crossover chronicle and I it's coming up.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC there are some ways to bring Pack members across the Gauntlet, at least, and a Pack can have non-Werewolf members no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T17:25:08-07:00","id":1488510,"title":"","content":"When spirits are recovering after Discorporating from aggravated damage, do they fully regrow lost limbs ? Do any scars remain, or a similar proof that they were defeated by a pack ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:08:43-07:00","id":1488513,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say werewolf attacks leave ugly scars on spirits. It fits thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:43:16-07:00","id":1488519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488510#post1488510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When spirits are recovering after Discorporating from aggravated damage, do they fully regrow lost limbs ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they've got limbs and have survived somehow encountering a full track of aggravated damage without running away, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do any scars remain, or a similar proof that they were defeated by a pack ? </div> </div> </div>That pack having gotten whatever they Discorporated it for and the relevant damage to its holdings is the scar, barring any specific narrative or mechanical consequences attached to that event.<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage is harder to recover from by the fact that it strips Essence from a spirit's holdings and therefore adds days to the recovery countdown. That's it. It's not like with vampires, where healing the damage takes extra effort and the alternative is The End.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T10:45:26-07:00","id":1488582,"title":"","content":"Are idigam Void-spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T12:15:42-07:00","id":1488593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488582#post1488582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are idigam Void-spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very clearly not, given that idigam do not do the things that void spirits do and being banished to the Moon from Earth or avoiding that fate is the main distinction between the two types of idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T14:57:03-07:00","id":1488599,"title":"","content":"I ask because planetary angels (I forget the actual First Tongue Name) aren\u2019t actually <i>from</i> those planets, instead being very bizarre Helions of that planet\u2019s light reflecting back to Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:25:22-07:00","id":1488614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488599#post1488599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask because planetary angels (I forget the actual First Tongue Name) aren\u2019t actually <i>from</i> those planets, instead being very bizarre Helions of that planet\u2019s light reflecting back to Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Mulhithim</i> are &quot;not from those planets&quot; in the same sense that Lunes aren't from the Moon \u2014 they're still <i>from</i> Mercury/Venus/Mars/Jupiter/Saturn/etc, they're just not spirits of planetary features from those places. Shunned by the Moon wouldn't use the phrase &quot;true progenitor&quot; opposite Helios in its description of their nature if they were just weird Helions.<br /> <br /> Which still doesn't provide much of a precedent for considering the idigam void spirits, because the Moon-Banished and the Earthbound are spiritual beings without a fixed essential nature, whereas void spirits are spirits <i>of nothing</i>, i.e. the emptiness of the cold darkness between the stars. The idigam may have Dread Powers that mess with the Shadow around them, but they're clearly not completely alien to the terrestrial Hisil the way the <i>gasuhathim</i> and their kin are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T07:59:00-07:00","id":1488820,"title":"","content":"Are Pangaeans from the Supernal Realms? You know, \u201cideas and truths and symbols made flesh\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:48:16-07:00","id":1488840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488820#post1488820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Pangaeans from the Supernal Realms? You know, \u201cideas and truths and symbols made flesh\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Dark eras, it seems that they are former Supernal gods dethroned by the Exarch s ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:49:59-07:00","id":1488841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488840#post1488840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From Dark eras, it seems that they are former Supernal gods dethroned by the Exarch s ascension</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the idea I got, too. Cast down and trying to remake their kingdom with Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:42:34-07:00","id":1488884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488820#post1488820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Pangaeans from the Supernal Realms? You know, \u201cideas and truths and symbols made flesh\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems too simplistic for an answer. I got the feeling that they were naturally Awakened as a sign of their immanent divinity, rather than a direct Supernal origin.<br /> <br /> The gods just Are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:52:50-07:00","id":1488885,"title":"","content":"Remember, they <i>were</i> in a Mage/Werewolf crossover Dark Era. I like them as the Old Gods, cast down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:56:49-07:00","id":1488887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488820#post1488820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Pangaeans from the Supernal Realms? You know, \u201cideas and truths and symbols made flesh\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're from the Border Marches \u2014 &quot;primeval divinities born in this rift between worlds.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T15:02:45-07:00","id":1488889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1488885#post1488885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, they <i>were</i> in a Mage/Werewolf crossover Dark Era. I like them as the Old Gods, cast down.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, sure you can have that as the behind-the-scenes secret truth at your table; people are hardly going to challenge that. It\u2019s just that I don\u2019t think there\u2019s much in-universe reason to claim so. Like, its not like some Sleepers becoming Awakened or miraculously crafting Artifacts meant that those Sleepers are sealed Old Gods (which, on hindsight, IS a cool story hook <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:48:24-07:00","id":1488953,"title":"","content":"They are highly tied to a specific realm (or two, if you also consider the Astral), uses Essence instead of Mana, and doesn't share any similarities to actually confirmed Supernal beings that have been cast down: the Bound.<br /> <br /> The two points for their Supernal origins are their conceptual nature (which is very likely tied to their spiritual nature rather than them being Supernal symbols) and their ability to use the Arcana. The latter doesn't have an explanation that I'm aware of, but it only implies a connection rather than origin. As mentioned, the Awakened also aren't Supernal entities just because they happen to have access to the Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T12:33:09-07:00","id":1488998,"title":"","content":"Ok! Thanks, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T04:25:09-07:00","id":1489215,"title":"","content":"Ivory Claw's blood gift, purity facet:<br /> <br /> BLEED (PURIT Y)<br /> The heart of the hunt is the spilling of blood, a crimson<br /> blossom marking the predator\u2019s triumph.<br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Brawl + Purity versus Stamina +<br /> Primal Urge<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: 1 day<br /> <u><i><b>The Uratha can use this Facet when inflicting damage<br /> while in the Gauru, Urshul or Urhan forms.</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <br /> Does it means that I add also purity to my strike ? Or I must do two different rolls?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T04:39:45-07:00","id":1489216,"title":"","content":"First you assume one of the named forms and make an attack. Roll the attack normally. If the attack hits and inflicts damage, then you can spend Essence and roll the Bleed dice pool to activate the Facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T04:43:38-07:00","id":1489219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1489216#post1489216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First you assume one of the named forms and make an attack. Roll the attack normally. If the attack hits and inflicts damage, then you can spend Essence and roll the Bleed dice pool to activate the Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. This doesn't make great sense but I suppose it would be broken otherwise. It's very unclear from the book, or maybe it's just my poor understanding of english","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T06:45:06-07:00","id":1489225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1489216#post1489216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First you assume one of the named forms and make an attack. Roll the attack normally. If the attack hits and inflicts damage, then you can spend Essence and roll the Bleed dice pool to activate the Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>also, can this gift be cumulative ?<br /> What can stop an uratha to strike at the liver and makes it bleed and then strike to another organ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T18:16:28-07:00","id":1489287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1489225#post1489225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, can this gift be cumulative ?<br /> What can stop an uratha to strike at the liver and makes it bleed and then strike to another organ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text is not explicit about this, but effects that can be applied additively usually use the word &quot;cumulative&quot; or &quot;stackable&quot; somewhere. I personally wouldn't allow this Facet to be stacked multiple times on the same target, but this is a judgment call.<br /> <br /> Narratively, you can strike the liver and cause the target to suffer supernatural bleeding. Now the target is suffering a condition of supernatural bleeding. You could strike another organ with the Facet but the target is already suffering the Facet's condition of supernatural bleeding. You already did the thing the Facet does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T22:38:30-07:00","id":1489999,"title":"","content":"How much of the identity of someone being spirit claimed remains intact? Is there some trace? Does the Claimed exhibits some tics of the host or does the spirit completely override the host identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T05:35:24-07:00","id":1490016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1489999#post1489999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of the identity of someone being spirit claimed remains intact? Is there some trace? Does the Claimed exhibits some tics of the host or does the spirit completely override the host identity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chef's choice, but spirits strong enough to Claim a person tend to be strong enough to condition their host through a period of Urging and, internal awareness notwithstanding, the Claimed Condition opens its description with the statement that the being is permanently possessed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T09:43:32-07:00","id":1490035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1490016#post1490016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chef's choice, but spirits strong enough to Claim a person tend to be strong enough to condition their host through a period of Urging and, internal awareness notwithstanding, the Claimed Condition opens its description with the statement that the being is permanently possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it\u2019s even easier for Hive-Claimed to overwrite their host\u2019s Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T14:28:42-07:00","id":1491654,"title":"","content":"Are Lunes elaborated on, somewhere? I've read the 2E corebook, and it talks about how Forsaken get Renown by telling their stories to the Lunes, but if there's a section where that's explained, I missed it. There are rules for explaining how to buy Renown with XP but I don't remember seeing anything about how that actually works. Is there a rite to call a Lune to talk to, or does a werewolf just wait until they come across a Lune out in the world somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T19:49:15-07:00","id":1491705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1491654#post1491654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Lunes elaborated on, somewhere? I've read the 2E corebook, and it talks about how Forsaken get Renown by telling their stories to the Lunes, but if there's a section where that's explained, I missed it. There are rules for explaining how to buy Renown with XP but I don't remember seeing anything about how that actually works.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e talked about them and provided examples of six different types in Predators (one choir for each auspice and the Glimmering spirits of moonbeams, while the alluded-to Secrets are not statted) and the more obscure Maslunim who might sponsor a lunar crusade are discussed in War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a rite to call a Lune to talk to, or does a werewolf just wait until they come across a Lune out in the world somewhere? </div> </div> </div>The Shadowcall rite from the corebook should suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to say which book the Maslunim are in. 09-11-2022, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T05:15:58-07:00","id":1492691,"title":"","content":"So, I've just double-checked the WtF book and I think I've been misunderstanding how buying Gifts is meant to work in terms of Experience for the last few years. That said, I'm not really sure how to parse this section, and the process more broadly. Would someone be able to explain this succinctly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlocking new Gifts takes Experiences. Characters can also use Experiences to purchase additional Facets. Buying the first Facet of a Shadow Gift that your auspice or tribe has an affinity for (per their description in Chapter One) costs three Experiences. Buying the first Facet of any other Gift costs five Experiences. Having bought that first Facet, the character has unlocked the Gift, allowing the werewolf to buy additional Facets with Renown or Experiences. A character learns a Facet of the appropriate Renown when she gains a dot in that Renown; this costs no Experiences. If she wants to buy additional Facets, each one costs two Experiences. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T06:33:20-07:00","id":1492696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492691#post1492691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've just double-checked the WtF book and I think I've been misunderstanding how buying Gifts is meant to work in terms of Experience for the last few years. That said, I'm not really sure how to parse this section, and the process more broadly. Would someone be able to explain this succinctly?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my version of how I understood it, starting from Character Creation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So here's Scarlet, a Cahalith of the Hunters in Darkness tribe. Her affinity Gifts are Gibbous Moon, Inspiration, Knowledge, Nature, Stealth, Warding. At Character Creation, she should have a dot of Glory and a dot of Purity. That first dot of Glory (her Auspice Renown) gives her the first Facet of Gibbous Moon (her Moon Gift).<br /> <br /> CC gives her two free Shadow Gift Facets among Auspice/Tribe affinity Gifts. I don't think these two Facets are limited to starting Renown, so let's pick Lunatic Inspiration (Inspiration; Cunning) and Knotted Paths (Nature; Honor). Reading in good faith, this should mean that the Gift of Inspiration and Nature's Gift are unlocked. Keep this in mind.<br /> <br /> If Scarlet was a Blood Talon instead of a HiD, or a Rahu instead of Cahalith, she should have double-dipped into two dots of either Glory or Purity, which would give her the second Moon Gift Facet. But she was not, so she instead gets a free Wolf Gift Facet instead. Again, I don't think this is limited to starting Renown, so let's pick Totem's Wrath (Pack; Honor). All Wolf Gifts are always unlocked.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, Scarlet does something glorious and gets a dot of Glory (paying 3 Exp for that). This gives her the second Facet of Gibbous Moon for free. It also gives her one Glory Facet among unlocked Gifts. Let's pick Black Earth Red Hunger (Nature; Glory).<br /> <br /> Scarlet then decides she wants to be stealthy, so she sets out to unlock the Gift of Stealth, which equals buying one Facet from it. Stealth is an affinity Gift, so this first Facet costs 3 Exp. Let's pick The Hunter Waits (Stealth; Purity). The Gift of Stealth is now unlocked.<br /> <br /> Scarlet next decides she wants to do airbending. She buys Breath of Air (Elementals; Cunning) at 5 Exp, because the Gift of the Elementals is a non-affinity Gift. But hey, at least it's now unlocked.<br /> <br /> Scarlet then decides she want to buy Running Silent (Stealth; Wisdom). The Gift of Stealth is already unlocked; so it costs only 2 Exp. If she wanted to buy Heart of Water (Elementals; Wisdom) for some reason, that would've also cost 2 Exp, same as Running Silent, cuz both are unlocked Gifts.<br /> <br /> Or she could just buy a Wisdom dot at 3 Exp. That would give her for free one of the following Facets; Running Silent, Heart of Water, Still Small Voice (Inspiration), Beast Ride (Nature), and any Wisdom Facet among Wolf Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-09-2022, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T08:36:27-07:00","id":1492699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492696#post1492696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CC gives her two free Shadow Gift Facets among Auspice/Tribe affinity Gifts. I don't think these two Facets are limited to starting Renown, so let's pick Lunatic Inspiration (Inspiration; Cunning) and Knotted Paths (Nature; Honor). Reading in good faith, this should mean that the Gift of Inspiration and Nature's Gift are unlocked. Keep this in mind.<br /> <br /> If Scarlet was a Blood Talon instead of a HiD, or a Rahu instead of Cahalith, she should have double-dipped into two dots of either Glory or Purity, which would give her the second Moon Gift Facet. But she was not, so she instead gets a free Wolf Gift Facet instead. Again, I don't think this is limited to starting Renown, so let's pick Totem's Wrath (Pack; Honor). All Wolf Gifts are always unlocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rest is more or less correct, but starting Gifts aren't exempt from the requirement that you have at least one dot in the Renown you've got a Facet for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T16:01:24-07:00","id":1492718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492699#post1492699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest is more or less correct, but starting Gifts aren't exempt from the requirement that you have at least one dot in the Renown you've got a Facet for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gah. Well, back to the drawing board for some pre-gen Characters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T21:22:07-07:00","id":1492736,"title":"","content":"Concerning Rites, what narrative effects do they have beyond the immediate and mechanical effects? Like do Rites give strength to spirits that it calls to? Asking because I recently read the idigram chronicles and thought the Last Rites story was super cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T21:57:13-07:00","id":1492737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492736#post1492736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning Rites, what narrative effects do they have beyond the immediate and mechanical effects? Like do Rites give strength to spirits that it calls to? Asking because I recently read the idigram chronicles and thought the Last Rites story was super cool</div> </div> </div> </div>A rite is a symbolic invocation of the pacts and agreements that make up the natural order the Shadow reflects in the world, the same bonds that mark the turning of the seasons and the rising of the tides.<br /> <br /> To compare them to things from other gamelines, they're the Hisil's counterpart to Embeds, Ceremonies, and Contracts; they're a magical framework of how-the-world-works, based in this case on the precedents established by powerful spirits acting in line with established relationships between phenomena and deeper underlying concepts like sacrifice, territory, exchange, dominance, violence, and other things most simply expressed by the Shadow's predatory food web. Possibly this is an echo of the nature of Pangaea as a place where the pillars of the world dwelled, but that's entirely speculation on my part.<br /> <br /> Insofar as any given rite empowers spirits, the ones that don't specifically deal with individual spirits as game-mechanical actors call upon the spirit world to produce an established outcome. Time and space aren't always super-huge concerns here \u2014 note that Shadowcall allows a spirit offered proper compensation to answer its call regardless of material and dimensional distance by virtue of the rite being performed appropriately. A rite does not deal with <i>spirits</i> so much as it deals with <i>the Shadow</i> as a means of producing an effect; it's just that spirits are how the Shadow manifests its ability to have an effect.<br /> <br /> The verbiage isn't echoed in Werewolf, but being the spiritual reflection of the entire world means rites are nevertheless operating in the same sort of headspace as Changeling and Demon's &quot;this set of magical rules is so complex no one person could reasonably expect to learn them all.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:49:41-07:00","id":1492837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492737#post1492737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rite is a symbolic invocation of the pacts and agreements that make up the natural order the Shadow reflects in the world, the same bonds that mark the turning of the seasons and the rising of the tides.<br /> <br /> To compare them to things from other gamelines, they're the Hisil's counterpart to Embeds, Ceremonies, and Contracts; they're a magical framework of how-the-world-works, based in this case on the precedents established by powerful spirits acting in line with established relationships between phenomena and deeper underlying concepts like sacrifice, territory, exchange, dominance, violence, and other things most simply expressed by the Shadow's predatory food web. Possibly this is an echo of the nature of Pangaea as a place where the pillars of the world dwelled, but that's entirely speculation on my part.<br /> <br /> Insofar as any given rite empowers spirits, the ones that don't specifically deal with individual spirits as game-mechanical actors call upon the spirit world to produce an established outcome. Time and space aren't always super-huge concerns here \u2014 note that Shadowcall allows a spirit offered proper compensation to answer its call regardless of material and dimensional distance by virtue of the rite being performed appropriately. A rite does not deal with <i>spirits</i> so much as it deals with <i>the Shadow</i> as a means of producing an effect; it's just that spirits are how the Shadow manifests its ability to have an effect.<br /> <br /> The verbiage isn't echoed in Werewolf, but being the spiritual reflection of the entire world means rites are nevertheless operating in the same sort of headspace as Changeling and Demon's &amp;quot;this set of magical rules is so complex no one person could reasonably expect to learn them all.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, gotcha. So the enacting of these rites actually shouldn't (normally) have too big of an effect after the intended one has passed? Is it safe to say a rite in of itself can have a narrative effect such as the one in Last Rites, or is that usually not gonna happen.<br /> <br /> And is it safe to assume a high dot rite would take a story's worth to discover/piece together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T17:55:13-07:00","id":1492847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492837#post1492837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, gotcha. So the enacting of these rites actually shouldn't (normally) have too big of an effect after the intended one has passed? Is it safe to say a rite in of itself can have a narrative effect such as the one in Last Rites, or is that usually not gonna happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have to specify what you mean here, because to all appearances the rite in Last Rites was a very particular one that the viewpoint character was able to best make use of from having received the Gift of Death from the spirit it reached out to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is it safe to assume a high dot rite would take a story's worth to discover/piece together? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Careful, years-long observation&quot; to figure out a rite without a teacher would seem to indicate this to be a reasonable assumption, yes, particularly given that uncommon lore is jealously guarded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T20:44:53-07:00","id":1493093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1492847#post1492847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may have to specify what you mean here, because to all appearances the rite in Last Rites was a very particular one that the viewpoint character was able to best make use of from having received the Gift of Death from the spirit it reached out to.<br /> <br /> &quot;Careful, years-long observation&quot; to figure out a rite without a teacher would seem to indicate this to be a reasonable assumption, yes, particularly given that uncommon lore is jealously guarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for not answering sooner regarding your question<br /> <br /> Concerning what I mean, It's that can rites be as interactive as the one seen in the story? Like, is it possible to make a scene where the Rite itself is essentially the main event rather than simply a means to an end (and semi regularly too)?<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm doing a poor job of articulating it. I would just like to run a werewolf chronicle and have Rites be something my players can look forward to and think &quot;what exciting, great, and horrid things may come of this&quot; every so often","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T20:20:07-07:00","id":1493144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1493093#post1493093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning what I mean, It's that can rites be as interactive as the one seen in the story? Like, is it possible to make a scene where the Rite itself is essentially the main event rather than simply a means to an end (and semi regularly too)?<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm doing a poor job of articulating it. I would just like to run a werewolf chronicle and have Rites be something my players can look forward to and think &quot;what exciting, great, and horrid things may come of this&quot; every so often</div> </div> </div> </div>The performance of the rite basically concludes as soon as Raven's Scribe arrives in the Keeper's domain; the rest of that chapter is essentially a sustained context imposed by the success of the rite, much as rites like Supplication or Hunting Ground or Shadowbind maintain their effects while the necessary conditions are in place.<br /> <br /> Rites draw upon the laws of the Shadow, and many of them require those laws to apply and be upheld for a ritemaster continue to benefit from them. You can absolutely have a rite whose effect exists to put characters into a frame of interaction that allows them to tackle a problem in a way they wouldn't otherwise be able to as long as they follow the rules that frame imposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T21:22:34-07:00","id":1493148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1493144#post1493144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The performance of the rite basically concludes as soon as Raven's Scribe arrives in the Keeper's domain; the rest of that chapter is essentially a sustained context imposed by the success of the rite, much as rites like Supplication or Hunting Ground or Shadowbind maintain their effects while the necessary conditions are in place.<br /> <br /> Rites draw upon the laws of the Shadow, and many of them require those laws to apply and be upheld for a ritemaster continue to benefit from them. You can absolutely have a rite whose effect exists to put characters into a frame of interaction that allows them to tackle a problem in a way they wouldn't otherwise be able to as long as they follow the rules that frame imposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok I get it now. Really excited to think up some rites now. Thank you for taking the time to answer, I really appreciate it!<br /> <br /> EDIT: also I must've misunderstood the rite in the story, I thought the rite was still considered &quot;in progress&quot; since raven's scribe is still underground in the coffin, I didn't connect that it was basically like the rites you mentioned in terms of what completion meant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 09-16-2022, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T12:27:43-07:00","id":1493348,"title":"","content":"Edited.<br /> <br /> Doubt about a gift because of my poor english.<br /> Girlfriend translated correctly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 09-19-2022, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T08:54:08-07:00","id":1494677,"title":"","content":"How might a Supernal Totem appear to werewolf senses/sensibilities? As a powerful spirit? As a strange thing masquerading as a Shadow denizen? Something other entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T11:02:48-07:00","id":1494683,"title":"","content":"It would appear...<i>similar</i>...to a Shadow spirit, but <i>something</i> would be \u201coff\u201d about it. At least, in MY opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T12:22:54-07:00","id":1494690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1494677#post1494677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might a Supernal Totem appear to werewolf senses/sensibilities? As a powerful spirit? As a strange thing masquerading as a Shadow denizen? Something other entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the human senses, probably the way mages non-Seeing seeing them. For wolf senses, possibly overwhelming depending on the Supernal entity in question. For spirit senses, nothing in particular since the spirit senses aren't attuned to the Supernal, unless the entity in question has relationship with with symbols related with the Shadow, spirits, and all that such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T14:08:01-07:00","id":1494697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1494690#post1494690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the human senses, probably the way mages non-Seeing seeing them. For wolf senses, possibly overwhelming depending on the Supernal entity in question. For spirit senses, nothing in particular since the spirit senses aren't attuned to the Supernal, unless the entity in question has relationship with with symbols related with the Shadow, spirits, and all that such.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Supernal Totem being a recondite entity of the Spirit Arcanum, it's probably going to register in some capacity if it's made itself known.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1494677#post1494677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might a Supernal Totem appear to werewolf senses/sensibilities? As a powerful spirit? As a strange thing masquerading as a Shadow denizen? Something other entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it's encountered in a context where it can be engaged with, it'll be visible in spiritual Twilight or the Shadow if it's in that phase of reality and materially if it's in the Flesh, it'll register to Scent the Unnatural if that Facet is used, a Boundary Ward can be set against it if the werewolf knows what it is, and the lack of Influences can probably be picked up on if you get its scent, but werewolves don't otherwise have any special facility for figuring out the nature of supernatural beings through innate senses. This feels like a &quot;non-Awakened supernatural beings count as Sleepwalkers&quot; situation, with all that that entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T11:14:11-07:00","id":1495445,"title":"","content":"Should a werewolf shift to Dalu mid combat, are they able to still roll Presence + Primal Urge to make everyone on the opposing side besides their prey back down, allowing them and their pack to hunt said prey ? In other words, does the ability only apply outside of combat ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-22-2022, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T12:45:04-07:00","id":1495454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1495445#post1495445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a werewolf shift to Dalu mid combat, are they able to still roll Presence + Primal Urge to make everyone on the opposing side besides their prey back down, allowing them and their pack to hunt said prey ? In other words, does the ability only apply outside of combat ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Badass Motherfucker is a power to be used for making a crowd give up the prey, contested by the prey alone. It's functionally there, among other things, to set the stage for Gauru's Primal Fear ability to work at its most effective by shortcutting the entire confrontation into Down and Dirty Combat, which you can't do in the middle of an existing combat scene. If you're mid-combat, you mostly have the ability to inflict the Beaten Down Tilt on characters you'd be using Badass Motherfucker on with a single hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T19:04:25-08:00","id":1497600,"title":"","content":"More a Spirit question than a Werewolf question, but is there an object equivalent to being Claimed? That is, a person who is Possessed to often and too frequently can become claimed, but is there a similar consequence for possessing, say, a rubber ball?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T23:07:52-08:00","id":1497608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1497600#post1497600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More a Spirit question than a Werewolf question, but is there an object equivalent to being Claimed? That is, a person who is Possessed to often and too frequently can become claimed, but is there a similar consequence for possessing, say, a rubber ball?</div> </div> </div> </div>To Claim a target you need te Controlled condition on it, that can results from repeated use of Possession.<br /> After that the Spirit must use the Claim manifestation.<br /> Both manifestation, Possess and Claim, states that they can be used on corpses and items","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T10:04:44-08:00","id":1498133,"title":"","content":"I ruled that it did work, but I just wanted to confirm if this was rules as intended.<br /> <br /> Garble (Technology gift Cunning) says that technology turns against the target and won't function as intended. I originally thought &quot;cool, communications disrupted&quot; but it also says that elevators drop the prey off where the Uratha wants, not where the prey directs the elevator.<br /> <br /> This being the case, when the prey tried to flee in a truck I ruled that it wouldn't leave neutral gear, and when they tried to pull a gun on the pack it misfired.<br /> <br /> Is this how it's meant to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T15:51:23-08:00","id":1498174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSV_FOtNMC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1498133#post1498133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ruled that it did work, but I just wanted to confirm if this was rules as intended.<br /> <br /> Garble (Technology gift Cunning) says that technology turns against the target and won't function as intended. I originally thought &quot;cool, communications disrupted&quot; but it also says that elevators drop the prey off where the Uratha wants, not where the prey directs the elevator.<br /> <br /> This being the case, when the prey tried to flee in a truck I ruled that it wouldn't leave neutral gear, and when they tried to pull a gun on the pack it misfired.<br /> <br /> Is this how it's meant to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it, given that the three examples include a communication-based one, a non-communication-based one, and one that gives options that are both communication-based and non-communication-based, thought the three examples all include some facet of the technology that makes it more than a direct mechanical process \u2014 I'd say the gun misfiring is probably beyond the scope of the Facet, and depending on how the transmission works the truck might be out of scope as well.<br /> <br /> My reading is that while the outcomes can be non-communication-based, the mechanism by which the Facet works requires there to be some kind of communicative process to mess with that's more complex than &quot;press lever to move part/ignite spark/etc.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T20:49:55-08:00","id":1498597,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to end Gauru form early, or does it have to last until at least the end of the base duration? If a character has gauru form for like 6 turns, but kills all his enemies on turn 1, will he go after his companions for the following 5 turns until he can shift down to a different form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T21:28:16-08:00","id":1498604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1498597#post1498597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to end Gauru form early, or does it have to last until at least the end of the base duration? If a character has gauru form for like 6 turns, but kills all his enemies on turn 1, will he go after his companions for the following 5 turns until he can shift down to a different form?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can shift back IF you have not entered Kuruth, but remember that you can enter Gauru only once per scene, after you had shift back you ll have to wait, so it s wise to be sure that all threats are gone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T16:16:44-07:00","id":1505204,"title":"","content":"Can an Uratha in the Shadow interact with object like opening doors etc?<br /> <br /> More specifically, if an Uratha wants to sneaking into the hideout of his prey without being noticed, can he cross the gauntlet, opening or smashing down all the closed doors to reappear in the room of his prey, whitout having been noticed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T06:25:13-07:00","id":1505245,"title":"","content":"Depends. Uratha can't cross Gauntlet at just any location. They can do that through a Locus or a Verge. Other than that, they have to resort to rare Gifts, Fetishes or help from powerful Spirits. The room the prey is hiding in might not allow entry through the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Werewolves <i>do</i> use the Shadow to circumvent obstacles. They can try to wreck all doors in the Hisil, without obvious effect in the material world. However, those will be Spirit doors that can wreck them right back. Negotiation might be necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T06:34:44-07:00","id":1505897,"title":"","content":"Can a Uratha take supernatural merits from other places if they qualify such as things like Medium or Biokinesis? If so, would 1 point of biokinesis which &quot;halves all healing times&quot; double the rate of regeneration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T07:17:26-07:00","id":1505900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1505897#post1505897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Uratha take supernatural merits from other places if they qualify such as things like Medium or Biokinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Most Supernatural Merits sections contain a note at the beginning that they are only available to otherwise ordinary humans, which is the case with Medium and Biokinesis in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T10:49:02-07:00","id":1505911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1505900#post1505900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Most Supernatural Merits sections contain a note at the beginning that they are only available to otherwise ordinary humans, which is the case with Medium and Biokinesis in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I thought I remembered that being the case but for the life of me I couldn't remember why I thought that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T08:05:42-07:00","id":1507406,"title":"","content":"Is there a pdf character sheet for Claimed in second edition? I'd take official or unofficial.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mr.Gone's 2 Page Predator sheet works perfectly well for claimed, it has enough dots to handle most claimed, a place for dread powers, and the second page is a spirit page so you can have stats for the spirit, including the influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":".  Answering my own question. 04-04-2023, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T16:12:14-07:00","id":1507793,"title":"","content":"More a Spirit question than a Werewolf question, but are there spirits with multiple &quot;bodies&quot;? Like a Hive-Souled in MtAw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T17:02:30-07:00","id":1507797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1507793#post1507793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More a Spirit question than a Werewolf question, but are there spirits with multiple &quot;bodies&quot;? Like a Hive-Souled in MtAw.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what the host are, they're shards of ancient gods trying to put themselves back together. <br /> <br /> But I don't believe it exists for spirits in Werewolf the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T17:53:12-07:00","id":1507806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1507793#post1507793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More a Spirit question than a Werewolf question, but are there spirits with multiple &quot;bodies&quot;? Like a Hive-Souled in MtAw.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIIRC, there was a spirit that Claimed an entire town in a 1e Night Horrors book. Closest thing printed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T07:38:26-07:00","id":1508357,"title":"","content":"How does influence works for an Uratha on both a mechanical and descriptive point of view? <br /> If an Uratha has Influence water 4 or 5, at this level it's stated he can create a new example of its sphere of influence. Does it means he can create water from nothing? How should that work and what should be the entity of the water created? How the roll determine the effect? <br /> Does influencing water allow to, in example, revert the flow of a river? or to make a river, lake becoming iced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T07:44:21-07:00","id":1508358,"title":"","content":"Another question which is separated from my last topic:<br /> how do you determine death for a werewolf? I'm aware that having all health boxes filled out with Lethal normally means that each minute one lethal becomes aggravated and once full of aggravated there's the final death but, as we are talking about werewolves with crazy regenerative skills, can they always heal back lethal or are they unconscious? Can they always turn into Gauru to fully recover from a health bar full of aggravated? I also remember I read about a rite which allows a pack to resurrect a dead mate leaving him with a permanent injury (losing an attribute). Where is this mentioned in the book (I cannot find it back)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T11:49:38-07:00","id":1508373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508357#post1508357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does influence works for an Uratha on both a mechanical and descriptive point of view?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you mean here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If an Uratha has Influence water 4 or 5, at this level it's stated he can create a new example of its sphere of influence. Does it means he can create water from nothing? How should that work and what should be the entity of the water created? How the roll determine the effect? </div> </div> </div>Yes, at rank 5 I believe they can create from nothing. Generally I'd say things created with influence have rank 0 sleeping spirits at most. And generally the way you gain your influence will tell you what roll you will need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does influencing water allow to, in example, revert the flow of a river? or to make a river, lake becoming iced? </div> </div> </div>A river is probably a bigger ask than influence 5 alone would influence. Even if your storyteller does allow it, it's not likely to be a permanent change, the water that flows in to replace the water you moved will follow the path of least resistance which will probably be the river's path.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> how do you determine death for a werewolf? I'm aware that having all health boxes filled out with Lethal normally means that each minute one lethal becomes aggravated and once full of aggravated there's the final death but, as we are talking about werewolves with crazy regenerative skills, can they always heal back lethal or are they unconscious? </div> </div> </div>There's a few things going on here. Werewolves in Gauru form do not suffer wound penalties nor go unconscious due to lethal damage. In other forms they take damage as humans do, though it is important to note their regeneration. Also equally important to note is that they do not &quot;bleed out&quot; so long as they can regenerate their right most health box.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they always turn into Gauru to fully recover from a health bar full of aggravated? </div> </div> </div>Gauru only heals the bar worth of lethal damage, it has no effect on aggravated damage. There are also important restrictions on when they can shift to Gauru, such as not shape shifting to it more than once per scene. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also remember I read about a rite which allows a pack to resurrect a dead mate leaving him with a permanent injury (losing an attribute). Where is this mentioned in the book (I cannot find it back)? </div> </div> </div>I have not read that, I do not believe it exists in Second Edition. You might have read a homebrew rite online or you might have read it in First Edition, I'm not certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 04-14-2023, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T13:48:55-07:00","id":1508387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508357#post1508357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Uratha has Influence water 4 or 5, at this level it's stated he can create a new example of its sphere of influence. Does it means he can create water from nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the function of the Create and Mass Create Influence effects, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How should that work and what should be the entity of the water created? How the roll determine the effect? </div> </div> </div>Gifts that provide access to an Influence indicate the dicepool that Influence uses \u2014 the Shadow Masquerade Facet of the Crescent Moon's Gift uses its own dicepool for copied Influences, for example, and every Facet of the Gift of the Elementals that isn't Catastrophe has a dicepool that that Influence uses \u2014 while Influences provided by the Wellspring rite or a talen use Presence + Wits. The rules for scale and duration are described in the Influence Effects and Influence Duration charts on pages 186 and 187 of WtF2e Core.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does influencing water allow to, in example, revert the flow of a river? or to make a river, lake becoming iced? </div> </div> </div>Influences are generally bigger-picture/utility powers compared to Numina, and the spiritual ecosystem generally has bigger actors accomplish bigger results by being able to marshal the resources of those beneath them rather than in single bursts of spiritual activity. A spirit with Influence (Water) 3 can make dramatic changes in water around it, but those changes are short-lived without upkeep (anything of a scale that bothers with stats is managing changes that last for hours at most).\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508358#post1508358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you determine death for a werewolf? I'm aware that having all health boxes filled out with Lethal normally means that each minute one lethal becomes aggravated and once full of aggravated there's the final death but, as we are talking about werewolves with crazy regenerative skills, can they always heal back lethal or are they unconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf outside of Gauru form who is not spending Essence to accelerate their regeneration does not regenerate lethal damage fast enough to outpace bleeding out; there's an ambiguously worded line in the section on healing that says &quot;As long as a werewolf can regenerate her rightmost Health box, she won't bleed out,&quot; which could be a simple observation that if you manage to heal the point of lethal damage that is filling your Health track then you've stopped meeting the conditions that cause you to be bleeding out, a statement that a werewolf with any Essence in their system that the could use to instantly heal lethal damage doesn't bleed out whether they spend that Essence or not, or a statement that as long as a werewolf has not had their regeneration stopped somehow (e.g. by the Cold Embrace Facet of the Gift of Death) they aren't subject to the rules for bleeding out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they always turn into Gauru to fully recover from a health bar full of aggravated? </div> </div> </div>As with demons assuming full demonic form, aggravated damage is damage that doesn't go away quickly from invoking the &quot;someone is almost certainly going to die&quot; state. Even with overall accelerated healing, the fastest recovery for agg is twelve hours by the 2e version of the Purified introduced in Mummy 2e's Book of Lasting Death, with most other sources of passive recovery (including werewolves') taking three or four days per box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T16:08:05-07:00","id":1508400,"title":"","content":"I just noticed this and was curious about it. As far as I can the only way to perform a killing blow is the merit. That merit can only be used in Gauru form and requires purity 2. But killing blow also says it's a breaking point for mortals. How can you perform a killing blow outside of using the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T17:40:04-07:00","id":1508402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508400#post1508400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed this and was curious about it. As far as I can the only way to perform a killing blow is the merit. That merit can only be used in Gauru form and requires purity 2. But killing blow also says it's a breaking point for mortals. How can you perform a killing blow outside of using the merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>By having the target at your mercy and unable to defend themselves. The newer iteration of the rules text presented in Changeling, Geist, Deviant, Mummy, and Hunter reads as follows (emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Killing Blow:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Inflict damage equal to your attack\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> dice pool + weapon bonus. <u>Requires an unconscious,</u></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><u> immobilized, or otherwise helpless target.</u> May prompt</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> a breaking point.</span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T18:35:35-07:00","id":1508405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508402#post1508402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By having the target at your mercy and unable to defend themselves. The newer iteration of the rules text presented in Changeling, Geist, Deviant, Mummy, and Hunter reads as follows (emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Killing Blow:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Inflict damage equal to your attack\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> dice pool + weapon bonus. <u>Requires an unconscious,</u></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><u> immobilized, or otherwise helpless target.</u> May prompt</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> a breaking point.</span>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm not crazy, in WtF there is no way for a mortal to do it. Ty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T18:50:23-07:00","id":1508406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508405#post1508405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm not crazy, in WtF there is no way for a mortal to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is the opposite of what I said.<br /> <br /> If you're a mortal and you only have your bare hands available to you in a fight where you're trying to kill somebody, once they're unconscious you no longer need to roll to hit them. If you're a mortal and you have a bound hostage in the middle of a fight you can inflict the maximum amount of damage a surprise attack would deal without 10-Again. If you're a werewolf who doesn't have the Efficient Killer Merit, you can still strike a Killing Blow against someone a packmate's got immobilized via grappling. The rules text presented in games published after Promethean 2e is a different presentation of the same rules for clarity \u2014 Efficient Killer just introduces a specific means of making a Killing Blow from a position of slightly less overwhelming advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T19:51:08-07:00","id":1508409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508406#post1508406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is the opposite of what I said.<br /> <br /> If you're a mortal and you only have your bare hands available to you in a fight where you're trying to kill somebody, once they're unconscious you no longer need to roll to hit them. If you're a mortal and you have a bound hostage in the middle of a fight you can inflict the maximum amount of damage a surprise attack would deal without 10-Again. If you're a werewolf who doesn't have the Efficient Killer Merit, you can still strike a Killing Blow against someone a packmate's got immobilized via grappling. The rules text presented in games published after Promethean 2e is a different presentation of the same rules for clarity \u2014 Efficient Killer just introduces a specific means of making a Killing Blow from a position of slightly less overwhelming advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I accept that is the intent, but the fact that they had to change the wording seems to indicate that the previous wording was insufficient. Not that it really matters, it wasn't for a game, I had just been reading the rules for it and I was like &quot;something is missing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T20:41:11-07:00","id":1508413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508409#post1508409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I accept that is the intent, but the fact that they had to change the wording seems to indicate that the previous wording was insufficient. Not that it really matters, it wasn't for a game, I had just been reading the rules for it and I was like &quot;something is missing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Performing a killing blow is a premeditated attempt to end a human life without the target having a chance to do anything about it&quot; is pretty clearly not &quot;the Killing Blow mechanic is exclusive to the Efficient Killer Merit&quot; even without the knowledge that the mechanic existed in 1e as well.* It's a very simple mechanic that most characters will not have the opportunity to use in a direct fight because it requires an overwhelming advantage and attempted murder tends to have psychospiritual consequences in these games.<br /> <br /> Werewolf 2e Core was one of the 2e corebooks being worked on before the determination that The Idigam Chronicle could actually be called a Second Edition and the layout decision to include the core mechanics in every gameline's core rulebook. The reformatting is pretty definitely at least partly a space-saving matter \u2014 there's fewer subsection headers and more bullet-pointed lists in general, the optional rules for Beaten Down and Surrender are consistently put in a sidebar and the starting step of declaring intent is explicitly labeled as such. This isn't &quot;they had to change the wording because the previous wording of 'a killing blow is when you go to kill someone in a way they can't stop' was insufficient,&quot; this is &quot;the gamelines that started development after the God-Machine Chronicle Rules Update stopped being the primary format of Revised Storytelling System rules text available were able to have a new iteration of that text that was clearer overall.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* &quot;A target who is tied up, unconscious or paralyzed not only gets no Defense, he can be felled by a single blow. A roll need not be made for an attacker; the damage points he inflicts equal his dice pool, modified by any armor worn by the target. Damage done is automatic, as is armor's protection. No attack roll is required.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-14-2023, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T01:13:00-07:00","id":1508423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508387#post1508387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with demons assuming full demonic form, aggravated damage is damage that doesn't go away quickly from invoking the &quot;someone is almost certainly going to die&quot; state. Even with overall accelerated healing, the fastest recovery for agg is twelve hours by the 2e version of the Purified introduced in Mummy 2e's Book of Lasting Death, with most other sources of passive recovery (including werewolves') taking three or four days per box.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do apologize, I mistakenly wrote: &quot;full of aggravated&quot; while I meant &quot;full of lethal&quot;. My question was related to the fact that, if a werewolf hits the last health box with lethal, is he still conscious to use his regenerative skills to stop bleeding out in time to save himself from death (or going Garou - death rage - to heal up all instantly)? Or is he falling in coma so that, like an human, without medical attention he's doomed to die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T06:23:58-07:00","id":1508435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508423#post1508423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question was related to the fact that, if a werewolf hits the last health box with lethal, is he still conscious to use his regenerative skills to stop bleeding out in time to save himself from death (or going Garou - death rage - to heal up all instantly)? Or is he falling in coma so that, like an human, without medical attention he's doomed to die?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been some disagreement among the writers over whether or not you have to be conscious to take the reflexive action of spending 1 Essence to make their turn-by-turn regeneration heal lethal damage, and by the same token there's no direct word on whether you could (Essence- and Harmony-permitting) reflexively shift to Gauru upon hitting a full track of lethal.<br /> <br /> Personally, given the class of things reflexive actions entail in this system includes a whole bunch of stuff that can happen without you being aware, conscious, or even alive, I'm inclined to say that you can reflexively supercharge your regeneration or take Gauru form, with the caveat that regeneration happens on your turn, so if additional enemies take a potshot at you while you're starting to die the additional damage has time to roll over to aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T15:26:48-07:00","id":1508786,"title":"","content":"Has there been any kind of write-up, official or otherwise, for using Social Maneuvering (or any system really) to bargain for favors from spirits? As in, some kind of mechanical guidelines for how hard it is to, say, persuade a spirit of Rank x to use Influence y, costing z Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T16:40:39-07:00","id":1508791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508786#post1508786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any kind of write-up, official or otherwise, for using Social Maneuvering (or any system really) to bargain for favors from spirits? As in, some kind of mechanical guidelines for how hard it is to, say, persuade a spirit of Rank x to use Influence y, costing z Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>See the &quot;Gathra&quot; section of the corebook on pages 181-192.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T13:51:28-07:00","id":1508924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1508791#post1508791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the &quot;Gathra&quot; section of the corebook on pages 181-192.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I had forgotten that there were some specifics in that section. Though I was mainly looking to see if there already existed precise guidelines on how to modify the number of Doors for \u201cgeneric\u201d spirit favors a shaman might request, like a single use of a Influence or Numina, making a Talen, and so forth, before taking a shot at writing them up myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:05:45-07:00","id":1509081,"title":"","content":"Can the blood created by Seep (The Cunning Renown power for the Gift of Blood) be used in blood transfusions? If yes, can a werewolf decide what blood type the blood is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:47:41-07:00","id":1509102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509081#post1509081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the blood created by Seep (The Cunning Renown power for the Gift of Blood) be used in blood transfusions? If yes, can a werewolf decide what blood type the blood is?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is significantly outside of what RAW provides for the spell so ultimately you'll have to ask your storyteller. I would personally say no, the blood is oozing out of the walls and everything, it's going to be dirty and contaminated with bacteria and germs, not to mention it'll begin clotting very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:53:58-07:00","id":1509104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509081#post1509081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the blood created by Seep (The Cunning Renown power for the Gift of Blood) be used in blood transfusions? If yes, can a werewolf decide what blood type the blood is?</div> </div> </div> </div>What ShadowcatX said above. A fetish (homebrewed for your table) might be able to do that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T16:11:20-07:00","id":1509111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509104#post1509104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What ShadowcatX said above. A fetish (homebrewed for your table) might be able to do that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rank 4 fetish granting influence: blood for create should be able to. To be fair though rank 1 strengthen blood might be enough to do the job though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T16:47:14-07:00","id":1509115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509111#post1509111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A rank 4 fetish granting influence: blood for create should be able to. To be fair though rank 1 strengthen blood might be enough to do the job though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was imagining 3-dot with that, actually \u2014 based on how the Gridlock Puzzle modifies the All Doors Locked Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T18:53:16-07:00","id":1509335,"title":"","content":"Would a werewolf who used their Gifts to pretend to be a witch, shaman, a psychic etc. be violating the &quot;Herd must not know&quot; rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T19:13:36-07:00","id":1509337,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think so, but really I think it would matter more if they think they're violating it. (And if Blood Talon elodoths think they are breaking it. Lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T20:05:04-07:00","id":1509549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509335#post1509335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a werewolf who used their Gifts to pretend to be a witch, shaman, a psychic etc. be violating the &quot;Herd must not know&quot; rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of people believe in psychic powers without also believing in werewolves. Posing as some other sort of mystic could be a cunning way of pulling the wool over someone's eyes and distracting them from the truth, especially if you leverage their own biases and beliefs in doing so. That said, you're definitely treading some dicey waters depending on the Gifts in question. People talk; spirits see things; someone might get the wrong idea that isn't the wrong idea you were going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:19:01-07:00","id":1509639,"title":"","content":"Can the Heart of Water power of the Gift of Elementals be used to pollute water and/or create acid rain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:35:31-07:00","id":1509641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509639#post1509639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Heart of Water power of the Gift of Elementals be used to pollute water and/or create acid rain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Control Influence (3-dot) could, I believe. (Away from my books atm, so take a grain of salt) Though acid rain is a bit stretch for me \u2014 you might want a fetish that modifies one of the Weather Gift\u2019s Facets for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:32:22-07:00","id":1509653,"title":"","content":"I feel it's important to point out acid rain isn't like raining sulfuric acid where it melts flesh off people's bones, it's regular rain that picks up certain pollutants on the way down, and while it's acidic enough to damage property it's not typically immediately dangerous.<br /> <br /> That said, I do not think influence water would be able to create acid rain, you're needing to add stuff to water. Influence pollution could probably do it if it was already raining.<br /> <br /> Influence water should be able to crank raining conditions up to dangerous amounts of rain if that's what you're wanting to do.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in more examples of what influence can do, the 3PP book Ephemeral Influence is really good and available on the Storyteller Vault.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've been thinking about this and I think I was wrong. I think acid rain would still be considered water so it should still work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":".  Changing my opinion. 04-26-2023, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:52:50-07:00","id":1509815,"title":"","content":"Can the Gift of Elements facets allow a werewolf to weaken or nullify magical sources of those elements? For example, if a Mage uses their magic to start a fire, can a werewolf use the Fire facet to decrease or put out the fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:59:50-07:00","id":1509816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509815#post1509815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Gift of Elements facets allow a werewolf to weaken or nullify magical sources of those elements? For example, if a Mage uses their magic to start a fire, can a werewolf use the Fire facet to decrease or put out the fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:01:35-07:00","id":1509817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509815#post1509815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Gift of Elements facets allow a werewolf to weaken or nullify magical sources of those elements? For example, if a Mage uses their magic to start a fire, can a werewolf use the Fire facet to decrease or put out the fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Control effect at Influence 3 should allow you to do that, I believe. The actual mechanics will work via Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T07:43:16-07:00","id":1509862,"title":"","content":"Only a Clash of Wills provided the mage creates an unexinguishable fire (i.e. the fire persists as long as the spell is active, as opposed to the spell creating a simple, mundane fire).<br /> <br /> Personally I allow inverse uses of Strengthen, which could be used to decrease the magnitude and size of the fire until it extinguishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-27-2023, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T22:18:18-07:00","id":1509922,"title":"","content":"Out of all the given examples of influences in the Ephemeral Influence source book, Influence Water was very, very, VERY underwhelmingly. As a given example, Influence Fire and Influence Earth are given access to tilts as early as two to three dots and given cool imagery like using a lighter to shoot out fire balls. Influence Earth can be used to throw sharpened stalagmites and cause knockdowns or to reach out with earthen tendrils to ensnare foes. Influence water doesn't get a tilt until <b>FOUR </b>dots and doesn't get any 'bender' like flourish despite the fact that the most deadly natural disasters involve water in someway. Would it be too game breaking to use earth influences as an example for what Influence Water can do? \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T03:46:01-07:00","id":1509940,"title":"","content":"Water gets the flood tilt at 3, the same level that earth gets earthquake. And isn't relocate (3 dots) what benders do? Or did you mean it doesn't have a direct attack other than drown? <br /> <br /> My concern wouldn't be &quot;is it broken&quot; to allow water to do the same things earth can do but if it made the influences too much the same. If that's not a concern for you I'd say go for it, the things in ephemeral influence are only meant to be examples anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T06:54:53-07:00","id":1509950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1509940#post1509940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water gets the flood tilt at 3, the same level that earth gets earthquake. And isn't relocate (3 dots) what benders do? Or did you mean it doesn't have a direct attack other than drown?<br /> <br /> My concern wouldn't be &quot;is it broken&quot; to allow water to do the same things earth can do but if it made the influences too much the same. If that's not a concern for you I'd say go for it, the things in ephemeral influence are only meant to be examples anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Water just feels like it isn't given a lot of options. You can use air influence to increase your speed by adding your rank and at the high end its <i>multiplied by your rank.</i> You can make usable tools out of earth or cause an earthquake out of nowhere. In contrast, water lets you swim better and lets you not dehydrate as fast if you drink 'magic' water made by your influence. In comparison its just so lacking I wonder why anyone would take Heart of Water. The fourth dot example, downpour, can only gives a tilt effect over a building meanwhile the fourth dot of earthquake can effect an entire neighborhood. And that flood tilt at dot 3 is dependent on if their is a flood already in progress meanwhile, again, Earth lets you cause an earthquake out of nowhere. Maybe if you could use strengthen to bust open a waterpipe in a house or street or make a fire hydrant fail but would that even be possible? You can't turn the water to ice and use icicles as weapons because that would be Influence Ice according to the book. Can't use steam because again that would be influence steam and I'm not sure about using the moisture in the air or taking water out of plant life. There's so many interesting things water can do that's locked behind the reasoning that if it isn't pure water in its liquid form, then you have no influence over it. Meanwhile those with the air influence are walking around in complete vacuum. Where are the tsunamis, the redirected rivers, the heavy storms that floods an entire neighborhood? Hell, you should be able to create your own geysers at strong enough influence but given the power levels of the examples given I just don't know if that's even remotely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T18:08:38-07:00","id":1510941,"title":"","content":"If a werewolf is in a polyamorous relationship, can all of their lovers count as one touchstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T09:27:52-07:00","id":1510988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1510941#post1510941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf is in a polyamorous relationship, can all of their lovers count as one touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone in a polyamorous relationship, I would probably handle the entirety of the polycule itself as probably a Flesh Touchstone, as it would presumably centre not only meaningful interactions with individual human members but facilitate meaningful participation in a human <i>system</i>. Plus, I'd count the polycule a viable Touchstone because it can potentially be threatened in various forms - threat of violence from the outside, threat of destabilization from the inside - and would essentially require the uratha's involvement to protect and resolve it. Granted, I think the limiting factor would be that I'd only count meaningful interaction with those whom the uratha is directly partnering with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:27:04-07:00","id":1510993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1510941#post1510941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf is in a polyamorous relationship, can all of their lovers count as one touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Old Gang&quot; is an example Physical Touchstone. Yes, if the polycule keeps you from slipping too far away from humanity and civilization and provides a source of dramatic tension it can be a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:11:13-07:00","id":1511000,"title":"","content":"Speaking of touchstones, do other supernatural beings like mages, vampires, demons count as spirit or flesh touchstones, or can they be either? In addition, could a human involved in the spirit world in some way such as a shaman, a hunter, exorcist etc. count as a spiritual touchstone?<br /> <br /> If a pack of werewolves is subordinate to another pack, do they count as two separate packs or one pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","user":"cybirddude","date":". 05-07-2023, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:50:36-07:00","id":1511005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1511000#post1511000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of touchstones, do other supernatural beings like mages, vampires, demons count as spirit or flesh touchstones, or can they be either? In addition, could a human involved in the spirit world in some way such as a shaman, a hunter, exorcist etc. count as a spiritual touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the major splats are too <i>involved</i> in the supernatural to count as Flesh Touchstones, personally; Flesh Touchstones should help to realign and remind the uratha of their roots in humanity, rather than simply a touchstone that is or used to be human. However, I <i>could</i> see a location or support group-style organization that reaches out to different supernatural entities like vampires, werewolves etc. to help them adjust to continuing the human aspect of their lives and get them back on track if they get too lost, but that would be due to the human-centric ideals and mission statement of such a group rather than the individual members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1511000#post1511000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a pack of werewolves is subordinate to another pack, do they count as two separate packs or one pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would count as two separate packs, as they would have two different totems, with the totem of the subordinate pack likely also being subordinate to the superior pack's totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:31:54-07:00","id":1511361,"title":"","content":"Can the Pack Kin ability be used on supernatural animals (for example ghouled animals, nonsapient hobgoblins, Manticores, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T12:13:03-07:00","id":1511396,"title":"","content":"I would generally allow it to work. Human ghouls, deviants, etc can all join a pack after all. If I were running the game you might enter clash of wills against a ghoul animal since you're trying to make them loyal to you while the blood bond / animalism makes them loyal to / obey to their master.<br /> <br /> ETA: The above is only for manticores and ghouls, I know nothing about hobgoblin animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:57:09-07:00","id":1511412,"title":"","content":"Can a werewolf have a touchstone that is a friendly rival (i.e. a rival pack in a protectorate, a romantic rival who doesn't go too far, a business rival who practices healthy competition etc.)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T15:11:40-07:00","id":1511413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1511412#post1511412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a werewolf have a touchstone that is a friendly rival (i.e. a rival pack in a protectorate, a romantic rival who doesn't go too far, a business rival who practices healthy competition etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's not particularly wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T18:05:17-07:00","id":1511420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1511412#post1511412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a werewolf have a touchstone that is a friendly rival (i.e. a rival pack in a protectorate, a romantic rival who doesn't go too far, a business rival who practices healthy competition etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does dedicating attention to the friendly rival pull the werewolf toward the Shadow or the Flesh in a way that brings conflict to the character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T14:18:40-07:00","id":1512148,"title":"","content":"Some questions about food<br /> <br /> 1: Does seafood/fish count as &quot;meat&quot; for primal urge purposes?<br /> <br /> 2: Can werewolves gain essence from formerly human or partly human supernaturals (i e. vampires, deviants, changelings etc.)?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b3: Do meat eating supernaturals count as &quot;predator meat?&quot;<br /> <br /> 4: Does eating formerly or partly human supernaturals violate the Oath tenet that says to not eat human meat?<br /> <br /> 5: Can werewolves gain essence from ephemeral entities other than spirits (i.e. ghosts, angels, goetia etc.)?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T15:38:58-07:00","id":1512154,"title":"","content":"<i>1) Fish are made of meat, yes. <br /> <br /> 2) DM dependent, but I would say yes.<br /> <br /> 3) Like what?<br /> <br /> 4) Should be the same answer as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/2\" >Onyx Path</a> <br /> <br /> 5) I would say no. Taking essence from spirits only happens with the sacred hunt and is tied to Father Wolf's purpose. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T16:11:12-07:00","id":1512156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512154#post1512154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>1) Fish are made of meat, yes.<br /> <br /> 2) DM dependent, but I would say yes.<br /> <br /> 3) Like what?<br /> <br /> 4) Should be the same answer as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/2\" >Onyx Path</a><br /> <br /> 5) I would say no. Taking essence from spirits only happens with the sacred hunt and is tied to Father Wolf's purpose. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>For 3, At a certain level on primal urge, werewolves must eat predator meat; normally this would apply to predatory animals like tigers, frogs, or snakes. I was asking if creatures like vampires, man-eating Beasts, or a predator Claimed would count as predator meat.<br /> <br /> For 4, I can't see the answer from the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","user":"cybirddude","date":". 05-19-2023, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T17:00:21-07:00","id":1512160,"title":"","content":"If it kills to eat, it's probably a predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:44:29-07:00","id":1512173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512160#post1512160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it kills to eat, it's probably a predator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think eating partially human or formerly human supernatural creatures (i.e vampires, claimed, deviants etc.) counts as violating the oath of the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T20:03:21-07:00","id":1512182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512156#post1512156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For 3, At a certain level on primal urge, werewolves must eat predator meat; normally this would apply to predatory animals like tigers, frogs, or snakes. I was asking if creatures like vampires, man-eating Beasts, or a predator Claimed would count as predator meat.<br /> <br /> For 4, I can't see the answer from the link.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why that's a link, I tried to say it's the same as number 2. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And for number 3 I would say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T20:56:41-07:00","id":1512183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512173#post1512173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think eating partially human or formerly human supernatural creatures (i.e vampires, claimed, deviants etc.) counts as violating the oath of the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it has Dread Powers (or is a Splat) then it's probably divorced enough from humanity to not fall under the aegis of the Oath. That being said, my knowledge of Werewolf is extremely limited","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T02:49:54-07:00","id":1512198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512173#post1512173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think eating partially human or formerly human supernatural creatures (i.e vampires, claimed, deviants etc.) counts as violating the oath of the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this dilemma came up in my Werewolf campaign, where the pack - uratha who had First Changed in the last six months - hunted and killed a decades old Claimed that was living in a nearby lake and discussed the ethics of eating its flesh, since it <i>was </i>once human. For the time being, I've allowed that tenet of the Oath to be interpreted how the pack's Elodoth wants so long as their reasoning is consistent. <i>I </i>wouldn't punish them for it, personally, since Claimed are seen as different enough from humans to be deemed as different types of sacred prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T04:28:35-07:00","id":1512204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512182#post1512182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea why that's a link, I tried to say it's the same as number 2.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And for number 3 I would say yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wrote &quot;#2&quot; which autolinks to what I think is post number 2 on this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T07:25:19-07:00","id":1512213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512204#post1512204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You wrote &quot;#2&quot; which autolinks to what I think is post number 2 on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had no idea that was how that worked, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T12:56:15-07:00","id":1512377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512198#post1512198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, this dilemma came up in my Werewolf campaign, where the pack - uratha who had First Changed in the last six months - hunted and killed a decades old Claimed that was living in a nearby lake and discussed the ethics of eating its flesh, since it <i>was </i>once human. For the time being, I've allowed that tenet of the Oath to be interpreted how the pack's Elodoth wants so long as their reasoning is consistent. <i>I </i>wouldn't punish them for it, personally, since Claimed are seen as different enough from humans to be deemed as different types of sacred prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>So hypothetically speaking, if a group of werewolves agree that claimed were not human, could they say, allow spirits to claim people, then eat the Claimed? After all, there is no tenet in the Oath of the Moon that says you <i>have</i> to prevent spirits from claiming people or that says you <i>can't</i> help a spirit Claim someone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T13:03:14-07:00","id":1512379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512377#post1512377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So hypothetically speaking, if a group of werewolves agree that claimed were not human, could they say, allow spirits to claim people, then eat the Claimed? After all, there is no tenet in the Oath of the Moon that says you <i>have</i> to prevent spirits from claiming people or that says you <i>can't</i> help a spirit Claim someone...</div> </div> </div> </div>To what benefit? If claimed aren't people they aren't people for all purposes. There's no gaming the system here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T13:26:00-07:00","id":1512381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512379#post1512379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To what benefit? If claimed aren't people they aren't people for all purposes. There's no gaming the system here.</div> </div> </div> </div>1:They want to eat humans, but don't want to violate the Oath.<br /> <br /> 2: They're foodies, they let different types of spirits claim people, then eat the claimed just to see what it tastes like.<br /> <br /> 3: Because they feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T18:20:35-07:00","id":1512394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512381#post1512381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1:They want to eat humans, but don't want to violate the Oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they're out of luck. Roll twice in either direction and take your double dose of probable destabilization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: They're foodies, they let different types of spirits claim people, then eat the claimed just to see what it tastes like.<br /> <br /> 3: Because they feel like it. </div> </div> </div>Neither of these strike me as the sort of aspiration or rationale for which keeping the Oath is a priority, and in fact the mindset that holds them seriously is almost precisely descriptive of the behavior of werewolves who've lost their balance.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon says that The Wolf Must Hunt and calls for the Forsaken to Respect Their Prey. It forbids the consumption of human flesh and commands them to cleave to humanity. If they're eating something that looks and acts like a human person and gaining Essence for it, they're succumbing to the temptation that the Oath specifically forbids regardless of what metaphysical legalese you try to push it through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T19:16:09-07:00","id":1512396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1512394#post1512394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they're out of luck. Roll twice in either direction and take your double dose of probable destabilization.<br /> <br /> Neither of these strike me as the sort of aspiration or rationale for which keeping the Oath is a priority, and in fact the mindset that holds them seriously is almost precisely descriptive of the behavior of werewolves who've lost their balance.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon says that The Wolf Must Hunt and calls for the Forsaken to Respect Their Prey. It forbids the consumption of human flesh and commands them to cleave to humanity. If they're eating something that looks and acts like a human person and gaining Essence for it, they're succumbing to the temptation that the Oath specifically forbids regardless of what metaphysical legalese you try to push it through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit Jim, I'm a werewolf, not a farmer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:16:51-07:00","id":1513330,"title":"","content":"Can non-human life (i.e. animals, plants, fungi etc.) be claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:40:50-07:00","id":1513336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1513330#post1513330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can non-human life (i.e. animals, plants, fungi etc.) be claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Devourer Hounds are claimed dogs in the core rule book, and first edition had claimed trees at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T14:48:30-07:00","id":1514134,"title":"","content":"Is there anywhere that details the Shadow Ocean? I can\u2019t imagine there are many werewolves in the deep, and ocean life, especially deep ocean life, is so bizarre and alien that I\u2019m curious as to what their spirits are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T15:25:14-07:00","id":1514138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1514134#post1514134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anywhere that details the Shadow Ocean? I can\u2019t imagine there are many werewolves in the deep, and ocean life, especially deep ocean life, is so bizarre and alien that I\u2019m curious as to what their spirits are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Chris Allen's commentary on the subject is an indicator, it hasn't really been covered in the books yet, thought Chris has a fair bit of fandom writing to touch on the subject <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings/page3#post1171051\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1238295-2e-lodge-the-lodge-of-odacon\">here</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1174969-six-pups-a-changing/page2#post1175434\">here</a>. Possibly more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T10:02:26-07:00","id":1514581,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to take Spirit or Ghost allies when purchasing the Allies Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T08:02:31-07:00","id":1514701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1514581#post1514581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to take Spirit or Ghost allies when purchasing the Allies Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing forbids such! But most spirits distrust Uratha and explicitly require gathra to negotiate services from them via Social Maneuvering. This implies that, if a werewolf has a spirit or an ilthum of spirits as an instance of Allies, the werewolf has accomplished quite a feat to earn their goodwill and trust. Even if it's in the character's backstory, you should flesh it out.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are less socially restricted in-universe, but the problem is in having means to reliably contact them to keep up the bond. I don't recall anything ATM that gives werewolves reliable generic access to death-Twilight, so this will be tricky. A fetish, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:29:30-07:00","id":1514768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1514701#post1514701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing forbids such! But most spirits distrust Uratha and explicitly require gathra to negotiate services from them via Social Maneuvering. This implies that, if a werewolf has a spirit or an ilthum of spirits as an instance of Allies, the werewolf has accomplished quite a feat to earn their goodwill and trust. Even if it's in the character's backstory, you should flesh it out.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are less socially restricted in-universe, but the problem is in having means to reliably contact them to keep up the bond. I don't recall anything ATM that gives werewolves reliable generic access to death-Twilight, so this will be tricky. A fetish, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death Gift, though I've forgotten the particular Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:32:30-07:00","id":1514770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1514768#post1514768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death Gift, though I've forgotten the particular Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barghest (Glory). Why did I forget that *facepalm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:33:49-07:00","id":1514771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1514770#post1514770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Barghest (Glory). Why did I forget that *facepalm</div> </div> </div> </div>Information overload is the defense I'm playing, I think it would work for you as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T09:49:53-07:00","id":1516895,"title":"","content":"Does a fresh First Changed Uratha start with a dot in their Auspice Renown or do all werewolves start with zero renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T09:53:50-07:00","id":1516897,"title":"","content":"Werewolves right out of character creation start with 3 renown, 1 for tribe, 1 for auspice, and 1 of choice. Unless they're a ghost wolf. <br /> <br /> The book doesn't get more particular than that about the exact moment the renown is assigned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T10:02:59-07:00","id":1516898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1516897#post1516897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves right out of character creation start with 3 renown, 1 for tribe, 1 for auspice, and 1 of choice. Unless they're a ghost wolf.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't get more particular than that about the exact moment the renown is assigned.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book implies at that point, your character has been a werewolf for awhile. What I mean is right after the First change, as in that night you wake up under your Auspice moon covered in blood and guts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T21:56:37-07:00","id":1516945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1516898#post1516898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book implies at that point, your character has been a werewolf for awhile. What I mean is right after the First change, as in that night you wake up under your Auspice moon covered in blood and guts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And per &quot;Gaining Gifts and Facets&quot; in the Gifts section, you get your first Moon Gift when you get your auspice; like any other Gift, you can't have a Facet you don't have dots in the Renown for, so logically the auspice comes with the first dot of its related Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T06:25:46-07:00","id":1516966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1516898#post1516898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book implies at that point, your character has been a werewolf for awhile. What I mean is right after the First change, as in that night you wake up under your Auspice moon covered in blood and guts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any reference to back this up with, but I'm pretty sure it's just the first dot of the Auspice Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T08:46:13-07:00","id":1516974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1516945#post1516945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And per &quot;Gaining Gifts and Facets&quot; in the Gifts section, you get your first Moon Gift when you get your auspice; like any other Gift, you can't have a Facet you don't have dots in the Renown for, so logically the auspice comes with the first dot of its related Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought. Was reading some 1st Edition weirdness and I just wanted to be sure. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T21:24:12-07:00","id":1517679,"title":"","content":"How common and how extreme are time-dilation effects within the Shadow, isolated strangenesses and Places-That-Aren't notwithstanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T22:12:20-07:00","id":1517683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1517679#post1517679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How common and how extreme are time-dilation effects within the Shadow, isolated strangenesses and Places-That-Aren't notwithstanding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much I suspect, with the Hedge having seized most of the \u2018lost in time\u2019 tropes in a meta pov. I\u2019d say most of the time shenanigans in the Shadow happen through influences of celestial spirits; Helions, Lunes, and the planetary angels. Idigam, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T16:47:41-07:00","id":1517719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1517683#post1517683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much I suspect, with the Hedge having seized most of the \u2018lost in time\u2019 tropes in a meta pov. I\u2019d say most of the time shenanigans in the Shadow happen through influences of celestial spirits; Helions, Lunes, and the planetary angels. Idigam, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, I'm asking about stuff in a wider range of possibility than full-on &quot;missing time&quot; stuff \u2014 I broadly recall but cannot presently produce a citation for cases of time in the Shadow being subject to the same aggregated shifts from perception and memory for time as for space, such that places in which time feels like it passes faster or slower or inconsistently actually do have a somewhat different progression of time to other places.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly wondering (especially given that we have the Lodge of the Clocktower and the Tindalosi as published but undetailed groups in-setting) if people think this kind of distortion is limited to unusual areas or present to some (often indistinguishable) degree basically everywhere with only notable examples standing out, and to what extent such a distortion not sustained by an effect, artifact, actor, or arrangement can actually stretch or squash the flow of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T19:36:56-07:00","id":1517730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1517719#post1517719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, I'm asking about stuff in a wider range of possibility than full-on &quot;missing time&quot; stuff \u2014 I broadly recall but cannot presently produce a citation for cases of time in the Shadow being subject to the same aggregated shifts from perception and memory for time as for space, such that places in which time feels like it passes faster or slower or inconsistently actually do have a somewhat different progression of time to other places.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly wondering (especially given that we have the Lodge of the Clocktower and the Tindalosi as published but undetailed groups in-setting) if people think this kind of distortion is limited to unusual areas or present to some (often indistinguishable) degree basically everywhere with only notable examples standing out, and to what extent such a distortion not sustained by an effect, artifact, actor, or arrangement can actually stretch or squash the flow of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, without canon examples, I\u2019d restrict such to a few hours at most without intervention, but make seconds and minutes widespread throughout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T18:55:11-07:00","id":1518341,"title":"","content":"The core books says that using the Unfetter manifestation only temporarily disconnects a Spirit from it's host and that if its not back within range of its fetter by scene's end, it goes dormant. Is there anyway for a Spirit to voluntarily end the Fetter permanently without going dormant or having to kill the host?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T20:04:26-07:00","id":1518344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1518341#post1518341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core books says that using the Unfetter manifestation only temporarily disconnects a Spirit from it's host and that if its not back within range of its fetter by scene's end, it goes dormant. Is there anyway for a Spirit to voluntarily end the Fetter permanently without going dormant or having to kill the host?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corebook also says a spirit can voluntarily end the Fettered Condition by using the Unfetter Manifestation, which I think it is reasonable to interpret as a different but identically-priced application to the &quot;temporarily suppresses the Condition&quot; option described on the Manifestation table.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you have Unfetter, you can either totally end the Fettered Condition (and need to spend the Essence in order to re-apply it later) or you can temporarily suppress it for the scene and regain its benefits at the end as long as you're back in range in time.<br /> <br /> Answering your question more literally, getting rid of the supporting Resonant or Open Conditions ends the Fettered Condition as normal for Manifestations in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T10:37:16-07:00","id":1522101,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves suffer the long term effects from smoking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T10:42:58-07:00","id":1522104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522101#post1522101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves suffer the long term effects from smoking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. They reduce toxicity by Primal Urge, and regenerate physical damages that would be permanent for regular humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T13:56:19-07:00","id":1522118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522101#post1522101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves suffer the long term effects from smoking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely consider smoking, unless you're smoking roll your owns with home grown tobacco, the same as eating processed food for breaking points on harmony 3 or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:03:45-07:00","id":1522122,"title":"","content":"If the gauntlet is a sundering consequence, does the gauntlet only exist in the earth's vicinity? Or gauntlet is a normal state and Pangea just...remove/open it in these times?<br /> <br /> And if the gauntlet is universal, without human activity outside moon orbit, will the gauntlet strength will be lower? Or high since not much essence is created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13664-jack-cross","name":"Jack Cross","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:06:16-07:00","id":1522123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522101#post1522101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves suffer the long term effects from smoking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to check Blood of the Wolf to be sure, but as a general rule, no-one of the catches to having a body that is effectively always regenerating is that a lot of the little damages that acumulate and get worse for humans doesn't really apply.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522118#post1522118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would definitely consider smoking, unless you're smoking roll your owns with home grown tobacco, the same as eating processed food for breaking points on harmony 3 or less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I feel needs to be noted, in the wake of the fishing thread, should again be noted as more a <i>good</i> thing when you're in a situation to take advantage of that breaking point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack Cross</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522122#post1522122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the gauntlet is a sundering consequence, does the gauntlet only exist in the earth's vicinity? Or gauntlet is a normal state and Pangea just...remove/open it in these times?<br /> <br /> And if the gauntlet is universal, without human activity outside moon orbit, will the gauntlet strength will be lower? Or high since not much essence is created?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this take is going to be dependent on how serious you take Infinite Macabre as a source of information given that it is a setting shard, but the implication is that the Sundering is a Cosmic level event, and the the Gauntlet is the....unnatural(?)* result that everyone deals with, because the Gauntlet still exists in Infinite Macabre(and suggestions that cosmologies are mixed only extend the Shadow into the Between Space, which is the setting specific Warp Solution), albeit at a truly low state (any attempt to cross over gains a +3 bonus).<br /> <br /> *THere's other elements of the setting that lay the development of the Gauntlet as inevitable along the death of Wolf and the end of the Border Marches as the Border Marches, in which case the Gauntlet is natural, but there's a vast cosmological argument that is the realm of fruitless academics and individual tables.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-05-2023, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:11:34-07:00","id":1522125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522123#post1522123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .Which I feel needs to be noted, in the wake of the fishing thread, should again be noted as more a <i>good</i> thing when you're in a situation to take advantage of that breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That entirely depends upon where you think the optimal harmony score is. Sure, 5 has a lot of advantages, but being able to nope out and cross the gauntlet to exit the physical world at will is REALLY nice. (But realistically if you're spending enough time on the physical to abuse that ability you're going to have a tough time hitting 3 most likely anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:16:28-07:00","id":1522126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1522125#post1522125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That entirely depends upon where you think the optimal harmony score is. Sure, 5 has a lot of advantages, but being able to nope out and cross the gauntlet to exit the physical world at will is REALLY nice. (But realistically if you're spending enough time on the physical to abuse that ability you're going to have a tough time hitting 3 most likely anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, it depends on what you're trying to get out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T05:49:49-07:00","id":1523459,"title":"","content":"Why did the Gurdilag hit where and when it did? Was it just because they wanted to do the Hunting Ground book or was it because of some tie between Colorado and the Moon Landing in 05?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T07:00:21-07:00","id":1523819,"title":"","content":"What happens if a thing's spirit is killed? (As in permanently killed, not just discoporated.) Does a new spirit come into existence for the thing over time? Does the thing wither and break down? Does another similar spirit just move in and feed on that thing's resonance? <br /> <br /> Also, vice versa, what happens to a spirit if it's thing is destroyed? (Thinking like cars and trees and animals here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T08:18:48-07:00","id":1523824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1523819#post1523819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a thing's spirit is killed? (As in permanently killed, not just discoporated.) Does a new spirit come into existence for the thing over time? Does the thing wither and break down? Does another similar spirit just move in and feed on that thing's resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last one, usually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, vice versa, what happens to a spirit if it's thing is destroyed? (Thinking like cars and trees and animals here.) </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spirit \u2014 1e suggests in places that some spirits are too much The Spirit Of Their Origin to survive and seek out similar Resonance \u2014 but unless it's very weak and unable to find a replacement food source they're liable to start looking as long as the spirit was either already awake or was shocked out of its original dormancy by the destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T14:52:19-07:00","id":1523887,"title":"","content":"Can Uratha cause aggravated damage to wolf spirits by eating their flesh/corpus, or does this only work on mundane wolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T18:35:08-07:00","id":1523895,"title":"","content":"I would say only on actual wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T00:17:52-07:00","id":1523904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1523887#post1523887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Uratha cause aggravated damage to wolf spirits by eating their flesh/corpus, or does this only work on mundane wolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they outrank the spirit by 2 rank levels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T04:08:08-07:00","id":1523910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1523904#post1523904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if they outrank the spirit by 2 rank levels</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they deal aggravated damage by virtue of being the spirit's Bane. They still don't get any Essence from it unlike regular wolves, and don't face the associated breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T17:30:36-07:00","id":1524023,"title":"","content":"Could a lone Uratha, a couple of Wolf-blooded and humans, and a Spirit-Brood make a viable Pack complete with Totem? If so, are the Spirits able to purchase the Totem Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T18:30:42-07:00","id":1524025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524023#post1524023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could a lone Uratha, a couple of Wolf-blooded and humans, and a Spirit-Brood make a viable Pack complete with Totem? If so, are the Spirits able to purchase the Totem Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could that make a pack? Yeah, easy peasy, lemon squeezy.<br /> <br /> Can spirits purchase the Totem Merit?<br /> <br /> Errrr. Mostly no, with an indulgence for an edge understanding.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, the Totem Merit is representative of the work it takes to feed and maintain the totem spirit or otherwise work to advance it-packs are pretty effectively the spirit brood for the totem, just with an understanding of mutual operation between the actors rather than a predatorial hierarchy. Conventionally, this evolves from the fact that the Uratha are usually present and able to object to power imbalances with reason, empathy, and also being apex predators who originally hunted gods, but can generally also accomodate the scraps of power that the Wolf-Blooded or humans can bring to bear with the totem to maintain an equitable relationship, particularly if Moon intercedes and grants her own power and authority to those Wolf-Blooded and humans (ala Moon's Grace from the Pack). And otherwise on all fronts, it also means the pack is conventionally keeping up the gathra to keep the totem sated<br /> <br /> Spirits have a different relationship to the totem, and there's no getting around it-either the spirits don't have any adjacency to the ilthum of the Totem and therefore just basically <i>can't</i> offer the gathra that merits the carrot of the relationship with the Totem, or the spirits are effectively of the Totem's brood and already giving it up as lower entities on the food web with the totem. It's a little....out there to suggest that spirits can basically do the things that having the Totem Merit means since it doesn't really reflect that. It's just dynamically a different operation that doesn't have the advantage of dis-similarity to make the wedge case for the Merit's operation.<br /> <br /> That said, if someone really wanted to argue that the pack's spirit brood side of things was doing enough that merits the contribution of gathra and cultivating Resonance that they are elevating the Totem and should be reaping benefits beyond sloppy seconds and not being the meal for the night, and more importantly the play group was willing to break some of the playstyle and feel of Forsaken to just enjoy the power of it all, then there are certainly more egregious things you could do than that-though I would argue on principle that Moon's Grace should be maxed out first before making that decision.<br /> <br /> On the whole though, no, I would lean towards spirits being unable to purchase Totem. It doesn't make sense within the lore, and mechanically it's just shortcutting past the gameplay that comes either frontloading the totem at character creation and setting up the upkeep as a conflict point or taking the time to grow the totem with the rest of the pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T19:02:09-07:00","id":1524026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524023#post1524023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could a lone Uratha, a couple of Wolf-blooded and humans, and a Spirit-Brood make a viable Pack complete with Totem? If so, are the Spirits able to purchase the Totem Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth pointing out that in addition to Arc's points that spirits have no way to gain merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T19:52:06-07:00","id":1524029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524026#post1524026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth pointing out that in addition to Arc's points that spirits have no way to gain merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be mildly fair on this one, a lot of fans have taken the basic setup of the Absent from Geist and applied it to spirits, mixing in the rules for Totem Advancement from The Pack. It happens enough I usually assume most people are working from that basis instead of &quot;Spirits haven't been made playable in the books.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, yep, that is a problem, particularly if you want to play canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T12:42:56-07:00","id":1524878,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the ghouls book and wondered why it was that they are seemingly the only &quot;minion&quot; splat that got a supplement all their own. What I really liked about that book, and Half Damned, was that it really fleshed them out and grew into their own rather than &quot;vampire lite&quot;. <br /> <br /> How do yall do the same with wilf blooded? I aint asking if a book is being made, I'm just wondering how yall futher give them an identity beyond werewolves who can't change<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T13:30:00-07:00","id":1524881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524878#post1524878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the ghouls book and wondered why it was that they are seemingly the only &quot;minion&quot; splat that got a supplement all their own. What I really liked about that book, and Half Damned, was that it really fleshed them out and grew into their own rather than &quot;vampire lite&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, it's because Sleepwalkers run the gamut from Second Sight characters to Literally Just Some Guy (ability to gaze upon the sacred without profaning it notwithstanding) and wolf-blooded didn't have Tells until this edition and so all their relevant material fit into their parts of Blood of the Wolf. Ghouls can be made at will, have access to Disciplines, serve as a vampire's daytime arms and legs, and are more likely to be deeply fucked-up than most other dyad splats, which, coupled with the more direct &quot;they're from the gameline that corresponds to the World of Darkness franchise's best-known gameline&quot; thing, gives them a lot more mechanical and narrative content to build a whole book out of in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do yall do the same with wilf blooded? I aint asking if a book is being made, I'm just wondering how yall futher give them an identity beyond werewolves who can't change </div> </div> </div>Expanding on Tells, the expansion of the pack, and other stuff like Pack Rites being usable by the right subset of them, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T13:52:31-07:00","id":1524882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524878#post1524878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the ghouls book and wondered why it was that they are seemingly the only &quot;minion&quot; splat that got a supplement all their own. What I really liked about that book, and Half Damned, was that it really fleshed them out and grew into their own rather than &quot;vampire lite&quot;.<br /> <br /> How do yall do the same with wilf blooded? I aint asking if a book is being made, I'm just wondering how yall futher give them an identity beyond werewolves who can't change</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are humans purposefully turned to serve a vampire and given power through that vampire's blood while the wolf blooded, on the other hand, are more often born to their position and are virtually never made intentionally. There isn't any controlling what powers they develop, nor are their powers always powers, many times they're just drawbacks with a slight upside. Nor can a Uratha pick the right individual for the right job, nor do Uratha have holes to fill like the vampires do their daylight hours. Lastly, and probably my favorite thing about the wolf blooded, they're pack members, not lackeys. All of that is to say, wolf blooded are individuals, they're not defined by their Uratha the way a ghoul is defined by their vampire and while everyone benefits from being an individual rather than &quot;generic ghoul A&quot; wolf blooded pretty much should always be individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T18:33:05-07:00","id":1524894,"title":"","content":"Do the shapeshifting forms take the uratha's attributes above what is noted as their maximum due to their Primal Urge? I haven't seen any direct ruling that says that they go beyond their Primal Urge imposed maximum, but it would seem silly that they wouldn't. This also goes for any Gifts that increase the uratha's attributes, since some don't explicitly state that they go beyond the normal limit unlike in Vampire and Mage. Any clarification would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T18:49:44-07:00","id":1524896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1524894#post1524894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the shapeshifting forms take the uratha's attributes above what is noted as their maximum due to their Primal Urge? I haven't seen any direct ruling that says that they go beyond their Primal Urge imposed maximum, but it would seem silly that they wouldn't. This also goes for any Gifts that increase the uratha's attributes, since some don't explicitly state that they go beyond the normal limit unlike in Vampire and Mage. Any clarification would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking across the franchise, unless a power or ability specifically states that it can't take an Attribute above the character's Supernatural Potency-based maximum, it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T14:28:08-08:00","id":1525133,"title":"","content":"Is the Locust Host effecting the Gauntlet retconned? I highly doubt since they are a Host, but it's strange that night horrors doesn't go over it (unless I've forgotten) while The Pack briefly mentions it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T17:26:11-08:00","id":1525139,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it is retconned, 2nd edition is a fairly different game than 1e, and that is especially true of the Hosts. That said, as one of the defining traits of the Hosts is messing with the Gauntlet and that it is stated they have that power in The Pack I would lean towards this being an accidental omission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T22:18:53-08:00","id":1525154,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable. Personally I like to think the Gauntlet becomes a danger zone where crossing risks being eaten by locusts.<br /> <br /> I do wonder what the honey thing implies for the origins of the locust hosts. Certainly isn't something you'd think they have. Wonder what their progenitor was like. Wouldn't be the first time one had powers adjacent to its themes (like the Plague king and his mad prophetic ability)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T11:56:02-08:00","id":1525383,"title":"","content":"Are there are any Gifts or merits that increase a werewolf's Defense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T16:43:53-08:00","id":1525390,"title":"","content":"I cannot think of anything that increases the defense stat universally and directly, but they have a plethora of defensive gifts and merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T19:12:19-08:00","id":1525392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1525383#post1525383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there are any Gifts or merits that increase a werewolf's Defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instinctive Defense allows you to calculate your Defense in wolf and near-wolf form using the higher of your Wits and Dexterity, and both of those forms add 2 to your base Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T08:33:23-08:00","id":1526320,"title":"","content":"So I'm working with MrGone's character sheet and I notice height and weight for the various forms. I'm someone who likes knowing how tall or heavy their character is for scenes when such would be referenced. <br /> <br /> So would this be right? (Werewolf forms start in the 2ed book page 96) <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dalu</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1.5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1.5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Gauru</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Urshul</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Urhan</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">??</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">??</td> </tr> </table></div> Or am I mistaken on my math in places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T09:54:14-08:00","id":1526324,"title":"","content":"With something like that I don't think there really is a right or wrong, it's left open enough for people to put their own spin on it. I believe Urshul is generally as big as a pony (or maybe a grown horse) if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T20:45:17-08:00","id":1526340,"title":"","content":"Do Idigam take aggravated damage from werewolves who outrank them by two like other spirits, or do they only specifically take agg from their banes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T20:55:53-08:00","id":1526341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1526340#post1526340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Idigam take aggravated damage from werewolves who outrank them by two like other spirits, or do they only specifically take agg from their banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think that\u2019s ever been mentioned. So in the absence of exceptions, I\u2019d rule that yes they do take agg from +2 Rank werewolves/spirits like any other. I don\u2019t think anything would break from that.<br /> However, I\u2019d also make the Formless an exception, since their shtick is the cannot-be-defined stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T21:02:58-08:00","id":1526342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1526340#post1526340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Idigam take aggravated damage from werewolves who outrank them by two like other spirits, or do they only specifically take agg from their banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that the weakest Formless idigam are Rank 3 and Coalescing gives an idigam an extra Rank, and bearing in mind that without Predator's Claim/Refinement of Spirit/other tricks the only way a werewolf is managing to hit that heightened floor is with a total combined Renown of <i>19 or more</i> (and Predator's Claim is costly and location-locked, Refinement of Spirit is an Ivory Claw Merit, and the main other published method is a unique phenomenon borne by a Night Horrors antagonist), I don't think anything particularly breaks from interpreting the lack of explicit statement to mean that they aren't an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T10:48:27-08:00","id":1526411,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is a question appropriate to here, but I was milling over possible rites to pick up and noticed for Hunting Ground &quot;certain rites and facets are effected by territory&quot;. The only two I could find offhand were Supplication (Rite) and boundary ward (Warding Gift - Wisdom). Was just curious if I missed any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T10:50:17-08:00","id":1526412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DioEon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1526411#post1526411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is a question appropriate to here, but I was milling over possible rites to pick up and noticed for Hunting Ground &quot;certain rites and facets are effected by territory&quot;. The only two I could find offhand were Supplication (Rite) and boundary ward (Warding Gift - Wisdom). Was just curious if I missed any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like that is often a bit of future proofing, that way if they print more rites / facets later the groundwork has already been laid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T11:27:26-08:00","id":1526415,"title":"","content":"Yea, just wanted to make sure I didn't miss anything printed. EXP Spends in a low EXP game have me sweating lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T13:25:48-08:00","id":1526417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DioEon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1526411#post1526411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is a question appropriate to here, but I was milling over possible rites to pick up and noticed for Hunting Ground &quot;certain rites and facets are effected by territory&quot;. The only two I could find offhand were Supplication (Rite) and boundary ward (Warding Gift - Wisdom). Was just curious if I missed any.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also Lore of the Land (Gift of Knowledge - Purity) and Read the World's Loom (Gift of Insight - Glory).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T07:06:23-08:00","id":1528710,"title":"","content":"I was looking at the Giver of Gifts article, but now I'm wondering, is there a similar guide for rituals somewhere? or just tips about it?<br /> <br /> The books already cover Pack Tactics and Fetish creation, and now that just got me thinking about werewolf only merits, what kind of thing should you be looking for when you want to design them?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T05:26:45-08:00","id":1530021,"title":"","content":"Can equipment, specifically mystical equipment or plans, assist in the activation rolls of gifts? For example can an Ithaeur with proper knowledge of the occult craft a piece of mystical equipment to help with the first level crescent moon gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T19:13:33-08:00","id":1530071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1530021#post1530021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can equipment, specifically mystical equipment or plans, assist in the activation rolls of gifts? For example can an Ithaeur with proper knowledge of the occult craft a piece of mystical equipment to help with the first level crescent moon gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's conceivable, but broadly speaking supernatural powers don't benefit from equipment bonuses because equipment tends to be for mundane Skill rolls whereas supernatural powers in the vein of Gifts tend to operate through channels that aren't by default assumed to be adjustable with readily-accessible materials and/or are themselves the tools being used to benefit a plan.<br /> <br /> Like, you could certainly do the legwork to justify rigging some occult nonsense to add dice to Shadow Gaze, but getting to that point in a way that justifies why other Ithaeur don't do so all the time is its own process, and no amount of planning is going to help make your werewolf eyes see into the heart of a spirit's nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T21:33:23-07:00","id":1532359,"title":"","content":"Does killing indirectly count as violating the Oath about People not Murdering the People? Some examples:<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> 1: Hiring a hitman to kill someone for you.<br /> 2: Manipulating others into doing the killing for you.<br /> 3: Working an enslaved enemy to death.<br /> 4: Starving an enemy to death.<br /> 5: Driving someone to suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T22:06:01-07:00","id":1532361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532359#post1532359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does killing indirectly count as violating the Oath about People not Murdering the People? Some examples:<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> 1: Hiring a hitman to kill someone for you.<br /> 2: Manipulating others into doing the killing for you.<br /> 3: Working an enslaved enemy to death.<br /> 4: Starving an enemy to death.<br /> 5: Driving someone to suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first, that is generally held to mean other Uratha and pack members / wolf blooded, not just humans. <br /> <br /> Secondly, if your Uratha are enslaving people your game is off the rails enough I don't think you have to split hairs over wether or not something is a violation of the oath of the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T06:46:17-07:00","id":1532374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532359#post1532359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does killing indirectly count as violating the Oath about People not Murdering the People? Some examples:<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> 1: Hiring a hitman to kill someone for you.<br /> 2: Manipulating others into doing the killing for you.<br /> 3: Working an enslaved enemy to death.<br /> 4: Starving an enemy to death.<br /> 5: Driving someone to suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your intention is to make someone die and actions you take \u2014 including incitement of other people \u2014 cause them to die, you are sufficiently involved in their death at the level of means and motive to be considered a murderer. If this were a matter of legal code we were talking about, a character might wriggle their way out of punishments specific to murder by claiming mere criminal negligence, but on the level of &quot;does this character know they're killing someone&quot; I would imagine it takes some severe distancing from the chain of events to not have &quot;I deliberately caused the death of one of the People&quot; result in the spiritual consequences of killing one of the People.<br /> <br /> Less finely-grained is the fact that &quot;the High Respect the Low&quot; means some of these are dicey methods to use in keeping with the Oath even without ending a life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T10:28:43-07:00","id":1532381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532374#post1532374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less finely-grained is the fact that &quot;the High Respect the Low&quot; means some of these are dicey methods to use in keeping with the Oath even without ending a life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Not only are these methods of killing all violations of the Oath provided they are of the People, most of them I would probably add a further stigma from your fellow People. These are not Glorious, Honorable, or Pure methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T12:59:54-07:00","id":1532385,"title":"","content":"Some clarifications about the oath about eating the flesh of humans and wolves:<br /> <br /> 1: When it comes to creatures that look like humans or can disguise themselves as humans, does eating their flesh count as a harmony violation if the werewolf believes that they're human? <br /> 2: If a werewolf is tricked into eating human or wolf flesh, do they suffer harmony violation immediately or after they find out?<br /> 3: Does eating the flesh of formerly human creatres like mummies, changelings, or vampires violate the oath?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b4: If a werewolf believes that certain groups of people (such as disabled people, people of certain races, untouchables in a caste system) are sub-human, does it count as a harmony violation if a werewolf only eats from those types of people?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T13:19:23-07:00","id":1532386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532385#post1532385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some clarifications about the oath about eating the flesh of humans and wolves:<br /> <br /> 1: When it comes to creatures that look like humans or can disguise themselves as humans, does eating their flesh count as a harmony violation if the werewolf believes that they're human?<br /> 2: If a werewolf is tricked into eating human or wolf flesh, do they suffer harmony violation immediately or after they find out?<br /> 3: Does eating the flesh of formerly human creatres like mummies, changelings, or vampires violate the oath?<br /> \u200b\u200b4: If a werewolf believes that certain groups of people (such as disabled people, people of certain races, untouchables in a caste system) are sub-human, does it count as a harmony violation if a werewolf only eats from those types of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're getting Essence from eating them, it counts, no two ways about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T13:25:29-07:00","id":1532387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532385#post1532385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b4: If a werewolf believes that certain groups of people (such as disabled people, people of certain races, untouchables in a caste system) are sub-human, does it count as a harmony violation if a werewolf only eats from those types of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have this going on I'd say you have either a player problem or a storyteller problem not a rules problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T03:08:42-07:00","id":1532428,"title":"","content":"I just had the craziest idea and I wanted to run it by you guys. So you got a werewolf and a demon.<br /> <br /> Werewolf goes Gauru and kills someone (like a mind controlled worker). Another worker gets freed from mind control and freaks out about dead friend. Demon then comes in and is like \u201chey, wanna forget what you just saw? Wanna forget your friend died from a weird bear attack? Sign here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Is that\u2026 \u201clegal\u201d? Like I feel like it shouldn\u2019t be \u2018legal\u2019 but i can\u2019t think of any reasons why aside from \u201csupernatural exploit\u201d (kinda funny given what Demon powers are called but I digress).<br /> <br /> <br /> For MY game I\u2019m not exactly planning on abusing it like crazy, and I can always say doing this too much could require compromise rolls (regardless of cover), maybe even a breaking point towards spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T05:38:50-07:00","id":1532432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532428#post1532428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had the craziest idea and I wanted to run it by you guys. So you got a werewolf and a demon.<br /> <br /> Werewolf goes Gauru and kills someone (like a mind controlled worker). Another worker gets freed from mind control and freaks out about dead friend. Demon then comes in and is like \u201chey, wanna forget what you just saw? Wanna forget your friend died from a weird bear attack? Sign here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Is that\u2026 \u201clegal\u201d? Like I feel like it shouldn\u2019t be \u2018legal\u2019 but i can\u2019t think of any reasons why aside from \u201csupernatural exploit\u201d (kinda funny given what Demon powers are called but I digress).</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the thing you are asking about the legality of in this situation? Lunacy deals with most memories of hybrid forms and demons using pacts to relieve someone of their memories do so by the other party writing an account of the events to be forgotten, which means the information is still out there and the fuzzy borders of The Herd Must Not Know come into play re: &quot;someone has written down their nightmarish encounter with the killing form of a practicing werewolf.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T21:30:11-07:00","id":1532476,"title":"","content":"What exactly does a Geryo look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T21:37:54-07:00","id":1532477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1532476#post1532476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly does a Geryo look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Geryo are all unique beings, they don't have a singular look. There are examples in Shunned by the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T01:50:01-07:00","id":1533686,"title":"","content":"So, bit of a question of interpretation re: the Gift of the Elementals that came up in my game. Players were looking at permanent Create Influence, and basically asking whether it works more as 'you create an example of the thing, which hangs around', or 'you create a font of the thing'. So, for instance, if you Create Water, could you create a spring that persistently brings forth water, or only a certain volume of water? You can create fire sourcelessly with Influence (Fire), but would that fire then keep burning without fuel, or just behave like normal fire from that point - what would a 'permanent' duration mean in that instance?<br /> <br /> There's also the question of how broadly to interpret an Influence - e.g. does Influence (Fire) let you control or create heat, independent of literal flames?<br /> <br /> I'm basically just wondering if there's any official, or just common, rulings on these issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T07:09:59-07:00","id":1533695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1533686#post1533686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, bit of a question of interpretation re: the Gift of the Elementals that came up in my game. Players were looking at permanent Create Influence, and basically asking whether it works more as 'you create an example of the thing, which hangs around', or 'you create a font of the thing'. So, for instance, if you Create Water, could you create a spring that persistently brings forth water, or only a certain volume of water? You can create fire sourcelessly with Influence (Fire), but would that fire then keep burning without fuel, or just behave like normal fire from that point - what would a 'permanent' duration mean in that instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral beings being called that for a reason and the overall flow of Essence within the social spaces of the Shadow toward maintaining and adjusting the state of things, I would say that using Mass Create Influence's permanent instance effect does as it describes rather than creating an immediate source of more than one instance of the thing; this is a power from the toolkit of spirits adapted for werewolf use.<br /> <br /> &quot;Permanent&quot; means it lasts as long as it would typically exist instead of one/ten minutes per success as is normal for things generated by Create and Mass Create Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the question of how broadly to interpret an Influence - e.g. does Influence (Fire) let you control or create heat, independent of literal flames? </div> </div> </div>There's the precedent of writers discussing fairly broad application of Influences by spirits (for instance, a spirit of hunger making weapons eat through their ammunition at a faster rate) and the way the Resonant Condition works doesn't exactly seem to discourage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T20:23:46-07:00","id":1535156,"title":"","content":"Two questions!<br /> <br /> <b>1</b> - About auspices. I know that there is huge differences between auspices from WtA and from WtF. In WtA I played mostly as a Ragabash, but usually more focused on the social/face of the party side of things. Spying to learn secrets and hoard information, making jokes to lift the pack's spirits, and questioning the status quo and the leaders to improve decisions.<br /> Which Auspice from WtF would fill this niche better? The Irraka feel too much like an assassin, and that's it. Maybe the Cahalith?<br /> <br /> <b>2</b> - Is it possible to have a fetish that grants Influence 5? Could a Fetish grow? Like, a level 1 Fetish is constantly being fed Essence that it's spirit grow in rank, becoming then a level 2 Fetish? (I mean, with xp being paid, and quests done to justify it, and justify even a good relation and connection between the Uratha and the Spirit...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T20:52:08-07:00","id":1535157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535156#post1535156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions!<br /> <br /> <b>1</b> - About auspices. I know that there is huge differences between auspices from WtA and from WtF. In WtA I played mostly as a Ragabash, but usually more focused on the social/face of the party side of things. Spying to learn secrets and hoard information, making jokes to lift the pack's spirits, and questioning the status quo and the leaders to improve decisions.<br /> Which Auspice from WtF would fill this niche better? The Irraka feel too much like an assassin, and that's it. Maybe the Cahalith?<br /> <br /> <b>2</b> - Is it possible to have a fetish that grants Influence 5? Could a Fetish grow? Like, a level 1 Fetish is constantly being fed Essence that it's spirit grow in rank, becoming then a level 2 Fetish? (I mean, with xp being paid, and quests done to justify it, and justify even a good relation and connection between the Uratha and the Spirit...)</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Remember WtF isn't Werewolf the Apocalypse, it's much more about a hunt than an eternal war and jokester isn't really a necessary role. Cahalith is the most likely to improve the mood, while any might be a spy. <br /> <br /> 2) Yes, influence = fetish level is a suggested option. Spirits inside fetishes don't grow typically but if you want it in your story go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T21:25:22-07:00","id":1535158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535156#post1535156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1</b> - About auspices. I know that there is huge differences between auspices from WtA and from WtF. In WtA I played mostly as a Ragabash, but usually more focused on the social/face of the party side of things. Spying to learn secrets and hoard information, making jokes to lift the pack's spirits, and questioning the status quo and the leaders to improve decisions.<br /> Which Auspice from WtF would fill this niche better? The Irraka feel too much like an assassin, and that's it. Maybe the Cahalith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs of the Moon is from 1e but dedicates a section or two of its Irraka chapter to discussing the auspice's role in testing and questioning established traditions. &quot;Making jokes to lift the pack's spirits&quot; doesn't really have an enshrined auspice role in Forsaken, but the kit most suited to inspiration and morale-boosting effects comes from the Cahalith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2</b> - Is it possible to have a fetish that grants Influence 5? </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, given that the non-exhaustive list of possible effects puts &quot;a moderate Influence at three dots&quot; as a three-dot effect and one of the sample four-dot fetishes grants four dots of Influence (Birds).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a Fetish grow? Like, a level 1 Fetish is constantly being fed Essence that it's spirit grow in rank, becoming then a level 2 Fetish? </div> </div> </div>Given that the spirit in a fetish is largely asleep, feeding Essence powers its abilities, and fetishes are the product of a binding ritual, to say nothing of how spirit growth thresholds aren't mechanically defined and most effects last longer than would justify pumping Essence into the fetish very frequently outside of extreme circumstances \u2014 if you want your item powered by a hibernating spirit to be stronger, it's typically more expedient to make a new fetish by binding the spirit or a new one of similar type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I mean, with xp being paid, and quests done to justify it, and justify even a good relation and connection between the Uratha and the Spirit...) </div> </div> </div>In addition to the above, fetishes aren't Merits nor purchased with Experiences, though Lore of the Forsaken has an interesting section on (1e's mechanics for) fetishes that might be work looking at for inspiration regarding other benefits for maintaining and caring for fetishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T08:54:33-07:00","id":1535173,"title":"","content":"Can a Fetish be a Tattoo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T10:59:34-07:00","id":1535178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535173#post1535173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Fetish be a Tattoo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending new releases to the contrary, yes, fetish tattoos are also discussed in Lore of the Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T19:50:57-07:00","id":1535319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535173#post1535173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Fetish be a Tattoo?</div> </div> </div> </div>In WW:tA, we had all binded objects as tattoos, so many WW had tattoos of klaives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T02:06:52-07:00","id":1535407,"title":"","content":"New Storyteller here looking for advice! Is it me or Killer Instinct is a little busted for being a starting gift for Rahu? The Rahu of my party activates this gift at the start of the combat and basically one tap everything he has in front without too much effort. How do you deal with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28474-tzasstan91","name":"Tzasstan91","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28474_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T05:29:48-07:00","id":1535409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzasstan91</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535407#post1535407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Storyteller here looking for advice! Is it me or Killer Instinct is a little busted for being a starting gift for Rahu? The Rahu of my party activates this gift at the start of the combat and basically one tap everything he has in front without too much effort. How do you deal with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>8-again is generally overrated, on average gaining 8-again on a dicepool of 10 amounts to around 3 extra dice, which is roughly 1 extra success (it's slightly less than that, but close enough). If your Rahu is one tapping everything without much effort they would probably do the same without KI because they're built for combat. <br /> <br /> Now how you deal with a character built for combat is a question people have been asking since the dawn of RPGs. Generally there's several ways. <br /> <br /> First, let them be good at combat. It's what they're meant for after all and obviously a goal of the player. Don't take that away just because. <br /> <br /> Secondly, there's always someone bigger and badder. Spirits rank 4+ are near gods that typically require a pack effort to defeat. Claimed are absolutely nuts. The Forsaken have a plethora of extremely powerful enemies, it's ok to use them sometimes. <br /> <br /> Third, not everything should be combat. Non-combat needs to be important as well and not just relegated to &quot;roleplay it&quot;. <br /> <br /> Fourth, if you're not in a medium that prevents cheating, watch your player's dice. I have found that many times watching a player's dice rolls dramatically reduces their &quot;one tap everything without much effort&quot; chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T10:24:13-07:00","id":1535415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1535409#post1535409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 8-again is generally overrated, on average gaining 8-again on a dicepool of 10 amounts to around 3 extra dice, which is roughly 1 extra success (it's slightly less than that, but close enough). If your Rahu is one tapping everything without much effort they would probably do the same without KI because they're built for combat.<br /> <br /> Now how you deal with a character built for combat is a question people have been asking since the dawn of RPGs. Generally there's several ways.<br /> <br /> First, let them be good at combat. It's what they're meant for after all and obviously a goal of the player. Don't take that away just because.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's always someone bigger and badder. Spirits rank 4+ are near gods that typically require a pack effort to defeat. Claimed are absolutely nuts. The Forsaken have a plethora of extremely powerful enemies, it's ok to use them sometimes.<br /> <br /> Third, not everything should be combat. Non-combat needs to be important as well and not just relegated to &quot;roleplay it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Fourth, if you're not in a medium that prevents cheating, watch your player's dice. I have found that many times watching a player's dice rolls dramatically reduces their &quot;one tap everything without much effort&quot; chances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the advice. I agree with the fact that I should let them be good. I don't want to make my player feel useless, I just want to give a fair challenge. I probably need to get more an hold of the bigger threats you mention rulewise.<br /> Aboput watching the dices closely, maybe i can give it a try in a subtle way. I don't think it's necessary but I guess there is no harm in keep an eye out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28474-tzasstan91","name":"Tzasstan91","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28474_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T11:34:39-07:00","id":1535416,"title":"","content":"One good thing about the Uratha, they are amazingly resilient. So long as you avoid giving NPCs silver weapons you'll probably not accidentally kill any PCs if they're even a little smart. (And if they're not and do something like fight a rank 5 spirit, well, they'll know better next time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T08:13:41-07:00","id":1539316,"title":"","content":"The Pure in 2nd edition do not have a numbers majority going on. I'm just wondering why that decision was made? I don't have issue with it. Just curious.<br /> <br /> Also, does it change the dynamic between the Pure and Forsaken in any way? I just know they aren't currently &quot;at war&quot; with one another","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T09:16:11-07:00","id":1539322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1539316#post1539316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure in 2nd edition do not have a numbers majority going on. I'm just wondering why that decision was made? I don't have issue with it. Just curious.<br /> <br /> Also, does it change the dynamic between the Pure and Forsaken in any way? I just know they aren't currently &quot;at war&quot; with one another</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparative numbers dynamic is a thing that later 1e made clear varies by time and place; the Brethren War was a thing going on in North America circa the mid-Aughts, but e.g. Shadows of the U.K. indicates that the Forsaken are the majority in the United Kingdom and there's a notable presence of Bale Hounds in the fens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T10:50:45-07:00","id":1539326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1539316#post1539316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure in 2nd edition do not have a numbers majority going on. I'm just wondering why that decision was made? I don't have issue with it. Just curious.<br /> <br /> Also, does it change the dynamic between the Pure and Forsaken in any way? I just know they aren't currently &quot;at war&quot; with one another</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general thing they just quit discussing numbers going into 2nd edition. There's no information saying the Pure don't outnumber the Forsaken 2:1, but as with a lot of things a lot of people carry over things that aren't explicitly contradicted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T09:54:16-07:00","id":1539642,"title":"","content":"Why do the firstborn, or at least seemingly Fenris-Ur according to the Blood Talons write-up, care about the oath of the moon? I know they are the great patrons to werewolves, but aren't themselves, not even children to Luna.<br /> <br /> Is it simply by dint of totemic relationship that they care?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T13:25:42-07:00","id":1539657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1539642#post1539642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do the firstborn, or at least seemingly Fenris-Ur according to the Blood Talons write-up, care about the oath of the moon? I know they are the great patrons to werewolves, but aren't themselves, not even children to Luna.<br /> <br /> Is it simply by dint of totemic relationship that they care?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not as front-and-center as it is in, say, Changeling, but spiritual society as a reflection of the Flesh runs on oaths \u2014 it is, in no small way, how Rites work. Spirits keep agreements with ritual significance, and the tribal totems care about the Oath of the Moon because it is part of their relationship with the Uratha that they are obliged to uphold as their spiritual patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T13:33:17-07:00","id":1539659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1539642#post1539642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do the firstborn, or at least seemingly Fenris-Ur according to the Blood Talons write-up, care about the oath of the moon? I know they are the great patrons to werewolves, but aren't themselves, not even children to Luna.<br /> <br /> Is it simply by dint of totemic relationship that they care?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an important part of that is the Blood Talons' position within the Forsaken society. The Blood Talons have taken it upon themselves to watch over the Uratha and to hunt the Uratha above all others and a portion of how they justify that is by hunting down Uratha whom they believe deserve it, and a portion of that determination is by hunting those who significantly break the oath of the moon. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, when your only bond to a bunch of psychopathic killers who brought down the greatest hunter ever is through an oath, it's probably a good thing for your survival to remind them oath breaking is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T16:33:41-07:00","id":1539668,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I was just wondering if there was some other reason I was missing. I never read tribes of the moon or whatever it's called","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T07:53:22-07:00","id":1539693,"title":"","content":"Final 2 question for Forsaken as of now<br /> <br /> So I've read up on some old posts, namely those from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, regarding the Purity Renown. So Purity is about the Oath and proof of following such an Oath. Unlike Honor, which is about establishing one's place, enforcing due consequences, mediating disputes, and practicing fairness (all to allow not only that the Urdaga mission is followed, but done efficiently), Purity is about embodying the actual ideals of the Urdaga. Just as errol said one fights another to establish the high and low, one finds a mate to as not only could that be truly cleaving to the human in the most literal sense, but to continue to the inheritance. A blood talon does not accept a generous surrender as it is not one he'd ever offer. It may be Honorable, as he understands he must concede defeat (or Cunning if he knows an advantage to the condition the offering party does not), but it is a thing of Purity he refuses to compromise as per his Vow. The pack kills off any human who knows of their true nature (friend or foe), and this is a thing of Purity. Just going through great lengths to ensure no human knows may be a thing of Purity<br /> <br /> Am I getting this right?<br /> <br /> second and last question. Renown for the Forsaken and Pure is slightly different rules correct? Since one is by Lunes and the other spirits. Is Purity especially effected since tribes of the moon have differing edicts than those of the Pure? For the record, I'm aware they both actually have the same Oaths spiritually speaking. I just mean is Purity slightly modified for Pure due to their tribal cultures involving hatred and penance?<br /> <br /> And sorry for all the questions I've had lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T10:57:41-07:00","id":1539712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1539693#post1539693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final 2 question for Forsaken as of now<br /> <br /> So I've read up on some old posts, namely those from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, regarding the Purity Renown. So Purity is about the Oath and proof of following such an Oath. Unlike Honor, which is about establishing one's place, enforcing due consequences, mediating disputes, and practicing fairness (all to allow not only that the Urdaga mission is followed, but done efficiently), Purity is about embodying the actual ideals of the Urdaga. Just as errol said one fights another to establish the high and low, one finds a mate to as not only could that be truly cleaving to the human in the most literal sense, but to continue to the inheritance. A blood talon does not accept a generous surrender as it is not one he'd ever offer. It may be Honorable, as he understands he must concede defeat (or Cunning if he knows an advantage to the condition the offering party does not), but it is a thing of Purity he refuses to compromise as per his Vow. The pack kills off any human who knows of their true nature (friend or foe), and this is a thing of Purity. Just going through great lengths to ensure no human knows may be a thing of Purity<br /> <br /> Am I getting this right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> second and last question. Renown for the Forsaken and Pure is slightly different rules correct? Since one is by Lunes and the other spirits. Is Purity especially effected since tribes of the moon have differing edicts than those of the Pure? For the record, I'm aware they both actually have the same Oaths spiritually speaking. I just mean is Purity slightly modified for Pure due to their tribal cultures involving hatred and penance? </div> </div> </div>The Pure's 1e sourcebook has a breakdown of the sorts of deeds the Anshega consider worthy of various types of Renown on pages 111-113, and that book also notes that the Pure tribes have different definitions of Purity from <i>each other</i>, but mechanically there's no distinction besides the probable range of things an Anshega werewolf might have earned Purity Renown for from their peers and totems compared to what the Forsaken would gain recognition for from the Lunes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T19:42:30-07:00","id":1539728,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much. I was just making sure. I knew about the renown stuff in the pure book, but didn't know if that sorta transitioned into 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T18:09:04-07:00","id":1540318,"title":"","content":"The Blood Talons Oath forbids them from offering surrender terms that they themselves wouldn't accept. Would it go against the Oath to falsely offer an enemy a chance to surrender in order trick the enemy into letting their guard down since you aren't technically offering them a chance to surrender, just falsely claiming you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T18:42:17-07:00","id":1540321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1540318#post1540318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blood Talons Oath forbids them from offering surrender terms that they themselves wouldn't accept. Would it go against the Oath to falsely offer an enemy a chance to surrender in order trick the enemy into letting their guard down since you aren't technically offering them a chance to surrender, just falsely claiming you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know why you would think an oath about giving and seeking no quarter would produce a werewolf who operates by trying to trick the enemy into surrendering in the first place, and the tribal oaths have long been understood to entail some degree of personal interpretation backed by legitimate belief in the spirit of the law (you as a player are not going to weasel-word your way past an oath written in proto-Sumerian unless you have a very particular table set up).<br /> <br /> I also do not know why this is a question, because the Blood Talon's tenet is about <i>them offering surrender</i>, i.e. violating the Oath for them is about trying to surrender in circumstances they would not accept if they were in their enemy's shoes. It's &quot;We killed one of them already, they'd all be dead no questions asked if they'd done the same to us, we're not walking away from this without giving them a good reason to be elsewhere,&quot; or &quot;We're professionals, we know better than to let a petty brawl escalate just because some unkind words were said, if they bite back madder than we expected we'll make our apology and see if they'll let us off the hook or if we need to re-establish our credentials.&quot;<br /> <br /> As discussed in Tribes of the Moon back in 1e, the alternate translations/interpretations of &quot;Offer no <i>terms of surrender</i> you would not accept&quot; and &quot;Do not surrender to [traitors/the Hosts/the Pure/etc]&quot; are also matters of individual interpretation, but all of them still assume that surrender is being offered and accepted or denied. If a Blood Talon is offering to surrender (or offering to spare an enemy's life if they surrender, or other legitimately-held interpretation of the oath) on terms that they would not accept if they were presented to them, they are breaking their Oath. If surrender isn't being offered in either direction, it doesn't come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T10:06:39-07:00","id":1540943,"title":"","content":"Question: If a Werewolf has both Gifts Glorious Lunacy and Gaze of the Moon, could they spend 2 Essence and inflict the Awestruck Condition with a look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T11:18:08-07:00","id":1540945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1540943#post1540943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: If a Werewolf has both Gifts Glorious Lunacy and Gaze of the Moon, could they spend 2 Essence and inflict the Awestruck Condition with a look?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Glorious Lunacy specifies it's activated when entering a form that inflicts Lunacy and Gaze of the Moon specifies you pick from the three Conditions the Lunacy resulting from its use inflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T11:55:12-07:00","id":1540946,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I was discussing this with a player and they felt some of the terminology allowed for an overlap, but it didn't seem that way to me. <br /> Another question, Can a Pack overlap with a Sin-Eater's Krewe? <br /> If the have a Werewolf as a PC who plans to have the other PCs and a few NPCs be part of the Pack, and a Sin-Eater is another PC who makes their Krewe during character creation, can they have members who overlap? Can other PCs overlap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T12:07:43-07:00","id":1540947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1540946#post1540946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I was discussing this with a player and they felt some of the terminology allowed for an overlap, but it didn't seem that way to me.<br /> Another question, Can a Pack overlap with a Sin-Eater's Krewe?<br /> If the have a Werewolf as a PC who plans to have the other PCs and a few NPCs be part of the Pack, and a Sin-Eater is another PC who makes their Krewe during character creation, can they have members who overlap? Can other PCs overlap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Membership can overlap in this case, yes. I went over <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1468827-2e-what-social-group-allows-another-supernaturals?p=1468841#post1468841\">a broader version of this question a few years ago</a>, if that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T07:28:16-07:00","id":1542509,"title":"","content":"What would werewolves think of someone who was Claimed or Urged by...<br /> <br /> Their Pack Totem<br /> <br /> Their Lodge Totem<br /> <br /> A Lune","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T08:22:43-07:00","id":1542510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1542509#post1542509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would werewolves think of someone who was Claimed or Urged by...<br /> <br /> Their Pack Totem<br /> <br /> Their Lodge Totem<br /> <br /> A Lune</div> </div> </div> </div>That is going to depend entirely on the werewolves, the spirit, and the Riding method.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Adherents and Possession&quot; sidebar from page 79 of The Pack suggests lodge totems inclined to take advantage of their deepened affinity for their adherents tend to use positive framing for the process, but pack totems are safe from Essence bleed in the material world and thus don't have the same pressures excusing them for using the Resonance provided by their pack for more than sustenance and are often weak enough that the implicit danger of crossing a line for the werewolves you have a working relationship with may deter them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T13:57:34-07:00","id":1544225,"title":"","content":"In the rulebook, it is written that going to Hisil or back is a roll 10 - Harmony or Harmony, modified by the Gauntlet strength. The time for crossing is two turns per point of the strength.<br /> <br /> My question is: What happens on failure? When can the Uratha try again? What happens on Dramatic Failure?<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T14:23:05-07:00","id":1544230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1544225#post1544225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the rulebook, it is written that going to Hisil or back is a roll 10 - Harmony or Harmony, modified by the Gauntlet strength. The time for crossing is two turns per point of the strength.<br /> <br /> My question is: What happens on failure? When can the Uratha try again? What happens on Dramatic Failure?<br /> <br /> Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, both non-success results for Stepping Sideways meant you stayed on the same side of the Gauntlet as you started; failure locked you out from trying again yourself for an hour, while dramatic failure prevented you from trying again until the following night, although in both cases a third party or an alternative method could bring you across.<br /> <br /> Translating that to Reaching may not be completely one-to-one \u2014 there's no Pathfinding mechanic described in 2e, for example \u2014 but you can probably transplant the dramatic failure result from Stepping Sideways and waive the cooldown on failure, since Reaching has a lower potential dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T14:41:11-08:00","id":1546878,"title":"","content":"The Oath of the moon is vague about &quot;the people must not kill the people&quot; , how can i translate this in game mechanics?<br /> For example, a Blood talon killing a Pure always rolls for a breaking point toward Flesh? Or it is a subjective thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T16:30:09-08:00","id":1546882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1546878#post1546878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Oath of the moon is vague about &quot;the people must not kill the people&quot; , how can i translate this in game mechanics?<br /> For example, a Blood talon killing a Pure always rolls for a breaking point toward Flesh? Or it is a subjective thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>As with questions about interpreting the tribal bans, assume some degree of flexibility tempered by the need for the character to genuinely believe whatever interpretation is being used to determine the mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> Killing a human or wolf is a breaking point toward Spirit, but violating the Oath of the Moon is a breaking point toward Flesh, which, like eating human flesh for Essence, means werewolves who've sworn the Oath risk destabilizing in either direction due to the need to roll twice and Harmony breaking points being penalized by how far from the middle you are if they think of killing another werewolf as as bad or worse than killing a human; if a werewolf doesn't draw that equivalence, then the spiritual consequence is &quot;just&quot; a higher than usual risk of falling out of alignment with your spiritual half due to breaking an oath with supernatural backing.<br /> <br /> Consistency and attention to the character's worldview is the primary point of focus, essentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T13:30:42-08:00","id":1547606,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have tips on what makes a good elodoth? Mine is a stormlord in San Francisco who has his own charter fishing boat for a living. I think I\u2019ve got his personality and stuff down but I just wanna make sure I\u2019m playing this auspice to the best of my ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T18:47:22-08:00","id":1547608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1547606#post1547606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have tips on what makes a good elodoth? Mine is a stormlord in San Francisco who has his own charter fishing boat for a living. I think I\u2019ve got his personality and stuff down but I just wanna make sure I\u2019m playing this auspice to the best of my ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awareness of proportionality and boundaries, to be brief. The auspice Renowned for its Honor is called upon to serve as judges because they're expected to be <i>fair</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fair&quot; doesn't mean dumb or soft, of course \u2014 taking a handicap in a duel is different from throwing the match, for instance, and using appropriate force to take down prey of a given magnitude doesn't mean letting bad actors act out until they're big enough problems to warrant a full-scale chase \u2014 but just as an Ithaeur should reasonably be expected to know what sort of fetish vessel is appropriate for a spirit to inhabit, any Elodoth worth their salt should at least have a functional understanding of the appropriate response to a situation within a complex system.<br /> <br /> Rahu lean on the core principles of Oath of the Moon above all others, Irraka do what it takes to get results even if it's &quot;cheating,&quot; but the Elodoth's focus is on staying impartial enough for things to <i>work out</i>. Sometimes that means giving up territory your pack is ill-suited to take care of. Sometimes it means testifying against your packmate in a formal inquiry. Werewolves with an affinity for Honor are coolheaded and in control enough that they have a proven (and testable) track record of doing The Right Thing for the contexts they find themselves in when it matters. The Ithaeur deal with spirits through mystical insight, but the Elodoth simply understand political and social dynamics; the Cahalith are often called the heart of the pack, but the Elodoth are its level heads, whether that translates to a leadership role or not.<br /> <br /> Half Moons are the folks you expect to have considered all the angles and gotten the big picture view of their circumstances (and those of their pack). Part and parcel with their ability to manipulate Rage is a certain amount of expectation that they be unlikely to fall into Kuruth themselves, and statistically that trends that archetype especially toward maintaining balanced Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T18:51:11-07:00","id":1549505,"title":"","content":"Do the Pure ever go after Vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T22:26:04-07:00","id":1549516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1549505#post1549505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Pure ever go after Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is within their ability to do so and the typical effect vampires can have on a territory is such that they may be inclined to go after them to deal with that effect, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-30T20:35:51-07:00","id":1549656,"title":"","content":"That makes sense; like the Foresaken, the don't have a particular beef with vampires, unless they get in the way.<br /> <br /> So my friend keeps saying if she saw a werewolf, she'd want to touch it's nose, and what if she could reduce frenzy as a numinia trait? Like, make the werewolf in Gauru form roll to get out of frenzy? <br /> <br /> She's already got a sort of arcane in which people can't remember her name and confuse her with other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T19:46:08-07:00","id":1550183,"title":"","content":"Stuff from 1e generally only carries across if you want it, but the Ivory Claws had the only real stance on vampires among the Pure. From The Pure, p83.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver Wolf\u2019s doctrine is clear here: Orthodox Ivory Claws should avoid vampires whenever possible. Silver Wolf says quite clearly that the worlds of the living and the dead should not mix. Such mixing renders both worlds impure. The undead are an impossible mixture, for surely death above all things is a binary state. </div> </div> </div>It's described as due to purity and about avoiding interactions with them. Not hunting them down but not running away from them just refusing to deal with them unless they need to.<br /> <br /> Regarding touching a raging werewolf on their nose to stop Kuruth, it's pretty crazy powerful and specific but would involve getting within killing range of a raging werewolf. They might want to check out the Plain Merit Template from Hurt Locker if they're interested in standing against violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T06:27:12-07:00","id":1551766,"title":"","content":"Question about the bane of Silver<br /> <br /> So it was a really big revelation that in Pangea, we learned werewolves had ALWAYS had the bane, so the Pure are even more wrong than simply not being as to Father Wolf as the Forsaken are. BUT, the Moon- Shunned, who Luna never witnessed, do not harbor the Bane.<br /> <br /> Is it fair to say that, with silver being so rare, it was only AFTER Pangea fell and many years later the Uratha discovered their bane? With that came the assumption it was cursed by Luna, or otherwise became distorted in Pure and Forsaken storytelling? <br /> <br /> finally, does that mean the Pure COULD claim that Luna did make them with a bane for some mysterious ad suspicious reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T09:04:35-07:00","id":1551769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1551766#post1551766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the bane of Silver<br /> <br /> So it was a really big revelation that in Pangea, we learned werewolves had ALWAYS had the bane, so the Pure are even more wrong than simply not being as to Father Wolf as the Forsaken are. BUT, the Moon- Shunned, who Luna never witnessed, do not harbor the Bane.<br /> <br /> Is it fair to say that, with silver being so rare, it was only AFTER Pangea fell and many years later the Uratha discovered their bane? With that came the assumption it was cursed by Luna, or otherwise became distorted in Pure and Forsaken storytelling?<br /> <br /> finally, does that mean the Pure COULD claim that Luna did make them with a bane for some mysterious ad suspicious reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Too many variables to conclusively say, particularly given that the Dark Era where we learned that werewolves had the bane of silver before the Sundering is also the Dark Era where ruins of the Time Before are still plentiful and mostly uneroded by Dissonance and the magical materials one can find in such ruins include a form of silver that counts as a bane for anything whose bane is any type of silver; the Moon-Shunned have more things that are weird about them spiritually than their lack of the bane as well, which does not paint a consistent picture of the metaphysical reason normal werewolves have it.<br /> <br /> Add to this the potential weirdness the Shadow can bring to bear and the scope of the entire inhabited world (even limiting ourselves to the range of the Vinca culture, there's silver in the Balkans and it's possible to occasionally find natural silver without mining it), spirits and/or Pangaeans could possibly have directly or indirectly made the Uratha aware of the bane, or a given region's werewolves could be completely unaware of it.<br /> <br /> The Sundering was an era before the tribes existed and the cults and sects that werewolves formed instead had a bunch of different beliefs. It's conceivable that some of them might think the rare metal that burns their flesh does so due to malevolent intent by a divine being while others might think it's just the spiritual tradeoff of their nature, but there's too much time and space involved between 5500 BC and the modern era to make declarative statements about the discovery of the bane and its sociological impact outside of the bounds of your own game, since the closest thing to a timeline we have for the Sundering is that it happens and things eventually change to become the current state of affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-19-2025, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T16:48:53-07:00","id":1551775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1551769#post1551769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many variables to conclusively say, particularly given that the Dark Era where we learned that werewolves had the bane of silver before the Sundering is also the Dark Era where ruins of the Time Before are still plentiful and mostly uneroded by Dissonance and the magical materials one can find in such ruins include a form of silver that counts as a bane for anything whose bane is any type of silver; the Moon-Shunned have more things that are weird about them spiritually than their lack of the bane as well, which does not paint a consistent picture of the metaphysical reason normal werewolves have it.<br /> <br /> Add to this the potential weirdness the Shadow can bring to bear and the scope of the entire inhabited world (even limiting ourselves to the range of the Vinca culture, there's silver in the Balkans and it's possible to occasionally find natural silver without mining it), spirits and/or Pangaeans could possibly have directly or indirectly made the Uratha aware of the bane, or a given region's werewolves could be completely unaware of it.<br /> <br /> The Sundering was an era before the tribes existed and the cults and sects that werewolves formed instead had a bunch of different beliefs. It's conceivable that some of them might think the rare metal that burns their flesh does so due to malevolent intent by a divine being while others might think it's just the spiritual tradeoff of their nature, but there's too much time and space involved between 5500 BC and the modern era to make declarative statements about the discovery of the bane and its sociological impact outside of the bounds of your own game, since the closest thing to a timeline we have for the Sundering is that it happens and things eventually change to become the current state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I was just wondering. I do like how the writers seem to show the Pure as wrong in more ways than one. Refreshing in a world where everything has to have both sides be arguably &quot;right&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T02:39:00-07:00","id":1551781,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> Seems to me that the 2e core indicates pretty explicitly that the Forsaken believe the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T09:48:09-07:00","id":1551786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1551781#post1551781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> Seems to me that the 2e core indicates pretty explicitly that the Forsaken believe the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies on that. I had forgotten. Yet it still causes the Pure to appear even more wrong as they consider it another reason to hate Luna","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T12:01:58-07:00","id":1552160,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves age?<br /> <br /> So, the Purified, when the ritual is completed, revert to a body of their youth, in their early-20's; since wolves are connect to the spirit-world in a similar-fashion the Purified are, would they age or would their bodies stay that of a teenager? <br /> <br /> I've seen art of old werewolves, but, you know, that's creative-license.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T12:25:42-07:00","id":1552162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1552160#post1552160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves age?<br /> <br /> So, the Purified, when the ritual is completed, revert to a body of their youth, in their early-20's; since wolves are connect to the spirit-world in a similar-fashion the Purified are, would they age or would their bodies stay that of a teenager?<br /> <br /> I've seen art of old werewolves, but, you know, that's creative-license.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are not connected to the Shadow in a similar fashion to the Purified, who are immortals made what they are by ritual means.<br /> <br /> There's no published content in 2e, though the 1e book Blood of the Wolf says that becoming a werewolf doesn't reverse aging, but aging seldom has an effect on Uratha until their 90s or 100s, and they tend to look no more than half their age at that point (counting the age they had their First Change normally in contrast) \u2014 the difficulties of attending a 30-year high school reunion still looking like you're in your twenties is highlighted, and high Primal Urge seems to enhance the effect.<br /> <br /> Given that 2e's material on the First Change restoring mobility and senses that one had lost as a mortal is contrary to the 1e material, How Werewolves Age is ultimately going to have to be a judgment call in your individual games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T17:04:31-07:00","id":1552173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1552160#post1552160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves age?<br /> <br /> So, the Purified, when the ritual is completed, revert to a body of their youth, in their early-20's; since wolves are connect to the spirit-world in a similar-fashion the Purified are, would they age or would their bodies stay that of a teenager?<br /> <br /> I've seen art of old werewolves, but, you know, that's creative-license.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they age, but very slow, and it has been hinted in 1ed and 2ed that at some point of power a Werewolf can transcend to a larger being, in 1ed we assumed it was to transform into a powerful spirit likely a Dihir, 2ed put the idea of bodhisattva predators and the uratha predecesors (Geryo) show alternative paths to being half spirit half flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> See the rest of my post for a couple of examples of high Primal Urge werewolves from 1ed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1552162#post1552162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are not connected to the Shadow in a similar fashion to the Purified, who are immortals made what they are by ritual means.<br /> <br /> There's no published content in 2e, though the 1e book Blood of the Wolf says that becoming a werewolf doesn't reverse aging, but aging seldom has an effect on Uratha until their 90s or 100s, and they tend to look no more than half their age at that point (counting the age they had their First Change normally in contrast) \u2014 the difficulties of attending a 30-year high school reunion still looking like you're in your twenties is highlighted, and high Primal Urge seems to enhance the effect.<br /> <br /> Given that 2e's material on the First Change restoring mobility and senses that one had lost as a mortal is contrary to the 1e material, How Werewolves Age is ultimately going to have to be a judgment call in your individual games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great points, from 1e also we have The Wolf of the Woods and Red Stick, who are at the bare minimum 200 years old and dont even look 60 years old. And that is the aesthetics of it, because stat wise they are not showing their age at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-08-2025, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T17:44:55-07:00","id":1552571,"title":"","content":"I just figured, that, since werewolves can continually heal, and since they heal from poisons and sickness fast, that, they wouldn't age because of their spirit-connections.<br /> <br /> <br /> Q: Can an Azarath-Crawler take over a major-splat like a Werewolf or Vampire in the same manner as they do a human? I suppose, maybe they can take over a vampire in torpor, that doesn't have enough blood to heal the damage to the brain, but , the Crawler would have to deal with the Vampire's Beast. I don't know what essence-points that would have. <br /> <br /> And what about a minor-splat like the Purifed? A sorcerer or a psychic would be easy, but the Purifed have ways of resisting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T20:09:31-07:00","id":1552575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1552571#post1552571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: Can an Azarath-Crawler take over a major-splat like a Werewolf or Vampire in the same manner as they do a human? I suppose, maybe they can take over a vampire in torpor, that doesn't have enough blood to heal the damage to the brain, but , the Crawler would have to deal with the Vampire's Beast. I don't know what essence-points that would have.<br /> <br /> And what about a minor-splat like the Purifed? A sorcerer or a psychic would be easy, but the Purifed have ways of resisting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, in fact, an Azlu-werewolf hybrid in 1e supplement Hunting Ground: the Rockies \u2014 see Broken Web on page 109 \u2014 but it's an Empty Wolf created by the idigam that was defeated within living memory.<br /> <br /> Going from more recent material, Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon's chapter on the Hosts includes on its first page a set of notes that the Shards of Hosts are spiritually incompatible with Claimed and nonhuman animals and that werewolves' regeneration prevents the Shard from killing them to take over their body.<br /> <br /> There's the very loose story hook that powerful Shards might be able to overcome these limits, but just running through the general principles the fact that the process kills the body and then uses more Shards to further empower the hybrid indicates that the only practical differences are liable to stem from plot hooks based on power in the flesh of the person thusly subverted. Werewolves have the precedent of being more nourishing to eat for Hosts, but between Claiming alone making a subject off-limits for typical Shards and about half the splats having some type of eject button, regeneration, or spiritual weirdness about them (up to and including &quot;a legitimate case can be made that this body is a particularly durable and elaborate construct made of ghost snot&quot;) we go well outside the realm of Simple Questions with Simple Answers unless &quot;if they can it's significant enough to be a plot device that we can't tell you how to run&quot; is satisfactory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-25-2025, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T08:10:31-07:00","id":1553228,"title":"","content":"Do gifts like Shadows Gaze implicitly work on ghosts if the Werewolf can see them? (It says any spirit they can see, but ghosts are not spirits...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T09:09:35-07:00","id":1553233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1553228#post1553228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do gifts like Shadows Gaze implicitly work on ghosts if the Werewolf can see them? (It says any spirit they can see, but ghosts are not spirits...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Werewolves have connections and insight into the hierarchies of the Shadow, but the Shadow is not the Underworld. An unusual Gift or fetish might provide information on ghosts, but that's not part of Standard Ithaeur Kit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T16:55:02-07:00","id":1553242,"title":"","content":"Is staying in the Underworld a Harmony issue, since you can't go to the Shadow? (Break towards human?) While eating ghosts (of humans) is a break towards the spirit? Is that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T18:04:18-07:00","id":1553244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1553242#post1553242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is staying in the Underworld a Harmony issue, since you can't go to the Shadow? (Break towards human?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not in either of the two worlds Harmony is concerned with, so I would make the rolls for both, since destabilization toward one side or the other is more likely as soon as you're not at Harmony 5, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While eating ghosts (of humans) is a break towards the spirit? Is that right? </div> </div> </div>With the probably-uncommon case that it's not also a breaking point toward Flesh for violating the Oath, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T17:36:23-07:00","id":1553628,"title":"","content":"In a game like werewolf combat is almost guaranteed. But for a character that\u2019s less combat focused how do you avoid being useless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T18:29:01-07:00","id":1553630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1553628#post1553628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game like werewolf combat is almost guaranteed. But for a character that\u2019s less combat focused how do you avoid being useless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Social/political maneuvering to get more assets for the pack, investigating mundane and occult aspects of your locale to arm yourself with knowledge, sabotaging prey with hit-and-run tactics, and making use of the multiple Merits that let you specialize your forms so you at least have some niche circumstances in which you can be more physically threatening than a newly Changed werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, one advantage to the way Creating The Pack works is that everyone has at least one extra character who isn't a werewolf that you can leverage to split the hunting party up to pursue on different leads on a story's focal problem; the Ithaeur doesn't need to be as deadly a combatant as the Rahu if they're accompanying two Wolf-Blooded packmates to do research in a spirit-haunted library.<br /> <br /> Finally and most simply, in the absence of mechanics that specifically stop this, every extra attacker in a fight pings the prey's Defense down further whenever they opt to use it before the Initiative cycles around again. Unless you're not just less combat-focused but actively bad at combat in spite of the natural advantages of the Uratha, having an extra pair of claws to throw at a problem is usually pretty helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T18:11:50-07:00","id":1553944,"title":"","content":"Since vamps don't appear on film (traditionally), would video-footage of the People in Garau, incite the delirium? Maybe willpower bonus? Kinda like the reverse of what vamps get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T18:58:58-07:00","id":1553946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1553944#post1553944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since vamps don't appear on film (traditionally), would video-footage of the People in Garau, incite the delirium? Maybe willpower bonus? Kinda like the reverse of what vamps get?</div> </div> </div> </div>The phenomenon you are asking about in Forsaken is called Lunacy; Delirium is an Apocalypse thing. Vampires in Requiem 2e likewise only outright don't appear in recorded media if they're the sort that also don't show up in mirrors, cast shadows, or have an echo, because those things belong to the unfriendly ghost that serves as their modified clan bane; most of the Kindred just instinctively know where to stand and/or are the subject of weirdly persistent errors in whatever image recording technology is being used to try to capture their likeness against their intention.<br /> <br /> 1e had a note that most people with a Willpower of 8 or lower would refuse to believe a picture of a werewolf in Gauru form isn't a hoax, in that version of the game's model of Lunacy as scaling in effects with the observer's Willpower rating. While 2e does not have a similar note, the &quot;Concepts in Werewolf: the Forsaken&quot; section of the corebook's Storytelling chapter suggests expanding the scope of Lunacy to hints of honesty about being a werewolf to emphasize the alienation it brings to the Uratha; the closest thing to a &quot;Willpower bonus&quot; involved is the fact that Lunacy is a modified Integrity breaking point roll for which exceptional success provides the equivalent of having Willpower 10 in the old system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T09:35:57-07:00","id":1553956,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I realized it was Lunacy, not Delirium; I first started playing using the Apocalypse rules. I think I might have read about people thinking it's a hoax before, I got my 1e book right next to me. <br /> <br /> And I knew about vamps' film and mirrors, but shadows and echos? That's new to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T10:53:01-07:00","id":1553958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1553956#post1553956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I knew about vamps' film and mirrors, but shadows and echos? That's new to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow Mekhet replace the normal Mekhet clan bane with their Reflection being a separate entity that goes around making trouble for them using their secondhand likeness. 1e mechanics for them can be found in <i>Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark</i>, while 2e provided an update in <i>Thousand Years of Night</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T21:46:55-07:00","id":1554000,"title":"","content":"What page in Forsaken is the camera thing on? I can't find it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, how many of Stephen King's supernatural monsters, could a pack of werewolves take out? IT, would be tough, but doable. Kurt Barlow would be easy. Reverend Lester Lowe is a Bane-wolf, or, perhaps he's Ridden or somehow, completely immune to the spirit-world as he focuses on his human-congregation. Randell flag might be difficult. Capt. Trips might work on the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T06:05:13-07:00","id":1554006,"title":"","content":"How do the Pure and Hosts interact (if they interact at all).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T06:31:27-07:00","id":1554007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554000#post1554000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What page in Forsaken is the camera thing on? I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tF 1e Core, page 176.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554006#post1554006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Pure and Hosts interact (if they interact at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>With the same breadth of possibilities as the Forsaken or Ghost Wolves, minus anything that specifically relies on instruction or advisement from Luna or the Lunes; they're potential prey if they mess with the Pure's territory, their plans, or the interests of their totems, but they might also be assets for whatever their intentions are in any given time and place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T07:14:45-07:00","id":1554008,"title":"","content":"Okay one more question that just popped into my head. Say I\u2019ve got a character whose main focus is vehicles and mechanics. His fighting stats are pretty bad for a werewolf. How practical do we think ramming, stunning, grappling with a chain, and then driving off as fast as possible would be?<br /> <br /> (Also anyone from eternal noire who sees this, no you don\u2019t)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T07:54:23-07:00","id":1554010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554008#post1554008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay one more question that just popped into my head. Say I\u2019ve got a character whose main focus is vehicles and mechanics. His fighting stats are pretty bad for a werewolf. How practical do we think ramming, stunning, grappling with a chain, and then driving off as fast as possible would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be at least three separate instant actions if you're doing it by yourself, and unless I'm forgetting something from Armory or Hurt Locker you'd have to come up with mechanics for &quot;grappling with a chain&quot; (as opposed to regular grappling using a chain to make the Restrain maneuver stick without your continued personal maintenance), plus you may have to adapt the 1e mechanics for jumping from a moving vehicle to 2e to get a system for how damaging being dragged by a vehicle is, but it's certainly not impossible.<br /> <br /> The primary issue of practicality is that in the time it would take you to do this even a not-especially-talented werewolf can still hit stuff pretty well in Urshul or Gauru, and getting vehicles into the Shadow (or even into tighter quarters in the material world) adds necessary preparation to get to the point where it's feasible to do this even without time constraints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T12:12:34-07:00","id":1554013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554008#post1554008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay one more question that just popped into my head. Say I\u2019ve got a character whose main focus is vehicles and mechanics. His fighting stats are pretty bad for a werewolf. How practical do we think ramming, stunning, grappling with a chain, and then driving off as fast as possible would be?<br /> <br /> (Also anyone from eternal noire who sees this, no you don\u2019t)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll put a small twist into what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said:<br /> <br /> You're not really exchanging normal combat for all this. You're exchanging normal combat for ramming with the vehicle. Everything else here may be a good idea or not regardless of how you fought.<br /> <br /> But that said, most of the time it isn't all that practical. You can't ram things with your car in places you can't get into with your car. It is a valid strategy when it applies, but it is quite circumstantial.<br /> <br /> What's more important is that this is still worrying too much with making a specific &quot;combat action&quot; for a character when none was asked for. In most combats even a weak Uratha still has enough dice to help. Any character whatsoever means an extra action, and that's by itself the single biggest advantage someone can hope in battle, especially in CoD. Their extra forms give enough extra dice to make those extra actions worth it. And never forget you have Willpower.<br /> <br /> Circumstantial opportunities like ramming the car will exist. In fact you'll probably find plenty of them. But what will help you with those isn't to prepare a specific &quot;combo&quot;, but to keep an eye for the environment for opportunities to do stuff with your other dice pools, all kinds of opportunities, attention helps more than focusing on a given action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T10:26:58-07:00","id":1554159,"title":"","content":"Are there any examples of fetish guns in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T23:16:59-07:00","id":1554217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554159#post1554159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any examples of fetish guns in the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think there's only one official one, though there's a few different fetish bullets.<br /> <br /> The Devil's Right Hand fetish. Heavy revolvers. When empty they can be activated to reload with ephemeral bullets. Reducing the damage rating by 1. Can also be used to make a medium burst autofire attack even though the revolver doesn't hold enough bullets for it.<br /> <br /> From Tribes of the Moon, p45.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T13:14:19-07:00","id":1554380,"title":"","content":"Sooo need a slight clarification for how Dark Power works in Shunned by the Moon. The rules explain how a Werewolf can accept it and get tainted, so my question is.... can a Werewolf be brought back from this and &quot;cured&quot; before they fully turn Bale Hound, or is this a one-way trip?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T13:47:36-07:00","id":1554381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554380#post1554380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo need a slight clarification for how Dark Power works in Shunned by the Moon. The rules explain how a Werewolf can accept it and get tainted, so my question is.... can a Werewolf be brought back from this and &quot;cured&quot; before they fully turn Bale Hound, or is this a one-way trip?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 34 mentions the following of Tarnished who decide to not accept the invitation to meet Soulless Wolf:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, the Uratha will forever remain marked and weakened. </div> </div> </div>Now, it's position is after the blooding, but I suspect it's meant to be the result for any use of Dark Power. It's a permanent mark on the Uratha that can't be easily healed, hence what makes it so tempting.<br /> <br /> That said, clearly it's not a one-way trip, you just have to accept this permanent weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T16:47:24-08:00","id":1555224,"title":"","content":"So, where are the Forsaken Baset? Mokole's etc. ? I know about the wererats and spiders, but, though out history, there are no wolves in South America, Australia, or parts of Asia. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1554006#post1554006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Pure and Hosts interact (if they interact at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>So I just read the Pure-book, and, both the Pure and the Forsaken have a hatred for the Azlu but, the Pure tolerate the Beshilu due to their connections to the spirit-world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T17:29:21-08:00","id":1555225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555224#post1555224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, where are the Forsaken Baset? Mokole's etc. ? I know about the wererats and spiders, but, though out history, there are no wolves in South America, Australia, or parts of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>War Against the Pure</i> is the book you want for non-wolf shapeshifters in the same general mold as Forsaken's werewolves, with <i>World of Darkness: Skinchangers</i> having a wider variety of types of shapeshifter, including the &quot;reverse Claimed&quot; siten uzu who borrow a lot of the expanded Claimed mechanics from <i>Predators</i>. (<i>Changing Breeds</i> is broadly maligned for being a little too Apocalypse for Chronicles, but you can certainly still mine it for content.)<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that the Hosts aren't were-animals, if only because Wolf Hosts were a thing in <i>Night Horrors: Wolfsbane</i> and a similar stark distinction being drawn between a spiritual shapeshifter akin to the Uratha and a fragmentary monster modeled on the same animal (likely derived from a Pangaean of the same name) makes for decent ready-made spiritual drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T03:16:25-08:00","id":1555230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555224#post1555224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...though out history, there are no wolves in South America, Australia, or parts of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's largely irrelevant. Uratha are werewolves because one of their progenitors was a Pangaean called Wolf, not because they have some affinity for real wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T13:57:36-08:00","id":1555247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555224#post1555224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, where are the Forsaken Baset? Mokole's etc. ? I know about the wererats and spiders, but, though out history, there are no wolves in South America, Australia, or parts of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Forsaken</i> Uratha aren't related to real wolves. While they like to have wolves in their Packs, and would likely at one time have been more common in places with wolves (because those were be places with wolf spirits), this was at pre-historic times.<br /> <br /> Uratha aren't limited in any way to places with wolves, so they just spread over the world with common humans. There's Werewolves everywhere with or without wolves.<br /> <br /> The same certainly applies to other Shapechangers as far as they're a thing in your chronicle. There are few formally canonized varieties, but literally nothing in the canon that limits how many can exist or their numbers, either. You could even decide Uratha aren't the most numerous Changers around. And whatever you do as a Changer, they may exist anywhere at all, regardless of the presence or not of the &quot;base animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wolf-spirits also exist anywhere the <i>notion</i> of a wolf exists, even if actual wolves don't (although life is certainly for them where wolves do exist). In fact, even extinct animals may still have spirits associated with them, which could result in Shapechangers based on them even if they formed after the extinction of the base animal.<br /> <br /> You can even theoretically have Changers based on non-existent animals or on whatever, actually, as long as you figure out how it happened. They not only could use similar rules, they would be the same class of being from a lore standpoint. There's a reason for animal Changers to be the rule, but no hard impediment for there to be exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T14:39:20-08:00","id":1555287,"title":"","content":"The problem is, for a Dark Eras game, that takes place, say on the Yucatan Peninsula, there aren't any wolves around so, a werewolf would be quite out of place; unless, I say, that a were-Jaguar, has the exact same stats as a werewolf, and carry on, or, not use them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T15:51:24-08:00","id":1555294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555287#post1555287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, for a Dark Eras game, that takes place, say on the Yucatan Peninsula, there aren't any wolves around so, a werewolf would be quite out of place; unless, I say, that a were-Jaguar, has the exact same stats as a werewolf, and carry on, or, not use them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how else to tell you this, but people don't often see wolves in most cities, period. The Yucatan at least has coyotes.<br /> <br /> Lunacy means the only practical issue is that Urhan doesn't have supernatural reinforcement of people convincing themselves to doubt the evidence of their own eyes and saying they must have seen some other big animal. It's not like becoming a werewolf runs on classic Spider-Man logic, and the Uratha as a society already emphasize keeping their activities under wraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T16:24:00-08:00","id":1555297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555287#post1555287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, for a Dark Eras game, that takes place, say on the Yucatan Peninsula, there aren't any wolves around so, a werewolf would be quite out of place; unless, I say, that a were-Jaguar, has the exact same stats as a werewolf, and carry on, or, not use them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that a problem?<br /> <br /> The <i>Sundering</i> happened around 7 thousand years ago, and the Uratha existed for an indeterminate amount of time before this. With their access to the Shadow and supernatural powers of travel, they could have reached any part of the world way before the first written record even if you assume it happened right after their birth.<br /> <br /> You can have other shapechangers no problem within canon, but just having plain Werewolves wouldn't be a problem at all. Given their apparent numbers they probably exist everywhere regardless. They only have to be cautious about people seeing animals that don't exist, but is that really that big of a deal? It isn't as if people would go nuts if they simply occasionally see a new animal, especially at a time when they occasionally saw far weirder things.<br /> <br /> Again: this is not Apocalypse. <u><b>Uratha are not wolves, nor related to wolves.</b></u> Their link to wolves is archetypal, not biological, and it doesn't need actual wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T21:04:40-08:00","id":1555302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555287#post1555287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, for a Dark Eras game, that takes place, say on the Yucatan Peninsula, there aren't any wolves around so, a werewolf would be quite out of place; unless, I say, that a were-Jaguar, has the exact same stats as a werewolf, and carry on, or, not use them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mexican Wolf is a thing, with fossils showing them having a long history in the Yucatan. Aside from Lunacy being pretty good at fogging details, most areas of the world have legends of big, hairy beast-men. The Yucatan has the Sisimito. And depending on how far back you go with Dark Eras it's reasonable to suspect there may be no zoologists around to tell you that whatever creature doesn't fit the environment.<br /> <br /> But if you need more. For the easy cost of 1 Experience any werewolf can get the Skin Thief Wolf Gift and they can grab an animal skin and change their wolf form to that of a predatory animal of roughly the same size, indefinitely. Then if they want to lounge around in their urhan form for some reason they can. So you can be a jaguar. Or a panther, or bobcat or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2025, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T10:19:06-08:00","id":1555320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555287#post1555287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, for a Dark Eras game, that takes place, say on the Yucatan Peninsula, there aren't any wolves around so, a werewolf would be quite out of place; unless, I say, that a were-Jaguar, has the exact same stats as a werewolf, and carry on, or, not use them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the history of people in various parts of the world believing in animals that definitely didn't exist such as basilisks, , or images of animals so odd that we can't tell if they were fanciful representations of real (possibly extinct) animals or totally made up, such as the Egyptian Seth animal, I don't think the odd wolf is much of a problem. It'll be somewhere between mistaken for a more familiar canid and recorded as an oddity in a book that won't survive the Spanish conquest of that peninsula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T11:16:24-08:00","id":1555325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1555302#post1555302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mexican Wolf is a thing, with fossils showing them having a long history in the Yucatan. Aside from Lunacy being pretty good at fogging details, most areas of the world have legends of big, hairy beast-men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brazil <i>literally</i> has legends on werewolves (lobisomem, literally wolf-man) despite not having anything besides the Manned Wolf, and those legends aren't from areas where the Manned Wolf lives.<br /> <br /> Our werewolves are just less well defined in descriptions since, you know, we don't have actual wolves and most people who believe in werewolves and say they saw werewolves have never seen a wolf in their lives, not even on TV.<br /> <br /> Most people seeing a real wolf here would take them for dogs and that's it, not even interacting with the animal for long would change a thing, which is another side of this. Trained professionals are certainly capable of noticing a wolf quickly, but the vast majority of people won't even if they actually saw a wolf on a zoo or the internet.<br /> <br /> Imagine that before zoos and internet. Dogs arrived in South America no later than 2500 BCE, probably earlier. So people actually <i>would</i> have a reference for describing an Urhan: a regular large dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T19:59:39-08:00","id":1558118,"title":"","content":"Longstanding question about locus formation: Given the way harvesting Essence is represented does not assign an actual quantity of Essence to non-loci before a harvesting roll is made (with the exception of the &quot;Raw Essence&quot; sidebar from Territories, which specifically concerns large outpourings of emotion and frames the result narratively and mechanically as a kind of temporary locus), how do people judge whether a location or situation is primed to form a locus without the intervention of a character with their own Essence pool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T17:03:36-08:00","id":1558124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558118#post1558118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longstanding question about locus formation: Given the way harvesting Essence is represented does not assign an actual quantity of Essence to non-loci before a harvesting roll is made (with the exception of the &quot;Raw Essence&quot; sidebar from Territories, which specifically concerns large outpourings of emotion and frames the result narratively and mechanically as a kind of temporary locus), how do people judge whether a location or situation is primed to form a locus without the intervention of a character with their own Essence pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you expand on that? Like who would not have an Essence pool but would want to determine the location of a locus?<br /> <br /> It seems to be just about Resonance creating Essence then a lack of spirits around to eat it. Since they can be artificially made it doesn't seem like a location needs to be primed beyond those two things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-05-2026, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T17:15:07-08:00","id":1558127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558124#post1558124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you expand on that? Like who would not have an Essence pool but would want to determine the location of a locus?<br /> <br /> It seems to be just about Resonance creating Essence then a lack of spirits around to eat it. Since they can be artificially made it doesn't seem like a location needs to be primed beyond those two things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very simple way to put it is &quot;How do you know if 150 points of Essence have accumulated in an area that doesn't have a locus or werewolves and/or spirits actively putting Essence there when the mechanics for loose Essence are 'a spirit rolls Power + Finesse - Gauntlet modifier around an appropriate phenomenon'?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T06:44:01-08:00","id":1558138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558127#post1558127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very simple way to put it is &quot;How do you know if 150 points of Essence have accumulated in an area that doesn't have a locus or werewolves and/or spirits actively putting Essence there when the mechanics for loose Essence are 'a spirit rolls Power + Finesse - Gauntlet modifier around an appropriate phenomenon'?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I could suppose that since a Resonant condition generates an Essence a day, then if 150 days had passed without a Spirit Gorging or simply being around for absorbing the daily output, then it becames a Locus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T20:40:41-08:00","id":1558151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558138#post1558138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could suppose that since a Resonant condition generates an Essence a day, then if 150 days had passed without a Spirit Gorging or simply being around for absorbing the daily output, then it becames a Locus</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it might be a point of Essence an hour (similar to how Essence Bleed impacts spirits at a point per hour). Perhaps with some variation due to a magnitude of Resonance (which is tinkery enough it only really came into play with Territories' Raw Essence feasting). That way even at a slow leak, as long as it's consistent you get 168 in a week, allowing for a locus. A tree or pond left by themselves have that time, but a store or busy intersection might get loads of Essence at certain peak hours then little for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> You'd just have a build-up of more Essence around the Faram. But as pointed out in various books, Essence isn't really an easily quantifiable thing, especially across the board. From Lore of the Forsaken, p129, the section on Loci and subsection on Essence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essence cannot be perceived as a thing in and of itself, but as a series of phenomena. Uratha have to use all of their senses to \ufb01nd free Essence as it bleeds through the Gauntlet and flickers into and out of existence in the spirit world \u2014 brie\ufb02y appearing as sensations related to its resonance. Essence \ufb02avored with joy might appear as a whirlwind of \ufb02ower petals, the sound of laughter, the scent of ice cream, the touch of satin. Essence might appear as each of these sensations to different beings at once.<br /> <br /> When describing free-\ufb02owing Essence, don\u2019t get caught up in the game mechanics. Each point of Essence does not correspond to a glowing ball of light, etc. Remember that \u201cpoints\u201d of Essence do not correspond to discrete objects or phenomena in Werewolf: The Forsaken. When dealing with loci and the power that \ufb02ows through them, a Storyteller may be tempted to mix metagaming concepts with his descriptions. While players deal with points of Essence as a matter of game mechanics, their characters do not. A Storyteller should try to avoid describing Essence directly. Describe it in terms of its effects, its resonance and its potential. Essence should not be pinned down as mere glowing bands of pink light, or multi-colored butter\ufb02ies or rivulets of black, metallic-tasting liquid. Essence is magical. It\u2019s an ineffable phenomenon and should only exist in the periphery of an Uratha\u2019s perception \u2014 an Uratha may be able to smell, but not quite identify its bouquet, see the changes, taste its sweet bounty, feel its warmth or hear it song. He should not pick up three points of Essence and jingle them in his pocket like loose change. </div> </div> </div>Then when it has formed a locus it does so, coalescing around something that will be the heart of the locus and forming the concealing faram around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2026, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T18:19:48-08:00","id":1558244,"title":"","content":"Who in the Americas, during Columbus' times, Forsake or the Pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T01:47:22-08:00","id":1558257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558244#post1558244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who in the Americas, during Columbus' times, Forsake or the Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you rephrase that? It's not very clear what you're asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T21:34:03-08:00","id":1558275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558257#post1558257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you rephrase that? It's not very clear what you're asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're asking which existed in the Americas at the period.<br /> <br /> If so, both did. Without something weirdly magical or determined going on you don't get regions wholly one way or another, and it would be difficult to keep up across entire continents. Even without Pure or Forsaken werewolves around, spirits can bring them into the tribes, even teach them the Flay Auspice rite. Blasphemies says during one of the Brotherhood write-ups that when the conquistadors arrived they found Pure and Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2026, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T18:22:07-08:00","id":1558477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1558257#post1558257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you rephrase that? It's not very clear what you're asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who <i>was </i>in the Americans, at Columbus' time, Foresaken or the Pure. I keep writing like that and I don't know why. Like, for the longest time, I'd write, &quot;How our you&quot;?.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T18:30:52-07:00","id":1559257,"title":"","content":"Werewolves and smoking; since nicotine is technically a poison, would an Uratha, upon taking a puff, start immediately coughing as their body instantly rejects the smoke and begins to heal? Like, they'd always cough, no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T18:32:44-07:00","id":1559258,"title":"","content":"Another question; what's cannon-lore for the Pure/Foresaken territories in Southern California? I put a Pure-locus on the Hollywood-Hills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T22:35:08-07:00","id":1559265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1559257#post1559257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves and smoking; since nicotine is technically a poison, would an Uratha, upon taking a puff, start immediately coughing as their body instantly rejects the smoke and begins to heal? Like, they'd always cough, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would seem to be a reaction if they were really vulnerable to poison and not resistant to it. People with asthma and other lung issues aren't coughing at smoke because they're healing.<br /> <br /> Nicotine also doesn't affect flesh like acid, dissolving lungs to the point that they need to be painfully rebuilt after a single inhale. A Uratha could smoke like a regular person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1559258#post1559258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question; what's cannon-lore for the Pure/Foresaken territories in Southern California? I put a Pure-locus on the Hollywood-Hills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much.<br /> <br /> The Distorted Aurora Reed is mentioned as working in the Hollywood world (in Shunned by the Moon). The Lodge of the Shield is described as originating in Los Angeles in both editions. Wandering Voice, a powerful Elodoth Bone Shadow of the Lodge of Harbingers, holds territory in San Diego and operates through Southern California (he's got a write-up in Signs of the Moon that mentions how he stopped a powerful Fire-Touched called the Mountain Man trying to lead an army of bound spirits to California).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T11:02:10-07:00","id":1559275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1559257#post1559257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves and smoking; since nicotine is technically a poison, would an Uratha, upon taking a puff, start immediately coughing as their body instantly rejects the smoke and begins to heal? Like, they'd always cough, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game rules don't treat intoxicants as actual poisons that deal damage and have Toxicity until you overdose. In general this is a petty view of what it takes to kick in the visceral regeneration of werewolves. 1e's Blood of the Wolf, which goes into several intoxicants, doesn't even bother mentioning any effect or interaction with nicotine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T19:49:17-07:00","id":1559335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1559265#post1559265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ' ' '<br /> <br /> Not much.<br /> <br /> The Distorted Aurora Reed is mentioned as working in the Hollywood world (in Shunned by the Moon). The Lodge of the Shield is described as originating in Los Angeles in both editions. Wandering Voice, a powerful Elodoth Bone Shadow of the Lodge of Harbingers, holds territory in San Diego and operates through Southern California (he's got a write-up in Signs of the Moon that mentions how he stopped a powerful Fire-Touched called the Mountain Man trying to lead an army of bound spirits to California).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, well, I found a cool map I could modify online of SoCal, ,but it doesn't having the Island of the Blue-Dolphin on it and I'd have to modify it, which would be a lotta work. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-21T20:38:51-07:00","id":1560145,"title":"","content":"How do you guys make and stay out npc\u2019s for games? I know the usual rule is to give them a few dice and move on but what about more important antagonists? Or even low level mooks? How do I know how many dice these fellas should have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da