ass=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how WW get more keep their damage, when they change forms right? Well, what would happen if an Uratha gorges themselves on meat while in Usrhul or Gauru-forms and then changes back to hishu-form? They still are full of all that meat they had their fill with while in a larger-form; do they scream: &quot;I GOTTA POOP&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that this depends on their current harmony. If the harmony is low, meat they had eaten will just naturally dissolve into their system without any setbacks. At high harmony they will rather puke or what you have said above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29097-ryukentuken","name":"Ryukentuken","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T23:41:32-07:00","id":1560611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1560607#post1560607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how WW get more keep their damage, when they change forms right? Well, what would happen if an Uratha gorges themselves on meat while in Usrhul or Gauru-forms and then changes back to hishu-form? They still are full of all that meat they had their fill with while in a larger-form; do they scream: &quot;I GOTTA POOP&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood of the Wolf covers this as such on pages 34-35: They're full to a normal degree and any excess food (that's <i>food</i>, not anything else that you happen to have in your stomach that isn't a source of nourishment) is effectively held in abeyance until you take a shape that's big enough to hold it, though after about a day or so it's likely to be gone anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T14:28:50-07:00","id":1561142,"title":"","content":"Hello, new here, running a Forsaken game using 2e wanted to do this for ages, this game is so good. There are some rules I don't understand (I may be missing them as the rules are a little spread around in the book). So in the form of a question: When do werewolves have to roll to remain conscious? in CofD humans have to when any damage is in their last health box, right? on streams I have watched (Very Angry Dogs with Chris Allen) this doesn't seem to come up even when damage is 'wrapping around' to cause aggravated damage, at which point humans would be bleeding out if I understand correctly. It would also mean that the stunned tilt is the closest you can get to knocking a werewolf out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29122-noob_st","name":"Noob_ST","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T15:16:25-07:00","id":1561143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noob_ST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1561142#post1561142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, new here, running a Forsaken game using 2e wanted to do this for ages, this game is so good. There are some rules I don't understand (I may be missing them as the rules are a little spread around in the book). So in the form of a question: When do werewolves have to roll to remain conscious? in CofD humans have to when any damage is in their last health box, right? on streams I have watched (Very Angry Dogs with Chris Allen) this doesn't seem to come up even when damage is 'wrapping around' to cause aggravated damage, at which point humans would be bleeding out if I understand correctly. It would also mean that the stunned tilt is the closest you can get to knocking a werewolf out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome<br /> Rules for this are at page 169<br /> Only Gauru form gives immunity to unconsciousness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T15:33:19-07:00","id":1561145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noob_ST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1561142#post1561142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, new here, running a Forsaken game using 2e wanted to do this for ages, this game is so good. There are some rules I don't understand (I may be missing them as the rules are a little spread around in the book). So in the form of a question: When do werewolves have to roll to remain conscious? in CofD humans have to when any damage is in their last health box, right? on streams I have watched (Very Angry Dogs with Chris Allen) this doesn't seem to come up even when damage is 'wrapping around' to cause aggravated damage, at which point humans would be bleeding out if I understand correctly. It would also mean that the stunned tilt is the closest you can get to knocking a werewolf out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are difficult to knock out for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Regeneration means taking damage in your rightmost health box requires you to roll Stamina to stay conscious, but bashing damage will be healed above that threshold in one turn and lethal damage only requires spending Essence to do the same; thus, the only way to normally ensure a werewolf stays unconscious is to tap their Essence (or make them unwilling to spend Essence to boost their regeneration) and hit them with enough lethal damage to knock them out. (There's some ambiguity in how to parse the &quot;can&quot; in &quot;as long as a werewolf can regenerate her rightmost Health box, she won't bleed out,&quot; but at bare minimum spending Essence on regeneration is reflexive.) This in turn brings us to the second issue:<br /> 2. While 2e doesn't have it as a universal Death Rage trigger like in 1e, being very near death highly incentivizes werewolves to assume Gauru form for its supercharged regeneration, which also prevents the character from needing to roll to remain conscious.<br /> <br /> So basically it's single turns with bashing damage or fifteen minutes with lethal damage if you can prevent them from assuming the killing form or spending Essence on regeneration, barring some other means of bringing their healing ability down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T05:37:20-07:00","id":1562182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1560145#post1560145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you guys make and stay out npc\u2019s for games? I know the usual rule is to give them a few dice and move on but what about more important antagonists? Or even low level mooks? How do I know how many dice these fellas should have?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's several schools of design for this, but most easy to follow. Main ones we can call as Detailed Sandbox, Simple Sandbox and Fit For Group.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Detailed Sandbox</b></u>: jolt down your interpretation of how frequent some values are for Attributes, then Skills, and how common Specializations and skill-related Merits are. Mine go as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Most people have a Weak Attribute at 1, one or two Main Attributes at 3, everything else is 2<br /> <br /> 2. Specializations and Merits are common. Most people rely on them rather than high skill baseline values. Most only have the full skill at 1, maybe 2.<br /> <br /> 3. Skill + Specialization/Merits: If a character works with something, 2. If they're veteran or above the cut, 3. trainees and dabblers, 1.<br /> <br /> 4. Common people make heavy use of optimal conditions, not high dots.<br /> <br /> 5. Anyone with a 4 in the stats deserves a more complete sheet.<br /> <br /> Those guidelines are intuitive after you get used to them, as long as they make sense for you. What I take from mine in practice is:<br /> <br /> - Define 3 Attributes, one at 1, two at 3.<br /> <br /> - Choose Specializations, not Skills. 2 to 5 work in most cases. For each decide if it's 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> - A character will avoid skills that use their Attribute at 1 and favor the Attributes at 3, so each Specialization has a Pool from 4 to 6. 4 is competent but mediocre, 6 is a capable veteran.<br /> <br /> - Only write down combat stats if relevant, as most people will react to combat by fleeing. Defense varies between 2 and 4, most fighters sit squarely at 3.<br /> <br /> At the end you have between 5 to 9 values for stats: 3 Attributes, 2 to 5 Actions and maybe Defense. Everything else you can adjudicate on the fly from those.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Simple Sandbox</b></u>: ditch the Attributes. Write 2 to 5 Actions with a Pool ranging from 4 to 6. Bias towards 5 without shame. Write Defense 3 or 4 if you want.<br /> <br /> Default everything else to 2 or 3 dice and Defense to 2. <hr /><br /> That's all you need, adjust with equipment bonus. Most people aren't doing their jobs with anything that happens to be at hand, they have dedicated tools and spaces if they need more dice, and won't even try under poor conditions.<br /> <br /> Also have NPCs abuse teamwork of any kind. If you need more challenge, add more people and have them use the rules in their favor.<br /> <br /> Fit For Group follows the same list, but the values are based in your PCs and the challenge you want to provide. Take One PC as reference and call their relevant pool X. A weak NPC has X/2, a leveled challenge has X-2, a strong opponent has X+1, an overwhelming threat has X+3. Do not include Equipment or Willpower in X, those are the levers your PCs will have to overcome stronger NPCs. Those are still values for mooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T16:30:02-07:00","id":1563964,"title":"","content":"Anyone use maejinn corrupted lines in their story? I feel like that could be a really cool enemy to throw at some players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T15:09:55-07:00","id":1563986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1563964#post1563964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone use maejinn corrupted lines in their story? I feel like that could be a really cool enemy to throw at some players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. My favorite antagonist group, though 2e brought a ton of competition, amping up pretty much everything else and introducing a lot of new threats. It's particularly nice how you can scale them up from Tarnished to Corrupted to Defiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T08:49:11-07:00","id":1564665,"title":"","content":"What happen in cases like this with Pack Totems, Bans, and Ban conditions?<br /> <br /> From the totem you get their Ban as a prohibited behaviour, but some Bans include a penalty, as an example, for a rank 3 spirit I am designing:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Influences: [X] 3<br /> <u>Ban: The spirit must be in the presence of someone indulging in [X] behaviour every 24 hours, otherwise it becomes morose and lethargic losing it\u2019s defense.</u><br /> Bane: A human that has been voluntarily not engaging in [X] behaviour for a year.</div> <br /> If you do not fulfil the Ban, you get penalised, BUT you also get the Ban condition for not upholding a Ban. So what to do in cases like this?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This type of Ban is wrong, you need simply to curtail behaviour not impose penalties in a Ban.</li> <li>You get both penalties.</li> <li>You get the largest/harshest of those (ST call?).</li> </ol><br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T09:52:23-07:00","id":1564666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1564665#post1564665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happen in cases like this with Pack Totems, Bans, and Ban conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>The totem constructed as an element of the pack provides the rest of the pack with an equivalent Ban in terms of the basic narrative description of what that spirit must or cannot do, which levies the consequences for disregarding it that are described in Step Two of Creating the Totem in Character Creation. Lodge totem Bans work similarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T20:55:25-07:00","id":1564677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1564666#post1564666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The totem constructed as an element of the pack provides the rest of the pack with an equivalent Ban in terms of the basic narrative description of what that spirit must or cannot do, which levies the consequences for disregarding it that are described in Step Two of Creating the Totem in Character Creation. Lodge totem Bans work similarly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I am asking about the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf Core 2ed p.92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">STEP TWO: ASPIRATION AND BAN<br /> Totems have Aspirations, just like any other character.<br /> The totem\u2019s Aspiration acts as a fourth Aspiration for each<br /> pack member.<b> A totem\u2019s ban is appropriate for its Rank, as<br /> described on p. 185. Pack members must uphold the totem\u2019s<br /> ban; a pack member who disregards the totem\u2019s ban once will<br /> suffer it as a Ban Condition. </b>If she breaches the ban again,<br /> she loses her dots in the Totem Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf Core 2ed p.185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">BANS<br /> All spirits suffer from a mystical compulsion known as<br /> the ban, a behavior that the spirit must or must not perform<br /> under certain conditions. Bans increase in both complexity<br /> and consequences with Rank.<br /> Rank 1 spirits have mild bans that are easily triggered<br /> but don\u2019t endanger the spirit. A spirit of bliss can\u2019t resist an<br /> offering of opiates.<br /> <b>Rank 2 and 3 spirits have moderate bans that curtail their<br /> activities in a more serious way than mere distraction. The<br /> murderous spirit of a car that has run down multiple people<br /> loses all Willpower if it doesn\u2019t kill one person a month.</b><br /> Rank 4 and 5 spirits have complicated bans that put an<br /> end to whatever the creature is trying to do \u2014 often in an<br /> explosive fashion. They have consequences in game traits or<br /> long-term actions, but esoteric requirements. The spirit of<br /> Mount Iliamna, a volcano in Alaska, must use its Numina to<br /> kill a victim named by anyone who makes it an offering of<br /> platinum that was mined from its foothills.\u200b.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> So, for Rank 2/3 murderous spirit of a car that has run down multiple people AND is a totem of a pack, if pack does not kill one person a month, they lose all Willpower AND get the ban condition?<br /> <br /> That was my example. Do you get both penalties (the one of not fulfilling the ban that has a stat penalty, willpower in this example, or defense on my previous post) AND the Ban condition? Either? Or is this type of Ban inapropiate for a PAck spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T22:56:39-07:00","id":1564679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1564677#post1564677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for Rank 2/3 murderous spirit of a car that has run down multiple people AND is a totem of a pack, if pack does not kill one person a month, they lose all Willpower AND get the ban condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Only the Condition. They're not the totem.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, they don't get the Ban as a Ban in the same sense. They don't suffer the same metaphysical effect of the spirit.<br /> <br /> What the totem does is set the conditions of their own metaphysical effect as followers of the totem.<br /> <br /> It's like an oath. They aren't affected by the Ban as the totem, they swear to live by the same limitation. Breaking <i>this oath</i> is what causes <u><i>their consequence</i></u>, which is the Ban Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T10:46:36-07:00","id":1564691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1564679#post1564679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Only the Condition. They're not the totem.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, they don't get the Ban as a Ban in the same sense. They don't suffer the same metaphysical effect of the spirit.<br /> <br /> What the totem does is set the conditions of their own metaphysical effect as followers of the totem.<br /> <br /> It's like an oath. They aren't affected by the Ban as the totem, they swear to live by the same limitation. Breaking <i>this oath</i> is what causes <u><i>their consequence</i></u>, which is the Ban Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That is the type explaination I needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T08:26:51-07:00","id":1564703,"title":"","content":"As per the Pack supplement, the members of a pack can be Werewolves, Wolf-Blooded, Humans, Animals, Spirits, and other Supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Can any of those belong to more than one pack? I was thinking of this paragraph regarding the humans (but it might be applicable to nearly all the others) in the Core and the one for Mages in The Pack:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 2ed Core p.91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">THE PERIPHERY<br /> Next, you create the humans who are in the pack, but <b>aren\u2019t<br /> quite aware that they\u2019re in a formal pack,</b> or that Uratha even<br /> exist. They\u2019re friends, family, coworkers, and other people who<br /> fall under the pack\u2019s auspices and protection</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 2ed The Pack p.54</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">MAGES<br /> ...<br /> Show off enough tricks, and every pack will want a<br /> piece of you. The ideologies and constructed religions of packs<br /> are infinitely variable, and <b>some mages try to hold membership<br /> in more than one pack at once\u200b.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T11:52:54-07:00","id":1564704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">lbeaumanior</a> I think it's a practical issue. Like, technically you can, but in practice it doesn't work. The demands of being in a pack are really too intense to make it feasible to split your attentions.<br /> <br /> The point with Mages is that they're the one kind of being that's likely to try it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T18:53:58-07:00","id":1564735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1564703#post1564703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the Pack supplement, the members of a pack can be Werewolves, Wolf-Blooded, Humans, Animals, Spirits, and other Supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Can any of those belong to more than one pack? I was thinking of this paragraph regarding the humans (but it might be applicable to nearly all the others) in the Core and the one for Mages in The Pack:</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it technically possible?<br /> <br /> Yes, it is. With the caveat that it doesn't means necessarily getting the mechanical benefits.<br /> <br /> Is it practically feasible?<br /> <br /> Very unlikely. Can't say a hard no, but it's a very demanding endeavor.<br /> <br /> Is it mechanically/magically beneficial?<br /> <br /> Up to the ST. It's an edge enough case that the game won't put hard rules on it. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Mages being Mages, the key difference is that their curiosity would lead some to try, against all challenges, to find out the metaphysical effect.<br /> <br /> Any character will have little reason to try and keen awareness of the problems for reduced if any benefits. Mages will have the Mystery itself as a legitimate reason to go ahead anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, can circumstances change this? Yes, but not lightly. Even humans unaware of being in a Pack are in a Pack. They live in Pack territory, have loyalties among this group, have a lot of work to do for them. Other Packs will notice at least that this person spend a lot of time in the other's territory and has little time for them.<br /> <br /> A multi-pack member depends first and foremost on the relationship between packs and how this person came in such a position that both want them in the family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}